{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T19:11:03.227Z","ordinal":8,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a13bd3-423a-7082-8f73-b169f3b37bba","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Continue implementing Project D in the existing ~/travel-expense-claim repository.\n\nThe previous milestone is committed and pushed as 65ee4f0. The offline replay already generates four linked batch snapshots, claims.csv, report.md, repair-queue.json, and offline-replay-state.json.\n\nImplement the next milestone now, not just a plan:\n\nInspect the current offline replay report generation, repair queue, and related tests.\n\nImprove report.md to clearly separate:\n\nClaim-specific actionable repair items, grouped by responsible owner, with traceable claim/subject/revision/source references and next actions.\n\nRun-level external blockers, including the inaccessible native Notion reimbursement policy and the unconfirmed authoritative case clock.\n\nClearly label this output as an offline replay of retained evidence, not a fresh live-source run.\n\nPreserve partial progress: unresolved claims must not prevent independent valid records from being processed.\n\nDo not invent policy rules, eligibility amounts, approvals, payment confirmations, or case-clock  dates.\n\nAdd or update automated tests for the report sections, grouping, traceability, and unresolved blockers.\n\nRun the complete test suite and git diff --check.\n\nRegenerate the offline replay outputs and summarize the actual results.\n\nDo not commit or push yet. Show me the files changed, tests passed, and any remaining blockers. Preserve all existing Git and Entire.io history."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a13bd3-3cec-7081-b847-b31e41528363","create_time":1792005063.2267163,"content_item_kinds":["user.text"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a13bd3-423a-7082-8f73-b169f3b37bba","turn_id":"01a13bd3-3cec-7081-b847-b31e41528363","role":"user"},"revisio