tion from revision 2 to 3 requires dependency revalidation: approvals. Next: obtain current-revision decisions; prior decisions remain historical only (opened `source-capture-20261014T100034Z` / `arrival-004`; sources: claim-updates-binder@03c15787d18e2928457cd0164b573dc03a3baade0ed26a391ba79c73a568da3b#PDF page 2, claim-updates-binder@03c15787d18e2928457cd0164b573dc03a3baade0ed26a391ba79c73a568da3b#PDF page 7, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Review ledger', row 61, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Review ledger', row 62, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Review ledger', row 63, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Finance activity', row 44, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Finance activity', row 22, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Finance activity', row 23, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Finance activity', row 24, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Finance activity', row 25).\n- `correction:C19:r3:calculations` — claim `C19` r3: Material correction from revision 2 to 3 requires dependency revalidation: calculations. Next: recalculate and verify amounts for the corrected claim revision (opened `source-capture-20261014T100034Z` / `arrival-004`; sources: claim-updates-binder@03c15787d18e2928457cd0164b573dc03a3baade0ed26a391ba79c73a568da3b#PDF page 2, claim-updates-binder@03c15787d18e2928457cd0164b573dc03a3baade0ed26a391ba79c73a568da3b#PDF page 7, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Review ledger', row 61, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Review ledger', row 62, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Review ledger', row 63, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Finance activity', row 44, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Finance activity', row 22, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Finance activity', row 23, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Finance activity', row 24, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Finance activity', row 25).\n- `correction:C19:r3:trip-permit` — claim `C19` r3: Material correction from revision 2 to 3 requires dependency revalidation: trip-permit. Next: recheck trip and permit identity and revision consistency (opened `source-capture-20261014T100034Z` / `arrival-004`; sources: claim-updates-binder@03c15787d18e2928457cd0164b573dc03a3baade0ed26a391ba79c73a568da3b#PDF page 2, claim-updates-binder@03c15787d18e2928457cd0164b573dc03a3baade0ed26a391ba79c73a568da3b#PDF page 7, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Review ledger', row 61, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Review ledger', row 62, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Review ledger', row 63, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Finance activity', row 44, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Finance activity', row 22, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Finance activity', row 23, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Finance activity', row 24, travel-registers-workbook@579691b671acc735d1fdbb4944a2daf397b13307075ba74f15fa8bc24daa75b8#tab 'Finance activity', row 25).\n\n### Scenario-level blockers\n\n- `scenario-case-clock` (scenario `arrival-batch-clock`): The task calls for a supplied case clock, but no explicit scenario date, time, or timezone was confirmed in the original task text or complete stakeholder interview export. Owner: Exercise facilitator. Next: Provide the authoritative scenario case clock before consuming any arrival batch. Evidence needed: Explicit scenario date, time, and timezone from the facilitator or original task material.\n- `reimbursement-policy-pol-2026-2` (policy `POL-2026.2`): The fresh native Notion attempt returned a generic HTML shell; earlier API access returned HTTP 401. No policy content was retained. Owner: Travel Administration Lead / exercise facilitator. Next: Provide an authorized native export or enable read access to the original Notion page, then perform a fresh native read. Evidence needed: Complete policy content from the original Notion page or authorized native export, with observed URL/version and retained-content hash.\n\n## Outputs\n\n- Current claims: `claims.csv` (exact required CSV columns).\n- Full integration state and source-linked histories: `offline-replay-state.json`.\n- Repair queue: `repair-queue.json` (grouped by owner, item identity retained).\n\nResume only after obtaining the authoritative case clock and an accessible native reimbursement policy, then perform fresh reads of all five source locations. This replay does not modify source content or send requests.\n.venv/\n__pycache__/\n.pytest_cache/\n*.egg-info/\nREADME.md:43:travel-claim offline-replay artifacts/runs/<retained-run-id>\nREADME.md:46:This command does **not** make native-source requests. It checks that parsed records bind the current `sources.json`, integrates arrival batches in numeric order, and writes immutable `batches/arrival-NNN.json` snapshots linked by predecessor hashes. It writes the latest `claims.csv`, `repair-queue.json`, `offline-replay-state.json`, and `report.md` alongside that run's retained inputs. The report, sidecar, and each snapshot label the result as an offline replay. Existing batch chains or output files are never overwritten; start a separately identified retained run to create a new chain. When the case clock is unresolved, snapshots retain the blocker and are only structural replay projections; no clock-dependent, policy-dependent, approval, or entitlement result is inferred.\nREADME.md:84:The implementation supports fresh source capture, byte-bound manifests, loss-aware transcription, schema/hash-checked snapshots, policy-neutral arrival-ordered replay, source-classified Finance reconciliation, exact CSV output, and local owner-grouped repair tracking. `offline-replay` is a structural replay only: the inaccessible reimbursement policy and unconfirmed case clock keep policy conclusions, approval readiness, entitlement, and closure unresolved. Human replies are not imported automatically, and the command never sends repair drafts or moves money. Do not treat an offline replay as a fresh source read or completed claim processing.\nsrc/travel_claim/cli.py:90:        \"offline-replay\",\nsrc/travel_claim/cli.py:183:    if args.command == \"offline-replay\":\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Deterministic claim summary CSV and owner-grouped local repair queue.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport csv\nimport json\nimport os\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\n\nCLAIMS_COLUMNS = (\n    \"claim_id\",\n    \"revision\",\n    \"trip_id\",\n    \"status\",\n    \"allowed_cents\",\n    \"paid_cents\",\n    \"balance_cents\",\n    \"next_owner\",\n    \"reason\",\n)\n\nCLAIM_STATUSES = {\n    \"pending\", \"held\", \"ready\", \"closed-reimbursed\", \"closed-no-payment\", \"rejected\", \"withdrawn\"\n}\n\nREPAIR_ITEM_FIELDS = (\n    \"item_id\",\n    \"subject_type\",\n    \"subject_id\",\n    \"revision\",\n    \"source_refs\",\n    \"missing_or_return_reason\",\n    \"owner\",\n    \"next_action\",\n)\n\n\ndef _money(value: Any, field: str, allow_negative: bool = False) -> int | None:\n    if value is None:\n        return None\n    if isinstance(value, bool) or not isinstance(value, int):\n        raise ValueError(f\"{field} must be integer cents or null\")\n    if not allow_negative and value < 0:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{field} cannot be negative\")\n    return value\n\n\ndef write_claims_csv(claims: list[dict], path: Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Write one row per supplied current claim with the required exact header.\"\"\"\n    ids = [claim.get(\"claim_id\") for claim in claims]\n    if any(not value for value in ids) or len(ids) != len(set(ids)):\n        raise ValueError(\"claims must contain one nonempty, unique current row per claim_id\")\n    prepared = []\n    for claim in sorted(claims, key=lambda row: row[\"claim_id\"]):\n        missing = set(CLAIMS_COLUMNS) - set(claim)\n        if missing:\n            raise ValueError(f\"claim {claim.get('claim_id')} is missing CSV fields: {sorted(missing)}\")\n        row = {key: claim[key] for key in CLAIMS_COLUMNS}\n        if isinstance(row[\"revision\"], bool) or not isinstance(row[\"revision\"], int) or row[\"revision\"] < 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"claim {claim['claim_id']} revision must be a positive integer\")\n        for key in (\"claim_id\", \"trip_id\", \"status\", \"reason\"):\n            if not isinstance(row[key], str) or not row[key]:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{key} must be a nonempty string\")\n        if row[\"status\"] not in CLAIM_STATUSES:\n            raise ValueError(f\"unsupported claim status {row['status']!r}\")\n        row[\"allowed_cents\"] = _money(row[\"allowed_cents\"], \"allowed_cents\")\n        row[\"paid_cents\"] = _money(row[\"paid_cents\"], \"paid_cents\")\n        row[\"balance_cents\"] = _money(row[\"balance_cents\"], \"balance_cents\", allow_negative=True)\n        for key in (\"next_owner\", \"reason\"):\n            if row[key] is not None and not isinstance(row[key], str):\n                raise ValueError(f\"{key} must be a string or null\")\n            row[key] = \"\" if row[key] is None else row[key]\n        prepared.append(row)\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    with path.open(\"x\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as stream:\n        writer = csv.DictWriter(stream, fieldnames=CLAIMS_COLUMNS, extrasaction=\"raise\")\n        writer.writeheader()\n        writer.writerows(prepared)\n\n\ndef new_repair_queue() -> dict:\n    return {\"queue_version\": \"owner-queue/1\", \"items\": {}, \"events\": []}\n\n\ndef add_repair_item(\n    queue: dict,\n    *,\n    item_id: str,\n    subject_type: str,\n    subject_id: str,\n    revision: int,\n    source_refs: list[str],\n    missing_or_return_reason: str,\n    owner: str,\n    next_action: str,\n    run_id: str,\n    batch_id: str,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Add a distinct open item. Request content is a local draft only.\"\"\"\n    if not item_id or item_id in queue[\"items\"]:\n        raise ValueError(f\"repair item ID is empty or already exists: {item_id!r}\")\n    if subject_type not in {\"claim\", \"trip\", \"permit\"}:\n        raise ValueError(\"subject_type must be claim, trip, or permit\")\n    if not subject_id or not owner or not missing_or_return_reason or not next_action:\n        raise ValueError(\"subject, owner, reason, and next action are required\")\n    if isinstance(revision, bool) or not isinstance(revision, int) or revision < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"revision must be a positive integer\")\n    if not isinstance(source_refs, list) or not all(isinstance(ref, str) and ref for ref in source_refs):\n        raise ValueError(\"source_refs must be a list of nonempty references\")\n    item = {\n        \"item_id\": item_id,\n        \"subject_type\": subject_type,\n        \"subject_id\": subject_id,\n        \"revision\": revision,\n        \"source_refs\": list(dict.fromkeys(source_refs)),\n        \"missing_or_return_reason\": missing_or_return_reason,\n        \"owner\": owner,\n        \"next_action\": next_action,\n        \"status\": \"open\",\n        \"run_id\": run_id,\n        \"batch_id\": batch_id,\n        \"response_id\": None,\n        \"resolution_source_refs\": [],\n        \"history\": [],\n        \"request_draft\": {\"status\": \"draft\", \"sent\": False},\n    }\n    queue[\"items\"][item_id] = item\n    queue[\"events\"].append({\n        \"event\": \"item-opened\",\n        \"item_id\": item_id,\n        \"run_id\": run_id,\n        \"batch_id\": batch_id,\n        \"status\": \"open\",\n    })\n\n\ndef apply_partial_response(\n    queue: dict,\n    *,\n    response_id: str,\n    item_outcomes: dict[str, dict],\n    run_id: str,\n    batch_id: str,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Record a supplied response against explicitly matched repair item IDs.\n\n    Only `supported` plus at least one retained source reference resolves an\n    item. Every other outcome remains open. Unmentioned items are untouched.\n    \"\"\"\n    allowed = {\"supported\", \"insufficient\", \"conflicting\", \"unanswered\"}\n    if not response_id:\n        raise ValueError(\"response_id is required\")\n    if not isinstance(item_outcomes, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"item_outcomes must map repair item IDs to outcomes\")\n    planned: list[tuple[str, dict, str, list[str], dict | None]] = []\n    for item_id, outcome in item_outcomes.items():\n        if item_id not in queue[\"items\"]:\n            raise KeyError(f\"response references unknown repair item {item_id}\")\n        if not isinstance(outcome, dict):\n            raise ValueError(f\"response outcome for {item_id} must be an object\")\n        kind = outcome.get(\"outcome\")\n        if kind not in allowed:\n            raise ValueError(f\"invalid response outcome for {item_id}: {kind!r}\")\n        refs = outcome.get(\"source_refs\", [])\n        if not isinstance(refs, list) or not all(isinstance(ref, str) and ref for ref in refs):\n            raise ValueError(f\"response source_refs must be a list of references for {item_id}\")\n        if kind == \"supported\" and not refs:\n            raise ValueError(f\"supported response {item_id} requires source references\")\n        item = queue[\"items\"][item_id]\n        if outcome.get(\"note\") is not None and not isinstance(outcome.get(\"note\"), str):\n            raise ValueError(f\"response note must be a string or null for {item_id}\")\n        prior_event = next(\n            (event for event in reversed(queue[\"events\"])\n             if event.get(\"event\") == \"response-recorded\"\n             and event.get(\"response_id\") == response_id\n             and event.get(\"item_id\") == item_id),\n            None,\n        )\n        normalized_refs = list(dict.fromkeys(refs))\n        if prior_event is not None:\n            same = (\n                prior_event.get(\"outcome\") == kind\n                and prior_event.get(\"source_refs\") == normalized_refs\n                and prior_event.get(\"note\") == outcome.get(\"note\")\n            )\n            if same:\n                planned.append((item_id, item, kind, normalized_refs, prior_event))\n                continue\n            raise ValueError(f\"conflicting replay for repair response {response_id}/{item_id}\")\n        planned.append((item_id, item, kind, normalized_refs, None))\n\n    # Mutate only after every item in this partial response passed validation.\n    for item_id, item, kind, normalized_refs, prior_event in planned:\n        if prior_event is not None:\n            continue\n        prior = {\n            \"response_id\": response_id,\n            \"outcome\": kind,\n            \"note\": item_outcomes[item_id].get(\"note\"),\n            \"source_refs\": normalized_refs,\n            \"run_id\": run_id,\n            \"batch_id\": batch_id,\n            \"previous_status\": item[\"status\"],\n        }\n        item[\"history\"].append(prior)\n        item[\"response_id\"] = response_id\n        if kind == \"supported\":\n            item[\"status\"] = \"resolved\"\n            item[\"resolution_source_refs\"] = normalized_refs\n        else:\n            item[\"status\"] = \"open\"\n        queue[\"events\"].append({\n            \"event\": \"response-recorded\",\n            \"item_id\": item_id,\n            \"response_id\": response_id,\n            \"outcome\": kind,\n            \"note\": outcome.get(\"note\"),\n            \"source_refs\": normalized_refs,\n            \"run_id\": run_id,\n            \"batch_id\": batch_id,\n            \"status\": item[\"status\"],\n        })\n\n\ndef update_repair_item(\n    queue: dict,\n    *,\n    item_id: str,\n    update_id: str,\n    run_id: str,\n    batch_id: str,\n    revision: int | None = None,\n    source_refs: list[str] | None = None,\n    missing_or_return_reason: str | None = None,\n    owner: str | None = None,\n    next_action: str | None = None,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Update a repair item's mutable trace fields without losing its history.\n\n    Item and subject identity never change. Advancing its subject revision\n    reopens the item and clears the prior resolution pointer while preserving\n    the prior response and fields in the append-only history.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not update_id:\n        raise ValueError(\"update_id is required\")\n    if item_id not in queue.get(\"items\", {}):\n        raise KeyError(f\"unknown repair item {item_id}\")\n    item = queue[\"items\"][item_id]\n    changes = {}\n    if revision is not None:\n        if isinstance(revision, bool) or not isinstance(revision, int) or revision < 1:\n            raise ValueError(\"revision