{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T19:15:34.561Z","ordinal":91,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a13bd1-7420-72c0-963e-58742d1be7bf","turn_id":"01a13bd7-3aa0-7972-adeb-ce27fff74914","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-82915e85-11bd-4ebb-9dd7-3c55e57f301a","process_id":"19507","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","git status --short; git diff -- README.md src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py tests/test_offline_replay.py; git diff --cached; git branch --show-current; git remote -v; git config --get core.hooksPath; ls .entire"],"cwd":"file:///home/maxg/travel-expense-claim","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short; git diff -- README.md src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py tests/test_offline_replay.py; git diff --cached; git branch --show-current; git remote -v; git config --get core.hooksPath; ls .entire"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":" M README.md\n M src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\n M tests/test_offline_replay.py\n?? artifacts/runs/\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 3eb867f..d8b58f3 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -45,6 +45,8 @@ travel-claim offline-replay artifacts/runs/<retained-run-id>\n \n This command does **not** make native-source requests. It checks that parsed records bind the current `sources.json`, integrates arrival batches in numeric order, and writes immutable `batches/arrival-NNN.json` snapshots linked by predecessor hashes. It writes the latest `claims.csv`, `repair-queue.json`, `offline-replay-state.json`, and `report.md` alongside that run's retained inputs. The report, sidecar, and each snapshot label the result as an offline replay. Existing batch chains or output files are never overwritten; start a separately identified retained run to create a new chain. When the case clock is unresolved, snapshots retain the blocker and are only structural replay projections; no clock-dependent, policy-dependent, approval, or entitlement result is inferred.\n \n+The report separates open claim repairs and trip/permit repairs by responsible owner from run-level external blockers. Each repair retains its subject, revision, source references, opening run/batch, and next action. Resolved items remain in the full queue history. Independent valid records continue processing while other claims remain unresolved.\n+\n Once authorized batch state has been processed, pass only evidence-derived state to the snapshot sealer. The first batch has no predecessor; every later batch references the previous snapshot and exact SHA-256. Binding paths are relative to the run directory (`sources.json`, `batches/<prior-batch>.json`).\n \n ```bash\ndiff --git a/src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py b/src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\nindex b8f9ac5..493d9b9 100644\n--- a/src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\n+++ b/src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\n@@ -66,24 +66,41 @@ def _report(\n         \"\",\n         \"Each snapshot retains the observed claim revision and matching decision IDs. Decisions are not treated as proof of policy compliance. Finance event identities and supported confirmed cash are retained; no obligation or entitlement is inferred. Claim monetary entitlement and balance remain null when unsupported.\",\n         \"\",\n-        \"## Outstanding work by owner\",\n-        \"\",\n-        f\"Full item-level queue and history: `{output_paths['queue'].name}`. Local request drafts are unsent.\",\n+        \"Independent valid records continue through the replay while unresolved claims remain pending. External blockers prevent authoritative live-run conclusions, not retention of independent evidence or partial progress.\",\n         \"\",\n     ])\n     queue = latest[\"domain\"][\"repair_queue\"]\n-    for owner, items in owner_grouped_view(queue).items():\n-        lines.append(f\"### {owner}\")\n-        lines.append(\"\")\n-        for item in items:\n-            lines.append(\n-                f\"- `{item['item_id']}` — {item['subject