 five native URLs again. The implementation has no cached/offline fallback. The caller supplies a case clock from the authorized scenario inputs; omit it only for source-acquisition-only capture before a batch clock is available.\\n\\n```bash\\ntravel-claim capture-sources <run-id> artifacts/runs/<run-id> --case-clock '<scenario ISO timestamp>'\\ntravel-claim verify-sources artifacts/runs/<run-id>\\ntravel-claim parse-retained artifacts/runs/<run-id>\\n```\\n\\n`capture-sources` writes `sources.json` and retains usable responses under `sources/`. It exits `0` only when all five source scopes were read, `2` when one or more are unavailable/partial, and `1` on a capture or output error. A successful HTTP response is not considered a read unless the expected source content is present and structurally usable. Existing run manifests and retained files are not overwritten. Google Drive PDFs and the workbook use native export routes; the manifest keeps the provided native URL, source locator, observed UTC time/version, retrieval outcome, scope and retained-byte SHA-256.\\n\\nWhen source access is partial, record usable pieces as `read` and inaccessible pieces as `unavailable`; unavailable entries have null path/hash/version and a specific error. Do not substitute prior downloads. A replay from retained inputs must be explicitly implemented and labeled as offline replay.\\n\\n`parse-retained` first verifies the manifest and retained-byte hashes, then writes `parsed-records.json`. PDF text stays grouped by page, workbook data stays grouped by tab and row, and every extracted record includes its source ID, SHA-256 and page/row locator. This is a transcription layer; it does not evaluate policy or infer claim outcomes. Its exit status is `2` for partial inputs or an unavailable case clock and `1` for a verification or parsing error.\\n\\n### Explicit offline replay\\n\\nWhen source retrieval is unavailable, replay only the previously retained and hash-verified inputs with an explicit offline command:\\n\\n```bash\\ntravel-claim offline-replay artifacts/runs/<retained-run-id>\\n```\\n\\nThis command does **not** make native-source requests. It checks that parsed records bind the current `sources.json`, integrates arrival batches in numeric order, and writes immutable `batches/arrival-NNN.json` snapshots linked by predecessor hashes. It writes the latest `claims.csv`, `repair-queue.json`, `offline-replay-state.json`, `report.md`, and `follow-up-drafts.md` alongside that run's retained inputs. The report, sidecar, and each snapshot label the result as an offline replay. Existing batch chains or output files are never overwritten; start a separately identified retained run to create a new chain. When the case clock is unresolved, snapshots retain the blocker and are only structural replay projections; no clock-dependent, policy-dependent, approval, or entitlement result is inferred.\\n\\nThe report separates open claim repairs and trip/permit repairs by responsible owner from run-level external blockers. Each repair retains its subject, revision, source references, opening run/batch, and next action. Resolved items remain in the full queue history. `follow-up-drafts.md` contains one unsent message per responsible owner, with separate claim, trip/permit, and external-blocker sections. Only unresolved items produce drafts; every message requires human review and retains reasons, requested actions, and evidence references. Independent valid records continue processing while other claims remain unresolved.\\n\\nOnce authorized batch state has been processed, pass only evidence-derived state to the snapshot sealer. The first batch has no predecessor; every later batch references the previous snapshot and exact SHA-256. Binding paths are relative to the run directory (`sources.json`, `batches/<prior-batch>.json`).\\n\\n```bash\\ntravel-claim seal-batch artifacts/runs/<run-id> <batch-id> state.json --run-id <run-id> [--predecessor artifacts/runs/<run-id>/batches/<prior-batch>.json]\\ntravel-claim verify-batch artifacts/runs/<run-id> artifacts/runs/<run-id>/batches/<batch-id>.json\\ntravel-claim write-claims-csv current-claims.json artifacts/runs/<run-id>/claims.csv\\n```\\n\\nThe state input is a JSON object with `claims`, `requests`, `travel_cancellations`, `admitted_event_ids`, and `issues` arrays matching `snapshot.schema.json`. No approval, Finance event, or claim answer is created by these foundation commands. The CSV writer accepts one current row per claim and emits exactly:\\n\\n```text\\nclaim_id,revision,trip_id,status,allowed_cents,paid_cents,balance_cents,next_owner,reason\\n```\\n\\nUnknown money is `null` in state and blank in CSV; zero remains `0`.\\n\\nThe policy-neutral structural APIs are in `travel_claim.workflow`: they retain claim/trip/permit revision histories, match decisions to exact subject revisions without applying outcomes, deduplicate immutable event IDs while surfacing payload conflicts, and reduce independent trip/permit cancellation requests and confirmations. Cancellation reductions have no claim or Finance side effects.\\n\\nThe owner-grouped repair queue API is in `travel_claim.outputs`. Queue items retain their item and subject identity, type/revision, source references, reason, owner, next action, run/batch history, and a local unsent draft marker. Partial response validation is item-specific and atomic; revision updates reopen affected work, preserve prior response history and recalculate the owner grouping. Unsupported, conflicting, insufficient, or unanswered items stay open.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n```bash\\npython -m pytest\\n```\\n\\nSnapshot validation can also be run directly:\\n\\n```bash\\ntravel-claim validate-snapshot artifacts/runs/<run-id>/batches/<batch-id>.json\\n```\\n\\n`verify-batch` also checks the source-manifest bytes, predecessor bytes, and cancellation-to-issue references. Do not overwrite a sealed snapshot; create a new run with a documented link if later processing changes its content.\\n\\n## Current implementation boundary\\n\\nThe implementation supports fresh source capture, byte-bound manifests, loss-aware transcription, schema/hash-checked snapshots, policy-neutral arrival-ordered replay, source-classified Finance reconciliation, exact CSV output, and local owner-grouped repair tracking. `offline-replay` is a structural replay only: the inaccessible reimbursement policy and unconfirmed case clock keep policy conclusions, approval readiness, entitlement, and closure un…292 tokens truncated….txt\\n.entire/metadata/01a1362a-c291-7d91-b238-dbd39c052b2e/full.jsonl\\n963dd8669b418490417a89e31dfe490f2d53a4b0 refs/entire/checkpoints/5K/01M4XXKKGWCVRE9H1RM4GDS95K\\n04ab5e8811b92cfcad03f19e92fd904cde97b644 refs/entire/checkpoints/E5/01M4V39WVQVRDZ35CG4NAPVKE5\\n62512e9159f5a5ab931b3ed0879d7bebb0364e80 refs/entire/checkpoints/G7/01M4X4X7VR3NGD79SS373686G7\\nd64a297b247d1f3ca152a5e11d41eec4cf1ed9c0 refs/entire/checkpoints/K4/01M4XSFYKTYR4N945RR3STV1K4\\n1b9ccfb709570ead46e47bcd46ce9426dc4511c9 refs/entire/checkpoints/RV/01M4XY39126AJFGDNDNGX0MJRV\\n76d0ea68b628678b160b195aed742ef216ee079d refs/entire/checkpoints/WY/01M4V30HBGR66T8EESNK12VRWY\\nd105c11f1e2ec7deb64dd30984894427c8837e90 refs/entire/checkpoints/XH/01M4XVE8KZ1XAFRTPH206H9RXH\\n15aa8571d85c69e6fd8bdfd39c88b95fbc76ed08 refs/entire/checkpoints/XN/01M4V3FDNC3QWXB07KVKK7EBXN\\n74a5f3699ca916a3564ef09525828fa55a54ba2c refs/heads/entire/efc7e91-e3b0c4\\nefc7e91504cc4c49cb7a9e96f6247e2584910bac refs/heads/main\\nefc7e91504cc4c49cb7a9e96f6247e2584910bac refs/remotes/origin/HEAD\\nefc7e91504cc4c49cb7a9e96f6247e2584910bac refs/remotes/origin/main\\n                lambda row: next((f[\\\"value\\\"] for f in row[\\\"fields\\\"] if f[\\\"label\\\"].strip().lower() == \\\"arrival batch\\\"), None))\\n    count_batch(\\\"decisions\\\", decisions, lambda row: _value(row, \\\"Arrival batch\\\"))\\n    count_batch(\\\"finance_events\\\", finance, lambda row: _value(row, \\\"Arrival batch\\\"))\\n    count_batch(\\\"cancellation_activities\\\", cancellations, lambda row: _value(row, \\\"Arrival batch\\\"))\\n\\n    result = {\\n        \\\"schema_version\\\": RECORD_SCHEMA,\\n        \\\"run_id\\\": manifest[\\\"run_id\\\"],\\n        \\\"source_manifest\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"sources.json\\\", \\\"sha256\\\": hashlib.sha256((run_dir / \\\"sources.json\\\").read_bytes()).hexdigest()},\\n        \\\"case_clock\\\": manifest[\\\"case_clock\\\"],\\n        \\\"case_clock_state\\\": \\\"supplied\\\" if manifest[\\\"case_clock\\\"] else \\\"not_in_accessible_retained_sources\\\",\\n        \\\"case_clock_issue\\\": None if manifest[\\\"case_clock\\\"] else {\\n            \\\"reason\\\": \\\"No supplied scenario case-clock value was present in the retained native PDFs, workbook, or interview record used for this run.\\\",\\n            \\\"owner\\\": \\\"Exercise facilitator\\\",\\n            \\\"next_action\\\": \\\"Provide the authoritative scenario case clock before consuming any arrival batch.\\\",\\n        },\\n        \\\"arrival_batches\\\": sorted(batch_ids),\\n        \\\"arrival_batch_contents\\\": batch_contents,\\n        \\\"missing_sources\\\": [\\n            {\\\"source_id\\\": row[\\\"source_id\\\"], \\\"url\\\": row[\\\"url\\\"], \\\"locator\\\": row[\\\"locator\\\"],\\n             \\\"error\\\": row[\\\"error\\\"], \\\"missing_scope\\\": row.get(\\\"missing_scope\\\", [])}\\n            for row in manifest[\\\"files\\\"] if row[\\\"status\\\"] != \\\"read\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"source_inventory\\\": parsed_sources,\\n        \\\"pdf_pages\\\": pages,\\n        \\\"workbook_sheets\\\": sheets,\\n        \\\"records\\\": {\\n            \\\"claim_revisions\\\": claim_revisions,\\n            \\\"trips\\\": trips,\\n            \\\"permits\\\": permits,\\n            \\\"receipts\\\": receipt_records,\\n            \\\"decisions\\\": decisions,\\n            \\\"finance_events\\\": finance,\\n            \\\"cancellation_activities\\\": cancellations,\\n        },\\n        \\\"processing_boundary\\\": {\\n            \\\"policy_dependent_conclusions\\\": \\\"unresolved\\\",\\n            \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Native reimbursement policy content is unavailable; parsed source values are not eligibility, entitlement, approval-readiness, or closure decisions.\\\",\\n            \\\"owner\\\": \\\"Travel Administration Lead / facilitator for source access\\\",\\n            \\\"next_action\\\": \\\"Provide an authorized native export or enable read access to the original Notion policy, then perform a fresh native read.\\\",\\n        },\\n        \\\"unresolved_issues\\\": [\\n            {\\n                \\\"record_id\\\": \\\"scenario-case-clock\\\",\\n                \\\"subject_type\\\": \\\"scenario\\\",\\n                \\\"subject_id\\\": \\\"arrival-batch-clock\\\",\\n                \\\"revision\\\": None,\\n                \\\"affected_scope\\\": \\\"all batch cutoff decisions and arrival-state consumption\\\",\\n                \\\"reason\\\": \\\"The task calls for a supplied case clock, but no explicit scenario date, time, or timezone was confirmed in the original task text or complete stakeholder interview export.\\\",\\n                \\\"owner\\\": \\\"Exercise facilitator\\\",\\n                \\\"next_action\\\": \\\"Provide the authoritative scenario case clock before consuming any arrival batch.\\\",\\n                \\\"evidence_needed\\\": \\\"Explicit scenario date, time, and timezone from the facilitator or original task material.\\\",\\n            },\\n            {\\n                \\\"record_id\\\": \\\"reimbursement-policy-pol-2026-2\\\",\\n                \\\"subject_type\\\": \\\"policy\\\",\\n                \\\"subject_id\\\": \\\"POL-2026.2\\\",\\n                \\\"revision\\\": None,\\n                \\\"affected_scope\\\": \\\"eligibility, entitlement, approval readiness, reimbursement caps and final closure\\\",\\n                \\\"reason\\\": \\\"The fresh native Notion attempt returned a generic HTML shell; earlier API access returned HTTP 401. No policy content was retained.\\\",\\n                \\\"owner\\\": \\\"Travel Administration Lead / exercise facilitator\\\",\\n                \\\"next_action\\\": \\\"Provide an authorized native export or enable read access to the original Notion page, then perform a fresh native read.\\\",\\n                \\\"evidence_needed\\\": \\\"Complete policy content from the original Notion page or authorized native export, with observed URL/version and retained-content hash.\\\",\\n            },\\n        ],\\n    }\\n    destination = output_path or (run_dir / OUTPUT_NAME)\\n    if destination.exists():\\n        raise FileExistsError(f\\\"Refusing to overwrite parsed output: {destination}\\\")\\n    destination.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    destination.write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \\\"\\\\n\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\nimport csv\\nimport hashlib\\nimport io\\nimport json\\nimport zipfile\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nimport pytest\\n\\nfrom travel_claim.outputs import (\\n    CLAIMS_COLUMNS,\\n    add_repair_item,\\n    apply_partial_response,\\n    load_repair_queue,\\n    new_repair_queue,\\n    owner_grouped_view,\\n    write_claims_csv,\\n    write_repair_queue,\\n)\\nfrom travel_claim.snapshots import seal_batch_snapshot, verify_snapshot\\nfrom travel_claim.sources import SOURCES, capture_sources, verify_source_manifest\\n\\n\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nSCHEMA = ROOT / \\\"snapshot.schema.json\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef _xlsx_bytes():\\n    buffer = io.BytesIO()\\n    with zipfile.ZipFile(buffer, \\\"w\\\") as archive:\\n        archive.writestr(\\\"xl/workbook.xml\\\", \\\"<workbook><sheets/></workbook>\\\")\\n    return buffer.getvalue()\\n\\n\\ndef _source_bodies():\\n    return {\\n        \\\"policy-pol-2026-2\\\": b\\\"<!doctype html><title>Travel reimbursement policy POL-2026.2 Alderbridge</title>\\\",\\n        \\\"initial-claim-binder\\\": b\\\"%PDF-1.4\\\\ninitial pdf\\\\n%%EOF\\\",\\n        \\\"claim-updates-binder\\\": b\\\"%PDF-1.4\\\\nupdates pdf\\\\n%%EOF\\\",\\n        \\\"receipt-binder\\\": b\\\"%PDF-1.4\\\\nreceipts pdf\\\\n%%EOF\\\",\\n        \\\"travel-registers-workbook\\\": _xlsx_bytes(),\\n    }\\n\\n\\ndef _capture(tmp_path, *, bodies=None, case_clock=\\\"2026-09-01T00:00:00Z\\\"):\\n    bodies = bodies or _source_bodies()\\n    attempts = []\\n\\n    def fetch(url, timeout):\\n        attempts.append(url)\\n        source = next(s for s in SOURCES if (s.export_url or s.url) == url)\\n        return bodies[source.source_id], {\\\"ETag\\\": f'\\\"{source.source_id}-v1\\\"'}, url\\n\\n    run_dir = tmp_path / \\\"run-1\\\"\\n    manifest = capture_sources(\\n        run_dir,\\n        run_id=\\\"run-1\\\",\\n        case_clock=case_clock,\\n        fetch=fetch,\\n        observed_at=iter([f\\\"2026-09-01T00:00:0{i}Z\\\" for i in range(10)]).__next__,\\n    )\\n    return run_dir, manifest, attempts\\n\\n\\ndef _empty_state():\\n    return {\\n        \\\"claims\\\": [],\\n        \\\"requests\\\": [],\\n        \\\"travel_cancellations\\\": [],\\n        \\\"admitted_event_ids\\\": [],\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a13be4-8a38-7ef3-b2cb-8b3e8591f919","create_time":1792006222.7673728}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
