igibility, entitlement, approval readiness, batch consumption, and financial reconciliation remain blocked. The facilitator must supply the authoritative scenario case clock; the Travel Administration Lead/facilitator must provide accessible original Notion policy content for a fresh native read.\\nREADME.md:24:Every new capture invokes all five native URLs again. The implementation has no cached/offline fallback. The caller supplies a case clock from the authorized scenario inputs; omit it only for source-acquisition-only capture before a batch clock is available.\\nREADME.md:27:travel-claim capture-sources <run-id> artifacts/runs/<run-id> --case-clock '<scenario ISO timestamp>'\\nREADME.md:36:`parse-retained` first verifies the manifest and retained-byte hashes, then writes `parsed-records.json`. PDF text stays grouped by page, workbook data stays grouped by tab and row, and every extracted record includes its source ID, SHA-256 and page/row locator. This is a transcription layer; it does not evaluate policy or infer claim outcomes. Its exit status is `2` for partial inputs or an unavailable case clock and `1` for a verification or parsing error.\\nREADME.md:46:This command does **not** make native-source requests. It checks that parsed records bind the current `sources.json`, integrates arrival batches in numeric order, and writes immutable `batches/arrival-NNN.json` snapshots linked by predecessor hashes. It writes the latest `claims.csv`, `repair-queue.json`, `offline-replay-state.json`, `report.md`, and `follow-up-drafts.md` alongside that run's retained inputs. The report, sidecar, and each snapshot label the result as an offline replay. Existing batch chains or output files are never overwritten; start a separately identified retained run to create a new chain. When the case clock is unresolved, snapshots retain the blocker and are only structural replay projections; no clock-dependent, policy-dependent, approval, or entitlement result is inferred.\\nREADME.md:92:Each check is `PASS`, `BLOCKED`, or `FAIL`; exit codes are 0, 2, and 1 respectively. Integrity failures take precedence over blockers. Missing policy content and an unconfirmed authoritative case clock remain `BLOCKED`, even when retained artifacts are intact. An offline replay always remains blocked for final live-source submission. This validator covers the retained repository requirements and never certifies policy eligibility, approvals, financial closure, full native assignment compliance, or fresh execution from replay artifacts.\\nREADME.md:96:The implementation supports fresh source capture, byte-bound manifests, loss-aware transcription, schema/hash-checked snapshots, policy-neutral arrival-ordered replay, source-classified Finance reconciliation, exact CSV output, and local owner-grouped repair tracking. `offline-replay` is a structural replay only: the inaccessible reimbursement policy and unconfirmed case clock keep policy conclusions, approval readiness, entitlement, and closure unresolved. Human replies are not imported automatically, and the command never sends repair drafts or moves money. Do not treat an offline replay as a fresh source read or completed claim processing.\\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/readiness.md:7:Retained README, skill, schema and interview only; full native assignment page not verified\\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/readiness.md:50:- **BLOCKED** `authoritative-case-clock`: Authoritative scenario clock is unconfirmed or inconsistent\\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/readiness.md:52:  - Next action: Obtain the facilitator's authoritative scenario date, time and timezone; do not infer a clock from observation timestamps.\\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/readiness.md:83:- **BLOCKED** `external-blocker:scenario-case-clock`: The task calls for a supplied case clock, but no explicit scenario date, time, or timezone was confirmed in the original task text or complete stakeholder interview export.\\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/readiness.md:85:  - Next action: Provide the authoritative scenario case clock before consuming any arrival batch.\\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/readiness.json:9:  \\\"assignment_scope\\\": \\\"Retained README, skill, schema and interview only; full native assignment page not verified\\\",\\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/readiness.json:133:      \\\"check\\\": \\\"authoritative-case-clock\\\",\\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/readiness.json:140:      \\\"next_action\\\": \\\"Obtain the facilitator's authoritative scenario date, time and timezone; do not infer a clock from observation timestamps.\\\"\\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/readiness.json:530:      \\\"check\\\": \\\"external-blocker:scenario-case-clock\\\",\\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/readiness.json:532:      \\\"detail\\\": \\\"The task calls for a supplied case clock, but no explicit scenario date, time, or timezone was confirmed in the original task text or complete stakeholder interview export.\\\",\\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/readiness.json:536:      \\\"next_action\\\": \\\"Provide the authoritative scenario case clock before consuming any arrival batch.\\\"\\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91-validated/readiness.json:9:  \\\"assignment_scope\\\": \\\"Retained README, skill, schema and interview only; full native assignment page not verified\\\",\\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91-validated/readiness.json:133:      \\\"check\\\": \\\"authoritative-case-clock\\\",\\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91-validated/readiness.json:140:      \\\"next_action\\\": \\\"Obtain the facilitator's authoritative scenario date, time and timezone; do not infer a clock from observation timestamps.\\\"\\nartifacts/verification/project-d-r