{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T19:45:21.916Z","ordinal":523,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a13bd1-7420-72c0-963e-58742d1be7bf","turn_id":"01a13bf2-628b-75c2-a43b-f19b5878b298","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-99f39b07-a67a-4ae1-bcbd-af04271dab67","process_id":"64529","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","cat interviews/project-d-travel-expense-claim-20261013-2210.md; cat skills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md; rg --files --hidden -g '!.git/**' -g '!.venv/**' -g '!.entire/**' -g '!artifacts/runs/**' -g '!**/__pycache__/**' -g '!.pytest_cache/**'; cat src/travel_claim/integration.py; cat src/travel_claim/finance.py"],"cwd":"file:///home/maxg/travel-expense-claim","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat interviews/project-d-travel-expense-claim-20261013-2210.md","name":"project-d-travel-expense-claim-20261013-2210.md","path":"interviews/project-d-travel-expense-claim-20261013-2210.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat skills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":"skills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md"},{"type":"list_files","cmd":"rg --files --hidden -g '!.git/**' -g '!.venv/**' -g '!.entire/**' -g '!artifacts/runs/**' -g '!**/__pycache__/**' -g '!.pytest_cache/**'","path":null},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat src/travel_claim/integration.py","name":"integration.py","path":"src/travel_claim/integration.py"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat src/travel_claim/finance.py","name":"finance.py","path":"src/travel_claim/finance.py"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# Project D — Travel Expense Claim Interview\n\nParticipant: Max Gabel · Exported: 10/13/2026, 6:10:03 PM\n\n## Travel Administration Lead · Travel Administration Lead\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:13 PM\n\nHello, thank you for your time.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:13 PM\n\nI coordinate travel reimbursements at Alderbridge. Much of my time goes into checking evidence, chasing reviews, and finding out what Finance actually paid, especially when a claim changes. I would like help making the whole process repeatable. You can ask me about how we work, policy, the records we use, or the problems that keep coming back.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:14 PM\n\nWhat policies?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:14 PM\n\nWe follow policy POL-2026.2, which governs how expenses are reviewed and reimbursed. It outlines separate requirements for international permits and claims, specifies approval roles like the budget owner and supervisor, and sets limits on categories like lodging and meals. You can find all the details in the Travel reimbursement policy.\n\n- [Travel reimbursement policy](https://private-pecorino-70e.notion.site/REDACTED)\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:14 PM\n\nWhich part of the reimbursement workflow would you like to explore next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:14 PM\n\nAre those all the policies?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:14 PM\n\nYes, policy POL-2026.2 is our primary reimbursement guide for 2026. It covers all the rules regarding approvals, expense categories and limits. Are there any specific categories you had in mind?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:15 PM\n\nI want to know what happens when there are exceptions to the policies.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:15 PM\n\nWhen there are exceptions, like for late filings or specific amount limits, we need a Finance exception. This official exception is issued by Finance for a specific claim version to resolve a set issue, like late filing or an unapproved permit. However, it doesn't waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:15 PM\n\nWhen you say Finance, is that a department?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:15 PM\n\nYes, Finance refers to our financial department. They are responsible for issuing monetary tables like currency rates and spending caps, providing official exceptions for policy issues, and handling actual payment execution and reconciliation for claims.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nI want to make sure I understand this.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nI'm happy to go over\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nThe financial department holds the sole authority to issue official exceptions for policy discrepancies. on a specific claim version. They cannot waive a missing evidence such as receipts or proof of payment.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nThat is correct. They are responsible for issuing official exceptions for specific issues on a claim version, but they cannot waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nWhere are receipts or a proof of payment stored?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nReceipts are stored in the Receipt binder, while proof of payment, such as settled merchant transactions, is found in the Merchant payments tab of the Travel registers workbook.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nWhich part of the work would you like to explore next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:17 PM\n\nDo receipts ever get destroyed or lost?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:17 PM\n\nIf a receipt is lost, the employee must provide alternative evidence or an explanation, but since Finance cannot waive missing receipts, the claim will remain unresolved until the evidence is provided.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:17 PM\n\nIs the Travel registers workbook a physical workbook or online?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:17 PM\n\nThe Travel registers workbook is an online spreadsheet that we use to track merchant payments and other financial activities.\n\n- [Travel registers](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:17 PM\n\nWhich part of the workflow would you like to discuss next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:18 PM\n\nWhat are the financial activities?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:18 PM\n\nFinancial activities include the pending, failed, or settled outcomes of payment requests, as well as accepted commitments, adjustments, refunds, and cancellations. These are all tracked and owned by the Finance department.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:18 PM\n\nTell me more about cancellations.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:18 PM\n\nCancellations can target an entire trip or just a permit version independently of a claim. They must be initiated by the employee and confirmed by the supervisor, and these actions are tracked in the Travel cancellations workbook. If there were paid costs or Finance commitments, Finance will need to issue a specific disposition and resolve the money separately.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nHow would they resolve the disposition?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nFinance will issue a specific disposition bound to the cancellation ID, which confirms the reimbursement eligibility and provides a new allowed amount and reason for the affected costs.\n\n- [Travel cancellations](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nIs there a limit to the allowed amount?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nYes, limits apply to specific categories. Lodging and meals are limited by daily or nightly caps set by Finance, based on the destination and date, which are then multiplied by the documented duration. Transport and conference expenses are not subject to these caps.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nHow is the lodging and meals determined? Like what pricing metrics?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nThe limits for lodging and meals are determined by daily or nightly caps set by Finance, based on your destination, expense currency, and the payment date. You can see these metrics in the Caps tab of the Travel registers workbook.\n\n- [Travel registers workbook](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:20 PM\n\nWhich part of the workflow would you like to discuss next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:20 PM\n\nHow do incomplete claims affect independent work?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:20 PM\n\nIncomplete claims are held while the missing facts are addressed. You can continue processing independent claims separately while others are held, as long as the business impact is made clear.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:20 PM\n\nWhen you say made clear, what types of data do you mean?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:20 PM\n\nWe need to identify the exact claim version, specify which facts are missing, name the owner responsible for supplying them, and outline the next action to resolve the issue.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nWhat actions do you have to choose from to resolve the issue?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nThe available actions include requesting missing evidence from the employee, seeking an official exception from Finance for specific issues, or holding the claim until Finance confirms the resolution or provides the missing definitions.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nOn average, how long does it take Finance to confirm resolution or provide the missing definitions?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nI don't have a set average for Finance response times. Their replies come in batches, and the time it takes depends on the volume and complexity of the request.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nWhen was the most recent time a Finance needed to confirm resolution that you can remember?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nI don't track specific dates for those resolutions in my head. Our Finance replies are delivered in versioned batches, and we process the needed resolutions as they arrive based on the specific claims and costs.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nHow many people are in a batch?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nThe batch size isn't fixed; it depends on the number of claims, requests, or reviewer replies being processed by Finance or the relevant budget owner at that time.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nHow are batches organized? For example, could they be organized by a time slot or with a certain amount of people inside?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nBatches aren't organized by fixed time slots or a specific number of people. They are versioned delivery packets supplied by the trainer based on the number of claims, requests, and reviewer replies processed and ready at that moment.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nHow are they assigned to a trainer?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nI don't assign claims to a trainer. The replies you see come from versioned batches provided by Finance or other appropriate reviewers based on the business workflow.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nHow many trainers are there?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nI don't have information about trainers. My work focuses on coordinating with the Finance department, budget owners, supervisors, and employees to process travel claims.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nWhat are the boundaries for trainers, meaning what can and can't they do in this?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nI don't have information about trainers. My role is Travel Administration Lead, and the replies I receive come from Finance, budget owners, supervisors, and directors within the established business workflow.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nTell me about the boundaries of Finance.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nFinance owns setting currency rates, managing spending caps, and issuing official policy exceptions. They also execute payments and resolve any monetary issues or cancellations, but they cannot waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nTell me about the boundaries of budget owners.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nBudget owners have the authority to approve, return, or reject a claim based on the complete department ledger. They assess funding availability and make discretionary decisions, which I receive in supplied reviewer replies.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nTell me about a discretionary decision.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nA discretionary decision is when the budget owner evaluates the department ledger and funding availability to decide whether to approve, return, or reject a claim. These judgments come directly from the budget owner's assessment and arrive in supplied reviewer replies.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nTell me about the boundaries of supervisors.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nSupervisors evaluate the business purpose of the trip, client commitment, schedule coverage, and permit consistency before providing their review reply. They also confirm travel cancellations initiated by the trip employee.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:25 PM\n\nTell me about the boundaries of directors.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:25 PM\n\nDirectors provide an additional layer of authorization for high-spend situations, typically when the reviewed claim entitlement or permit estimate exceeds EUR 1,000.00. They evaluate the business necessity, exceptions, and alternatives, and their decisions arrive in supplied reply batches.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nWhich work to revalidate after material corrections is the norm?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nThe policy requires a full or justified recheck of all affected dependencies, including calculations and approvals, when material changes are made. Even if the total amount remains the same, any change in evidence or facts invalidates prior readiness, so a fresh review is required.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nWhat are the financial completion conditions?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nFinancial completion requires that current approvals match the reviewed entitlement, net confirmed payments equal the authorized amount, no issues remain, and all required Finance resolutions have been received.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:27 PM\n\nWho owns the entitlement?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:27 PM\n\nI calculate the reviewed entitlement based on policy, evidence, and spending caps, but the budget owner owns the discretionary decision to fund or approve the specific claim amount.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:27 PM\n\nWhat is the delivery scope that is accept? After inspecting the actual result.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:27 PM\n\nThe accepted delivery scope is confirmed when the current approvals and reviewed entitlement agree with the net confirmed payment, and all required Finance resolutions have been received with no remaining issues.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nWhen you say issues, and what are the constraints for the repair work?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nIssues refer to unresolved problems like missing receipts, incomplete payment proof, late filings, or mismatched data. For repair work, constraints involve organizing the missing evidence into usable local tasks, retaining the subject and revision, identifying the responsible owner, and ensuring corrections go through required reviews.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nHow do you organize the repair work in partial response constraints?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nYou can organize repair work either by per-claim packages or by grouping all missing-evidence items by the specific person responsible for supplying them. The key constraint is to retain each item's subject, revision, missing fact, and owner for tracking.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nWhat's the best way to adopt these constraints before they guide the work?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nYou can choose between per-claim packages or grouping items by the person responsible, provided you clearly track the subject, revision, missing fact, and owner for every single item.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:29 PM\n\nWhich one of those is the most difficult to maintain?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:29 PM\n\nBoth approaches have trade-offs; per-claim packages require less cross-referencing but result in more packages, whereas grouping by the person reduces the number of units but requires item-level matching and careful partial completion tracking.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:30 PM\n\nCan cases remain unresolved when the facts require it?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:30 PM\n\nYes, cases can be placed on hold for missing facts or Finance resolutions, but they cannot be closed or considered complete until all required evidence and decisions are obtained.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:30 PM\n\nWhat type of report will affect the work, reason, responsible person, and evidence needed to resume?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:30 PM\n\nYou can use any format, such as a per-claim package or a grouped task list, as long as it consistently retains the specific claim version, the missing evidence or fact, the responsible owner, and the next action required to resume.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nWhat happens if inaccessible required sources must be erased with the lead facilitator rather than otherwise unknown?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nAs the Travel Administration Lead, I cannot invent or bypass required sources. If a required document or definition is inaccessible and cannot be obtained, it remains an unresolved issue that I must escalate to the exercise operator for guidance.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nHow long does that process take?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nThere is no set timeframe for how long the exercise operator takes to resolve an escalation, as it depends on the nature of the issue in the specific case.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nHow do you communicate?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nI communicate through formal requests and notifications. These include the subject type, IDs, stable role requesters, and relevant source versions, and I wait for replies from the authorized reviewers and Finance.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:33 PM\n\nLet me summarize to make sure I understand: the system route work based on four distinct human authority profiles: supervisors, budget owners, directors, and Finance.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:33 PM\n\nThat is correct. I coordinate the process by submitting requests for these different authorities and waiting for their determinations and resolutions to ensure claims are processed accurately and policy checks are met.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:38 PM\n\nHello, thank you for talking with me.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:38 PM\n\nHello! I coordinate travel reimbursements at Alderbridge. Much of my time goes into checking evidence, chasing reviews, and finding out what Finance actually paid, especially when a claim changes. You can ask me about how we work, our policy, the records we use, or the problems that keep coming back.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:38 PM\n\nCan you give me a the ordinary claim life cycle?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:38 PM\n\nThe ordinary cycle begins when an employee pays for a travel cost and submits a claim. I review the claim against the trip permits, receipts, and merchant payments to calculate the reviewed entitlement. Then, I coordinate the necessary approvals based on the amount and policy, submit the request to Finance for transfer, and reconcile the payments until the case is closed.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:39 PM\n\nWhat specific matching keys do you use to connect the submitted expense claims to its corresponding trip permit?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:39 PM\n\nI connect claims to trip permits using the employee's identity, the exact trip ID, and the specific trip revision number to ensure everything matches the approved travel records.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:39 PM\n\nI connect claims to trip permits using the employee's identity, the exact trip ID, and the specific trip revision number to ensure everything matches the approved travel records.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:40 PM\n\nWhen you submit the request to Finance for transfer. what type of files or formats do you submit?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:40 PM\n\nI submit an identifiable request containing the employee or payee, the total authorized EUR amount, and references to all supporting evidence, required approvals, and funding commitments.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:40 PM\n\nAnd at what point of the ordinary claim life cycle were the funding commitments established?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:40 PM\n\nFunding commitments are established when Finance accepts the reimbursement request, confirming the obligation and reserving the funds for budget tracking.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:41 PM\n\nLet's discuss more about the process of cancellations when the original permit process is not fully reconstructed.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:41 PM\n\nWhen a cancellation occurs, the valid confirmation pauses payment readiness but does not erase the Finance commitment. If the original permit was lawful before arrangements, it remains lawful, and we record a specific cancellation issue rather than invalidating the permit.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:42 PM\n\nWhen you say lawful, are you referring to the travel reimbursement policy?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:42 PM\n\nA permit is considered lawful when all required administrative, budget, and supervisor approvals are obtained and recorded prior to the first commitment date, as required by our travel reimbursement policy.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:42 PM\n\nWhen is the first commitment date usually started from the ordinary claim life cycle beginning?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:42 PM\n\nThe first commitment date is the date the employee makes the first arrangement or pays for a travel cost, such as booking a flight. This date is strictly based on the employee's actions and must occur after the permit is approved for international travel.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:43 PM\n\nWhat if the employee is not traveling internationally?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:43 PM\n\nFor domestic travel, the permit requirement is skipped, meaning there is no permit approval process or first commitment date check needed before travel arrangements can be made.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:43 PM\n\nHow does that affect the overall process, those two different types?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:43 PM\n\nThe main difference is the permit stage. For international trips, you must obtain all necessary approvals before any travel arrangements are made. For domestic travel, that entire permit process is skipped, and you proceed directly to reviewing paid costs and receipts. Did you want to explore the specific approval requirements for international permits?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:44 PM\n\nTell me more about that.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:44 PM\n\nFor international permits, I verify administrative completeness, then obtain reviews from the budget owner and supervisor. If the estimated cost is over one thousand euros, a director must also approve the permit before any travel arrangements are made.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:44 PM\n\nTell me more about the payment reconciliation process.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:44 PM\n\nI match Finance outcomes against the authorized obligation for each claim. I calculate net paid by taking confirmed transfers minus any refunds, and compare that to the authorized amount to find the remaining balance or identify any overpayments requiring resolution.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:45 PM\n\nWhat type of errors can you encounter when doing this process?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:45 PM\n\nCommon errors include missing receipts or payment proof, conflicting data like mismatched amounts or currencies, late filings, and unrecognized transactions that require Finance to resolve.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:45 PM\n\nWhen Finance resolves it, do they give you a piece of data so you can keep filling out your report?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:45 PM\n\nYes, Finance provides formal records like eligibility exceptions or resolution events that include the covered issues, authorized amounts, and specific reason codes for the claim version.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:45 PM\n\nIs there ever a case where Finance can't resolve it and it becomes unresolved?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:45 PM\n\nYes, if a required piece of evidence, such as a receipt or proof of payment, is persistently missing or a policy definition is unavailable, Finance cannot issue a resolution, and the item remains unresolved until the correct data is provided.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:46 PM\n\nIs there a time constraint to that?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:46 PM\n\nThere is no fixed timeframe. The case simply remains on hold until the required facts or policy definitions are successfully supplied.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:46 PM\n\nIs the trip the same cost as getting a permit?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:46 PM\n\nNo, the permit process itself does not have a cost; it is an administrative permission phase. The cost refers to the actual travel expenses for transportation, lodging, and meals that the employee pays and later submits for reimbursement after the trip.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:46 PM\n\nWhat are the business sources?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:46 PM\n\nOur business sources include the travel reimbursement policy, trip and permit records, expense claim forms paired with their receipts, and Finance activity logs for transfers and obligations.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:47 PM\n\nGoing back to the unresolved work, who gets the handoff results?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:47 PM\n\nI coordinate with the exercise operator for policy definition gaps and with Finance for monetary exceptions, ensuring all data is resolved before any claims can move forward.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:47 PM\n\nWhat are the five native source locations?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:47 PM\n\nThe five sources are the Travel reimbursement policy, the Initial claim binder, the Claim updates binder, the Receipt binder, and the Travel registers workbook.\n\n- [Travel reimbursement policy](https://private-pecorino-70e.notion.site/REDACTED)\n- [Initial claim binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/13sRj6s_kMeP1hsYGstWWmfkb6SCN1YOS/view)\n- [Claim updates binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/REDACTED/view)\n- [Receipt binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/REDACTED/view)\n- [Travel registers workbook](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:47 PM\n\nThe five sources are the Travel reimbursement policy, the Initial claim binder, the Claim updates binder, the Receipt binder, and the Travel registers workbook.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:48 PM\n\nWhen I hear the phrase \"business data is not bundled in a starter,\" what does that mean?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:48 PM\n\nIt means that the specific claim records, receipts, and transaction data are not preloaded into your environment. Instead, you must retrieve them directly from the provided external source locations as you work through each specific case.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:48 PM\n\nThat's it. Just to clarify, that might be things like receipts?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:48 PM\n\nYes, exactly. Items like specific receipts, detailed expense claims, and Finance transaction logs are accessed directly from the official external registries during your case review.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:49 PM\n\nTo make sure I have understanding with the skill you're requesting, that it must not fabricate or apply, make professional approval recommendations, send real requests, book travel, or move money.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:49 PM\n\nThat is exactly correct. The skill must process and organize data but does not possess discretionary decision-making authority or the ability to execute tasks like payments or bookings.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:50 PM\n\nAnd to understand the travel expense claim whole process, I want to summarize with you to make sure I understand. First, claim or change received, then gather and validate evidence. Then apply business rules, then a human decision for payment authority stands with people, then reconcile and close for the normal process.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:50 PM\n\nThat is precisely correct. Every claim involves receiving the submission, validating all evidence and calculations, applying the policy rules, awaiting the necessary human approvals, and finally reconciling the payments for closure.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:51 PM\n\nIs there anything else we haven't covered that you think is important?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:51 PM\n\nWe have covered the main workflow stages. Which specific part of the work would you like to explore next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:51 PM\n\nWhat part of the workflow becomes the most complicated among batches rather than working with just individual case by case?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:51 PM\n\nReconciling multiple batches becomes complicated when tracking Finance outcomes, such as partial payments or late transfers, across various batches and different versions of a claim.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:51 PM\n\nIs there a limit to how many batches you can handle at one time?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:51 PM\n\nThere is no fixed limit on the number of batches I can process at once. The main challenge is carefully matching transaction IDs and amounts across all historical records and versions.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:52 PM\n\nIs there ever a different type of historical record that needs to be imported?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:52 PM\n\nYes, we access several types of historical records, including previous claim versions, original receipt cards, past approval decisions, and historical Finance events like prior payments or adjustments.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:53 PM\n\nAt what point does the approval and payment authority not stay with the people?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:53 PM\n\nAuthority for financial payments, settlements, and eligibility exceptions always rests with Finance, as they are the sole authority for monetary transfers and resolutions.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:54 PM\n\nWhat happens when Finance has their own expense travel claims?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:54 PM\n\nAll employees, including those in Finance, follow the exact same reimbursement policy and workflow. Finance personnel still need reviews from budget owners, supervisors, and directors for their claims, depending on the amount and travel type.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:54 PM\n\nIs Finance allowed to handle their own files and cases?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:54 PM\n\nTo maintain impartiality, Finance personnel cannot approve their own claims; they must still go through the required budget owner, supervisor, and director reviews based on the amount.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:54 PM\n\nDoes that rule apply with every other person, including the budget owner, supervisor, and director?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:54 PM\n\nYes, the rule applies universally; no individual can approve their own travel claim, regardless of their role or authority level within the company.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:55 PM\n\nIs there a limit to how many travel claims can be made per person?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:55 PM\n\nThere is no limit on the number of travel claims a person can make; each claim is processed individually based on the specific trip, expenses, and required approvals.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:56 PM\n\nIs inflation accounted for for the specific types of reimbursements?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:56 PM\n\nReimbursement caps for categories like lodging and meals are defined periodically by Finance, taking specific costs into account as set in the annual policy.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:59 PM\n\nHello.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:59 PM\n\nHello! Which part of the reimbursement workflow would you like to explore next? Hello. Since we've discussed how our processes work and the roles involved, which specific part of the workflow would you like to explore next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:00 PM\n\nI want to discuss more about the re-entry lifecycle in regard to an employee resubmits a correction that changes a claim. How do you structurally invalidate the old record? while preserving its history?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:00 PM\n\nWhen a correction is submitted, it receives a new version number while the old version is retained in the history. The material changes structurally invalidate the prior reviews and approvals, requiring the claim to go through the required approval process again based on the new facts. You can see how we track these in the Initial claim binder and the Claim updates binder.\n\n- [Initial claim binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/13sRj6s_kMeP1hsYGstWWmfkb6SCN1YOS/view)\n- [Claim updates binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/REDACTED/view)\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:01 PM\n\nFor permit cancellation lifecycle. Without an associated expense claim. What specific document or log entry serves as verification?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:01 PM\n\nFor a permit cancellation without a claim, the verification is a confirmed cancellation record in the Travel cancellations tab of the Travel registers workbook. This record shows the initiation by the employee and confirmation by their supervisor.\n\n- [Travel registers](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:02 PM\n\nIf a supervisor approves a business's purpose but the budget owner rejects the claim due to department funding shortages. How will this be handled? And who becomes the next owner?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:02 PM\n\nWhen a claim is rejected by the budget owner due to funding, the claim is closed without payment, and the specific non-payment reason is recorded. Since it is a rejection, there is no next owner; the process concludes unless the employee chooses to submit a correction later.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:02 PM\n\nWhen you say the process concludes, does that mean there is no reimbursement?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:02 PM\n\nThat is correct. A rejection by the budget owner means the claim is formally closed, and no reimbursement will be paid for that specific submission, with the non-payment reason clearly documented.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:03 PM\n\nSo, I want to clarify, that's not a payment execution failure, that's more of a resolution?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:03 PM\n\nExactly. A budget rejection is a funding decision regarding entitlement, not a payment execution failure. It is documented as a rejection with its specific reason, separate from any Finance transfer issues.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:03 PM\n\nSo, in the case of a payment execution failure, what types of codes or labels does Finance use?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:03 PM\n\nFinance provides specific outcome labels such as \"failed,\" \"pending,\" or \"cancelled\" in the Finance activity log. These indicate the status of the monetary transfer rather than a decision on the claim's entitlement.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:03 PM\n\nWhat's the difference between those three? Are they interchangeable?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:03 PM\n\nThey are not interchangeable. \"Failed\" indicates an attempted transfer was unsuccessful, \"pending\" means the transfer is awaiting completion, and \"cancelled\" means the proposed payment was formally revoked before or after being initiated.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:04 PM\n\nSo the data is held between Google Sheets workbook and PDFs, or are there more operational types of data?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:04 PM\n\nWe rely on a combination of sources for operational data. This includes the Travel reimbursement policy on Notion, the Initial claim and Claim updates PDFs, the Receipt binder, and the Travel registers Google Sheets workbook.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:05 PM\n\nSo, there's no contradiction between those sources?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:05 PM\n\nThe operational sources are designed to be complementary and consistent. Each serves a different purpose in the workflow, such as policy definitions or payment records, and together they provide a complete case record.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:05 PM\n\nDoes that ever lead to partial reviewer or Finance with replies with outdated revisions?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:05 PM\n\nYes, when a reply comes with an outdated revision, it is rejected as not current authorization. We only accept responses that match the most recent claim revision and specific subject ID.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:05 PM\n\nHow often is that encountered?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:05 PM\n\nIt varies depending on when the reviewer or Finance processes the request, but I do not track the specific frequency, as my focus is on verifying each individual case.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:06 PM\n\nTell me about a situation on how an agent should handle when Finance replies from an old claim version after an employee already submitted a correct version.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:06 PM\n\nWhen Finance replies for an outdated version, we reject that response since it isn't current authorization. We retain that record in the history but do not apply it to the new claim, simply waiting for the reply that matches the correct claim revision.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:06 PM\n\nSo, the newer source takes legal and operational precedence?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:06 PM\n\nIt matches the specific version of the claim or permit. A newer version supersedes an older version on the same subject, but every decision must match the correct subject and revision to be structurally valid.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:07 PM\n\nWhen you say valid, can that also mean single evidence can be missing and be marked as resolved?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:07 PM\n\nNo, core evidence such as a receipt or settled merchant payment cannot be marked as resolved if it is missing. Those are structural requirements under the policy, and the claim must be held until the required evidence or an explicit Finance exception is provided.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:09 PM\n\nTo make sure I understand this, I want to summarize: an incoming batch component either there's a decision/reply input or a new claim correction, and if it's a decision/reply input, it's checking the version is current, whereas a new claim correction increments revisions and wipes downstream approvals.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:09 PM\n\nThat is correct. Incoming batches contain either reviewer decisions or claim corrections; decisions must match the current revision, while corrections increment revisions and necessitate re-evaluation of subsequent approvals.\n---\nname: travel-expense-claim\ndescription: Prepare traceable Alderbridge travel claim reviews, independent trip and permit work, repair drafts, and financial reconciliation from freshly retrieved native sources and authorized batch decisions. Never approve, invent evidence, send requests, book travel, or move money.\n---\n\n# Alderbridge Travel Expense Claim Skill\n\n## Inputs\n\n- A new run ID and the scenario's supplied case clock.\n- The five native source locations listed below, retrieved afresh on every new run.\n- The authorized arrival batch and its boundary/version, supplied by the exercise operator.\n- Any prior retained snapshot only when performing an explicitly labeled offline replay; this never substitutes for fresh reads on a new run.\n- Human reviewer, employee, and Finance responses only when present in supplied records.\n\nNever infer an approval, exception, source value, reply, or payment from a missing record.\n\n## Invocation\n\nInstall as described in the repository [README](../../README.md). Capture sources for a new run with:\n\n```bash\ntravel-claim capture-sources <run-id> artifacts/runs/<run-id> --case-clock '<scenario ISO timestamp>'\n```\n\nInspect the manifest status and verify retained bytes before processing a batch:\n\n```bash\ntravel-claim verify-sources artifacts/runs/<run-id>\ntravel-claim parse-retained artifacts/runs/<run-id>\n```\n\nSource-only acquisition does not consume a batch. Batch processing must preserve supplied arrival boundaries and use the public [`snapshot.schema.json`](../../snapshot.schema.json). Current foundation helpers are documented in [`travel_claim.sources`](../../src/travel_claim/sources.py), [`travel_claim.parsing`](../../src/travel_claim/parsing.py), [`travel_claim.workflow`](../../src/travel_claim/workflow.py), [`travel_claim.snapshots`](../../src/travel_claim/snapshots.py), and [`travel_claim.outputs`](../../src/travel_claim/outputs.py).\n\n`parse-retained` hash-verifies the run before transcribing the PDFs and workbook into page- and row-referenced records. The extracted source text and workbook values are evidence only. If the case clock or policy source is unavailable, leave it unresolved and do not consume policy-dependent decisions.\n\nStructural workflow helpers preserve every claim, trip and permit revision; identify whether a supplied decision references a found historical or latest source revision without applying its outcome; deduplicate repeated event IDs and report payload conflicts; and track independent trip/permit cancellation states. They do not calculate policy results. Repair items can be updated with new owner, evidence, reason, action, and subject revision while preserving prior updates. Revision advances reopen the item.\n\n## Native sources\n\n1. [Travel reimbursement policy — POL-2026.2](https://private-pecorino-70e.notion.site/REDACTED)\n2. [Initial claim binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/13sRj6s_kMeP1hsYGstWWmfkb6SCN1YOS/view)\n3. [Claim updates binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/REDACTED/view)\n4. [Receipt binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/REDACTED/view)\n5. [Travel registers workbook](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n\nRetain complete relevant bytes actually accessed. A response code or URL alone does not establish content access. Record partial and unavailable scopes separately. Never silently reuse a previous run's bytes in a new run.\n\n## Processing and authority boundaries\n\n1. Bind every fact and decision to its source, subject, and revision.\n2. Hold only claims or dependent work affected by missing/conflicting facts. Continue independent valid work. Each unresolved item retains subject type and exact ID, revision, missing/conflicting fact, responsible owner, source reference, and next action.\n3. Preserve every claim revision. After a material correction, use the corrected revision and revalidate affected evidence, calculations, trip/permit consistency, approvals, and Finance authorization. Preserve unrelated evidence only where it remains valid. Retain historical commitments, transfers, and refunds; do not use stale approvals as current.\n4. Keep trip cancellation and permit cancellation as independent processes, including processes without claims. Cancellation does not itself erase entitlement or Finance obligations. Record Finance disposition and monetary resolution separately when required.\n5. Use the owner-grouped local repair queue. Keep each item individually traceable. A partial response may resolve only the item(s) explicitly matched and supported by retained source evidence; unanswered, insufficient, or conflicting items stay open. Draft locally; never send requests.\n6. Preserve immutable Finance event identifiers. Reconcile only confirmed transfers and refunds. Do not duplicate events or obligations on replay.\n7. The provisional financial closure choice is to require current evidence and approvals, agreement between reviewed entitlement and authorized obligation, net confirmed payment equal to the authorized amount, required Finance resolutions, and no blocking issue. After the first actual processing result, pause for the operator to inspect reconciliation and unresolved cases and confirm final completion conditions and delivery scope.\n\nPeople retain business approval, exception, and payment authority. This Skill prepares work, validates supplied decisions, and records effects; it does not make discretionary approval recommendations, create replies, issue Finance exceptions, book travel, or move funds.\n\n## Outputs\n\n- `artifacts/runs/<run-id>/sources.json` and retained source bytes.\n- One immutable schema-valid `batches/<batch-id>.json` per consumed batch, with relative source and predecessor paths plus SHA-256 hashes.\n- `claims.csv` with exactly `claim_id,revision,trip_id,status,allowed_cents,paid_cents,balance_cents,next_owner,reason`.\n- Owner-grouped local repair queue with individual items and run/batch update history.\n- `report.md` describing completed work, obligations, unresolved items, owners, next actions, cancellations without claims, and source/run references.\n\nUnknown money is null in JSON and blank in CSV. Zero is a known amount. Never label incomplete work complete.\n\n## Errors, retries, and limitations\n\n- On source failure, retain the attempt URL, locator, UTC observation time, error, and missing scope. Hold only affected work and report its owner and resumption evidence.\n- On partial source access, retain usable pieces and explicitly list missing scope. Do not claim the source was fully read.\n- On invalid or conflicting batch data, preserve the input evidence, reject admission of unsupported effects, and create an owned issue; do not silently discard it.\n- Retry a failed fresh retrieval only by making another live request and recording the new observation. Do not overwrite a prior run's manifest, retained bytes, or sealed snapshot.\n- On replay, preserve obligation/event identity and money; detect conflicting content under an existing event ID.\n- Foundation implementation currently covers source capture/verification, retained PDF/workbook transcription, snapshot sealing/verification, the claims CSV writer, and local repair queue primitives. Scenario-state processing, policy/evidence decisions, approvals, Finance reconciliation, replay orchestration, and the complete operations report remain to be implemented and verified.\nREADME.md\nsnapshot.schema.json\n.codex/hooks.json\n.gitignore\nsrc/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\nsrc/travel_claim/cli.py\nsrc/travel_claim/outputs.py\nsrc/travel_claim/finance.py\nsrc/travel_claim/workflow.py\nsrc/travel_claim/parsing.py\nsrc/travel_claim/integration.py\nsrc/travel_claim/sources.py\nsrc/travel_claim/readiness.py\nsrc/travel_claim/__init__.py\nsrc/travel_claim/snapshots.py\nsrc/travel_claim/follow_up.py\nsrc/main.py\ninterviews/project-d-travel-expense-claim-20261013-2210.md\nartifacts/verification/project-d-incremental-verification-20261014.md\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91-validated/readiness.json\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91-validated/readiness.md\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/readiness.json\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/readiness.md\npyproject.toml\nskills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md\ntests/test_validate_snapshot.py\ntests/test_follow_up.py\ntests/test_finance.py\ntests/test_readiness.py\ntests/test_project_d_foundation.py\ntests/test_offline_replay.py\ntests/test_integration.py\ntests/test_parsing.py\ntests/test_workflow_structure.py\n\"\"\"Arrival-ordered, policy-neutral integration of Project D records.\n\nThis module prepares schema-shaped batch state but never seals snapshots,\ninfers eligibility, applies review decisions, or authorizes obligations.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom .finance import reconcile_finance_events\nfrom .outputs import add_repair_item, new_repair_queue, update_repair_item\nfrom .workflow import (\n    build_revision_history,\n    match_decisions_to_subjects,\n    reduce_cancellation_activities,\n    row_values,\n)\n\n\n_REVALIDATION_AREAS = (\n    (\"expense-evidence\", \"recheck expense evidence against the corrected claim revision\", \"employee\"),\n    (\"calculations\", \"recalculate and verify amounts for the corrected claim revision\", \"Travel Administration Lead\"),\n    (\"trip-permit\", \"recheck trip and permit identity and revision consistency\", \"Travel Administration Lead\"),\n    (\"approvals\", \"obtain current-revision decisions; prior decisions remain historical only\", \"Travel Administration Lead\"),\n    (\"finance-authorization\", \"revalidate Finance authorization for the corrected claim revision\", \"Finance\"),\n)\n\n\ndef _page_values(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {field.get(\"label\", \"\").strip(): field.get(\"value\") for field in record.get(\"fields\", [])}\n\n\ndef _page_batch(record: dict[str, Any]) -> int | None:\n    value = _page_values(record).get(\"Arrival batch\")\n    return _as_batch(value)\n\n\ndef _as_batch(value: Any) -> int | None:\n    if isinstance(value, bool) or value is None:\n        return None\n    try:\n        number = int(value)\n    except (ValueError, TypeError, OverflowError):\n        return None\n    return number if number > 0 and float(value) == number else None\n\n\ndef _ref(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: record.get(key) for key in (\"source_id\", \"source_sha256\", \"locator\")}\n\n\ndef _ref_text(reference: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    return f\"{reference.get('source_id')}@{reference.get('source_sha256')}#{reference.get('locator')}\"\n\n\ndef _stamp(value: Any) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Project an explicitly UTC source field into the schema's date-time form.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(value, str) or not value:\n        return None\n    if value.endswith(\"Z\") or \"+\" in value[10:] or \"-\" in value[10:]:\n        return value\n    return f\"{value}Z\"\n\n\ndef _delta(parsed: dict[str, Any], arrival_batch: int) -> dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]]:\n    records = parsed.get(\"records\", {})\n    selected = {\n        \"claim_revisions\": [row for row in records.get(\"claim_revisions\", []) if _page_batch(row) == arrival_batch],\n        \"decisions\": [row for row in records.get(\"decisions\", []) if _as_batch(row_values(row).get(\"Arrival batch\")) == arrival_batch],\n        \"finance_events\": [row for row in records.get(\"finance_events\", []) if _as_batch(row_values(row).get(\"Arrival batch\")) == arrival_batch],\n        \"cancellation_activities\": [row for row in records.get(\"cancellation_activities\", []) if _as_batch(row_values(row).get(\"Arrival batch\")) == arrival_batch],\n    }\n    selected[\"claim_revisions\"].sort(key=lambda row: (row.get(\"page\", 0), _ref(row).get(\"locator\") or \"\"))\n    for kind in (\"decisions\", \"finance_events\", \"cancellation_activities\"):\n        selected[kind].sort(key=lambda row: (row.get(\"row\", 0), _ref(row).get(\"locator\") or \"\"))\n    return selected\n\n\ndef _digest(value: Any) -> str:\n    payload = json.dumps(value, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"), default=str).encode(\"utf-8\")\n    return hashlib.sha256(payload).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef _domain_seed() -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\n        \"processed_batches\": [],\n        \"batch_input_hashes\": {},\n        \"claim_records\": [],\n        \"decision_records\": [],\n        \"finance_records\": [],\n        \"cancellation_records\": [],\n        \"revision_history\": None,\n        \"decision_history\": [],\n        \"finance_reconciliations\": {},\n        \"authorized_obligations\": {},\n        \"source_classifications\": {},\n        \"cancellation_state\": {},\n        \"material_corrections\": [],\n        \"repair_queue\": new_repair_queue(),\n        \"policy_clock_blockers\": [],\n        \"structural_blockers\": [],\n        \"projection_issues\": [],\n    }\n\n\ndef _issue_from_item(item: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\n        \"record_id\": item[\"item_id\"],\n        \"reason\": item[\"missing_or_return_reason\"],\n        \"owner\": item[\"owner\"],\n        \"resolution_needed\": item[\"next_action\"],\n        \"subject_type\": item[\"subject_type\"],\n        \"subject_id\": item[\"subject_id\"],\n        \"revision\": item[\"revision\"],\n        \"source_refs\": item[\"source_refs\"],\n        \"run_id\": item[\"run_id\"],\n        \"batch_id\": item[\"batch_id\"],\n    }\n\n\ndef _open_issue_for_subject(\n    queue: dict[str, Any], *, item_id: str, subject_type: str, subject_id: str,\n    revision: int, refs: list[str], reason: str, owner: str, next_action: str,\n    run_id: str, batch_id: str,\n) -> None:\n    if item_id not in queue[\"items\"]:\n        add_repair_item(\n            queue, item_id=item_id, subject_type=subject_type, subject_id=subject_id,\n            revision=revision, source_refs=refs, missing_or_return_reason=reason,\n            owner=owner, next_action=next_action, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n        )\n\n\ndef _sync_finance_repairs(domain: dict[str, Any], reconciliations: dict[str, Any], *, run_id: str, batch_id: str) -> None:\n    queue = domain[\"repair_queue\"]\n    for claim_id, result in reconciliations.items():\n        for issue in result[\"repair_issues\"]:\n            item_id = f\"finance:{issue['record_id']}\"\n            if item_id in queue[\"items\"]:\n                continue\n            refs = [_ref_text(ref) for ref in issue.get(\"source_refs\", []) if isinstance(ref, dict)]\n            _open_issue_for_subject(\n                queue, item_id=item_id, subject_type=\"claim\", subject_id=claim_id,\n                revision=result[\"claim_revision\"], refs=refs,\n                reason=issue.get(\"missing_or_return_reason\", issue.get(\"reason\", \"Finance evidence unresolved\")),\n                owner=issue[\"owner\"],\n                next_action=issue.get(\"next_action\", \"Finance to resolve the identified item\"),\n                run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n            )\n\n\ndef _subject_claim_revisions(history: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, dict[str, Any]]:\n    return history.get(\"claim\", {})\n\n\ndef _material_correction_tasks(\n    domain: dict[str, Any], *, history: dict[str, Any], run_id: str, batch_id: str,\n    previous_revisions: dict[str, int],\n) -> None:\n    queue = domain[\"repair_queue\"]\n    for claim_id, claim in _subject_claim_revisions(history).items():\n        revision = claim[\"current_revision\"]\n        old_revision = previous_revisions.get(claim_id)\n        if old_revision is None or revision <= old_revision:\n            continue\n        current = next(row for row in reversed(claim[\"revisions\"]) if row[\"revision\"] == revision)\n        prior = [row for row in claim[\"revisions\"] if row[\"revision\"] == old_revision]\n        refs = [_ref_text(row[\"source_ref\"]) for row in prior + [current]]\n        old_decisions = [\n            decision for decision in domain[\"decision_history\"]\n            if decision.get(\"subject_type\") == \"claim\" and decision.get(\"subject_id\") == claim_id\n            and decision.get(\"revision\") == old_revision\n        ]\n        refs.extend(_ref_text(row[\"decision_source_ref\"]) for row in old_decisions)\n        affected_finance = [row for row in domain[\"finance_records\"] if row_values(row).get(\"Claim reference\") == claim_id]\n        refs.extend(_ref_text(_ref(row)) for row in affected_finance)\n        refs = list(dict.fromkeys(refs))\n        invalidated = {\n            \"claim_id\": claim_id,\n            \"from_revision\": old_revision,\n            \"to_revision\": revision,\n            \"invalidated_decision_ids\": [row.get(\"decision_id\") for row in old_decisions if row.get(\"decision_id\")],\n            \"preserved_finance_event_ids\": [row_values(row).get(\"Activity reference\") for row in affected_finance if row_values(row).get(\"Activity reference\")],\n            \"revalidate\": [area for area, _, _ in _REVALIDATION_AREAS],\n            \"source_refs\": [deepcopy(row[\"source_ref\"]) for row in prior + [current]],\n            \"arrival_batch\": batch_id,\n        }\n        domain[\"material_corrections\"].append(invalidated)\n        for area, next_action, owner_role in _REVALIDATION_AREAS:\n            if owner_role == \"employee\":\n                owner = str(current[\"record\"].get(\"employee\") or _page_values(current[\"record\"]).get(\"Employee\") or \"Employee\")\n            elif owner_role == \"Finance\":\n                finance_owners = [row_values(row).get(\"Finance officer\") for row in affected_finance]\n                owner = str(next((value for value in reversed(finance_owners) if value), \"Finance\"))\n            else:\n                owner = owner_role\n            item_id = f\"correction:{claim_id}:r{revision}:{area}\"\n            _open_issue_for_subject(\n                queue, item_id=item_id, subject_type=\"claim\", subject_id=claim_id,\n                revision=revision, refs=refs,\n                reason=f\"Material correction from revision {old_revision} to {revision} requires dependency revalidation: {area}\",\n                owner=owner, next_action=next_action, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n            )\n\n\ndef _cancellation_rows(\n    domain: dict[str, Any], *, history: dict[str, Any], run_id: str, batch_id: str,\n) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    reduced = reduce_cancellation_activities(domain[\"cancellation_records\"])\n    domain[\"cancellation_state\"] = reduced\n    raw_by_id = {\n        row_values(record).get(\"Cancellation activity reference\"): record\n        for record in domain[\"cancellation_records\"]\n    }\n    claim_revisions = _subject_claim_revisions(history)\n    snapshot_rows = []\n    for cancellation_id, process in sorted(reduced[\"processes\"].items()):\n        target = process[\"target\"]\n        target_revision = target.get(\"revision\")\n        if (target.get(\"subject_type\") not in {\"trip\", \"permit\"} or not target.get(\"subject_id\")\n                or isinstance(target_revision, bool) or not isinstance(target_revision, int) or target_revision < 1):\n            domain[\"projection_issues\"].append({\n                \"record_id\": f\"cancellation-projection:{cancellation_id}\",\n                \"reason\": \"cancellation process lacks a supported target identity and revision; process remains in the integration sidecar\",\n                \"owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n                \"resolution_needed\": \"verify the cancellation target and revision in the native workbook\",\n            })\n            continue\n        record_order = process[\"activity_ids\"]\n        request_id = record_order[0]\n        request = raw_by_id[request_id]\n        request_values = row_values(request)\n        confirmation = next((raw_by_id[event_id] for event_id in record_order\n                             if row_values(raw_by_id[event_id]).get(\"Action\") == \"confirmed\"), None)\n        confirmation_values = row_values(confirmation) if confirmation else {}\n        trip_id = request_values.get(\"Trip reference\")\n        trip_revision = _as_batch(request_values.get(\"Trip revision\"))\n        permit_id = request_values.get(\"Permit reference\") if target[\"subject_type\"] == \"permit\" else None\n        permit_revision = request_values.get(\"Permit revision\") if target[\"subject_type\"] == \"permit\" else None\n        permit_revision = _as_batch(permit_revision) if permit_revision is not None else None\n        affected = []\n        for claim_id, claim in claim_revisions.items():\n            for claim_rev in claim[\"revisions\"]:\n                if target[\"subject_type\"] == \"trip\":\n                    matches = claim_rev.get(\"trip_id\") == target[\"subject_id\"] and claim_rev.get(\"trip_revision\") == target[\"revision\"]\n                else:\n                    trip_index = history.get(\"trip\", {}).get(str(claim_rev.get(\"trip_id\")), {})\n                    matches = any(\n                        trip_rev.get(\"revision\") == claim_rev.get(\"trip_revision\")\n                        and trip_rev.get(\"permit_id\") == target[\"subject_id\"]\n                        and trip_rev.get(\"permit_revision\") == target[\"revision\"]\n                        for trip_rev in trip_index.get(\"revisions\", [])\n                    )\n                if matches:\n                    affected.append(claim_id)\n                    break\n        affected = sorted(set(affected))\n        task_id = f\"cancellation-financial:{cancellation_id}\"\n        refs = [_ref_text(_ref(raw_by_id[event_id])) for event_id in record_order]\n        reason = \"Finance effect of the independent travel cancellation has not been resolved from an authorized Finance record\"\n        next_action = \"Finance to record whether this cancellation affects an accepted obligation, transfer, payment, or refund\"\n        queue = domain[\"repair_queue\"]\n        if task_id not in queue[\"items\"]:\n            _open_issue_for_subject(\n                queue, item_id=task_id,\n                subject_type=target[\"subject_type\"], subject_id=str(target[\"subject_id\"]),\n                revision=target_revision, refs=refs, reason=reason,\n                owner=\"Finance\", next_action=next_action, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n            )\n        else:\n            item = queue[\"items\"][task_id]\n            additions = list(dict.fromkeys(item[\"source_refs\"] + refs))\n            changes = {}\n            if additions != item[\"source_refs\"]:\n                changes[\"source_refs\"] = additions\n            if process[\"state\"] == \"confirmed\" and item[\"next_action\"] != next_action:\n                changes[\"next_action\"] = next_action\n            if changes:\n                update_repair_item(\n                    queue, item_id=task_id,\n                    update_id=f\"cancellation-update:{cancellation_id}:batch-{batch_id}\",\n                    run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id, **changes,\n                )\n        cancellation_issue = task_id\n        requested_at = _stamp(request_values.get(\"Activity time (UTC)\"))\n        if not trip_id or not trip_revision or not requested_at:\n            domain.setdefault(\"projection_issues\", []).append({\n                \"record_id\": f\"cancellation-projection:{cancellation_id}\",\n                \"reason\": \"cancellation source lacks the trip binding or requested time required by snapshot.schema.json; process remains in the integration sidecar\",\n                \"owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n                \"resolution_needed\": \"verify the cancellation subject and original UTC request time from the retained workbook\",\n            })\n            continue\n        snapshot_rows.append({\n            \"cancellation_id\": cancellation_id,\n            \"target_type\": target[\"subject_type\"],\n            \"trip_id\": str(trip_id),\n            \"trip_revision\": trip_revision,\n            \"permit_id\": str(permit_id) if permit_id else None,\n            \"permit_revision\": int(permit_revision) if permit_revision is not None else None,\n            \"status\": \"confirmed\" if process[\"state\"] == \"confirmed\" else \"requested\",\n            \"admitted_cancellation_event_ids\": list(dict.fromkeys(record_order)),\n            \"requested_at\": requested_at,\n            \"confirmed_at\": _stamp(confirmation_values.get(\"Activity time (UTC)\")) if confirmation else None,\n            \"effective_at\": _stamp(confirmation_values.get(\"Effective time (UTC)\")) if confirmation else None,\n            \"affected_claim_ids\": affected,\n            \"original_request_ids\": [],\n            \"financial_status\": \"unresolved\",\n            \"next_owner\": \"Finance\",\n            \"reason\": str(request_values.get(\"Business reason\") or \"Travel cancellation recorded; financial effect remains unresolved\"),\n            \"issue_record_ids\": [cancellation_issue],\n        })\n    return snapshot_rows\n\n\ndef _sync_decision_and_revision_issues(\n    domain: dict[str, Any], *, history: dict[str, Any], run_id: str, batch_id: str,\n) -> None:\n    queue = domain[\"repair_queue\"]\n    blockers = []\n    for conflict in history.get(\"issues\", {}).get(\"repeated_subject_revisions\", []):\n        kind = conflict[\"kind\"]\n        subject_id = conflict[\"subject_id\"]\n        revision = conflict[\"revision\"]\n        refs = [_ref_text(ref) for ref in conflict.get(\"occurrences\", [])]\n        item_id = f\"revision-conflict:{kind}:{subject_id}:r{revision}\"\n        _open_issue_for_subject(\n            queue, item_id=item_id, subject_type=kind, subject_id=subject_id,\n            revision=revision, refs=refs,\n            reason=f\"multiple retained source records use {kind} {subject_id} revision {revision}; their business content requires review\",\n            owner=\"Travel Administration Lead\", next_action=\"compare the source occurrences and establish the supported revision record\",\n            run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n        )\n    for malformed in history.get(\"issues\", {}).get(\"malformed_revision_records\", []):\n        blockers.append({\n            \"record_id\": f\"malformed-revision:{_digest(malformed)[:16]}\",\n            \"reason\": malformed[\"reason\"],\n            \"owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n            \"resolution_needed\": \"identify the subject and revision from the native source record\",\n            \"source_ref\": malformed.get(\"source_ref\"),\n        })\n    for decision in domain[\"decision_history\"]:\n        if decision[\"structural_match\"] in {\"revision_match_current\", \"revision_match_historical\"}:\n            continue\n        kind, subject_id, revision = decision.get(\"subject_type\"), decision.get(\"subject_id\"), decision.get(\"revision\")\n        decision_id = decision.get(\"decision_id\") or _digest(decision)[:16]\n        if kind in {\"claim\", \"trip\", \"permit\"} and isinstance(subject_id, str) and isinstance(revision, int) and revision > 0:\n            item_id = f\"decision-match:{decision_id}\"\n            _open_issue_for_subject(\n                queue, item_id=item_id, subject_type=kind, subject_id=subject_id,\n                revision=revision, refs=[_ref_text(decision[\"decision_source_ref\"])],\n                reason=f\"recorded decision {decision_id} does not structurally match an available {kind} revision ({decision['structural_match']})\",\n                owner=\"Travel Administration Lead\", next_action=\"resolve the decision subject or revision against the native review ledger\",\n                run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n            )\n        else:\n            blockers.append({\n                \"record_id\": f\"decision-match:{decision_id}\",\n                \"reason\": f\"recorded decision has no traceable supported subject/revision ({decision['structural_match']})\",\n                \"owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n                \"resolution_needed\": \"identify its subject and revision in the native review ledger\",\n                \"source_ref\": decision[\"decision_source_ref\"],\n            })\n    domain[\"structural_blockers\"] = blockers\n\n\ndef integrate_arrival_batch(\n    parsed: dict[str, Any],\n    *,\n    arrival_batch: int,\n    run_id: str,\n    batch_id: str,\n    source_binding: dict[str, str],\n    predecessor: dict[str, str] | None = None,\n    prior_result: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n    authorized_obligations: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] | None = None,\n    source_classifications: dict[str, str] | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Integrate exactly the next arrival batch into a schema-shaped projection.\n\n    The function retains raw subject/activity rows in a sidecar `domain`,\n    carries earlier state forward, and supports exact same-batch replay. It\n    does not consume or seal a scenario snapshot; callers must separately\n    verify access, case clock, policy, and authorities before doing that.\n    \"\"\"\n    if isinstance(arrival_batch, bool) or not isinstance(arrival_batch, int) or arrival_batch < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"arrival_batch must be a positive integer\")\n    if not run_id or not batch_id or not isinstance(source_binding, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"run_id, batch_id, and source_binding are required\")\n    delta = _delta(parsed, arrival_batch)\n    digest = _digest({\n        \"delta\": delta,\n        \"run_id\": run_id,\n        \"batch_id\": batch_id,\n        \"source_binding\": source_binding,\n        \"predecessor\": predecessor,\n        \"authorized_obligations\": authorized_obligations or {},\n        \"source_classifications\": source_classifications or {},\n        \"trip_reference_records\": parsed.get(\"records\", {}).get(\"trips\", []),\n        \"unresolved_issues\": parsed.get(\"unresolved_issues\", []),\n    })\n    previous_domain = deepcopy(prior_result[\"domain\"]) if prior_result else _domain_seed()\n    processed = previous_domain[\"processed_batches\"]\n    if processed and arrival_batch == processed[-1]:\n        if previous_domain[\"batch_input_hashes\"].get(str(arrival_batch)) == digest:\n            return deepcopy(prior_result)\n        raise ValueError(f\"conflicting replay for arrival batch {arrival_batch}\")\n    expected_batch = processed[-1] + 1 if processed else 1\n    if arrival_batch != expected_batch:\n        raise ValueError(f\"arrival batches must be integrated in explicit order; expected {expected_batch}, got {arrival_batch}\")\n    if prior_result is None and predecessor is not None:\n        raise ValueError(\"the first integrated batch must have a null predecessor\")\n    if prior_result is not None:\n        if prior_result.get(\"snapshot\", {}).get(\"run_id\") != run_id:\n            raise ValueError(\"prior integration state belongs to a different run\")\n        if predecessor is None:\n            raise ValueError(\"a later integrated batch must carry a predecessor binding\")\n\n    domain = previous_domain\n    if authorized_obligations:\n        domain[\"authorized_obligations\"].update(deepcopy(authorized_obligations))\n    if source_classifications:\n        domain[\"source_classifications\"].update(deepcopy(source_classifications))\n    previous_claim_revisions = {\n        subject_id: value[\"current_revision\"]\n        for subject_id, value in (domain.get(\"revision_history\") or {}).get(\"claim\", {}).items()\n    }\n    for name in (\"claim_revisions\", \"decisions\", \"finance_events\", \"cancellation_activities\"):\n        target_name = {\n            \"claim_revisions\": \"claim_records\", \"decisions\": \"decision_records\",\n            \"finance_events\": \"finance_records\", \"cancellation_activities\": \"cancellation_records\",\n        }[name]\n        domain[target_name].extend(deepcopy(delta[name]))\n    domain[\"processed_batches\"].append(arrival_batch)\n    domain[\"batch_input_hashes\"][str(arrival_batch)] = digest\n\n    history = build_revision_history({\n        \"records\": {\"claim_revisions\": domain[\"claim_records\"], \"trips\": parsed.get(\"records\", {}).get(\"trips\", [])}\n    })\n    domain[\"revision_history\"] = history\n    domain[\"decision_history\"] = match_decisions_to_subjects(domain[\"decision_records\"], history)\n    for decision, raw in zip(domain[\"decision_history\"], domain[\"decision_records\"]):\n        decision[\"arrival_batch\"] = row_values(raw).get(\"Arrival batch\")\n        decision[\"applied\"] = False\n    _sync_decision_and_revision_issues(domain, history=history, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id)\n    _material_correction_tasks(\n        domain, history=history, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n        previous_revisions=previous_claim_revisions,\n    )\n\n    current_claims = {}\n    for claim_id, record_set in history.get(\"claim\", {}).items():\n        current_revision = record_set[\"current_revision\"]\n        claim_revision = next(row for row in reversed(record_set[\"revisions\"]) if row[\"revision\"] == current_revision)\n        current_claims[claim_id] = claim_revision\n    finance_results = {}\n    for claim_id, claim_revision in current_claims.items():\n        record_set = history[\"claim\"][claim_id]\n        prior_finance = domain[\"finance_reconciliations\"].get(claim_id)\n        finance_results[claim_id] = reconcile_finance_events(\n            domain[\"finance_records\"], claim_id=claim_id,\n            current_revision=claim_revision[\"revision\"],\n            authorized_obligation=domain[\"authorized_obligations\"].get(claim_id),\n            revision_history=record_set[\"revisions\"],\n            previous_reconciliation=prior_finance,\n            source_classifications=domain[\"source_classifications\"],\n        )\n    domain[\"finance_reconciliations\"] = finance_results\n    _sync_finance_repairs(domain, finance_results, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id)\n\n    # Policy and case-clock blockers are copied from parser/source evidence and\n    # deliberately remain outside any fabricated claim/decision outcome.\n    blockers = []\n    for row in parsed.get(\"unresolved_issues\", []):\n        blocker = {\n            \"record_id\": row[\"record_id\"],\n            \"reason\": row.get(\"reason\", \"Unresolved source issue\"),\n            \"owner\": row.get(\"owner\", \"Exercise facilitator\"),\n            \"resolution_needed\": row.get(\"next_action\", \"Obtain the missing authoritative evidence\"),\n            \"subject_type\": row.get(\"subject_type\"),\n            \"subject_id\": row.get(\"subject_id\"),\n            \"affected_scope\": row.get(\"affected_scope\"),\n            \"evidence_needed\": row.get(\"evidence_needed\"),\n        }\n        blockers.append(blocker)\n    domain[\"policy_clock_blockers\"] = blockers\n\n    cancellation_rows = _cancellation_rows(domain, history=history, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id)\n    schema_issues = list(blockers) + list(domain.get(\"structural_blockers\", []))\n    schema_issues.extend(_issue_from_item(item) for item in domain[\"repair_queue\"][\"items\"].values() if item[\"status\"] == \"open\")\n    # Every cancellation issue reference must resolve in issues[].record_id.\n    known_issue_ids = {issue[\"record_id\"] for issue in schema_issues}\n    for cancellation in cancellation_rows:\n        cancellation[\"issue_record_ids\"] = [\n            issue_id for issue_id in cancellation[\"issue_record_ids\"] if issue_id in known_issue_ids\n        ]\n\n    snapshot_claims = []\n    projection_issues = []\n    for claim_id, revision_row in sorted(current_claims.items()):\n        revision = revision_row[\"revision\"]\n        record = revision_row[\"record\"]\n        values = _page_values(record)\n        trip_id = revision_row.get(\"trip_id\")\n        trip_revision = revision_row.get(\"trip_revision\")\n        if not trip_id or not trip_revision:\n            projection_issues.append({\n                \"record_id\": f\"snapshot-claim-link:{claim_id}:r{revision}\",\n                \"reason\": \"claim source lacks the trip identity or revision required by snapshot.schema.json; claim omitted from snapshot projection\",\n                \"owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n                \"resolution_needed\": \"obtain and verify the current claim-to-trip revision binding\",\n            })\n            continue\n        trip_record_set = history.get(\"trip\", {}).get(str(trip_id), {})\n        linked_trip = any(row[\"revision\"] == trip_revision for row in trip_record_set.get(\"revisions\", []))\n        if not linked_trip:\n            item_id = f\"trip-link:{claim_id}:r{revision}\"\n            _open_issue_for_subject(\n                domain[\"repair_queue\"], item_id=item_id, subject_type=\"claim\", subject_id=claim_id,\n                revision=revision, refs=[_ref_text(revision_row[\"source_ref\"])],\n                reason=f\"claim references trip {trip_id} revision {trip_revision}, which is not present in the retained trip register\",\n                owner=\"Travel Administration Lead\", next_action=\"verify the trip revision from an accessible native travel register\",\n                run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n            )\n            schema_issues.append(_issue_from_item(domain[\"repair_queue\"][\"items\"][item_id]))\n        matches = [row for row in domain[\"decision_history\"]\n                   if row.get(\"subject_type\") == \"claim\" and row.get(\"subject_id\") == claim_id\n                   and row.get(\"revision\") == revision and row.get(\"structural_match\") == \"revision_match_current\"]\n        finance = finance_results[claim_id]\n        snapshot_claims.append({\n            \"claim_id\": claim_id,\n            \"revision\": revision,\n            \"trip_id\": str(trip_id),\n            \"trip_revision\": trip_revision,\n            \"status\": \"pending\",\n            \"lines\": [],\n            \"allowed_cents\": None,\n            \"paid_cents\": finance[\"net_confirmed_cents\"],\n            \"balance_cents\": finance[\"balance_cents\"],\n            \"decision_ids\": list(dict.fromkeys(row[\"decision_id\"] for row in matches if row.get(\"decision_id\"))),\n            \"next_owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n            \"reason\": \"Structural integration only; reimbursement policy and current-revision compliance remain unresolved.\",\n        })\n\n    schema_issues.extend(projection_issues)\n    schema_issues.extend(domain.get(\"projection_issues\", []))\n    # Deduplicate by record_id while preserving issue order.\n    unique_issues = {}\n    for issue in schema_issues:\n        unique_issues.setdefault(issue[\"record_id\"], issue)\n    schema_issues = list(unique_issues.values())\n\n    finance_ids = []\n    unresolved_ids = set()\n    conflicting_ids = set()\n    for result in finance_results.values():\n        unresolved_ids.update(result[\"unresolved_event_ids\"])\n        conflicting_ids.update(issue[\"event_id\"] for issue in result[\"conflicting_events\"])\n        for event in result[\"event_history\"]:\n            event_id = event[\"event_id\"]\n            if (event_id and event_id not in unresolved_ids and event_id not in conflicting_ids\n                    and event[\"classification\"] not in {\"unresolved\", \"conflicting_event_id\", \"missing_event_id\"}):\n                finance_ids.append(event_id)\n    finance_ids = list(dict.fromkeys(event_id for event_id in finance_ids if event_id not in unresolved_ids | conflicting_ids))\n\n    snapshot = {\n        \"schema_version\": \"travel-claim-snapshot/2\",\n        \"run_id\": run_id,\n        \"batch_id\": batch_id,\n        \"predecessor\": deepcopy(predecessor),\n        \"source_binding\": deepcopy(source_binding),\n        \"claims\": snapshot_claims,\n        \"requests\": [],\n        \"travel_cancellations\": cancellation_rows,\n        \"admitted_event_ids\": finance_ids,\n        \"issues\": schema_issues,\n    }\n    domain[\"processed_batches\"] = list(domain[\"processed_batches\"])\n    return {\n        \"snapshot\": snapshot,\n        \"domain\": domain,\n        \"decision_history\": deepcopy(domain[\"decision_history\"]),\n        \"finance_reconciliations\": deepcopy(finance_results),\n        \"revision_history\": deepcopy(history),\n        \"repair_queue_by_owner\": _owner_view(domain[\"repair_queue\"]),\n        \"batch_delta_counts\": {key: len(value) for key, value in delta.items()},\n        \"input_sha256\": digest,\n    }\n\n\ndef _owner_view(queue: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]]:\n    grouped: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = {}\n    for item in queue[\"items\"].values():\n        grouped.setdefault(item[\"owner\"], []).append(item)\n    return {owner: sorted(items, key=lambda row: row[\"item_id\"]) for owner, items in sorted(grouped.items())}\n\"\"\"Source-traceable Finance reconciliation primitives.\n\nOnly explicit, source-classified settled and refund events affect confirmed\ncash. Finance obligations remain separate from caller-supplied authorized\nobligations. No policy entitlement or approval decision is made here.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\nfrom typing import Any\n\n\n_NATIVE_EVENT_CLASSES = {\n    \"accepted\": \"obligation_accepted\",\n    \"settled\": \"confirmed_payment\",\n    \"refund\": \"confirmed_refund\",\n    \"failed\": \"failed_transfer\",\n    \"retry_authorized\": \"retry_authorization\",\n    \"cancellation_requested\": \"finance_cancellation_requested\",\n    \"cancelled\": \"finance_cancelled\",\n    # These are retained as non-cash Finance records; their amount describes\n    # an obligation, not a payment.\n    \"adjustment\": \"finance_adjustment\",\n    \"resolution\": \"finance_resolution\",\n}\n\n\ndef _values(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: cell.get(\"value\") for key, cell in record.get(\"values\", {}).items()}\n\n\ndef _source_ref(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: record.get(key) for key in (\"source_id\", \"source_sha256\", \"locator\")}\n\n\ndef _cents(value: Any) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"Convert exact EUR decimal input to integer cents; reject rounding.\"\"\"\n    if value is None or isinstance(value, bool):\n        return None\n    try:\n        amount = Decimal(str(value))\n    except (InvalidOperation, ValueError):\n        return None\n    if not amount.is_finite():\n        return None\n    scaled = amount * 100\n    if scaled != scaled.to_integral_value() or scaled < 0:\n        return None\n    return int(scaled)\n\n\ndef _payload(values: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: values[key] for key in sorted(values) if key != \"Arrival batch\"}\n\n\ndef reconcile_finance_events(\n    events: list[dict[str, Any]],\n    *,\n    claim_id: str,\n    current_revision: int,\n    authorized_obligation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n    revision_history: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None,\n    previous_reconciliation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n    owner: str = \"Finance\",\n    source_classifications: dict[str, str] | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Reconcile source events for a claim without making policy decisions.\n\n    `authorized_obligation` is an independent, already-authorized input of\n    `{amount_cents, claim_revision, source_refs}`. This function neither\n    derives nor authorizes it. `source_classifications` may extend the native\n    workbook vocabulary when a retained source defines another event type;\n    unrecognized types otherwise remain unresolved.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not claim_id or isinstance(current_revision, bool) or not isinstance(current_revision, int) or current_revision < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"claim_id and a positive current_revision are required\")\n    if not owner:\n        raise ValueError(\"owner is required for reconciliation issues\")\n\n    classes = dict(_NATIVE_EVENT_CLASSES)\n    if source_classifications:\n        allowed_classes = {\n            \"confirmed_payment\", \"confirmed_refund\", \"pending_transfer\",\n            \"obligation_accepted\", \"failed_transfer\", \"retry_authorization\",\n            \"finance_cancellation_requested\", \"finance_cancelled\",\n            \"finance_adjustment\", \"finance_resolution\",\n        }\n        for event_type, classification in source_classifications.items():\n            if not isinstance(event_type, str) or classification not in allowed_classes:\n                raise ValueError(f\"unsupported source event classification: {event_type!r} -> {classification!r}\")\n            classes[event_type] = classification\n\n    by_id: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n    missing_id_records: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    for record in events:\n        event_id = _values(record).get(\"Activity reference\")\n        if not isinstance(event_id, str) or not event_id:\n            if _values(record).get(\"Claim reference\") == claim_id:\n                missing_id_records.append(record)\n        else:\n            by_id[event_id].append(record)\n\n    relevant_occurrences: list[tuple[str | None, dict[str, Any], dict[str, Any], bool]] = []\n    duplicate_events = []\n    conflicting_events = []\n    for event_id, occurrences in by_id.items():\n        relevant = [record for record in occurrences if _values(record).get(\"Claim reference\") == claim_id]\n        if not relevant:\n            continue\n        payloads = [_payload(_values(record)) for record in occurrences]\n        conflict = any(payload != payloads[0] for payload in payloads[1:])\n        for record in relevant:\n            relevant_occurrences.append((event_id, record, _values(record), conflict))\n        if conflict:\n            conflicting_events.append({\n                \"event_id\": event_id,\n                \"source_refs\": [_source_ref(record) for record in occurrences],\n                \"payloads\": payloads,\n            })\n        elif len(occurrences) > 1:\n            duplicate_events.append({\n                \"event_id\": event_id,\n                \"source_refs\": [_source_ref(record) for record in occurrences],\n                \"delivery_batches\": [_values(record).get(\"Arrival batch\") for record in occurrences],\n            })\n    relevant_occurrences.extend((None, record, _values(record), True) for record in missing_id_records)\n    relevant_occurrences.sort(key=lambda row: (\n        str(row[2].get(\"Arrival batch\") or \"\"),\n        int(row[1].get(\"row\") or 0),\n        row[0] or \"\",\n    ))\n\n    history = []\n    event_issue_by_id: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\n    typed = []\n    unresolved = []\n    for event_id, record, values, conflict in relevant_occurrences:\n        event_type = values.get(\"Activity type\")\n        classification = classes.get(event_type, \"unresolved\")\n        item = {\n            \"event_id\": event_id,\n            \"source_ref\": _source_ref(record),\n            \"source_record\": deepcopy(values),\n            \"event_type\": event_type,\n            \"classification\": (\n                \"conflicting_event_id\" if conflict and event_id else\n                \"missing_event_id\" if conflict else classification\n            ),\n            \"amount_cents\": _cents(values.get(\"Amount (EUR)\")),\n            \"obligation_cents\": _cents(values.get(\"Obligation (EUR)\")),\n            \"currency\": values.get(\"Currency\"),\n            \"original_activity_id\": values.get(\"Original activity reference\"),\n        }\n        history.append(item)\n        if conflict:\n            if event_id:\n                event_issue_by_id[event_id] = {\n                    \"record_id\": f\"finance-event-conflict:{event_id}\",\n                    \"event_id\": event_id,\n                    \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n                    \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n                    \"revision\": current_revision,\n                    \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"same Finance event ID has conflicting source content; none of its occurrences were counted\",\n                    \"source_refs\": [_source_ref(row) for row in by_id[event_id]],\n                    \"owner\": owner,\n                    \"next_action\": \"Finance to resolve the source record conflict\",\n                }\n            else:\n                event_issue_by_id[f\"missing:{record.get('locator')}\"] = {\n                    \"record_id\": f\"finance-event-missing-id:{record.get('row') or len(event_issue_by_id) + 1}\",\n                    \"event_id\": None,\n                    \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n                    \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n                    \"revision\": current_revision,\n                    \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"Finance event has no activity reference and cannot be safely deduplicated or counted\",\n                    \"source_refs\": [_source_ref(record)],\n                    \"owner\": owner,\n                    \"next_action\": \"Finance to identify this ledger event and provide its native activity reference\",\n                }\n            continue\n        if classification == \"unresolved\":\n            unresolved.append(item)\n            continue\n        if classification in {\"confirmed_payment\", \"confirmed_refund\"}:\n            if values.get(\"Currency\") != \"EUR\" or item[\"amount_cents\"] is None:\n                unresolved.append(item)\n                continue\n        typed.append(item)\n\n    payments = {item[\"event_id\"]: item for item in typed if item[\"classification\"] == \"confirmed_payment\"}\n    confirmed_refunds: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    refund_candidates = [item for item in typed if item[\"classification\"] == \"confirmed_refund\"]\n    refund_groups: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n    for item in refund_candidates:\n        original_id = item[\"original_activity_id\"]\n        original = payments.get(original_id) if isinstance(original_id, str) else None\n        if original is None or original.get(\"currency\") != item.get(\"currency\"):\n            unresolved.append(item)\n            continue\n        refund_groups[original_id].append(item)\n    for original_id, refunds in refund_groups.items():\n        original = payments[original_id]\n        refund_total = sum(item[\"amount_cents\"] for item in refunds)\n        if refund_total > original[\"amount_cents\"]:\n            unresolved.extend(refunds)\n            continue\n        confirmed_refunds.extend(refunds)\n\n    invalid_payments = [item for item in payments.values() if item[\"amount_cents\"] is None]\n    unresolved.extend(invalid_payments)\n    confirmed_payment_cents = sum(item[\"amount_cents\"] for item in payments.values() if item[\"amount_cents\"] is not None)\n    confirmed_refund_cents = sum(item[\"amount_cents\"] for item in confirmed_refunds)\n    net_confirmed_cents = confirmed_payment_cents - confirmed_refund_cents\n\n    issues = list(event_issue_by_id.values())\n    for number, item in enumerate(unresolved, 1):\n        issue_id = f\"finance-unresolved:{item['event_id'] or number}\"\n        issue = {\n            \"record_id\": issue_id,\n            \"event_id\": item[\"event_id\"],\n            \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n            \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n            \"revision\": current_revision,\n            \"source_refs\": [item[\"source_ref\"]],\n            \"missing_or_return_reason\": (\n                f\"Finance event {item['event_id']!r} is not sufficiently classified or linked for cash reconciliation\"\n            ),\n            \"owner\": owner,\n            \"next_action\": \"Finance to confirm event meaning, amount, currency, or refund link from the native ledger\",\n        }\n        issues.append(issue)\n    issues_by_owner: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n    for issue in issues:\n        issues_by_owner[issue[\"owner\"]].append(issue)\n    issues_by_owner = {key: sorted(value, key=lambda row: row[\"record_id\"]) for key, value in sorted(issues_by_owner.items())}\n\n    obligation = None\n    obligation_issue = None\n    if authorized_obligation is not None:\n        amount = authorized_obligation.get(\"amount_cents\")\n        obligation_revision = authorized_obligation.get(\"claim_revision\")\n        refs = authorized_obligation.get(\"source_refs\")\n        if (isinstance(amount, int) and not isinstance(amount, bool) and amount >= 0\n                and obligation_revision == current_revision and isinstance(refs, list)\n                and refs and all(isinstance(ref, str) and ref for ref in refs)):\n            obligation = {\"amount_cents\": amount, \"claim_revision\": obligation_revision, \"source_refs\": list(dict.fromkeys(refs))}\n        else:\n            obligation_issue = {\n                \"record_id\": f\"finance-obligation-invalid:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n                \"event_id\": None,\n                \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n                \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n                \"revision\": current_revision,\n                \"source_refs\": list(refs) if isinstance(refs, list) else [],\n                \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"authorized obligation is missing exact cents, current-revision match, or supporting source reference\",\n                \"owner\": owner,\n                \"next_action\": \"Finance to provide or confirm the authorized obligation for this claim revision\",\n            }\n    else:\n        obligation_issue = {\n            \"record_id\": f\"finance-obligation-missing:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n            \"event_id\": None,\n            \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n            \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n            \"revision\": current_revision,\n            \"source_refs\": [],\n            \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"no supported authorized obligation was supplied for this claim revision\",\n            \"owner\": owner,\n            \"next_action\": \"Finance to provide or confirm the authorized obligation for this claim revision\",\n        }\n    if obligation_issue is not None:\n        issues.append(obligation_issue)\n        issues_by_owner.setdefault(owner, []).append(obligation_issue)\n        issues_by_owner[owner].sort(key=lambda row: row[\"record_id\"])\n\n    has_unclassified_cash_event = any(item[\"classification\"] == \"unresolved\" for item in history)\n    event_set_complete = not unresolved and not conflicting_events and not missing_id_records and not has_unclassified_cash_event\n    balance = None\n    if obligation is not None and event_set_complete:\n        balance = obligation[\"amount_cents\"] - net_confirmed_cents\n\n    invalidated = None\n    if previous_reconciliation is not None:\n        previous_revision = previous_reconciliation.get(\"claim_revision\")\n        if previous_revision != current_revision:\n            invalidated = {\n                \"claim_revision\": previous_revision,\n                \"reason\": \"material revision change invalidates the prior reconciliation basis\",\n                \"prior_net_confirmed_cents\": previous_reconciliation.get(\"net_confirmed_cents\"),\n                \"prior_balance_cents\": previous_reconciliation.get(\"balance_cents\"),\n            }\n    return {\n        \"claim_id\": claim_id,\n        \"claim_revision\": current_revision,\n        \"revision_history\": deepcopy(revision_history or []),\n        \"event_history\": history,\n        \"event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in history if item[\"event_id\"] is not None],\n        \"duplicate_events\": duplicate_events,\n        \"conflicting_events\": conflicting_events,\n        \"confirmed_payment_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in payments.values() if item[\"amount_cents\"] is not None],\n        \"confirmed_refund_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in confirmed_refunds],\n        \"pending_transfer_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in typed if item[\"classification\"] == \"pending_transfer\"],\n        \"unresolved_event_ids\": list(dict.fromkeys(item[\"event_id\"] for item in unresolved if item[\"event_id\"] is not None)),\n        \"finance_obligation_events\": [item for item in history if item[\"classification\"] == \"obligation_accepted\"],\n        \"authorized_obligation\": obligation,\n        \"confirmed_payment_cents\": confirmed_payment_cents,\n        \"confirmed_refund_cents\": confirmed_refund_cents,\n        \"net_confirmed_cents\": net_confirmed_cents,\n        \"balance_cents\": balance,\n        \"inputs_complete\": balance is not None,\n        \"repair_issues\": issues,\n        \"repair_issues_by_owner\": issues_by_owner,\n        \"invalidated_previous_reconciliation\": invalidated,\n    }\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Project D — Travel Expense Claim Interview\n\nParticipant: Max Gabel · Exported: 10/13/2026, 6:10:03 PM\n\n## Travel Administration Lead · Travel Administration Lead\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:13 PM\n\nHello, thank you for your time.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:13 PM\n\nI coordinate travel reimbursements at Alderbridge. Much of my time goes into checking evidence, chasing reviews, and finding out what Finance actually paid, especially when a claim changes. I would like help making the whole process repeatable. You can ask me about how we work, policy, the records we use, or the problems that keep coming back.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:14 PM\n\nWhat policies?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:14 PM\n\nWe follow policy POL-2026.2, which governs how expenses are reviewed and reimbursed. It outlines separate requirements for international permits and claims, specifies approval roles like the budget owner and supervisor, and sets limits on categories like lodging and meals. You can find all the details in the Travel reimbursement policy.\n\n- [Travel reimbursement policy](https://private-pecorino-70e.notion.site/REDACTED)\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:14 PM\n\nWhich part of the reimbursement workflow would you like to explore next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:14 PM\n\nAre those all the policies?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:14 PM\n\nYes, policy POL-2026.2 is our primary reimbursement guide for 2026. It covers all the rules regarding approvals, expense categories and limits. Are there any specific categories you had in mind?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:15 PM\n\nI want to know what happens when there are exceptions to the policies.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:15 PM\n\nWhen there are exceptions, like for late filings or specific amount limits, we need a Finance exception. This official exception is issued by Finance for a specific claim version to resolve a set issue, like late filing or an unapproved permit. However, it doesn't waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:15 PM\n\nWhen you say Finance, is that a department?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:15 PM\n\nYes, Finance refers to our financial department. They are responsible for issuing monetary tables like currency rates and spending caps, providing official exceptions for policy issues, and handling actual payment execution and reconciliation for claims.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nI want to make sure I understand this.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nI'm happy to go over\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nThe financial department holds the sole authority to issue official exceptions for policy discrepancies. on a specific claim version. They cannot waive a missing evidence such as receipts or proof of payment.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nThat is correct. They are responsible for issuing official exceptions for specific issues on a claim version, but they cannot waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nWhere are receipts or a proof of payment stored?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nReceipts are stored in the Receipt binder, while proof of payment, such as settled merchant transactions, is found in the Merchant payments tab of the Travel registers workbook.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nWhich part of the work would you like to explore next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:17 PM\n\nDo receipts ever get destroyed or lost?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:17 PM\n\nIf a receipt is lost, the employee must provide alternative evidence or an explanation, but since Finance cannot waive missing receipts, the claim will remain unresolved until the evidence is provided.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:17 PM\n\nIs the Travel registers workbook a physical workbook or online?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:17 PM\n\nThe Travel registers workbook is an online spreadsheet that we use to track merchant payments and other financial activities.\n\n- [Travel registers](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:17 PM\n\nWhich part of the workflow would you like to discuss next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:18 PM\n\nWhat are the financial activities?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:18 PM\n\nFinancial activities include the pending, failed, or settled outcomes of payment requests, as well as accepted commitments, adjustments, refunds, and cancellations. These are all tracked and owned by the Finance department.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:18 PM\n\nTell me more about cancellations.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:18 PM\n\nCancellations can target an entire trip or just a permit version independently of a claim. They must be initiated by the employee and confirmed by the supervisor, and these actions are tracked in the Travel cancellations workbook. If there were paid costs or Finance commitments, Finance will need to issue a specific disposition and resolve the money separately.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nHow would they resolve the disposition?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nFinance will issue a specific disposition bound to the cancellation ID, which confirms the reimbursement eligibility and provides a new allowed amount and reason for the affected costs.\n\n- [Travel cancellations](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nIs there a limit to the allowed amount?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nYes, limits apply to specific categories. Lodging and meals are limited by daily or nightly caps set by Finance, based on the destination and date, which are then multiplied by the documented duration. Transport and conference expenses are not subject to these caps.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nHow is the lodging and meals determined? Like what pricing metrics?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nThe limits for lodging and meals are determined by daily or nightly caps set by Finance, based on your destination, expense currency, and the payment date. You can see these metrics in the Caps tab of the Travel registers workbook.\n\n- [Travel registers workbook](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:20 PM\n\nWhich part of the workflow would you like to discuss next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:20 PM\n\nHow do incomplete claims affect independent work?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:20 PM\n\nIncomplete claims are held while the missing facts are addressed. You can continue processing independent claims separately while others are held, as long as the business impact is made clear.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:20 PM\n\nWhen you say made clear, what types of data do you mean?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:20 PM\n\nWe need to identify the exact claim version, specify which facts are missing, name the owner responsible for supplying them, and outline the next action to resolve the issue.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nWhat actions do you have to choose from to resolve the issue?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nThe available actions include requesting missing evidence from the employee, seeking an official exception from Finance for specific issues, or holding the claim until Finance confirms the resolution or provides the missing definitions.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nOn average, how long does it take Finance to confirm resolution or provide the missing definitions?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nI don't have a set average for Finance response times. Their replies come in batches, and the time it takes depends on the volume and complexity of the request.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nWhen was the most recent time a Finance needed to confirm resolution that you can remember?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nI don't track specific dates for those resolutions in my head. Our Finance replies are delivered in versioned batches, and we process the needed resolutions as they arrive based on the specific claims and costs.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nHow many people are in a batch?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nThe batch size isn't fixed; it depends on the number of claims, requests, or reviewer replies being processed by Finance or the relevant budget owner at that time.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nHow are batches organized? For example, could they be organized by a time slot or with a certain amount of people inside?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nBatches aren't organized by fixed time slots or a specific number of people. They are versioned delivery packets supplied by the trainer based on the number of claims, requests, and reviewer replies processed and ready at that moment.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nHow are they assigned to a trainer?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nI don't assign claims to a trainer. The replies you see come from versioned batches provided by Finance or other appropriate reviewers based on the business workflow.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nHow many trainers are there?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nI don't have information about trainers. My work focuses on coordinating with the Finance department, budget owners, supervisors, and employees to process travel claims.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nWhat are the boundaries for trainers, meaning what can and can't they do in this?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nI don't have information about trainers. My role is Travel Administration Lead, and the replies I receive come from Finance, budget owners, supervisors, and directors within the established business workflow.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nTell me about the boundaries of Finance.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nFinance owns setting currency rates, managing spending caps, and issuing official policy exceptions. They also execute payments and resolve any monetary issues or cancellations, but they cannot waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nTell me about the boundaries of budget owners.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nBudget owners have the authority to approve, return, or reject a claim based on the complete department ledger. They assess funding availability and make discretionary decisions, which I receive in supplied reviewer replies.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nTell me about a discretionary decision.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nA discretionary decision is when the budget owner evaluates the department ledger and funding availability to decide whether to approve, return, or reject a claim. These judgments come directly from the budget owner's assessment and arrive in supplied reviewer replies.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nTell me about the boundaries of supervisors.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nSupervisors evaluate the business purpose of the trip, client commitment, schedule coverage, and permit consistency before providing their review reply. They also confirm travel cancellations initiated by the trip employee.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:25 PM\n\nTell me about the boundaries of directors.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:25 PM\n\nDirectors provide an additional layer of authorization for high-spend situations, typically when the reviewed claim entitlement or permit estimate exceeds EUR 1,000.00. They evaluate the business necessity, exceptions, and alternatives, and their decisions arrive in supplied reply batches.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nWhich work to revalidate after material corrections is the norm?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nThe policy requires a full or justified recheck of all affected dependencies, including calculations and approvals, when material changes are made. Even if the total amount remains the same, any change in evidence or facts invalidates prior readiness, so a fresh review is required.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nWhat are the financial completion conditions?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nFinancial completion requires that current approvals match the reviewed entitlement, net confirmed payments equal the authorized amount, no issues remain, and all required Finance resolutions have been received.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:27 PM\n\nWho owns the entitlement?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:27 PM\n\nI calculate the reviewed entitlement based on policy, evidence, and spending caps, but the budget owner owns the discretionary decision to fund or approve the specific claim amount.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:27 PM\n\nWhat is the delivery scope that is accept? After inspecting the actual result.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:27 PM\n\nThe accepted delivery scope is confirmed when the current approvals and reviewed entitlement agree with the net confirmed payment, and all required Finance resolutions have been received with no remaining issues.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nWhen you say issues, and what are the constraints for the repair work?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nIssues refer to unresolved problems like missing receipts, incomplete payment proof, late filings, or mismatched data. For repair work, constraints involve organizing the missing evidence into usable local tasks, retaining the subject and revision, identifying the responsible owner, and ensuring corrections go through required reviews.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nHow do you organize the repair work in partial response constraints?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nYou can organize repair work either by per-claim packages or by grouping all missing-evidence items by the specific person responsible for supplying them. The key constraint is to retain each item's subject, revision, missing fact, and owner for tracking.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nWhat's the best way to adopt these constraints before they guide the work?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nYou can choose between per-claim packages or grouping items by the person responsible, provided you clearly track the subject, revision, missing fact, and owner for every single item.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:29 PM\n\nWhich one of those is the most difficult to maintain?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:29 PM\n\nBoth approaches have trade-offs; per-claim packages require less cross-referencing but result in more packages, whereas grouping by the person reduces the number of units but requires item-level matching and careful partial completion tracking.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:30 PM\n\nCan cases remain unresolved when the facts require it?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:30 PM\n\nYes, cases can be placed on hold for missing facts or Finance resolutions, but they cannot be closed or considered complete until all required evidence and decisions are obtained.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:30 PM\n\nWhat type of report will affect the work, reason, responsible person, and evidence needed to resume?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:30 PM\n\nYou can use any format, such as a per-claim package or a grouped task list, as long as it consistently retains the specific claim version, the missing evidence or fact, the responsible owner, and the next action required to resume.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nWhat happens if inaccessible required sources must be erased with the lead facilitator rather than otherwise unknown?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nAs the Travel Administration Lead, I cannot invent or bypass required sources. If a required document or definition is inaccessible and cannot be obtained, it remains an unresolved issue that I must escalate to the exercise operator for guidance.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nHow long does that process take?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nThere is no set timeframe for how long the exercise operator takes to resolve an escalation, as it depends on the nature of the issue in the specific case.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nHow do you communicate?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nI communicate through formal requests and notifications. These include the subject type, IDs, stable role requesters, and relevant source versions, and I wait for replies from the authorized reviewers and Finance.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:33 PM\n\nLet me summarize to make sure I understand: the system route work based on four distinct human authority profiles: supervisors, budget owners, directors, and Finance.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:33 PM\n\nThat is correct. I coordinate the process by submitting requests for these different authorities and waiting for their determinations and resolutions to ensure claims are processed accurately and policy checks are met.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:38 PM\n\nHello, thank you for talking with me.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:38 PM\n\nHello! I coordinate travel reimbursements at Alderbridge. Much of my time goes into checking evidence, chasing reviews, and finding out what Finance actually paid, especially when a claim changes. You can ask me about how we work, our policy, the records we use, or the problems that keep coming back.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:38 PM\n\nCan you give me a the ordinary claim life cycle?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:38 PM\n\nThe ordinary cycle begins when an employee pays for a travel cost and submits a claim. I review the claim against the trip permits, receipts, and merchant payments to calculate the reviewed entitlement. Then, I coordinate the necessary approvals based on the amount and policy, submit the request to Finance for transfer, and reconcile the payments until the case is closed.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:39 PM\n\nWhat specific matching keys do you use to connect the submitted expense claims to its corresponding trip permit?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:39 PM\n\nI connect claims to trip permits using the employee's identity, the exact trip ID, and the specific trip revision number to ensure everything matches the approved travel records.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:39 PM\n\nI connect claims to trip permits using the employee's identity, the exact trip ID, and the specific trip revision number to ensure everything matches the approved travel records.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:40 PM\n\nWhen you submit the request to Finance for transfer. what type of files or formats do you submit?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:40 PM\n\nI submit an identifiable request containing the employee or payee, the total authorized EUR amount, and references to all supporting evidence, required approvals, and funding commitments.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:40 PM\n\nAnd at what point of the ordinary claim life cycle were the funding commitments established?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:40 PM\n\nFunding commitments are established when Finance accepts the reimbursement request, confirming the obligation and reserving the funds for budget tracking.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:41 PM\n\nLet's discuss more about the process of cancellations when the original permit process is not fully reconstructed.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:41 PM\n\nWhen a cancellation occurs, the valid confirmation pauses payment readiness but does not erase the Finance commitment. If the original permit was lawful before arrangements, it remains lawful, and we record a specific cancellation issue rather than invalidating the permit.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:42 PM\n\nWhen you say lawful, are you referring to the travel reimbursement policy?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:42 PM\n\nA permit is considered lawful when all required administrative, budget, and supervisor approvals are obtained and recorded prior to the first commitment date, as required by our travel reimbursement policy.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:42 PM\n\nWhen is the first commitment date usually started from the ordinary claim life cycle beginning?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:42 PM\n\nThe first commitment date is the date the employee makes the first arrangement or pays for a travel cost, such as booking a flight. This date is strictly based on the employee's actions and must occur after the permit is approved for international travel.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:43 PM\n\nWhat if the employee is not traveling internationally?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:43 PM\n\nFor domestic travel, the permit requirement is skipped, meaning there is no permit approval process or first commitment date check needed before travel arrangements can be made.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:43 PM\n\nHow does that affect the overall process, those two different types?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:43 PM\n\nThe main difference is the permit stage. For international trips, you must obtain all necessary approvals before any travel arrangements are made. For domestic travel, that entire permit process is skipped, and you proceed directly to reviewing paid costs and receipts. Did you want to explore the specific approval requirements for international permits?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:44 PM\n\nTell me more about that.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:44 PM\n\nFor international permits, I verify administrative completeness, then obtain reviews from the budget owner and supervisor. If the estimated cost is over one thousand euros, a director must also approve the permit before any travel arrangements are made.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:44 PM\n\nTell me more about the payment reconciliation process.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:44 PM\n\nI match Finance outcomes against the authorized obligation for each claim. I calculate net paid by taking confirmed transfers minus any refunds, and compare that to the authorized amount to find the remaining balance or identify any overpayments requiring resolution.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:45 PM\n\nWhat type of errors can you encounter when doing this process?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:45 PM\n\nCommon errors include missing receipts or payment proof, conflicting data like mismatched amounts or currencies, late filings, and unrecognized transactions that require Finance to resolve.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:45 PM\n\nWhen Finance resolves it, do they give you a piece of data so you can keep filling out your report?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:45 PM\n\nYes, Finance provides formal records like eligibility exceptions or resolution events that include the covered issues, authorized amounts, and specific reason codes for the claim version.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:45 PM\n\nIs there ever a case where Finance can't resolve it and it becomes unresolved?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:45 PM\n\nYes, if a required piece of evidence, such as a receipt or proof of payment, is persistently missing or a policy definition is unavailable, Finance cannot issue a resolution, and the item remains unresolved until the correct data is provided.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:46 PM\n\nIs there a time constraint to that?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:46 PM\n\nThere is no fixed timeframe. The case simply remains on hold until the required facts or policy definitions are successfully supplied.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:46 PM\n\nIs the trip the same cost as getting a permit?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:46 PM\n\nNo, the permit process itself does not have a cost; it is an administrative permission phase. The cost refers to the actual travel expenses for transportation, lodging, and meals that the employee pays and later submits for reimbursement after the trip.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:46 PM\n\nWhat are the business sources?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:46 PM\n\nOur business sources include the travel reimbursement policy, trip and permit records, expense claim forms paired with their receipts, and Finance activity logs for transfers and obligations.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:47 PM\n\nGoing back to the unresolved work, who gets the handoff results?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:47 PM\n\nI coordinate with the exercise operator for policy definition gaps and with Finance for monetary exceptions, ensuring all data is resolved before any claims can move forward.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:47 PM\n\nWhat are the five native source locations?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:47 PM\n\nThe five sources are the Travel reimbursement policy, the Initial claim binder, the Claim updates binder, the Receipt binder, and the Travel registers workbook.\n\n- [Travel reimbursement policy](https://private-pecorino-70e.notion.site/REDACTED)\n- [Initial claim binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/13sRj6s_kMeP1hsYGstWWmfkb6SCN1YOS/view)\n- [Claim updates binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/REDACTED/view)\n- [Receipt binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/REDACTED/view)\n- [Travel registers workbook](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:47 PM\n\nThe five sources are the Travel reimbursement policy, the Initial claim binder, the Claim updates binder, the Receipt binder, and the Travel registers workbook.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:48 PM\n\nWhen I hear the phrase \"business data is not bundled in a starter,\" what does that mean?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:48 PM\n\nIt means that the specific claim records, receipts, and transaction data are not preloaded into your environment. Instead, you must retrieve them directly from the provided external source locations as you work through each specific case.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:48 PM\n\nThat's it. Just to clarify, that might be things like receipts?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:48 PM\n\nYes, exactly. Items like specific receipts, detailed expense claims, and Finance transaction logs are accessed directly from the official external registries during your case review.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:49 PM\n\nTo make sure I have understanding with the skill you're requesting, that it must not fabricate or apply, make professional approval recommendations, send real requests, book travel, or move money.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:49 PM\n\nThat is exactly correct. The skill must process and organize data but does not possess discretionary decision-making authority or the ability to execute tasks like payments or bookings.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:50 PM\n\nAnd to understand the travel expense claim whole process, I want to summarize with you to make sure I understand. First, claim or change received, then gather and validate evidence. Then apply business rules, then a human decision for payment authority stands with people, then reconcile and close for the normal process.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:50 PM\n\nThat is precisely correct. Every claim involves receiving the submission, validating all evidence and calculations, applying the policy rules, awaiting the necessary human approvals, and finally reconciling the payments for closure.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:51 PM\n\nIs there anything else we haven't covered that you think is important?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:51 PM\n\nWe have covered the main workflow stages. Which specific part of the work would you like to explore next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:51 PM\n\nWhat part of the workflow becomes the most complicated among batches rather than working with just individual case by case?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:51 PM\n\nReconciling multiple batches becomes complicated when tracking Finance outcomes, such as partial payments or late transfers, across various batches and different versions of a claim.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:51 PM\n\nIs there a limit to how many batches you can handle at one time?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:51 PM\n\nThere is no fixed limit on the number of batches I can process at once. The main challenge is carefully matching transaction IDs and amounts across all historical records and versions.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:52 PM\n\nIs there ever a different type of historical record that needs to be imported?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:52 PM\n\nYes, we access several types of historical records, including previous claim versions, original receipt cards, past approval decisions, and historical Finance events like prior payments or adjustments.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:53 PM\n\nAt what point does the approval and payment authority not stay with the people?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:53 PM\n\nAuthority for financial payments, settlements, and eligibility exceptions always rests with Finance, as they are the sole authority for monetary transfers and resolutions.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:54 PM\n\nWhat happens when Finance has their own expense travel claims?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:54 PM\n\nAll employees, including those in Finance, follow the exact same reimbursement policy and workflow. Finance personnel still need reviews from budget owners, supervisors, and directors for their claims, depending on the amount and travel type.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:54 PM\n\nIs Finance allowed to handle their own files and cases?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:54 PM\n\nTo maintain impartiality, Finance personnel cannot approve their own claims; they must still go through the required budget owner, supervisor, and director reviews based on the amount.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:54 PM\n\nDoes that rule apply with every other person, including the budget owner, supervisor, and director?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:54 PM\n\nYes, the rule applies universally; no individual can approve their own travel claim, regardless of their role or authority level within the company.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:55 PM\n\nIs there a limit to how many travel claims can be made per person?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:55 PM\n\nThere is no limit on the number of travel claims a person can make; each claim is processed individually based on the specific trip, expenses, and required approvals.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:56 PM\n\nIs inflation accounted for for the specific types of reimbursements?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:56 PM\n\nReimbursement caps for categories like lodging and meals are defined periodically by Finance, taking specific costs into account as set in the annual policy.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:59 PM\n\nHello.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:59 PM\n\nHello! Which part of the reimbursement workflow would you like to explore next? Hello. Since we've discussed how our processes work and the roles involved, which specific part of the workflow would you like to explore next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:00 PM\n\nI want to discuss more about the re-entry lifecycle in regard to an employee resubmits a correction that changes a claim. How do you structurally invalidate the old record? while preserving its history?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:00 PM\n\nWhen a correction is submitted, it receives a new version number while the old version is retained in the history. The material changes structurally invalidate the prior reviews and approvals, requiring the claim to go through the required approval process again based on the new facts. You can see how we track these in the Initial claim binder and the Claim updates binder.\n\n- [Initial claim binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/13sRj6s_kMeP1hsYGstWWmfkb6SCN1YOS/view)\n- [Claim updates binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/REDACTED/view)\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:01 PM\n\nFor permit cancellation lifecycle. Without an associated expense claim. What specific document or log entry serves as verification?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:01 PM\n\nFor a permit cancellation without a claim, the verification is a confirmed cancellation record in the Travel cancellations tab of the Travel registers workbook. This record shows the initiation by the employee and confirmation by their supervisor.\n\n- [Travel registers](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:02 PM\n\nIf a supervisor approves a business's purpose but the budget owner rejects the claim due to department funding shortages. How will this be handled? And who becomes the next owner?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:02 PM\n\nWhen a claim is rejected by the budget owner due to funding, the claim is closed without payment, and the specific non-payment reason is recorded. Since it is a rejection, there is no next owner; the process concludes unless the employee chooses to submit a correction later.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:02 PM\n\nWhen you say the process concludes, does that mean there is no reimbursement?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:02 PM\n\nThat is correct. A rejection by the budget owner means the claim is formally closed, and no reimbursement will be paid for that specific submission, with the non-payment reason clearly documented.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:03 PM\n\nSo, I want to clarify, that's not a payment execution failure, that's more of a resolution?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:03 PM\n\nExactly. A budget rejection is a funding decision regarding entitlement, not a payment execution failure. It is documented as a rejection with its specific reason, separate from any Finance transfer issues.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:03 PM\n\nSo, in the case of a payment execution failure, what types of codes or labels does Finance use?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:03 PM\n\nFinance provides specific outcome labels such as \"failed,\" \"pending,\" or \"cancelled\" in the Finance activity log. These indicate the status of the monetary transfer rather than a decision on the claim's entitlement.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:03 PM\n\nWhat's the difference between those three? Are they interchangeable?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:03 PM\n\nThey are not interchangeable. \"Failed\" indicates an attempted transfer was unsuccessful, \"pending\" means the transfer is awaiting completion, and \"cancelled\" means the proposed payment was formally revoked before or after being initiated.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:04 PM\n\nSo the data is held between Google Sheets workbook and PDFs, or are there more operational types of data?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:04 PM\n\nWe rely on a combination of sources for operational data. This includes the Travel reimbursement policy on Notion, the Initial claim and Claim updates PDFs, the Receipt binder, and the Travel registers Google Sheets workbook.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:05 PM\n\nSo, there's no contradiction between those sources?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:05 PM\n\nThe operational sources are designed to be complementary and consistent. Each serves a different purpose in the workflow, such as policy definitions or payment records, and together they provide a complete case record.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:05 PM\n\nDoes that ever lead to partial reviewer or Finance with replies with outdated revisions?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:05 PM\n\nYes, when a reply comes with an outdated revision, it is rejected as not current authorization. We only accept responses that match the most recent claim revision and specific subject ID.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:05 PM\n\nHow often is that encountered?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:05 PM\n\nIt varies depending on when the reviewer or Finance processes the request, but I do not track the specific frequency, as my focus is on verifying each individual case.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:06 PM\n\nTell me about a situation on how an agent should handle when Finance replies from an old claim version after an employee already submitted a correct version.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:06 PM\n\nWhen Finance replies for an outdated version, we reject that response since it isn't current authorization. We retain that record in the history but do not apply it to the new claim, simply waiting for the reply that matches the correct claim revision.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:06 PM\n\nSo, the newer source takes legal and operational precedence?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:06 PM\n\nIt matches the specific version of the claim or permit. A newer version supersedes an older version on the same subject, but every decision must match the correct subject and revision to be structurally valid.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:07 PM\n\nWhen you say valid, can that also mean single evidence can be missing and be marked as resolved?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:07 PM\n\nNo, core evidence such as a receipt or settled merchant payment cannot be marked as resolved if it is missing. Those are structural requirements under the policy, and the claim must be held until the required evidence or an explicit Finance exception is provided.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 06:09 PM\n\nTo make sure I understand this, I want to summarize: an incoming batch component either there's a decision/reply input or a new claim correction, and if it's a decision/reply input, it's checking the version is current, whereas a new claim correction increments revisions and wipes downstream approvals.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 06:09 PM\n\nThat is correct. Incoming batches contain either reviewer decisions or claim corrections; decisions must match the current revision, while corrections increment revisions and necessitate re-evaluation of subsequent approvals.\n---\nname: travel-expense-claim\ndescription: Prepare traceable Alderbridge travel claim reviews, independent trip and permit work, repair drafts, and financial reconciliation from freshly retrieved native sources and authorized batch decisions. Never approve, invent evidence, send requests, book travel, or move money.\n---\n\n# Alderbridge Travel Expense Claim Skill\n\n## Inputs\n\n- A new run ID and the scenario's supplied case clock.\n- The five native source locations listed below, retrieved afresh on every new run.\n- The authorized arrival batch and its boundary/version, supplied by the exercise operator.\n- Any prior retained snapshot only when performing an explicitly labeled offline replay; this never substitutes for fresh reads on a new run.\n- Human reviewer, employee, and Finance responses only when present in supplied records.\n\nNever infer an approval, exception, source value, reply, or payment from a missing record.\n\n## Invocation\n\nInstall as described in the repository [README](../../README.md). Capture sources for a new run with:\n\n```bash\ntravel-claim capture-sources <run-id> artifacts/runs/<run-id> --case-clock '<scenario ISO timestamp>'\n```\n\nInspect the manifest status and verify retained bytes before processing a batch:\n\n```bash\ntravel-claim verify-sources artifacts/runs/<run-id>\ntravel-claim parse-retained artifacts/runs/<run-id>\n```\n\nSource-only acquisition does not consume a batch. Batch processing must preserve supplied arrival boundaries and use the public [`snapshot.schema.json`](../../snapshot.schema.json). Current foundation helpers are documented in [`travel_claim.sources`](../../src/travel_claim/sources.py), [`travel_claim.parsing`](../../src/travel_claim/parsing.py), [`travel_claim.workflow`](../../src/travel_claim/workflow.py), [`travel_claim.snapshots`](../../src/travel_claim/snapshots.py), and [`travel_claim.outputs`](../../src/travel_claim/outputs.py).\n\n`parse-retained` hash-verifies the run before transcribing the PDFs and workbook into page- and row-referenced records. The extracted source text and workbook values are evidence only. If the case clock or policy source is unavailable, leave it unresolved and do not consume policy-dependent decisions.\n\nStructural workflow helpers preserve every claim, trip and permit revision; identify whether a supplied decision references a found historical or latest source revision without applying its outcome; deduplicate repeated event IDs and report payload conflicts; and track independent trip/permit cancellation states. They do not calculate policy results. Repair items can be updated with new owner, evidence, reason, action, and subject revision while preserving prior updates. Revision advances reopen the item.\n\n## Native sources\n\n1. [Travel reimbursement policy — POL-2026.2](https://private-pecorino-70e.notion.site/REDACTED)\n2. [Initial claim binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/13sRj6s_kMeP1hsYGstWWmfkb6SCN1YOS/view)\n3. [Claim updates binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/REDACTED/view)\n4. [Receipt binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/REDACTED/view)\n5. [Travel registers workbook](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n\nRetain complete relevant bytes actually accessed. A response code or URL alone does not establish content access. Record partial and unavailable scopes separately. Never silently reuse a previous run's bytes in a new run.\n\n## Processing and authority boundaries\n\n1. Bind every fact and decision to its source, subject, and revision.\n2. Hold only claims or dependent work affected by missing/conflicting facts. Continue independent valid work. Each unresolved item retains subject type and exact ID, revision, missing/conflicting fact, responsible owner, source reference, and next action.\n3. Preserve every claim revision. After a material correction, use the corrected revision and revalidate affected evidence, calculations, trip/permit consistency, approvals, and Finance authorization. Preserve unrelated evidence only where it remains valid. Retain historical commitments, transfers, and refunds; do not use stale approvals as current.\n4. Keep trip cancellation and permit cancellation as independent processes, including processes without claims. Cancellation does not itself erase entitlement or Finance obligations. Record Finance disposition and monetary resolution separately when required.\n5. Use the owner-grouped local repair queue. Keep each item individually traceable. A partial response may resolve only the item(s) explicitly matched and supported by retained source evidence; unanswered, insufficient, or conflicting items stay open. Draft locally; never send requests.\n6. Preserve immutable Finance event identifiers. Reconcile only confirmed transfers and refunds. Do not duplicate events or obligations on replay.\n7. The provisional financial closure choice is to require current evidence and approvals, agreement between reviewed entitlement and authorized obligation, net confirmed payment equal to the authorized amount, required Finance resolutions, and no blocking issue. After the first actual processing result, pause for the operator to inspect reconciliation and unresolved cases and confirm final completion conditions and delivery scope.\n\nPeople retain business approval, exception, and payment authority. This Skill prepares work, validates supplied decisions, and records effects; it does not make discretionary approval recommendations, create replies, issue Finance exceptions, book travel, or move funds.\n\n## Outputs\n\n- `artifacts/runs/<run-id>/sources.json` and retained source bytes.\n- One immutable schema-valid `batches/<batch-id>.json` per consumed batch, with relative source and predecessor paths plus SHA-256 hashes.\n- `claims.csv` with exactly `claim_id,revision,trip_id,status,allowed_cents,paid_cents,balance_cents,next_owner,reason`.\n- Owner-grouped local repair queue with individual items and run/batch update history.\n- `report.md` describing completed work, obligations, unresolved items, owners, next actions, cancellations without claims, and source/run references.\n\nUnknown money is null in JSON and blank in CSV. Zero is a known amount. Never label incomplete work complete.\n\n## Errors, retries, and limitations\n\n- On source failure, retain the attempt URL, locator, UTC observation time, error, and missing scope. Hold only affected work and report its owner and resumption evidence.\n- On partial source access, retain usable pieces and explicitly list missing scope. Do not claim the source was fully read.\n- On invalid or conflicting batch data, preserve the input evidence, reject admission of unsupported effects, and create an owned issue; do not silently discard it.\n- Retry a failed fresh retrieval only by making another live request and recording the new observation. Do not overwrite a prior run's manifest, retained bytes, or sealed snapshot.\n- On replay, preserve obligation/event identity and money; detect conflicting content under an existing event ID.\n- Foundation implementation currently covers source capture/verification, retained PDF/workbook transcription, snapshot sealing/verification, the claims CSV writer, and local repair queue primitives. Scenario-state processing, policy/evidence decisions, approvals, Finance reconciliation, replay orchestration, and the complete operations report remain to be implemented and verified.\nREADME.md\nsnapshot.schema.json\n.codex/hooks.json\n.gitignore\nsrc/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\nsrc/travel_claim/cli.py\nsrc/travel_claim/outputs.py\nsrc/travel_claim/finance.py\nsrc/travel_claim/workflow.py\nsrc/travel_claim/parsing.py\nsrc/travel_claim/integration.py\nsrc/travel_claim/sources.py\nsrc/travel_claim/readiness.py\nsrc/travel_claim/__init__.py\nsrc/travel_claim/snapshots.py\nsrc/travel_claim/follow_up.py\nsrc/main.py\ninterviews/project-d-travel-expense-claim-20261013-2210.md\nartifacts/verification/project-d-incremental-verification-20261014.md\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91-validated/readiness.json\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91-validated/readiness.md\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/readiness.json\nartifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/readiness.md\npyproject.toml\nskills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md\ntests/test_validate_snapshot.py\ntests/test_follow_up.py\ntests/test_finance.py\ntests/test_readiness.py\ntests/test_project_d_foundation.py\ntests/test_offline_replay.py\ntests/test_integration.py\ntests/test_parsing.py\ntests/test_workflow_structure.py\n\"\"\"Arrival-ordered, policy-neutral integration of Project D records.\n\nThis module prepares schema-shaped batch state but never seals snapshots,\ninfers eligibility, applies review decisions, or authorizes obligations.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom .finance import reconcile_finance_events\nfrom .outputs import add_repair_item, new_repair_queue, update_repair_item\nfrom .workflow import (\n    build_revision_history,\n    match_decisions_to_subjects,\n    reduce_cancellation_activities,\n    row_values,\n)\n\n\n_REVALIDATION_AREAS = (\n    (\"expense-evidence\", \"recheck expense evidence against the corrected claim revision\", \"employee\"),\n    (\"calculations\", \"recalculate and verify amounts for the corrected claim revision\", \"Travel Administration Lead\"),\n    (\"trip-permit\", \"recheck trip and permit identity and revision consistency\", \"Travel Administration Lead\"),\n    (\"approvals\", \"obtain current-revision decisions; prior decisions remain historical only\", \"Travel Administration Lead\"),\n    (\"finance-authorization\", \"revalidate Finance authorization for the corrected claim revision\", \"Finance\"),\n)\n\n\ndef _page_values(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {field.get(\"label\", \"\").strip(): field.get(\"value\") for field in record.get(\"fields\", [])}\n\n\ndef _page_batch(record: dict[str, Any]) -> int | None:\n    value = _page_values(record).get(\"Arrival batch\")\n    return _as_batch(value)\n\n\ndef _as_batch(value: Any) -> int | None:\n    if isinstance(value, bool) or value is None:\n        return None\n    try:\n        number = int(value)\n    except (ValueError, TypeError, OverflowError):\n        return None\n    return number if number > 0 and float(value) == number else None\n\n\ndef _ref(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: record.get(key) for key in (\"source_id\", \"source_sha256\", \"locator\")}\n\n\ndef _ref_text(reference: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    return f\"{reference.get('source_id')}@{reference.get('source_sha256')}#{reference.get('locator')}\"\n\n\ndef _stamp(value: Any) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Project an explicitly UTC source field into the schema's date-time form.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(value, str) or not value:\n        return None\n    if value.endswith(\"Z\") or \"+\" in value[10:] or \"-\" in value[10:]:\n        return value\n    return f\"{value}Z\"\n\n\ndef _delta(parsed: dict[str, Any], arrival_batch: int) -> dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]]:\n    records = parsed.get(\"records\", {})\n    selected = {\n        \"claim_revisions\": [row for row in records.get(\"claim_revisions\", []) if _page_batch(row) == arrival_batch],\n        \"decisions\": [row for row in records.get(\"decisions\", []) if _as_batch(row_values(row).get(\"Arrival batch\")) == arrival_batch],\n        \"finance_events\": [row for row in records.get(\"finance_events\", []) if _as_batch(row_values(row).get(\"Arrival batch\")) == arrival_batch],\n        \"cancellation_activities\": [row for row in records.get(\"cancellation_activities\", []) if _as_batch(row_values(row).get(\"Arrival batch\")) == arrival_batch],\n    }\n    selected[\"claim_revisions\"].sort(key=lambda row: (row.get(\"page\", 0), _ref(row).get(\"locator\") or \"\"))\n    for kind in (\"decisions\", \"finance_events\", \"cancellation_activities\"):\n        selected[kind].sort(key=lambda row: (row.get(\"row\", 0), _ref(row).get(\"locator\") or \"\"))\n    return selected\n\n\ndef _digest(value: Any) -> str:\n    payload = json.dumps(value, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"), default=str).encode(\"utf-8\")\n    return hashlib.sha256(payload).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef _domain_seed() -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\n        \"processed_batches\": [],\n        \"batch_input_hashes\": {},\n        \"claim_records\": [],\n        \"decision_records\": [],\n        \"finance_records\": [],\n        \"cancellation_records\": [],\n        \"revision_history\": None,\n        \"decision_history\": [],\n        \"finance_reconciliations\": {},\n        \"authorized_obligations\": {},\n        \"source_classifications\": {},\n        \"cancellation_state\": {},\n        \"material_corrections\": [],\n        \"repair_queue\": new_repair_queue(),\n        \"policy_clock_blockers\": [],\n        \"structural_blockers\": [],\n        \"projection_issues\": [],\n    }\n\n\ndef _issue_from_item(item: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\n        \"record_id\": item[\"item_id\"],\n        \"reason\": item[\"missing_or_return_reason\"],\n        \"owner\": item[\"owner\"],\n        \"resolution_needed\": item[\"next_action\"],\n        \"subject_type\": item[\"subject_type\"],\n        \"subject_id\": item[\"subject_id\"],\n        \"revision\": item[\"revision\"],\n        \"source_refs\": item[\"source_refs\"],\n        \"run_id\": item[\"run_id\"],\n        \"batch_id\": item[\"batch_id\"],\n    }\n\n\ndef _open_issue_for_subject(\n    queue: dict[str, Any], *, item_id: str, subject_type: str, subject_id: str,\n    revision: int, refs: list[str], reason: str, owner: str, next_action: str,\n    run_id: str, batch_id: str,\n) -> None:\n    if item_id not in queue[\"items\"]:\n        add_repair_item(\n            queue, item_id=item_id, subject_type=subject_type, subject_id=subject_id,\n            revision=revision, source_refs=refs, missing_or_return_reason=reason,\n            owner=owner, next_action=next_action, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n        )\n\n\ndef _sync_finance_repairs(domain: dict[str, Any], reconciliations: dict[str, Any], *, run_id: str, batch_id: str) -> None:\n    queue = domain[\"repair_queue\"]\n    for claim_id, result in reconciliations.items():\n        for issue in result[\"repair_issues\"]:\n            item_id = f\"finance:{issue['record_id']}\"\n            if item_id in queue[\"items\"]:\n                continue\n            refs = [_ref_text(ref) for ref in issue.get(\"source_refs\", []) if isinstance(ref, dict)]\n            _open_issue_for_subject(\n                queue, item_id=item_id, subject_type=\"claim\", subject_id=claim_id,\n                revision=result[\"claim_revision\"], refs=refs,\n                reason=issue.get(\"missing_or_return_reason\", issue.get(\"reason\", \"Finance evidence unresolved\")),\n                owner=issue[\"owner\"],\n                next_action=issue.get(\"next_action\", \"Finance to resolve the identified item\"),\n                run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n            )\n\n\ndef _subject_claim_revisions(history: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, dict[str, Any]]:\n    return history.get(\"claim\", {})\n\n\ndef _material_correction_tasks(\n    domain: dict[str, Any], *, history: dict[str, Any], run_id: str, batch_id: str,\n    previous_revisions: dict[str, int],\n) -> None:\n    queue = domain[\"repair_queue\"]\n    for claim_id, claim in _subject_claim_revisions(history).items():\n        revision = claim[\"current_revision\"]\n        old_revision = previous_revisions.get(claim_id)\n        if old_revision is None or revision <= old_revision:\n            continue\n        current = next(row for row in reversed(claim[\"revisions\"]) if row[\"revision\"] == revision)\n        prior = [row for row in claim[\"revisions\"] if row[\"revision\"] == old_revision]\n        refs = [_ref_text(row[\"source_ref\"]) for row in prior + [current]]\n        old_decisions = [\n            decision for decision in domain[\"decision_history\"]\n            if decision.get(\"subject_type\") == \"claim\" and decision.get(\"subject_id\") == claim_id\n            and decision.get(\"revision\") == old_revision\n        ]\n        refs.extend(_ref_text(row[\"decision_source_ref\"]) for row in old_decisions)\n        affected_finance = [row for row in domain[\"finance_records\"] if row_values(row).get(\"Claim reference\") == claim_id]\n        refs.extend(_ref_text(_ref(row)) for row in affected_finance)\n        refs = list(dict.fromkeys(refs))\n        invalidated = {\n            \"claim_id\": claim_id,\n            \"from_revision\": old_revision,\n            \"to_revision\": revision,\n            \"invalidated_decision_ids\": [row.get(\"decision_id\") for row in old_decisions if row.get(\"decision_id\")],\n            \"preserved_finance_event_ids\": [row_values(row).get(\"Activity reference\") for row in affected_finance if row_values(row).get(\"Activity reference\")],\n            \"revalidate\": [area for area, _, _ in _REVALIDATION_AREAS],\n            \"source_refs\": [deepcopy(row[\"source_ref\"]) for row in prior + [current]],\n            \"arrival_batch\": batch_id,\n        }\n        domain[\"material_corrections\"].append(invalidated)\n        for area, next_action, owner_role in _REVALIDATION_AREAS:\n            if owner_role == \"employee\":\n                owner = str(current[\"record\"].get(\"employee\") or _page_values(current[\"record\"]).get(\"Employee\") or \"Employee\")\n            elif owner_role == \"Finance\":\n                finance_owners = [row_values(row).get(\"Finance officer\") for row in affected_finance]\n                owner = str(next((value for value in reversed(finance_owners) if value), \"Finance\"))\n            else:\n                owner = owner_role\n            item_id = f\"correction:{claim_id}:r{revision}:{area}\"\n            _open_issue_for_subject(\n                queue, item_id=item_id, subject_type=\"claim\", subject_id=claim_id,\n                revision=revision, refs=refs,\n                reason=f\"Material correction from revision {old_revision} to {revision} requires dependency revalidation: {area}\",\n                owner=owner, next_action=next_action, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n            )\n\n\ndef _cancellation_rows(\n    domain: dict[str, Any], *, history: dict[str, Any], run_id: str, batch_id: str,\n) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    reduced = reduce_cancellation_activities(domain[\"cancellation_records\"])\n    domain[\"cancellation_state\"] = reduced\n    raw_by_id = {\n        row_values(record).get(\"Cancellation activity reference\"): record\n        for record in domain[\"cancellation_records\"]\n    }\n    claim_revisions = _subject_claim_revisions(history)\n    snapshot_rows = []\n    for cancellation_id, process in sorted(reduced[\"processes\"].items()):\n        target = process[\"target\"]\n        target_revision = target.get(\"revision\")\n        if (target.get(\"subject_type\") not in {\"trip\", \"permit\"} or not target.get(\"subject_id\")\n                or isinstance(target_revision, bool) or not isinstance(target_revision, int) or target_revision < 1):\n            domain[\"projection_issues\"].append({\n                \"record_id\": f\"cancellation-projection:{cancellation_id}\",\n                \"reason\": \"cancellation process lacks a supported target identity and revision; process remains in the integration sidecar\",\n                \"owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n                \"resolution_needed\": \"verify the cancellation target and revision in the native workbook\",\n            })\n            continue\n        record_order = process[\"activity_ids\"]\n        request_id = record_order[0]\n        request = raw_by_id[request_id]\n        request_values = row_values(request)\n        confirmation = next((raw_by_id[event_id] for event_id in record_order\n                             if row_values(raw_by_id[event_id]).get(\"Action\") == \"confirmed\"), None)\n        confirmation_values = row_values(confirmation) if confirmation else {}\n        trip_id = request_values.get(\"Trip reference\")\n        trip_revision = _as_batch(request_values.get(\"Trip revision\"))\n        permit_id = request_values.get(\"Permit reference\") if target[\"subject_type\"] == \"permit\" else None\n        permit_revision = request_values.get(\"Permit revision\") if target[\"subject_type\"] == \"permit\" else None\n        permit_revision = _as_batch(permit_revision) if permit_revision is not None else None\n        affected = []\n        for claim_id, claim in claim_revisions.items():\n            for claim_rev in claim[\"revisions\"]:\n                if target[\"subject_type\"] == \"trip\":\n                    matches = claim_rev.get(\"trip_id\") == target[\"subject_id\"] and claim_rev.get(\"trip_revision\") == target[\"revision\"]\n                else:\n                    trip_index = history.get(\"trip\", {}).get(str(claim_rev.get(\"trip_id\")), {})\n                    matches = any(\n                        trip_rev.get(\"revision\") == claim_rev.get(\"trip_revision\")\n                        and trip_rev.get(\"permit_id\") == target[\"subject_id\"]\n                        and trip_rev.get(\"permit_revision\") == target[\"revision\"]\n                        for trip_rev in trip_index.get(\"revisions\", [])\n                    )\n                if matches:\n                    affected.append(claim_id)\n                    break\n        affected = sorted(set(affected))\n        task_id = f\"cancellation-financial:{cancellation_id}\"\n        refs = [_ref_text(_ref(raw_by_id[event_id])) for event_id in record_order]\n        reason = \"Finance effect of the independent travel cancellation has not been resolved from an authorized Finance record\"\n        next_action = \"Finance to record whether this cancellation affects an accepted obligation, transfer, payment, or refund\"\n        queue = domain[\"repair_queue\"]\n        if task_id not in queue[\"items\"]:\n            _open_issue_for_subject(\n                queue, item_id=task_id,\n                subject_type=target[\"subject_type\"], subject_id=str(target[\"subject_id\"]),\n                revision=target_revision, refs=refs, reason=reason,\n                owner=\"Finance\", next_action=next_action, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n            )\n        else:\n            item = queue[\"items\"][task_id]\n            additions = list(dict.fromkeys(item[\"source_refs\"] + refs))\n            changes = {}\n            if additions != item[\"source_refs\"]:\n                changes[\"source_refs\"] = additions\n            if process[\"state\"] == \"confirmed\" and item[\"next_action\"] != next_action:\n                changes[\"next_action\"] = next_action\n            if changes:\n                update_repair_item(\n                    queue, item_id=task_id,\n                    update_id=f\"cancellation-update:{cancellation_id}:batch-{batch_id}\",\n                    run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id, **changes,\n                )\n        cancellation_issue = task_id\n        requested_at = _stamp(request_values.get(\"Activity time (UTC)\"))\n        if not trip_id or not trip_revision or not requested_at:\n            domain.setdefault(\"projection_issues\", []).append({\n                \"record_id\": f\"cancellation-projection:{cancellation_id}\",\n                \"reason\": \"cancellation source lacks the trip binding or requested time required by snapshot.schema.json; process remains in the integration sidecar\",\n                \"owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n                \"resolution_needed\": \"verify the cancellation subject and original UTC request time from the retained workbook\",\n            })\n            continue\n        snapshot_rows.append({\n            \"cancellation_id\": cancellation_id,\n            \"target_type\": target[\"subject_type\"],\n            \"trip_id\": str(trip_id),\n            \"trip_revision\": trip_revision,\n            \"permit_id\": str(permit_id) if permit_id else None,\n            \"permit_revision\": int(permit_revision) if permit_revision is not None else None,\n            \"status\": \"confirmed\" if process[\"state\"] == \"confirmed\" else \"requested\",\n            \"admitted_cancellation_event_ids\": list(dict.fromkeys(record_order)),\n            \"requested_at\": requested_at,\n            \"confirmed_at\": _stamp(confirmation_values.get(\"Activity time (UTC)\")) if confirmation else None,\n            \"effective_at\": _stamp(confirmation_values.get(\"Effective time (UTC)\")) if confirmation else None,\n            \"affected_claim_ids\": affected,\n            \"original_request_ids\": [],\n            \"financial_status\": \"unresolved\",\n            \"next_owner\": \"Finance\",\n            \"reason\": str(request_values.get(\"Business reason\") or \"Travel cancellation recorded; financial effect remains unresolved\"),\n            \"issue_record_ids\": [cancellation_issue],\n        })\n    return snapshot_rows\n\n\ndef _sync_decision_and_revision_issues(\n    domain: dict[str, Any], *, history: dict[str, Any], run_id: str, batch_id: str,\n) -> None:\n    queue = domain[\"repair_queue\"]\n    blockers = []\n    for conflict in history.get(\"issues\", {}).get(\"repeated_subject_revisions\", []):\n        kind = conflict[\"kind\"]\n        subject_id = conflict[\"subject_id\"]\n        revision = conflict[\"revision\"]\n        refs = [_ref_text(ref) for ref in conflict.get(\"occurrences\", [])]\n        item_id = f\"revision-conflict:{kind}:{subject_id}:r{revision}\"\n        _open_issue_for_subject(\n            queue, item_id=item_id, subject_type=kind, subject_id=subject_id,\n            revision=revision, refs=refs,\n            reason=f\"multiple retained source records use {kind} {subject_id} revision {revision}; their business content requires review\",\n            owner=\"Travel Administration Lead\", next_action=\"compare the source occurrences and establish the supported revision record\",\n            run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n        )\n    for malformed in history.get(\"issues\", {}).get(\"malformed_revision_records\", []):\n        blockers.append({\n            \"record_id\": f\"malformed-revision:{_digest(malformed)[:16]}\",\n            \"reason\": malformed[\"reason\"],\n            \"owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n            \"resolution_needed\": \"identify the subject and revision from the native source record\",\n            \"source_ref\": malformed.get(\"source_ref\"),\n        })\n    for decision in domain[\"decision_history\"]:\n        if decision[\"structural_match\"] in {\"revision_match_current\", \"revision_match_historical\"}:\n            continue\n        kind, subject_id, revision = decision.get(\"subject_type\"), decision.get(\"subject_id\"), decision.get(\"revision\")\n        decision_id = decision.get(\"decision_id\") or _digest(decision)[:16]\n        if kind in {\"claim\", \"trip\", \"permit\"} and isinstance(subject_id, str) and isinstance(revision, int) and revision > 0:\n            item_id = f\"decision-match:{decision_id}\"\n            _open_issue_for_subject(\n                queue, item_id=item_id, subject_type=kind, subject_id=subject_id,\n                revision=revision, refs=[_ref_text(decision[\"decision_source_ref\"])],\n                reason=f\"recorded decision {decision_id} does not structurally match an available {kind} revision ({decision['structural_match']})\",\n                owner=\"Travel Administration Lead\", next_action=\"resolve the decision subject or revision against the native review ledger\",\n                run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n            )\n        else:\n            blockers.append({\n                \"record_id\": f\"decision-match:{decision_id}\",\n                \"reason\": f\"recorded decision has no traceable supported subject/revision ({decision['structural_match']})\",\n                \"owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n                \"resolution_needed\": \"identify its subject and revision in the native review ledger\",\n                \"source_ref\": decision[\"decision_source_ref\"],\n            })\n    domain[\"structural_blockers\"] = blockers\n\n\ndef integrate_arrival_batch(\n    parsed: dict[str, Any],\n    *,\n    arrival_batch: int,\n    run_id: str,\n    batch_id: str,\n    source_binding: dict[str, str],\n    predecessor: dict[str, str] | None = None,\n    prior_result: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n    authorized_obligations: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] | None = None,\n    source_classifications: dict[str, str] | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Integrate exactly the next arrival batch into a schema-shaped projection.\n\n    The function retains raw subject/activity rows in a sidecar `domain`,\n    carries earlier state forward, and supports exact same-batch replay. It\n    does not consume or seal a scenario snapshot; callers must separately\n    verify access, case clock, policy, and authorities before doing that.\n    \"\"\"\n    if isinstance(arrival_batch, bool) or not isinstance(arrival_batch, int) or arrival_batch < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"arrival_batch must be a positive integer\")\n    if not run_id or not batch_id or not isinstance(source_binding, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"run_id, batch_id, and source_binding are required\")\n    delta = _delta(parsed, arrival_batch)\n    digest = _digest({\n        \"delta\": delta,\n        \"run_id\": run_id,\n        \"batch_id\": batch_id,\n        \"source_binding\": source_binding,\n        \"predecessor\": predecessor,\n        \"authorized_obligations\": authorized_obligations or {},\n        \"source_classifications\": source_classifications or {},\n        \"trip_reference_records\": parsed.get(\"records\", {}).get(\"trips\", []),\n        \"unresolved_issues\": parsed.get(\"unresolved_issues\", []),\n    })\n    previous_domain = deepcopy(prior_result[\"domain\"]) if prior_result else _domain_seed()\n    processed = previous_domain[\"processed_batches\"]\n    if processed and arrival_batch == processed[-1]:\n        if previous_domain[\"batch_input_hashes\"].get(str(arrival_batch)) == digest:\n            return deepcopy(prior_result)\n        raise ValueError(f\"conflicting replay for arrival batch {arrival_batch}\")\n    expected_batch = processed[-1] + 1 if processed else 1\n    if arrival_batch != expected_batch:\n        raise ValueError(f\"arrival batches must be integrated in explicit order; expected {expected_batch}, got {arrival_batch}\")\n    if prior_result is None and predecessor is not None:\n        raise ValueError(\"the first integrated batch must have a null predecessor\")\n    if prior_result is not None:\n        if prior_result.get(\"snapshot\", {}).get(\"run_id\") != run_id:\n            raise ValueError(\"prior integration state belongs to a different run\")\n        if predecessor is None:\n            raise ValueError(\"a later integrated batch must carry a predecessor binding\")\n\n    domain = previous_domain\n    if authorized_obligations:\n        domain[\"authorized_obligations\"].update(deepcopy(authorized_obligations))\n    if source_classifications:\n        domain[\"source_classifications\"].update(deepcopy(source_classifications))\n    previous_claim_revisions = {\n        subject_id: value[\"current_revision\"]\n        for subject_id, value in (domain.get(\"revision_history\") or {}).get(\"claim\", {}).items()\n    }\n    for name in (\"claim_revisions\", \"decisions\", \"finance_events\", \"cancellation_activities\"):\n        target_name = {\n            \"claim_revisions\": \"claim_records\", \"decisions\": \"decision_records\",\n            \"finance_events\": \"finance_records\", \"cancellation_activities\": \"cancellation_records\",\n        }[name]\n        domain[target_name].extend(deepcopy(delta[name]))\n    domain[\"processed_batches\"].append(arrival_batch)\n    domain[\"batch_input_hashes\"][str(arrival_batch)] = digest\n\n    history = build_revision_history({\n        \"records\": {\"claim_revisions\": domain[\"claim_records\"], \"trips\": parsed.get(\"records\", {}).get(\"trips\", [])}\n    })\n    domain[\"revision_history\"] = history\n    domain[\"decision_history\"] = match_decisions_to_subjects(domain[\"decision_records\"], history)\n    for decision, raw in zip(domain[\"decision_history\"], domain[\"decision_records\"]):\n        decision[\"arrival_batch\"] = row_values(raw).get(\"Arrival batch\")\n        decision[\"applied\"] = False\n    _sync_decision_and_revision_issues(domain, history=history, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id)\n    _material_correction_tasks(\n        domain, history=history, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n        previous_revisions=previous_claim_revisions,\n    )\n\n    current_claims = {}\n    for claim_id, record_set in history.get(\"claim\", {}).items():\n        current_revision = record_set[\"current_revision\"]\n        claim_revision = next(row for row in reversed(record_set[\"revisions\"]) if row[\"revision\"] == current_revision)\n        current_claims[claim_id] = claim_revision\n    finance_results = {}\n    for claim_id, claim_revision in current_claims.items():\n        record_set = history[\"claim\"][claim_id]\n        prior_finance = domain[\"finance_reconciliations\"].get(claim_id)\n        finance_results[claim_id] = reconcile_finance_events(\n            domain[\"finance_records\"], claim_id=claim_id,\n            current_revision=claim_revision[\"revision\"],\n            authorized_obligation=domain[\"authorized_obligations\"].get(claim_id),\n            revision_history=record_set[\"revisions\"],\n            previous_reconciliation=prior_finance,\n            source_classifications=domain[\"source_classifications\"],\n        )\n    domain[\"finance_reconciliations\"] = finance_results\n    _sync_finance_repairs(domain, finance_results, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id)\n\n    # Policy and case-clock blockers are copied from parser/source evidence and\n    # deliberately remain outside any fabricated claim/decision outcome.\n    blockers = []\n    for row in parsed.get(\"unresolved_issues\", []):\n        blocker = {\n            \"record_id\": row[\"record_id\"],\n            \"reason\": row.get(\"reason\", \"Unresolved source issue\"),\n            \"owner\": row.get(\"owner\", \"Exercise facilitator\"),\n            \"resolution_needed\": row.get(\"next_action\", \"Obtain the missing authoritative evidence\"),\n            \"subject_type\": row.get(\"subject_type\"),\n            \"subject_id\": row.get(\"subject_id\"),\n            \"affected_scope\": row.get(\"affected_scope\"),\n            \"evidence_needed\": row.get(\"evidence_needed\"),\n        }\n        blockers.append(blocker)\n    domain[\"policy_clock_blockers\"] = blockers\n\n    cancellation_rows = _cancellation_rows(domain, history=history, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id)\n    schema_issues = list(blockers) + list(domain.get(\"structural_blockers\", []))\n    schema_issues.extend(_issue_from_item(item) for item in domain[\"repair_queue\"][\"items\"].values() if item[\"status\"] == \"open\")\n    # Every cancellation issue reference must resolve in issues[].record_id.\n    known_issue_ids = {issue[\"record_id\"] for issue in schema_issues}\n    for cancellation in cancellation_rows:\n        cancellation[\"issue_record_ids\"] = [\n            issue_id for issue_id in cancellation[\"issue_record_ids\"] if issue_id in known_issue_ids\n        ]\n\n    snapshot_claims = []\n    projection_issues = []\n    for claim_id, revision_row in sorted(current_claims.items()):\n        revision = revision_row[\"revision\"]\n        record = revision_row[\"record\"]\n        values = _page_values(record)\n        trip_id = revision_row.get(\"trip_id\")\n        trip_revision = revision_row.get(\"trip_revision\")\n        if not trip_id or not trip_revision:\n            projection_issues.append({\n                \"record_id\": f\"snapshot-claim-link:{claim_id}:r{revision}\",\n                \"reason\": \"claim source lacks the trip identity or revision required by snapshot.schema.json; claim omitted from snapshot projection\",\n                \"owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n                \"resolution_needed\": \"obtain and verify the current claim-to-trip revision binding\",\n            })\n            continue\n        trip_record_set = history.get(\"trip\", {}).get(str(trip_id), {})\n        linked_trip = any(row[\"revision\"] == trip_revision for row in trip_record_set.get(\"revisions\", []))\n        if not linked_trip:\n            item_id = f\"trip-link:{claim_id}:r{revision}\"\n            _open_issue_for_subject(\n                domain[\"repair_queue\"], item_id=item_id, subject_type=\"claim\", subject_id=claim_id,\n                revision=revision, refs=[_ref_text(revision_row[\"source_ref\"])],\n                reason=f\"claim references trip {trip_id} revision {trip_revision}, which is not present in the retained trip register\",\n                owner=\"Travel Administration Lead\", next_action=\"verify the trip revision from an accessible native travel register\",\n                run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n            )\n            schema_issues.append(_issue_from_item(domain[\"repair_queue\"][\"items\"][item_id]))\n        matches = [row for row in domain[\"decision_history\"]\n                   if row.get(\"subject_type\") == \"claim\" and row.get(\"subject_id\") == claim_id\n                   and row.get(\"revision\") == revision and row.get(\"structural_match\") == \"revision_match_current\"]\n        finance = finance_results[claim_id]\n        snapshot_claims.append({\n            \"claim_id\": claim_id,\n            \"revision\": revision,\n            \"trip_id\": str(trip_id),\n            \"trip_revision\": trip_revision,\n            \"status\": \"pending\",\n            \"lines\": [],\n            \"allowed_cents\": None,\n            \"paid_cents\": finance[\"net_confirmed_cents\"],\n            \"balance_cents\": finance[\"balance_cents\"],\n            \"decision_ids\": list(dict.fromkeys(row[\"decision_id\"] for row in matches if row.get(\"decision_id\"))),\n            \"next_owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n            \"reason\": \"Structural integration only; reimbursement policy and current-revision compliance remain unresolved.\",\n        })\n\n    schema_issues.extend(projection_issues)\n    schema_issues.extend(domain.get(\"projection_issues\", []))\n    # Deduplicate by record_id while preserving issue order.\n    unique_issues = {}\n    for issue in schema_issues:\n        unique_issues.setdefault(issue[\"record_id\"], issue)\n    schema_issues = list(unique_issues.values())\n\n    finance_ids = []\n    unresolved_ids = set()\n    conflicting_ids = set()\n    for result in finance_results.values():\n        unresolved_ids.update(result[\"unresolved_event_ids\"])\n        conflicting_ids.update(issue[\"event_id\"] for issue in result[\"conflicting_events\"])\n        for event in result[\"event_history\"]:\n            event_id = event[\"event_id\"]\n            if (event_id and event_id not in unresolved_ids and event_id not in conflicting_ids\n                    and event[\"classification\"] not in {\"unresolved\", \"conflicting_event_id\", \"missing_event_id\"}):\n                finance_ids.append(event_id)\n    finance_ids = list(dict.fromkeys(event_id for event_id in finance_ids if event_id not in unresolved_ids | conflicting_ids))\n\n    snapshot = {\n        \"schema_version\": \"travel-claim-snapshot/2\",\n        \"run_id\": run_id,\n        \"batch_id\": batch_id,\n        \"predecessor\": deepcopy(predecessor),\n        \"source_binding\": deepcopy(source_binding),\n        \"claims\": snapshot_claims,\n        \"requests\": [],\n        \"travel_cancellations\": cancellation_rows,\n        \"admitted_event_ids\": finance_ids,\n        \"issues\": schema_issues,\n    }\n    domain[\"processed_batches\"] = list(domain[\"processed_batches\"])\n    return {\n        \"snapshot\": snapshot,\n        \"domain\": domain,\n        \"decision_history\": deepcopy(domain[\"decision_history\"]),\n        \"finance_reconciliations\": deepcopy(finance_results),\n        \"revision_history\": deepcopy(history),\n        \"repair_queue_by_owner\": _owner_view(domain[\"repair_queue\"]),\n        \"batch_delta_counts\": {key: len(value) for key, value in delta.items()},\n        \"input_sha256\": digest,\n    }\n\n\ndef _owner_view(queue: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]]:\n    grouped: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = {}\n    for item in queue[\"items\"].values():\n        grouped.setdefault(item[\"owner\"], []).append(item)\n    return {owner: sorted(items, key=lambda row: row[\"item_id\"]) for owner, items in sorted(grouped.items())}\n\"\"\"Source-traceable Finance reconciliation primitives.\n\nOnly explicit, source-classified settled and refund events affect confirmed\ncash. Finance obligations remain separate from caller-supplied authorized\nobligations. No policy entitlement or approval decision is made here.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\nfrom typing import Any\n\n\n_NATIVE_EVENT_CLASSES = {\n    \"accepted\": \"obligation_accepted\",\n    \"settled\": \"confirmed_payment\",\n    \"refund\": \"confirmed_refund\",\n    \"failed\": \"failed_transfer\",\n    \"retry_authorized\": \"retry_authorization\",\n    \"cancellation_requested\": \"finance_cancellation_requested\",\n    \"cancelled\": \"finance_cancelled\",\n    # These are retained as non-cash Finance records; their amount describes\n    # an obligation, not a payment.\n    \"adjustment\": \"finance_adjustment\",\n    \"resolution\": \"finance_resolution\",\n}\n\n\ndef _values(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: cell.get(\"value\") for key, cell in record.get(\"values\", {}).items()}\n\n\ndef _source_ref(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: record.get(key) for key in (\"source_id\", \"source_sha256\", \"locator\")}\n\n\ndef _cents(value: Any) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"Convert exact EUR decimal input to integer cents; reject rounding.\"\"\"\n    if value is None or isinstance(value, bool):\n        return None\n    try:\n        amount = Decimal(str(value))\n    except (InvalidOperation, ValueError):\n        return None\n    if not amount.is_finite():\n        return None\n    scaled = amount * 100\n    if scaled != scaled.to_integral_value() or scaled < 0:\n        return None\n    return int(scaled)\n\n\ndef _payload(values: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: values[key] for key in sorted(values) if key != \"Arrival batch\"}\n\n\ndef reconcile_finance_events(\n    events: list[dict[str, Any]],\n    *,\n    claim_id: str,\n    current_revision: int,\n    authorized_obligation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n    revision_history: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None,\n    previous_reconciliation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n    owner: str = \"Finance\",\n    source_classifications: dict[str, str] | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Reconcile source events for a claim without making policy decisions.\n\n    `authorized_obligation` is an independent, already-authorized input of\n    `{amount_cents, claim_revision, source_refs}`. This function neither\n    derives nor authorizes it. `source_classifications` may extend the native\n    workbook vocabulary when a retained source defines another event type;\n    unrecognized types otherwise remain unresolved.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not claim_id or isinstance(current_revision, bool) or not isinstance(current_revision, int) or current_revision < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"claim_id and a positive current_revision are required\")\n    if not owner:\n        raise ValueError(\"owner is required for reconciliation issues\")\n\n    classes = dict(_NATIVE_EVENT_CLASSES)\n    if source_classifications:\n        allowed_classes = {\n            \"confirmed_payment\", \"confirmed_refund\", \"pending_transfer\",\n            \"obligation_accepted\", \"failed_transfer\", \"retry_authorization\",\n            \"finance_cancellation_requested\", \"finance_cancelled\",\n            \"finance_adjustment\", \"finance_resolution\",\n        }\n        for event_type, classification in source_classifications.items():\n            if not isinstance(event_type, str) or classification not in allowed_classes:\n                raise ValueError(f\"unsupported source event classification: {event_type!r} -> {classification!r}\")\n            classes[event_type] = classification\n\n    by_id: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n    missing_id_records: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    for record in events:\n        event_id = _values(record).get(\"Activity reference\")\n        if not isinstance(event_id, str) or not event_id:\n            if _values(record).get(\"Claim reference\") == claim_id:\n                missing_id_records.append(record)\n        else:\n            by_id[event_id].append(record)\n\n    relevant_occurrences: list[tuple[str | None, dict[str, Any], dict[str, Any], bool]] = []\n    duplicate_events = []\n    conflicting_events = []\n    for event_id, occurrences in by_id.items():\n        relevant = [record for record in occurrences if _values(record).get(\"Claim reference\") == claim_id]\n        if not relevant:\n            continue\n        payloads = [_payload(_values(record)) for record in occurrences]\n        conflict = any(payload != payloads[0] for payload in payloads[1:])\n        for record in relevant:\n            relevant_occurrences.append((event_id, record, _values(record), conflict))\n        if conflict:\n            conflicting_events.append({\n                \"event_id\": event_id,\n                \"source_refs\": [_source_ref(record) for record in occurrences],\n                \"payloads\": payloads,\n            })\n        elif len(occurrences) > 1:\n            duplicate_events.append({\n                \"event_id\": event_id,\n                \"source_refs\": [_source_ref(record) for record in occurrences],\n                \"delivery_batches\": [_values(record).get(\"Arrival batch\") for record in occurrences],\n            })\n    relevant_occurrences.extend((None, record, _values(record), True) for record in missing_id_records)\n    relevant_occurrences.sort(key=lambda row: (\n        str(row[2].get(\"Arrival batch\") or \"\"),\n        int(row[1].get(\"row\") or 0),\n        row[0] or \"\",\n    ))\n\n    history = []\n    event_issue_by_id: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\n    typed = []\n    unresolved = []\n    for event_id, record, values, conflict in relevant_occurrences:\n        event_type = values.get(\"Activity type\")\n        classification = classes.get(event_type, \"unresolved\")\n        item = {\n            \"event_id\": event_id,\n            \"source_ref\": _source_ref(record),\n            \"source_record\": deepcopy(values),\n            \"event_type\": event_type,\n            \"classification\": (\n                \"conflicting_event_id\" if conflict and event_id else\n                \"missing_event_id\" if conflict else classification\n            ),\n            \"amount_cents\": _cents(values.get(\"Amount (EUR)\")),\n            \"obligation_cents\": _cents(values.get(\"Obligation (EUR)\")),\n            \"currency\": values.get(\"Currency\"),\n            \"original_activity_id\": values.get(\"Original activity reference\"),\n        }\n        history.append(item)\n        if conflict:\n            if event_id:\n                event_issue_by_id[event_id] = {\n                    \"record_id\": f\"finance-event-conflict:{event_id}\",\n                    \"event_id\": event_id,\n                    \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n                    \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n                    \"revision\": current_revision,\n                    \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"same Finance event ID has conflicting source content; none of its occurrences were counted\",\n                    \"source_refs\": [_source_ref(row) for row in by_id[event_id]],\n                    \"owner\": owner,\n                    \"next_action\": \"Finance to resolve the source record conflict\",\n                }\n            else:\n                event_issue_by_id[f\"missing:{record.get('locator')}\"] = {\n                    \"record_id\": f\"finance-event-missing-id:{record.get('row') or len(event_issue_by_id) + 1}\",\n                    \"event_id\": None,\n                    \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n                    \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n                    \"revision\": current_revision,\n                    \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"Finance event has no activity reference and cannot be safely deduplicated or counted\",\n                    \"source_refs\": [_source_ref(record)],\n                    \"owner\": owner,\n                    \"next_action\": \"Finance to identify this ledger event and provide its native activity reference\",\n                }\n            continue\n        if classification == \"unresolved\":\n            unresolved.append(item)\n            continue\n        if classification in {\"confirmed_payment\", \"confirmed_refund\"}:\n            if values.get(\"Currency\") != \"EUR\" or item[\"amount_cents\"] is None:\n                unresolved.append(item)\n                continue\n        typed.append(item)\n\n    payments = {item[\"event_id\"]: item for item in typed if item[\"classification\"] == \"confirmed_payment\"}\n    confirmed_refunds: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    refund_candidates = [item for item in typed if item[\"classification\"] == \"confirmed_refund\"]\n    refund_groups: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n    for item in refund_candidates:\n        original_id = item[\"original_activity_id\"]\n        original = payments.get(original_id) if isinstance(original_id, str) else None\n        if original is None or original.get(\"currency\") != item.get(\"currency\"):\n            unresolved.append(item)\n            continue\n        refund_groups[original_id].append(item)\n    for original_id, refunds in refund_groups.items():\n        original = payments[original_id]\n        refund_total = sum(item[\"amount_cents\"] for item in refunds)\n        if refund_total > original[\"amount_cents\"]:\n            unresolved.extend(refunds)\n            continue\n        confirmed_refunds.extend(refunds)\n\n    invalid_payments = [item for item in payments.values() if item[\"amount_cents\"] is None]\n    unresolved.extend(invalid_payments)\n    confirmed_payment_cents = sum(item[\"amount_cents\"] for item in payments.values() if item[\"amount_cents\"] is not None)\n    confirmed_refund_cents = sum(item[\"amount_cents\"] for item in confirmed_refunds)\n    net_confirmed_cents = confirmed_payment_cents - confirmed_refund_cents\n\n    issues = list(event_issue_by_id.values())\n    for number, item in enumerate(unresolved, 1):\n        issue_id = f\"finance-unresolved:{item['event_id'] or number}\"\n        issue = {\n            \"record_id\": issue_id,\n            \"event_id\": item[\"event_id\"],\n            \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n            \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n            \"revision\": current_revision,\n            \"source_refs\": [item[\"source_ref\"]],\n            \"missing_or_return_reason\": (\n                f\"Finance event {item['event_id']!r} is not sufficiently classified or linked for cash reconciliation\"\n            ),\n            \"owner\": owner,\n            \"next_action\": \"Finance to confirm event meaning, amount, currency, or refund link from the native ledger\",\n        }\n        issues.append(issue)\n    issues_by_owner: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n    for issue in issues:\n        issues_by_owner[issue[\"owner\"]].append(issue)\n    issues_by_owner = {key: sorted(value, key=lambda row: row[\"record_id\"]) for key, value in sorted(issues_by_owner.items())}\n\n    obligation = None\n    obligation_issue = None\n    if authorized_obligation is not None:\n        amount = authorized_obligation.get(\"amount_cents\")\n        obligation_revision = authorized_obligation.get(\"claim_revision\")\n        refs = authorized_obligation.get(\"source_refs\")\n        if (isinstance(amount, int) and not isinstance(amount, bool) and amount >= 0\n                and obligation_revision == current_revision and isinstance(refs, list)\n                and refs and all(isinstance(ref, str) and ref for ref in refs)):\n            obligation = {\"amount_cents\": amount, \"claim_revision\": obligation_revision, \"source_refs\": list(dict.fromkeys(refs))}\n        else:\n            obligation_issue = {\n                \"record_id\": f\"finance-obligation-invalid:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n                \"event_id\": None,\n                \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n                \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n                \"revision\": current_revision,\n                \"source_refs\": list(refs) if isinstance(refs, list) else [],\n                \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"authorized obligation is missing exact cents, current-revision match, or supporting source reference\",\n                \"owner\": owner,\n                \"next_action\": \"Finance to provide or confirm the authorized obligation for this claim revision\",\n            }\n    else:\n        obligation_issue = {\n            \"record_id\": f\"finance-obligation-missing:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n            \"event_id\": None,\n            \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n            \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n            \"revision\": current_revision,\n            \"source_refs\": [],\n            \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"no supported authorized obligation was supplied for this claim revision\",\n            \"owner\": owner,\n            \"next_action\": \"Finance to provide or confirm the authorized obligation for this claim revision\",\n        }\n    if obligation_issue is not None:\n        issues.append(obligation_issue)\n        issues_by_owner.setdefault(owner, []).append(obligation_issue)\n        issues_by_owner[owner].sort(key=lambda row: row[\"record_id\"])\n\n    has_unclassified_cash_event = any(item[\"classification\"] == \"unresolved\" for item in history)\n    event_set_complete = not unresolved and not conflicting_events and not missing_id_records and not has_unclassified_cash_event\n    balance = None\n    if obligation is not None and event_set_complete:\n        balance = obligation[\"amount_cents\"] - net_confirmed_cents\n\n    invalidated = None\n    if previous_reconciliation is not None:\n        previous_revision = previous_reconciliation.get(\"claim_revision\")\n        if previous_revision != current_revision:\n            invalidated = {\n                \"claim_revision\": previous_revision,\n                \"reason\": \"material revision change invalidates the prior reconciliation basis\",\n                \"prior_net_confirmed_cents\": previous_reconciliation.get(\"net_confirmed_cents\"),\n                \"prior_balance_cents\": previous_reconciliation.get(\"balance_cents\"),\n            }\n    return {\n        \"claim_id\": claim_id,\n        \"claim_revision\": current_revision,\n        \"revision_history\": deepcopy(revision_history or []),\n        \"event_history\": history,\n        \"event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in history if item[\"event_id\"] is not None],\n        \"duplicate_events\": duplicate_events,\n        \"conflicting_events\": conflicting_events,\n        \"confirmed_payment_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in payments.values() if item[\"amount_cents\"] is not None],\n        \"confirmed_refund_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in confirmed_refunds],\n        \"pending_transfer_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in typed if item[\"classification\"] == \"pending_transfer\"],\n        \"unresolved_event_ids\": list(dict.fromkeys(item[\"event_id\"] for item in unresolved if item[\"event_id\"] is not None)),\n        \"finance_obligation_events\": [item for item in history if item[\"classification\"] == \"obligation_accepted\"],\n        \"authorized_obligation\": obligation,\n        \"confirmed_payment_cents\": confirmed_payment_cents,\n        \"confirmed_refund_cents\": confirmed_refund_cents,\n        \"net_confirmed_cents\": net_confirmed_cents,\n        \"balance_cents\": balance,\n        \"inputs_complete\": balance is not None,\n        \"repair_issues\": issues,\n        \"repair_issues_by_owner\": issues_by_owner,\n        \"invalidated_previous_reconciliation\": invalidated,\n    }\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":56574320},"formatted_output":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 23486)\nTotal output lines: 1828\n\n# Project D — Travel Expense Claim Interview\n\nParticipant: Max Gabel · Exported: 10/13/2026, 6:10:03 PM\n\n## Travel Administration Lead · Travel Administration Lead\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:13 PM\n\nHello, thank you for your time.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:13 PM\n\nI coordinate travel reimbursements at Alderbridge. Much of my time goes into checking evidence, chasing reviews, and finding out what Finance actually paid, especially when a claim changes. I would like help making the whole process repeatable. You can ask me about how we work, policy, the records we use, or the problems that keep coming back.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:14 PM\n\nWhat policies?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:14 PM\n\nWe follow policy POL-2026.2, which governs how expenses are reviewed and reimbursed. It outlines separate requirements for international permits and claims, specifies approval roles like the budget owner and supervisor, and sets limits on categories like lodging and meals. You can find all the details in the Travel reimbursement policy.\n\n- [Travel reimbursement policy](https://private-pecorino-70e.notion.site/REDACTED)\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:14 PM\n\nWhich part of the reimbursement workflow would you like to explore next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:14 PM\n\nAre those all the policies?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:14 PM\n\nYes, policy POL-2026.2 is our primary reimbursement guide for 2026. It covers all the rules regarding approvals, expense categories and limits. Are there any specific categories you had in mind?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:15 PM\n\nI want to know what happens when there are exceptions to the policies.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:15 PM\n\nWhen there are exceptions, like for late filings or specific amount limits, we need a Finance exception. This official exception is issued by Finance for a specific claim version to resolve a set issue, like late filing or an unapproved permit. However, it doesn't waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:15 PM\n\nWhen you say Finance, is that a department?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:15 PM\n\nYes, Finance refers to our financial department. They are responsible for issuing monetary tables like currency rates and spending caps, providing official exceptions for policy issues, and handling actual payment execution and reconciliation for claims.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nI want to make sure I understand this.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nI'm happy to go over\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nThe financial department holds the sole authority to issue official exceptions for policy discrepancies. on a specific claim version. They cannot waive a missing evidence such as receipts or proof of payment.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nThat is correct. They are responsible for issuing official exceptions for specific issues on a claim version, but they cannot waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nWhere are receipts or a proof of payment stored?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nReceipts are stored in the Receipt binder, while proof of payment, such as settled merchant transactions, is found in the Merchant payments tab of the Travel registers workbook.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\n\nWhich part of the work would you like to explore next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:17 PM\n\nDo receipts ever get destroyed or lost?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:17 PM\n\nIf a receipt is lost, the employee must provide alternative evidence or an explanation, but since Finance cannot waive missing receipts, the claim will remain unresolved until the evidence is provided.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:17 PM\n\nIs the Travel registers workbook a physical workbook or online?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:17 PM\n\nThe Travel registers workbook is an online spreadsheet that we use to track merchant payments and other financial activities.\n\n- [Travel registers](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:17 PM\n\nWhich part of the workflow would you like to discuss next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:18 PM\n\nWhat are the financial activities?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:18 PM\n\nFinancial activities include the pending, failed, or settled outcomes of payment requests, as well as accepted commitments, adjustments, refunds, and cancellations. These are all tracked and owned by the Finance department.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:18 PM\n\nTell me more about cancellations.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:18 PM\n\nCancellations can target an entire trip or just a permit version independently of a claim. They must be initiated by the employee and confirmed by the supervisor, and these actions are tracked in the Travel cancellations workbook. If there were paid costs or Finance commitments, Finance will need to issue a specific disposition and resolve the money separately.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nHow would they resolve the disposition?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nFinance will issue a specific disposition bound to the cancellation ID, which confirms the reimbursement eligibility and provides a new allowed amount and reason for the affected costs.\n\n- [Travel cancellations](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nIs there a limit to the allowed amount?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nYes, limits apply to specific categories. Lodging and meals are limited by daily or nightly caps set by Finance, based on the destination and date, which are then multiplied by the documented duration. Transport and conference expenses are not subject to these caps.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nHow is the lodging and meals determined? Like what pricing metrics?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:19 PM\n\nThe limits for lodging and meals are determined by daily or nightly caps set by Finance, based on your destination, expense currency, and the payment date. You can see these metrics in the Caps tab of the Travel registers workbook.\n\n- [Travel registers workbook](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:20 PM\n\nWhich part of the workflow would you like to discuss next?\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:20 PM\n\nHow do incomplete claims affect independent work?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:20 PM\n\nIncomplete claims are held while the missing facts are addressed. You can continue processing independent claims separately while others are held, as long as the business impact is made clear.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:20 PM\n\nWhen you say made clear, what types of data do you mean?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:20 PM\n\nWe need to identify the exact claim version, specify which facts are missing, name the owner responsible for supplying them, and outline the next action to resolve the issue.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nWhat actions do you have to choose from to resolve the issue?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nThe available actions include requesting missing evidence from the employee, seeking an official exception from Finance for specific issues, or holding the claim until Finance confirms the resolution or provides the missing definitions.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nOn average, how long does it take Finance to confirm resolution or provide the missing definitions?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nI don't have a set average for Finance response times. Their replies come in batches, and the time it takes depends on the volume and complexity of the request.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nWhen was the most recent time a Finance needed to confirm resolution that you can remember?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:21 PM\n\nI don't track specific dates for those resolutions in my head. Our Finance replies are delivered in versioned batches, and we process the needed resolutions as they arrive based on the specific claims and costs.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nHow many people are in a batch?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nThe batch size isn't fixed; it depends on the number of claims, requests, or reviewer replies being processed by Finance or the relevant budget owner at that time.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nHow are batches organized? For example, could they be organized by a time slot or with a certain amount of people inside?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nBatches aren't organized by fixed time slots or a specific number of people. They are versioned delivery packets supplied by the trainer based on the number of claims, requests, and reviewer replies processed and ready at that moment.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nHow are they assigned to a trainer?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:22 PM\n\nI don't assign claims to a trainer. The replies you see come from versioned batches provided by Finance or other appropriate reviewers based on the business workflow.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nHow many trainers are there?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nI don't have information about trainers. My work focuses on coordinating with the Finance department, budget owners, supervisors, and employees to process travel claims.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nWhat are the boundaries for trainers, meaning what can and can't they do in this?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nI don't have information about trainers. My role is Travel Administration Lead, and the replies I receive come from Finance, budget owners, supervisors, and directors within the established business workflow.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nTell me about the boundaries of Finance.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:23 PM\n\nFinance owns setting currency rates, managing spending caps, and issuing official policy exceptions. They also execute payments and resolve any monetary issues or cancellations, but they cannot waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nTell me about the boundaries of budget owners.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nBudget owners have the authority to approve, return, or reject a claim based on the complete department ledger. They assess funding availability and make discretionary decisions, which I receive in supplied reviewer replies.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nTell me about a discretionary decision.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nA discretionary decision is when the budget owner evaluates the department ledger and funding availability to decide whether to approve, return, or reject a claim. These judgments come directly from the budget owner's assessment and arrive in supplied reviewer replies.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nTell me about the boundaries of supervisors.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:24 PM\n\nSupervisors evaluate the business purpose of the trip, client commitment, schedule coverage, and permit consistency before providing their review reply. They also confirm travel cancellations initiated by the trip employee.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:25 PM\n\nTell me about the boundaries of directors.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:25 PM\n\nDirectors provide an additional layer of authorization for high-spend situations, typically when the reviewed claim entitlement or permit estimate exceeds EUR 1,000.00. They evaluate the business necessity, exceptions, and alternatives, and their decisions arrive in supplied reply batches.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nWhich work to revalidate after material corrections is the norm?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nThe policy requires a full or justified recheck of all affected dependencies, including calculations and approvals, when material changes are made. Even if the total amount remains the same, any change in evidence or facts invalidates prior readiness, so a fresh review is required.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nWhat are the financial completion conditions?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nFinancial completion requires that current approvals match the reviewed entitlement, net confirmed payments equal the authorized amount, no issues remain, and all required Finance resolutions have been received.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:27 PM\n\nWho owns the entitlement?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:27 PM\n\nI calculate the reviewed entitlement based on policy, evidence, and spending caps, but the budget owner owns the discretionary decision to fund or approve the specific claim amount.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:27 PM\n\nWhat is the delivery scope that is accept? After inspecting the actual result.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:27 PM\n\nThe accepted delivery scope is confirmed when the current approvals and reviewed entitlement agree with the net confirmed payment, and all required Finance resolutions have been received with no remaining issues.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nWhen you say issues, and what are the constraints for the repair work?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nIssues refer to unresolved problems like missing receipts, incomplete payment proof, late filings, or mismatched data. For repair work, constraints involve organizing the missing evidence into usable local tasks, retaining the subject and revision, identifying the responsible owner, and ensuring corrections go through required reviews.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nHow do you organize the repair work in partial response constraints?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nYou can organize repair work either by per-claim packages or by grouping all missing-evidence items by the specific person responsible for supplying them. The key constraint is to retain each item's subject, revision, missing fact, and owner for tracking.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nWhat's the best way to adopt these constraints before they guide the work?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:28 PM\n\nYou can choose between per-claim packages or grouping items by the person responsible, provided you clearly track the subject, revision, missing fact, and owner for every single item.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:29 PM\n\nWhich one of those is the most difficult to maintain?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:29 PM\n\nBoth approaches have trade-offs; per-claim packages require less cross-referencing but result in more packages, whereas grouping by the person reduces the number of units but requires item-level matching and careful partial completion tracking.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:30 PM\n\nCan cases remain unresolved when the facts require it?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:30 PM\n\nYes, cases can be placed on hold for missing facts or Finance resolutions, but they cannot be closed or considered complete until all required evidence and decisions are obtained.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:30 PM\n\nWhat type of report will affect the work, reason, responsible person, and evidence needed to resume?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:30 PM\n\nYou can use any format, such as a per-claim package or a grouped task list, as long as it consistently retains the specific claim version, the missing evidence or fact, the responsible owner, and the next action required to resume.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nWhat happens if inaccessible required sources must be erased with the lead facilitator rather than otherwise unknown?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nAs the Travel Administration Lead, I cannot invent or bypass required sources. If a required document or definition is inaccessible and cannot be obtained, it remains an unresolved issue that I must escalate to the exercise operator for guidance.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nHow long does that process take?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nThere is no set timeframe for how long the exercise operator takes to resolve an escalation, as it depends on the nature of the issue in the specific case.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nHow do you communicate?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:31 PM\n\nI communicate through formal requests and notifications. These include the subject type, IDs, stable role requesters, and relevant source versions, and I wait for replies from the authorized reviewers and Finance.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:33 PM\n\nLet me summarize to make sure I understand: the system route work based on four distinct human authority profiles: supervisors, budget owners, directors, and Finance.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:33 PM\n\nThat is correct. I coordinate the process by submitting requests for these different authorities and waiting for their determinations and resolutions to ensure claims are processed accurately and policy checks are met.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:38 PM\n\nHello, thank you for talking with me.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:38 PM\n\nHello! I coordinate travel reimbursements at Alderbridge. Much of my time goes into checking evidence, chasing reviews, and finding out what Finance actually paid, especially when a claim changes. You can ask me about how we work, our policy, the records we use, or the problems that keep coming back.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:38 PM\n\nCan you give me a the ordinary claim life cycle?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:38 PM\n\nThe ordinary cycle begins when an employee pays for a travel cost and submits a claim. I review the claim against the trip permits, receipts, and merchant payments to calculate the reviewed entitlement. Then, I coordinate the necessary approvals based on the amount and policy, submit the request to Finance for transfer, and reconcile the payments until the case is closed.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:39 PM\n\nWhat specific matching keys do you use to connect the submitted expense claims to its corresponding trip permit?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:39 PM\n\nI connect claims to trip permits using the employee's identity, the exact trip ID, and the specific trip revision number to ensure everything matches the approved travel records.\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:39 PM\n\nI connect claims to trip permits using the employee's identity, the exact trip ID, and the specific trip revision number to ensure everything matches the approved travel records.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:40 PM\n\nWhen you submit the request to Finance for transfer. what type of files or formats do you submit?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:40 PM\n\nI submit an identifiable request containing the employee or payee, the total authorized EUR amount, and references to all supporting evidence, required approvals, and funding commitments.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:40 PM\n\nAnd at what point of the ordinary claim life cycle were the funding commitments established?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:40 PM\n\nFunding commitments are established when Finance accepts the reimbursement request, confirming the obligation and reserving the funds for budget tracking.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:41 PM\n\nLet's discuss more about the process of cancellations when the original perm…13486 tokens truncated…    projection_issues.append({\n                \"record_id\": f\"snapshot-claim-link:{claim_id}:r{revision}\",\n                \"reason\": \"claim source lacks the trip identity or revision required by snapshot.schema.json; claim omitted from snapshot projection\",\n                \"owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n                \"resolution_needed\": \"obtain and verify the current claim-to-trip revision binding\",\n            })\n            continue\n        trip_record_set = history.get(\"trip\", {}).get(str(trip_id), {})\n        linked_trip = any(row[\"revision\"] == trip_revision for row in trip_record_set.get(\"revisions\", []))\n        if not linked_trip:\n            item_id = f\"trip-link:{claim_id}:r{revision}\"\n            _open_issue_for_subject(\n                domain[\"repair_queue\"], item_id=item_id, subject_type=\"claim\", subject_id=claim_id,\n                revision=revision, refs=[_ref_text(revision_row[\"source_ref\"])],\n                reason=f\"claim references trip {trip_id} revision {trip_revision}, which is not present in the retained trip register\",\n                owner=\"Travel Administration Lead\", next_action=\"verify the trip revision from an accessible native travel register\",\n                run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n            )\n            schema_issues.append(_issue_from_item(domain[\"repair_queue\"][\"items\"][item_id]))\n        matches = [row for row in domain[\"decision_history\"]\n                   if row.get(\"subject_type\") == \"claim\" and row.get(\"subject_id\") == claim_id\n                   and row.get(\"revision\") == revision and row.get(\"structural_match\") == \"revision_match_current\"]\n        finance = finance_results[claim_id]\n        snapshot_claims.append({\n            \"claim_id\": claim_id,\n            \"revision\": revision,\n            \"trip_id\": str(trip_id),\n            \"trip_revision\": trip_revision,\n            \"status\": \"pending\",\n            \"lines\": [],\n            \"allowed_cents\": None,\n            \"paid_cents\": finance[\"net_confirmed_cents\"],\n            \"balance_cents\": finance[\"balance_cents\"],\n            \"decision_ids\": list(dict.fromkeys(row[\"decision_id\"] for row in matches if row.get(\"decision_id\"))),\n            \"next_owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n            \"reason\": \"Structural integration only; reimbursement policy and current-revision compliance remain unresolved.\",\n        })\n\n    schema_issues.extend(projection_issues)\n    schema_issues.extend(domain.get(\"projection_issues\", []))\n    # Deduplicate by record_id while preserving issue order.\n    unique_issues = {}\n    for issue in schema_issues:\n        unique_issues.setdefault(issue[\"record_id\"], issue)\n    schema_issues = list(unique_issues.values())\n\n    finance_ids = []\n    unresolved_ids = set()\n    conflicting_ids = set()\n    for result in finance_results.values():\n        unresolved_ids.update(result[\"unresolved_event_ids\"])\n        conflicting_ids.update(issue[\"event_id\"] for issue in result[\"conflicting_events\"])\n        for event in result[\"event_history\"]:\n            event_id = event[\"event_id\"]\n            if (event_id and event_id not in unresolved_ids and event_id not in conflicting_ids\n                    and event[\"classification\"] not in {\"unresolved\", \"conflicting_event_id\", \"missing_event_id\"}):\n                finance_ids.append(event_id)\n    finance_ids = list(dict.fromkeys(event_id for event_id in finance_ids if event_id not in unresolved_ids | conflicting_ids))\n\n    snapshot = {\n        \"schema_version\": \"travel-claim-snapshot/2\",\n        \"run_id\": run_id,\n        \"batch_id\": batch_id,\n        \"predecessor\": deepcopy(predecessor),\n        \"source_binding\": deepcopy(source_binding),\n        \"claims\": snapshot_claims,\n        \"requests\": [],\n        \"travel_cancellations\": cancellation_rows,\n        \"admitted_event_ids\": finance_ids,\n        \"issues\": schema_issues,\n    }\n    domain[\"processed_batches\"] = list(domain[\"processed_batches\"])\n    return {\n        \"snapshot\": snapshot,\n        \"domain\": domain,\n        \"decision_history\": deepcopy(domain[\"decision_history\"]),\n        \"finance_reconciliations\": deepcopy(finance_results),\n        \"revision_history\": deepcopy(history),\n        \"repair_queue_by_owner\": _owner_view(domain[\"repair_queue\"]),\n        \"batch_delta_counts\": {key: len(value) for key, value in delta.items()},\n        \"input_sha256\": digest,\n    }\n\n\ndef _owner_view(queue: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]]:\n    grouped: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = {}\n    for item in queue[\"items\"].values():\n        grouped.setdefault(item[\"owner\"], []).append(item)\n    return {owner: sorted(items, key=lambda row: row[\"item_id\"]) for owner, items in sorted(grouped.items())}\n\"\"\"Source-traceable Finance reconciliation primitives.\n\nOnly explicit, source-classified settled and refund events affect confirmed\ncash. Finance obligations remain separate from caller-supplied authorized\nobligations. No policy entitlement or approval decision is made here.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\nfrom typing import Any\n\n\n_NATIVE_EVENT_CLASSES = {\n    \"accepted\": \"obligation_accepted\",\n    \"settled\": \"confirmed_payment\",\n    \"refund\": \"confirmed_refund\",\n    \"failed\": \"failed_transfer\",\n    \"retry_authorized\": \"retry_authorization\",\n    \"cancellation_requested\": \"finance_cancellation_requested\",\n    \"cancelled\": \"finance_cancelled\",\n    # These are retained as non-cash Finance records; their amount describes\n    # an obligation, not a payment.\n    \"adjustment\": \"finance_adjustment\",\n    \"resolution\": \"finance_resolution\",\n}\n\n\ndef _values(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: cell.get(\"value\") for key, cell in record.get(\"values\", {}).items()}\n\n\ndef _source_ref(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: record.get(key) for key in (\"source_id\", \"source_sha256\", \"locator\")}\n\n\ndef _cents(value: Any) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"Convert exact EUR decimal input to integer cents; reject rounding.\"\"\"\n    if value is None or isinstance(value, bool):\n        return None\n    try:\n        amount = Decimal(str(value))\n    except (InvalidOperation, ValueError):\n        return None\n    if not amount.is_finite():\n        return None\n    scaled = amount * 100\n    if scaled != scaled.to_integral_value() or scaled < 0:\n        return None\n    return int(scaled)\n\n\ndef _payload(values: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: values[key] for key in sorted(values) if key != \"Arrival batch\"}\n\n\ndef reconcile_finance_events(\n    events: list[dict[str, Any]],\n    *,\n    claim_id: str,\n    current_revision: int,\n    authorized_obligation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n    revision_history: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None,\n    previous_reconciliation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n    owner: str = \"Finance\",\n    source_classifications: dict[str, str] | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Reconcile source events for a claim without making policy decisions.\n\n    `authorized_obligation` is an independent, already-authorized input of\n    `{amount_cents, claim_revision, source_refs}`. This function neither\n    derives nor authorizes it. `source_classifications` may extend the native\n    workbook vocabulary when a retained source defines another event type;\n    unrecognized types otherwise remain unresolved.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not claim_id or isinstance(current_revision, bool) or not isinstance(current_revision, int) or current_revision < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"claim_id and a positive current_revision are required\")\n    if not owner:\n        raise ValueError(\"owner is required for reconciliation issues\")\n\n    classes = dict(_NATIVE_EVENT_CLASSES)\n    if source_classifications:\n        allowed_classes = {\n            \"confirmed_payment\", \"confirmed_refund\", \"pending_transfer\",\n            \"obligation_accepted\", \"failed_transfer\", \"retry_authorization\",\n            \"finance_cancellation_requested\", \"finance_cancelled\",\n            \"finance_adjustment\", \"finance_resolution\",\n        }\n        for event_type, classification in source_classifications.items():\n            if not isinstance(event_type, str) or classification not in allowed_classes:\n                raise ValueError(f\"unsupported source event classification: {event_type!r} -> {classification!r}\")\n            classes[event_type] = classification\n\n    by_id: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n    missing_id_records: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    for record in events:\n        event_id = _values(record).get(\"Activity reference\")\n        if not isinstance(event_id, str) or not event_id:\n            if _values(record).get(\"Claim reference\") == claim_id:\n                missing_id_records.append(record)\n        else:\n            by_id[event_id].append(record)\n\n    relevant_occurrences: list[tuple[str | None, dict[str, Any], dict[str, Any], bool]] = []\n    duplicate_events = []\n    conflicting_events = []\n    for event_id, occurrences in by_id.items():\n        relevant = [record for record in occurrences if _values(record).get(\"Claim reference\") == claim_id]\n        if not relevant:\n            continue\n        payloads = [_payload(_values(record)) for record in occurrences]\n        conflict = any(payload != payloads[0] for payload in payloads[1:])\n        for record in relevant:\n            relevant_occurrences.append((event_id, record, _values(record), conflict))\n        if conflict:\n            conflicting_events.append({\n                \"event_id\": event_id,\n                \"source_refs\": [_source_ref(record) for record in occurrences],\n                \"payloads\": payloads,\n            })\n        elif len(occurrences) > 1:\n            duplicate_events.append({\n                \"event_id\": event_id,\n                \"source_refs\": [_source_ref(record) for record in occurrences],\n                \"delivery_batches\": [_values(record).get(\"Arrival batch\") for record in occurrences],\n            })\n    relevant_occurrences.extend((None, record, _values(record), True) for record in missing_id_records)\n    relevant_occurrences.sort(key=lambda row: (\n        str(row[2].get(\"Arrival batch\") or \"\"),\n        int(row[1].get(\"row\") or 0),\n        row[0] or \"\",\n    ))\n\n    history = []\n    event_issue_by_id: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\n    typed = []\n    unresolved = []\n    for event_id, record, values, conflict in relevant_occurrences:\n        event_type = values.get(\"Activity type\")\n        classification = classes.get(event_type, \"unresolved\")\n        item = {\n            \"event_id\": event_id,\n            \"source_ref\": _source_ref(record),\n            \"source_record\": deepcopy(values),\n            \"event_type\": event_type,\n            \"classification\": (\n                \"conflicting_event_id\" if conflict and event_id else\n                \"missing_event_id\" if conflict else classification\n            ),\n            \"amount_cents\": _cents(values.get(\"Amount (EUR)\")),\n            \"obligation_cents\": _cents(values.get(\"Obligation (EUR)\")),\n            \"currency\": values.get(\"Currency\"),\n            \"original_activity_id\": values.get(\"Original activity reference\"),\n        }\n        history.append(item)\n        if conflict:\n            if event_id:\n                event_issue_by_id[event_id] = {\n                    \"record_id\": f\"finance-event-conflict:{event_id}\",\n                    \"event_id\": event_id,\n                    \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n                    \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n                    \"revision\": current_revision,\n                    \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"same Finance event ID has conflicting source content; none of its occurrences were counted\",\n                    \"source_refs\": [_source_ref(row) for row in by_id[event_id]],\n                    \"owner\": owner,\n                    \"next_action\": \"Finance to resolve the source record conflict\",\n                }\n            else:\n                event_issue_by_id[f\"missing:{record.get('locator')}\"] = {\n                    \"record_id\": f\"finance-event-missing-id:{record.get('row') or len(event_issue_by_id) + 1}\",\n                    \"event_id\": None,\n                    \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n                    \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n                    \"revision\": current_revision,\n                    \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"Finance event has no activity reference and cannot be safely deduplicated or counted\",\n                    \"source_refs\": [_source_ref(record)],\n                    \"owner\": owner,\n                    \"next_action\": \"Finance to identify this ledger event and provide its native activity reference\",\n                }\n            continue\n        if classification == \"unresolved\":\n            unresolved.append(item)\n            continue\n        if classification in {\"confirmed_payment\", \"confirmed_refund\"}:\n            if values.get(\"Currency\") != \"EUR\" or item[\"amount_cents\"] is None:\n                unresolved.append(item)\n                continue\n        typed.append(item)\n\n    payments = {item[\"event_id\"]: item for item in typed if item[\"classification\"] == \"confirmed_payment\"}\n    confirmed_refunds: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    refund_candidates = [item for item in typed if item[\"classification\"] == \"confirmed_refund\"]\n    refund_groups: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n    for item in refund_candidates:\n        original_id = item[\"original_activity_id\"]\n        original = payments.get(original_id) if isinstance(original_id, str) else None\n        if original is None or original.get(\"currency\") != item.get(\"currency\"):\n            unresolved.append(item)\n            continue\n        refund_groups[original_id].append(item)\n    for original_id, refunds in refund_groups.items():\n        original = payments[original_id]\n        refund_total = sum(item[\"amount_cents\"] for item in refunds)\n        if refund_total > original[\"amount_cents\"]:\n            unresolved.extend(refunds)\n            continue\n        confirmed_refunds.extend(refunds)\n\n    invalid_payments = [item for item in payments.values() if item[\"amount_cents\"] is None]\n    unresolved.extend(invalid_payments)\n    confirmed_payment_cents = sum(item[\"amount_cents\"] for item in payments.values() if item[\"amount_cents\"] is not None)\n    confirmed_refund_cents = sum(item[\"amount_cents\"] for item in confirmed_refunds)\n    net_confirmed_cents = confirmed_payment_cents - confirmed_refund_cents\n\n    issues = list(event_issue_by_id.values())\n    for number, item in enumerate(unresolved, 1):\n        issue_id = f\"finance-unresolved:{item['event_id'] or number}\"\n        issue = {\n            \"record_id\": issue_id,\n            \"event_id\": item[\"event_id\"],\n            \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n            \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n            \"revision\": current_revision,\n            \"source_refs\": [item[\"source_ref\"]],\n            \"missing_or_return_reason\": (\n                f\"Finance event {item['event_id']!r} is not sufficiently classified or linked for cash reconciliation\"\n            ),\n            \"owner\": owner,\n            \"next_action\": \"Finance to confirm event meaning, amount, currency, or refund link from the native ledger\",\n        }\n        issues.append(issue)\n    issues_by_owner: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n    for issue in issues:\n        issues_by_owner[issue[\"owner\"]].append(issue)\n    issues_by_owner = {key: sorted(value, key=lambda row: row[\"record_id\"]) for key, value in sorted(issues_by_owner.items())}\n\n    obligation = None\n    obligation_issue = None\n    if authorized_obligation is not None:\n        amount = authorized_obligation.get(\"amount_cents\")\n        obligation_revision = authorized_obligation.get(\"claim_revision\")\n        refs = authorized_obligation.get(\"source_refs\")\n        if (isinstance(amount, int) and not isinstance(amount, bool) and amount >= 0\n                and obligation_revision == current_revision and isinstance(refs, list)\n                and refs and all(isinstance(ref, str) and ref for ref in refs)):\n            obligation = {\"amount_cents\": amount, \"claim_revision\": obligation_revision, \"source_refs\": list(dict.fromkeys(refs))}\n        else:\n            obligation_issue = {\n                \"record_id\": f\"finance-obligation-invalid:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n                \"event_id\": None,\n                \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n                \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n                \"revision\": current_revision,\n                \"source_refs\": list(refs) if isinstance(refs, list) else [],\n                \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"authorized obligation is missing exact cents, current-revision match, or supporting source reference\",\n                \"owner\": owner,\n                \"next_action\": \"Finance to provide or confirm the authorized obligation for this claim revision\",\n            }\n    else:\n        obligation_issue = {\n            \"record_id\": f\"finance-obligation-missing:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n            \"event_id\": None,\n            \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n            \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n            \"revision\": current_revision,\n            \"source_refs\": [],\n            \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"no supported authorized obligation was supplied for this claim revision\",\n            \"owner\": owner,\n            \"next_action\": \"Finance to provide or confirm the authorized obligation for this claim revision\",\n        }\n    if obligation_issue is not None:\n        issues.append(obligation_issue)\n        issues_by_owner.setdefault(owner, []).append(obligation_issue)\n        issues_by_owner[owner].sort(key=lambda row: row[\"record_id\"])\n\n    has_unclassified_cash_event = any(item[\"classification\"] == \"unresolved\" for item in history)\n    event_set_complete = not unresolved and not conflicting_events and not missing_id_records and not has_unclassified_cash_event\n    balance = None\n    if obligation is not None and event_set_complete:\n        balance = obligation[\"amount_cents\"] - net_confirmed_cents\n\n    invalidated = None\n    if previous_reconciliation is not None:\n        previous_revision = previous_reconciliation.get(\"claim_revision\")\n        if previous_revision != current_revision:\n            invalidated = {\n                \"claim_revision\": previous_revision,\n                \"reason\": \"material revision change invalidates the prior reconciliation basis\",\n                \"prior_net_confirmed_cents\": previous_reconciliation.get(\"net_confirmed_cents\"),\n                \"prior_balance_cents\": previous_reconciliation.get(\"balance_cents\"),\n            }\n    return {\n        \"claim_id\": claim_id,\n        \"claim_revision\": current_revision,\n        \"revision_history\": deepcopy(revision_history or []),\n        \"event_history\": history,\n        \"event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in history if item[\"event_id\"] is not None],\n        \"duplicate_events\": duplicate_events,\n        \"conflicting_events\": conflicting_events,\n        \"confirmed_payment_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in payments.values() if item[\"amount_cents\"] is not None],\n        \"confirmed_refund_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in confirmed_refunds],\n        \"pending_transfer_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in typed if item[\"classification\"] == \"pending_transfer\"],\n        \"unresolved_event_ids\": list(dict.fromkeys(item[\"event_id\"] for item in unresolved if item[\"event_id\"] is not None)),\n        \"finance_obligation_events\": [item for item in history if item[\"classification\"] == \"obligation_accepted\"],\n        \"authorized_obligation\": obligation,\n        \"confirmed_payment_cents\": confirmed_payment_cents,\n        \"confirmed_refund_cents\": confirmed_refund_cents,\n        \"net_confirmed_cents\": net_confirmed_cents,\n        \"balance_cents\": balance,\n        \"inputs_complete\": balance is not None,\n        \"repair_issues\": issues,\n        \"repair_issues_by_owner\": issues_by_owner,\n        \"invalidated_previous_reconciliation\": invalidated,\n    }\n"},"started_at_ms":1792007121855,"completed_at_ms":1792007121913}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T19:45:22.479Z","ordinal":524,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a13bf2-ae2f-7841-a377-ef8cff7e2b42","call_id":"call_d260e93b1e9545eca13a413957c1c362","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 23857)\nTotal output lines: 1\n\n{\"chunk_id\":\"84077a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.05660083,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":23486,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 23486)\\nTotal output lines: 1828\\n\\n# Project D — Travel Expense Claim Interview\\n\\nParticipant: Max Gabel · Exported: 10/13/2026, 6:10:03 PM\\n\\n## Travel Administration Lead · Travel Administration Lead\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:13 PM\\n\\nHello, thank you for your time.\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:13 PM\\n\\nI coordinate travel reimbursements at Alderbridge. Much of my time goes into checking evidence, chasing reviews, and finding out what Finance actually paid, especially when a claim changes. I would like help making the whole process repeatable. You can ask me about how we work, policy, the records we use, or the problems that keep coming back.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:14 PM\\n\\nWhat policies?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:14 PM\\n\\nWe follow policy POL-2026.2, which governs how expenses are reviewed and reimbursed. It outlines separate requirements for international permits and claims, specifies approval roles like the budget owner and supervisor, and sets limits on categories like lodging and meals. You can find all the details in the Travel reimbursement policy.\\n\\n- [Travel reimbursement policy](https://private-pecorino-70e.notion.site/REDACTED)\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:14 PM\\n\\nWhich part of the reimbursement workflow would you like to explore next?\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:14 PM\\n\\nAre those all the policies?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:14 PM\\n\\nYes, policy POL-2026.2 is our primary reimbursement guide for 2026. It covers all the rules regarding approvals, expense categories and limits. Are there any specific categories you had in mind?\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:15 PM\\n\\nI want to know what happens when there are exceptions to the policies.\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:15 PM\\n\\nWhen there are exceptions, like for late filings or specific amount limits, we need a Finance exception. This official exception is issued by Finance for a specific claim version to resolve a set issue, like late filing or an unapproved permit. However, it doesn't waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:15 PM\\n\\nWhen you say Finance, is that a department?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:15 PM\\n\\nYes, Finance refers to our financial department. They are responsible for issuing monetary tables like currency rates and spending caps, providing official exceptions for policy issues, and handling actual payment execution and reconciliation for claims.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:16 PM\\n\\nI want to make sure I understand this.\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\\n\\nI'm happy to go over\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:16 PM\\n\\nThe financial department holds the sole authority to issue official exceptions for policy discrepancies. on a specific claim version. They cannot waive a missing evidence such as receipts or proof of payment.\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\\n\\nThat is correct. They are responsible for issuing official exceptions for specific issues on a claim version, but they cannot waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:16 PM\\n\\nWhere are receipts or a proof of payment stored?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\\n\\nReceipts are stored in the Receipt binder, while proof of payment, such as settled merchant transactions, is found in the Merchant payments tab of the Travel registers workbook.\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:16 PM\\n\\nWhich part of the work would you like to explore next?\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:17 PM\\n\\nDo receipts ever get destroyed or lost?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:17 PM\\n\\nIf a receipt is lost, the employee must provide alternative evidence or an explanation, but since Finance cannot waive missing receipts, the claim will remain unresolved until the evidence is provided.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:17 PM\\n\\nIs the Travel registers workbook a physical workbook or online?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:17 PM\\n\\nThe Travel registers workbook is an online spreadsheet that we use to track merchant payments and other financial activities.\\n\\n- [Travel registers](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:17 PM\\n\\nWhich part of the workflow would you like to discuss next?\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:18 PM\\n\\nWhat are the financial activities?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:18 PM\\n\\nFinancial activities include the pending, failed, or settled outcomes of payment requests, as well as accepted commitments, adjustments, refunds, and cancellations. These are all tracked and owned by the Finance department.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:18 PM\\n\\nTell me more about cancellations.\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:18 PM\\n\\nCancellations can target an entire trip or just a permit version independently of a claim. They must be initiated by the employee and confirmed by the supervisor, and these actions are tracked in the Travel cancellations workbook. If there were paid costs or Finance commitments, Finance will need to issue a specific disposition and resolve the money separately.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:19 PM\\n\\nHow would they resolve the disposition?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:19 PM\\n\\nFinance will issue a specific disposition bound to the cancellation ID, which confirms the reimbursement eligibility and provides a new allowed amount and reason for the affected costs.\\n\\n- [Travel cancellations](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:19 PM\\n\\nIs there a limit to the allowed amount?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:19 PM\\n\\nYes, limits apply to specific categories. Lodging and meals are limited by daily or nightly caps set by Finance, based on the destination and date, which are then multiplied by the documented duration. Transport and conference expenses are not subject to these caps.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:19 PM\\n\\nHow is the lodging and meals determined? Like what pricing metrics?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:19 PM\\n\\nThe limits for lodging and meals are determined by daily or nightly caps set by Finance, based on your destination, expense currency, and the payment date. You can see these metrics in the Caps tab of the Travel registers workbook.\\n\\n- [Travel registers workbook](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:20 PM\\n\\nWhich part of the workflow would you like to discuss next?\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:20 PM\\n\\nHow do incomplete claims affect independent work?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:20 PM\\n\\nIncomplete claims are held while the missing facts are addressed. You can continue processing independent claims separately while others are held, as long as the business impact is made clear.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:20 PM\\n\\nWhen you say made clear, what types of data do you mean?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:20 PM\\n\\nWe need to identify the exact claim version, specify which facts are missing, name the owner responsible for supplying them, and outline the next action to resolve the issue.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:21 PM\\n\\nWhat actions do you have to choose from to resolve the issue?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:21 PM\\n\\nThe available actions include requesting missing evidence from the employee, seeking an official exception from Finance for specific issues, or holding the claim until Finance confirms the resolution or provides the missing definitions.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:21 PM\\n\\nOn average, how long does it take Finance to confirm resolution or provide the missing definitions?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:21 PM\\n\\nI don't have a set average for Finance response times. Their replies come in batches, and the time it takes depends on the volume and complexity of the request.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:21 PM\\n\\nWhen was the most recent time a Finance needed to confirm resolution that you can remember?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:21 PM\\n\\nI don't track specific dates for those resolutions in my head. Our Finance replies are delivered in versioned batches, and we process the needed resolutions as they arrive based on the specific claims and costs.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:22 PM\\n\\nHow many people are in a batch?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:22 PM\\n\\nThe batch size isn't fixed; it depends on the number of claims, requests, or reviewer replies being processed by Finance or the relevant budget owner at that time.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:22 PM\\n\\nHow are batches organized? For example, could they be organized by a time slot or with a certain amount of people inside?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:22 PM\\n\\nBatches aren't organized by fixed time slots or a specific number of people. They are versioned delivery packets supplied by the trainer based on the number of claims, requests, and reviewer replies processed and ready at that moment.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:22 PM\\n\\nHow are they assigned to a trainer?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:22 PM\\n\\nI don't assign claims to a trainer. The replies you see come from versioned batches provided by Finance or other appropriate reviewers based on the business workflow.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:23 PM\\n\\nHow many trainers are there?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:23 PM\\n\\nI don't have information about trainers. My work focuses on coordinating with the Finance department, budget owners, supervisors, and employees to process travel claims.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:23 PM\\n\\nWhat are the boundaries for trainers, meaning what can and can't they do in this?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:23 PM\\n\\nI don't have information about trainers. My role is Travel Administration Lead, and the replies I receive come from Finance, budget owners, supervisors, and directors within the established business workflow.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:23 PM\\n\\nTell me about the boundaries of Finance.\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:23 PM\\n\\nFinance owns setting currency rates, managing spending caps, and issuing official policy exceptions. They also execute payments and resolve any monetary issues or cancellations, but they cannot waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:24 PM\\n\\nTell me about the boundaries of budget owners.\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:24 PM\\n\\nBudget owners have the authority to approve, return, or reject a claim based on the complete department ledger. They assess funding availability and make discretionary decisions, which I receive in supplied reviewer replies.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:24 PM\\n\\nTell me about a discretionary decision.\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:24 PM\\n\\nA discretionary decision is when the budget owner evaluates the department ledger and funding availability to decide whether to approve, return, or reject a claim. These judgments come directly from the budget owner's assessment and arrive in supplied reviewer replies.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:24 PM\\n\\nTell me about the boundaries of supervisors.\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:24 PM\\n\\nSupervisors evaluate the business purpose of the trip, client commitment, schedule coverage, and permit consistency before providing their review reply. They also confirm travel cancellations initiated by the trip employee.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:25 PM\\n\\nTell me about the boundaries of directors.\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:25 PM\\n\\nDirectors provide an additional layer of authorization for high-spend situations, typically when the reviewed claim entitlement or permit estimate exceeds EUR 1,000.00. They evaluate the business necessity, exceptions, and alternatives, and their decisions arrive in supplied reply batches.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:26 PM\\n\\nWhich work to revalidate after material corrections is the norm?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:26 PM\\n\\nThe policy requires a full or justified recheck of all affected dependencies, including calculations and approvals, when material changes are made. Even if the total amount remains the same, any change in evidence or facts invalidates prior readiness, so a fresh review is required.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:26 PM\\n\\nWhat are the financial completion conditions?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:26 PM\\n\\nFinancial completion requires that current approvals match the reviewed entitlement, net confirmed payments equal the authorized amount, no issues remain, and all required Finance resolutions have been received.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:27 PM\\n\\nWho owns the entitlement?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:27 PM\\n\\nI calculate the reviewed entitlement based on policy, evidence, and spending caps, but the budget owner owns the discretionary decision to fund or approve the specific claim amount.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:27 PM\\n\\nWhat is the delivery scope that is accept? After inspecting the actual result.\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:27 PM\\n\\nThe accepted delivery scope is confirmed when the current approvals and reviewed entitlement agree with the net confirmed payment, and all required Finance resolutions have been received with no remaining issues.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:28 PM\\n\\nWhen you say issues, and what are the constraints for the repair work?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:28 PM\\n\\nIssues refer to unresolved problems like missing receipts, incomplete payment proof, late filings, or mismatched data. For repair work, constraints involve organizing the missing evidence into usable local tasks, retaining the subject and revision, identifying the responsible owner, and ensuring corrections go through required reviews.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:28 PM\\n\\nHow do you organize the repair work in partial response constraints?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:28 PM\\n\\nYou can organize repair work either by per-claim packages or by grouping all missing-evidence items by the specific person responsible for supplying them. The key constraint is to retain each item's subject, revision, missing fact, and owner for tracking.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:28 PM\\n\\nWhat's the best way to adopt these constraints before they guide the work?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:28 PM\\n\\nYou can choose between per-claim packages or grouping items by the person responsible, provided you clearly track the subject, revision, missing fact, and owner for every single item.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:29 PM\\n\\nWhich one of those is the most difficult to maintain?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:29 PM\\n\\nBoth approaches have trade-offs; per-claim packages require less cross-referencing but result in more packages, whereas grouping by the person reduces the number of units but requires item-level matching and careful partial completion tracking.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:30 PM\\n\\nCan cases remain unresolved when the facts require it?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:30 PM\\n\\nYes, cases can be placed on hold for missing facts or Finance resolutions, but they cannot be closed or considered complete until all required evidence and decisions are obtained.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:30 PM\\n\\nWhat type of report will affect the work, reason, responsible person, and evidence needed to resume?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:30 PM\\n\\nYou can use any format, such as a per-claim package or a grouped task list, as long as it consistently retains the specific claim version, the missing evidence or fact, the responsible owner, and the next action required to resume.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:31 PM\\n\\nWhat happens if inaccessible required sources must be erased with the lead facilitator rather than otherwise unknown?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:31 PM\\n\\nAs the Travel Administration Lead, I cannot invent or bypass required sources. If a required document or definition is inaccessible and cannot be obtained, it remains an unresolved issue that I must escalate to the exercise operator for guidance.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:31 PM\\n\\nHow long does that process take?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:31 PM\\n\\nThere is no set timeframe for how long the exercise operator takes to resolve an escalation, as it depends on the nature of the issue in the specific case.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:31 PM\\n\\nHow do you communicate?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:31 PM\\n\\nI communicate through formal requests and notifications. These include the subject type, IDs, stable role requesters, and relevant source versions, and I wait for replies from the authorized reviewers and Finance.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:33 PM\\n\\nLet me summarize to make sure I understand: the system route work based on four distinct human authority profiles: supervisors, budget owners, directors, and Finance.\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:33 PM\\n\\nThat is correct. I coordinate the process by submitting requests for these different authorities and waiting for their determinations and resolutions to ensure claims are processed accurately and policy checks are met.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:38 PM\\n\\nHello, thank you for talking with me.\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:38 PM\\n\\nHello! I coordinate travel reimbursements at Alderbridge. Much of my time goes into checking evidence, chasing reviews, and finding out what Finance actually paid, especially when a claim changes. You can ask me about how we work, our policy, the records we use, or the problems that keep coming back.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:38 PM\\n\\nCan you give me a the ordinary claim life cycle?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:38 PM\\n\\nThe ordinary cycle begins when an employee pays for a travel cost and submits a claim. I review the claim against the trip permits, receipts, and merchant payments to calculate the reviewed entitlement. Then, I coordinate the necessary approvals based on the amount and policy, submit the request to Finance for transfer, and reconcile the payments until the case is closed.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:39 PM\\n\\nWhat specific matching keys do you use to connect the submitted expense claims to its corresponding trip permit?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:39 PM\\n\\nI connect claims to trip permits using the employee's identity, the exact trip ID, and the specific trip revision number to ensure everything matches the approved travel records.\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:39 PM\\n\\nI connect claims to trip permits using the employee's identity, the exact trip ID, and the specific trip revision number to ensure everything matches the approved travel records.\\n\\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:40 PM\\n\\nWhen you submit the request to Finance for transfer. what type of files or formats do you submit?\\n\\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:40 PM\\n\\nI submit an identifiable request c…13857 tokens truncated…ferences trip {trip_id} revision {trip_revision}, which is not present in the retained trip register\\\",\\n                owner=\\\"Travel Administration Lead\\\", next_action=\\\"verify the trip revision from an accessible native travel register\\\",\\n                run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\\n            )\\n            schema_issues.append(_issue_from_item(domain[\\\"repair_queue\\\"][\\\"items\\\"][item_id]))\\n        matches = [row for row in domain[\\\"decision_history\\\"]\\n                   if row.get(\\\"subject_type\\\") == \\\"claim\\\" and row.get(\\\"subject_id\\\") == claim_id\\n                   and row.get(\\\"revision\\\") == revision and row.get(\\\"structural_match\\\") == \\\"revision_match_current\\\"]\\n        finance = finance_results[claim_id]\\n        snapshot_claims.append({\\n            \\\"claim_id\\\": claim_id,\\n            \\\"revision\\\": revision,\\n            \\\"trip_id\\\": str(trip_id),\\n            \\\"trip_revision\\\": trip_revision,\\n            \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\",\\n            \\\"lines\\\": [],\\n            \\\"allowed_cents\\\": None,\\n            \\\"paid_cents\\\": finance[\\\"net_confirmed_cents\\\"],\\n            \\\"balance_cents\\\": finance[\\\"balance_cents\\\"],\\n            \\\"decision_ids\\\": list(dict.fromkeys(row[\\\"decision_id\\\"] for row in matches if row.get(\\\"decision_id\\\"))),\\n            \\\"next_owner\\\": \\\"Travel Administration Lead\\\",\\n            \\\"reason\\\": \\\"Structural integration only; reimbursement policy and current-revision compliance remain unresolved.\\\",\\n        })\\n\\n    schema_issues.extend(projection_issues)\\n    schema_issues.extend(domain.get(\\\"projection_issues\\\", []))\\n    # Deduplicate by record_id while preserving issue order.\\n    unique_issues = {}\\n    for issue in schema_issues:\\n        unique_issues.setdefault(issue[\\\"record_id\\\"], issue)\\n    schema_issues = list(unique_issues.values())\\n\\n    finance_ids = []\\n    unresolved_ids = set()\\n    conflicting_ids = set()\\n    for result in finance_results.values():\\n        unresolved_ids.update(result[\\\"unresolved_event_ids\\\"])\\n        conflicting_ids.update(issue[\\\"event_id\\\"] for issue in result[\\\"conflicting_events\\\"])\\n        for event in result[\\\"event_history\\\"]:\\n            event_id = event[\\\"event_id\\\"]\\n            if (event_id and event_id not in unresolved_ids and event_id not in conflicting_ids\\n                    and event[\\\"classification\\\"] not in {\\\"unresolved\\\", \\\"conflicting_event_id\\\", \\\"missing_event_id\\\"}):\\n                finance_ids.append(event_id)\\n    finance_ids = list(dict.fromkeys(event_id for event_id in finance_ids if event_id not in unresolved_ids | conflicting_ids))\\n\\n    snapshot = {\\n        \\\"schema_version\\\": \\\"travel-claim-snapshot/2\\\",\\n        \\\"run_id\\\": run_id,\\n        \\\"batch_id\\\": batch_id,\\n        \\\"predecessor\\\": deepcopy(predecessor),\\n        \\\"source_binding\\\": deepcopy(source_binding),\\n        \\\"claims\\\": snapshot_claims,\\n        \\\"requests\\\": [],\\n        \\\"travel_cancellations\\\": cancellation_rows,\\n        \\\"admitted_event_ids\\\": finance_ids,\\n        \\\"issues\\\": schema_issues,\\n    }\\n    domain[\\\"processed_batches\\\"] = list(domain[\\\"processed_batches\\\"])\\n    return {\\n        \\\"snapshot\\\": snapshot,\\n        \\\"domain\\\": domain,\\n        \\\"decision_history\\\": deepcopy(domain[\\\"decision_history\\\"]),\\n        \\\"finance_reconciliations\\\": deepcopy(finance_results),\\n        \\\"revision_history\\\": deepcopy(history),\\n        \\\"repair_queue_by_owner\\\": _owner_view(domain[\\\"repair_queue\\\"]),\\n        \\\"batch_delta_counts\\\": {key: len(value) for key, value in delta.items()},\\n        \\\"input_sha256\\\": digest,\\n    }\\n\\n\\ndef _owner_view(queue: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]]:\\n    grouped: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = {}\\n    for item in queue[\\\"items\\\"].values():\\n        grouped.setdefault(item[\\\"owner\\\"], []).append(item)\\n    return {owner: sorted(items, key=lambda row: row[\\\"item_id\\\"]) for owner, items in sorted(grouped.items())}\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Source-traceable Finance reconciliation primitives.\\n\\nOnly explicit, source-classified settled and refund events affect confirmed\\ncash. Finance obligations remain separate from caller-supplied authorized\\nobligations. No policy entitlement or approval decision is made here.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom collections import defaultdict\\nfrom copy import deepcopy\\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\\nfrom typing import Any\\n\\n\\n_NATIVE_EVENT_CLASSES = {\\n    \\\"accepted\\\": \\\"obligation_accepted\\\",\\n    \\\"settled\\\": \\\"confirmed_payment\\\",\\n    \\\"refund\\\": \\\"confirmed_refund\\\",\\n    \\\"failed\\\": \\\"failed_transfer\\\",\\n    \\\"retry_authorized\\\": \\\"retry_authorization\\\",\\n    \\\"cancellation_requested\\\": \\\"finance_cancellation_requested\\\",\\n    \\\"cancelled\\\": \\\"finance_cancelled\\\",\\n    # These are retained as non-cash Finance records; their amount describes\\n    # an obligation, not a payment.\\n    \\\"adjustment\\\": \\\"finance_adjustment\\\",\\n    \\\"resolution\\\": \\\"finance_resolution\\\",\\n}\\n\\n\\ndef _values(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    return {key: cell.get(\\\"value\\\") for key, cell in record.get(\\\"values\\\", {}).items()}\\n\\n\\ndef _source_ref(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    return {key: record.get(key) for key in (\\\"source_id\\\", \\\"source_sha256\\\", \\\"locator\\\")}\\n\\n\\ndef _cents(value: Any) -> int | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Convert exact EUR decimal input to integer cents; reject rounding.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if value is None or isinstance(value, bool):\\n        return None\\n    try:\\n        amount = Decimal(str(value))\\n    except (InvalidOperation, ValueError):\\n        return None\\n    if not amount.is_finite():\\n        return None\\n    scaled = amount * 100\\n    if scaled != scaled.to_integral_value() or scaled < 0:\\n        return None\\n    return int(scaled)\\n\\n\\ndef _payload(values: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    return {key: values[key] for key in sorted(values) if key != \\\"Arrival batch\\\"}\\n\\n\\ndef reconcile_finance_events(\\n    events: list[dict[str, Any]],\\n    *,\\n    claim_id: str,\\n    current_revision: int,\\n    authorized_obligation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\\n    revision_history: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None,\\n    previous_reconciliation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\\n    owner: str = \\\"Finance\\\",\\n    source_classifications: dict[str, str] | None = None,\\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Reconcile source events for a claim without making policy decisions.\\n\\n    `authorized_obligation` is an independent, already-authorized input of\\n    `{amount_cents, claim_revision, source_refs}`. This function neither\\n    derives nor authorizes it. `source_classifications` may extend the native\\n    workbook vocabulary when a retained source defines another event type;\\n    unrecognized types otherwise remain unresolved.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if not claim_id or isinstance(current_revision, bool) or not isinstance(current_revision, int) or current_revision < 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"claim_id and a positive current_revision are required\\\")\\n    if not owner:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"owner is required for reconciliation issues\\\")\\n\\n    classes = dict(_NATIVE_EVENT_CLASSES)\\n    if source_classifications:\\n        allowed_classes = {\\n            \\\"confirmed_payment\\\", \\\"confirmed_refund\\\", \\\"pending_transfer\\\",\\n            \\\"obligation_accepted\\\", \\\"failed_transfer\\\", \\\"retry_authorization\\\",\\n            \\\"finance_cancellation_requested\\\", \\\"finance_cancelled\\\",\\n            \\\"finance_adjustment\\\", \\\"finance_resolution\\\",\\n        }\\n        for event_type, classification in source_classifications.items():\\n            if not isinstance(event_type, str) or classification not in allowed_classes:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"unsupported source event classification: {event_type!r} -> {classification!r}\\\")\\n            classes[event_type] = classification\\n\\n    by_id: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\\n    missing_id_records: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\\n    for record in events:\\n        event_id = _values(record).get(\\\"Activity reference\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(event_id, str) or not event_id:\\n            if _values(record).get(\\\"Claim reference\\\") == claim_id:\\n                missing_id_records.append(record)\\n        else:\\n            by_id[event_id].append(record)\\n\\n    relevant_occurrences: list[tuple[str | None, dict[str, Any], dict[str, Any], bool]] = []\\n    duplicate_events = []\\n    conflicting_events = []\\n    for event_id, occurrences in by_id.items():\\n        relevant = [record for record in occurrences if _values(record).get(\\\"Claim reference\\\") == claim_id]\\n        if not relevant:\\n            continue\\n        payloads = [_payload(_values(record)) for record in occurrences]\\n        conflict = any(payload != payloads[0] for payload in payloads[1:])\\n        for record in relevant:\\n            relevant_occurrences.append((event_id, record, _values(record), conflict))\\n        if conflict:\\n            conflicting_events.append({\\n                \\\"event_id\\\": event_id,\\n                \\\"source_refs\\\": [_source_ref(record) for record in occurrences],\\n                \\\"payloads\\\": payloads,\\n            })\\n        elif len(occurrences) > 1:\\n            duplicate_events.append({\\n                \\\"event_id\\\": event_id,\\n                \\\"source_refs\\\": [_source_ref(record) for record in occurrences],\\n                \\\"delivery_batches\\\": [_values(record).get(\\\"Arrival batch\\\") for record in occurrences],\\n            })\\n    relevant_occurrences.extend((None, record, _values(record), True) for record in missing_id_records)\\n    relevant_occurrences.sort(key=lambda row: (\\n        str(row[2].get(\\\"Arrival batch\\\") or \\\"\\\"),\\n        int(row[1].get(\\\"row\\\") or 0),\\n        row[0] or \\\"\\\",\\n    ))\\n\\n    history = []\\n    event_issue_by_id: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}\\n    typed = []\\n    unresolved = []\\n    for event_id, record, values, conflict in relevant_occurrences:\\n        event_type = values.get(\\\"Activity type\\\")\\n        classification = classes.get(event_type, \\\"unresolved\\\")\\n        item = {\\n            \\\"event_id\\\": event_id,\\n            \\\"source_ref\\\": _source_ref(record),\\n            \\\"source_record\\\": deepcopy(values),\\n            \\\"event_type\\\": event_type,\\n            \\\"classification\\\": (\\n                \\\"conflicting_event_id\\\" if conflict and event_id else\\n                \\\"missing_event_id\\\" if conflict else classification\\n            ),\\n            \\\"amount_cents\\\": _cents(values.get(\\\"Amount (EUR)\\\")),\\n            \\\"obligation_cents\\\": _cents(values.get(\\\"Obligation (EUR)\\\")),\\n            \\\"currency\\\": values.get(\\\"Currency\\\"),\\n            \\\"original_activity_id\\\": values.get(\\\"Original activity reference\\\"),\\n        }\\n        history.append(item)\\n        if conflict:\\n            if event_id:\\n                event_issue_by_id[event_id] = {\\n                    \\\"record_id\\\": f\\\"finance-event-conflict:{event_id}\\\",\\n                    \\\"event_id\\\": event_id,\\n                    \\\"subject_type\\\": \\\"claim\\\",\\n                    \\\"subject_id\\\": claim_id,\\n                    \\\"revision\\\": current_revision,\\n                    \\\"missing_or_return_reason\\\": \\\"same Finance event ID has conflicting source content; none of its occurrences were counted\\\",\\n                    \\\"source_refs\\\": [_source_ref(row) for row in by_id[event_id]],\\n                    \\\"owner\\\": owner,\\n                    \\\"next_action\\\": \\\"Finance to resolve the source record conflict\\\",\\n                }\\n            else:\\n                event_issue_by_id[f\\\"missing:{record.get('locator')}\\\"] = {\\n                    \\\"record_id\\\": f\\\"finance-event-missing-id:{record.get('row') or len(event_issue_by_id) + 1}\\\",\\n                    \\\"event_id\\\": None,\\n                    \\\"subject_type\\\": \\\"claim\\\",\\n                    \\\"subject_id\\\": claim_id,\\n                    \\\"revision\\\": current_revision,\\n                    \\\"missing_or_return_reason\\\": \\\"Finance event has no activity reference and cannot be safely deduplicated or counted\\\",\\n                    \\\"source_refs\\\": [_source_ref(record)],\\n                    \\\"owner\\\": owner,\\n                    \\\"next_action\\\": \\\"Finance to identify this ledger event and provide its native activity reference\\\",\\n                }\\n            continue\\n        if classification == \\\"unresolved\\\":\\n            unresolved.append(item)\\n            continue\\n        if classification in {\\\"confirmed_payment\\\", \\\"confirmed_refund\\\"}:\\n            if values.get(\\\"Currency\\\") != \\\"EUR\\\" or item[\\\"amount_cents\\\"] is None:\\n                unresolved.append(item)\\n                continue\\n        typed.append(item)\\n\\n    payments = {item[\\\"event_id\\\"]: item for item in typed if item[\\\"classification\\\"] == \\\"confirmed_payment\\\"}\\n    confirmed_refunds: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\\n    refund_candidates = [item for item in typed if item[\\\"classification\\\"] == \\\"confirmed_refund\\\"]\\n    refund_groups: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\\n    for item in refund_candidates:\\n        original_id = item[\\\"original_activity_id\\\"]\\n        original = payments.get(original_id) if isinstance(original_id, str) else None\\n        if original is None or original.get(\\\"currency\\\") != item.get(\\\"currency\\\"):\\n            unresolved.append(item)\\n            continue\\n        refund_groups[original_id].append(item)\\n    for original_id, refunds in refund_groups.items():\\n        original = payments[original_id]\\n        refund_total = sum(item[\\\"amount_cents\\\"] for item in refunds)\\n        if refund_total > original[\\\"amount_cents\\\"]:\\n            unresolved.extend(refunds)\\n            continue\\n        confirmed_refunds.extend(refunds)\\n\\n    invalid_payments = [item for item in payments.values() if item[\\\"amount_cents\\\"] is None]\\n    unresolved.extend(invalid_payments)\\n    confirmed_payment_cents = sum(item[\\\"amount_cents\\\"] for item in payments.values() if item[\\\"amount_cents\\\"] is not None)\\n    confirmed_refund_cents = sum(item[\\\"amount_cents\\\"] for item in confirmed_refunds)\\n    net_confirmed_cents = confirmed_payment_cents - confirmed_refund_cents\\n\\n    issues = list(event_issue_by_id.values())\\n    for number, item in enumerate(unresolved, 1):\\n        issue_id = f\\\"finance-unresolved:{item['event_id'] or number}\\\"\\n        issue = {\\n            \\\"record_id\\\": issue_id,\\n            \\\"event_id\\\": item[\\\"event_id\\\"],\\n            \\\"subject_type\\\": \\\"claim\\\",\\n            \\\"subject_id\\\": claim_id,\\n            \\\"revision\\\": current_revision,\\n            \\\"source_refs\\\": [item[\\\"source_ref\\\"]],\\n            \\\"missing_or_return_reason\\\": (\\n                f\\\"Finance event {item['event_id']!r} is not sufficiently classified or linked for cash reconciliation\\\"\\n            ),\\n            \\\"owner\\\": owner,\\n            \\\"next_action\\\": \\\"Finance to confirm event meaning, amount, currency, or refund link from the native ledger\\\",\\n        }\\n        issues.append(issue)\\n    issues_by_owner: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\\n    for issue in issues:\\n        issues_by_owner[issue[\\\"owner\\\"]].append(issue)\\n    issues_by_owner = {key: sorted(value, key=lambda row: row[\\\"record_id\\\"]) for key, value in sorted(issues_by_owner.items())}\\n\\n    obligation = None\\n    obligation_issue = None\\n    if authorized_obligation is not None:\\n        amount = authorized_obligation.get(\\\"amount_cents\\\")\\n        obligation_revision = authorized_obligation.get(\\\"claim_revision\\\")\\n        refs = authorized_obligation.get(\\\"source_refs\\\")\\n        if (isinstance(amount, int) and not isinstance(amount, bool) and amount >= 0\\n                and obligation_revision == current_revision and isinstance(refs, list)\\n                and refs and all(isinstance(ref, str) and ref for ref in refs)):\\n            obligation = {\\\"amount_cents\\\": amount, \\\"claim_revision\\\": obligation_revision, \\\"source_refs\\\": list(dict.fromkeys(refs))}\\n        else:\\n            obligation_issue = {\\n                \\\"record_id\\\": f\\\"finance-obligation-invalid:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\\\",\\n                \\\"event_id\\\": None,\\n                \\\"subject_type\\\": \\\"claim\\\",\\n                \\\"subject_id\\\": claim_id,\\n                \\\"revision\\\": current_revision,\\n                \\\"source_refs\\\": list(refs) if isinstance(refs, list) else [],\\n                \\\"missing_or_return_reason\\\": \\\"authorized obligation is missing exact cents, current-revision match, or supporting source reference\\\",\\n                \\\"owner\\\": owner,\\n                \\\"next_action\\\": \\\"Finance to provide or confirm the authorized obligation for this claim revision\\\",\\n            }\\n    else:\\n        obligation_issue = {\\n            \\\"record_id\\\": f\\\"finance-obligation-missing:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\\\",\\n            \\\"event_id\\\": None,\\n            \\\"subject_type\\\": \\\"claim\\\",\\n            \\\"subject_id\\\": claim_id,\\n            \\\"revision\\\": current_revision,\\n            \\\"source_refs\\\": [],\\n            \\\"missing_or_return_reason\\\": \\\"no supported authorized obligation was supplied for this claim revision\\\",\\n            \\\"owner\\\": owner,\\n            \\\"next_action\\\": \\\"Finance to provide or confirm the authorized obligation for this claim revision\\\",\\n        }\\n    if obligation_issue is not None:\\n        issues.append(obligation_issue)\\n        issues_by_owner.setdefault(owner, []).append(obligation_issue)\\n        issues_by_owner[owner].sort(key=lambda row: row[\\\"record_id\\\"])\\n\\n    has_unclassified_cash_event = any(item[\\\"classification\\\"] == \\\"unresolved\\\" for item in history)\\n    event_set_complete = not unresolved and not conflicting_events and not missing_id_records and not has_unclassified_cash_event\\n    balance = None\\n    if obligation is not None and event_set_complete:\\n        balance = obligation[\\\"amount_cents\\\"] - net_confirmed_cents\\n\\n    invalidated = None\\n    if previous_reconciliation is not None:\\n        previous_revision = previous_reconciliation.get(\\\"claim_revision\\\")\\n        if previous_revision != current_revision:\\n            invalidated = {\\n                \\\"claim_revision\\\": previous_revision,\\n                \\\"reason\\\": \\\"material revision change invalidates the prior reconciliation basis\\\",\\n                \\\"prior_net_confirmed_cents\\\": previous_reconciliation.get(\\\"net_confirmed_cents\\\"),\\n                \\\"prior_balance_cents\\\": previous_reconciliation.get(\\\"balance_cents\\\"),\\n            }\\n    return {\\n        \\\"claim_id\\\": claim_id,\\n        \\\"claim_revision\\\": current_revision,\\n        \\\"revision_history\\\": deepcopy(revision_history or []),\\n        \\\"event_history\\\": history,\\n        \\\"event_ids\\\": [item[\\\"event_id\\\"] for item in history if item[\\\"event_id\\\"] is not None],\\n        \\\"duplicate_events\\\": duplicate_events,\\n        \\\"conflicting_events\\\": conflicting_events,\\n        \\\"confirmed_payment_event_ids\\\": [item[\\\"event_id\\\"] for item in payments.values() if item[\\\"amount_cents\\\"] is not None],\\n        \\\"confirmed_refund_event_ids\\\": [item[\\\"event_id\\\"] for item in confirmed_refunds],\\n        \\\"pending_transfer_event_ids\\\": [item[\\\"event_id\\\"] for item in typed if item[\\\"classification\\\"] == \\\"pending_transfer\\\"],\\n        \\\"unresolved_event_ids\\\": list(dict.fromkeys(item[\\\"event_id\\\"] for item in unresolved if item[\\\"event_id\\\"] is not None)),\\n        \\\"finance_obligation_events\\\": [item for item in history if item[\\\"classification\\\"] == \\\"obligation_accepted\\\"],\\n        \\\"authorized_obligation\\\": obligation,\\n        \\\"confirmed_payment_cents\\\": confirmed_payment_cents,\\n        \\\"confirmed_refund_cents\\\": confirmed_refund_cents,\\n        \\\"net_confirmed_cents\\\": net_confirmed_cents,\\n        \\\"balance_cents\\\": balance,\\n        \\\"inputs_complete\\\": balance is not None,\\n        \\\"repair_issues\\\": issues,\\n        \\\"repair_issues_by_owner\\\": issues_by_owner,\\n        \\\"invalidated_previous_reconciliation\\\": invalidated,\\n    }\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a13bf2-628b-75c2-a43b-f19b5878b298","create_time":1792007122.4797883}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
