{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T19:59:29.914Z","ordinal":754,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a13bd1-7420-72c0-963e-58742d1be7bf","turn_id":"01a13bff-6c35-74c3-badb-76002d27261c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-fca715f2-8476-44e2-a9b8-8a53b67b6272","process_id":"27703","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","git status --short; git diff --cached; git diff -- README.md snapshot.schema.json src/travel_claim/finance.py src/travel_claim/integration.py src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py; cat tests/test_retained_finance.py; git branch --show-current; git log -1 --oneline; cat .git/hooks/prepare-commit-msg .git/hooks/post-commit .git/hooks/pre-push"],"cwd":"file:///home/maxg/travel-expense-claim","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short; git diff --cached; git diff -- README.md snapshot.schema.json src/travel_claim/finance.py src/travel_claim/integration.py src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py; cat tests/test_retained_finance.py; git branch --show-current; git log -1 --oneline; cat .git/hooks/prepare-commit-msg .git/hooks/post-commit .git/hooks/pre-push"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":" M README.md\n M snapshot.schema.json\n M src/travel_claim/finance.py\n M src/travel_claim/integration.py\n M src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\n?? artifacts/runs/\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-evidence-audit-f98e044.md\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91-validated/\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/\n?? tests/fixtures/\n?? tests/test_retained_finance.py\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 10bd03c..b844ea2 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -81,6 +81,28 @@ travel-claim validate-snapshot artifacts/runs/<run-id>/batches/<batch-id>.json\n \n `verify-batch` also checks the source-manifest bytes, predecessor bytes, and cancellation-to-issue references. Do not overwrite a sealed snapshot; create a new run with a documented link if later processing changes its content.\n \n+## Recorded Finance obligations\n+\n+Offline replay connects Finance ledger observations to claim IDs and request IDs, retaining event IDs, arrival deliveries, source cells, and obligation history. The retained `Finance activity` headers mean:\n+\n+| Retained field | Interpretation used by replay |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Activity reference | Immutable event identity; identical redeliveries count once. |\n+| Arrival batch | Delivery membership, separate from business event time. |\n+| Activity type | Recorded event vocabulary; accepted/adjustment/resolution carry obligation observations, while settled/refund carry confirmed cash. |\n+| Request reference / Claim reference | Explicit request and claim links; neither encodes an explicit revision. |\n+| Finance officer / Payee ID | Recorded officer and payee identities, not evidence that every required human approval is present. |\n+| Currency / Amount (EUR) | Currency and cash amount; only sufficiently supported EUR cash is reconciled. |\n+| Original activity reference | Refund linkage to the original confirmed payment. |\n+| Obligation (EUR) | Recorded commitment amount; observations are not summed as additional cash or assumed reimbursement entitlement. |\n+| Reason / Activity time (UTC) | Retained description and UTC event time; neither establishes a scenario case clock. |\n+\n+The interview's acceptance description is retained at `interviews/project-d-travel-expense-claim-20261013-2210.md:425`; native headers and examples are retained in `Finance activity`, row 5 and rows 23–25/33. Native Finance rows have no claim-revision column. Replay therefore records the source-observed revision context at **first delivery**, leaving the explicit revision null. Redelivery never rebinds an old event to a corrected revision. An explicit `Claim revision` field, if supplied in source records, is checked against retained revision history.\n+\n+The sidecar and optional claim `finance_evidence` projection expose recorded obligation history and `recorded_ledger_balance_cents` (recorded obligation minus confirmed net cash for the same request/payee). Adjustments/resolutions record amounts, not additive payment events. Unknown ordering, conflicting events, missing links, or undefined reversal semantics leave the affected ledger difference unresolved. Transfer cancellation does not itself erase the obligation or reverse cash. Corrections preserve historical cash/commitments and reopen revision-dependent review; unrelated claim evidence remains intact.\n+\n+This ledger arithmetic is separate from current-revision authorization and reviewed entitlement. Without separately supported authorization, `allowed_cents` and `balance_cents` remain null/blank and claims remain pending. A zero ledger difference does not establish policy eligibility, complete approvals, or closure. The exact CSV header is unchanged; `report.md` explains recorded financial facts separately from unresolved repairs and external blockers.\n+\n ## Submission-readiness validation\n \n ```bash\ndiff --git a/snapshot.schema.json b/snapshot.schema.json\nindex dc3067d..e240461 100644\n--- a/snapshot.schema.json\n+++ b/snapshot.schema.json\n@@ -193,6 +193,40 @@\n             \"type\": \"integer\",\n             \"minimum\": 1,\n             \"description\": \"Exact trip revision from the supplied trip source, independent of claim revision.\"\n+          },\n+          \"finance_evidence\": {\n+            \"type\": \"object\",\n+            \"required\": [\n+              \"recorded_obligation\",\n+              \"recorded_ledger_balance_cents\",\n+              \"basis\",\n+              \"current_revision_authority_confirmed\",\n+              \"closure_authority_confirmed\"\n+            ],\n+            \"properties\": {\n+              \"recorded_obligation\": {\n+                \"type\": [\n+                  \"object\",\n+                  \"null\"\n+                ]\n+              },\n+              \"recorded_ledger_balance_cents\": {\n+                \"type\": [\n+                  \"integer\",\n+                  \"null\"\n+                ]\n+              },\n+              \"basis\": {\n+                \"type\": \"string\",\n+                \"minLength\": 1\n+              },\n+              \"current_revision_authority_confirmed\": {\n+                \"const\": false\n+              },\n+              \"closure_authority_confirmed\": {\n+                \"const\": false\n+              }\n+            }\n           }\n         }\n       }\ndiff --git a/src/travel_claim/finance.py b/src/travel_claim/finance.py\nindex de40f0d..24c444b 100644\n--- a/src/travel_claim/finance.py\n+++ b/src/travel_claim/finance.py\n@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ from __future__ import annotations\n from collections import defaultdict\n from copy import deepcopy\n from decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\n+from datetime import datetime\n from typing import Any\n \n \n@@ -56,6 +57,86 @@ def _payload(values: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n     return {key: values[key] for key in sorted(values) if key != \"Arrival batch\"}\n \n \n+def _reference_text(ref: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n+    return f\"{ref.get('source_id')}@{ref.get('source_sha256')}#{ref.get('locator')}\"\n+\n+\n+def _positive_integer(value: Any) -> int | None:\n+    try:\n+        return int(value) if not isinstance(value, bool) and int(value) > 0 and float(value) == int(value) else None\n+    except (ValueError, TypeError, OverflowError):\n+        return None\n+\n+\n+def _recorded_obligations(history: list[dict], *, claim_id: str, current_revision: int,\n+                          revisions: list[dict]) -> tuple[list[dict], dict | None, str | None]:\n+    \"\"\"Read ledger observations, without deriving reimbursement authorization.\n+\n+    Obligation (EUR) is a recorded amount, not a cash delta. Native rows omit\n+    claim revision; arrival context is retained separately from explicit links.\n+    Only the first delivery establishes context; redelivery cannot rebind it.\n+    \"\"\"\n+    groups: dict[str, list[dict]] = defaultdict(list)\n+    for event in history:\n+        if event['classification'] in {'obligation_accepted', 'finance_adjustment', 'finance_resolution'}:\n+            groups[event['event_id']].append(event)\n+    records = []\n+    problem = None\n+    for event_id, occurrences in groups.items():\n+        event = occurrences[0]\n+        values = event['source_record']\n+        batches = [e['source_record'].get('Arrival batch') for e in occurrences]\n+        first_batch = min((_positive_integer(b) for b in batches if _positive_integer(b)), default=None)\n+        context_rows = [r for r in revisions if first_batch is not None\n+                        and _positive_integer(r.get('arrival_batch')) is not None\n+                        and _positive_integer(r['arrival_batch']) <= first_batch]\n+        context = max((r['revision'] for r in context_rows), default=None)\n+        explicit = _positive_integer(values.get('Claim revision'))\n+        matches = [r for r in revisions if r['revision'] == explicit] if explicit else []\n+        link = ('explicit_current' if explicit == current_revision else 'explicit_historical') if matches else 'arrival_context_only' if context else 'unmatched'\n+        refs = [_reference_text(e['source_ref']) for e in occurrences]\n+        record = {\n+            'event_id': event_id, 'event_type': event['event_type'], 'claim_id': claim_id,\n+            'request_id': values.get('Request reference'), 'finance_officer': values.get('Finance officer'),\n+            'payee_id': values.get('Payee ID'), 'currency': event['currency'],\n+            'amount_cents': event['obligation_cents'], 'activity_time_utc': values.get('Activity time (UTC)'),\n+            'claim_revision': explicit if matches else None, 'arrival_revision_context': context,\n+            'revision_link_status': link, 'first_arrival_batch': first_batch,\n+            'delivery_batches': batches, 'source_refs': list(dict.fromkeys(refs)),\n+            'claim_source_refs': [deepcopy(r['source_ref']) for r in (matches or context_rows)\n+                                  if r['revision'] == (explicit if matches else context)],\n+        }\n+        records.append(record)\n+        if (event['currency'] != 'EUR' or event['obligation_cents'] is None or not first_batch\n+                or not all(isinstance(values.get(key), str) and values[key].strip()\n+                           for key in ('Request reference', 'Finance officer', 'Payee ID'))\n+                or not all(all(e['source_ref'].get(key) for key in ('source_id', 'source_sha256', 'locator')) for e in occurrences)\n+                or (values.get('Claim revision') is not None and not matches)):\n+            problem = 'Obligation record lacks supported amount, request/payee/officer, source identity, arrival, or explicit revision match'\n+    if not records:\n+        return [], None, None\n+    if len({(r['request_id'], r['payee_id'], r['currency']) for r in records}) != 1:\n+        problem = 'Multiple request/payee/currency ledgers cannot be combined as one obligation'\n+    # A single observation needs no ordering assumption. Multiple observations\n+    # require explicit UTC event times; arrival numbers do not define business time.\n+    if len(records) > 1:\n+        try:\n+            def stamp(record):\n+                dt = datetime.fromisoformat(record['activity_time_utc'].replace('Z', '+00:00'))\n+                # The retained header explicitly names UTC even when the cell\n+                # serialization omits an offset.\n+                if dt.utcoffset() is not None and dt.utcoffset().total_seconds() != 0:\n+                    raise ValueError('not UTC')\n+                return dt.replace(tzinfo=None)\n+            records.sort(key=lambda r: (stamp(r), r['event_id']))\n+            for left, right in zip(records, records[1:]):\n+                if stamp(left) == stamp(right) and left['amount_cents'] != right['amount_cents']:\n+                    problem = 'Conflicting obligation amounts have the same event time'\n+        except (ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):\n+            problem = 'Multiple obligation observations lack unambiguous UTC ordering'\n+    return records, deepcopy(records[-1]) if not problem else None, problem\n+\n+\n def reconcile_finance_events(\n     events: list[dict[str, Any]],\n     *,\n@@ -128,7 +209,7 @@ def reconcile_finance_events(\n             })\n     relevant_occurrences.extend((None, record, _values(record), True) for record in missing_id_records)\n     relevant_occurrences.sort(key=lambda row: (\n-        str(row[2].get(\"Arrival batch\") or \"\"),\n+        _positive_integer(row[2].get(\"Arrival batch\")) or 0,\n         int(row[1].get(\"row\") or 0),\n         row[0] or \"\",\n     ))\n@@ -192,7 +273,7 @@ def reconcile_finance_events(\n \n     payments = {item[\"event_id\"]: item for item in typed if item[\"classification\"] == \"confirmed_payment\"}\n     confirmed_refunds: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n-    refund_candidates = [item for item in typed if item[\"classification\"] == \"confirmed_refund\"]\n+    refund_candidates = list({item[\"event_id\"]: item for item in typed if item[\"classification\"] == \"confirmed_refund\"}.values())\n     refund_groups: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n     for item in refund_candidates:\n         original_id = item[\"original_activity_id\"]\n@@ -232,11 +313,17 @@ def reconcile_finance_events(\n             \"next_action\": \"Finance to confirm event meaning, amount, currency, or refund link from the native ledger\",\n         }\n         issues.append(issue)\n-    issues_by_owner: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n-    for issue in issues:\n-        issues_by_owner[issue[\"owner\"]].append(issue)\n-    issues_by_owner = {key: sorted(value, key=lambda row: row[\"record_id\"]) for key, value in sorted(issues_by_owner.items())}\n-\n+    obligation_history, recorded_obligation, recorded_problem = _recorded_obligations(\n+        history, claim_id=claim_id, current_revision=current_revision, revisions=revision_history or [],\n+    )\n+    if recorded_problem:\n+        issues.append({\n+            \"record_id\": f\"finance-recorded-obligation:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n+            \"subject_type\": \"claim\", \"subject_id\": claim_id, \"revision\": current_revision,\n+            \"source_refs\": [e[\"source_ref\"] for e in history if e[\"event_id\"] in {r[\"event_id\"] for r in obligation_history}],\n+            \"owner\": owner, \"missing_or_return_reason\": recorded_problem,\n+            \"next_action\": \"Finance to confirm the obligation's request, amount, chronology and exact claim revision from retained source evidence\",\n+        })\n     obligation = None\n     obligation_issue = None\n     if authorized_obligation is not None:\n@@ -266,15 +353,14 @@ def reconcile_finance_events(\n             \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n             \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n             \"revision\": current_revision,\n-            \"source_refs\": [],\n-            \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"no supported authorized obligation was supplied for this claim revision\",\n+            \"source_refs\": [e[\"source_ref\"] for e in history if e[\"event_id\"] in {r[\"event_id\"] for r in obligation_history}],\n+            \"missing_or_return_reason\": (\"recorded Finance obligation exists, but current-revision reimbursement authorization and entitlement remain unconfirmed\"\n+                                         if recorded_obligation else \"no supported authorized obligation was supplied for this claim revision\"),\n             \"owner\": owner,\n             \"next_action\": \"Finance to provide or confirm the authorized obligation for this claim revision\",\n         }\n     if obligation_issue is not None:\n         issues.append(obligation_issue)\n-        issues_by_owner.setdefault(owner, []).append(obligation_issue)\n-        issues_by_owner[owner].sort(key=lambda row: row[\"record_id\"])\n \n     has_unclassified_cash_event = any(item[\"classification\"] == \"unresolved\" for item in history)\n     event_set_complete = not unresolved and not conflicting_events and not missing_id_records and not has_unclassified_cash_event\n@@ -282,6 +368,26 @@ def reconcile_finance_events(\n     if obligation is not None and event_set_complete:\n         balance = obligation[\"amount_cents\"] - net_confirmed_cents\n \n+    ledger_balance = None\n+    if recorded_obligation is not None and event_set_complete and not recorded_problem:\n+        # Cash for a different/missing request cannot be silently applied to this ledger.\n+        cash_rows = [e for e in history if e['classification'] in {'confirmed_payment', 'confirmed_refund'}]\n+        if all(e['source_record'].get('Request reference') == recorded_obligation['request_id']\n+               and e['source_record'].get('Payee ID') == recorded_obligation['payee_id'] for e in cash_rows):\n+            ledger_balance = recorded_obligation['amount_cents'] - net_confirmed_cents\n+    if recorded_obligation is not None and event_set_complete and ledger_balance is None:\n+        issues.append({\n+            \"record_id\": f\"finance-recorded-cash-link:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n+            \"subject_type\": \"claim\", \"subject_id\": claim_id, \"revision\": current_revision,\n+            \"source_refs\": [e[\"source_ref\"] for e in history if e['classification'] in {'confirmed_payment', 'confirmed_refund', 'obligation_accepted'}],\n+            \"owner\": owner,\n+            \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"Confirmed claim cash cannot be matched to the recorded obligation's request and payee\",\n+            \"next_action\": \"Finance to verify each cash event's request and payee link before calculating a ledger difference\",\n+        })\n+    issues_by_owner = {}\n+    for issue in issues:\n+        issues_by_owner.setdefault(issue['owner'], []).append(issue)\n+    issues_by_owner = {key: sorted(value, key=lambda row: row['record_id']) for key, value in sorted(issues_by_owner.items())}\n     invalidated = None\n     if previous_reconciliation is not None:\n         previous_revision = previous_reconciliation.get(\"claim_revision\")\n@@ -291,7 +397,12 @@ def reconcile_finance_events(\n                 \"reason\": \"material revision change invalidates the prior reconciliation basis\",\n                 \"prior_net_confirmed_cents\": previous_reconciliation.get(\"net_confirmed_cents\"),\n                 \"prior_balance_cents\": previous_reconciliation.get(\"balance_cents\"),\n+                \"prior_recorded_obligation\": deepcopy(previous_reconciliation.get(\"recorded_obligation\")),\n+                \"next_action\": \"Revalidate exact revision authorization; historical ledger and cash remain retained\",\n             }\n+    revalidation_history = deepcopy((previous_reconciliation or {}).get(\"financial_revalidation_history\", []))\n+    if invalidated is not None:\n+        revalidation_history.append(deepcopy(invalidated))\n     return {\n         \"claim_id\": claim_id,\n         \"claim_revision\": current_revision,\n@@ -305,6 +416,11 @@ def reconcile_finance_events(\n         \"pending_transfer_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in typed if item[\"classification\"] == \"pending_transfer\"],\n         \"unresolved_event_ids\": list(dict.fromkeys(item[\"event_id\"] for item in unresolved if item[\"event_id\"] is not None)),\n         \"finance_obligation_events\": [item for item in history if item[\"classification\"] == \"obligation_accepted\"],\n+        \"recorded_obligation_history\": obligation_history,\n+        \"recorded_obligation\": recorded_obligation,\n+        \"recorded_ledger_balance_cents\": ledger_balance,\n+        \"reimbursement_entitlement_confirmed\": False,\n+        \"closure_authority_confirmed\": False,\n         \"authorized_obligation\": obligation,\n         \"confirmed_payment_cents\": confirmed_payment_cents,\n         \"confirmed_refund_cents\": confirmed_refund_cents,\n@@ -314,4 +430,5 @@ def reconcile_finance_events(\n         \"repair_issues\": issues,\n         \"repair_issues_by_owner\": issues_by_owner,\n         \"invalidated_previous_reconciliation\": invalidated,\n+        \"financial_revalidation_history\": revalidation_history,\n     }\ndiff --git a/src/travel_claim/integration.py b/src/travel_claim/integration.py\nindex b3c5d71..46f7c73 100644\n--- a/src/travel_claim/integration.py\n+++ b/src/travel_claim/integration.py\n@@ -140,9 +140,19 @@ def _sync_finance_repairs(domain: dict[str, Any], reconciliations: dict[str, Any\n     for claim_id, result in reconciliations.items():\n         for issue in result[\"repair_issues\"]:\n             item_id = f\"finance:{issue['record_id']}\"\n+            refs = [_ref_text(ref) for ref in issue.get(\"source_refs\", []) if isinstance(ref, dict)]\n             if item_id in queue[\"items\"]:\n+                item = queue[\"items\"][item_id]\n+                changes = {key: value for key, value in {\n+                    \"source_refs\": refs,\n+                    \"missing_or_return_reason\": issue[\"missing_or_return_reason\"],\n+                    \"next_action\": issue[\"next_action\"],\n+                }.items() if item[key] != value}\n+                if changes:\n+                    update_repair_item(queue, item_id=item_id,\n+                                       update_id=f\"finance-evidence:{item_id}:{batch_id}\",\n+                                       run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id, **changes)\n                 continue\n-            refs = [_ref_text(ref) for ref in issue.get(\"source_refs\", []) if isinstance(ref, dict)]\n             _open_issue_for_subject(\n                 queue, item_id=item_id, subject_type=\"claim\", subject_id=claim_id,\n                 revision=result[\"claim_revision\"], refs=refs,\n@@ -539,6 +549,13 @@ def integrate_arrival_batch(\n             \"status\": \"pending\",\n             \"lines\": [],\n             \"allowed_cents\": None,\n+            \"finance_evidence\": {\n+                \"recorded_obligation\": deepcopy(finance[\"recorded_obligation\"]),\n+                \"recorded_ledger_balance_cents\": finance[\"recorded_ledger_balance_cents\"],\n+                \"basis\": \"Recorded request ledger only; not reviewed entitlement or current-revision authorization\",\n+                \"current_revision_authority_confirmed\": False,\n+                \"closure_authority_confirmed\": False,\n+            },\n             \"paid_cents\": finance[\"net_confirmed_cents\"],\n             \"balance_cents\": finance[\"balance_cents\"],\n             \"decision_ids\": list(dict.fromkeys(row[\"decision_id\"] for row in matches if row.get(\"decision_id\"))),\ndiff --git a/src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py b/src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\nindex 680831e..e59ac5a 100644\n--- a/src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\n+++ b/src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\n@@ -74,11 +74,38 @@ def _report(\n         )\n     lines.extend([\n         \"\",\n-        \"Each snapshot retains the observed claim revision and matching decision IDs. Decisions are not treated as proof of policy compliance. Finance event identities and supported confirmed cash are retained; no obligation or entitlement is inferred. Claim monetary entitlement and balance remain null when unsupported.\",\n+        \"Each snapshot retains the observed claim revision and matching decision IDs. Decisions are not treated as proof of policy compliance. Finance event identities and supported confirmed cash are retained. Recorded ledger obligations are separate from entitlement and current-revision authorization. Claim monetary entitlement and balance remain null when unsupported.\",\n         \"\",\n         \"Independent valid records continue through the replay while unresolved claims remain pending. External blockers prevent authoritative live-run conclusions, not retention of independent evidence or partial progress.\",\n         \"\",\n     ])\n+    lines.extend([\n+        \"## Recorded Finance obligations and cash\", \"\",\n+        \"Obligation (EUR) is the ledger's recorded commitment amount, not a payment or approved reimbursement entitlement. \"\n+        \"Ledger differences below compare that recorded amount with confirmed transfers minus linked refunds. \"\n+        \"They do not establish claim eligibility, payment readiness or closure. Claim balance_cents remains null without a separately supported current-revision authorization.\", \"\",\n+        \"Native Finance rows have no claim-revision column. Arrival revision context identifies the source-observed revision at first delivery; \"\n+        \"it is not an explicit authorization binding, and redelivery never changes it. Adjustments/resolutions record obligation amounts rather than cash. \"\n+        \"Cancellation/retry events are not refunds or proof that an obligation is zero.\", \"\",\n+    ])\n+    latest_snapshot = json.loads(snapshots[-1].read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n+    for claim in latest_snapshot[\"claims\"]:\n+        evidence = claim.get(\"finance_evidence\", {})\n+        obligation = evidence.get(\"recorded_obligation\")\n+        if obligation is None:\n+            continue\n+        delta = evidence.get(\"recorded_ledger_balance_cents\")\n+        lines.extend([\n+            f\"- Claim `{claim['claim_id']}` current revision {claim['revision']}; request `{obligation['request_id']}`: \"\n+            f\"recorded obligation **{obligation['amount_cents']} cents**, confirmed net cash **{claim['paid_cents']} cents**, \"\n+            f\"recorded ledger difference **{delta if delta is not None else 'unresolved'}** cents.\",\n+            f\"  - Event `{obligation['event_id']}` ({obligation['event_type']}); first arrival batch {obligation['first_arrival_batch']}; \"\n+            f\"arrival revision context {obligation['arrival_revision_context']}; explicit claim revision {obligation['claim_revision']}; \"\n+            f\"link status `{obligation['revision_link_status']}`. Exact revision authority and closure remain unconfirmed.\",\n+            \"  - Retained evidence: \" + \"; \".join(f\"`{ref}`\" for ref in obligation['source_refs']) + \". \"\n+            \"Complete obligation changes and cash histories remain in `offline-replay-state.json`.\",\n+        ])\n+    lines.append(\"\")\n     queue = latest[\"domain\"][\"repair_queue\"]\n     for title, subject_types in (\n         (\"Claim-specific actionable repairs by owner\", {\"claim\"}),\n\"\"\"Regression examples transcribed verbatim from the retained native workbook.\"\"\"\n\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom travel_claim.finance import reconcile_finance_events\nfrom travel_claim.integration import integrate_arrival_batch\n\nFIXTURE = Path(__file__).parent / \"fixtures/retained_finance_records.json\"\n\n\ndef _fixture():\n    return json.loads(FIXTURE.read_text())\n\n\ndef _batches(parsed):\n    prior = None\n    results = []\n    for batch in parsed['arrival_batches']:\n        prior = integrate_arrival_batch(\n            parsed, arrival_batch=batch, run_id='retained-regression', batch_id=f'arrival-{batch:03d}',\n            source_binding={'path': 'sources.json', 'sha256': 'a' * 64},\n            predecessor={'path': f'batches/arrival-{batch-1:03d}.json', 'sha256': 'b' * 64} if prior else None,\n            prior_result=prior,\n        )\n        results.append(prior)\n    return results\n\n\ndef test_native_obligation_fields_and_ledger_balances_do_not_become_entitlement():\n    parsed = _fixture()\n    assert 'Claim revision' not in parsed['provenance']['finance_headers']\n    results = _batches(parsed)\n    final = results[-1]\n    c1 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C01']\n    obligation = c1['recorded_obligation']\n    assert obligation['event_id'] == 'F-C01-accepted'\n    assert obligation['request_id'] == 'REQ-C01'\n    assert obligation['finance_officer'] == 'FIN-01'\n    assert obligation['payee_id'] == 'EMP-01'\n    assert obligation['amount_cents'] == 10000\n    assert obligation['claim_revision'] is None\n    assert obligation['arrival_revision_context'] == 1\n    assert obligation['revision_link_status'] == 'arrival_context_only'\n    assert obligation['first_arrival_batch'] == 1\n    assert obligation['source_refs'] == [\n        'travel-registers-workbook@' + parsed['provenance']['workbook_sha256'] + \"#tab 'Finance activity', row 33\"\n    ]\n    assert obligation['claim_source_refs'][0]['locator'] == 'PDF page 1'\n    assert c1['net_confirmed_cents'] == 10000  # delivered twice, counted once\n    assert c1['duplicate_events'][0]['delivery_batches'] == [2, 4]\n    assert c1['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n    assert c1['authorized_obligation'] is None\n    assert c1['balance_cents'] is None\n    assert c1['closure_authority_confirmed'] is False\n    projected = next(c for c in final['snapshot']['claims'] if c['claim_id'] == 'C01')\n    assert projected['finance_evidence']['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n    assert projected['allowed_cents'] is None and projected['status'] == 'pending'\n\n\ndef test_native_corrections_keep_ledger_history_and_revalidate_authority_only_where_affected():\n    results = _batches(_fixture())\n    first, _, third, final = results\n    initial = deepcopy(first)\n    c19 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C19']\n    assert [(r['event_id'], r['amount_cents'], r['arrival_revision_context']) for r in c19['recorded_obligation_history']] == [\n        ('F-C19-accepted', 10000, 1), ('F-C19-2', 8000, 2), ('F-C19-4', 8000, 3),\n    ]\n    assert c19['confirmed_payment_cents'] == 10000\n    assert c19['confirmed_refund_cents'] == 2000\n    assert c19['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n    assert c19['recorded_obligation']['claim_revision'] is None\n    assert c19['invalidated_previous_reconciliation']['claim_revision'] == 2\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C09']['recorded_obligation']['arrival_revision_context'] == 2\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C12']['recorded_obligation']['amount_cents'] == 7000\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C01']['recorded_obligation'] == first['finance_reconciliations']['C01']['recorded_obligation']\n    # C18 correction has no newly bound accepted amount. Retain r1 context;\n    # neither cancellation nor a fresh payment silently reauthorizes revision 2.\n    c18 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C18']\n    assert c18['claim_revision'] == 2\n    assert c18['recorded_obligation']['arrival_revision_context'] == 1\n    assert c18['authorized_obligation'] is None\n    assert c18['confirmed_payment_cents'] == 10000\n    item = final['domain']['repair_queue']['items']['finance:finance-obligation-missing:C09:1']\n    # Historic question remains historic; r2 has its own current authorization question.\n    assert item['revision'] == 1\n    current = final['domain']['repair_queue']['items']['finance:finance-obligation-missing:C09:2']\n    assert current['source_refs']\n    assert 'recorded Finance obligation exists' in current['missing_or_return_reason']\n    assert current['status'] == 'open'\n    assert first == initial\n\n\ndef test_native_refund_and_finance_cancellation_are_independent_of_business_cancellations():\n    final = _batches(_fixture())[-1]\n    cancellations = {c['cancellation_id']: c for c in final['snapshot']['travel_cancellations']}\n    assert cancellations['TC122']['affected_claim_ids'] == []\n    assert cancellations['TC122']['target_type'] == 'trip'\n    assert cancellations['TC121']['target_type'] == 'permit'\n    assert all(c['financial_status'] == 'unresolved' for c in cancellations.values())\n    c18 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C18']\n    assert c18['recorded_obligation']['amount_cents'] == 10000\n    assert c18['confirmed_refund_cents'] == 0  # cancelled transfer is not a refund\n    c20 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C20']\n    assert c20['recorded_obligation']['amount_cents'] == 10000\n    assert c20['confirmed_refund_cents'] == 1000\n    assert c20['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n\n\ndef test_duplicate_refund_and_accepted_redelivery_keep_identity_and_original_revision_context():\n    parsed = _fixture()\n    accepted = deepcopy(next(r for r in parsed['records']['finance_events'] if r['values']['Activity reference']['value'] == 'F-C18-accepted'))\n    accepted['row'] = 998\n    accepted['locator'] = \"tab 'Finance activity', row 998 (synthetic redelivery)\"\n    accepted['values']['Arrival batch']['value'] = 4\n    refund = deepcopy(next(r for r in parsed['records']['finance_events'] if r['values']['Activity reference']['value'] == 'F-C20-2'))\n    refund['row'] = 999\n    refund['locator'] = \"tab 'Finance activity', row 999 (synthetic redelivery)\"\n    refund['values']['Arrival batch']['value'] = 4\n    parsed['records']['finance_events'].extend([accepted, refund])\n    final = _batches(parsed)[-1]\n    c18 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C18']\n    assert len(c18['recorded_obligation_history']) == 1\n    assert c18['recorded_obligation']['delivery_batches'] == [1, 4]\n    assert c18['recorded_obligation']['arrival_revision_context'] == 1\n    assert len(c18['recorded_obligation']['source_refs']) == 2\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C20']['confirmed_refund_cents'] == 1000\n\n\ndef _accepted_and_revision():\n    parsed = _fixture()\n    result = _batches(parsed)[0]\n    event = deepcopy(next(r for r in parsed['records']['finance_events'] if r['values']['Activity reference']['value'] == 'F-C01-accepted'))\n    return event, result['revision_history']['claim']['C01']['revisions']\n\n\ndef test_explicit_revision_link_is_distinct_from_arrival_context_and_does_not_approve():\n    event, revisions = _accepted_and_revision()\n    event['values']['Claim revision'] = {'value': 1}  # synthetic explicit field\n    result = reconcile_finance_events([event], claim_id='C01', current_revision=1, revision_history=revisions)\n    assert result['recorded_obligation']['claim_revision'] == 1\n    assert result['recorded_obligation']['revision_link_status'] == 'explicit_current'\n    assert result['authorized_obligation'] is None\n    assert result['balance_cents'] is None\n    assert result['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 10000\n\n\ndef test_missing_amount_and_conflicting_obligation_events_do_not_produce_known_ledger_balance():\n    event, revisions = _accepted_and_revision()\n    missing = deepcopy(event)\n    missing['values'].pop('Obligation (EUR)')\n    result = reconcile_finance_events([missing], claim_id='C01', current_revision=1, revision_history=revisions)\n    assert result['recorded_obligation'] is None\n    assert result['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] is None\n    conflict = deepcopy(event)\n    conflict['values']['Obligation (EUR)']['value'] = 999\n    result = reconcile_finance_events([event, conflict], claim_id='C01', current_revision=1, revision_history=revisions)\n    assert result['recorded_obligation'] is None\n    assert result['net_confirmed_cents'] == 0\n    assert result['conflicting_events'][0]['event_id'] == 'F-C01-accepted'\n\n\ndef test_unknown_reversal_semantics_are_unresolved_and_never_turned_into_cash():\n    event, revisions = _accepted_and_revision()\n    reversal = deepcopy(event)\n    reversal['values']['Activity reference']['value'] = 'SYNTHETIC-REVERSAL'\n    reversal['values']['Activity type']['value'] = 'reversal'\n    reversal['values']['Amount (EUR)'] = {'value': 100}\n    result = reconcile_finance_events([event, reversal], claim_id='C01', current_revision=1, revision_history=revisions)\n    assert result['net_confirmed_cents'] == 0\n    assert result['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] is None\n    assert result['unresolved_event_ids'] == ['SYNTHETIC-REVERSAL']\n\n\ndef test_cash_request_mismatch_keeps_ledger_difference_unresolved_with_owned_repair():\n    parsed = _fixture()\n    for row in parsed['records']['finance_events']:\n        if row['values']['Activity reference']['value'] == 'F-C01-1':\n            row['values']['Request reference']['value'] = 'SYNTHETIC-WRONG-REQUEST'\n    final = _batches(parsed)[-1]['finance_reconciliations']['C01']\n    assert final['net_confirmed_cents'] == 10000  # still an observed claim payment\n    assert final['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] is None\n    assert 'finance-recorded-cash-link:C01:1' in {i['record_id'] for i in final['repair_issues']}\n\n\ndef test_queue_updates_missing_evidence_question_without_erasing_its_history():\n    parsed = _fixture()\n    # Synthetic delayed delivery of an unchanged native amount tests a later\n    # evidence arrival for the same revision, without inventing authority.\n    for row in parsed['records']['finance_events']:\n        if row['values']['Activity reference']['value'] == 'F-C01-accepted':\n            row['values']['Arrival batch']['value'] = 2\n    results = _batches(parsed)\n    first, second, _, final = results\n    item_id = 'finance:finance-obligation-missing:C01:1'\n    item = first['domain']['repair_queue']['items'][item_id]\n    assert item['source_refs'] == []\n    updated = second['domain']['repair_queue']['items'][item_id]\n    assert updated['source_refs']\n    assert updated['status'] == 'open'  # recorded commitment is not approval\n    assert updated['history'][0]['previous']['source_refs'] == []\n    assert updated['history'][0]['changes']['source_refs'] == updated['source_refs']\n    assert updated['request_draft'] == {'status': 'draft', 'sent': False}\n    assert first['domain']['repair_queue']['items'][item_id] == item\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C19']['financial_revalidation_history'][0]['claim_revision'] == 1\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C19']['financial_revalidation_history'][1]['claim_revision'] == 2\n\n\ndef test_finance_report_separates_observed_ledger_difference_from_authority(tmp_path):\n    from travel_claim.offline_replay import _report\n\n    parsed = _fixture()\n    results = _batches(parsed)\n    run = tmp_path / 'report-fixture'\n    batches = run / 'batches'\n    batches.mkdir(parents=True)\n    (run / 'sources.json').write_text(json.dumps({'files': [\n        {'source_id': 'travel-registers-workbook', 'status': 'read'},\n        {'source_id': 'policy-pol-2026-2', 'status': 'unavailable'},\n    ]}))\n    (run / 'parsed-records.json').write_text(json.dumps(parsed))\n    snapshots = []\n    for result in results:\n        path = batches / (result['snapshot']['batch_id'] + '.json')\n        path.write_text(json.dumps(result['snapshot']))\n        snapshots.append(path)\n    report = _report(run_id='retained-regression', parsed=parsed, snapshots=snapshots,\n                     latest=results[-1], output_paths={\n                         'queue': run / 'repair-queue.json', 'state': run / 'offline-replay-state.json',\n                         'claims': run / 'claims.csv', 'drafts': run / 'follow-up-drafts.md',\n                     })\n    section = report.split('## Recorded Finance obligations and cash', 1)[1].split('## Claim-specific', 1)[0]\n    assert 'Claim `C19` current revision 3; request `REQ-C19`' in section\n    assert 'recorded obligation **8000 cents**' in section\n    assert 'confirmed net cash **8000 cents**' in section\n    assert 'recorded ledger difference **0** cents' in section\n    assert 'arrival revision context 3; explicit claim revision None' in section\n    assert \"#tab 'Finance activity', row 25\" in section\n    assert 'Exact revision authority and closure remain unconfirmed' in section\n    assert 'not a payment or approved reimbursement entitlement' in section\n    assert 'OFFLINE REPLAY' in report\nmain\nf98e044 feat: validate Project D submission readiness\n#!/bin/sh\n# Entire CLI hooks\nif command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then entire hooks git prepare-commit-msg \"$1\" \"$2\" 2>/dev/null || true; else :; fi\n#!/bin/sh\n# Entire CLI hooks\n# Post-commit hook: condense session data if commit has Entire-Checkpoint trailer\nif command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then entire hooks git post-commit 2>/dev/null || true; else :; fi\n#!/bin/sh\n# Entire CLI hooks\n# Pre-push hook: push session logs alongside user's push\n# $1 is the remote name (e.g., \"origin\")\nif command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then entire hooks git pre-push \"$1\"; else :; fi\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":" M README.md\n M snapshot.schema.json\n M src/travel_claim/finance.py\n M src/travel_claim/integration.py\n M src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\n?? artifacts/runs/\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-evidence-audit-f98e044.md\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91-validated/\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/\n?? tests/fixtures/\n?? tests/test_retained_finance.py\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 10bd03c..b844ea2 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -81,6 +81,28 @@ travel-claim validate-snapshot artifacts/runs/<run-id>/batches/<batch-id>.json\n \n `verify-batch` also checks the source-manifest bytes, predecessor bytes, and cancellation-to-issue references. Do not overwrite a sealed snapshot; create a new run with a documented link if later processing changes its content.\n \n+## Recorded Finance obligations\n+\n+Offline replay connects Finance ledger observations to claim IDs and request IDs, retaining event IDs, arrival deliveries, source cells, and obligation history. The retained `Finance activity` headers mean:\n+\n+| Retained field | Interpretation used by replay |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Activity reference | Immutable event identity; identical redeliveries count once. |\n+| Arrival batch | Delivery membership, separate from business event time. |\n+| Activity type | Recorded event vocabulary; accepted/adjustment/resolution carry obligation observations, while settled/refund carry confirmed cash. |\n+| Request reference / Claim reference | Explicit request and claim links; neither encodes an explicit revision. |\n+| Finance officer / Payee ID | Recorded officer and payee identities, not evidence that every required human approval is present. |\n+| Currency / Amount (EUR) | Currency and cash amount; only sufficiently supported EUR cash is reconciled. |\n+| Original activity reference | Refund linkage to the original confirmed payment. |\n+| Obligation (EUR) | Recorded commitment amount; observations are not summed as additional cash or assumed reimbursement entitlement. |\n+| Reason / Activity time (UTC) | Retained description and UTC event time; neither establishes a scenario case clock. |\n+\n+The interview's acceptance description is retained at `interviews/project-d-travel-expense-claim-20261013-2210.md:425`; native headers and examples are retained in `Finance activity`, row 5 and rows 23–25/33. Native Finance rows have no claim-revision column. Replay therefore records the source-observed revision context at **first delivery**, leaving the explicit revision null. Redelivery never rebinds an old event to a corrected revision. An explicit `Claim revision` field, if supplied in source records, is checked against retained revision history.\n+\n+The sidecar and optional claim `finance_evidence` projection expose recorded obligation history and `recorded_ledger_balance_cents` (recorded obligation minus confirmed net cash for the same request/payee). Adjustments/resolutions record amounts, not additive payment events. Unknown ordering, conflicting events, missing links, or undefined reversal semantics leave the affected ledger difference unresolved. Transfer cancellation does not itself erase the obligation or reverse cash. Corrections preserve historical cash/commitments and reopen revision-dependent review; unrelated claim evidence remains intact.\n+\n+This ledger arithmetic is separate from current-revision authorization and reviewed entitlement. Without separately supported authorization, `allowed_cents` and `balance_cents` remain null/blank and claims remain pending. A zero ledger difference does not establish policy eligibility, complete approvals, or closure. The exact CSV header is unchanged; `report.md` explains recorded financial facts separately from unresolved repairs and external blockers.\n+\n ## Submission-readiness validation\n \n ```bash\ndiff --git a/snapshot.schema.json b/snapshot.schema.json\nindex dc3067d..e240461 100644\n--- a/snapshot.schema.json\n+++ b/snapshot.schema.json\n@@ -193,6 +193,40 @@\n             \"type\": \"integer\",\n             \"minimum\": 1,\n             \"description\": \"Exact trip revision from the supplied trip source, independent of claim revision.\"\n+          },\n+          \"finance_evidence\": {\n+            \"type\": \"object\",\n+            \"required\": [\n+              \"recorded_obligation\",\n+              \"recorded_ledger_balance_cents\",\n+              \"basis\",\n+              \"current_revision_authority_confirmed\",\n+              \"closure_authority_confirmed\"\n+            ],\n+            \"properties\": {\n+              \"recorded_obligation\": {\n+                \"type\": [\n+                  \"object\",\n+                  \"null\"\n+                ]\n+              },\n+              \"recorded_ledger_balance_cents\": {\n+                \"type\": [\n+                  \"integer\",\n+                  \"null\"\n+                ]\n+              },\n+              \"basis\": {\n+                \"type\": \"string\",\n+                \"minLength\": 1\n+              },\n+              \"current_revision_authority_confirmed\": {\n+                \"const\": false\n+              },\n+              \"closure_authority_confirmed\": {\n+                \"const\": false\n+              }\n+            }\n           }\n         }\n       }\ndiff --git a/src/travel_clai