{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:17:48.699Z","ordinal":948,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02f4b2bd528e1b90016acfe350af7c8190b2adeb8e4f42784a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_83e41ab12a184d5fac576704b50792a7","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\np=Path('src/travel_claim/ordinary.py');s=p.read_text();s += '''\\\\n\\\\ndef ordinary_demo(workflows):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Render one observed claim with every stage, owner and retained reference.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    claim_id = \\\"C01\\\" if \\\"C01\\\" in workflows else next(iter(sorted(workflows)), None)\\n    lines = [\\\"# Connected ordinary claim workflow — OFFLINE REPLAY\\\", \\\"\\\",\\n             \\\"Retained-input evaluation; no fresh reads, requests, approvals or payments were generated.\\\", \\\"\\\"]\\n    if not claim_id:\\n        return \\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\".join(lines + [\\\"No retained claim available for demonstration.\\\", \\\"\\\"])\\n    workflow = workflows[claim_id]\\n    lines += [f\\\"Claim `{claim_id}` revision {workflow['revision']}; trip `{workflow['trip_id']}` revision {workflow['trip_revision']}; status **{workflow['status']}**.\\\", \\\"\\\"]\\n    for stage in workflow['stages']:\\n        lines += [f\\\"## {stage['stage']} — {stage['status']}\\\", \\\"\\\", stage['detail'], \\\"\\\",\\n                  f\\\"Owner: {stage['owner']}. Next action: {stage['next_action']}\\\", \\\"\\\"]\\n        lines.extend(f\\\"- `{reference}`\\\" for reference in stage['source_refs'])\\n        lines.append(\\\"\\\")\\n    return \\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\".join(lines) + \\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\"\\n''';p.write_text(s)\\np=Path('src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py');s=p.read_text().replace('from .integration import integrate_arrival_batch','from .integration import integrate_arrival_batch\\\\nfrom .ordinary import ordinary_demo');start=s.index('    demo_id = \\\"C01\\\"');end=s.index('    drafts, draft_count =',start);s=s[:start]+'''    output_paths[\\\"demo\\\"].write_text(ordinary_demo(workflows), encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n'''+s[end:];p.write_text(s)\\np=Path('src/travel_claim/readiness.py');s=p.read_text().replace('from .outputs import CLAIMS_COLUMNS', 'from .ordinary import ordinary_demo\\\\nfrom .outputs import CLAIMS_COLUMNS');s=s.replace('''    \\\"claims.csv\\\", \\\"report.md\\\", \\\"repair-queue.json\\\", \\\"follow-up-drafts.md\\\",''','''    \\\"claims.csv\\\", \\\"report.md\\\", \\\"repair-queue.json\\\", \\\"follow-up-drafts.md\\\",\\n    \\\"ordinary-workflow.json\\\", \\\"ordinary-workflow-demo.md\\\",''')\\nanchor='    def report_trace():'\\nhelper='''    def ordinary_trace():\\n        require(snapshots, \\\"Verified snapshots required\\\")\\n        obj = objects['ordinary-workflow.json']\\n        require(obj['mode'] == 'offline-replay' and obj['fresh_native_reads_performed'] is False\\n                and obj['run_id'] == state['run_id'], \\\"Ordinary workflow run/mode mismatch\\\")\\n        current = {c['claim_id']: c['ordinary_workflow'] for c in json.loads(snapshots[-1].read_text())['claims']}\\n        require(obj['claims'] == state['ordinary_workflows'] == current, \\\"Ordinary current workflow differs from sealed claims\\\")\\n        expected = {(path.stem, c['claim_id']): c['ordinary_workflow'] for path in snapshots\\n                    for c in json.loads(path.read_text())['claims']}\\n        history = obj['history']\\n        observed = {(r['batch_id'], r['workflow']['claim_id']): r['workflow'] for r in history}\\n        require(len(history) == len(observed) and observed == expected and history == state['ordinary_workflow_history'],\\n                \\\"Ordinary workflow history differs from the complete sealed batch chain\\\")\\n        require((run_dir / 'ordinary-workflow-demo.md').read_text() == ordinary_demo(current), \\\"Ordinary demonstration differs from retained stage evidence\\\")\\n    check('ordinary-workflow-traceability', [run_dir / 'ordinary-workflow.json', run_dir / 'ordinary-workflow-demo.md'], ordinary_trace)\\n\\n'''\\ns=s.replace(anchor,helper+anchor);p.write_text(s)\\np=Path('README.md');s=p.read_text();anchor='## Recorded Finance obligations';s=s.replace(anchor,'''## Connected ordinary workflow (Step 152)\\n\\nEach offline arrival batch now connects exact claim/trip/employee identity, current-revision expense lines, receipts and settled merchant proof, travel permission, eligibility, human review packets, explicit reimbursement requests, Finance obligations, cash reconciliation and financial closure. `ordinary-workflow.json` retains every claim's stage results and all batch transitions; `ordinary-workflow-demo.md` demonstrates C01 when present. `report.md` summarizes the same stages. Every blocked stage produces an owner-specific unsent repair action. Supported rechecks resolve only their matching items, with an explicit local evidence-validation event rather than an invented human reply.\\n\\nThe retained C01 fixture matches trip T01, receipt R-COST-01, merchant transaction M-COST-01, three observed review packets and request ledger REQ-C01. Its recorded ledger balances, but permission, policy eligibility, approval completeness, exact request/revision authority and closure remain blocked. A matched receipt is evidence, not automatic reimbursement eligibility. Every correction starts evaluation of the current revision again and preserves earlier decisions, cash and stage history. Independent cancellations block only affected claims' ordinary closure paths.\\n\\nActual native policy content is still unavailable. The evaluator never extracts policy rules from an interview summary, Finance acceptance, a cap table alone, or a keyword in HTML. It accepts only explicitly supplied, source-hash-matched normalized `workflow_policy_rules` records for its supported `exact-paid-costs-v1` rule set. Definitions specify receipt/settlement requirements, eligible/uncapped categories, FX date basis, required human roles (and any explicit director threshold), permission requirements and completion conditions. Unsupported or incomplete definitions remain blocked. International permission additionally needs exact permit revisions, named reviewers and expressly UTC commitment/approval timing; local date-only commitment cells cannot supply a missing timezone.\\n\\nClosure also needs a source-backed exact-revision `reimbursement_requests` record, a matching explicitly revision-bound Finance obligation, current required approval evidence, exact entitlement/authorized-obligation/net-cash agreement, an authoritative clock and source-backed `closure_authorities` confirmation of completion conditions. Failed/cancelled/pending Finance dependencies cannot silently disappear. The current native records do not supply those missing authorities. Nothing sends requests or makes discretionary human decisions.\\n\\n`tests/test_ordinary.py` contains an explicitly labeled **synthetic-test** successful path (pending → closed after confirmed payment), missing-condition regressions, correction reopening, and an unrelated cancellation. Its synthetic policy/clock/request/authority records are confined to the test fixture and are never substituted into real replay evidence. The supported rule set does not claim to implement the complete inaccessible native policy, its exceptions, or unprovided rule definitions.\\n\\n'''+anchor);p.write_text(s)\\nPY\\n.venv/bin/pytest -q\\n git diff --check\",\"max_output_tokens\":1800}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a13c07-abde-7561-8a83-1bb986e74dae","create_time":1792009040.6895475}}}
