ity-dependent stages remain blocked.\n\nThe synthetic fixture reaches pending → closed after the confirmed payment arrives. Tests also verify that a correction reopens the path, missing required evidence prevents closure, and an unrelated cancellation does not block an independent claim.","turn_id":"01a13c07-abde-7561-8a83-1bb986e74dae"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02f4b2bd528e1b90016acfe3cade588190a63d65ec21e7a2a9","order":67,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a13c11-d6e4-7d60-a647-b52e4d5d6433","text":"I’ve added closure guards for stale review-packet facts, conflicting review IDs, and unresolved Finance control events. A balanced cash total cannot bypass those checks. The synthetic tests also exercise an explicitly supplied cap rule and a missing director approval; those fixture rules are not applied to the retained claims.","turn_id":"01a13c07-abde-7561-8a83-1bb986e74dae"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02f4b2bd528e1b90016acfe49b9dd881909a4f4a57b20b06ca","order":68,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a13c15-07c0-7791-a00b-50b54cb8e0ca","text":"The full replay evaluated 121 claims across all four batches and retained 482 claim-stage histories. All real claims remain pending. C01 has four passing evidence/fact stages and five blocked authority-dependent stages.\n\nThe new replay preserves confirmed cash totals, all six correction transitions, cancellation and event histories, and prior artifacts. The synthetic closure path passes without unresolved dependencies; a separate test confirms that an affected cancellation holds closure without erasing supported entitlement or cash.","turn_id":"01a13c07-abde-7561-8a83-1bb986e74dae"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02f4b2bd528e1b90016acfe4ba7b5c8190887f75531cbd6e9b","order":69,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a13c15-8e14-7473-a0d3-2a0a04a9ab40","text":"Implemented Step 152 without committing or pushing.\n\nChanged: `README.md`, `snapshot.schema.json`, `ordinary.py` (new), `integration.py`, `offline_replay.py`, `outputs.py`, `readiness.py`, `test_ordinary.py` (new), `test_offline_replay.py`, and `fixtures/ordinary_claim_c01.json` (new).\n\nThe [C01 demonstration](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/artifacts/runs/source-capture-20261014T100034Z-step152-ordinary/ordinary-workflow-demo.md) shows exact source references:\n\n- **PASS:** trip/employee linkage, receipt and settled merchant proof, recorded review evidence, Finance ledger reconciliation.\n- **BLOCKED:** travel permission, policy eligibility, approval completeness, explicit request/revision authority, financial closure.\n\nC01 has €100 confirmed net cash and a zero recorded ledger difference. Its entitlement and authorized balance remain unresolved.\n\nClearly labeled synthetic tests verify pending → closed after confirmed payment, correction → pending, missing-condition guards, and cancellation independence.\n\n**102 tests passed**; `git diff --check` passed. New replay integrity passed; submission readiness remains **BLOCKED**.\n\nThe replay preserves four batches, 482 workflow histories, six correction transitions, all event histories, and unchanged cash totals. All 64 prior artifact files and the original interview remain unchanged.\n\nRemaining gaps include native policy content and unsupported rules/exceptions, exact permit/request authority, the authoritative clock, and closure confirmation. All 121 real claims remain pending.","turn_id":"01a13c07-abde-7561-8a83-1bb986e74dae"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02f4b2bd528e1b90016acfe50c1b508190aefa9a28252034e3","order":71,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a13c16-bb10-73d0-bd61-bc7846ee0639","text":"I’ll inspect the diffs and staging area, stage only the ten named files, and run validation before committing and pushing. I’ll then verify remote `main`, the Entire.io refs, and the original interview and retained artifact hashes.","turn_id":"01a13c16-a6a3-7421-b7b1-82744f6027a9"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02f4b2bd