travel_claim/cli.py`\n   - `src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py`\n   - `src/travel_claim/readiness.py`\n   - `tests/test_readiness.py`\n3. Do not stage `artifacts/runs/`, `artifacts/verification/`, or unrelated files.\n4. Run `git diff --cached --check` and the complete pytest suite.\n5. If validation passes, commit with:\n   `feat: validate Project D submission readiness`\n6. Push to `origin main`, allowing the existing Entire.io hooks to run.\n7. Verify the remote main commit and Entire.io checkpoint references.\n\nDo not force-push, rewrite history, or modify retained artifacts.\n\nReport the exact commit hash, test results, push status, checkpoint verification, and any warnings.","turn_id":"01a13beb-f5b1-7430-847f-20bf35334bf7"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a13bf2-65cf-7fc3-a667-222215bed839","order":43,"revision":"retained_01a13bf2-65cf-7fc3-a667-224f6aa900cf","text":"Continue Project D from verified commit f98e044.\n\nI have now provided the original Project D assignment requirements. Before implementing more features, audit the existing interview and retained native-source evidence for the two outstanding blockers.\n\nSearch the complete original interview export and all retained source content for an explicit authoritative case clock, including date, time, timezone, and arrival-batch boundaries.\n\nExamine the retained sources.json and source observations for the Notion reimbursement policy. Determine exactly what content was accessible and what was not.\n\nDistinguish an explicit scenario fact from a document timestamp, an inference, or an invented default.\n\nCompare the assignment requirements against the current implementation and identify material coverage gaps, especially the connected ordinary path, corrections, independent cancellations, financial closure, and full-record verification.\n\nProduce a concise evidence audit with exact file paths, source references, findings, and remaining questions.\n\nDo not alter existing source artifacts, change financial conclusions, or invent missing policy rules or case-clock values.\n\nDo not commit or push.\n\nThis is an evidence audit, not a request to automate the stakeholder interview. Use only the interview export already created by me and the existing retained evidence.","turn_id":"01a13bf2-628b-75c2-a43b-f19b5878b298"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a13bf7-8871-7d10-8b35-9dea435e5af1","order":48,"revision":"retained_01a13bf7-8871-7d10-8b35-9e0566b7f80f","text":"Continue implementing Project D in ~/travel-expense-claim from commit f98e044.\n\nThe evidence audit identified a material integration gap: the retained workbook contains accepted-obligation records, but the offline replay does not consistently connect those records to claim revisions and financial reconciliation.\n\nImplement the next coding milestone now.\n\n    Inspect the existing Finance parser, native retained workbook records, finance.py, integration.py, and related tests.\n\n    Identify the exact meaning of each accepted-obligation field from source headers and retained evidence. Do not assume an accepted Finance event is equivalent to a human-approved reimbursement entitlement unless the source supports that interpretation.\n\n    Connect supported obligation records to the correct claim ID and revision, preserving event identity, source references, arrival batches, and history.\n\nReconcile supported obligations against confirmed payments, refunds, reversals, and corrections without double-counting duplicate events.\n\nDistinguish known financial facts from missing approvals, unresolved policy eligibility, and unconfirmed closure authority.\n\nRevalidate affected financial dependencies after material claim corrections, preserving unaffected records.\n\nUpdate claim projections, repair queue items, and report outputs only where supported by evidence.\n\nAdd regression tests using representative retained records, including duplicate events, corrections, and independent cancellations.\n\nRun the full test suite and git diff --check.\n\nGenerate a new labeled offline replay without overwriting prior artifacts.\n\nDo not invent approvals, payment confirmations, policy limits, or case-clock dates. Do not commit or push yet.\n\nReport changed files, tests passed, which financial facts were successfully linked, and what remains blocked.","turn_id":"01a13bf7-84ed-7580-8f9b-351b17474778"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a13bff-70d1-7ac3-8f43-c0fef55fce73","order":54,"revision":"retained_01a13bff-70d1-7ac3-8f43-c11ec14e69d3","text":"Preserve the completed Project D financial source reconciliation milestone.\n\n    Inspect git status, the exact source diff, and all staged changes.\n\n    Stage ONLY these files:\n\n        README.md\n\n        snapshot.schema.json\n\n        src/travel_claim/finance.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/integration.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\n\n        tests/test_retained_finance.py\n\n        tests/fixtures/retained_finance_records.json\n\n    Do not stage artifacts/runs/, artifacts/verification/, or unrelated files.\n\n    Run git diff --cached --check and the complete pytest suite.\n\n    If validation passes, commit with:\n    feat: reconcile retained Finance obligations and refunds\n\n    Push to origin main, allowing existing Entire.io hooks to run.\n\n    Verify the exact remote main commit and Entire.io checkpoint references.\n\nDo not force-push, rewrite history, or modify retained artifacts.\n\nReport the commit hash, tests passed, push verification, and any warnings.","turn_id":"01a13bff-6c35-74c3-badb-76002d27261c"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a13c07-b4f9-7913-b15e-0a8645c80fc3","order":63,"revision":"retained_01a13c07-b4fa-76b2-91d1-03edd9a54695","text":"Continue Project D from verified GitHub commit 74fad6313b1f65ce7fbf015c3cbfa35122d09896.\n\nImplement Step 152: the connected ordinary travel-expense claim workflow.\n\nUse the existing code, original interview export, retained source 