{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:32:05.059Z","ordinal":1176,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a13bd1-7420-72c0-963e-58742d1be7bf","turn_id":"01a13c1b-19a6-7c30-952c-e0611fda1bab","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b5fb00ed-b298-4aa7-85cd-ccec46b031bf","process_id":"27760","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","sed -n '270,290p' interviews/project-d-travel-expense-claim-20261013-2210.md; sed -n '175,215p' src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py; sed -n '265,300p' src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py; sed -n '85,105p' src/travel_claim/ordinary.py; rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g SKILL.md; sed -n '1,65p' src/travel_claim/integration.py"],"cwd":"file:///home/maxg/travel-expense-claim","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '270,290p' interviews/project-d-travel-expense-claim-20261013-2210.md","name":"project-d-travel-expense-claim-20261013-2210.md","path":"interviews/project-d-travel-expense-claim-20261013-2210.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '175,215p' src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py","name":"offline_replay.py","path":"src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '265,300p' src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py","name":"offline_replay.py","path":"src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '85,105p' src/travel_claim/ordinary.py","name":"ordinary.py","path":"src/travel_claim/ordinary.py"},{"type":"list_files","cmd":"rg --files -g AGENTS.md -g SKILL.md","path":null},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,65p' src/travel_claim/integration.py","name":"integration.py","path":"src/travel_claim/integration.py"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nWhich work to revalidate after material corrections is the norm?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nThe policy requires a full or justified recheck of all affected dependencies, including calculations and approvals, when material changes are made. Even if the total amount remains the same, any change in evidence or facts invalidates prior readiness, so a fresh review is required.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nWhat are the financial completion conditions?\n\n**Travel Administration Lead** · Voice · 05:26 PM\n\nFinancial completion requires that current approvals match the reviewed entitlement, net confirmed payments equal the authorized amount, no issues remain, and all required Finance resolutions have been received.\n\n**Max Gabel** · Voice · 05:27 PM\n\nWho owns the entitlement?\n\n    if errors:\n        raise ValueError(\"Retained source manifest verification failed: \" + \"; \".join(errors))\n    manifest_path = run_dir / \"sources.json\"\n    manifest = json.loads(manifest_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    parsed_path = run_dir / OUTPUT_NAME\n    parsed = json.loads(parsed_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    actual_manifest_hash = hashlib.sha256(manifest_path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n    if parsed.get(\"run_id\") != manifest.get(\"run_id\"):\n        raise ValueError(\"Parsed records run_id does not match the retained source manifest\")\n    if parsed.get(\"source_manifest\") != {\"path\": \"sources.json\", \"sha256\": actual_manifest_hash}:\n        raise ValueError(\"Parsed records are not bound to the current retained sources.json bytes\")\n    batches = parsed.get(\"arrival_batches\")\n    if not isinstance(batches, list) or not batches or batches != list(range(1, len(batches) + 1)):\n        raise ValueError(\"Retained arrival batches must be a nonempty contiguous explicit sequence starting at 1\")\n    output_paths = {\n        \"claims\": run_dir / \"claims.csv\",\n        \"report\": run_dir / \"report.md\",\n        \"queue\": run_dir / \"repair-queue.json\",\n        \"state\": run_dir / \"offline-replay-state.json\",\n        \"drafts\": run_dir / \"follow-up-drafts.md\",\n        \"workflow\": run_dir / \"ordinary-workflow.json\",\n        \"demo\": run_dir / \"ordinary-workflow-demo.md\",\n    }\n    occupied = [str(path) for path in output_paths.values() if path.exists()]\n    if occupied:\n        raise FileExistsError(\"Refusing to overwrite offline replay outputs: \" + \", \".join(occupied))\n    batches_dir = run_dir / \"batches\"\n    if batches_dir.exists() and any(batches_dir.iterdir()):\n        raise FileExistsError(f\"Refusing to overwrite or append to existing sealed batch chain: {batches_dir}\")\n\n    binding = {\"path\": \"sources.json\", \"sha256\": actual_manifest_hash}\n    previous: dict[str, Any] | None = None\n    previous_path: Path | None = None\n    sealed: list[Path] = []\n    for number in batches:\n        batch_id = f\"arrival-{number:03d}\"\n        predecessor = None\n        if previous_path is not None:\n            predecessor = {\n                \"path\": f\"batches/{previous_path.name}\",\n                \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(previous_path.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n    _exclusive_json(output_paths[\"state\"], {\n        \"mode\": \"offline-replay\",\n        \"fresh_native_reads_performed\": False,\n        \"run_id\": manifest[\"run_id\"],\n        \"case_clock\": manifest.get(\"case_clock\"),\n        \"source_manifest_sha256\": actual_manifest_hash,\n        \"parsed_records_path\": OUTPUT_NAME,\n        \"parsed_records_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(parsed_path.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\n        \"parsed_record_counts\": {name: len(rows) for name, rows in parsed.get(\"records\", {}).items()},\n        \"sealed_batches\": [path.relative_to(run_dir).as_posix() for path in sealed],\n        \"revision_history\": latest[\"revision_history\"],\n        \"decision_history\": latest[\"decision_history\"],\n        \"finance_reconciliations\": latest[\"finance_reconciliations\"],\n        \"cancellation_state\": latest[\"domain\"][\"cancellation_state\"],\n        \"material_corrections\": latest[\"domain\"][\"material_corrections\"],\n        \"ordinary_workflows\": latest[\"domain\"][\"ordinary_workflows\"],\n        \"ordinary_workflow_history\": latest[\"domain\"][\"ordinary_workflow_history\"],\n        \"source_record_history\": {\n            \"claim_revisions\": latest[\"domain\"][\"claim_records\"],\n            \"decisions\": latest[\"domain\"][\"decision_records\"],\n            \"finance_events\": latest[\"domain\"][\"finance_records\"],\n            \"cancellation_activities\": latest[\"domain\"][\"cancellation_records\"],\n        },\n        \"repair_queue\": queue,\n    })\n    workflows = latest[\"domain\"][\"ordinary_workflows\"]\n    _exclusive_json(output_paths[\"workflow\"], {\"mode\": \"offline-replay\", \"fresh_native_reads_performed\": False,\n        \"run_id\": manifest[\"run_id\"], \"claims\": workflows, \"history\": latest[\"domain\"][\"ordinary_workflow_history\"]})\n    output_paths[\"demo\"].write_text(ordinary_demo(workflows), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    drafts, draft_count = render_follow_up_drafts(\n        run_id=manifest[\"run_id\"], queue=queue, blockers=parsed.get(\"unresolved_issues\", []),\n    )\n    with output_paths[\"drafts\"].open(\"x\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\\n\") as stream:\n        stream.write(drafts)\n    report = _report(\n        run_id=manifest[\"run_id\"], parsed=parsed, snapshots=sealed, latest=latest,\n                        and set(policy.get('Required claim roles')) <= set(ROLE_FIELDS)\n                        and policy.get('Receipt required') is True and policy.get('Settled merchant proof required') is True\n                        and policy.get('No self review') is True and policy.get('FX date basis') == 'paid-date'\n                        and policy.get('Closure rule') == 'entitlement-authorization-net-cash-no-blockers'\n                        and isinstance(policy.get('Domestic permit required'), bool))\n    policy_refs = [ref(policy_record)] if policy_record else []\n    affected = [c for c in cancellations if claim_id in c['affected_claim_ids']]\n    permission = False\n    permission_refs = [ref(r) for r in trips] + policy_refs\n    if linked and policy_supported:\n        if trip.get('International') is False and policy.get('Domestic permit required') is False:\n            permission = True\n        else:\n            # UTC timing must be expressly supplied; local calendar dates do\n            # not establish an exact commitment instant.\n            permit_roles = policy.get('Required permit roles')\n            commitment = trip.get('First commitment time (UTC)')\n            relevant = [r for r in decisions if fields(r).get('Subject type') == 'permit'\n                        and fields(r).get('Subject reference') == trip.get('Permit reference')\n                        and fields(r).get('Revision') == trip.get('Permit revision')]\n            permission_refs += [ref(r) for r in relevant]\nskills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md\n\"\"\"Arrival-ordered, policy-neutral integration of Project D records.\n\nThis module prepares schema-shaped batch state but never seals snapshots,\ninfers eligibility, applies review decisions, or authorizes obligations.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom .finance import reconcile_finance_events\nfrom .ordinary import connect_claim\nfrom .outputs import add_repair_item, new_repair_queue, update_repair_item, record_evidence_validation\nfrom .workflow import (\n    build_revision_history,\n    match_decisions_to_subjects,\n    reduce_cancellation_activities,\n    row_values,\n)\n\n\n_REVALIDATION_AREAS = (\n    (\"expense-evidence\", \"recheck expense evidence against the corrected claim revision\", \"employee\"),\n    (\"calculations\", \"recalculate and verify amounts for the corrected claim revision\", \"Travel Administration Lead\"),\n    (\"trip-permit\", \"recheck trip and permit identity and revision consistency\", \"Travel Administration Lead\"),\n    (\"approvals\", \"obtain current-revision decisions; prior decisions remain historical only\", 