{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:35:13.147Z","ordinal":1285,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a13bd1-7420-72c0-963e-58742d1be7bf","turn_id":"01a13c1b-19a6-7c30-952c-e0611fda1bab","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_02f4b2bd528e1b90016acfe77f50e881908dce2ba41f5af961","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The new regressions exposed an update-history bug: a later batch could try to record an unchanged cancellation disposition as a new repair update. I fixed that. Partial and orphan confirmations now retain their evidence and open owned repair items without crashing the replay.\n\nTC122 is the retained no-claim cancellation case. C18 keeps its historical T18 cancellation link after moving to T18B; the cancelled transfer remains a noncash event, separate from the later confirmed payment."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1792010111643,"completed_at_ms":1792010113147}}
