{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:39:21.679Z","ordinal":1346,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a13bd1-7420-72c0-963e-58742d1be7bf","turn_id":"01a13c23-fc3d-7aa1-be2f-35410ab86ebd","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b3c67432-da84-4782-8572-b10c68cc8466","process_id":"16458","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","git status --short; git diff --cached; git diff -- README.md src/travel_claim/integration.py src/travel_claim/ordinary.py src/travel_claim/workflow.py src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py src/travel_claim/readiness.py tests/test_readiness.py; cat src/travel_claim/revalidation.py tests/test_revalidation.py"],"cwd":"file:///home/maxg/travel-expense-claim","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git status --short; git diff --cached; git diff -- README.md src/travel_claim/integration.py src/travel_claim/ordinary.py src/travel_claim/workflow.py src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py src/travel_claim/readiness.py tests/test_readiness.py; cat src/travel_claim/revalidation.py tests/test_revalidation.py"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":" M README.md\n M src/travel_claim/integration.py\n M src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\n M src/travel_claim/ordinary.py\n M src/travel_claim/readiness.py\n M src/travel_claim/workflow.py\n M tests/test_readiness.py\n?? artifacts/runs/\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-evidence-audit-f98e044.md\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91-validated/\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-step157-revalidation/\n?? src/travel_claim/revalidation.py\n?? tests/test_revalidation.py\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex d7267d9..2571251 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -130,3 +130,11 @@ Each check is `PASS`, `BLOCKED`, or `FAIL`; exit codes are 0, 2, and 1 respectiv\n The implementation supports fresh source capture, byte-bound manifests, loss-aware transcription, schema/hash-checked snapshots, policy-neutral arrival-ordered replay, source-classified Finance reconciliation, exact CSV output, and local owner-grouped repair tracking. `offline-replay` is a structural replay only: the inaccessible reimbursement policy and unconfirmed case clock keep policy conclusions, approval readiness, entitlement, and closure unresolved. Human replies are not imported automatically, and the command never sends repair drafts or moves money. Do not treat an offline replay as a fresh source read or completed claim processing.\n \n If native evidence is unavailable or a business definition conflicts, record the affected scope and escalate to the exercise operator. People retain approval, exception, and payment authority. This tooling never sends requests, books travel, or moves money.\n+\n+## Step 157: correction and independent cancellation rechecks\n+\n+Every corrected revision executes the connected evidence, calculation, trip/permit, human-review, request and Finance checks again. `material_corrections` retains changed field and expense-line facts, unchanged cost identities, excluded historical decisions, before-state evidence, and each executed batch result. A changed receipt invalidates readiness even when the amount is unchanged. Cash events and prior revision history remain intact; a passed receipt recheck cannot manufacture new approvals or current request authority.\n+\n+`correction-cancellation-verification.json` and `.md` demonstrate all retained corrections and independent trip/permit processes with source references, before/after cash facts, executed check results and next actions. They are explicitly retained-input offline outputs. The readiness command compares these artifacts with a deterministic replay and checks the sealed snapshot chain.\n+\n+Cancellation processing preserves the first event delivery, duplicate deliveries, employee/supervisor evidence, initiation/confirmation chronology, historical versus current claim links, and observed Finance request IDs. Orphan or partial confirmations remain unresolved with owned repair actions. Linked requests are held; unrelated claims continue. Explicit cancellation-bound Finance exceptions are recorded separately from policy eligibility and financial completion. A transfer cancellation never counts as a cash refund. Unknown disposition, approval, policy, case clock or closure authority remains blocked; absence of a claim does not imply absence of financial effects.\ndiff --git a/src/travel_claim/integration.py b/src/travel_claim/integration.py\nindex 9288a34..922b736 100644\n--- a/src/travel_claim/integration.py\n+++ b/src/travel_claim/integration.py\n@@ -12,7 +12,8 @@ from copy import deepcopy\n from typing import Any\n \n from .finance import reconcile_finance_events\n-from .ordinary import connect_claim\n+from .ordinary import connect_claim, fields, table\n+from .revalidation import record_executed_rechecks\n from .outputs import add_repair_item, new_repair_queue, update_repair_item, record_evidence_validation\n from .workflow import (\n     build_revision_history,\n@@ -259,14 +260,26 @@ def _material_correction_tasks(\n \n \n def _cancellation_rows(\n-    domain: dict[str, Any], *, history: dict[str, Any], run_id: str, batch_id: str,\n+    domain: dict[str, Any], *, history: dict[str, Any], run_id: str, batch_id: str, parsed: dict[str, Any],\n ) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n     reduced = reduce_cancellation_activities(domain[\"cancellation_records\"])\n     domain[\"cancellation_state\"] = reduced\n-    raw_by_id = {\n-        row_values(record).get(\"Cancellation activity reference\"): record\n-        for record in domain[\"cancellation_records\"]\n-    }\n+    raw_by_id = {}\n+    for record in domain[\"cancellation_records\"]:\n+        raw_by_id.setdefault(row_values(record).get(\"Cancellation activity reference\"), record)\n+    domain[\"cancellation_evidence\"] = {}\n+    for index, issue in enumerate(reduced[\"issues\"]):\n+        event = raw_by_id.get(issue.get(\"event_id\