{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:50:52.863Z","ordinal":1549,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02f4b2bd528e1b90016acfeb148e188190b189e83559fc477c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_67233a6baa5146b6825e90ca0e7d103c","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\".venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\np=Path('src/travel_claim/parsing.py');s=p.read_text().replace('from datetime import date, datetime, time','from datetime import date, datetime, time\\\\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation')\\na=s.index('    batch_ids: set[int] = set()');b=s.index('    batch_contents:',a)\\ns=s[:a]+'''    batch_ids: set[int] = set()\\n    invalid_batches = set()\\n    def explicit_batch(value, record):\\n        try:\\n            number = Decimal(str(value))\\n            if isinstance(value, bool) or not number.is_finite() or number < 1 or number != number.to_integral_value():\\n                raise ValueError(\\\"not a positive integer batch\\\")\\n            return int(number)\\n        except (InvalidOperation, ValueError, TypeError):\\n            key = (record.get('source_id'), record.get('locator'), str(value))\\n            if key not in invalid_batches:\\n                invalid_batches.add(key)\\n                transcription_issues.append({'source_id': record.get('source_id'),\\n                    'source_sha256': record.get('source_sha256'), 'path': record.get('locator'),\\n                    'error': f\\\"Arrival batch is not an explicit positive integer: {value!r}; raw value preserved\\\",\\n                    'owner': 'Travel Administration Lead', 'next_action': 'Obtain the authoritative arrival membership without rounding or defaulting'})\\n            return None\\n    for record in claim_revisions + decisions + finance + cancellations:\\n        value = (next((f['value'] for f in record['fields'] if f['label'].strip().lower() == 'arrival batch'), None)\\n                 if 'fields' in record else _value(record, 'Arrival batch'))\\n        batch = explicit_batch(value, record)\\n        if batch is not None:\\n            batch_ids.add(batch)\\n\\n'''+s[b:]\\ns=s.replace('            if value is None or value == \\\"\\\":\\\\n                continue\\\\n            key = str(int(value))','            batch = explicit_batch(value, record)\\\\n            if batch is None:\\\\n                continue\\\\n            key = str(batch)')\\np.write_text(s)\\np=Path('src/travel_claim/sources.py');s=p.read_text().replace('        if manifest.get(\\\"source_version\\\") == \\\"native-source-manifest/2\\\":', '        if sid in specs and record[\\\"url\\\"] != specs[sid].url:\\\\n            errors.append(f\\\"{sid}: source identity does not match its original native URL\\\")\\\\n        if manifest.get(\\\"source_version\\\") == \\\"native-source-manifest/2\\\":');p.write_text(s)\\nPY\\ncat >> README.md <<'EOF'\\n\\n## Fresh native-source acquisition and transcription\\n\\n```bash\\ntravel-claim live-run <new-run-id> artifacts/runs/<new-run-id> [--case-clock '<authoritative scenario timestamp>']\\n```\\n\\n`live-run` attempts all five original locations using direct HTTP and native Google PDF/XLSX export routes, then verifies the manifest and transcribes accessible content from **this invocation**. It accepts no prior-run or cache input. Every run requires a new empty directory; existing manifests, parsed inputs, response files and snapshots cannot be reused. The optional clock is caller-supplied scenario evidence; retrieval timestamps never become a case clock.\\n\\nNew captures use `native-source-manifest/2`. Each entry records the original source identity/URL, attempted export URL, redirect destination, HTTP status, start/end UTC observations, ETag or Last-Modified when supplied, content hash/version, accessible scope, error and missing scope. Complete response bodies are retained verbatim under `responses/`, including error pages and unusable shells; usable complete or partial documents are also bound under `sources/`. The verifier checks hashes, scope/status consistency and fresh response bindings. Legacy `/1` manifests remain readable for historical replay; they do not gain fresh-access evidence.\\n\\nA `read` PDF must be structurally readable with extractable text on every page. Scanned or partially readable documents require further verification. XLSX exports must contain all ten known workbook tabs; all returned bytes, tab content, cell values and numeric source evidence remain retained. Partial HTTP responses, mismatched byte counts, corrupt documents and incomplete workbook exports cannot pass complete acquisition. Usable partial sources are transcribed independently, with missing scope retained. Malformed arrival membership is reported without rounding or supplying a default.\\n\\nPlain HTTP access to a Notion shell does not establish policy access. Even policy-related HTML is marked **partial** because this reader cannot establish the complete authoritative block tree. The current reader has no authenticated Notion API/browser/export adapter. Complete policy access and policy rule interpretation remain required before policy-dependent execution; source bytes are never replaced by interview-derived rules or earlier downloads.\\n\\n`live-run.json` and `live-run.md` distinguish acquisition status from final business compliance. Exit `2` means **BLOCKED** (source access, transcription, clock or policy processing remains incomplete); exit `1` means **FAIL** for integrity/execution errors. The command performs fresh acquisition and loss-aware transcription, but does not consume arrival batches or certify final live-source claim compliance. The separate `offline-replay` command remains explicitly labeled retained-input evaluation. A successful `verify-sources` establishes integrity of recorded evidence, including failure observations, rather than completeness of all five sources.\\nEOF\\n.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\np=Path('skills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md');s=p.read_text().replace('Capture sources for a new run with:', 'Perform fresh acquisition and transcription for a new run with:\\\\n\\\\n```bash\\\\ntravel-claim live-run <new-run-id> artifacts/runs/<new-run-id> [--case-clock \\\\'<authoritative scenario timestamp>\\\\']\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThis attempts all five original sources, retains response evidence and emits `live-run.json`/`.md`. It never accepts prior inputs or consumes batches when clock/policy authority is missing. Direct Notion HTML cannot establish a complete policy block-tree read; authenticated native access remains required. Retrieval timestamps are observations, never an invented case clock. Source-only capture is also available:')\\ns=s.replace('- Foundation implementation currently covers source capture/verification, retained PDF/workbook transcription, snapshot sealing/verification, the claims CSV writer, and local repair queue primitives. Scenario-state processing, policy/evidence decisions, approvals, Finance reconciliation, replay orchestration, and the complete operations report remain to be implemented and verified.', '- Implemented paths include fresh HTTP/export acquisition and source-bound transcription, plus explicitly offline connected claim, correction, independent cancellation and Finance replay. New source manifests retain response observations and partial/error bodies. Complete native policy access, rule interpretation, authoritative case clock and supported completion authority remain required for final live business compliance; acquisition or offline integrity alone does not establish it.')\\np.write_text(s)\\nPY\\n.venv/bin/pytest -q\",\"yield_time_ms\":1000,\"max_output_tokens\":1500}));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:78481,chars:\"\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:1500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a13c28-c6bd-7171-9c10-8efd3c67b498","create_time":1792011