 else _value(record, 'Arrival batch'))\n        batch = explicit_batch(value, record)\n        if batch is not None:\n            batch_ids.add(batch)\n\n'''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('            if value is None or value == \"\":\\n                continue\\n            key = str(int(value))','            batch = explicit_batch(value, record)\\n            if batch is None:\\n                continue\\n            key = str(batch)')\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('src/travel_claim/sources.py');s=p.read_text().replace('        if manifest.get(\"source_version\") == \"native-source-manifest/2\":', '        if sid in specs and record[\"url\"] != specs[sid].url:\\n            errors.append(f\"{sid}: source identity does not match its original native URL\")\\n        if manifest.get(\"source_version\") == \"native-source-manifest/2\":');p.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Fresh native-source acquisition and transcription\n\n```bash\ntravel-claim live-run <new-run-id> artifacts/runs/<new-run-id> [--case-clock '<authoritative scenario timestamp>']\n```\n\n`live-run` attempts all five original locations using direct HTTP and native Google PDF/XLSX export routes, then verifies the manifest and transcribes accessible content from **this invocation**. It accepts no prior-run or cache input. Every run requires a new empty directory; existing manifests, parsed inputs, response files and snapshots cannot be reused. The optional clock is caller-supplied scenario evidence; retrieval timestamps never become a case clock.\n\nNew captures use `native-source-manifest/2`. Each entry records the original source identity/URL, attempted export URL, redirect destination, HTTP status, start/end UTC observations, ETag or Last-Modified when supplied, content hash/version, accessible scope, error and missing scope. Complete response bodies are retained verbatim under `responses/`, including error pages and unusable shells; usable complete or partial documents are also bound under `sources/