{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:53:57.358Z","ordinal":1642,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02f4b2bd528e1b90016acfebd5e4788190936606846c4a761c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_ad108c51ddea412f9dffbca7943c5c77","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\".venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\npath=Path('artifacts/verification/project-d-live-source-audit-87dbd1c.md')\\ntext='''# Project D fresh native-source workflow audit\\n\\nBase commit: `87dbd1c504034f6393326ed2aa9a5e09fbe7a14f`. Changes remain uncommitted.\\n\\nThe existing `capture-sources` already issued five unconditional native HTTP/export requests and had no retained-input fallback. Its completeness checks only tested PDF signatures/trailers and XLSX archive presence; its Notion HTML keyword heuristic could overstate access. It dropped rejected response bodies, redirect destinations and HTTP observations, did not implement partial scope, and printed “complete” after partial acquisition. The parser repeated an old policy error without consulting the current observation. The only connected batch execution command was explicitly offline replay.\\n\\nImplemented `live-run` in `src/travel_claim/cli.py:67` and `src/travel_claim/live_run.py:15`: fresh capture, manifest verification, independent source transcription and machine/human status reports. No prior-run input is accepted. It never consumes arrival batches or certifies final business compliance. Native claim processing still requires the missing policy rules and authoritative scenario clock; adding a source acquisition command does not establish those authorities.\\n\\n`src/travel_claim/sources.py:162` requires all five original source specifications and an empty run directory. Manifest version 2 retains full response bodies, including failures; original and requested URLs, redirect destination, HTTP status, UTC start/end observations, supplied version headers, content hash/version, scope and errors. No-cache request headers request revalidation without conditional cached-body reuse. `assess_payload` at line 132 reads every PDF page, checks all ten known workbook tabs, and marks partial HTTP responses, missing text, corrupt documents and unverified policy HTML incomplete. `verify_source_manifest` at line 259 checks source identity, response bindings, byte hashes and scope/status consistency. Historical version 1 manifests remain verifiable without claiming fresh observations.\\n\\n`src/travel_claim/parsing.py:150` transcribes accessible partial documents alongside independent sources, preserves raw bytes and source references, reports transcription problems and invalid arrival membership without rounding, and derives policy errors from this run. Raw policy HTML is retained without inferred rules. Snapshot schema and sealing were inspected; this fresh attempt does not invoke offline replay or consume a business snapshot with unsupported authority. README and Skill now document this boundary.\\n\\n## Actual fresh attempt\\n\\nRun: `artifacts/runs/project-d-live-20261014T204849Z/`. Evidence: `sources.json`, `responses/`, `sources/`, `parsed-records.json`, `live-run.json` and `live-run.md`.\\n\\nAll five requests returned HTTP 200. Initial claims, claim updates and receipts PDFs were read completely by the supported text reader. The XLSX export contained all ten tabs. The Notion response was a 20,022-byte generic application shell, retained under `responses/policy-pol-2026-2.body` and hashed in the manifest; no policy body was accessible. PDF Last-Modified headers and workbook content hashes are retrieval/version facts, not a scenario clock.\\n\\nFresh transcription: 127 claim revisions, 123 trips, 5 permit records, 203 receipts, 307 decisions, 220 Finance activities and 9 cancellation activities. Source arrival membership remains batches 1–4. No case clock was supplied, no policy rules substituted, and no batches consumed. Overall and acquisition status are BLOCKED; final live-source compliance is false.\\n\\nMissing mechanism: no authenticated Notion API/block-tree, browser session or authorized native export adapter is exposed to this reader. Direct anonymous HTTP access is available and was attempted. Full policy access and verified rule interpretation, the authoritative date/time/timezone and supported processing authority remain necessary for a complete native claim execution.\\n\\n## Validation and preservation\\n\\n131 tests passed, including fresh retrieval, partial and failed access, error-body retention, duplicate-version fresh attempts, cache-directory rejection, response tampering, scanned PDF/missing tab handling, incomplete clock rejection and fractional batch preservation. `git diff --check` passed. All seven retained source manifests validate, including the fresh attempt. All 104 previously retained files and the original interview match their pre-work hashes; the interview also matches HEAD. No prior run was overwritten. Nothing staged, committed or pushed.\\n'''\\nwith path.open('x',encoding='utf-8') as f:f.write(text)\\nprint(path)\\nPY\\n git diff --check\\n git diff --cached --stat\",\"max_output_tokens\":500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a13c28-c6bd-7171-9c10-8efd3c67b498","create_time":1792011221.8962228}}}
