\n src/travel_claim/cli.py              |  24 +++-\n src/travel_claim/parsing.py          |  86 +++++++++---\n src/travel_claim/readiness.py        |   2 +-\n src/travel_claim/sources.py          | 262 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------\n tests/test_offline_replay.py         |  13 +-\n tests/test_parsing.py                |   2 +-\n tests/test_project_d_foundation.py   |  13 +-\n tests/test_readiness.py              |   2 +\n 10 files changed, 303 insertions(+), 127 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\nindex 2571251..16ea0a1 100644\n--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -138,3 +138,19 @@ Every corrected revision executes the connected evidence, calculation, trip/perm\n `correction-cancellation-verification.json` and `.md` demonstrate all retained corrections and independent trip/permit processes with source references, before/after cash facts, executed check results and next actions. They are explicitly retained-input offline outputs. The readiness command compares these artifacts with a deterministic replay and checks the sealed snapshot chain.\n \n Cancellation processing preserves the first event delivery, duplicate deliveries, employee/supervisor evidence, initiation/confirmation chronology, historical versus current claim links, and observed Finance request IDs. Orphan or partial confirmations remain unresolved with owned repair actions. Linked requests are held; unrelated claims continue. Explicit cancellation-bound Finance exceptions are recorded separately from policy eligibility and financial completion. A transfer cancellation never counts as a cash refund. Unknown disposition, approval, policy, case clock or closure authority remains blocked; absence of a claim does not imply absence of financial effects.\n+\n+## Fresh native-source acquisition and transcription\n+\n+```bash\n+travel-claim live-run <new-run-id> artifacts/runs/<new-run-id> [--case-clock '<authoritative scenario timestamp>']\n+```\n+\n+`live-run` attempts all five original locations using direct HTTP and native Google PDF/XLSX export routes, then verifies the manifest and transcribes accessible content from **this invocation**. It accepts no prior-run or cache input. Every run requires a new empty directory; existing manifests, parsed inputs, response files and snapshots cannot be reused. The optional clock is caller-supplied scenario evidence; retrieval timestamps never become a case clock.\n+\n+New captures use `native-source-manifest/2`. Each entry records the original source identity/URL, attempted export URL, redirect destination, HTTP status, start/end UTC observations, ETag or Last-Modified when supplied, content hash/version, accessible scope, error and missing scope. Complete response bodies are retained verbatim under `responses/`, including error pages and unusable shells; usable complete or partial documents are also bound under `sources/`. The verifier checks hashes, scope/status consistency and fresh response bindings. Legacy `/1` manifests remain readable for historical replay; they do not gain fresh-access evidence.\n+\n+A `read` PDF must be structurally readable with extractable text on every page. Scanned or partially readable documents require further verification. XLSX exports must contain all ten known workbook tabs; all returned bytes, tab content, cell values and numeric source evidence remain retained. Partial HTTP responses, mismatched byte counts, corrupt documents and incomplete workbook exports cannot pass complete acquisition. Usable partial sources are transcribed independently, with missing scope retained. Malformed arrival membership is reported without rounding or supplying a default.\n+\n+Plain HTTP access to a Notion shell does not establish policy access. Even policy-related HTML is marked **partial** because this reader cannot establish the complete authoritative block tree. The current reader has no authenticated Notion API/browser/export adapter. Complete policy access and policy rule interpretation remain required before policy-dependent execution; source bytes are never replaced by interview-derived rules or earlier downloads.\n+\n+`live-run.json` and `live-run.md` distinguish acquisition status from final business compliance. Exit `2` means **BLOCKED** (source access, transcription, clock or policy processing remains incomplete); exit `1` means **FAIL** for integrity/execution errors. The command performs fresh acquisition and loss-aware transcription, but does not consume arrival batches or certify final live-source claim compliance. The separate `offline-replay` command remains explicitly labeled retained-input evaluation. A successful `verify-sources` establishes integrity of recorded evidence, including failure observations, rather than completeness of all five sources.\ndiff --git a/skills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md b/skills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md\nindex 9e05b48..d79cb9d 100644\n--- a/skills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md\n+++ b/skills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md\n@@ -17,7 +17,13 @@ Never infer an approval, exception, source value, reply, or payment from a missi\n \n ## Invocation\n \n-Install as described in the repository [README](../../README.md). Capture sources for a new run with:\n+Install as described in the repository [README](../../README.md). Perform fresh acquisition and transcription for a new run with:\n+\n+```bash\n+travel-claim live-run <new-run-id> artifacts/runs/<new-run-id> [--case-clock '<authoritative scenario timestamp>']\n+```\n+\n+This attempts all five original sources, retains response evidence and emits `live-run.json`/`.md`. It never accepts prior inputs or consumes batches when clock/policy authority is missing. Direct Notion HTML cannot establish a complete policy block-tree read; authenticated native access remains required. Retrieval timestamps are observations, never an invented case clock. Source-only capture is also available:\n \n ```bash\n travel-claim capture-sources <run-id> artifacts/runs/<run-id> --case-clock '<scenario ISO timestamp>'\n@@ -75,4 +81,4 @@ Unknown money is null in JSON and blank in CSV. Zero is a known amount. Never la\n - On invalid or conflicting batch data, preserve the input evidence, reject admission of unsupported effects, and create an owned issue; do not silently discard it.\n - Retry a failed fresh retrieval only by making another live request and recording the new observation. Do not overwrite a prior run's manifest, retained bytes, or sealed snapshot.\n - On replay, preserve obligation/event identity and money; detect conflicting content under an existing event ID.\n-- Foundation implementation currently covers source capture/verification, retained PDF/workbook transcription, snapshot sealing/verification, the claims CSV writer, and local repair queue primitives. Scenario-state processing, policy/evidence decisions, approvals, Finance reconciliation, replay orchestration, and the complete operations report remain to be implemented and verified.\n+- Implemented paths include fresh HTTP/export acquisition and source-bound transcription, plus explicitly offline connected claim, correction, independent cancellation and Finance replay. New source manifests retain response observations and partial/error bodies. Complete native policy access, rule interpretation, authoritative case clock and supported completion authority remain required for final live business compliance; acquisition or offline integrity alone does not establish it.\ndiff --git a/src/travel_claim/cli.py b/src/travel_claim/cli.py\nindex 3be1433..27f028f 100644\n--- a/src/travel_claim/cli.py\n+++ b/src/travel_claim/cli.py\n@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ from pathlib import Path\n from jsonschema import Draft202012Validator, FormatChecker\n \n from .outputs import write_claims_csv\n+from .live_run import run_live_sources\n from .offline_replay import run_offline_replay\n from .readiness import readiness_summary, validate_readiness, write_readiness_reports\n from .parsing import parse_retained_run\n@@ -63,6 +64,12 @@ def build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n     capture.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path, help=\"new artifacts/runs/<run-id> directory\")\n     capture.add_argument(\"--case-clock\", help=\"supplied scenario clock; omit only for source-only capture\")\n \n+    live = commands.add_parser(\"live-run\", help=\"freshly attempt all five sources, retain and transcribe; report blockers without offline fallback\")\n+    live.add_argument(\"run_id\")\n+    live.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path)\n+    live.add_argument(\"--case-clock\", help=\"explicit authoritative scenario clock; never inferred from retrieval time\")\n+    live.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=float, default=30.0, help=\"per-request timeout seconds\")\n+\n     verify_sources = commands.add_parser(\"verify-sources\", help=\"verify source manifest and retained-byte hashes\")\n     verify_sources.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path)\n \n@@ -126,15 +133,24 @@ def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\n             return 1\n         print(f\"Snapshot is valid: {args.snapshot}\")\n         return 0\n+    if args.command == \"live-run\":\n+        try:\n+            report = run_live_sources(args.run_dir, run_id=args.run_id, case_clock=args.case_clock, timeout=args.timeout)\n+        except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:\n+            print(f\"Live-source attempt failed: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n+            return 1\n+        print(f\"LIVE SOURCE ATTEMPT {report['status']}: {args.run_id}; acquisition {report['acquisition_status']}; no cached fallback; final compliance not established\")\n+        print(f\"Report: {args.run_dir / 'live-run.md'}\")\n+        return {\"PASS\": 0, \"BLOCKED\": 2, \"FAIL\": 1}[report['status']]\n     if args.command == \"capture-sources\":\n         try:\n             manifest = capture_sources(args.run_dir, run_id=args.run_id, case_clock=args.case_clock)\n         except Exception as exc:\n             print(f\"Source capture failed: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n             return 1\n-        counts = {state: sum(row[\"status\"] == state for row in manifest[\"files\"]) for state in (\"read\", \"unavailable\")}\n-        print(f\"Source capture complete: {args.run_id} ({counts['read']} read, {counts['unavailable']} unavailable)\")\n-        return 0 if not counts[\"unavailable\"] else 2\n+        counts = {state: sum(row[\"status\"] == state for row in manifest[\"files\"]) for state in (\"read\", \"partial\", \"unavailable\")}\n+        print(f\"Source capture {'PASS' if counts['read'] == 5 else 'BLOCKED'}: {args.run_id} ({counts['read']} read, {counts['partial']} partial, {counts['unavailable']} unavailable)\")\n+        return 0 if counts[\"read\"] == 5 else 2\n     if args.command == \"verify-sources\":\n         errors = verify_source_manifest(args.run_dir)\n         if errors:\n@@ -159,7 +175,7 @@ def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\n             f\"{len(parsed['records']['cancellation_activities'])} cancellation activities; \"\n             f\"arrival batches {parsed['arrival_batches']}; case clock {parsed['case_clock_state']}\"\n         )\n-        return 0 if not parsed[\"missing_sources\"] and parsed[\"case_clock\"] else 2\n+        return 0 if not parsed[\"missing_sources\"] and not parsed.get(\"transcription_issues\") and parsed[\"case_clock\"] else 2\n     if args.command == \"seal-batch\":\n         try:\n             state = json.loads(args.state.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\ndiff --git a/src/travel_claim/parsing.py b/src/travel_claim/parsing.py\nindex fdf94e7..4b54531 100644\n--- a/src/travel_claim/parsing.py\n+++ b/src/travel_claim/parsing.py\n@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@ import hashlib\n import json\n import re\n from datetime import date, datetime, time\n+from decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\n from pathlib import Path\n from typing import Any\n \n@@ -46,7 +47,7 @@ def _pdf_pages(path: Path, source_id: str, sha256: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n     reader = PdfReader(path, strict=True)\n     pages: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n     for page_no, page in enumerate(reader.pages, 1):\n-        text = page.extract_text(extraction_mode=\"layout\") or \"\"\n+        text = (page.extract_text(extraction_mode=\"layout\") or \"\") if \"/Contents\" in page else \"\"\n         claim = re.search(r\"^\\s*Claim reference:\\s*(.+)$\", text, re.M)\n         receipt_refs = re.findall(r\"^\\s*Receipt reference:\\s*(.+)$\", text, re.M)\n         pages.append({\n@@ -152,22 +153,33 @@ def parse_retained_run(run_dir: Path, *, output_path: Path | None = None) -> dic\n     if errors:\n         raise ValueError(\"Cannot parse unverified retained sources: \" + \"; \".join(errors))\n     manifest = json.loads((run_dir / \"sources.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n-    read = {row[\"source_id\"]: row for row in manifest[\"files\"] if row[\"status\"] == \"read\"}\n+    read = {row[\"source_id\"]: row for row in manifest[\"files\"] if row[\"status\"] in {\"read\", \"partial\"}}\n     parsed_sources: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n+    transcription_issues = []\n     pages: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n     sheets: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n     for source_id, meta in read.items():\n         source_path = run_dir / meta[\"path\"]\n         if hashlib.sha256(source_path.read_bytes()).hexdigest() != meta[\"sha256\"]:\n             raise ValueError(f\"Retained-source hash changed during parse: {source_id}\")\n-        if source_path.suffix.lower() == \".pdf\":\n-            extracted = _pdf_pages(source_path, source_id, meta[\"sha256\"])\n-            pages.extend(extracted)\n-            parsed_sources.append({\"source_id\": source_id, \"kind\": \"pdf\", \"page_count\": len(extracted)})\n-        elif source_path.suffix.lower() == \".xlsx\":\n-            extracted_sheets = _workbook_sheets(source_path, source_id, meta[\"sha256\"])\n-            sheets.extend(extracted_sheets)\n-            parsed_sources.append({\"source_id\": source_id, \"kind\": \"xlsx\", \"sheet_c