{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T21:13:51.293Z","ordinal":1880,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02f4b2bd528e1b90016acff03ab3dc81909c7c9f0a12103392","status":"completed","call_id":"call_d15cad30f1d2475593946be57615a549","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat > /tmp/write-step167-audit.py <<'PY'\\nimport hashlib,json,subprocess\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom datetime import datetime,timezone\\nroot=Path.cwd()\\npolicy=root/'user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt'\\nraw=policy.read_bytes();text=raw.decode('utf-8',errors='strict')\\nexpected='f547ee77729be8ad431a5ddf2e2907f94f29ad50092231191abd2f72c04f54d2'\\nassert hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()==expected\\nassert text.splitlines()[0]=='# Project D · Alderbridge travel reimbursement policy · POL-2026.2'\\nassert 'Case clock: 2026-11-15, Europe/Amsterdam.' in text.splitlines()[2]\\nhead=subprocess.run(['git','rev-parse','HEAD'],capture_output=True,text=True,check=True).stdout.strip()\\nprovenance={'schema_version':'project-d-user-provided-policy/1','source_id':'user-browser-policy-pol-2026-2-step167',\\n 'path':str(policy.relative_to(root)),'sha256':expected,'expected_sha256_supplied_by':'user','hash_verified':True,\\n 'encoding':'UTF-8','utf8_decoding':'strict; successful','bytes':len(raw),'lines':len(text.splitlines()),\\n 'preserved_original_bytes':True,'policy_identifier':'POL-2026.2','identifier_reference':'line 1',\\n 'provenance_type':'user-provided authenticated/browser-visible copy',\\n 'source_url':'https://private-pecorino-70e.notion.site/REDACTED',\\n 'acquisition_attestation':'User states they personally copied the complete visible text from the original Notion page.',\\n 'browser_retrieval_time':None,'remote_block_tree_completeness_independently_verified':False,\\n 'complete_visible_text_user_attested':True,'native_http_or_api_read_performed_for_this_copy':False,\\n 'earlier_native_captures_reclassified':False,'audit_base_commit':head,\\n 'verification_observed_at_utc':datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\\n 'case_clock':{'case_date':'2026-11-15','timezone':'Europe/Amsterdam','time_of_day':None,'utc_instant':None,\\n  'precision':'local calendar date','policy_reference':'line 3','exact_source_text':'Case clock: 2026-11-15, Europe/Amsterdam.',\\n  'interpretation':'No midnight, end-of-day or event cutoff instant inferred.'}}\\nwith policy.with_suffix('.provenance.json').open('x',encoding='utf-8') as f:json.dump(provenance,f,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False);f.write('\\\\n')\\nprobes=json.loads(Path('/tmp/project-d-step167-probe-results.json').read_text())\\nwith Path('artifacts/verification/project-d-step167-audit-probes.json').open('x') as f:json.dump({'purpose':'Read-only synthetic audit probes; not retained claim outcomes','implementation_commit':head,'results':probes},f,indent=2);f.write('\\\\n')\\ndef link(path,line):return f'[{Path(path).name}:{line}]({root/path}:{line})'\\ndef pol(line):return link(str(policy.relative_to(root)),line)\\ndef code(module,line):return link('src/travel_claim/'+module+'.py',line)\\ndef test(file,line):return link('tests/'+file+'.py',line)\\nrows=[\\n(1,'Identity, effective scope and provenance','Verified evidence; adapter missing',f'Title identifies POL-2026.2; line 3 applies it to 2026 employee cost payments. Raw UTF-8 hash matches the user value. The engine accepts only trusted normalized policy records with a specific source ID and rule-set shape, not this browser-copy source. No ingestion/provenance adapter exists. {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",75)}; {code(\\\"parsing\\\",153)}.',f'Wrong policy-source masquerading is tested ({test(\\\"test_ordinary\\\",275)}); user-copy hash/provenance and rule mapping are not covered.'),\\n(3,'Case date, timezone, local dates and UTC events','Resolved date evidence; representation defect',f'Authoritative local case date is 2026-11-15 in Europe/Amsterdam, with no time of day. Current capture and closure gates require an offset-bearing datetime and live-run never consumes batches. Do not manufacture midnight or a UTC instant. Date-based decisions can use the declared local date; same-day instant ordering stays uncertain where material. {code(\\\"sources\\\",179)}; {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",279)}; {code(\\\"live_run\\\",39)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_live_run\\\",145)} currently rejects date-only values, so a provenance-bound date+zone needs new coverage. Fresh five-location attempts remain a requirement; the copy does not repair earlier captures.'),\\n(5,'Actual paid costs, personal/unknown category, evidence and gross VAT','Partial; missing personal-zero rule',f'Current receipt/settled merchant matching checks employee, trip, cost, currency and gross amount. Gross rather than VAT recovery is used. Unknowns remain null. Personal purchases are treated as unsupported category rather than an explicit zero-entitlement finding; no native-policy eligibility mapping exists. {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",125)}; {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",168)}.',f'Identity/proof are covered by {test(\\\"test_ordinary\\\",84)} and missing-condition cases at line 135. Add explicit personal zero versus unknown unresolved, gross-tax and category cases.'),\\n(7,'Transport/conference uncapped; lodging/night and meal/day caps','Partial; integer-unit defect',f'Destination/category/currency/payment-date cap lookup and minimum arithmetic exist, but positive integral total_limit is checked instead of integral documented units. A synthetic lodging line with 1.5 units and a 40.00 cap produces 6000 allowed cents. Unknown/multiple rates/caps hold. {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",171)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_ordinary\\\",221)} tests a synthetic capped transport rule, not the native category/unit contract. Add lodging/meals, positive integers, missing caps and effective-date boundaries.'),\\n(7,'Payment-date FX, EUR=1, line half-up conversion and rounded-line sum','Defect',f'FX lookup is payment-date based, but EUR still requires an FX row. Conversion rejects fractional cents instead of decimal half-up rounding. Synthetic 100.00 USD at 1.23455 has matched evidence but no allowed amount; policy requires 12346 cents. Summation exists only after exact-integer conversions. {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",184)}; {code(\\\"finance\\\",40)}.', 'No native half-up/per-line-versus-total rounding, EUR implicit rate or multi-rate payment-date boundary regressions exist. Preserve original exact rate/currency evidence.'),\\n(7,'Version/cost-bound Finance exceptions and covered issues','Missing application',f'Claim fields are transcribed and cancellation dispositions observed, but ordinary entitlement never applies replacement allowed original amounts or covered_issues. Actor membership, exact expense/revision, issue-specific coverage and retained original findings need validation. An exception must not replace missing paid proof or retroactively approve arrangements. {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",163)}; {code(\\\"integration\\\",385)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_revalidation\\\",108)} records native exceptions without entitlement changes. Add amount-only versus late_filing/late_permit/permit_unapproved/travel_cancellation coverage and rejected wrong bindings.'),\\n(9,'Domestic/international permission and blank commitment date','Partial; over-restrictive and incomplete',f'Domestic no-permit path exists with normalized rules. International path demands First commitment time (UTC), although native Trips provides a local First commitment date; blank explicitly means no commitment, not an invented missing timestamp. Same-day uncertain ordering must remain held; unambiguous calendar ordering need not demand a fabricated instant. Permit checks do not apply cancellation retirement. {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",94)}.', 'Add blank commitment, timely/late permit, date-only uncertainty, separate trip/permit revisions and renewed travel basis cases.'),\\n(9,'Separate permit/claim approvals, >1000 director, allowed role collapse','Partial; permit-role defects',f'Claim roles use directory identities and a configurable strict greater-than threshold; no native 100000-cent definition is loaded. Permit required roles are static, do not derive director need from estimate, and exact role-string equality rejects combined budget_owner/supervisor responses. Claim multi-role handling can combine roles but has no explicit administration/director non-collapse guard. {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",100)}; {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",219)}; {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",236)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_ordinary\\\",241)} tests a synthetic 5000-cent threshold, not permit/claim 100000 boundaries or allowed/forbidden role collapse.'),\\n(11,'Advance-paid filing; inclusive two calendar months; correction dates','Missing',f'Line first-submission dates are extracted, but no two-month/clamped inclusive deadline or submission-after-paid check is executed. Initial filing dates are not compared across revisions; new cost dates are not separately validated. Planned trip end must survive cancellation. {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",32)}; {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",163)}; {code(\\\"revalidation\\\",7)}.', 'Add 31-August to 31-October, month-end/leap-year, exact deadline/next day, paid-before-travel, late filing with/without exception, unchanged and added-cost dates.'),\\n(13,'Administration checks and full department/project/period budget','Major missing calculation',f'Packets only check that cited budget IDs exist; no allocation minus net settled expenditure minus remaining commitments calculation, ledger scope, pre-batch obligations or accepted-new-request accumulation is performed. Native Budget rows 6–8 contain allocation and prior obligation/settled data. Do not subtract both the full commitment and its settled component. {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",213)}.', 'No full-ledger/no-double-subtraction tests. Budget sufficiency must remain separate from human budget-owner approval.'),\\n(13,'Supervisor/director judgment and review context','Partial; packet sufficiency gap',f'Current packet matching compares trip business fields and expense IDs, but not calculated reviewed entitlement, complete estimate/director basis or full budget snapshot/position. Purpose/client/schedule/alternatives fields are retained. Automation correctly does not invent discretionary judgment. {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",220)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_ordinary\\\",192)} checks changed trip facts; add altered reviewed amount, estimate, budget-owner position and full packet source-version checks.'),\\n(15,'Decision subject/version/role/source validation; return/reject/withdrawal','Partial; state transitions missing',f'Claim current revision, roles and stable actor checks exist; rejected imports remain in history. Source revisions, affected fields and reason/repair requirements are not fully validated. Return/reject stop approvals but do not execute reviewer-specific reopening or legitimate rejected/withdrawn nonpayment terminal states. {code(\\\"workflow\\\",115)}; {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",202)}; {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",318)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_ordinary\\\",213)} tests conflicting review IDs; add stale source versions, wrong subject/actor, missing reason, concrete return routing, rejection/clean withdrawal and preserved paid effects.'),\\n(17,'Material corrections and dispatch/replacement readiness','Partial; affected authority gaps',f'All current ordinary/Finance checks rerun after revision increases with before/after audit and historical decisions retained. However inherited checks omit deadlines, exceptions, budget and cancellation-aware approvals. The audit trigger is revision increase; changed source authority under an unchanged claim revision is not independently represented as correction history. No dispatched/replacement-request state machine waits for explicit Finance status. {code(\\\"integration\\\",212)}; {code(\\\"revalidation\\\",26)}; {code(\\\"integration\\\",725)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_revalidation\\\",25)} covers stale approvals/receipt/amount changes; add source-policy/authority-only change and before/after-dispatch replacement holds.'),\\n(19,'Stable requests, shared/prepaid costs, linked adjustments','Major missing cross-claim ledger',f'Recorded request IDs and historical obligations are retained, but formal request linkage requires a separate normalized request record and explicit Finance claim revision absent from native headers. There is no cross-claim cost obligation index or subtraction of already committed/settled cost. C24 update page 3 reuses COST-03 and adds COST-24; this is a retained regression candidate, not a new entitlement result. {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",250)}; {code(\\\"finance\\\",94)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_retained_finance\\\",31)} covers ledger observations only. Add shared cost C03/C24, stable request redelivery, original request/cost/claim adjustment links and no duplicate reimbursement.'),\\n(21,'Finance event admission, failed/retry authorization and immutable conflicts','Critical defects',f'Cash admission checks EUR and exact nonnegative cents, but does not require a valid request, payee, directory Finance actor or event time; zero cash is allowed. Conflict recomputation excludes all occurrences including already admitted payments, reducing synthetic prior net cash 1000 to 0. Native retry-authorized events are classified but new attempts are not validated against them. {code(\\\"finance\\\",177)}; {code(\\\"finance\\\",239)}; {code(\\\"finance\\\",268)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_finance\\\",85)} currently asserts zero cash for a conflict; distinguish first-seen conflicted event from a later conflicting redelivery of admitted money. Existing synthetic payment tests omit mandatory authority fields.'),\\n(21,'Confirmed refunds and unrecovered transfer amount','Partial',f'Only supplied refund events change cash; linked original payment and aggregate upper bound exist. Refund request/payee/actor/time are not independently validated, and no chronological admission ledger preserves an already admitted refund when later invalid refund candidates exceed the original. {code(\\\"finance\\\",274)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_finance\\\",107)} covers orphan/over-refund and {test(\\\"test_retained_finance\\\",111)} duplicate refund. Add wrong payee/request/actor/time, sequential remaining-recoverable limit and preservation of earlier admitted refunds.'),\\n(23,'Balance, overpayment, partial settlement and financial closure','Partial; excessive and missing gates',f'Authorized obligation minus net paid exists, including negative balances; incomplete/unclassified events hold. Closure demands extra per-claim closure_authorities and an exact timestamp, which this policy does not require as separate blanket documents. It also holds every linked cancellation permanently, even after a possible valid disposition, and generic failed/cancelled controls require synthetic resolved-ID fields. Conversely correction after acceptance/payment does not universally require explicit current Finance resolution unless it happens to be a listed control event. {code(\\\"finance\\\",365)}; {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",277)}; {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",294)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_ordinary\\\",108)} closes only a synthetic extra-authority path. Add policy-native closure, overpayment repair, partial settlement, negative balance, correction/post-payment resolution, late transfer reopening and no-payment closure.'),\\n(25,'Independent progress, human authority and imported instructions as data','Mostly covered; incomplete-policy caveat',f'Integration processes claims independently and preserves owner-specific repairs. It does not send drafts, book travel or create human decisions. Imported text is transcribed data rather than execution permission. Passing local stages must not be advertised as full policy compliance while these gaps exist. {code(\\\"integration\\\",588)}; {code(\\\"live_run\\\",44)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_ordinary\\\",181)} checks unaffected claim closure; add malicious imported comment/receipt text and all-policy readiness reporting.'),\\n(27,'Cancellation actors, exact targets, initiation and strict times','Critical defects',f'Reducer admits structural confirmation before integration checks actors; wrong actor can remain confirmed in snapshot. It does not enforce no initiation/effective fields on request, full associated trip+permit target equality, strictly-later confirmation or effective==occurrence. Equal times and scheduled effective times pass synthetic probes. Blank commitment is not implemented as explicit no-commitment. {code(\\\"workflow\\\",216)}; {code(\\\"workflow\\\",247)}; {code(\\\"integration\\\",371)}; {code(\\\"integration\\\",417)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_revalidation\\\",75)} covers orphan/missing-effective/backward time but not equal time, scheduled/backdated effective, wrong actor or complete target tuples.'),\\n(29,'Arrival dependency recheck, conflicting redelivery and authority retirement','Critical/missing lifecycle behavior',f'Sorting by arrival batch then row causes a confirmation before its request in row/delivery order to remain unresolved even after the initiation is present. Conflicting IDs are excluded wholesale, so prior admitted history can disappear. No active/retired travel-authority state prevents old approval replies or later claim versions restoring permission; current versus historical claim linkage alone is insufficient. Future observations have no case-date cutoff. {code(\\\"workflow\\\",169)}; {code(\\\"workflow\\\",200)}; {code(\\\"workflow\\\",234)}; {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",94)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_workflow_structure\\\",111)} and {test(\\\"test_revalidation\\\",63)} cover structural lifecycle/dedup. Add deferred reference resolution, stale targets, future observations, process action conflicts and trip-versus-permit retirement/renewal.'),\\n(31,'Requested holds, no-financial-effect and cancellation-aware eligibility/reviews','Major missing semantics',f'Linked payment readiness holds, but new-arrangement pause is not modeled. Every process is projected financial_status=unresolved; supported no-cost/no-obligation processes cannot resolve to no-financial-effect. Cancellation exceptions are observed without covered-issue validation/application. Packet Travel cancellation references is present in retained evidence but ignored by current review checks. Existing lawful arrangements must not gain permit_unapproved solely from later cancellation. {code(\\\"integration\\\",330)}; {code(\\\"integration\\\",380)}; {code(\\\"integration\\\",391)}; {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",220)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_revalidation\\\",63)} currently expects an unresolved no-claim process; absence of a claim alone is not proof of no financial effect. Add scoped disposition coverage, post-confirmation packets, preserved planned end/initial filings and same-day ambiguity.'),\\n(33,'Pre-acceptance versus post-acceptance/payment cancellation','Major lifecycle over-hold and missing resolution linkage',f'Ordinary closure rejects any affected cancellation, regardless of timing/disposition. Policy permits pre-acceptance cancellation with bound disposition and fresh cancellation-aware reviews without a separate Finance resolution event. Post-acceptance/payment requires explicit resolution while preserving original obligations and observing late money; business confirmation cannot release commitment. Current Finance-cancelled classification does not update an accepted-commitment state, and financial_status never becomes resolved. {code(\\\"ordinary\\\",309)}; {code(\\\"integration\\\",380)}; {code(\\\"finance\\\",81)}.',f'{test(\\\"test_retained_finance\\\",95)} distinguishes transfer cancellation/refund and {test(\\\"test_revalidation\\\",108)} retains dispositions; add both timing branches, original-request late transfer, post-payment refund/resolution agreement and eventual supported cancellation closure.')]\\nlines=['# Step 167 — POL-2026.2 evidence and implementation gap audit','',f'Implementation inspected: `{head}`. Audit only; no implementation, prior capture, snapshot, or financial conclusion changed.','',\\n'## Verified policy and provenance','',f'- Exact UTF-8 file: {pol(1)}. SHA-256: `{expected}`. {len(raw)} bytes; {len(text.splitlines())} lines; strict UTF-8 decoding passed. The title says POL-2026.2.',\\n'- Complete browser-visible text is attested by the user, who states they personally copied it from the original Notion page. Hash matching verifies the supplied bytes; it does not independently prove a complete remote Notion block tree.',\\n'- Provenance is recorded separately in `user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.provenance.json`. This is not a fresh native HTTP/API capture, and earlier failed native observations remain unchanged.',\\nf'- {pol(3)} gives case date **2026-11-15**, timezone **Europe/Amsterdam**, with **no time of day**. No midnight/end-of-day default or UTC instant is inferred. Date-only filing and unambiguously earlier events do not need an invented instant. If a same-day future/cancellation ordering is material and cannot be resolved from UTC events/local dates, obtain only that missing timing evidence.',\\n'', '## Policy-section coverage matrix','', 'Each row summarizes a requirement; the original policy file remains the exact wording authority. Code/test links are exact audit anchors. “Missing” means no corresponding policy execution was found in the inspected source/tests, not missing user policy text.','', '| Policy reference | Section | Finding | Implementation evidence and impact | Tests and material gaps |','|---|---|---|---|---|']\\nfor n,section,status,evidence,tests in rows:lines.append(f'| {pol(n)} | {section} | **{status}** | {evidence} | {tests} |')\\nlines += ['', '## Prioritized findings','',\\n'1. **Admission/history defects:** prevent unsupported Finance money and wrong-actor/invalid-time cancellation admission; preserve previously admitted money and process history on conflicting redelivery. These are correctness defects, not newly missing human approvals.',\\n'2. **Policy calculations:** implement native category/personal-zero behavior, integer cap units, EUR=1, line half-up FX, date-based deadlines and scoped Finance exceptions. Budget accounting and shared-cost/prepayment exclusion are missing.',\\n'3. **Authority/lifecycle:** validate complete review packets/source versions, permit director/combined-role rules, returns/rejections/withdrawals, dispatch/replacement holds and cancellation authority retirement. Add the separate pre-/post-acceptance cancellation resolution paths.',\\n'4. **Source/clock integration:** retain user-copy provenance and derive reviewed policy definitions without masquerading as native HTTP content; represent date+zone without invented time. Revisit extra exact-clock/per-claim closure-authority gates now that policy completion conditions are supplied.',\\n'', '## Resolved knowledge blockers versus remaining evidence','',\\n'**Resolved for this audit:** the exact supplied policy wording and POL-2026.2 identifier; policy definition of category eligibility, amounts/caps/FX, roles/threshold, filing, correction, money and cancellation rules; the authoritative case date and timezone; the general financial-completion rule. The earlier “policy unknown” and “clock completely unknown” descriptions are historical evidence, not current audit findings. No earlier run is retroactively reclassified.',\\n'**Still not established:** a fresh programmatic native Notion read and independent remote completeness; a provenance-aware adapter linking this browser copy to future runs; implementation coverage; any missing claim-specific receipt/payment/rate/cap/role/review/exception/status/refund/resolution evidence; discretionary human decisions; timing only where actually material. Do not demand a separate generic facilitator closure approval or fabricated timestamp merely because the old synthetic implementation expects those fields.',\\n'**Concrete retained cases (observations, not new closure decisions):**',\\n'- C121: claim-updates-binder PDF page 6 contains the TC121-bound Finance exception; Review ledger/Review packets rows 307–309 contain r2 reviews with TC121 context; Travel cancellations rows 8–9 show the permit process; Finance activity row 224 first accepts REQ-C121 on 2026-09-13 and row 225 settles on 2026-09-14, after the 2026-09-12 confirmation. This is the policy line-33 pre-acceptance branch candidate. Absence of a separate resolution event is not automatically an external defect for that branch; full source validation and the other policy checks still remain.',\\n'- C19: claim-updates-binder PDF page 7 and Review ledger/Review packets rows 310–312 contain current TC019 disposition/context. Finance activity rows 44, 22–25 retain acceptance, payment, adjustment, linked refund and resolution. Those observations exist and must be semantically validated, not replaced by invented new approvals/events.',\\n'- C18: claim-updates-binder PDF page 4 reassigns T18 to T18B. Review ledger contains r1 decisions at rows 47–49 but no C18 r2 claim decisions in the retained input. Current r2 reviews are an independent missing scenario input; old-trip Finance request REQ-C18 and late payment must remain observable. Do not let the historical cancellation retire the different T18B travel basis.',\\n'- Source anchors above refer to `artifacts/runs/project-d-live-20261014T204849Z/parsed-records.json` and its byte-bound PDFs/XLSX in `sources/`; workbook SHA-256 `3cf8b225b20b9ac99b8d493b14a95fdde261d677aab77daaf399a37fb4dcef2f`. The audit does not change existing allowed/paid/balance/status projections.',\\n'', '## Validation and preservation','',\\n'- Existing tests are rerun unchanged. Passing existing tests does not establish compliance with the recovered policy; several synthetic fixtures deliberately omit newly grounded mandatory fields, and the conflict test currently codifies blanket cash exclusion.',\\n'- Nine read-only synthetic diagnostic probes are retained in `artifacts/verification/project-d-step167-audit-probes.json`; they do not represent real claims or new automated regression tests. No implementation or test files were edited.',\\n'- Raw policy bytes, all earlier artifact bytes, original interview and tracked implementation are checked for preservation. No new live capture, replay, financial projection, commit or push is performed.',\\n'', 'Stop point: evidence audit complete. Findings require a separately authorized implementation milestone; no fixes applied here.','']\\nwith Path('artifacts/verification/project-d-step167-policy-gap-audit.md').open('x',encoding='utf-8') as f:f.write('\\\\n'.join(lines))\\nprint('Wrote provenance, audit report and nine synthetic probe observations. Policy unchanged.')\\nPY\\n.venv/bin/python /tmp/write-step167-audit.py\",\"max_output_tokens\":1000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a13c40-3bbc-7d50-8ce8-5e7628d5b3da","create_time":1792012346.7072399}}}
