d historical obligations are retained, but formal request linkage requires a separate normalized request record and explicit Finance claim revision absent from native headers. There is no cross-claim cost obligation index or subtraction of already committed/settled cost. C24 update page 3 reuses COST-03 and adds COST-24; this is a retained regression candidate, not a new entitlement result. {code(\"ordinary\",250)}; {code(\"finance\",94)}.',f'{test(\"test_retained_finance\",31)} covers ledger observations only. Add shared cost C03/C24, stable request redelivery, original request/cost/claim adjustment links and no duplicate reimbursement.'),\n(21,'Finance event admission, failed/retry authorization and immutable conflicts','Critical defects',f'Cash admission checks EUR and exact nonnegative cents, but does not require a valid request, payee, directory Finance actor or event time; zero cash is allowed. Conflict recomputation excludes all occurrences including already admitted payments, reducing synthetic prior net cash 1000 to 0. Native retry-authorized events are classified but new attempts are not validated against them. {code(\"finance\",177)}; {code(\"finance\",239)}; {code(\"finance\",268)}.',f'{test(\"test_finance\",85)} currently asserts zero cash for a conflict; distinguish first-seen conflicted event from a later conflicting redelivery of admitted money. Existing synthetic payment tests omit mandatory authority fields.'),\n(21,'Confirmed refunds and unrecovered transfer amount','Partial',f'Only supplied refund events change cash; linked original payment and aggregate upper bound exist. Refund request/payee/actor/time are not independently validated, and no chronological admission ledger preserves an already admitted refund when later invalid refund candidates exceed the original. {code(\"finance\",274)}.',f'{test(\"test_finance\",107)} covers orphan/over-refund and {test(\"test_retained_finance\",111)} duplicate refund. Add wrong payee/request/actor/time, sequential remaining-recoverable limit and preservation of earlier admitted refunds.'),\n(23,'Balance, overpayment, partial settlement and financial closure','Partial; excessive and missing gates',f'Authorized obligation minus net paid exists, including negative balances; incomplete/unclassified events hold. Closure demands extra per-claim closure_authorities and an exact timestamp, which this policy does not require as separate blanket documents. It also holds every linked cancellation permanently, even after a possible valid disposition, and generic failed/cancelled controls require synthetic resolved-ID fields. Conversely correction after acceptance/payment does not universally require explicit current Finance resolution unless it happens to be a listed control event. {code(\"finance\",365)}; {code(\"ordinary\",277)}; {code(\"ordinary\",294)}.',f'{test(\"test_ordinary\",108)} closes only a synthetic extra-authority path. Add policy-native closure, overpayment repair, partial settlement, negative balance, correction/post-payment resolution, late transfer reopening and no-payment closure.'),\n(25,'Independent progress, human authority and imported instructions as data','Mostly covered; incomplete-policy caveat',f'Integration processes claims independently and preserves owner-specific repairs. It does not send drafts, book travel or create human decisions. Imported text is transcribed data rather than execution permission. Passing local stages must not be advertised as full policy compliance while these gaps exist. {code(\"integration\",588)}; {code(\"live_run\",44)}.',f'{test(\"test_ordinary\",181)} checks unaffected claim closure; add malicious imported comment/receipt text and all-policy readiness reporting.'),\n(27,'Cancellation actors, exact targets, initiation and strict times','Critical defects',f'Reducer admits structural confirmation before integration checks actors; wrong actor can remain confirmed in snapshot. It does not enforce no initiation/effective fiel