 rules, returns/rejections/withdrawals, dispatch/replacement holds and cancellation authority retirement. Add the separate pre-/post-acceptance cancellation resolution paths.',\n'4. **Source/clock integration:** retain user-copy provenance and derive reviewed policy definitions without masquerading as native HTTP content; represent date+zone without invented time. Revisit extra exact-clock/per-claim closure-authority gates now that policy completion conditions are supplied.',\n'', '## Resolved knowledge blockers versus remaining evidence','',\n'**Resolved for this audit:** the exact supplied policy wording and POL-2026.2 identifier; policy definition of category eligibility, amounts/caps/FX, roles/threshold, filing, correction, money and cancellation rules; the authoritative case date and timezone; the general financial-completion rule. The earlier “policy unknown” and “clock completely unknown” descriptions are historical evidence, not current audit findings. No earlier run is retroactively reclassified.',\n'**Still not established:** a fresh programmatic native Notion read and independent remote completeness; a provenance-aware adapter linking this browser copy to future runs; implementation coverage; any missing claim-specific receipt/payment/rate/cap/role/review/exception/status/refund/resolution evidence; discretionary human decisions; timing only where actually material. Do not demand a separate generic facilitator closure approval or fabricated timestamp merely because the old synthetic implementation expects those fields.',\n'**Concrete retained cases (observations, not new closure decisions):**',\n'- C121: claim-updates-binder PDF page 6 contains the TC121-bound Finance exception; Review ledger/Review packets rows 307–309 contain r2 reviews with TC121 context; Travel cancellations rows 8–9 show the permit process; Finance activity row 224 first accepts REQ-C121 on 2026-09-13 and row 225 settles on 2026-09-14, after the 2026-09-12 confirmation. This is the policy line-33 pre-acceptance branch candidate. Absence of a separate resolution event is not automatically an external defect for that branch; full source validation and the other policy checks still remain.',\n'- C19: claim-updates-binder PDF page 7 and Review ledger/Review packets rows 310–312 contain current TC019 disposition/context. Finance activity rows 44, 22–25 retain acceptance, payment, adjustment, linked refund and resolution. Those observations exist and must be semantically validated, not replaced by invented new approvals/events.',\n'- C18: claim-updates-binder PDF page 4 reassigns T18 to T18B. Review ledger contains r1 decisions at rows 47–49 but no C18 r2 claim decisions in the retained input. Current r2 reviews are an independent missing scenario input; old-trip Finance request REQ-C18 and late payment must remain observable. Do not let the historical cancellation retire the different T18B travel basis.',\n'- Source anchors above refer to `artifacts/runs/project-d-live-20261014T204849Z/parsed-records.json` and its byte-bound PDFs/XLSX in `sources/`; workbook SHA-256 `3cf8b225b20b9ac99b8d493b14a95fdde261d677aab77daaf399a37fb4dcef2f`. The audit does not change existing allowed/paid/balance/status projections.',\n'', '## Validation and preservation','',\n'- Existing tests are rerun unchanged. Passing existing tests does not establish compliance with the recovered policy; several synthetic fixtures deliberately omit newly grounded mandatory fields, and the conflict test currently codifies blanket cash exclusion.',\n'- Nine read-only synthetic diagnostic probes are retained in `artifacts/verification/project-d-step167-audit-probes.json`; they do not represent real claims or new automated regression tests. No implementation or test files were edited.',\n'- Raw policy bytes, all earlier artifact bytes, original interview and tracked implementation are checked for preservation. No new live capture, replay, financial projection, commit or push is performed.',\n'', 'Stop point: evidence audit complete. Findings require a separately authorized implementation milestone; no fixes applied here.','']\nwith Path('artifacts/verification/project-d-step167-policy-gap-audit.md').open('x',encoding='utf-8') as f:f.write('\\n'.join(lines))\nprint('Wrote provenance, audit report and nine synthetic probe observations. Policy unchanged.')\nPY\n.venv/bin/python /tmp/write-step167-audit.py"],"cwd":"file:///home/maxg/travel-expense-claim","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cat > /tmp/write-step167-audit.py <<'PY'\nimport hashlib,json,subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom datetime import datetime,timezone\nroot=Path.cwd()\npolicy=root/'user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt'\nraw=policy.read_bytes();text=raw.decode('utf-8',errors='strict')\nexpected='f547ee77729be8ad431a5ddf2e2907f94f29ad50092231191abd2f72c04f54d2'\nassert hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()==expected\nassert text.splitlines()[0]=='# Project D · Alderbridge travel reimbursement policy · POL-2026.2'\nassert 'Case clock: 2026-11-15, Europe/Amsterdam.' in text.splitlines()[2]\nhead=subprocess.run(['git','rev-parse','HEAD'],capture_output=True,text=True,check=True).stdout.strip()\nprovenance={'schema_version':'project-d-user-provided-policy/1','source_id':'user-browser-policy-pol-2026-2-step167',\n 'path':str(policy.relative_to(root)),'sha256':expected,'expected_sha256_supplied_by':'user','hash_verified':True,\n 'encoding':'UTF-8','utf8_decoding':'strict; successful','bytes':len(raw),'lines':len(text.splitlines()),\n 'preserved_original_bytes':True,'policy_identifier':'POL-2026.2','identifier_reference':'line 1',\n 'provenance_type':'user-provided authenticated/browser-visible copy',\n 'source_url':'https://private-pecorino-70e.notion.site/REDACTED',\n 'acquisition_attestation':'User states they personally copied the complete visible text from the original Notion page.',\n 'browser_retrieval_time':None,'remote_block_tree_completeness_independently_verified':False,\n 'complete_visible_text_user_attested':True,'native_http_or_api_read_performed_for_this_copy':False,\n 'earlier_native_captures_reclassified':False,'audit_base_commit':head,\n 'verification_observed_at_utc':datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n 'case_clock':{'case_date':'2026-11-15','timezone':'Europe/Amsterdam','time_of_day':None,'utc_instant':None,\n  'precision':'local calendar date','policy_reference':'line 3','exact_source_text':'Case clock: 2026-11-15, Europe/Amsterdam.',\n  'interpretation':'No midnight, end-of-day or event cutoff instant inferred.'}}\nwith policy.with_suffix('.provenance.json').open('x',encoding='utf-8') as f:json.dump(provenance,f,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False);f.write('\\n')\nprobes=json.loads(Path('/tmp/project-d-step167-probe-results.json').read_text())\nwith Path('artifacts/verification/project-d-step167-audit-probes.json').open('x') as f:json.dump({'purpose':'Read-only synthetic audit probes; not retained claim outcomes','implementation_commit':head,'results':probes},f,indent=2);f.write('\\n')\ndef link(path,line):return f'[{Path(path).name}:{line}]({root/path}:{line})'\ndef pol(line):return link(str(policy.relative_to(root)),line)\ndef code(module,line):return link('src/travel_claim/'+module+'.py',line)\ndef test(file,line):return link('tests/'+file+'.py',line)\nrows=[\n(1,'Identity, effective scope and provenance','Verified evidence; adapter missing',f'Title identifies POL-2026.2; line 3 applies it to 2026 employee cost payments. Raw UTF-8 hash matches the user value. The engine accepts only trusted normalized policy records with a specific source ID and rule-set shape, not this browser-copy source. No ingestion/provenance adapter exists. {code(\"ordinary\",75)}; {code(\"parsing\",153)}.',f'Wrong policy-source masquerading is tested ({test(\"test_ordinary\",275)}); user-copy hash/provenance and rule mapping are not covered.'),\n(3,'Case date, timezone, local dates and UTC events','Resolved date evidence; representation defect',f'Authoritative local case date is 2026-11-15 in Europe/Amsterdam, with no time of day. Current capture and closure gates require an offset-bearing datetime and live-run never consumes batches. Do not manufacture midnight or a UTC instant. Date-based decisions can use the declared local date; same-day instant ordering stays uncertain where material. {code(\"sources\",179)}; {code(\"ordinary\",279)}; {code(\"live_run\",39)}.',f'{test(\"test_live_run\",145)} currently rejects date-only values, so a provenance-bound date+zone needs new coverage. Fresh five-location attempts remain a requirement; the copy does not repair earlier captures.'),\n(5,'Actual paid costs, personal/unknown category, evidence and gross VAT','Partial; missing personal-zero rule',f'Current receipt/settled merchant matching checks employee, trip, cost, currency and gross amount. Gross rather than VAT recovery is used. Unknowns remain null. Personal purchases are treated as unsupported category rather than an explicit zero-entitlement finding; no native-policy eligibility mapping exists. {code(\"ordinary\",125)}; {code(\"ordinary\",168)}.',f'Identity/proof are covered by {test(\"test_ordinary\",84)} and missing-condition cases at line 135. Add explicit personal zero versus unknown unresolved, gross-tax and category cases.'),\n(7,'Transport/conference uncapped; lodging/night and meal/day caps','Partial; integer-unit defect',f'Destination/category/currency/payment-date cap lookup and minimum arithmetic exist, but positive integral total_limit is checked instead of integral documented units. A synthetic lodging line with 1.5 units and a 40.00 cap produces 6000 allowed cents. Unknown/multiple rates/caps hold. {code(\"ordinary\",171)}.',f'{test(\"test_ordinary\",221)} tests a synthetic capped transport rule, not the native category/unit contract. Add lodging/meals, positive integers, missing caps and effective-date boundaries.'),\n(7,'Payment-date FX, EUR=1, line half-up conversion and rounded-line sum','Defect',f'FX lookup is payment-date based, but EUR still requires an FX row. Conversion rejects fractional cents instead of decimal half-up rounding. Synthetic 100.00 USD at 1.23455 has matched evidence but no allowed amount; policy requires 12346 cents. Summation exists only after exact-integer conversions. {code(\"ordinary\",184)}; {code(\"finance\",40)}.', 'No native half-up/per-line-versus-total rounding, EUR implicit rate or multi-rate payment-date boundary regressions exist. Preserve original exact rate/currency evidence.'),\n(7,'Version/cost-bound Finance exceptions and covered issues','Missing application',f'Claim fields are transcribed and cancellation dispositions observed, but ordinary entitlement never applies replacement allowed original amounts or covered_issues. Actor membership, exact expense/revision, issue-specific coverage and retained original findings need validation. An exception must not replace missing paid proof or retroactively approve arrangements. {code(\"ordinary\",163)}; {code(\"integration\",385)}.',f'{test(\"test_revalidation\",108)} records native exceptions without entitlement changes. Add amount-only versus late_filing/late_permit/permit_unapproved/travel_cancellation coverage and rejected wrong bindings.'),\n(9,'Domestic/international permission and blank commitment date','Partial; over-restrictive and incomplete',f'Domestic no-permit path exists with normalized rules. International path demands First commitment time (UTC), although native Trips provides a local First commitment date; blank explicitly means no commitment, not an invented missing timestamp. Same-day uncertain ordering must remain held; unambiguous calendar ordering need not demand a fabricated instant. Permit checks do not apply cancellation retirement. {code(\"ordinary\",94)}.', 'Add blank commitment, timely/late permit, date-only uncertainty, separate trip/permit revisions and renewed travel basis cases.'),\n(9,'Separate permit/claim approvals, >1000 d