d without covered-issue validation/application. Packet Travel cancellation references is present in retained evidence but ignored by current review checks. Existing lawful arrangements must not gain permit_unapproved solely from later cancellation. {code(\"integration\",330)}; {code(\"integration\",380)}; {code(\"integration\",391)}; {code(\"ordinary\",220)}.',f'{test(\"test_revalidation\",63)} currently expects an unresolved no-claim process; absence of a claim alone is not proof of no financial effect. Add scoped disposition coverage, post-confirmation packets, preserved planned end/initial filings and same-day ambiguity.'),\n(33,'Pre-acceptance versus post-acceptance/payment cancellation','Major lifecycle over-hold and missing resolution linkage',f'Ordinary closure rejects any affected cancellation, regardless of timing/disposition. Policy permits pre-acceptance cancellation with bound disposition and fresh cancellation-aware reviews without a separate Finance resolution event. Post-acceptance/payment requires explicit resolution while preserving original obligations and observing late money; business confirmation cannot release commitment. Current Finance-cancelled classification does not update an accepted-commitment state, and financial_status never becomes resolved. {code(\"ordinary\",309)}; {code(\"integration\",380)}; {code(\"finance\",81)}.',f'{test(\"test_retained_finance\",95)} distinguishes transfer cancellation/refund and {test(\"test_revalidation\",108)} retains dispositions; add both timing branches, original-request late transfer, post-payment refund/resolution agreement and eventual supported cancellation closure.')]\nlines=['# Step 167 — POL-2026.2 evidence and implementation gap audit','',f'Implementation inspected: `{head}`. Audit only; no implementation, prior capture, snapshot, or financial conclusion changed.','',\n'## Verified policy and provenance','',f'- Exact UTF-8 file: {pol(1)}. SHA-256: `{expected}`. {len(raw)} bytes; {len(text.splitli