{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T21:16:16.913Z","ordinal":1922,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a13bd1-7420-72c0-963e-58742d1be7bf","turn_id":"01a13c45-9846-7111-9cb7-eca8b1cc3957","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a25d14fd-379b-4ed1-a13e-a061b29232c0","process_id":"12985","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","cat tests/test_integration.py | head -165; sed -n '15,125p' tests/test_retained_finance.py; sed -n '90,155p' tests/test_workflow_structure.py; sed -n '90,118p' src/travel_claim/integration.py; cat skills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md | tail -28"],"cwd":"file:///home/maxg/travel-expense-claim","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat tests/test_integration.py","name":"test_integration.py","path":"tests/test_integration.py"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '15,125p' tests/test_retained_finance.py","name":"test_retained_finance.py","path":"tests/test_retained_finance.py"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '90,155p' tests/test_workflow_structure.py","name":"test_workflow_structure.py","path":"tests/test_workflow_structure.py"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '90,118p' src/travel_claim/integration.py","name":"integration.py","path":"src/travel_claim/integration.py"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat skills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":"skills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"\"\"\"Synthetic end-to-end integration tests; no real arrival batch is consumed.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom jsonschema import Draft202012Validator, FormatChecker\nimport pytest\n\nfrom travel_claim.integration import integrate_arrival_batch\n\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nSCHEMA = json.loads((ROOT / \"snapshot.schema.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n\n\ndef _claim(claim_id, revision, *, trip_id, trip_revision=1, batch=1, employee=\"EMP-SYN-01\"):\n    return {\n        \"source_id\": \"synthetic-claim-binder\",\n        \"source_sha256\": \"a\" * 64,\n        \"locator\": f\"PDF page {revision} (SYNTHETIC {claim_id} revision {revision})\",\n        \"page\": revision,\n        \"fields\": [\n            {\"label\": \"Claim reference\", \"value\": claim_id},\n            {\"label\": \"Revision\", \"value\": str(revision)},\n            {\"label\": \"Arrival batch\", \"value\": str(batch)},\n            {\"label\": \"Employee\", \"value\": employee},\n            {\"label\": \"Trip reference\", \"value\": trip_id},\n            {\"label\": \"Trip revision\", \"value\": str(trip_revision)},\n            {\"label\": \"Claim reason\", \"value\": \"SYNTHETIC fixture\"},\n        ],\n        \"text\": f\"SYNTHETIC TEST FIXTURE ONLY: {claim_id} revision {revision}\",\n    }\n\n\ndef _row(row, source_id, tab, **values):\n    return {\n        \"source_id\": source_id,\n        \"source_sha256\": \"b\" * 64,\n        \"locator\": f\"tab '{tab}', row {row} (SYNTHETIC)\",\n        \"row\": row,\n        \"values\": {\n            key: {\"value\": value, \"source_text\": str(value), \"cell\": f\"A{row}\"}\n            for key, value in values.items()\n        },\n    }\n\n\ndef _decision(row, decision_id, claim_id, revision, batch=1):\n    return _row(\n        row, \"synthetic-review-ledger\", \"Review ledger\",\n        **{\n            \"Decision reference\": decision_id,\n            \"Arrival batch\": batch,\n            \"Subject type\": \"claim\",\n            \"Subject reference\": claim_id,\n            \"Revision\": revision,\n            \"Review roles\": \"administration\",\n            \"Reviewer\": \"ADMIN-SYN-01\",\n            \"Outcome\": \"approve\",\n            \"Reason\": \"SYNTHETIC observed decision; no policy conclusion\",\n            \"Decision time (UTC)\": \"2026-09-01T12:00:00\",\n        },\n    )\n\n\ndef _finance(row, event_id, claim_id, batch, event_type, *, amount=None, obligation=None):\n    values = {\n        \"Activity reference\": event_id,\n        \"Arrival batch\": batch,\n        \"Activity type\": event_type,\n        \"Request reference\": f\"REQ-{claim_id}\",\n        \"Claim reference\": claim_id,\n        \"Finance officer\": \"FIN-SYN-01\",\n        \"Payee ID\": \"EMP-SYN-01\",\n        \"Currency\": \"EUR\",\n        \"Reason\": f\"SYNTHETIC Finance fixture: {event_type}\",\n    }\n    if amount is not None:\n        values[\"Amount (EUR)\"] = amount\n    if obligation is not None:\n        values[\"Obligation (EUR)\"] = obligation\n    return _row(row, \"synthetic-finance-register\", \"Finance activity\", **values)\n\n\ndef _cancel(row, event_id, cancellation_id, action, subject_type, *, batch, initiation=None):\n    is_permit = subject_type == \"permit\"\n    values = {\n        \"Cancellation activity reference\": event_id,\n        \"Cancellation reference\": cancellation_id,\n        \"Action\": action,\n        \"Cancelled subject\": subject_type,\n        \"Trip reference\": \"T-SYN-01\",\n        \"Trip revision\": 1,\n        \"Permit reference\": \"P-SYN-01\",\n        \"Permit revision\": 1,\n        \"Acting employee or supervisor\": \"EMP-SYN-01\",\n        \"Activity time (UTC)\": f\"2026-09-0{batch}T09:00:00\",\n        \"Arrival batch\": batch,\n        \"Business reason\": \"SYNTHETIC client rescheduling\",\n    }\n    if action == \"confirmed\":\n        values[\"Initiation activity reference\"] = initiation\n        values[\"Effective time (UTC)\"] = f\"2026-09-0{batch}T09:30:00\"\n    return _row(row, \"synthetic-travel-register\", \"Travel cancellations\", **values)\n\n\ndef _parsed_fixture():\n    return {\n        \"run_id\": \"run-synthetic-integration\",\n        \"case_clock\": None,\n        \"unresolved_issues\": [\n            {\n                \"record_id\": \"scenario-case-clock\",\n                \"subject_type\": \"scenario\",\n                \"subject_id\": \"arrival-batch-clock\",\n                \"affected_scope\": \"all batches\",\n                \"reason\": \"SYNTHETIC fixture: clock withheld\",\n                \"owner\": \"Exercise facilitator\",\n                \"next_action\": \"provide the scenario clock\",\n                \"evidence_needed\": \"explicit date, time, and zone\",\n            },\n            {\n                \"record_id\": \"reimbursement-policy-pol-2026-2\",\n                \"subject_type\": \"policy\",\n                \"subject_id\": \"POL-2026.2\",\n                \"affected_scope\": \"eligibility and entitlement\",\n                \"reason\": \"SYNTHETIC fixture: policy withheld\",\n                \"owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n                \"next_action\": \"provide an authorized native policy export\",\n                \"evidence_needed\": \"complete policy content\",\n            },\n        ],\n        \"records\": {\n            \"claim_revisions\": [\n                _claim(\"C-SYN-01\", 1, trip_id=\"T-SYN-01\", batch=1),\n                _claim(\"C-SYN-02\", 1, trip_id=\"T-SYN-02\", batch=1, employee=\"EMP-SYN-02\"),\n                _claim(\"C-SYN-01\", 2, trip_id=\"T-SYN-01\", batch=3),\n            ],\n            \"trips\": [\n                _row(6, \"synthetic-travel-register\", \"Trips\", **{\n                    \"Trip reference\": \"T-SYN-01\", \"Trip revision\": 1,\n                    \"Permit reference\": \"P-SYN-01\", \"Permit revision\": 1,\n                }),\n                _row(7, \"synthetic-travel-register\", \"Trips\", **{\n                    \"Trip reference\": \"T-SYN-02\", \"Trip revision\": 1,\n                    \"Permit reference\": \"P-SYN-02\", \"Permit revision\": 1,\n                }),\n            ],\n            \"decisions\": [\n                _decision(6, \"D-SYN-01-R1\", \"C-SYN-01\", 1),\n                _decision(7, \"D-SYN-02-R1\", \"C-SYN-02\", 1),\n            ],\n            \"finance_events\": [\n                _finance(6, \"F-SYN-01-SETTLED\", \"C-SYN-01\", 2, \"settled\", amount=10.00),\n                _finance(7, \"F-SYN-01-PENDING\", \"C-SYN-01\", 2, \"transfer_pending\", amount=5.00),\n                _finance(8, \"F-SYN-02-SETTLED\", \"C-SYN-02\", 2, \"settled\", amount=4.00),\n            ],\n            \"cancellation_activities\": [\n                _cancel(6, \"TC-SYN-TRIP-REQ\", \"TC-SYN-TRIP\", \"requested\", \"trip\", batch=1),\n                _cancel(7, \"TC-SYN-PERMIT-REQ\", \"TC-SYN-PERMIT\", \"requested\", \"permit\", batch=1),\n                _cancel(8, \"TC-SYN-TRIP-CFM\", \"TC-SYN-TRIP\", \"confirmed\", \"trip\", batch=2,\n                        initiation=\"TC-SYN-TRIP-REQ\"),\n                _cancel(9, \"TC-SYN-PERMIT-CFM\", \"TC-SYN-PERMIT\", \"confirmed\", \"permit\", batch=2,\n                        initiation=\"TC-SYN-PERMIT-REQ\"),\n\n\ndef _batches(parsed):\n    prior = None\n    results = []\n    for batch in parsed['arrival_batches']:\n        prior = integrate_arrival_batch(\n            parsed, arrival_batch=batch, run_id='retained-regression', batch_id=f'arrival-{batch:03d}',\n            source_binding={'path': 'sources.json', 'sha256': 'a' * 64},\n            predecessor={'path': f'batches/arrival-{batch-1:03d}.json', 'sha256': 'b' * 64} if prior else None,\n            prior_result=prior,\n        )\n        results.append(prior)\n    return results\n\n\ndef test_native_obligation_fields_and_ledger_balances_do_not_become_entitlement():\n    parsed = _fixture()\n    assert 'Claim revision' not in parsed['provenance']['finance_headers']\n    results = _batches(parsed)\n    final = results[-1]\n    c1 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C01']\n    obligation = c1['recorded_obligation']\n    assert obligation['event_id'] == 'F-C01-accepted'\n    assert obligation['request_id'] == 'REQ-C01'\n    assert obligation['finance_officer'] == 'FIN-01'\n    assert obligation['payee_id'] == 'EMP-01'\n    assert obligation['amount_cents'] == 10000\n    assert obligation['claim_revision'] is None\n    assert obligation['arrival_revision_context'] == 1\n    assert obligation['revision_link_status'] == 'arrival_context_only'\n    assert obligation['first_arrival_batch'] == 1\n    assert obligation['source_refs'] == [\n        'travel-registers-workbook@' + parsed['provenance']['workbook_sha256'] + \"#tab 'Finance activity', row 33\"\n    ]\n    assert obligation['claim_source_refs'][0]['locator'] == 'PDF page 1'\n    assert c1['net_confirmed_cents'] == 10000  # delivered twice, counted once\n    assert c1['duplicate_events'][0]['delivery_batches'] == [2, 4]\n    assert c1['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n    assert c1['authorized_obligation'] is None\n    assert c1['balance_cents'] is None\n    assert c1['closure_authority_confirmed'] is False\n    projected = next(c for c in final['snapshot']['claims'] if c['claim_id'] == 'C01')\n    assert projected['finance_evidence']['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n    assert projected['allowed_cents'] is None and projected['status'] == 'pending'\n\n\ndef test_native_corrections_keep_ledger_history_and_revalidate_authority_only_where_affected():\n    results = _batches(_fixture())\n    first, _, third, final = results\n    initial = deepcopy(first)\n    c19 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C19']\n    assert [(r['event_id'], r['amount_cents'], r['arrival_revision_context']) for r in c19['recorded_obligation_history']] == [\n        ('F-C19-accepted', 10000, 1), ('F-C19-2', 8000, 2), ('F-C19-4', 8000, 3),\n    ]\n    assert c19['confirmed_payment_cents'] == 10000\n    assert c19['confirmed_refund_cents'] == 2000\n    assert c19['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n    assert c19['recorded_obligation']['claim_revision'] is None\n    assert c19['invalidated_previous_reconciliation']['claim_revision'] == 2\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C09']['recorded_obligation']['arrival_revision_context'] == 2\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C12']['recorded_obligation']['amount_cents'] == 7000\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C01']['recorded_obligation'] == first['finance_reconciliations']['C01']['recorded_obligation']\n    # C18 correction has no newly bound accepted amount. Retain r1 context;\n    # neither cancellation nor a fresh payment silently reauthorizes revision 2.\n    c18 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C18']\n    assert c18['claim_revision'] == 2\n    assert c18['recorded_obligation']['arrival_revision_context'] == 1\n    assert c18['authorized_obligation'] is None\n    assert c18['confirmed_payment_cents'] == 10000\n    item = final['domain']['repair_queue']['items']['finance:finance-obligation-missing:C09:1']\n    # Historic question remains historic; r2 has its own current authorization question.\n    assert item['revision'] == 1\n    current = final['domain']['repair_queue']['items']['finance:finance-obligation-missing:C09:2']\n    assert current['source_refs']\n    assert 'recorded Finance obligation exists' in current['missing_or_return_reason']\n    assert current['status'] == 'open'\n    assert first == initial\n\n\ndef test_native_refund_and_finance_cancellation_are_independent_of_business_cancellations():\n    final = _batches(_fixture())[-1]\n    cancellations = {c['cancellation_id']: c for c in final['snapshot']['travel_cancellations']}\n    assert cancellations['TC122']['affected_claim_ids'] == []\n    assert cancellations['TC122']['target_type'] == 'trip'\n    assert cancellations['TC121']['target_type'] == 'permit'\n    assert all(c['financial_status'] == 'unresolved' for c in cancellations.values())\n    c18 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C18']\n    assert c18['recorded_obligation']['amount_cents'] == 10000\n    assert c18['confirmed_refund_cents'] == 0  # cancelled transfer is not a refund\n    c20 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C20']\n    assert c20['recorded_obligation']['amount_cents'] == 10000\n    assert c20['confirmed_refund_cents'] == 1000\n    assert c20['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n\n\ndef test_duplicate_refund_and_accepted_redelivery_keep_identity_and_original_revision_context():\n    parsed = _fixture()\n    accepted = deepcopy(next(r for r in parsed['records']['finance_events'] if r['values']['Activity reference']['value'] == 'F-C18-accepted'))\n    accepted['row'] = 998\n    accepted['locator'] = \"tab 'Finance activity', row 998 (synthetic redelivery)\"\n    accepted['values']['Arrival batch']['value'] = 4\n    refund = deepcopy(next(r for r in parsed['records']['finance_events'] if r['values']['Activity reference']['value'] == 'F-C20-2'))\n    refund['row'] = 999\n    refund['locator'] = \"tab 'Finance activity', row 999 (synthetic redelivery)\"\n    refund['values']['Arrival batch']['value'] = 4\n    parsed['records']['finance_events'].extend([accepted, refund])\n    final = _batches(parsed)[-1]\n    c18 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C18']\n    assert len(c18['recorded_obligation_history']) == 1\n    assert c18['recorded_obligation']['delivery_batches'] == [1, 4]\n        }\n    }\n    history = build_revision_history(parsed)\n    assert [row[\"revision\"] for row in history[\"claim\"][\"C-SYN-01\"][\"revisions\"]] == [1, 2]\n    assert history[\"claim\"][\"C-SYN-01\"][\"current_revision\"] == 2\n    assert history[\"trip\"][\"T-SYN-01\"][\"current_revision\"] == 2\n    assert history[\"permit\"][\"P-SYN-01\"][\"current_revision\"] == 1\n    assert history[\"claim\"][\"C-SYN-01\"][\"revisions\"][1][\"trip_revision\"] == 1\n\n    decisions = [\n        _workbook_record(10, **{\"Decision reference\": \"D-SYN-OLD\", \"Subject type\": \"claim\",\n                                \"Subject reference\": \"C-SYN-01\", \"Revision\": 1, \"Outcome\": \"approve\"}),\n        _workbook_record(11, **{\"Decision reference\": \"D-SYN-UNKNOWN\", \"Subject type\": \"trip\",\n                                \"Subject reference\": \"T-SYN-01\", \"Revision\": 9, \"Outcome\": \"return\"}),\n    ]\n    matches = match_decisions_to_subjects(decisions, history)\n    assert [row[\"structural_match\"] for row in matches] == [\"revision_match_historical\", \"revision_not_found\"]\n    assert [row[\"applied\"] for row in matches] == [False, False]\n    assert matches[0][\"observed_outcome\"] == \"approve\"  # preserved observation; no approval is performed\n\n\ndef test_cancellation_state_machine_keeps_trip_and_permit_processes_independent():\n    events = [\n        _cancellation_row(6, event_id=\"TC-SYN-P-REQ\", cancellation_id=\"TC-SYN-P\",\n                          action=\"requested\", target_type=\"permit\", target_id=\"P-SYN-01\", batch=1),\n        _cancellation_row(7, event_id=\"TC-SYN-T-REQ\", cancellation_id=\"TC-SYN-T\",\n                          action=\"requested\", target_type=\"trip\", target_id=\"T-SYN-01\", batch=1),\n        _cancellation_row(8, event_id=\"TC-SYN-P-CFM\", cancellation_id=\"TC-SYN-P\",\n                          action=\"confirmed\", target_type=\"permit\", target_id=\"P-SYN-01\", batch=2,\n                          initiation=\"TC-SYN-P-REQ\", effective=\"2026-11-16T09:00:00+01:00\"),\n    ]\n    result = reduce_cancellation_activities(events)\n    assert result[\"processes\"][\"TC-SYN-P\"][\"state\"] == \"confirmed\"\n    assert result[\"processes\"][\"TC-SYN-T\"][\"state\"] == \"requested\"\n    assert result[\"processes\"][\"TC-SYN-T\"][\"next_action\"] == \"await a linked confirmation activity\"\n    assert result[\"finance_effects\"] == []\n    assert result[\"claim_effects\"] == []\n    assert result[\"processes\"][\"TC-SYN-P\"][\"target\"] == {\n        \"subject_type\": \"permit\", \"subject_id\": \"P-SYN-01\", \"revision\": 1,\n    }\n\n\ndef test_event_deduplication_is_replay_safe_and_flags_same_id_payload_conflicts():\n    # Synthetic Finance-like event IDs; arrival batch is delivery metadata.\n    first = _workbook_record(6, **{\"Activity reference\": \"F-SYN-01\", \"Arrival batch\": 2,\n                                  \"Activity type\": \"settled\", \"Amount (EUR)\": 100.0,\n                                  \"Claim reference\": \"C-SYN-01\"})\n    replay = _workbook_record(31, **{\"Activity reference\": \"F-SYN-01\", \"Arrival batch\": 4,\n                                    \"Activity type\": \"settled\", \"Amount (EUR)\": 100.0,\n                                    \"Claim reference\": \"C-SYN-01\"})\n    changed = _workbook_record(32, **{\"Activity reference\": \"F-SYN-01\", \"Arrival batch\": 4,\n                                      \"Activity type\": \"settled\", \"Amount (EUR)\": 120.0,\n                                      \"Claim reference\": \"C-SYN-01\"})\n    exact = deduplicate_activity_records([first, replay], id_field=\"Activity reference\")\n    assert len(exact[\"unique_events\"]) == 1\n    assert exact[\"duplicates\"][0][\"delivery_batches\"] == [2, 4]\n    assert exact[\"conflicts\"] == []\n    conflict = deduplicate_activity_records([first, changed], id_field=\"Activity reference\")\n    assert conflict[\"unique_events\"] == []\n    assert conflict[\"conflicts\"][0][\"event_id\"] == \"F-SYN-01\"\n\n\ndef test_actual_retained_activity_replays_are_deduplicated_and_cancellation_ids_are_separate(tmp_path):\n    parsed = parse_retained_run(CAPTURE, output_path=tmp_path / \"parsed.json\")\n    history = build_revision_history(parsed)\n    c09 = history[\"claim\"][\"C09\"]\ndef _domain_seed() -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\n        \"processed_batches\": [],\n        \"batch_input_hashes\": {},\n        \"claim_records\": [],\n        \"decision_records\": [],\n        \"finance_records\": [],\n        \"cancellation_records\": [],\n        \"revision_history\": None,\n        \"decision_history\": [],\n        \"finance_reconciliations\": {},\n        \"ordinary_workflows\": {},\n        \"ordinary_workflow_history\": [],\n        \"authorized_obligations\": {},\n        \"source_classifications\": {},\n        \"cancellation_state\": {},\n        \"material_corrections\": [],\n        \"repair_queue\": new_repair_queue(),\n        \"policy_clock_blockers\": [],\n        \"structural_blockers\": [],\n        \"projection_issues\": [],\n    }\n\n\ndef _issue_from_item(item: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\n        \"record_id\": item[\"item_id\"],\n        \"reason\": item[\"missing_or_return_reason\"],\n        \"owner\": item[\"owner\"],\n1. Bind every fact and decision to its source, subject, and revision.\n2. Hold only claims or dependent work affected by missing/conflicting facts. Continue independent valid work. Each unresolved item retains subject type and exact ID, revision, missing/conflicting fact, responsible owner, source reference, and next action.\n3. Preserve every claim revision. After a material correction, use the corrected revision and revalidate affected evidence, calculations, trip/permit consistency, approvals, and Finance authorization. Preserve unrelated evidence only where it remains valid. Retain historical commitments, transfers, and refunds; do not use stale approvals as current.\n4. Keep trip cancellation and permit cancellation as independent processes, including processes without claims. Cancellation does not itself erase entitlement or Finance obligations. Record Finance disposition and monetary resolution separately when required.\n5. Use the owner-grouped local repair queue. Keep each item individually traceable. A partial response may resolve only the item(s) explicitly matched and supported by retained source evidence; unanswered, insufficient, or conflicting items stay open. Draft locally; never send requests.\n6. Preserve immutable Finance event identifiers. Reconcile only confirmed transfers and refunds. Do not duplicate events or obligations on replay.\n7. The provisional financial closure choice is to require current evidence and approvals, agreement between reviewed entitlement and authorized obligation, net confirmed payment equal to the authorized amount, required Finance resolutions, and no blocking issue. After the first actual processing result, pause for the operator to inspect reconciliation and unresolved cases and confirm final completion conditions and delivery scope.\n\nPeople retain business approval, exception, and payment authority. This Skill prepares work, validates supplied decisions, and records effects; it does not make discretionary approval recommendations, create replies, issue Finance exceptions, book travel, or move funds.\n\n## Outputs\n\n- `artifacts/runs/<run-id>/sources.json` and retained source bytes.\n- One immutable schema-valid `batches/<batch-id>.json` per consumed batch, with relative source and predecessor paths plus SHA-256 hashes.\n- `claims.csv` with exactly `claim_id,revision,trip_id,status,allowed_cents,paid_cents,balance_cents,next_owner,reason`.\n- Owner-grouped local repair queue with individual items and run/batch update history.\n- `report.md` describing completed work, obligations, unresolved items, owners, next actions, cancellations without claims, and source/run references.\n\nUnknown money is null in JSON and blank in CSV. Zero is a known amount. Never label incomplete work complete.\n\n## Errors, retries, and limitations\n\n- On source failure, retain the attempt URL, locator, UTC observation time, error, and missing scope. Hold only affected work and report its owner and resumption evidence.\n- On partial source access, retain usable pieces and explicitly list missing scope. Do not claim the source was fully read.\n- On invalid or conflicting batch data, preserve the input evidence, reject admission of unsupported effects, and create an owned issue; do not silently discard it.\n- Retry a failed fresh retrieval only by making another live request and recording the new observation. Do not overwrite a prior run's manifest, retained bytes, or sealed snapshot.\n- On replay, preserve obligation/event identity and money; detect conflicting content under an existing event ID.\n- Implemented paths include fresh HTTP/export acquisition and source-bound transcription, plus explicitly offline connected claim, correction, independent cancellation and Finance replay. New source manifests retain response observations and partial/error bodies. Complete native policy access, rule interpretation, authoritative case clock and supported completion authority remain required for final live business compliance; acquisition or offline integrity alone does not establish it.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Synthetic end-to-end integration tests; no real arrival batch is consumed.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom jsonschema import Draft202012Validator, FormatChecker\nimport pytest\n\nfrom travel_claim.integration import integrate_arrival_batch\n\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nSCHEMA = json.loads((ROOT / \"snapshot.schema.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n\n\ndef _claim(claim_id, revision, *, trip_id, trip_revision=1, batch=1, employee=\"EMP-SYN-01\"):\n    return {\n        \"source_id\": \"synthetic-claim-binder\",\n        \"source_sha256\": \"a\" * 64,\n        \"locator\": f\"PDF page {revision} (SYNTHETIC {claim_id} revision {revision})\",\n        \"page\": revision,\n        \"fields\": [\n            {\"label\": \"Claim reference\", \"value\": claim_id},\n            {\"label\": \"Revision\", \"value\": str(revision)},\n            {\"label\": \"Arrival batch\", \"value\": str(batch)},\n            {\"label\": \"Employee\", \"value\": employee},\n            {\"label\": \"Trip reference\", \"value\": trip_id},\n            {\"label\": \"Trip revision\", \"value\": str(trip_revision)},\n            {\"label\": \"Claim reason\", \"value\": \"SYNTHETIC fixture\"},\n        ],\n        \"text\": f\"SYNTHETIC TEST FIXTURE ONLY: {claim_id} revision {revision}\",\n    }\n\n\ndef _row(row, source_id, tab, **values):\n    return {\n        \"source_id\": source_id,\n        \"source_sha256\": \"b\" * 64,\n        \"locator\": f\"tab '{tab}', row {row} (SYNTHETIC)\",\n        \"row\": row,\n        \"values\": {\n            key: {\"value\": value, \"source_text\": str(value), \"cell\": f\"A{row}\"}\n            for key, value in values.items()\n        },\n    }\n\n\ndef _decision(row, decision_id, claim_id, revision, batch=1):\n    return _row(\n        row, \"synthetic-review-ledger\", \"Review ledger\",\n        **{\n            \"Decision reference\": decision_id,\n            \"Arrival batch\": batch,\n            \"Subject type\": \"claim\",\n            \"Subject reference\": claim_id,\n            \"Revision\": revision,\n            \"Review roles\": \"administration\",\n            \"Reviewer\": \"ADMIN-SYN-01\",\n            \"Outcome\": \"approve\",\n            \"Reason\": \"SYNTHETIC observed decision; no policy conclusion\",\n            \"Decision time (UTC)\": \"2026-09-01T12:00:00\",\n        },\n    )\n\n\ndef _finance(row, event_id, claim_id, batch, event_type, *, amount=None, obligation=None):\n    values = {\n        \"Activity reference\": event_id,\n        \"Arrival batch\": batch,\n        \"Activity type\": event_type,\n        \"Request reference\": f\"REQ-{claim_id}\",\n        \"Claim reference\": claim_id,\n        \"Finance officer\": \"FIN-SYN-01\",\n        \"Payee ID\": \"EMP-SYN-01\",\n        \"Currency\": \"EUR\",\n        \"Reason\": f\"SYNTHETIC Finance fixture: {event_type}\",\n    }\n    if amount is not None:\n        values[\"Amount (EUR)\"] = amount\n    if obligation is not None:\n        values[\"Obligation (EUR)\"] = obligation\n    return _row(row, \"synthetic-finance-register\", \"Finance activity\", **values)\n\n\ndef _cancel(row, event_id, cancellation_id, action, subject_type, *, batch, initiation=None):\n    is_permit = subject_type == \"permit\"\n    values = {\n        \"Cancellation activity reference\": event_id,\n        \"Cancellation reference\": cancellation_id,\n        \"Action\": action,\n        \"Cancelled subject\": subject_type,\n        \"Trip reference\": \"T-SYN-01\",\n        \"Trip revision\": 1,\n        \"Permit reference\": \"P-SYN-01\",\n        \"Permit revision\": 1,\n        \"Acting employee or supervisor\": \"EMP-SYN-01\",\n        \"Activity time (UTC)\": f\"2026-09-0{batch}T09:00:00\",\n        \"Arrival batch\": batch,\n        \"Business reason\": \"SYNTHETIC client rescheduling\",\n    }\n    if action == \"confirmed\":\n        values[\"Initiation activity reference\"] = initiation\n        values[\"Effective time (UTC)\"] = f\"2026-09-0{batch}T09:30:00\"\n    return _row(row, \"synthetic-travel-register\", \"Travel cancellations\", **values)\n\n\ndef _parsed_fixture():\n    return {\n        \"run_id\": \"run-synthetic-integration\",\n        \"case_clock\": None,\n        \"unresolved_issues\": [\n            {\n                \"record_id\": \"scenario-case-clock\",\n                \"subject_type\": \"scenario\",\n                \"subject_id\": \"arrival-batch-clock\",\n                \"affected_scope\": \"all batches\",\n                \"reason\": \"SYNTHETIC fixture: clock withheld\",\n                \"owner\": \"Exercise facilitator\",\n                \"next_action\": \"provide the scenario clock\",\n                \"evidence_needed\": \"explicit date, time, and zone\",\n            },\n            {\n                \"record_id\": \"reimbursement-policy-pol-2026-2\",\n                \"subject_type\": \"policy\",\n                \"subject_id\": \"POL-2026.2\",\n                \"affected_scope\": \"eligibility and entitlement\",\n                \"reason\": \"SYNTHETIC fixture: policy withheld\",\n                \"owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n                \"next_action\": \"provide an authorized native policy export\",\n                \"evidence_needed\": \"complete policy content\",\n            },\n        ],\n        \"records\": {\n            \"claim_revisions\": [\n                _claim(\"C-SYN-01\", 1, trip_id=\"T-SYN-01\", batch=1),\n                _claim(\"C-SYN-02\", 1, trip_id=\"T-SYN-02\", batch=1, employee=\"EMP-SYN-02\"),\n                _claim(\"C-SYN-01\", 2, trip_id=\"T-SYN-01\", batch=3),\n            ],\n            \"trips\": [\n                _row(6, \"synthetic-travel-register\", \"Trips\", **{\n                    \"Trip reference\": \"T-SYN-01\", \"Trip revision\": 1,\n                    \"Permit reference\": \"P-SYN-01\", \"Permit revision\": 1,\n                }),\n                _row(7, \"synthetic-travel-register\", \"Trips\", **{\n                    \"Trip reference\": \"T-SYN-02\", \"Trip revision\": 1,\n                    \"Permit reference\": \"P-SYN-02\", \"Permit revision\": 1,\n                }),\n            ],\n            \"decisions\": [\n                _decision(6, \"D-SYN-01-R1\", \"C-SYN-01\", 1),\n                _decision(7, \"D-SYN-02-R1\", \"C-SYN-02\", 1),\n            ],\n            \"finance_events\": [\n                _finance(6, \"F-SYN-01-SETTLED\", \"C-SYN-01\", 2, \"settled\", amount=10.00),\n                _finance(7, \"F-SYN-01-PENDING\", \"C-SYN-01\", 2, \"transfer_pending\", amount=5.00),\n                _finance(8, \"F-SYN-02-SETTLED\", \"C-SYN-02\", 2, \"settled\", amount=4.00),\n            ],\n            \"cancellation_activities\": [\n                _cancel(6, \"TC-SYN-TRIP-REQ\", \"TC-SYN-TRIP\", \"requested\", \"trip\", batch=1),\n                _cancel(7, \"TC-SYN-PERMIT-REQ\", \"TC-SYN-PERMIT\", \"requested\", \"permit\", batch=1),\n                _cancel(8, \"TC-SYN-TRIP-CFM\", \"TC-SYN-TRIP\", \"confirmed\", \"trip\", batch=2,\n                        initiation=\"TC-SYN-TRIP-REQ\"),\n                _cancel(9, \"TC-SYN-PERMIT-CFM\", \"TC-SYN-PERMIT\", \"confirmed\", \"permit\", batch=2,\n                        initiation=\"TC-SYN-PERMIT-REQ\"),\n\n\ndef _batches(parsed):\n    prior = None\n    results = []\n    for batch in parsed['arrival_batches']:\n        prior = integrate_arrival_batch(\n            parsed, arrival_batch=batch, run_id='retained-regression', batch_id=f'arrival-{batch:03d}',\n            source_binding={'path': 'sources.json', 'sha256': 'a' * 64},\n            predecessor={'path': f'batches/arrival-{batch-1:03d}.json', 'sha256': 'b' * 64} if prior else None,\n            prior_result=prior,\n        )\n        results.append(prior)\n    return results\n\n\ndef test_native_obligation_fields_and_ledger_balances_do_not_become_entitlement():\n    parsed = _fixture()\n    assert 'Claim revision' not in parsed['provenance']['finance_headers']\n    results = _batches(parsed)\n    final = results[-1]\n    c1 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C01']\n    obligation = c1['recorded_obligation']\n    assert obligation['event_id'] == 'F-C01-accepted'\n    assert obligation['request_id'] == 'REQ-C01'\n    assert obligation['finance_officer'] == 'FIN-01'\n    assert obligation['payee_id'] == 'EMP-01'\n    assert obligation['amount_cents'] == 10000\n    assert obligation['claim_revision'] is None\n    assert obligation['arrival_revision_context'] == 1\n    assert obligation['revision_link_status'] == 'arrival_context_only'\n    assert obligation['first_arrival_batch'] == 1\n    assert obligation['source_refs'] == [\n        'travel-registers-workbook@' + parsed['provenance']['workbook_sha256'] + \"#tab 'Finance activity', row 33\"\n    ]\n    assert obligation['claim_source_refs'][0]['locator'] == 'PDF page 1'\n    assert c1['net_confirmed_cents'] == 10000  # delivered twice, counted once\n    assert c1['duplicate_events'][0]['delivery_batches'] == [2, 4]\n    assert c1['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n    assert c1['authorized_obligation'] is None\n    assert c1['balance_cents'] is None\n    assert c1['closure_authority_confirmed'] is False\n    projected = next(c for c in final['snapshot']['claims'] if c['claim_id'] == 'C01')\n    assert projected['finance_evidence']['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n    assert projected['allowed_cents'] is None and projected['status'] == 'pending'\n\n\ndef test_native_corrections_keep_ledger_history_and_revalidate_authority_only_where_affected():\n    results = _batches(_fixture())\n    first, _, third, final = results\n    initial = deepcopy(first)\n    c19 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C19']\n    assert [(r['event_id'], r['amount_cents'], r['arrival_revision_context']) for r in c19['recorded_obligation_history']] == [\n        ('F-C19-accepted', 10000, 1), ('F-C19-2', 8000, 2), ('F-C19-4', 8000, 3),\n    ]\n    assert c19['confirmed_payment_cents'] == 10000\n    assert c19['confirmed_refund_cents'] == 2000\n    assert c19['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n    assert c19['recorded_obligation']['claim_revision'] is None\n    assert c19['invalidated_previous_reconciliation']['claim_revision'] == 2\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C09']['recorded_obligation']['arrival_revision_context'] == 2\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C12']['recorded_obligation']['amount_cents'] == 7000\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C01']['recorded_obligation'] == first['finance_reconciliations']['C01']['recorded_obligation']\n    # C18 correction has no newly bound accepted amount. Retain r1 context;\n    # neither cancellation nor a fresh payment silently reauthorizes revision 2.\n    c18 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C18']\n    assert c18['claim_revision'] == 2\n    assert c18['recorded_obligation']['arrival_revision_context'] == 1\n    assert c18['authorized_obligation'] is None\n    assert c18['confirmed_payment_cents'] == 10000\n    item = final['domain']['repair_queue']['items']['finance:finance-obligation-missing:C09:1']\n    # Historic question remains historic; r2 has its own current authorization question.\n    assert item['revision'] == 1\n    current = final['domain']['repair_queue']['items']['finance:finance-obligation-missing:C09:2']\n    assert current['source_refs']\n    assert 'recorded Finance obligation exists' in current['missing_or_return_reason']\n    assert current['status'] == 'open'\n    assert first == initial\n\n\ndef test_native_refund_and_finance_cancellation_are_independent_of_business_cancellations():\n    final = _batches(_fixture())[-1]\n    cancellations = {c['cancellation_id']: c for c in final['snapshot']['travel_cancellations']}\n    assert cancellations['TC122']['affected_claim_ids'] == []\n    assert cancellations['TC122']['target_type'] == 'trip'\n    assert cancellations['TC121']['target_type'] == 'permit'\n    assert all(c['financial_status'] == 'unresolved' for c in cancellations.values())\n    c18 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C18']\n    assert c18['recorded_obligation']['amount_cents'] == 10000\n    assert c18['confirmed_refund_cents'] == 0  # cancelled transfer is not a refund\n    c20 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C20']\n    assert c20['recorded_obligation']['amount_cents'] == 10000\n    assert c20['confirmed_refund_cents'] == 1000\n    assert c20['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n\n\ndef test_duplicate_refund_and_accepted_redelivery_keep_identity_and_original_revision_context():\n    parsed = _fixture()\n    accepted = deepcopy(next(r for r in parsed['records']['finance_events'] if r['values']['Activity reference']['value'] == 'F-C18-accepted'))\n    accepted['row'] = 998\n    accepted['locator'] = \"tab 'Finance activity', row 998 (synthetic redelivery)\"\n    accepted['values']['Arrival batch']['value'] = 4\n    refund = deepcopy(next(r for r in parsed['records']['finance_events'] if r['values']['Activity reference']['value'] == 'F-C20-2'))\n    refund['row'] = 999\n    refund['locator'] = \"tab 'Finance activity', row 999 (synthetic redelivery)\"\n    refund['values']['Arrival batch']['value'] = 4\n    parsed['records']['finance_events'].extend([accepted, refund])\n    final = _batches(parsed)[-1]\n    c18 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C18']\n    assert len(c18['recorded_obligation_history']) == 1\n    assert c18['recorded_obligation']['delivery_batches'] == [1, 4]\n        }\n    }\n    history = build_revision_history(parsed)\n    assert [row[\"revision\"] for row in history[\"claim\"][\"C-SYN-01\"][\"revisions\"]] == [1, 2]\n    assert history[\"claim\"][\"C-SYN-01\"][\"current_revision\"] == 2\n    assert history[\"trip\"][\"T-SYN-01\"][\"current_revision\"] == 2\n    assert history[\"permit\"][\"P-SYN-01\"][\"current_revision\"] == 1\n    assert history[\"claim\"][\"C-SYN-01\"][\"revisions\"][1][\"trip_revision\"] == 1\n\n    decisions = [\n        _workbook_record(10, **{\"Decision reference\": \"D-SYN-OLD\", \"Subject type\": \"claim\",\n                                \"Subject reference\": \"C-SYN-01\", \"Revision\": 1, \"Outcome\": \"approve\"}),\n        _workbook_record(11, **{\"Decision reference\": \"D-SYN-UNKNOWN\", \"Subject type\": \"trip\",\n                                \"Subject reference\": \"T-SYN-01\", \"Revision\": 9, \"Outcome\": \"return\"}),\n    ]\n    matches = match_decisions_to_subjects(decisions, history)\n    assert [row[\"structural_match\"] for row in matches] == [\"revision_match_historical\", \"revision_not_found\"]\n    assert [row[\"applied\"] for row in matches] == [False, False]\n    assert matches[0][\"observed_outcome\"] == \"approve\"  # preserved observation; no approval is performed\n\n\ndef test_cancellation_state_machine_keeps_trip_and_permit_processes_independent():\n    events = [\n        _cancellation_row(6, event_id=\"TC-SYN-P-REQ\", cancellation_id=\"TC-SYN-P\",\n                          action=\"requested\", target_type=\"permit\", target_id=\"P-SYN-01\", batch=1),\n        _cancellation_row(7, event_id=\"TC-SYN-T-REQ\", cancellation_id=\"TC-SYN-T\",\n                          action=\"requested\", target_type=\"trip\", target_id=\"T-SYN-01\", batch=1),\n        _cancellation_row(8, event_id=\"TC-SYN-P-CFM\", cancellation_id=\"TC-SYN-P\",\n                          action=\"confirmed\", target_type=\"permit\", target_id=\"P-SYN-01\", batch=2,\n                          initiation=\"TC-SYN-P-REQ\", effective=\"2026-11-16T09:00:00+01:00\"),\n    ]\n    result = reduce_cancellation_activities(events)\n    assert result[\"processes\"][\"TC-SYN-P\"][\"state\"] == \"confirmed\"\n    assert result[\"processes\"][\"TC-SYN-T\"][\"state\"] == \"requested\"\n    assert result[\"processes\"][\"TC-SYN-T\"][\"next_action\"] == \"await a linked confirmation activity\"\n    assert result[\"finance_effects\"] == []\n    assert result[\"claim_effects\"] == []\n    assert result[\"processes\"][\"TC-SYN-P\"][\"target\"] == {\n        \"subject_type\": \"permit\", \"subject_id\": \"P-SYN-01\", \"revision\": 1,\n    }\n\n\ndef test_event_deduplication_is_replay_safe_and_flags_same_id_payload_conflicts():\n    # Synthetic Finance-like event IDs; arrival batch is delivery metadata.\n    first = _workbook_record(6, **{\"Activity reference\": \"F-SYN-01\", \"Arrival batch\": 2,\n                                  \"Activity type\": \"settled\", \"Amount (EUR)\": 100.0,\n                                  \"Claim reference\": \"C-SYN-01\"})\n    replay = _workbook_record(31, **{\"Activity reference\": \"F-SYN-01\", \"Arrival batch\": 4,\n                                    \"Activity type\": \"settled\", \"Amount (EUR)\": 100.0,\n                                    \"Claim reference\": \"C-SYN-01\"})\n    changed = _workbook_record(32, **{\"Activity reference\": \"F-SYN-01\", \"Arrival batch\": 4,\n                                      \"Activity type\": \"settled\", \"Amount (EUR)\": 120.0,\n                                      \"Claim reference\": \"C-SYN-01\"})\n    exact = deduplicate_activity_records([first, replay], id_field=\"Activity reference\")\n    assert len(exact[\"unique_events\"]) == 1\n    assert exact[\"duplicates\"][0][\"delivery_batches\"] == [2, 4]\n    assert exact[\"conflicts\"] == []\n    conflict = deduplicate_activity_records([first, changed], id_field=\"Activity reference\")\n    assert conflict[\"unique_events\"] == []\n    assert conflict[\"conflicts\"][0][\"event_id\"] == \"F-SYN-01\"\n\n\ndef test_actual_retained_activity_replays_are_deduplicated_and_cancellation_ids_are_separate(tmp_path):\n    parsed = parse_retained_run(CAPTURE, output_path=tmp_path / \"parsed.json\")\n    history = build_revision_history(parsed)\n    c09 = history[\"claim\"][\"C09\"]\ndef _domain_seed() -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\n        \"processed_batches\": [],\n        \"batch_input_hashes\": {},\n        \"claim_records\": [],\n        \"decision_records\": [],\n        \"finance_records\": [],\n        \"cancellation_records\": [],\n        \"revision_history\": None,\n        \"decision_history\": [],\n        \"finance_reconciliations\": {},\n        \"ordinary_workflows\": {},\n        \"ordinary_workflow_history\": [],\n        \"authorized_obligations\": {},\n        \"source_classifications\": {},\n        \"cancellation_state\": {},\n        \"material_corrections\": [],\n        \"repair_queue\": new_repair_queue(),\n        \"policy_clock_blockers\": [],\n        \"structural_blockers\": [],\n        \"projection_issues\": [],\n    }\n\n\ndef _issue_from_item(item: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\n        \"record_id\": item[\"item_id\"],\n        \"reason\": item[\"missing_or_return_reason\"],\n        \"owner\": item[\"owner\"],\n1. Bind every fact and decision to its source, subject, and revision.\n2. Hold only claims or dependent work affected by missing/conflicting facts. Continue independent valid work. Each unresolved item retains subject type and exact ID, revision, missing/conflicting fact, responsible owner, source reference, and next action.\n3. Preserve every claim revision. After a material correction, use the corrected revision and revalidate affected evidence, calculations, trip/permit consistency, approvals, and Finance authorization. Preserve unrelated evidence only where it remains valid. Retain historical commitments, transfers, and refunds; do not use stale approvals as current.\n4. Keep trip cancellation and permit cancellation as independent processes, including processes without claims. Cancellation does not itself erase entitlement or Finance obligations. Record Finance disposition and monetary resolution separately when required.\n5. Use the owner-grouped local repair queue. Keep each item individually traceable. A partial response may resolve only the item(s) explicitly matched and supported by retained source evidence; unanswered, insufficient, or conflicting items stay open. Draft locally; never send requests.\n6. Preserve immutable Finance event identifiers. Reconcile only confirmed transfers and refunds. Do not duplicate events or obligations on replay.\n7. The provisional financial closure choice is to require current evidence and approvals, agreement between reviewed entitlement and authorized obligation, net confirmed payment equal to the authorized amount, required Finance resolutions, and no blocking issue. After the first actual processing result, pause for the operator to inspect reconciliation and unresolved cases and confirm final completion conditions and delivery scope.\n\nPeople retain business approval, exception, and payment authority. This Skill prepares work, validates supplied decisions, and records effects; it does not make discretionary approval recommendations, create replies, issue Finance exceptions, book travel, or move funds.\n\n## Outputs\n\n- `artifacts/runs/<run-id>/sources.json` and retained source bytes.\n- One immutable schema-valid `batches/<batch-id>.json` per consumed batch, with relative source and predecessor paths plus SHA-256 hashes.\n- `claims.csv` with exactly `claim_id,revision,trip_id,status,allowed_cents,paid_cents,balance_cents,next_owner,reason`.\n- Owner-grouped local repair queue with individual items and run/batch update history.\n- `report.md` describing completed work, obligations, unresolved items, owners, next actions, cancellations without claims, and source/run references.\n\nUnknown money is null in JSON and blank in CSV. Zero is a known amount. Never label incomplete work complete.\n\n## Errors, retries, and limitations\n\n- On source failure, retain the attempt URL, locator, UTC observation time, error, and missing scope. Hold only affected work and report its owner and resumption evidence.\n- On partial source access, retain usable pieces and explicitly list missing scope. Do not claim the source was fully read.\n- On invalid or conflicting batch data, preserve the input evidence, reject admission of unsupported effects, and create an owned issue; do not silently discard it.\n- Retry a failed fresh retrieval only by making another live request and recording the new observation. Do not overwrite a prior run's manifest, retained bytes, or sealed snapshot.\n- On replay, preserve obligation/event identity and money; detect conflicting content under an existing event ID.\n- Implemented paths include fresh HTTP/export acquisition and source-bound transcription, plus explicitly offline connected claim, correction, independent cancellation and Finance replay. New source manifests retain response observations and partial/error bodies. Complete native policy access, rule interpretation, authoritative case clock and supported completion authority remain required for final live business compliance; acquisition or offline integrity alone does not establish it.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":54520290},"formatted_output":"\"\"\"Synthetic end-to-end integration tests; no real arrival batch is consumed.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom jsonschema import Draft202012Validator, FormatChecker\nimport pytest\n\nfrom travel_claim.integration import integrate_arrival_batch\n\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nSCHEMA = json.loads((ROOT / \"snapshot.schema.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n\n\ndef _claim(claim_id, revision, *, trip_id, trip_revision=1, batch=1, employee=\"EMP-SYN-01\"):\n    return {\n        \"source_id\": \"synthetic-claim-binder\",\n        \"source_sha256\": \"a\" * 64,\n        \"locator\": f\"PDF page {revision} (SYNTHETIC {claim_id} revision {revision})\",\n        \"page\": revision,\n        \"fields\": [\n            {\"label\": \"Claim reference\", \"value\": claim_id},\n            {\"label\": \"Revision\", \"value\": str(revision)},\n            {\"label\": \"Arrival batch\", \"value\": str(batch)},\n            {\"label\": \"Employee\", \"value\": employee},\n            {\"label\": \"Trip reference\", \"value\": trip_id},\n            {\"label\": \"Trip revision\", \"value\": str(trip_revision)},\n            {\"label\": \"Claim reason\", \"value\": \"SYNTHETIC fixture\"},\n        ],\n        \"text\": f\"SYNTHETIC TEST FIXTURE ONLY: {claim_id} revision {revision}\",\n    }\n\n\ndef _row(row, source_id, tab, **values):\n    return {\n        \"source_id\": source_id,\n        \"source_sha256\": \"b\" * 64,\n        \"locator\": f\"tab '{tab}', row {row} (SYNTHETIC)\",\n        \"row\": row,\n        \"values\": {\n            key: {\"value\": value, \"source_text\": str(value), \"cell\": f\"A{row}\"}\n            for key, value in values.items()\n        },\n    }\n\n\ndef _decision(row, decision_id, claim_id, revision, batch=1):\n    return _row(\n        row, \"synthetic-review-ledger\", \"Review ledger\",\n        **{\n            \"Decision reference\": decision_id,\n            \"Arrival batch\": batch,\n            \"Subject type\": \"claim\",\n            \"Subject reference\": claim_id,\n            \"Revision\": revision,\n            \"Review roles\": \"administration\",\n            \"Reviewer\": \"ADMIN-SYN-01\",\n            \"Outcome\": \"approve\",\n            \"Reason\": \"SYNTHETIC observed decision; no policy conclusion\",\n            \"Decision time (UTC)\": \"2026-09-01T12:00:00\",\n        },\n    )\n\n\ndef _finance(row, event_id, claim_id, batch, event_type, *, amount=None, obligation=None):\n    values = {\n        \"Activity reference\": event_id,\n        \"Arrival batch\": batch,\n        \"Activity type\": event_type,\n        \"Request reference\": f\"REQ-{claim_id}\",\n        \"Claim reference\": claim_id,\n        \"Finance officer\": \"FIN-SYN-01\",\n        \"Payee ID\": \"EMP-SYN-01\",\n        \"Currency\": \"EUR\",\n        \"Reason\": f\"SYNTHETIC Finance fixture: {event_type}\",\n    }\n    if amount is not None:\n        values[\"Amount (EUR)\"] = amount\n    if obligation is not None:\n        values[\"Obligation (EUR)\"] = obligation\n    return _row(row, \"synthetic-finance-register\", \"Finance activity\", **values)\n\n\ndef _cancel(row, event_id, cancellation_id, action, subject_type, *, batch, initiation=None):\n    is_permit = subject_type == \"permit\"\n    values = {\n        \"Cancellation activity reference\": event_id,\n        \"Cancellation reference\": cancellation_id,\n        \"Action\": action,\n        \"Cancelled subject\": subject_type,\n        \"Trip reference\": \"T-SYN-01\",\n        \"Trip revision\": 1,\n        \"Permit reference\": \"P-SYN-01\",\n        \"Permit revision\": 1,\n        \"Acting employee or supervisor\": \"EMP-SYN-01\",\n        \"Activity time (UTC)\": f\"2026-09-0{batch}T09:00:00\",\n        \"Arrival batch\": batch,\n        \"Business reason\": \"SYNTHETIC client rescheduling\",\n    }\n    if action == \"confirmed\":\n        values[\"Initiation activity reference\"] = initiation\n        values[\"Effective time (UTC)\"] = f\"2026-09-0{batch}T09:30:00\"\n    return _row(row, \"synthetic-travel-register\", \"Travel cancellations\", **values)\n\n\ndef _parsed_fixture():\n    return {\n        \"run_id\": \"run-synthetic-integration\",\n        \"case_clock\": None,\n        \"unresolved_issues\": [\n            {\n                \"record_id\": \"scenario-case-clock\",\n                \"subject_type\": \"scenario\",\n                \"subject_id\": \"arrival-batch-clock\",\n                \"affected_scope\": \"all batches\",\n                \"reason\": \"SYNTHETIC fixture: clock withheld\",\n                \"owner\": \"Exercise facilitator\",\n                \"next_action\": \"provide the scenario clock\",\n                \"evidence_needed\": \"explicit date, time, and zone\",\n            },\n            {\n                \"record_id\": \"reimbursement-policy-pol-2026-2\",\n                \"subject_type\": \"policy\",\n                \"subject_id\": \"POL-2026.2\",\n                \"affected_scope\": \"eligibility and entitlement\",\n                \"reason\": \"SYNTHETIC fixture: policy withheld\",\n                \"owner\": \"Travel Administration Lead\",\n                \"next_action\": \"provide an authorized native policy export\",\n                \"evidence_needed\": \"complete policy content\",\n            },\n        ],\n        \"records\": {\n            \"claim_revisions\": [\n                _claim(\"C-SYN-01\", 1, trip_id=\"T-SYN-01\", batch=1),\n                _claim(\"C-SYN-02\", 1, trip_id=\"T-SYN-02\", batch=1, employee=\"EMP-SYN-02\"),\n                _claim(\"C-SYN-01\", 2, trip_id=\"T-SYN-01\", batch=3),\n            ],\n            \"trips\": [\n                _row(6, \"synthetic-travel-register\", \"Trips\", **{\n                    \"Trip reference\": \"T-SYN-01\", \"Trip revision\": 1,\n                    \"Permit reference\": \"P-SYN-01\", \"Permit revision\": 1,\n                }),\n                _row(7, \"synthetic-travel-register\", \"Trips\", **{\n                    \"Trip reference\": \"T-SYN-02\", \"Trip revision\": 1,\n                    \"Permit reference\": \"P-SYN-02\", \"Permit revision\": 1,\n                }),\n            ],\n            \"decisions\": [\n                _decision(6, \"D-SYN-01-R1\", \"C-SYN-01\", 1),\n                _decision(7, \"D-SYN-02-R1\", \"C-SYN-02\", 1),\n            ],\n            \"finance_events\": [\n                _finance(6, \"F-SYN-01-SETTLED\", \"C-SYN-01\", 2, \"settled\", amount=10.00),\n                _finance(7, \"F-SYN-01-PENDING\", \"C-SYN-01\", 2, \"transfer_pending\", amount=5.00),\n                _finance(8, \"F-SYN-02-SETTLED\", \"C-SYN-02\", 2, \"settled\", amount=4.00),\n            ],\n            \"cancellation_activities\": [\n                _cancel(6, \"TC-SYN-TRIP-REQ\", \"TC-SYN-TRIP\", \"requested\", \"trip\", batch=1),\n                _cancel(7, \"TC-SYN-PERMIT-REQ\", \"TC-SYN-PERMIT\", \"requested\", \"permit\", batch=1),\n                _cancel(8, \"TC-SYN-TRIP-CFM\", \"TC-SYN-TRIP\", \"confirmed\", \"trip\", batch=2,\n                        initiation=\"TC-SYN-TRIP-REQ\"),\n                _cancel(9, \"TC-SYN-PERMIT-CFM\", \"TC-SYN-PERMIT\", \"confirmed\", \"permit\", batch=2,\n                        initiation=\"TC-SYN-PERMIT-REQ\"),\n\n\ndef _batches(parsed):\n    prior = None\n    results = []\n    for batch in parsed['arrival_batches']:\n        prior = integrate_arrival_batch(\n            parsed, arrival_batch=batch, run_id='retained-regression', batch_id=f'arrival-{batch:03d}',\n            source_binding={'path': 'sources.json', 'sha256': 'a' * 64},\n            predecessor={'path': f'batches/arrival-{batch-1:03d}.json', 'sha256': 'b' * 64} if prior else None,\n            prior_result=prior,\n        )\n        results.append(prior)\n    return results\n\n\ndef test_native_obligation_fields_and_ledger_balances_do_not_become_entitlement():\n    parsed = _fixture()\n    assert 'Claim revision' not in parsed['provenance']['finance_headers']\n    results = _batches(parsed)\n    final = results[-1]\n    c1 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C01']\n    obligation = c1['recorded_obligation']\n    assert obligation['event_id'] == 'F-C01-accepted'\n    assert obligation['request_id'] == 'REQ-C01'\n    assert obligation['finance_officer'] == 'FIN-01'\n    assert obligation['payee_id'] == 'EMP-01'\n    assert obligation['amount_cents'] == 10000\n    assert obligation['claim_revision'] is None\n    assert obligation['arrival_revision_context'] == 1\n    assert obligation['revision_link_status'] == 'arrival_context_only'\n    assert obligation['first_arrival_batch'] == 1\n    assert obligation['source_refs'] == [\n        'travel-registers-workbook@' + parsed['provenance']['workbook_sha256'] + \"#tab 'Finance activity', row 33\"\n    ]\n    assert obligation['claim_source_refs'][0]['locator'] == 'PDF page 1'\n    assert c1['net_confirmed_cents'] == 10000  # delivered twice, counted once\n    assert c1['duplicate_events'][0]['delivery_batches'] == [2, 4]\n    assert c1['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n    assert c1['authorized_obligation'] is None\n    assert c1['balance_cents'] is None\n    assert c1['closure_authority_confirmed'] is False\n    projected = next(c for c in final['snapshot']['claims'] if c['claim_id'] == 'C01')\n    assert projected['finance_evidence']['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n    assert projected['allowed_cents'] is None and projected['status'] == 'pending'\n\n\ndef test_native_corrections_keep_ledger_history_and_revalidate_authority_only_where_affected():\n    results = _batches(_fixture())\n    first, _, third, final = results\n    initial = deepcopy(first)\n    c19 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C19']\n    assert [(r['event_id'], r['amount_cents'], r['arrival_revision_context']) for r in c19['recorded_obligation_history']] == [\n        ('F-C19-accepted', 10000, 1), ('F-C19-2', 8000, 2), ('F-C19-4', 8000, 3),\n    ]\n    assert c19['confirmed_payment_cents'] == 10000\n    assert c19['confirmed_refund_cents'] == 2000\n    assert c19['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n    assert c19['recorded_obligation']['claim_revision'] is None\n    assert c19['invalidated_previous_reconciliation']['claim_revision'] == 2\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C09']['recorded_obligation']['arrival_revision_context'] == 2\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C12']['recorded_obligation']['amount_cents'] == 7000\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C01']['recorded_obligation'] == first['finance_reconciliations']['C01']['recorded_obligation']\n    # C18 correction has no newly bound accepted amount. Retain r1 context;\n    # neither cancellation nor a fresh payment silently reauthorizes revision 2.\n    c18 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C18']\n    assert c18['claim_revision'] == 2\n    assert c18['recorded_obligation']['arrival_revision_context'] == 1\n    assert c18['authorized_obligation'] is None\n    assert c18['confirmed_payment_cents'] == 10000\n    item = final['domain']['repair_queue']['items']['finance:finance-obligation-missing:C09:1']\n    # Historic question remains historic; r2 has its own current authorization question.\n    assert item['revision'] == 1\n    current = final['domain']['repair_queue']['items']['finance:finance-obligation-missing:C09:2']\n    assert current['source_refs']\n    assert 'recorded Finance obligation exists' in current['missing_or_return_reason']\n    assert current['status'] == 'open'\n    assert first == initial\n\n\ndef test_native_refund_and_finance_cancellation_are_independent_of_business_cancellations():\n    final = _batches(_fixture())[-1]\n    cancellations = {c['cancellation_id']: c for c in final['snapshot']['travel_cancellations']}\n    assert cancellations['TC122']['affected_claim_ids'] == []\n    assert cancellations['TC122']['target_type'] == 'trip'\n    assert cancellations['TC121']['target_type'] == 'permit'\n    assert all(c['financial_status'] == 'unresolved' for c in cancellations.values())\n    c18 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C18']\n    assert c18['recorded_obligation']['amount_cents'] == 10000\n    assert c18['confirmed_refund_cents'] == 0  # cancelled transfer is not a refund\n    c20 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C20']\n    assert c20['recorded_obligation']['amount_cents'] == 10000\n    assert c20['confirmed_refund_cents'] == 1000\n    assert c20['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\n\n\ndef test_duplicate_refund_and_accepted_redelivery_keep_identity_and_original_revision_context():\n    parsed = _fixture()\n    accepted = deepcopy(next(r for r in parsed['records']['finance_events'] if r['values']['Activity reference']['value'] == 'F-C18-accepted'))\n    accepted['row'] = 998\n    accepted['locator'] = \"tab 'Finance activity', row 998 (synthetic redelivery)\"\n    accepted['values']['Arrival batch']['value'] = 4\n    refund = deepcopy(next(r for r in parsed['records']['finance_events'] if r['values']['Activity reference']['value'] == 'F-C20-2'))\n    refund['row'] = 999\n    refund['locator'] = \"tab 'Finance activity', row 999 (synthetic redelivery)\"\n    refund['values']['Arrival batch']['value'] = 4\n    parsed['records']['finance_events'].extend([accepted, refund])\n    final = _batches(parsed)[-1]\n    c18 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C18']\n    assert len(c18['recorded_obligation_history']) == 1\n    assert c18['recorded_obligation']['delivery_batches'] == [1, 4]\n        }\n    }\n    history = build_revision_history(parsed)\n    assert [row[\"revision\"] for row in history[\"claim\"][\"C-SYN-01\"][\"revisions\"]] == [1, 2]\n    assert history[\"claim\"][\"C-SYN-01\"][\"current_revision\"] == 2\n    assert history[\"trip\"][\"T-SYN-01\"][\"current_revision\"] == 2\n    assert history[\"permit\"][\"P-SYN-01\"][\"current_revision\"] == 1\n    assert history[\"claim\"][\"C-SYN-01\"][\"revisions\"][1][\"trip_revision\"] == 1\n\n    decisions = [\n        _workbook_record(10, **{\"Decision reference\": \"D-SYN-OLD\", \"Subject type\": \"claim\",\n                                \"Subject reference\": \"C-SYN-01\", \"Revision\": 1, \"Outcome\": \"approve\"}),\n        _workbook_record(11, **{\"Decision reference\": \"D-SYN-UNKNOWN\", \"Subject type\": \"trip\",\n                                \"Subject reference\": \"T-SYN-01\", \"Revision\": 9, \"Outcome\": \"return\"}),\n    ]\n    matches = match_decisions_to_subjects(decisions, history)\n    assert [row[\"structural_match\"] for row in matches] == [\"revision_match_historical\", \"revision_not_found\"]\n    assert [row[\"applied\"] for row in matches] == [False, False]\n    assert matches[0][\"observed_outcome\"] == \"approve\"  # preserved observation; no approval is performed\n\n\ndef test_cancellation_state_machine_keeps_trip_and_permit_processes_independent():\n    events = [\n        _cancellation_row(6, event_id=\"TC-SYN-P-REQ\", cancellation_id=\"TC-SYN-P\",\n                          action=\"requested\", target_type=\"permit\", target_id=\"P-SYN-01\", batch=1),\n        _cancellation_row(7, event_id=\"TC-SYN-T-REQ\", cancellation_id=\"TC-SYN-T\",\n                          action=\"requested\", target_type=\"trip\", target_id=\"T-SYN-01\", batch=1),\n        _cancellation_row(8, event_id=\"TC-SYN-P-CFM\", cancellation_id=\"TC-SYN-P\",\n                          action=\"confirmed\", target_type=\"permit\", target_id=\"P-SYN-01\", batch=2,\n                          initiation=\"TC-SYN-P-REQ\", effective=\"2026-11-16T09:00:00+01:00\"),\n    ]\n    result = reduce_cancellation_activities(events)\n    assert result[\"processes\"][\"TC-SYN-P\"][\"state\"] == \"confirmed\"\n    assert result[\"processes\"][\"TC-SYN-T\"][\"state\"] == \"requested\"\n    assert result[\"processes\"][\"TC-SYN-T\"][\"next_action\"] == \"await a linked confirmation activity\"\n    assert result[\"finance_effects\"] == []\n    assert result[\"claim_effects\"] == []\n    assert result[\"processes\"][\"TC-SYN-P\"][\"target\"] == {\n        \"subject_type\": \"permit\", \"subject_id\": \"P-SYN-01\", \"revision\": 1,\n    }\n\n\ndef test_event_deduplication_is_replay_safe_and_flags_same_id_payload_conflicts():\n    # Synthetic Finance-like event IDs; arrival batch is delivery metadata.\n    first = _workbook_record(6, **{\"Activity reference\": \"F-SYN-01\", \"Arrival batch\": 2,\n                                  \"Activity type\": \"settled\", \"Amount (EUR)\": 100.0,\n                                  \"Claim reference\": \"C-SYN-01\"})\n    replay = _workbook_record(31, **{\"Activity reference\": \"F-SYN-01\", \"Arrival batch\": 4,\n                                    \"Activity type\": \"settled\", \"Amount (EUR)\": 100.0,\n                                    \"Claim reference\": \"C-SYN-01\"})\n    changed = _workbook_record(32, **{\"Activity reference\": \"F-SYN-01\", \"Arrival batch\": 4,\n                                      \"Activity type\": \"settled\", \"Amount (EUR)\": 120.0,\n                                      \"Claim reference\": \"C-SYN-01\"})\n    exact = deduplicate_activity_records([first, replay], id_field=\"Activity reference\")\n    assert len(exact[\"unique_events\"]) == 1\n    assert exact[\"duplicates\"][0][\"delivery_batches\"] == [2, 4]\n    assert exact[\"conflicts\"] == []\n    conflict = deduplicate_activity_records([first, changed], id_field=\"Activity reference\")\n    assert conflict[\"unique_events\"] == []\n    assert conflict[\"conflicts\"][0][\"event_id\"] == \"F-SYN-01\"\n\n\ndef test_actual_retained_activity_replays_are_deduplicated_and_cancellation_ids_are_separate(tmp_path):\n    parsed = parse_retained_run(CAPTURE, output_path=tmp_path / \"parsed.json\")\n    history = build_revision_history(parsed)\n    c09 = history[\"claim\"][\"C09\"]\ndef _domain_seed() -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\n        \"processed_batches\": [],\n        \"batch_input_hashes\": {},\n        \"claim_records\": [],\n        \"decision_records\": [],\n        \"finance_records\": [],\n        \"cancellation_records\": [],\n        \"revision_history\": None,\n        \"decision_history\": [],\n        \"finance_reconciliations\": {},\n        \"ordinary_workflows\": {},\n        \"ordinary_workflow_history\": [],\n        \"authorized_obligations\": {},\n        \"source_classifications\": {},\n        \"cancellation_state\": {},\n        \"material_corrections\": [],\n        \"repair_queue\": new_repair_queue(),\n        \"policy_clock_blockers\": [],\n        \"structural_blockers\": [],\n        \"projection_issues\": [],\n    }\n\n\ndef _issue_from_item(item: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {\n        \"record_id\": item[\"item_id\"],\n        \"reason\": item[\"missing_or_return_reason\"],\n        \"owner\": item[\"owner\"],\n1. Bind every fact and decision to its source, subject, and revision.\n2. Hold only claims or dependent work affected by missing/conflicting facts. Continue independent valid work. Each unresolved item retains subject type and exact ID, revision, missing/conflicting fact, responsible owner, source reference, and next action.\n3. Preserve every claim revision. After a material correction, use the corrected revision and revalidate affected evidence, calculations, trip/permit consistency, approvals, and Finance authorization. Preserve unrelated evidence only where it remains valid. Retain historical commitments, transfers, and refunds; do not use stale approvals as current.\n4. Keep trip cancellation and permit cancellation as independent processes, including processes without claims. Cancellation does not itself erase entitlement or Finance obligations. Record Finance disposition and monetary resolution separately when required.\n5. Use the owner-grouped local repair queue. Keep each item individually traceable. A partial response may resolve only the item(s) explicitly matched and supported by retained source evidence; unanswered, insufficient, or conflicting items stay open. Draft locally; never send requests.\n6. Preserve immutable Finance event identifiers. Reconcile only confirmed transfers and refunds. Do not duplicate events or obligations on replay.\n7. The provisional financial closure choice is to require current evidence and approvals, agreement between reviewed entitlement and authorized obligation, net confirmed payment equal to the authorized amount, required Finance resolutions, and no blocking issue. After the first actual processing result, pause for the operator to inspect reconciliation and unresolved cases and confirm final completion conditions and delivery scope.\n\nPeople retain business approval, exception, and payment authority. This Skill prepares work, validates supplied decisions, and records effects; it does not make discretionary approval recommendations, create replies, issue Finance exceptions, book travel, or move funds.\n\n## Outputs\n\n- `artifacts/runs/<run-id>/sources.json` and retained source bytes.\n- One immutable schema-valid `batches/<batch-id>.json` per consumed batch, with relative source and predecessor paths plus SHA-256 hashes.\n- `claims.csv` with exactly `claim_id,revision,trip_id,status,allowed_cents,paid_cents,balance_cents,next_owner,reason`.\n- Owner-grouped local repair queue with individual items and run/batch update history.\n- `report.md` describing completed work, obligations, unresolved items, owners, next actions, cancellations without claims, and source/run references.\n\nUnknown money is null in JSON and blank in CSV. Zero is a known amount. Never label incomplete work complete.\n\n## Errors, retries, and limitations\n\n- On source failure, retain the attempt URL, locator, UTC observation time, error, and missing scope. Hold only affected work and report its owner and resumption evidence.\n- On partial source access, retain usable pieces and explicitly list missing scope. Do not claim the source was fully read.\n- On invalid or conflicting batch data, preserve the input evidence, reject admission of unsupported effects, and create an owned issue; do not silently discard it.\n- Retry a failed fresh retrieval only by making another live request and recording the new observation. Do not overwrite a prior run's manifest, retained bytes, or sealed snapshot.\n- On replay, preserve obligation/event identity and money; detect conflicting content under an existing event ID.\n- Implemented paths include fresh HTTP/export acquisition and source-bound transcription, plus explicitly offline connected claim, correction, independent cancellation and Finance replay. New source manifests retain response observations and partial/error bodies. Complete native policy access, rule interpretation, authoritative case clock and supported completion authority remain required for final live business compliance; acquisition or offline integrity alone does not establish it.\n"},"started_at_ms":1792012576859,"completed_at_ms":1792012576913}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-14T21:16:23.419Z","ordinal":1923,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a13c46-01fb-7d51-aa62-62cdd546a0f5","call_id":"call_b64ea619907e4f45b253e53bfb3a8659","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"f593f4\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.05462567,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":5471,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5471)\\nTotal output lines: 399\\n\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Synthetic end-to-end integration tests; no real arrival batch is consumed.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport json\\nfrom copy import deepcopy\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nfrom jsonschema import Draft202012Validator, FormatChecker\\nimport pytest\\n\\nfrom travel_claim.integration import integrate_arrival_batch\\n\\n\\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\\nSCHEMA = json.loads((ROOT / \\\"snapshot.schema.json\\\").read_text(encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\"))\\n\\n\\ndef _claim(claim_id, revision, *, trip_id, trip_revision=1, batch=1, employee=\\\"EMP-SYN-01\\\"):\\n    return {\\n        \\\"source_id\\\": \\\"synthetic-claim-binder\\\",\\n        \\\"source_sha256\\\": \\\"a\\\" * 64,\\n        \\\"locator\\\": f\\\"PDF page {revision} (SYNTHETIC {claim_id} revision {revision})\\\",\\n        \\\"page\\\": revision,\\n        \\\"fields\\\": [\\n            {\\\"label\\\": \\\"Claim reference\\\", \\\"value\\\": claim_id},\\n            {\\\"label\\\": \\\"Revision\\\", \\\"value\\\": str(revision)},\\n            {\\\"label\\\": \\\"Arrival batch\\\", \\\"value\\\": str(batch)},\\n            {\\\"label\\\": \\\"Employee\\\", \\\"value\\\": employee},\\n            {\\\"label\\\": \\\"Trip reference\\\", \\\"value\\\": trip_id},\\n            {\\\"label\\\": \\\"Trip revision\\\", \\\"value\\\": str(trip_revision)},\\n            {\\\"label\\\": \\\"Claim reason\\\", \\\"value\\\": \\\"SYNTHETIC fixture\\\"},\\n        ],\\n        \\\"text\\\": f\\\"SYNTHETIC TEST FIXTURE ONLY: {claim_id} revision {revision}\\\",\\n    }\\n\\n\\ndef _row(row, source_id, tab, **values):\\n    return {\\n        \\\"source_id\\\": source_id,\\n        \\\"source_sha256\\\": \\\"b\\\" * 64,\\n        \\\"locator\\\": f\\\"tab '{tab}', row {row} (SYNTHETIC)\\\",\\n        \\\"row\\\": row,\\n        \\\"values\\\": {\\n            key: {\\\"value\\\": value, \\\"source_text\\\": str(value), \\\"cell\\\": f\\\"A{row}\\\"}\\n            for key, value in values.items()\\n        },\\n    }\\n\\n\\ndef _decision(row, decision_id, claim_id, revision, batch=1):\\n    return _row(\\n        row, \\\"synthetic-review-ledger\\\", \\\"Review ledger\\\",\\n        **{\\n            \\\"Decision reference\\\": decision_id,\\n            \\\"Arrival batch\\\": batch,\\n            \\\"Subject type\\\": \\\"claim\\\",\\n            \\\"Subject reference\\\": claim_id,\\n            \\\"Revision\\\": revision,\\n            \\\"Review roles\\\": \\\"administration\\\",\\n            \\\"Reviewer\\\": \\\"ADMIN-SYN-01\\\",\\n            \\\"Outcome\\\": \\\"approve\\\",\\n            \\\"Reason\\\": \\\"SYNTHETIC observed decision; no policy conclusion\\\",\\n            \\\"Decision time (UTC)\\\": \\\"2026-09-01T12:00:00\\\",\\n        },\\n    )\\n\\n\\ndef _finance(row, event_id, claim_id, batch, event_type, *, amount=None, obligation=None):\\n    values = {\\n        \\\"Activity reference\\\": event_id,\\n        \\\"Arrival batch\\\": batch,\\n        \\\"Activity type\\\": event_type,\\n        \\\"Request reference\\\": f\\\"REQ-{claim_id}\\\",\\n        \\\"Claim reference\\\": claim_id,\\n        \\\"Finance officer\\\": \\\"FIN-SYN-01\\\",\\n        \\\"Payee ID\\\": \\\"EMP-SYN-01\\\",\\n        \\\"Currency\\\": \\\"EUR\\\",\\n        \\\"Reason\\\": f\\\"SYNTHETIC Finance fixture: {event_type}\\\",\\n    }\\n    if amount is not None:\\n        values[\\\"Amount (EUR)\\\"] = amount\\n    if obligation is not None:\\n        values[\\\"Obligation (EUR)\\\"] = obligation\\n    return _row(row, \\\"synthetic-finance-register\\\", \\\"Finance activity\\\", **values)\\n\\n\\ndef _cancel(row, event_id, cancellation_id, action, subject_type, *, batch, initiation=None):\\n    is_permit = subject_type == \\\"permit\\\"\\n    values = {\\n        \\\"Cancellation activity reference\\\": event_id,\\n        \\\"Cancellation reference\\\": cancellation_id,\\n        \\\"Action\\\": action,\\n        \\\"Cancelled subject\\\": subject_type,\\n        \\\"Trip reference\\\": \\\"T-SYN-01\\\",\\n        \\\"Trip revision\\\": 1,\\n        \\\"Permit reference\\\": \\\"P-SYN-01\\\",\\n        \\\"Permit revision\\\": 1,\\n        \\\"Acting employee or supervisor\\\": \\\"EMP-SYN-01\\\",\\n        \\\"Activity time (UTC)\\\": f\\\"2026-09-0{batch}T09:00:00\\\",\\n        \\\"Arrival batch\\\": batch,\\n        \\\"Business reason\\\": \\\"SYNTHETIC client rescheduling\\\",\\n    }\\n    if action == \\\"confirmed\\\":\\n        values[\\\"Initiation activity reference\\\"] = initiation\\n        values[\\\"Effective time (UTC)\\\"] = f\\\"2026-09-0{batch}T09:30:00\\\"\\n    return _row(row, \\\"synthetic-travel-register\\\", \\\"Travel cancellations\\\", **values)\\n\\n\\ndef _parsed_fixture():\\n    return {\\n        \\\"run_id\\\": \\\"run-synthetic-integration\\\",\\n        \\\"case_clock\\\": None,\\n        \\\"unresolved_issues\\\": [\\n            {\\n                \\\"record_id\\\": \\\"scenario-case-clock\\\",\\n                \\\"subject_type\\\": \\\"scenario\\\",\\n                \\\"subject_id\\\": \\\"arrival-batch-clock\\\",\\n                \\\"affected_scope\\\": \\\"all batches\\\",\\n                \\\"reason\\\": \\\"SYNTHETIC fixture: clock withheld\\\",\\n                \\\"owner\\\": \\\"Exercise facilitator\\\",\\n                \\\"next_action\\\": \\\"provide the scenario clock\\\",\\n                \\\"evidence_needed\\\": \\\"explicit date, time, and zone\\\",\\n            },\\n            {\\n                \\\"record_id\\\": \\\"reimbursement-policy-pol-2026-2\\\",\\n                \\\"subject_type\\\": \\\"policy\\\",\\n                \\\"subject_id\\\": \\\"POL-2026.2\\\",\\n                \\\"affected_scope\\\": \\\"eligibility and entitlement\\\",\\n                \\\"reason\\\": \\\"SYNTHETIC fixture: policy withheld\\\",\\n                \\\"owner\\\": \\\"Travel Administration Lead\\\",\\n                \\\"next_action\\\": \\\"provide an authorized native policy export\\\",\\n                \\\"evidence_needed\\\": \\\"complete policy content\\\",\\n            },\\n        ],\\n        \\\"records\\\": {\\n            \\\"claim_revisions\\\": [\\n                _claim(\\\"C-SYN-01\\\", 1, trip_id=\\\"T-SYN-01\\\", batch=1),\\n                _claim(\\\"C-SYN-02\\\", 1, trip_id=\\\"T-SYN-02\\\", batch=1, employee=\\\"EMP-SYN-02\\\"),\\n                _claim(\\\"C-SYN-01\\\", 2, trip_id=\\\"T-SYN-01\\\", batch=3),\\n            ],\\n            \\\"trips\\\": [\\n                _row(6, \\\"synthetic-travel-register\\\", \\\"Trips\\\", **{\\n                    \\\"Trip reference\\\": \\\"T-SYN-01\\\", \\\"Trip revision\\\": 1,\\n                    \\\"Permit reference\\\": \\\"P-SYN-01\\\", \\\"Permit revision\\\": 1,\\n                }),\\n                _row(7, \\\"synthetic-travel-register\\\", \\\"Trips\\\", **{\\n                    \\\"Trip reference\\\": \\\"T-SYN-02\\\", \\\"Trip revision\\\": 1,\\n                    \\\"Permit reference\\\": \\\"P-SYN-02\\\", \\\"Permit revision\\\": 1,\\n                }),\\n            ],\\n            \\\"decisions\\\": [\\n                _decision(6, \\\"D-SYN-01-R1\\\", \\\"C-SYN-01\\\", 1),\\n                _decision(7, \\\"D-SYN-02-R1\\\", \\\"C-SYN-02\\\", 1),\\n            ],\\n            \\\"finance_events\\\": [\\n                _finance(6, \\\"F-SYN-01-SETTLED\\\", \\\"C-SYN-01\\\", 2, \\\"settled\\\", amount=10.00),\\n                _finance(7, \\\"F-SYN-01-PENDING\\\", \\\"C-SYN-01\\\", 2, \\\"transfer_pending\\\", amount=5.00),\\n                _finance(8, \\\"F-SYN-02-SETTLED\\\", \\\"C-SYN-02\\\", 2, \\\"settled\\\", amount=4.00),\\n            ],\\n            \\\"cancellation_activities\\\": [\\n                _cancel(6, \\\"TC-SYN-TRIP-REQ\\\", \\\"TC-SYN-TRIP\\\", \\\"requested\\\", \\\"trip\\\", batch=1),\\n                _cancel(7, \\\"TC-SYN-PERMIT-REQ\\\", \\\"TC-SYN-PERMIT\\\", \\\"requested\\\", \\\"permit\\\", batch=1),\\n                _cancel(8, \\\"TC-SYN-TRIP-CFM\\\", \\\"TC-SYN-TRIP\\\", \\\"confirmed\\\", \\\"trip\\\", batch=2,\\n                        initiation=\\\"TC-SYN-TRIP-REQ\\\"),\\n                _cancel(9, \\\"TC-SYN-PERMIT-CFM\\\", \\\"TC-SYN-PERMIT\\\", \\\"confirmed\\\", \\\"permit\\\", batch=2,\\n                        initiation=\\\"TC-SYN-PERMIT-REQ\\\"),\\n\\n\\ndef _batches(parsed):\\n    prior = None\\n    results = []\\n    for batch in parsed['arrival_batches']:\\n        prior = integrate_arrival_batch(\\n            parsed, arrival_batch=batch, run_id='retained-regression', batch_id=f'arrival-{batch:03d}',\\n            source_binding={'path': 'sources.json', 'sha256': 'a' * 64},\\n            predecessor={'path': f'batches/arrival-{batch-1:03d}.json', 'sha256': 'b' * 64} if prior else None,\\n            prior_result=prior,\\n        )\\n        results.append(prior)\\n    return results\\n\\n\\ndef test_native_obligation_fields_and_ledger_balances_do_not_become_entitlement():\\n    parsed = _fixture()\\n    assert 'Claim revision' not in parsed['provenance']['finance_headers']\\n    results = _batches(parsed)\\n    final = results[-1]\\n    c1 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C01']\\n    obligation = c1['recorded_obligation']\\n    assert obligation['event_id'] == 'F-C01-accepted'\\n    assert obligation['request_id'] == 'REQ-C01'\\n    assert obligation['finance_officer'] == 'FIN-01'\\n    assert obligation['payee_id'] == 'EMP-01'\\n    assert obligation['amount_cents'] == 10000\\n    assert obligation['claim_revision'] is None\\n    assert obligation['arrival_revision_context'] == 1\\n    assert obligation['revision_link_status'] == 'arrival_context_only'\\n    assert obligation['first_arrival_batch'] == 1\\n    assert obligation['source_refs'] == [\\n        'travel-registers-workbook@' + parsed['provenance']['workbook_sha256'] + \\\"#tab 'Finance activity', row 33\\\"\\n    ]\\n    assert obligation['claim_source_refs'][0]['locator'] == 'PDF page 1'\\n    assert c1['net_confirmed_cents'] == 10000 …1271 tokens truncated… 1, \\\"Outcome\\\": \\\"approve\\\"}),\\n        _workbook_record(11, **{\\\"Decision reference\\\": \\\"D-SYN-UNKNOWN\\\", \\\"Subject type\\\": \\\"trip\\\",\\n                                \\\"Subject reference\\\": \\\"T-SYN-01\\\", \\\"Revision\\\": 9, \\\"Outcome\\\": \\\"return\\\"}),\\n    ]\\n    matches = match_decisions_to_subjects(decisions, history)\\n    assert [row[\\\"structural_match\\\"] for row in matches] == [\\\"revision_match_historical\\\", \\\"revision_not_found\\\"]\\n    assert [row[\\\"applied\\\"] for row in matches] == [False, False]\\n    assert matches[0][\\\"observed_outcome\\\"] == \\\"approve\\\"  # preserved observation; no approval is performed\\n\\n\\ndef test_cancellation_state_machine_keeps_trip_and_permit_processes_independent():\\n    events = [\\n        _cancellation_row(6, event_id=\\\"TC-SYN-P-REQ\\\", cancellation_id=\\\"TC-SYN-P\\\",\\n                          action=\\\"requested\\\", target_type=\\\"permit\\\", target_id=\\\"P-SYN-01\\\", batch=1),\\n        _cancellation_row(7, event_id=\\\"TC-SYN-T-REQ\\\", cancellation_id=\\\"TC-SYN-T\\\",\\n                          action=\\\"requested\\\", target_type=\\\"trip\\\", target_id=\\\"T-SYN-01\\\", batch=1),\\n        _cancellation_row(8, event_id=\\\"TC-SYN-P-CFM\\\", cancellation_id=\\\"TC-SYN-P\\\",\\n                          action=\\\"confirmed\\\", target_type=\\\"permit\\\", target_id=\\\"P-SYN-01\\\", batch=2,\\n                          initiation=\\\"TC-SYN-P-REQ\\\", effective=\\\"2026-11-16T09:00:00+01:00\\\"),\\n    ]\\n    result = reduce_cancellation_activities(events)\\n    assert result[\\\"processes\\\"][\\\"TC-SYN-P\\\"][\\\"state\\\"] == \\\"confirmed\\\"\\n    assert result[\\\"processes\\\"][\\\"TC-SYN-T\\\"][\\\"state\\\"] == \\\"requested\\\"\\n    assert result[\\\"processes\\\"][\\\"TC-SYN-T\\\"][\\\"next_action\\\"] == \\\"await a linked confirmation activity\\\"\\n    assert result[\\\"finance_effects\\\"] == []\\n    assert result[\\\"claim_effects\\\"] == []\\n    assert result[\\\"processes\\\"][\\\"TC-SYN-P\\\"][\\\"target\\\"] == {\\n        \\\"subject_type\\\": \\\"permit\\\", \\\"subject_id\\\": \\\"P-SYN-01\\\", \\\"revision\\\": 1,\\n    }\\n\\n\\ndef test_event_deduplication_is_replay_safe_and_flags_same_id_payload_conflicts():\\n    # Synthetic Finance-like event IDs; arrival batch is delivery metadata.\\n    first = _workbook_record(6, **{\\\"Activity reference\\\": \\\"F-SYN-01\\\", \\\"Arrival batch\\\": 2,\\n                                  \\\"Activity type\\\": \\\"settled\\\", \\\"Amount (EUR)\\\": 100.0,\\n                                  \\\"Claim reference\\\": \\\"C-SYN-01\\\"})\\n    replay = _workbook_record(31, **{\\\"Activity reference\\\": \\\"F-SYN-01\\\", \\\"Arrival batch\\\": 4,\\n                                    \\\"Activity type\\\": \\\"settled\\\", \\\"Amount (EUR)\\\": 100.0,\\n                                    \\\"Claim reference\\\": \\\"C-SYN-01\\\"})\\n    changed = _workbook_record(32, **{\\\"Activity reference\\\": \\\"F-SYN-01\\\", \\\"Arrival batch\\\": 4,\\n                                      \\\"Activity type\\\": \\\"settled\\\", \\\"Amount (EUR)\\\": 120.0,\\n                                      \\\"Claim reference\\\": \\\"C-SYN-01\\\"})\\n    exact = deduplicate_activity_records([first, replay], id_field=\\\"Activity reference\\\")\\n    assert len(exact[\\\"unique_events\\\"]) == 1\\n    assert exact[\\\"duplicates\\\"][0][\\\"delivery_batches\\\"] == [2, 4]\\n    assert exact[\\\"conflicts\\\"] == []\\n    conflict = deduplicate_activity_records([first, changed], id_field=\\\"Activity reference\\\")\\n    assert conflict[\\\"unique_events\\\"] == []\\n    assert conflict[\\\"conflicts\\\"][0][\\\"event_id\\\"] == \\\"F-SYN-01\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef test_actual_retained_activity_replays_are_deduplicated_and_cancellation_ids_are_separate(tmp_path):\\n    parsed = parse_retained_run(CAPTURE, output_path=tmp_path / \\\"parsed.json\\\")\\n    history = build_revision_history(parsed)\\n    c09 = history[\\\"claim\\\"][\\\"C09\\\"]\\ndef _domain_seed() -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    return {\\n        \\\"processed_batches\\\": [],\\n        \\\"batch_input_hashes\\\": {},\\n        \\\"claim_records\\\": [],\\n        \\\"decision_records\\\": [],\\n        \\\"finance_records\\\": [],\\n        \\\"cancellation_records\\\": [],\\n        \\\"revision_history\\\": None,\\n        \\\"decision_history\\\": [],\\n        \\\"finance_reconciliations\\\": {},\\n        \\\"ordinary_workflows\\\": {},\\n        \\\"ordinary_workflow_history\\\": [],\\n        \\\"authorized_obligations\\\": {},\\n        \\\"source_classifications\\\": {},\\n        \\\"cancellation_state\\\": {},\\n        \\\"material_corrections\\\": [],\\n        \\\"repair_queue\\\": new_repair_queue(),\\n        \\\"policy_clock_blockers\\\": [],\\n        \\\"structural_blockers\\\": [],\\n        \\\"projection_issues\\\": [],\\n    }\\n\\n\\ndef _issue_from_item(item: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    return {\\n        \\\"record_id\\\": item[\\\"item_id\\\"],\\n        \\\"reason\\\": item[\\\"missing_or_return_reason\\\"],\\n        \\\"owner\\\": item[\\\"owner\\\"],\\n1. Bind every fact and decision to its source, subject, and revision.\\n2. Hold only claims or dependent work affected by missing/conflicting facts. Continue independent valid work. Each unresolved item retains subject type and exact ID, revision, missing/conflicting fact, responsible owner, source reference, and next action.\\n3. Preserve every claim revision. After a material correction, use the corrected revision and revalidate affected evidence, calculations, trip/permit consistency, approvals, and Finance authorization. Preserve unrelated evidence only where it remains valid. Retain historical commitments, transfers, and refunds; do not use stale approvals as current.\\n4. Keep trip cancellation and permit cancellation as independent processes, including processes without claims. Cancellation does not itself erase entitlement or Finance obligations. Record Finance disposition and monetary resolution separately when required.\\n5. Use the owner-grouped local repair queue. Keep each item individually traceable. A partial response may resolve only the item(s) explicitly matched and supported by retained source evidence; unanswered, insufficient, or conflicting items stay open. Draft locally; never send requests.\\n6. Preserve immutable Finance event identifiers. Reconcile only confirmed transfers and refunds. Do not duplicate events or obligations on replay.\\n7. The provisional financial closure choice is to require current evidence and approvals, agreement between reviewed entitlement and authorized obligation, net confirmed payment equal to the authorized amount, required Finance resolutions, and no blocking issue. After the first actual processing result, pause for the operator to inspect reconciliation and unresolved cases and confirm final completion conditions and delivery scope.\\n\\nPeople retain business approval, exception, and payment authority. This Skill prepares work, validates supplied decisions, and records effects; it does not make discretionary approval recommendations, create replies, issue Finance exceptions, book travel, or move funds.\\n\\n## Outputs\\n\\n- `artifacts/runs/<run-id>/sources.json` and retained source bytes.\\n- One immutable schema-valid `batches/<batch-id>.json` per consumed batch, with relative source and predecessor paths plus SHA-256 hashes.\\n- `claims.csv` with exactly `claim_id,revision,trip_id,status,allowed_cents,paid_cents,balance_cents,next_owner,reason`.\\n- Owner-grouped local repair queue with individual items and run/batch update history.\\n- `report.md` describing completed work, obligations, unresolved items, owners, next actions, cancellations without claims, and source/run references.\\n\\nUnknown money is null in JSON and blank in CSV. Zero is a known amount. Never label incomplete work complete.\\n\\n## Errors, retries, and limitations\\n\\n- On source failure, retain the attempt URL, locator, UTC observation time, error, and missing scope. Hold only affected work and report its owner and resumption evidence.\\n- On partial source access, retain usable pieces and explicitly list missing scope. Do not claim the source was fully read.\\n- On invalid or conflicting batch data, preserve the input evidence, reject admission of unsupported effects, and create an owned issue; do not silently discard it.\\n- Retry a failed fresh retrieval only by making another live request and recording the new observation. Do not overwrite a prior run's manifest, retained bytes, or sealed snapshot.\\n- On replay, preserve obligation/event identity and money; detect conflicting content under an existing event ID.\\n- Implemented paths include fresh HTTP/export acquisition and source-bound transcription, plus explicitly offline connected claim, correction, independent cancellation and Finance replay. New source manifests retain response observations and partial/error bodies. Complete native policy access, rule interpretation, authoritative case clock and supported completion authority remain required for final live business compliance; acquisition or offline integrity alone does not establish it.\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id"