acts.\n\nRun the complete pytest suite, snapshot integrity checks, and git diff --check.\n\nDo not invent approvals, policy rules, cancellation confirmations, refunds, or the missing case clock. Preserve all earlier artifacts and the original interview.\n\nDo not commit or push yet.\n\nReport changed files, demonstrated cases, executed transitions, remaining blockers, and tests passed.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":80},"id":"msg_01a13c1b-1f15-76b0-86df-f439e8dab010","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792009772.8211133,"turn_id":"01a13c1b-19a6-7c30-952c-e0611fda1bab"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Preserve the completed Project D Step 157 correction revalidation and independent cancellation milestone.\n\n    Inspect git status, the complete source diff, and the staging area.\n\n    Stage ONLY these nine files:\n\n        README.md\n\n        src/travel_claim/integration.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/ordinary.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/workflow.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/readiness.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/revalidation.py\n\n        tests/test_readiness.py\n\n        tests/test_revalidation.py\n\n    Do not stage artifacts/runs/, artifacts/verification/, the original interview, or unrelated files.\n\nRun git diff --cached --check and the complete pytest suite.\n\nIf validation passes, commit with:\nfeat: revalidate corrections and independent cancellations\n\nPush to origin main, allowing existing Entire.io hooks to run.\n\nVerify the exact remote main commit and Entire.io checkpoint references.\n\nVerify the original interview and all 82 previously retained files remain unchanged.\n\nDo not force-push, rewrite history, or modify retained artifacts.\n\nReport the commit hash, tests passed, push verification, checkpoint results, and any warnings.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":88},"id":"msg_01a13c24-0261-7422-af77-805703d54b52","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792010355.2979228,"turn_id":"01a13c23-fc3d-7aa1-be2f-35410ab86ebd"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Continue Project D from verified commit 87dbd1c504034f6393326ed2aa9a5e09fbe7a14f.\n\nAudit and, where necessary, implement the fresh native-source execution workflow required by the original Project D assignment.\n\nThe assignment requires every new live run to attempt fresh reads of all five native source locations, preserve complete relevant content actually used, bind it in sources.json, and explicitly report inaccessible or incomplete sources.\n\nInspect the current CLI, source capture, parsing, snapshots, Skill, and README.\n\nDetermine whether the current implementation can perform a fresh live run from the five original URLs without silently reusing prior retained inputs.\n\nImplement missing live-run functionality where technically possible, including distinct run IDs, retrieval observations, completeness checks, source hashes, source versions, and failure scope.\n\nPreserve source wording, identities, numeric precision, arrival batches, and history.\n\nEnsure inaccessible policy content remains explicitly blocked rather than substituted with assumptions.\n\nVerify that a failed or partial live retrieval cannot be mislabeled as a complete successful run.\n\nAdd regression tests for successful retrieval, partial access, failed retrieval, and prohibited fallback to cached inputs.\n\nPerform a new live-source attempt if the supported browser/API/export access is available. Otherwise explain exactly which access mechanism is missing.\n\nRun the full test suite, source-manifest validation, and git diff --check.\n\nDo not overwrite earlier runs or modify the original interview. Do not invent policy content or a case clock.\n\nDo not commit or push yet.\n\nReport changed files, native source access results, test count, and remaining blockers.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":95},"id":"msg_01a13c28-ce86-7022-8198-88f4bc47f48c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792010669.7020998,"turn_id":"01a13c28-c6bd-7171-9c10-8efd3c67b498"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Preserve the completed Project D Step 162 fresh native-source execution milestone.\n\n    Inspect git status, all source diffs, and the staging area.\n\n    Stage ONLY these implementation files, if present and changed:\n\n        README.md\n\n        skills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md\n\n        src/travel_claim/cli.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/sources.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/parsing.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/readiness.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/live_run.py\n\n        The changed or newly created test/helper files for this milestone, after listing their exact paths and verifying their contents.\n\n    Do not stage artifacts/runs/, artifacts/verification/, the original interview, or unrelated files.\n\n    Run git diff --cached --check and the complete pytest suite.\n\nVerify the new live-source manifest and retained response evidence.\n\nIf validation passes, commit with:\nfeat: capture and validate fresh native source runs\n\nPush to origin main, allowing the existing Entire.io hooks to run.\n\nVerify the exact remote main commit and Entire.io checkpoint references.\n\nConfirm the original interview and all 104 previously retained files remain unchanged.\n\nDo not force-push, rewrite history, or modify retained artifacts.\n\nReport the exact committed files, commit hash, test count, source-verification results, push verification, and warnings.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":