cellation processing.\n\nInspect the original retained interview, source records, existing integration, ordinary workflow, Finance reconciliation, snapshots, and tests.\n\nTrace all material claim corrections across arrival batches and determine exactly which dependent evidence, approvals, requests, and financial states require revalidation.\n\nExecute the required rechecks rather than merely recording revalidation tasks. Preserve valid unaffected evidence and full revision history.\n\nProcess trip and permit cancellations independently of claim existence. Preserve initiation, confirmation, source references, and any unresolved financial disposition.\n\nPropagate cancellation effects to linked claims and requests without incorrectly blocking unrelated claims.\n\nDistinguish a cancelled transfer from a cash refund, and preserve actual Finance event identity and history.\n\nDemonstrate representative retained correction and cancellation cases with exact source references and before/after states.\n\nAdd regression tests for stale approvals, changed receipts, revised amounts, duplicate events, partial cancellation information, and independent no-claim cancellations.\n\nGenerate a new labeled offline replay and verification report without overwriting prior artifacts.\n\nRun the complete pytest suite, snapshot integrity checks, and git diff --check.\n\nDo not invent approvals, policy rules, cancellation confirmations, refunds, or the missing case clock. Preserve all earlier artifacts and the original interview.\n\nDo not commit or push yet.\n\nReport changed files, demonstrated cases, executed transitions, remaining blockers, and tests passed.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a13c1b-1f15-76b0-86df-f439e8dab010","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792009772.8211133,"turn_id":"01a13c1b-19a6-7c30-952c-e0611fda1bab"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Preserve the completed Project D Step 157 correction revalidation and independent cancellation milestone.\n\n    Inspect git status, the complete source diff, and the staging area.\n\n    Stage ONLY these nine files:\n\n        README.md\n\n        src/travel_claim/integration.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/ordinary.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/workflow.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/readiness.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/revalidation.py\n\n        tests/test_readiness.py\n\n        tests/test_revalidation.py\n\n    Do not stage artifacts/runs/, artifacts/verification/, the original interview, or unrelated files.\n\nRun git diff --cached --check and the complete pytest suite.\n\nIf validation passes, commit with:\nfeat: revalidate corrections and independent cancellations\n\nPush to origin main, allowing existing Entire.io hooks to run.\n\nVerify the exact remote main commit and Entire.io checkpoint references.\n\nVerify the original interview and all 82 previously retained files remain unchanged.\n\nDo not force-push, rewrite history, or modify retained artifacts.\n\nReport the commit hash, tests passed, push verification, checkpoint results, and any warnings.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a13c24-0261-7422-af77-805703d54b52","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792010355.2979228,"turn_id":"01a13c23-fc3d-7aa1-be2f-35410ab86ebd"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Continue Project D from verified commit 87dbd1c504034f6393326ed2aa9a5e09fbe7a14f.\n\nAudit and, where necessary, implement the fresh native-source execution workflow required by the original Project D assignment.\n\nThe assignment requires every new live run to attempt fresh reads of all five native source locations, preserve complete relevant content actually used, bind it in sources.json, and explicitly report inaccessible or incomplete sources.\n\nInspect the current CLI, source capture, parsing, snapshots, Skill, and README.\n\nDetermine whether the current implementation can perform a fresh live run from the five original URLs without silently reusing prior retained inputs.\n\nImplement missing live-run functionality where technically possible, including distinct run IDs, retrieval observations, completeness checks, source hashes, source versions, and failure scope.\n\nPreserve source wording, identities, numeric precision, arrival batches, and history.\n\nEnsure inaccessible policy content remains explicitly blocked rather than substituted with assumptions.\n\nVerify that a failed or partial live retrieval cannot be mislabeled as a complete successful run.\n\nAdd regression tests for successful retrieval, partial access, failed retrieval, and prohibited fallback to cached inputs.\n\nPerform a new live-source attempt if the supported browser/API/export access is available. Otherwise explain exactly which access mechanism is missing.\n\nRun the full test suite, source-manifest validation, and git diff --check.\n\nDo not overwrite earlier runs or modify the original interview. Do not invent policy content or a case clock.\n\nDo not commit or push yet.\n\nReport changed files, native source access results, test count, and remaining blockers.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a13c28-ce86-7022-8198-88f4bc47f48c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792010669.7020998,"turn_id":"01a13c28-c6bd-7171-9c10-8efd3c67b498"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Preserve the completed Project D Step 162 fresh native-source execution milestone.\n\n    Inspect git status, all source diffs, and the staging area.\n\n    Stage ONLY these implementation files, if present and changed:\n\n        README.md\n\n        skills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md\n\n        src/travel_claim/cli.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/sources.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/parsing.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/readiness.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/live_run.py\n\n        The changed or newly created test/helper files for this milestone, after listing their exact paths and verifying their contents.\n\n    Do not stage artifacts/runs/, artifacts/verification/, the original interview, or unrelated files.\n\n    Run git diff --cached --check and the complete pytest suite.\n\nVerify the new live-source manifest and retained response evidence.\n\nIf validation passes, commit with:\nfeat: capture and validate fresh native source runs\n\nPush to origin main, allowing the existing Entire.io hooks to run.\n\nVerify the exact remote main commit and Entire.io checkpoint references.\n\nConfirm the original interview and all 104 previously retained files remain unchanged.\n\nDo not force-push, rewrite history, or modify retained artifacts.\n\nReport the exact committed files, commit hash, test count, source-verification results, push verification, and warnings.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a13c32-aa2f-73f1-901a-e19eda017436","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792011315.7594304,"turn_id":"01a13c32-a4fc-7732-902b-be443b2f0740"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Project D — Step 167: Incorporate the newly recovered authoritative policy.\n\nI personally opened the original Alderbridge Consulting Notion policy URL in my browser and copied its complete visible text. It identifies itself as POL-2026.2 and explicitly states the case clock is 2026-11-15, Europe/Amsterdam.\n\nThe policy text is available from me, the user. Do not invent, paraphrase, or reconstruct any missing wording.\n\nFirst, help me save the exact policy text as a UTF-8 file under a clearly labeled user-provided-source directory. Ask me for the file or exact text if it is not accessible in your environment.\n\nPreserve its original wording and distinguish my authenticated/browser-visible copy from a fresh native Notion API or HTTP read. Do not retroactively mark earlier failed Notion captures successful.\n\nThen:\n\nVerify the policy identifier, case clock, and complete retained text.\n\nInspect the current implementation against every policy section, including eligibility, approvals, filing deadlines, caps, FX, Finance reconciliation, corrections, and independent cancellations.\n\nProduce a source-grounded implementation gap report with exact code and policy references.\n\nIdentify which blockers are resolved by the recovered policy and which still require independent evidence or human decisions.\n\nDo not alter earlier runs, snapshots, or financial conclusions.\n\nDo not commit or push yet.\n\nStop after the evidence audit and report the findings before making implementation changes.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a13c3b-aed3-74d2-9d9f-47b124fb6cac","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792011906.7714906,"turn_id":"01a13c3b-a823-7ce1-9b0c-108a6e62bf92"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"The complete original POL-2026.2 browser copy is now available at:\n\n`user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt`\n\nThis is the policy I personally copied from the original Notion page.\n\nVerify its SHA-256 against:\n\n`f547ee77729be8ad431a5ddf2e2907f94f29ad50092231191abd2f72c04f54d2`\n\nPreserve its exact text and provenance. The policy states a case date of 2026-11-15 in Europe/Amsterdam; do not invent a time of day.\n\nNow perform the Step 167 policy-to-implementation gap audit. Do not modify earlier captures, implement changes, commit, or push yet.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a13c3d-08ba-7140-ade6-5f1ea52ccca3","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792011995.3221362,"turn_id":"01a13c3d-01ac-7382-a75c-f5f6b0ed7d61"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"The recovered POL-2026.2 policy file is now present at:\n\n/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt\n\nI verified its SHA-256:\n\nf547ee77729be8ad431a5ddf2e2907f94f29ad50092231191abd2f72c04f54d2\n\nThis is the complete browser-visible policy text I personally copied from the original Notion page.\n\nPlease resume Step 167:\n\nVerify the file, policy version, and case clock.\n\nRecord its provenance separately from native source captures.\n\nAudit every policy section against the existing implementation and tests.\n\nIdentify missing rules, defects, and remaining external blockers.\n\nPreserve all prior runs, snapshots, and financial conclusions.\n\nDo not implement changes, commit, or push yet.\n\nStop after presenting the policy-to-implementation gap report.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a13c40-42a7-7720-bad1-016e57645ad1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792012206.7595844,"turn_id":"01a13c40-3bbc-7d50-8ce8-5e7628d5b3da"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Project D — Step 171: Fix high-risk policy compliance defects.\n\nUse the verified POL-2026.2 browser copy and the completed Step 167 audit as authoritative references.\n\nFocus ONLY on these two areas:\n\nFinance event integrity:\n\nAn admitted confirmed transfer must never disappear because of a later conflicting event redelivery.\n\nExact immutable-event replay must have no additional effect.\n\nConflicting replay must retain the admitted event and hold the affected case for Finance resolution.\n\nValidate Finance event identity, request, payee, currency, positive integer cents, time and actor.\n\nPreserve unmatched and invalid events for review.\n\nIndependent cancellation validation:\n\nOnly the authorized directory supervisor can confirm a cancellation.\n\nConfirmation must reference the matching initiation and target.\n\nConfirmation must occur strictly after initiation.\n\nReject scheduled, backdated, stale-target, wrong-actor and future-observation confirmations as authority.\n\nPreserve invalid deliveries as visible evidence without changing admitted cancellation history.\n\nKeep business cancellation separate from Finance cancellation.\n\nRequirements:\n\nAdd focused regression tests reproducing the defects identified in the Step 167 synthetic probes.\n\nPreserve all earlier snapshots, financial outputs, original interview and policy copy.\n\nDo not silently alter unrelated eligibility, approval or closure rules.\n\nRun the complete test suite and report the results.\n\nReport any remaining ambiguity rather than inventing facts.\n\nDo not commit or push yet.\n\nStop after implementation, tests and a concise change summary.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a13c45-9e2e-7f42-8320-94e33cef53b3","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792012557.8708947,"turn_id":"01a13c45-9846-7111-9cb7-eca8b1cc3957"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Project D — Step 172: Commit and push the verified event-integrity fixes.\n\nBefore committing:\n\n    Verify the current branch, Git status and diff.\n\n    Confirm the changes are limited to Step 171 Finance event integrity, cancellation validation, supporting fixtures and regression tests.\n\n    Run the complete test suite again and git diff --check.\n\n    Verify the original policy, interview, prior snapshots and retained outputs remain unchanged.\n\n    Stage only the reviewed Step 171 implementation and test files. Do not stage unrelated untracked artifacts or audit reports.\n\n    Commit with message: fix: preserve admitted finance and cancellation event integrity\n\nPush normally to the existing GitHub main branch. Do not force-push.\n\nVerify the remote commit matches the local commit and confirm the Entire.io checkpoint references were pushed.\n\nReport the full commit SHA, number of passing tests, changed files, remote verification and Entire.io checkpoint status.\n\nIf any verification fails, stop without pushing and explain the issue.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a13c51-eb95-7671-8964-a9f57fb3039f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792013364.1171467,"turn_id":"01a13c51-e5b0-75a2-acee-0c608041a033"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cskills_instructions\u003e\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and a short path that can be expanded into an absolute path using the skill roots table.\n### Skill roots\n- `r0` = `/home/maxg/.codex/skills/.system`\n- `r1` = `/home/maxg/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote`\n- `r2` = `/home/maxg/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated-remote/work-pets/0.1.6/skills`\n### Available skills\n- imagegen: Generate or edit raster images when the task benefits from AI-created bitmap visuals such as photos, illustrations, textures, sprites, mockups, or transparent-background cutouts. Use when Codex should create a brand-new image, transform an existing image, or derive visual variants from references, and the output should be a bitmap asset rather than repo-native code or vector. Do not use when the task is better handled by editing existing SVG/vector/code-native assets, extending an established icon or logo system, or building the visual directly in HTML/CSS/canvas. (file: r0/imagegen/SKILL.md)\n- openai-docs: Use for Codex models/pricing, scheduled tasks, skills, settings, setup, troubleshooting, customization, automations, and self-knowledge—including 'you,' 'your,' 'this app,' or 'this coding agent' when they refer to Codex—and for OpenAI APIs/products and ChatGPT Work. Also use for model choice/migration, prompting, SDKs, Responses, Realtime, agents, evals, and Chat/Work/Codex comparisons. Do not use for generic app/software tasks that merely mention Codex. (file: r0/openai-docs/SKILL.md)\n- skill-creator: Create or update a Codex skill with appropriately scoped instructions and any needed supporting resources. (file: r0/skill-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-installer: Install Codex skills into $CODEX_HOME/skills from a curated list or a GitHub repo path. Use when a user asks to list installable skills, install a curated skill, or install a skill from another repo (including private repos). (file: r0/skill-installer/SKILL.md)\n- plugin-management:plugin-management: Discover and suggest relevant plugins, inspect app permissions and dependencies, and manage plugin connections or removal. Use when the user asks about plugins or when a task would materially benefit from an external app, account, service, or data source that available tools cannot access. (file: r1/plugin-management/0.1.0/skills/plugin-management/SKILL.md)\n- sites:sites: Use Sites when the user wants a website built for them (including a landing page, portfolio, dashboard, portal, tracker, hub, game, event registration, or tool), requests changes to a website already built with Sites, wants to publish a website with Sites, or wants to manage Sites hosting. (file: r1/sites/1.0.0/skills/sites/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:create-pet: Create, repair, validate, preview, upload, or activate an animated v2 pet in ChatGPT Work mode from a character idea, brand cue, or reference image. Use for new ChatGPT Pets, custom mascots, non-pixel styles, and unattached sprite sheets requiring nine animation states plus sixteen look directions. Preserve Library artifacts and Pets MCP lifecycle behavior. Exclude real pets, standalone images, and other-app pets; clarify before invoking. (file: r2/create-pet/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:pets: List, inspect, select, download, or delete animated pets in ChatGPT Work mode. Use for an explicit pet in ChatGPT or established ChatGPT Pets context. Exclude real-world and other-app pets; clarify before invoking. (file: r2/pets/SKILL.md)\n- work-pets:update-pet: Inspect, validate, preview, repair, or update a custom pet in ChatGPT Work mode, including its name, description, or sprite sheet. Use for a pet in ChatGPT or established ChatGPT Pets context. Exclude real-world and other-app pets; clarify before invoking. (file: r2/update-pet/SKILL.md)\n\u003c/skills_instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003cpermissions instructions\u003e\nFilesystem sandboxing defines which files can be read or written. `sandbox_mode` is `workspace-write`: The sandbox permits reading files, and editing files in `cwd` and `writable_roots`. Editing files in other directories requires approval. Network access is restricted.\n# Escalation Requests\n\nCommands are run outside the sandbox if they are approved by the user, or match an existing rule that allows it to run unrestricted. The command string is split into independent command segments at shell control operators, including but not limited to:\n\n- Pipes: |\n- Logical operators: \u0026\u0026, ||\n- Command separators: ;\n- Subshell boundaries: (...), $(...)\n\nEach resulting segment is evaluated independently for sandbox restrictions and approval requirements.\n\nExample:\n\ngit pull | tee output.txt\n\nThis is treated as two command segments:\n\n[\"git\", \"pull\"]\n\n[\"tee\", \"output.txt\"]\n\nCommands that use more advanced shell features like redirection (\u003e, \u003e\u003e, \u003c), substitutions ($(...), ...), environment variables (FOO=bar), or wildcard patterns (*, ?) will not be evaluated against rules, to limit the scope of what an approved rule allows.\n\n## How to request escalation\n\nIMPORTANT: To request approval to execute a command that will require escalated privileges:\n\n- Provide the `sandbox_permissions` parameter with the value `\"require_escalated\"`\n- Include a short question asking the user if they want to allow the action in `justification` parameter. e.g. \"Do you want to download and install dependencies for this project?\"\n- Optionally suggest a `prefix_rule` - this will be shown to the user with an option to persist the rule approval for future sessions.\n\nIf you run a command that is important to solving the user's query, but it fails because of sandboxing or with a likely sandbox-related network error (for example DNS/host resolution, registry/index access, or dependency download failure), rerun the command with \"require_escalated\". ALWAYS proceed to use the `justification` parameter - do not message the user before requesting approval for the command.\n\n## When to request escalation\n\nWhile commands are running inside the sandbox, here are some scenarios that will require escalation outside the sandbox:\n\n- You need to run a command that writes to a directory that requires it (e.g. running tests that write to /var)\n- You need to run a GUI app (e.g., open/xdg-open/osascript) to open browsers or files.\n- If you run a command that is important to solving the user's query, but it fails because of sandboxing or with a likely sandbox-related network error (for example DNS/host resolution, registry/index access, or dependency download failure), rerun the command with `require_escalated`. ALWAYS proceed to use the `sandbox_permissions` and `justification` parameters. do not message the user before requesting approval for the command.\n- You are about to take a potentially destructive action such as an `rm` or `git reset` that the user did not explicitly ask for.\n- Be judicious with escalating, but if completing the user's request requires it, you should do so - don't try and circumvent approvals by using other tools.\n\n## prefix_rule guidance\n\nWhen choosing a `prefix_rule`, request one that will allow you to fulfill similar requests from the user in the future without re-requesting escalation. It should be categorical and reasonably scoped to similar capabilities. You should rarely pass the entire command into `prefix_rule`.\n\n### Banned prefix_rules \nAvoid requesting overly broad prefixes that the user would be ill-advised to approve. For example, do not request [\"python3\"], [\"python\", \"-\"], or other similar prefixes that would allow arbitrary scripting.\nNEVER provide a prefix_rule argument for destructive commands like rm.\nNEVER provide a prefix_rule if your command uses a heredoc or herestring. \n\n### Examples\nGood examples of prefixes:\n- [\"npm\", \"run\", \"dev\"]\n- [\"gh\", \"pr\", \"check\"]\n- [\"cargo\", \"test\"]\n The writable roots are `/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim`, `/tmp`.\n\u003c/permissions instructions\u003e","type":"input_text"},{"text":"\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e# Collaboration Mode: Default\n\nYou are now in Default mode. Any previous instructions for other modes (e.g. Plan mode) are no longer active.\n\nYour active mode changes only when new developer instructions with a different `\u003ccollaboration_mode\u003e...\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e` change it; user requests or tool descriptions do not change mode by themselves. Known mode names are Default and Plan.\n\n## request_user_input availability\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only when it is listed in the available tools for this turn.\n\nUse the `request_user_input` tool only for optional questions where the answer would materially improve the quality of the work.\n\nIf `request_user_input` returns no answers, continue with best judgment instead of asking again or treating the turn as blocked.\n\nNever use the `request_user_input` tool for permission requests or permission-related escalations.\n\u003c/collaboration_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a13c5b-9919-7e32-b226-9d791e42522a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["host_skills.instructions","permissions.instructions","collaboration_mode.instructions"],"turn_id":"01a13c57-6fc6-7d93-a6e4-729352fb610c"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_role\u003eYou are `/root`, the primary agent in a team of agents collaborating to fulfill the user's goals.\n\nAt the start of your turn, you are the active agent.\nYou can spawn sub-agents to handle subtasks, and those sub-agents can spawn their own sub-agents.\nAll agents in the team, including the agents that you can assign tasks to, are equally intelligent and capable, and have access to the same set of tools.\n\nYou can use `spawn_agent` to create a new agent, `followup_task` to give an existing agent a new task and trigger a turn, and `send_message` to pass a message to a running agent without triggering a turn.\n`send_message` calls may be read by a human, so ensure they are legible. Always put proper spaces between words and/or numbers.\nChild agents can also spawn their own sub-agents.\nYou can decide how much context you want to propagate to your sub-agents with the `fork_turns` parameter.\n\nYou will receive messages in the analysis channel in the form:\n```\nMessage Type: MESSAGE | FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: \u003crecipient\u003e\nSender: \u003cauthor\u003e\nPayload:\n\u003cpayload text\u003e\n```\nThey may be addressed as to=/root\n\nNote that collaboration tools cannot be called from inside `functions.exec`. Call `spawn_agent`, `send_message`, `followup_task`, `wait_agent`, `interrupt_agent`, and `list_agents` only as direct tool calls using the recipient shown in their tool definitions, such as `to=functions.collaboration.spawn_agent`, since they are intentionally absent from the `functions.exec` `tools.*` namespace. Available tools in `functions.exec` are explicitly described with a `tools` namespace in the developer message.\n\nAll agents share the same directory. In detail:\n- All agents have access to the same container and filesystem as you.\n- All agents use the same current working directory.\n- As a result, edits made by one agent are immediately visible to all other agents.\n\nWhen calling `wait_agent`, prefer longer waits (minutes) to avoid busy polling.\n\nThere are 4 available concurrency slots, meaning that up to 4 agents can be active at once, including you.\n\nFull-history forks (`fork_turns` omitted or `\"all\"`) inherit the parent model and reasoning effort and do not accept overrides. Only set `model` or `reasoning_effort` when explicitly requested by the user, applicable `AGENTS.md` instructions, or skill instructions; when doing so, set `fork_turns` to `\"none\"` or a positive integer string.\u003c/multi_agent_role\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a13c5b-9919-7e32-b226-9d86f5b932ed","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.role_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a13c57-6fc6-7d93-a6e4-729352fb610c"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cmulti_agent_mode\u003eAny earlier instruction enabling proactive multi-agent delegation no longer applies. Do not spawn sub-agents unless the user or applicable AGENTS.md/skill instructions explicitly ask for sub-agents, delegation, or parallel agent work.\u003c/multi_agent_mode\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a13c5b-9919-7e32-b226-9d9dd91f6dfc","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["multi_agent.mode_instructions"],"turn_id":"01a13c57-6fc6-7d93-a6e4-729352fb610c"},"role":"developer","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\u003cenvironment_context\u003e\n  \u003ccwd\u003e/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim\u003c/cwd\u003e\n  \u003cshell\u003ebash\u003c/shell\u003e\n  \u003ccurrent_date\u003e2026-10-14\u003c/current_date\u003e\n  \u003ctimezone\u003eAmerica/New_York\u003c/timezone\u003e\n  \u003cfilesystem\u003e\u003cworkspace_roots\u003e\u003croot\u003e/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim\u003c/root\u003e\u003c/workspace_roots\u003e\u003cpermission_profile type=\"managed\"\u003e\u003cfile_system type=\"restricted\"\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cspecial\u003e:root\u003c/special\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"write\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"write\"\u003e\u003cspecial\u003e:slash_tmp\u003c/special\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"write\"\u003e\u003cspecial\u003e:tmpdir\u003c/special\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/.git\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/.agents\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/.codex\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003centry access=\"read\"\u003e\u003cpath\u003e/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/.aws\u003c/path\u003e\u003c/entry\u003e\u003c/file_system\u003e\u003c/permission_profile\u003e\u003c/filesystem\u003e\n\u003c/environment_context\u003e","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a13c5b-9919-7e32-b226-9da62883a6d0","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["environments.environment_context"],"turn_id":"01a13c57-6fc6-7d93-a6e4-729352fb610c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Project D — Step 173: Implement policy-compliant expense calculations and filing deadlines.\n\nUse the exact recovered POL-2026.2 browser copy and the Step 167 policy gap audit.\n\nImplement only:\n\n    Expense calculation rules:\n\n    Require actual employee-paid expenses supported by matching receipt and settled merchant transaction.\n\n    Validate employee, trip, cost ID, currency and gross amount.\n\n    Treat personal purchases as zero entitlement.\n\n    Transport and conference costs have no category cap.\n\n    Lodging uses the applicable nightly cap; meals use the applicable daily cap.\n\n    Require positive integer documented units for capped expenses.\n\n    Resolve caps using destination, expense currency and employee-payment date.\n\n    Unknown categories, missing evidence, rates or caps must remain unresolved rather than becoming zero.\n\nApply Finance's exact payment-date EUR exchange rate; EUR rate is 1.\n\nRound each converted line to EUR cents using decimal ROUND_HALF_UP, then sum rounded lines.\n\nPreserve original expense and conversion evidence.\n\nFiling deadlines:\n\nCalculate the deadline as two calendar months after the trip end, inclusive, clamping nonexistent days to month end.\n\nAllow filing before travel when employee payment is established.\n\nUse submission dates rather than arrival/import dates.\n\nPreserve the original submission date for unchanged costs after correction.\n\nNewly added costs use their own first submission date.\n\nLate filing remains held pending an explicit Finance exception; do not invent one.\n\nRequirements:\n\nUse real retained source schemas and source-bound references.\n\nAdd tests for normal, missing-data and boundary cases, including August 31 to October 31, leap years, exactly-on-deadline filing, fractional units and half-cent FX rounding.\n\nDo not change Finance event admission, cancellation validation, approvals, closure gates or prior retained outputs.\n\nPreserve the original policy and interview.\n\nRun the complete test suite and report the results.\n\nDo not commit or push yet.\n\nStop after implementation and verification, reporting any policy ambiguity or missing source data.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a13c57-7704-7291-ab72-dd6efbc80ce2","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792013727.4922955,"turn_id":"01a13c57-6fc6-7d93-a6e4-729352fb610c"},"role":"user","type":"message"}],"replacement_history_metadata":[{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a13bd3-423a-7082-8f73-b169f3b37bba","role":"user","turn_id":"01a13bd3-3cec-7081-b847-b31e41528363"},"revision":"retained_01a13bd3-423a-7082-8f73-b18698ae74cc"},"user_input_order":0},{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a13bd7-4146-7772-a00f-d514bd3f3bd7","role":"user","turn_id":"01a13bd7-3aa0-7972-adeb-ce27fff74914"},"