n.py:588); [live_run.py:44](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/live_run.py:44). | [test_ordinary.py:181](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/tests/test_ordinary.py:181) checks unaffected claim closure; add malicious imported comment/receipt text and all-policy readiness reporting. |\n| [POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:27](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:27) | Cancellation actors, exact targets, initiation and strict times | **Critical defects** | Reducer admits structural confirmation before integration checks actors; wrong actor can remain confirmed in snapshot. It does not enforce no initiation/effective fields on request, full associated trip+permit target equality (trip-target projections also null the associated permit fields), strictly-later confirmation or effective==occurrence. Equal times and scheduled effective times pass synthetic probes. Blank commitment is not implemented as explicit no-commitment. [workflow.py:216](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/workflow.py:216); [workflow.py:247](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/workflow.py:247); [integration.py:371](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/integration.py:371); [integration.py:417](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/integration.py:417). | [test_revalidation.py:75](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/tests/test_revalidation.py:75) covers orphan/missing-effective/backward time but not equal time, scheduled/backdated effective, wrong actor or complete target tuples. |\n| [POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:29](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:29) | Arrival dependency recheck, conflicting redelivery and authority retirement | **Critical/missing lifecycle behavior** | Sorting by arrival batch then row causes a confirmation before its request in row/delivery order to remain unresolved even after the initiation is present. Conflicting IDs are 