{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T00:54:34.353Z","ordinal":3198,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad0244648c48190b0cd1bf0fbaef672","status":"completed","call_id":"call_e32d77093913460ebc8296b916f7183d","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '7,23p' tests/fixtures/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt; cat src/travel_claim/finance.py; sed -n '565,660p' src/travel_claim/integration.py; cat src/travel_claim/approvals.py\",\"max_output_tokens\":11000}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\".venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\\nimport json\\nfrom travel_claim.ordinary import fields\\np=json.load(open('artifacts/runs/project-d-live-20261014T204849Z/parsed-records.json'))\\nfor tab in ('Budget','Finance activity'):\\n s=next(s for s in p['workbook_sheets'] if s['name']==tab); print(tab,s['headers'],len(s['records']))\\n for r in s['records'][:8]:print(r['locator'],fields(r))\\nfor r in p['records']['claim_revisions']:\\n if fields(r).get('Claim reference') in {'C03','C24'}:print(r['locator'],r['text'])\\nPY\\nrg -n -i 'budget|prepaid|commitment' artifacts/verification/project-d-step167-policy-gap-audit.md\",\"max_output_tokens\":4500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a13d0d-9f67-7c00-8955-722676671362","create_time":1792025670.2903183}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T00:54:34.565Z","ordinal":3199,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a13bd1-7420-72c0-963e-58742d1be7bf","turn_id":"01a13d0d-9f67-7c00-8955-722676671362","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ab9a3e51-d467-44b3-9e15-744c5146533c","process_id":"26942","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","sed -n '7,23p' tests/fixtures/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt; cat src/travel_claim/finance.py; sed -n '565,660p' src/travel_claim/integration.py; cat src/travel_claim/approvals.py"],"cwd":"file:///home/maxg/travel-expense-claim","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '7,23p' tests/fixtures/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt","name":"POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt","path":"tests/fixtures/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat src/travel_claim/finance.py","name":"finance.py","path":"src/travel_claim/finance.py"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '565,660p' src/travel_claim/integration.py","name":"integration.py","path":"src/travel_claim/integration.py"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat src/travel_claim/approvals.py","name":"approvals.py","path":"src/travel_claim/approvals.py"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"Transport and conference have no category cap. Lodging uses the supplied cap per night; meals use the supplied cap per day. For each line, allowed original amount = min(supported gross amount, applicable cap × documented units); transport/conference use supported gross amount. Caps are in the expense currency for the destination and employee-payment date. Units are positive integers. No per diem or automatic allowance is payable. Apply Finance's exact payment-date EUR-per-currency-unit rate; EUR uses 1. Round each converted line to EUR cents using decimal half-up; sum rounded line amounts. Finance can issue an explicit, version-bound exception with a replacement allowed amount and reason; neither the employee nor automation invents one. Each supplied exception states actor, claim/revision, cost, replacement allowed original amount, reason and `covered_issues`. That list may explicitly resolve `late_filing`, `late_permit`, `permit_unapproved` or `travel_cancellation` for reimbursement eligibility only; an amount-only exception uses an empty list. Retain the original finding and exception reference. No exception makes an unpaid cost paid or retroactively approves arrangements.\n\nDomestic trips do not need a permit. An international trip needs its own approved permit before the first arrangement/payment commitment. Permit administration, budget owner and supervisor review the trip estimate. Claim administration, budget owner and supervisor separately review actual reimbursement. A director additionally reviews amounts strictly above EUR 1,000.00 (reviewed estimate for permit, reviewed entitlement for claim). Exactly EUR 1,000.00 does not require a director. When budget owner and supervisor are the same stable person, one response with both roles satisfies those two positions for that subject/version. Administration and director never collapse into another role. A permit response never approves a claim. A late permit does not retroactively authorize travel arrangements; Finance may explicitly resolve reimbursement eligibility while the permit exception remains recorded.\n\nCosts may be claimed as soon as the employee has paid, including before travel. The latest ordinary filing date is two calendar months after trip end, inclusive, with a nonexistent day clamped to month end. For a trip ending 31 August, the deadline is 31 October. Earlier filing is allowed after payment. A later filing requires a Finance exception or remains held. The claim's submission date, not import time, is used. Corrections retain the initial submission date for unchanged costs; newly added costs use their own first submission date.\n\nAdministration checks identity, receipt/paid proof, trip/permit, category, deadline, rates/caps, prior cost obligations and calculated amount. Budget review receives the whole department/project/period ledger: allocation less net settled expenditure less remaining commitments. A commitment includes its settled portion; do not subtract the full commitment and its settled portion again. Include prior obligations outside the current batch and all accepted new requests. Adequate funds alone are not a budget approval. Supervisor considers business purpose, client commitment, schedule coverage and permit consistency. Director considers high spend, the documented exception, alternatives and budget-owner position. Reviewers may approve, return with a concrete repair request, or reject with a reason; their discretionary judgment is supplied by the scenario, not performed by the learner.\n\nRequests and replies identify subject type, subject ID/revision, role(s), stable actor, relevant source versions and reason. Consume only the trainer-supplied decision batches and the directory's applicable actor/roles. Missing responses for otherwise complete requests wait; missing policy/input definitions are package defects. Reject wrong-role, stale-version or wrong-subject replies for current authorization. Keep rejected imports visible. A return reopens the appropriate review; explicit rejection or clean withdrawal can close with a non-payment reason.\n\nA material change to employee, trip, dates, money, policy/evidence or authority invalidates dependent review, approvals and payment readiness even if the total is unchanged. Full recheck and justified dependency recheck are both valid. Preserve old versions and decisions as history. Before dispatch, rebuild readiness from current facts. After dispatch, hold replacement requests until Finance confirms cancellation/status. Pending cancellation is not confirmed cancellation. Withdrawal never erases an actual payment.\n\nA payment request is a proposal to Finance, not a transfer. Use a stable request ID for the same obligation; replay cannot create another request or reimbursement of a previously committed/settled cost. A later final claim may contain a previously prepaid cost; link and exclude that settled obligation, showing the remaining entitlement rather than paying it twice. Legitimate adjustments link the original claim/cost/request and preserve its transfers.\n\nOnly supplied Finance outcomes establish pending, failed, settled, cancellation, refund and resolution facts. Failed attempts do not change paid amount; a new attempt requires Finance authorization. An immutable event ID identifies one payload across all batches/versions: exact replay has no extra effect, conflicting replay holds the case without erasing admitted money. Validate request, payee, currency, positive integer cents, time and actor before admission. Unmatched/invalid events remain visible for Finance resolution. A confirmed refund must name a prior settled transfer and cannot exceed its unrecovered amount. Refund promises/requests do not change paid amount.\n\nNet paid = admitted confirmed transfers minus linked confirmed refunds. Current balance = current authorized obligation minus net paid; a negative balance is an overpayment requiring Finance resolution. Partial settlement stays pending. Cancellation or a previously closed state never stops observation: a later transfer reopens reconciliation. A correction or cancellation that occurs after Finance has accepted or dispatched the affected reimbursement request requires explicit Finance resolution before closure. A post-payment adjustment also requires that resolution, even if net paid happens to match. Close reimbursed only when current approvals, obligation, net paid and all required resolutions agree and no issue remains. Zero entitlement, rejection and clean withdrawal close with an explicit non-payment reason and no unresolved financial effect.\n\"\"\"Source-traceable Finance reconciliation primitives.\n\nOnly explicit, source-classified settled and refund events affect confirmed\ncash. Finance obligations remain separate from caller-supplied authorized\nobligations. No policy entitlement or approval decision is made here.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom .event_validation import finance_errors, utc_time\nfrom typing import Any\n\n\n_NATIVE_EVENT_CLASSES = {\n    \"accepted\": \"obligation_accepted\",\n    \"settled\": \"confirmed_payment\",\n    \"refund\": \"confirmed_refund\",\n    \"failed\": \"failed_transfer\",\n    \"retry_authorized\": \"retry_authorization\",\n    \"cancellation_requested\": \"finance_cancellation_requested\",\n    \"cancelled\": \"finance_cancelled\",\n    # These are retained as non-cash Finance records; their amount describes\n    # an obligation, not a payment.\n    \"adjustment\": \"finance_adjustment\",\n    \"resolution\": \"finance_resolution\",\n}\n\n\ndef _values(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: cell.get(\"value\") for key, cell in record.get(\"values\", {}).items()}\n\n\ndef _source_ref(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: record.get(key) for key in (\"source_id\", \"source_sha256\", \"locator\")}\n\n\ndef _cents(value: Any) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"Convert exact EUR decimal input to integer cents; reject rounding.\"\"\"\n    if value is None or isinstance(value, bool):\n        return None\n    try:\n        amount = Decimal(str(value))\n    except (InvalidOperation, ValueError):\n        return None\n    if not amount.is_finite():\n        return None\n    scaled = amount * 100\n    if scaled != scaled.to_integral_value() or scaled < 0:\n        return None\n    return int(scaled)\n\n\ndef _payload(values: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: values[key] for key in sorted(values) if key != \"Arrival batch\"}\n\n\ndef _reference_text(ref: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    return f\"{ref.get('source_id')}@{ref.get('source_sha256')}#{ref.get('locator')}\"\n\n\ndef _positive_integer(value: Any) -> int | None:\n    try:\n        return int(value) if not isinstance(value, bool) and int(value) > 0 and float(value) == int(value) else None\n    except (ValueError, TypeError, OverflowError):\n        return None\n\n\ndef _recorded_obligations(history: list[dict], *, claim_id: str, current_revision: int,\n                          revisions: list[dict]) -> tuple[list[dict], dict | None, str | None]:\n    \"\"\"Read ledger observations, without deriving reimbursement authorization.\n\n    Obligation (EUR) is a recorded amount, not a cash delta. Native rows omit\n    claim revision; arrival context is retained separately from explicit links.\n    Only the first delivery establishes context; redelivery cannot rebind it.\n    \"\"\"\n    groups: dict[str, list[dict]] = defaultdict(list)\n    for event in history:\n        if event['classification'] in {'obligation_accepted', 'finance_adjustment', 'finance_resolution'}:\n            groups[event['event_id']].append(event)\n    records = []\n    problem = None\n    for event_id, occurrences in groups.items():\n        event = occurrences[0]\n        values = event['source_record']\n        batches = [e['source_record'].get('Arrival batch') for e in occurrences]\n        first_batch = min((_positive_integer(b) for b in batches if _positive_integer(b)), default=None)\n        context_rows = [r for r in revisions if first_batch is not None\n                        and _positive_integer(r.get('arrival_batch')) is not None\n                        and _positive_integer(r['arrival_batch']) <= first_batch]\n        context = max((r['revision'] for r in context_rows), default=None)\n        explicit = _positive_integer(values.get('Claim revision'))\n        matches = [r for r in revisions if r['revision'] == explicit] if explicit else []\n        link = ('explicit_current' if explicit == current_revision else 'explicit_historical') if matches else 'arrival_context_only' if context else 'unmatched'\n        refs = [_reference_text(e['source_ref']) for e in occurrences]\n        record = {\n            'event_id': event_id, 'event_type': event['event_type'], 'claim_id': claim_id,\n            'request_id': values.get('Request reference'), 'finance_officer': values.get('Finance officer'),\n            'payee_id': values.get('Payee ID'), 'currency': event['currency'],\n            'amount_cents': event['obligation_cents'], 'activity_time_utc': values.get('Activity time (UTC)'),\n            'claim_revision': explicit if matches else None, 'arrival_revision_context': context,\n            'revision_link_status': link, 'first_arrival_batch': first_batch,\n            'delivery_batches': batches, 'source_refs': list(dict.fromkeys(refs)),\n            'claim_source_refs': [deepcopy(r['source_ref']) for r in (matches or context_rows)\n                                  if r['revision'] == (explicit if matches else context)],\n        }\n        records.append(record)\n        if (event['currency'] != 'EUR' or event['obligation_cents'] is None or not first_batch\n                or not all(isinstance(values.get(key), str) and values[key].strip()\n                           for key in ('Request reference', 'Finance officer', 'Payee ID'))\n                or not all(all(e['source_ref'].get(key) for key in ('source_id', 'source_sha256', 'locator')) for e in occurrences)\n                or (values.get('Claim revision') is not None and not matches)):\n            problem = 'Obligation record lacks supported amount, request/payee/officer, source identity, arrival, or explicit revision match'\n    if not records:\n        return [], None, None\n    if len({(r['request_id'], r['payee_id'], r['currency']) for r in records}) != 1:\n        problem = 'Multiple request/payee/currency ledgers cannot be combined as one obligation'\n    # A single observation needs no ordering assumption. Multiple observations\n    # require explicit UTC event times; arrival numbers do not define business time.\n    if len(records) > 1:\n        try:\n            def stamp(record):\n                dt = datetime.fromisoformat(record['activity_time_utc'].replace('Z', '+00:00'))\n                # The retained header explicitly names UTC even when the cell\n                # serialization omits an offset.\n                if dt.utcoffset() is not None and dt.utcoffset().total_seconds() != 0:\n                    raise ValueError('not UTC')\n                return dt.replace(tzinfo=None)\n            records.sort(key=lambda r: (stamp(r), r['event_id']))\n            for left, right in zip(records, records[1:]):\n                if stamp(left) == stamp(right) and left['amount_cents'] != right['amount_cents']:\n                    problem = 'Conflicting obligation amounts have the same event time'\n        except (ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):\n            problem = 'Multiple obligation observations lack unambiguous UTC ordering'\n    return records, deepcopy(records[-1]) if not problem else None, problem\n\n\ndef reconcile_finance_events(\n    events: list[dict[str, Any]],\n    *,\n    claim_id: str,\n    current_revision: int,\n    authorized_obligation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n    revision_history: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None,\n    previous_reconciliation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n    owner: str = \"Finance\",\n    source_classifications: dict[str, str] | None = None,\n    event_context: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Reconcile source events for a claim without making policy decisions.\n\n    `authorized_obligation` is an independent, already-authorized input of\n    `{amount_cents, claim_revision, source_refs}`. This function neither\n    derives nor authorizes it. `source_classifications` may extend the native\n    workbook vocabulary when a retained source defines another event type;\n    unrecognized types otherwise remain unresolved.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not claim_id or isinstance(current_revision, bool) or not isinstance(current_revision, int) or current_revision < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"claim_id and a positive current_revision are required\")\n    if not owner:\n        raise ValueError(\"owner is required for reconciliation issues\")\n    if (previous_reconciliation and 'admitted_events' not in previous_reconciliation\n            and any(previous_reconciliation.get(k) for k in ('confirmed_payment_event_ids', 'confirmed_refund_event_ids',\n                'confirmed_payment_cents', 'confirmed_refund_cents', 'net_confirmed_cents'))):\n        raise ValueError('Legacy admission state requires explicit verified migration; refusing to erase or invent admitted money')\n\n    classes = dict(_NATIVE_EVENT_CLASSES)\n    if source_classifications:\n        allowed_classes = {\n            \"confirmed_payment\", \"confirmed_refund\", \"pending_transfer\",\n            \"obligation_accepted\", \"failed_transfer\", \"retry_authorization\",\n            \"finance_cancellation_requested\", \"finance_cancelled\",\n            \"finance_adjustment\", \"finance_resolution\",\n        }\n        for event_type, classification in source_classifications.items():\n            if not isinstance(event_type, str) or classification not in allowed_classes:\n                raise ValueError(f\"unsupported source event classification: {event_type!r} -> {classification!r}\")\n            classes[event_type] = classification\n\n    # Accept full-history or delta calls without dropping earlier raw deliveries.\n    retained = [{**deepcopy(h['source_ref']), 'values': {k: {'value': v} for k, v in h['source_record'].items()}}\n                for h in (previous_reconciliation or {}).get('event_history', []) if isinstance(h.get('source_ref'), dict) and 'source_record' in h]\n    deliveries = []\n    for record in retained + events:\n        if not any(_source_ref(r) == _source_ref(record) and _values(r) == _values(record) for r in deliveries):\n            deliveries.append(record)\n    events = deliveries\n    by_id: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n    missing_id_records: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    for record in events:\n        event_id = _values(record).get(\"Activity reference\")\n        if not isinstance(event_id, str) or not event_id:\n            if _values(record).get(\"Claim reference\") == claim_id:\n                missing_id_records.append(record)\n        else:\n            by_id[event_id].append(record)\n\n    prior = deepcopy((previous_reconciliation or {}).get('admitted_events', {}))\n    admitted = deepcopy(prior)\n    history, duplicate_events, conflicting_events, unresolved = [], [], [], []\n    event_issue_by_id = {}\n\n    def item_for(record):\n        values = _values(record)\n        return {\"event_id\": values.get(\"Activity reference\"), \"source_ref\": _source_ref(record),\n                \"source_record\": deepcopy(values), \"event_type\": values.get(\"Activity type\"),\n                \"classification\": classes.get(values.get(\"Activity type\"), \"unresolved\"),\n                \"amount_cents\": _cents(values.get(\"Amount (EUR)\")),\n                \"obligation_cents\": _cents(values.get(\"Obligation (EUR)\")),\n                \"currency\": values.get(\"Currency\"), \"original_activity_id\": values.get(\"Original activity reference\")}\n\n    for event_id, occurrences in by_id.items():\n        relevant = [r for r in occurrences if _values(r).get('Claim reference') == claim_id]\n        if not relevant and event_id not in prior:\n            continue\n        payloads = [_payload(_values(r)) for r in occurrences]\n        if event_id in prior:\n            payloads.append(_payload(prior[event_id]['source_record']))\n        conflict = any(v != payloads[0] for v in payloads[1:])\n        if conflict:\n            conflicting_events.append({'event_id': event_id, 'source_refs': [_source_ref(r) for r in occurrences], 'payloads': payloads})\n            event_issue_by_id[event_id] = {\n                'record_id': f'finance-event-conflict:{event_id}', 'event_id': event_id,\n                'subject_type': 'claim', 'subject_id': claim_id, 'revision': current_revision,\n                'missing_or_return_reason': 'Conflicting immutable event replay; admitted history retained, new payload held',\n                'source_refs': [_source_ref(r) for r in occurrences], 'owner': owner,\n                'next_action': 'Finance to resolve the conflicting delivery without erasing admitted money'}\n        elif len(occurrences) > 1:\n            duplicate_events.append({'event_id': event_id, 'source_refs': [_source_ref(r) for r in occurrences],\n                                     'delivery_batches': [_values(r).get('Arrival batch') for r in occurrences]})\n        if event_id not in admitted:\n            batches = [_positive_integer(_values(r).get('Arrival batch')) for r in occurrences]\n            first_batch = min((v for v in batches if v is not None), default=None)\n            first = [r for r in occurrences if first_batch is not None and _positive_integer(_values(r).get('Arrival batch')) == first_batch]\n            if not first:\n                candidate = item_for(relevant[0])\n                candidate['validation_errors'] = ['missing or invalid positive integer arrival batch']\n                unresolved.append(candidate)\n            # Same-batch conflicting payloads have no supplied authority order.\n            if first and all(_payload(_values(r)) == _payload(_values(first[0])) for r in first):\n                candidate = item_for(first[0])\n                values = candidate['source_record']\n                reasons = finance_errors(values, candidate['classification'], event_context, _cents)\n                if candidate['classification'] == 'unresolved':\n                    reasons.append('unknown Finance event vocabulary')\n                if values.get('Claim reference') == claim_id and not reasons:\n                    candidate['validation_context'] = deepcopy(event_context)\n                    admitted[event_id] = candidate\n                elif values.get('Claim reference') == claim_id:\n                    candidate['validation_errors'] = reasons\n                    unresolved.append(candidate)\n        for record in relevant:\n            item = item_for(record)\n            canonical = admitted.get(event_id)\n            same = canonical is not None and _payload(item['source_record']) == _payload(canonical['source_record'])\n            item['admission_status'] = 'admitted-or-exact-replay' if same else 'held'\n            if not same:\n                item['classification'] = 'conflicting_event_id' if conflict else 'unresolved'\n            history.append(item)\n    for record in missing_id_records:\n        item = item_for(record); item['classification'] = 'missing_event_id'\n        item['validation_errors'] = ['immutable event identity missing']; history.append(item); unresolved.append(item)\n    # Previously admitted facts remain observable even on a delta-only invocation.\n    for event_id, item in prior.items():\n        if not any(h['event_id'] == event_id and _payload(h['source_record']) == _payload(item['source_record']) for h in history):\n            history.append(deepcopy(item))\n    typed = list(admitted.values())\n    payments = {item['event_id']: item for item in typed if item['classification'] == 'confirmed_payment'}\n    confirmed_refunds = [deepcopy(item) for item in prior.values() if item['classification'] == 'confirmed_refund']\n    recovered = defaultdict(int)\n    for item in confirmed_refunds:\n        recovered[item['original_activity_id']] += item['amount_cents']\n    refund_candidates = [item for item in typed if item['classification'] == 'confirmed_refund' and item['event_id'] not in prior]\n    refund_candidates.sort(key=lambda h: (_positive_integer(h['source_record'].get('Arrival batch')) or 0,\n                                         utc_time(h['source_record']['Activity time (UTC)']), h['event_id']))\n    for item in refund_candidates:\n        original = payments.get(item['original_activity_id'])\n        valid = original is not None and all(item['source_record'].get(k) == original['source_record'].get(k)\n                                             for k in ('Request reference', 'Payee ID', 'Currency', 'Claim reference'))\n        if valid:\n            valid = (utc_time(item['source_record']['Activity time (UTC)']) >= utc_time(original['source_record']['Activity time (UTC)'])\n                     and recovered[item['original_activity_id']] + item['amount_cents'] <= original['amount_cents'])\n        if not valid:\n            item['validation_errors'] = ['refund lacks matching settled request/payee/time or exceeds unrecovered transfer']\n            unresolved.append(item); admitted.pop(item['event_id'], None)\n        else:\n            confirmed_refunds.append(item); recovered[item['original_activity_id']] += item['amount_cents']\n    typed = list(admitted.values())\n    invalid_ids = {item['event_id'] for item in unresolved}\n    for item in history:\n        if item['event_id'] in invalid_ids and item['event_id'] not in admitted:\n            item['classification'] = 'unresolved'; item['admission_status'] = 'held'\n    invalid_payments = [item for item in payments.values() if item[\"amount_cents\"] is None]\n    unresolved.extend(invalid_payments)\n    confirmed_payment_cents = sum(item[\"amount_cents\"] for item in payments.values() if item[\"amount_cents\"] is not None)\n    confirmed_refund_cents = sum(item[\"amount_cents\"] for item in confirmed_refunds)\n    net_confirmed_cents = confirmed_payment_cents - confirmed_refund_cents\n\n    issues = list(event_issue_by_id.values())\n    for number, item in enumerate(unresolved, 1):\n        issue_id = f\"finance-unresolved:{item['event_id'] or number}\"\n        issue = {\n            \"record_id\": issue_id,\n            \"event_id\": item[\"event_id\"],\n            \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n            \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n            \"revision\": current_revision,\n            \"source_refs\": [item[\"source_ref\"]],\n            \"missing_or_return_reason\": (\n                f\"Finance event {item['event_id']!r} held: {', '.join(item.get('validation_errors', ['unmatched event']))}\"\n            ),\n            \"owner\": owner,\n            \"next_action\": \"Finance to confirm event meaning, amount, currency, or refund link from the native ledger\",\n        }\n        issues.append(issue)\n    obligation_history, recorded_obligation, recorded_problem = _recorded_obligations(\n        history, claim_id=claim_id, current_revision=current_revision, revisions=revision_history or [],\n    )\n    if recorded_problem:\n        issues.append({\n            \"record_id\": f\"finance-recorded-obligation:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n            \"subject_type\": \"claim\", \"subject_id\": claim_id, \"revision\": current_revision,\n            \"source_refs\": [e[\"source_ref\"] for e in history if e[\"event_id\"] in {r[\"event_id\"] for r in obligation_history}],\n            \"owner\": owner, \"missing_or_return_reason\": recorded_problem,\n            \"next_action\": \"Finance to confirm the obligation's request, amount, chronology and exact claim revision from retained source evidence\",\n        })\n    obligation = None\n    obligation_issue = None\n    if authorized_obligation is not None:\n        amount = authorized_obligation.get(\"amount_cents\")\n        obligation_revision = authorized_obligation.get(\"claim_revision\")\n        refs = authorized_obligation.get(\"source_refs\")\n        if (isinstance(amount, int) and not isinstance(amount, bool) and amount >= 0\n                and obligation_revision == current_revision and isinstance(refs, list)\n                and refs and all(isinstance(ref, str) and ref for ref in refs)):\n            obligation = {\"amount_cents\": amount, \"claim_revision\": obligation_revision, \"source_refs\": list(dict.fromkeys(refs))}\n        else:\n            obligation_issue = {\n                \"record_id\": f\"finance-obligation-invalid:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n                \"event_id\": None,\n                \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n                \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n                \"revision\": current_revision,\n                \"source_refs\": list(refs) if isinstance(refs, list) else [],\n                \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"authorized obligation is missing exact cents, current-revision match, or supporting source reference\",\n                \"owner\": owner,\n                \"next_action\": \"Finance to provide or confirm the authorized obligation for this claim revision\",\n            }\n    else:\n        obligation_issue = {\n            \"record_id\": f\"finance-obligation-missing:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n            \"event_id\": None,\n            \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n            \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n            \"revision\": current_revision,\n            \"source_refs\": [e[\"source_ref\"] for e in history if e[\"event_id\"] in {r[\"event_id\"] for r in obligation_history}],\n            \"missing_or_return_reason\": (\"recorded Finance obligation exists, but current-revision reimbursement authorization and entitlement remain unconfirmed\"\n                                         if recorded_obligation else \"no supported authorized obligation was supplied for this claim revision\"),\n            \"owner\": owner,\n            \"next_action\": \"Finance to provide or confirm the authorized obligation for this claim revision\",\n        }\n    if obligation_issue is not None:\n        issues.append(obligation_issue)\n\n    has_unclassified_cash_event = any(item[\"classification\"] == \"unresolved\" for item in history)\n    event_set_complete = not unresolved and not conflicting_events and not missing_id_records and not has_unclassified_cash_event\n    balance = None\n    if obligation is not None and event_set_complete:\n        balance = obligation[\"amount_cents\"] - net_confirmed_cents\n\n    ledger_balance = None\n    if recorded_obligation is not None and event_set_complete and not recorded_problem:\n        # Cash for a different/missing request cannot be silently applied to this ledger.\n        cash_rows = [e for e in history if e['classification'] in {'confirmed_payment', 'confirmed_refund'}]\n        if all(e['source_record'].get('Request reference') == recorded_obligation['request_id']\n               and e['source_record'].get('Payee ID') == recorded_obligation['payee_id'] for e in cash_rows):\n            ledger_balance = recorded_obligation['amount_cents'] - net_confirmed_cents\n    if recorded_obligation is not None and event_set_complete and ledger_balance is None:\n        issues.append({\n            \"record_id\": f\"finance-recorded-cash-link:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n            \"subject_type\": \"claim\", \"subject_id\": claim_id, \"revision\": current_revision,\n            \"source_refs\": [e[\"source_ref\"] for e in history if e['classification'] in {'confirmed_payment', 'confirmed_refund', 'obligation_accepted'}],\n            \"owner\": owner,\n            \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"Confirmed claim cash cannot be matched to the recorded obligation's request and payee\",\n            \"next_action\": \"Finance to verify each cash event's request and payee link before calculating a ledger difference\",\n        })\n    issues_by_owner = {}\n    for issue in issues:\n        issues_by_owner.setdefault(issue['owner'], []).append(issue)\n    issues_by_owner = {key: sorted(value, key=lambda row: row['record_id']) for key, value in sorted(issues_by_owner.items())}\n    invalidated = None\n    if previous_reconciliation is not None:\n        previous_revision = previous_reconciliation.get(\"claim_revision\")\n        if previous_revision != current_revision:\n            invalidated = {\n                \"claim_revision\": previous_revision,\n                \"reason\": \"material revision change invalidates the prior reconciliation basis\",\n                \"prior_net_confirmed_cents\": previous_reconciliation.get(\"net_confirmed_cents\"),\n                \"prior_balance_cents\": previous_reconciliation.get(\"balance_cents\"),\n                \"prior_recorded_obligation\": deepcopy(previous_reconciliation.get(\"recorded_obligation\")),\n                \"next_action\": \"Revalidate exact revision authorization; historical ledger and cash remain retained\",\n            }\n    revalidation_history = deepcopy((previous_reconciliation or {}).get(\"financial_revalidation_history\", []))\n    if invalidated is not None:\n        revalidation_history.append(deepcopy(invalidated))\n    return {\n        \"admitted_events\": deepcopy(admitted),\n        \"event_context\": deepcopy(event_context),\n        \"admitted_event_ids\": list(admitted),\n        \"claim_id\": claim_id,\n        \"claim_revision\": current_revision,\n        \"revision_history\": deepcopy(revision_history or []),\n        \"event_history\": history,\n        \"event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in history if item[\"event_id\"] is not None],\n        \"duplicate_events\": duplicate_events,\n        \"conflicting_events\": conflicting_events,\n        \"confirmed_payment_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in payments.values() if item[\"amount_cents\"] is not None],\n        \"confirmed_refund_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in confirmed_refunds],\n        \"pending_transfer_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in typed if item[\"classification\"] == \"pending_transfer\"],\n        \"unresolved_event_ids\": list(dict.fromkeys(item[\"event_id\"] for item in unresolved if item[\"event_id\"] is not None)),\n        \"finance_obligation_events\": [item for item in history if item[\"classification\"] == \"obligation_accepted\"],\n        \"recorded_obligation_history\": obligation_history,\n        \"recorded_obligation\": recorded_obligation,\n        \"recorded_ledger_balance_cents\": ledger_balance,\n        \"reimbursement_entitlement_confirmed\": False,\n        \"closure_authority_confirmed\": False,\n        \"authorized_obligation\": obligation,\n        \"confirmed_payment_cents\": confirmed_payment_cents,\n        \"confirmed_refund_cents\": confirmed_refund_cents,\n        \"net_confirmed_cents\": net_confirmed_cents,\n        \"balance_cents\": balance,\n        \"inputs_complete\": balance is not None,\n        \"repair_issues\": issues,\n        \"repair_issues_by_owner\": issues_by_owner,\n        \"invalidated_previous_reconciliation\": invalidated,\n        \"financial_revalidation_history\": revalidation_history,\n    }\n    if source_classifications:\n        domain[\"source_classifications\"].update(deepcopy(source_classifications))\n    previous_claim_revisions = {\n        subject_id: value[\"current_revision\"]\n        for subject_id, value in (domain.get(\"revision_history\") or {}).get(\"claim\", {}).items()\n    }\n    for name in (\"claim_revisions\", \"decisions\", \"finance_events\", \"cancellation_activities\"):\n        target_name = {\n            \"claim_revisions\": \"claim_records\", \"decisions\": \"decision_records\",\n            \"finance_events\": \"finance_records\", \"cancellation_activities\": \"cancellation_records\",\n        }[name]\n        domain[target_name].extend(deepcopy(delta[name]))\n    domain[\"processed_batches\"].append(arrival_batch)\n    domain[\"batch_input_hashes\"][str(arrival_batch)] = digest\n\n    history = build_revision_history({\n        \"records\": {\"claim_revisions\": domain[\"claim_records\"], \"trips\": parsed.get(\"records\", {}).get(\"trips\", [])}\n    })\n    domain[\"revision_history\"] = history\n    domain[\"decision_history\"] = match_decisions_to_subjects(domain[\"decision_records\"], history)\n    for decision, raw in zip(domain[\"decision_history\"], domain[\"decision_records\"]):\n        decision[\"arrival_batch\"] = row_values(raw).get(\"Arrival batch\")\n        decision[\"applied\"] = False\n    _sync_decision_and_revision_issues(domain, history=history, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id)\n    _material_correction_tasks(\n        domain, history=history, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n        previous_revisions=previous_claim_revisions,\n    )\n\n    current_claims = {}\n    for claim_id, record_set in history.get(\"claim\", {}).items():\n        current_revision = record_set[\"current_revision\"]\n        claim_revision = next(row for row in reversed(record_set[\"revisions\"]) if row[\"revision\"] == current_revision)\n        current_claims[claim_id] = claim_revision\n    cancellation_rows = _cancellation_rows(domain, history=history, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id, parsed=parsed)\n    from .approvals import evaluate_permit\n    domain['permit_approvals']={}\n    for permit_id,subject in history.get('permit',{}).items():\n        current=next(r for r in reversed(subject['revisions']) if r['revision']==subject['current_revision'])\n        key=f\"{permit_id}:r{current['revision']}\"\n        review=evaluate_permit(parsed=parsed,trip_record=current['record'],decisions=domain['decision_records'],\n            arrival_batch=arrival_batch,observations=source_observations or [],\n            prior=before_batch.get('permit_approvals',{}).get(key),cancellations=cancellation_rows)\n        domain['permit_approvals'][key]=review\n        if not review['approved'] or not review['arrangement_authorized']:\n            item_id=f\"permit-approval:{key}\"\n            _open_issue_for_subject(domain['repair_queue'],item_id=item_id,subject_type='permit',subject_id=permit_id,\n                revision=current['revision'],refs=review['source_refs'],reason=f\"Permit review state: {review['state']}; arrangement authority/timing requires current evidence\",\n                owner='Travel Administration Lead',next_action='Obtain current permit-role decisions and resolve timing or cancellation holds',run_id=run_id,batch_id=batch_id)\n        if f\"permit-approval:{key}\" in domain['repair_queue']['items']:\n            record_evidence_validation(domain['repair_queue'],item_id=f\"permit-approval:{key}\",\n                supported=review['approved'] and review['arrangement_authorized'],source_refs=review['source_refs'],run_id=run_id,batch_id=batch_id)\n    domain.setdefault('permit_approval_history',[]).append({'batch_id':batch_id,'permits':deepcopy(domain['permit_approvals'])})\n    finance_results = {}\n    for claim_id, claim_revision in current_claims.items():\n        record_set = history[\"claim\"][claim_id]\n        prior_finance = domain[\"finance_reconciliations\"].get(claim_id)\n        finance_results[claim_id] = reconcile_finance_events(\n            domain[\"finance_records\"], claim_id=claim_id,\n            current_revision=claim_revision[\"revision\"],\n            authorized_obligation=domain[\"authorized_obligations\"].get(claim_id),\n            revision_history=record_set[\"revisions\"],\n            previous_reconciliation=prior_finance,\n            source_classifications=domain[\"source_classifications\"],\n            event_context=finance_context(parsed, record_set[\"revisions\"], domain[\"finance_records\"], claim_id, arrival_batch),\n        )\n        workflow = connect_claim(parsed=parsed, claim=claim_revision, decisions=domain[\"decision_records\"],\n            finance_events=domain[\"finance_records\"], finance=finance_results[claim_id],\n            cancellations=cancellation_rows, arrival_batch=arrival_batch,\n            source_observations=source_observations or [], prior_finance=prior_finance,\n            source_classifications=domain[\"source_classifications\"],\n            prior_workflow=before_batch.get(\"ordinary_workflows\", {}).get(claim_id))\n        finance_results[claim_id] = workflow.pop(\"finance\")\n        domain[\"ordinary_workflows\"][claim_id] = workflow\n        domain[\"ordinary_workflow_history\"].append({\"batch_id\": batch_id, \"workflow\": deepcopy(workflow)})\n    domain[\"finance_reconciliations\"] = finance_results\n    record_executed_rechecks(domain, before_batch, batch_id=batch_id)\n    _sync_finance_repairs(domain, finance_results, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id)\n\n    # Policy and case-clock blockers are copied from parser/source evidence and\n    # deliberately remain outside any fabricated claim/decision outcome.\n    blockers = []\n    for row in parsed.get(\"unresolved_issues\", []):\n        blocker = {\n            \"record_id\": row[\"record_id\"],\n            \"reason\": row.get(\"reason\", \"Unresolved source issue\"),\n            \"owner\": row.get(\"owner\", \"Exercise facilitator\"),\n            \"resolution_needed\": row.get(\"next_action\", \"Obtain the missing authoritative evidence\"),\n            \"subject_type\": row.get(\"subject_type\"),\n            \"subject_id\": row.get(\"subject_id\"),\n            \"affected_scope\": row.get(\"affected_scope\"),\n            \"evidence_needed\": row.get(\"evidence_needed\"),\n        }\n        blockers.append(blocker)\n    domain[\"policy_clock_blockers\"] = blockers\n\n\"\"\"POL-2026.2 review authority and business transitions, without financial closure.\"\"\"\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport re\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo\n\nfrom .exceptions import source_bound\nfrom .expenses import policy_valid, local_date\nfrom .workflow import _revision, row_values\n\nROLES = {'administration': 'Administration reviewer', 'budget_owner': 'Budget owner',\n         'supervisor': 'Supervisor', 'director': 'Director'}\n\n\ndef fields(row):\n    return {f['label'].strip(): f['value'] for f in row.get('fields', [])} if 'fields' in row else row_values(row)\n\n\ndef ref(row):\n    return f\"{row.get('source_id')}@{row.get('source_sha256')}#{row.get('locator')}\"\n\n\ndef table(parsed, key, name):\n    return parsed.get('records', {}).get(key, next((s['records'] for s in parsed.get('workbook_sheets', []) if s['name'] == name), []))\n\n\ndef utc_time(value):\n    if not isinstance(value, str) or 'T' not in value:\n        raise ValueError('Missing decision UTC time')\n    stamp = datetime.fromisoformat(value.replace('Z', '+00:00'))\n    # Native workbook column explicitly specifies UTC.\n    return stamp.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc) if stamp.tzinfo is None else stamp.astimezone(timezone.utc)\n\n\ndef versions(row):\n    return set(re.findall(r'\\b(?:SRC-D-\\d+|POL-\\d{4}\\.\\d+)\\b', row.get('text', '')))\n\n\ndef evidence_digest(rows, amount):\n    \"\"\"Compare material facts, retaining source versions but ignoring arrival metadata.\"\"\"\n    content=[]\n    for row in rows:\n        value=fields(row)\n        content.append(dict(source_id=row.get('source_id'), sha256=row.get('source_sha256'),\n                            values={k:v for k,v in value.items() if k not in {'Arrival batch', 'Status', 'Claim reason'}}))\n    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(dict(rows=content, amount=amount), sort_keys=True, default=str).encode()).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef evaluate_reviews(*, parsed, kind, subject_id, revision, trip_record, employee,\n                     subject_record, amount_cents, decisions, arrival_batch, observations,\n                     cost_ids=(), prior=None, dependency_rows=(), withdrawn=False, cancellation_ids=()):\n    \"\"\"Evaluate supplied replies only. Invalid/stale imports stay in deliveries.\"\"\"\n    trip=fields(trip_record); policy=policy_valid(parsed.get('expense_policy'))\n    people=[r for r in table(parsed,'people','People') if fields(r).get('Employee ID')==employee]\n    person=fields(people[0]) if len(people)==1 else {}\n    packets=table(parsed,'review_packets','Review packets')\n    required=['administration','budget_owner','supervisor']\n    amount_known=isinstance(amount_cents,int) and not isinstance(amount_cents,bool) and amount_cents>=0\n    if amount_known and amount_cents>100000: required.append('director')\n    basis_rows=[subject_record,trip_record]+people+list(dependency_rows)\n    digest=evidence_digest(basis_rows,dict(amount_cents=amount_cents,cost_ids=sorted(cost_ids) if kind=='claim' else [],cancellation_ids=sorted(cancellation_ids)))\n    material_same_revision=bool(prior and prior.get('revision')==revision and\n        (prior.get('evidence_digest')!=digest or prior.get('material_same_revision')))\n    invalidated_batch=(prior.get('invalidated_batch') if prior and prior.get('material_same_revision') and prior.get('revision')==revision else arrival_batch) if material_same_revision else None\n    deliveries=[]; identities={}; conflicts=set()\n    budget_ids={fields(r).get('Ledger reference') for r in table(parsed,'budget','Budget')}\n    for decision in decisions:\n        dv=fields(decision); identity=dv.get('Decision reference')\n        ps=[p for p in packets if fields(p).get('Decision reference')==identity]\n        relevant=(dv.get('Subject reference')==subject_id or any(fields(p).get('Trip reference')==trip.get('Trip reference')\n                  and fields(p).get('Employee ID')==employee for p in ps))\n        if not relevant: continue\n        item=dict(decision_id=identity, outcome=dv.get('Outcome'), roles=str(dv.get('Review roles') or '').splitlines(),\n                  reason=dv.get('Reason'), repair_requested=dv.get('Repair requested'), evidence_valid=False,\n                  active=False, import_status='rejected-import', source_refs=[ref(decision)]+[ref(p) for p in ps],\n                  raw_record=deepcopy(decision), rejection_reasons=[])\n        deliveries.append(item)\n        try:\n            batch=_revision(dv.get('Arrival batch'))\n            if batch is None or batch>arrival_batch: raise ValueError('Reply outside consumed arrival batches')\n            if not subject_id or _revision(revision) is None or not source_bound(subject_record,observations) or not source_bound(trip_record,observations):\n                raise ValueError('Missing verified subject/trip identity or revision')\n            if dv.get('Subject type')!=kind or dv.get('Subject reference')!=subject_id or _revision(dv.get('Revision'))!=revision:\n                raise ValueError('Wrong or stale subject type/ID/revision')\n            if not identity or not source_bound(decision,observations): raise ValueError('Missing decision identity/source binding')\n            if len(people)!=1 or not source_bound(people[0],observations): raise ValueError('Missing verified directory authority')\n            roles=item['roles']\n            if not roles or len(set(roles))!=len(roles) or not set(roles)<=set(ROLES): raise ValueError('Unknown or repeated role')\n            if len(roles)>1 and not (set(roles)=={'budget_owner','supervisor'} and person.get('Budget owner')==person.get('Supervisor')):\n                raise ValueError('Only directory-identical budget owner/supervisor may combine explicit roles')\n            if any(not person.get(ROLES[r]) or dv.get('Reviewer')!=person[ROLES[r]] or dv.get('Reviewer')==employee for r in roles):\n                raise ValueError('Wrong-role, self-review or unauthorized stable actor')\n            if not isinstance(dv.get('Reason'),str) or not dv['Reason'].strip(): raise ValueError('Missing review reason')\n            if item['outcome'] not in {'approve','return','reject'}: raise ValueError('Unknown decision outcome')\n            if item['outcome']=='return' and (not isinstance(dv.get('Repair requested'),str) or not dv['Repair requested'].strip()):\n                raise ValueError('Return requires a concrete repair request')\n            if len(ps)!=1 or not source_bound(ps[0],observations): raise ValueError('Missing, conflicting or unbound review packet')\n            pv=fields(ps[0]); supplied=str(dv.get('Source revisions') or '').splitlines()\n            policy_versions={v for v in supplied if v.startswith('POL-')}\n            if not supplied or pv.get('Policy revision')!='POL-2026.2' or policy_versions!={'POL-2026.2'}:\n                raise ValueError('Missing/stale policy source version')\n            exact=ref(subject_record) in supplied or subject_record.get('source_sha256') in supplied\n            printed=versions(subject_record)\n            declared={v for v in supplied if v.startswith('SRC-D-')}\n            if printed and declared-printed:\n                raise ValueError('Reply contains a stale printed source version')\n            if material_same_revision and batch<invalidated_batch:\n                raise ValueError('Reply predates material evidence revalidation')\n            if not exact and (material_same_revision or not printed.intersection(supplied)):\n                raise ValueError('Reply does not bind current subject source version')\n            if (pv.get('Employee ID')!=employee or pv.get('Trip reference')!=trip.get('Trip reference')\n                    or _revision(pv.get('Trip revision'))!=_revision(trip.get('Trip revision'))\n                    or any(pv.get(k)!=trip.get(k) for k in ('Business purpose','Client','Schedule coverage','Alternatives considered','Permit reference','Permit revision'))):\n                raise ValueError('Packet does not match current trip/permit evidence')\n            if kind=='claim' and set(str(pv.get('Expense references') or '').splitlines())!=set(cost_ids):\n                raise ValueError('Packet expense list does not match review subject')\n            if kind=='permit':\n                from .finance import _cents\n                if not amount_known or _cents(pv.get('Reviewed estimate (EUR)'))!=amount_cents:\n                    raise ValueError('Missing/mismatched reviewed permit estimate')\n            if not set(cancellation_ids)<=set(str(pv.get('Travel cancellation references') or '').splitlines()):\n                raise ValueError('Packet lacks current cancellation context')\n            budget_refs=set(str(pv.get('Budget record references') or '').splitlines())\n            if not budget_refs or not budget_refs<=budget_ids: raise ValueError('Missing referenced budget records; no budget decision inferred')\n            stamp=utc_time(dv.get('Decision time (UTC)'))\n            payload={k:v for k,v in dv.items() if k!='Arrival batch'}\n            if identity in identities and identities[identity][0]!=payload:\n                conflicts.add(identity)\n            elif identity not in identities: identities[identity]=(payload,item)\n            else:\n                item.update(import_status='exact-replay',replayed_decision_id=identity)\n                continue\n            item.update(evidence_valid=True,import_status='valid',order=stamp.isoformat(),decision_time=stamp.isoformat())\n        except (ValueError,TypeError,InvalidOperation) as exc:\n            item['rejection_reasons'].append(str(exc))\n    # Conflicting redelivery must hold an identity even when its later payload fails validation.\n    all_payloads={}\n    for item in deliveries:\n        dv=fields(item['raw_record']); identity=item['decision_id']\n        if (identity and dv.get('Subject reference')==subject_id and _revision(dv.get('Revision'))==revision\n                and _revision(dv.get('Arrival batch')) is not None and _revision(dv.get('Arrival batch'))<=arrival_batch):\n            payload={k:v for k,v in dv.items() if k!='Arrival batch'}\n            if identity in all_payloads and all_payloads[identity]!=payload: conflicts.add(identity)\n            all_payloads[identity]=payload\n    for item in deliveries:\n        if item['decision_id'] in conflicts:\n            item.update(evidence_valid=False,import_status='conflicting-replay')\n            item['rejection_reasons'].append('Immutable decision identity has conflicting deliveries')\n    role_states={}; selected=[]\n    for role in required:\n        candidates=[d for d in deliveries if d['evidence_valid'] and role in d['roles']]\n        if not candidates: role_states[role]='missing'; continue\n        latest=max(d['order'] for d in candidates)\n        matches=[d for d in candidates if d['order']==latest]\n        if len(matches)!=1:\n            role_states[role]='conflicting';continue\n        chosen=matches[0];chosen['active']=True;role_states[role]=chosen['outcome']\n        if chosen not in selected: selected.append(chosen)\n    withdrawal_valid=bool(withdrawn and source_bound(subject_record,observations) and source_bound(trip_record,observations)\n        and trip.get('Employee ID')==employee and len(people)==1 and source_bound(people[0],observations)\n        and isinstance(fields(subject_record).get('Claim reason'),str) and fields(subject_record)['Claim reason'].strip())\n    states=set(role_states.values())\n    state=('withdrawn' if withdrawal_valid else 'rejected' if 'reject' in states else 'returned' if 'return' in states\n           else 'approved' if states=={'approve'} and policy and amount_known else 'pending')\n    if not policy or conflicts and not withdrawal_valid: state='pending'\n    policy_binding=parsed.get('expense_policy') or {}\n    policy_refs=[f\"{policy_binding.get('path')}@{policy_binding.get('sha256')}#line {n}\" for n in (9,13,15,17)] if policy else []\n    return dict(policy_source_refs=policy_refs,subject_type=kind,subject_id=subject_id,revision=revision,state=state,required_roles=required,\n                amount_cents=amount_cents,amount_known=amount_known,evidence_digest=digest,withdrawal_requested=withdrawn,withdrawal_valid=withdrawal_valid,\n                material_same_revision=material_same_revision,invalidated_batch=invalidated_batch,policy_verified=policy,role_states=role_states,\n                deliveries=deliveries,active_decision_ids=[d['decision_id'] for d in selected],\n                source_refs=list(dict.fromkeys([ref(r) for r in basis_rows]+[r for d in deliveries for r in d['source_refs']])),\n                approved=state=='approved',repair_requests=[d['repair_requested'] for d in selected if d['outcome']=='return'])\n\n\ndef evaluate_permit(*, parsed, trip_record, decisions, arrival_batch, observations, prior=None, cost_ids=(), cancellations=()):\n    trip=fields(trip_record)\n    if trip.get('International') is False:\n        affected=[c for c in cancellations if c.get('trip_id')==trip.get('Trip reference')\n            and _revision(c.get('trip_revision'))==_revision(trip.get('Trip revision'))]\n        return dict(subject_type='permit',subject_id=None,revision=None,state='not-required',approved=True,\n                    arrangement_authorized=policy_valid(parsed.get('expense_policy')) and not affected,\n                    arrangements_at_commitment_supported=policy_valid(parsed.get('expense_policy')),\n                    cancellation_ids=[c['cancellation_id'] for c in affected], source_refs=[ref(trip_record)],deliveries=[])\n    from .finance import _cents\n    subject=deepcopy(trip_record)\n    # Newly parsed workbooks retain the printed source version in their preamble.\n    subject['text']='\\n'.join(str(c.get('value','')) for s in parsed.get('workbook_sheets',[])\n        if s.get('source_id')==trip_record.get('source_id') for c in s.get('preamble',[]))\n    result=evaluate_reviews(parsed=parsed,kind='permit',subject_id=trip.get('Permit reference'),revision=_revision(trip.get('Permit revision')),\n        trip_record=trip_record,employee=trip.get('Employee ID'),subject_record=subject,amount_cents=_cents(trip.get('Estimate (EUR)')),\n        decisions=decisions,arrival_batch=arrival_batch,observations=observations,cost_ids=cost_ids,prior=prior)\n    result['arrangement_authorized']=False\n    if result['approved'] and trip.get('International') is True:\n        commitment=trip.get('First commitment date')\n        if commitment in (None,''):\n            result['arrangement_authorized']=True\n        else:\n            try:\n                day=local_date(commitment)\n                active=[d for d in result['deliveries'] if d['active']]\n                latest=max(utc_time(d['decision_time']) for d in active).astimezone(ZoneInfo('Europe/Amsterdam')).date()\n                result['arrangement_authorized']=latest<day\n                result['timing_finding']=None if latest<day else 'late_permit' if latest>day else 'same-day-order-unconfirmed'\n            except (ValueError,TypeError): result['timing_finding']='missing-commitment-evidence'\n    result['arrangements_at_commitment_supported']=result['arrangement_authorized']\n    affected=[c for c in cancellations if c.get('trip_id')==trip.get('Trip reference')\n        and _revision(c.get('trip_revision'))==_revision(trip.get('Trip revision'))\n        and (c.get('target_type')=='trip' or (c.get('permit_id')==trip.get('Permit reference')\n             and _revision(c.get('permit_revision'))==_revision(trip.get('Permit revision'))))]\n    result['cancellation_ids']=[c['cancellation_id'] for c in affected]\n    if affected: result['arrangement_authorized']=False\n    return result\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Transport and conference have no category cap. Lodging uses the supplied cap per night; meals use the supplied cap per day. For each line, allowed original amount = min(supported gross amount, applicable cap × documented units); transport/conference use supported gross amount. Caps are in the expense currency for the destination and employee-payment date. Units are positive integers. No per diem or automatic allowance is payable. Apply Finance's exact payment-date EUR-per-currency-unit rate; EUR uses 1. Round each converted line to EUR cents using decimal half-up; sum rounded line amounts. Finance can issue an explicit, version-bound exception with a replacement allowed amount and reason; neither the employee nor automation invents one. Each supplied exception states actor, claim/revision, cost, replacement allowed original amount, reason and `covered_issues`. That list may explicitly resolve `late_filing`, `late_permit`, `permit_unapproved` or `travel_cancellation` for reimbursement eligibility only; an amount-only exception uses an empty list. Retain the original finding and exception reference. No exception makes an unpaid cost paid or retroactively approves arrangements.\n\nDomestic trips do not need a permit. An international trip needs its own approved permit before the first arrangement/payment commitment. Permit administration, budget owner and supervisor review the trip estimate. Claim administration, budget owner and supervisor separately review actual reimbursement. A director additionally reviews amounts strictly above EUR 1,000.00 (reviewed estimate for permit, reviewed entitlement for claim). Exactly EUR 1,000.00 does not require a director. When budget owner and supervisor are the same stable person, one response with both roles satisfies those two positions for that subject/version. Administration and director never collapse into another role. A permit response never approves a claim. A late permit does not retroactively authorize travel arrangements; Finance may explicitly resolve reimbursement eligibility while the permit exception remains recorded.\n\nCosts may be claimed as soon as the employee has paid, including before travel. The latest ordinary filing date is two calendar months after trip end, inclusive, with a nonexistent day clamped to month end. For a trip ending 31 August, the deadline is 31 October. Earlier filing is allowed after payment. A later filing requires a Finance exception or remains held. The claim's submission date, not import time, is used. Corrections retain the initial submission date for unchanged costs; newly added costs use their own first submission date.\n\nAdministration checks identity, receipt/paid proof, trip/permit, category, deadline, rates/caps, prior cost obligations and calculated amount. Budget review receives the whole department/project/period ledger: allocation less net settled expenditure less remaining commitments. A commitment includes its settled portion; do not subtract the full commitment and its settled portion again. Include prior obligations outside the current batch and all accepted new requests. Adequate funds alone are not a budget approval. Supervisor considers business purpose, client commitment, schedule coverage and permit consistency. Director considers high spend, the documented exception, alternatives and budget-owner position. Reviewers may approve, return with a concrete repair request, or reject with a reason; their discretionary judgment is supplied by the scenario, not performed by the learner.\n\nRequests and replies identify subject type, subject ID/revision, role(s), stable actor, relevant source versions and reason. Consume only the trainer-supplied decision batches and the directory's applicable actor/roles. Missing responses for otherwise complete requests wait; missing policy/input definitions are package defects. Reject wrong-role, stale-version or wrong-subject replies for current authorization. Keep rejected imports visible. A return reopens the appropriate review; explicit rejection or clean withdrawal can close with a non-payment reason.\n\nA material change to employee, trip, dates, money, policy/evidence or authority invalidates dependent review, approvals and payment readiness even if the total is unchanged. Full recheck and justified dependency recheck are both valid. Preserve old versions and decisions as history. Before dispatch, rebuild readiness from current facts. After dispatch, hold replacement requests until Finance confirms cancellation/status. Pending cancellation is not confirmed cancellation. Withdrawal never erases an actual payment.\n\nA payment request is a proposal to Finance, not a transfer. Use a stable request ID for the same obligation; replay cannot create another request or reimbursement of a previously committed/settled cost. A later final claim may contain a previously prepaid cost; link and exclude that settled obligation, showing the remaining entitlement rather than paying it twice. Legitimate adjustments link the original claim/cost/request and preserve its transfers.\n\nOnly supplied Finance outcomes establish pending, failed, settled, cancellation, refund and resolution facts. Failed attempts do not change paid amount; a new attempt requires Finance authorization. An immutable event ID identifies one payload across all batches/versions: exact replay has no extra effect, conflicting replay holds the case without erasing admitted money. Validate request, payee, currency, positive integer cents, time and actor before admission. Unmatched/invalid events remain visible for Finance resolution. A confirmed refund must name a prior settled transfer and cannot exceed its unrecovered amount. Refund promises/requests do not change paid amount.\n\nNet paid = admitted confirmed transfers minus linked confirmed refunds. Current balance = current authorized obligation minus net paid; a negative balance is an overpayment requiring Finance resolution. Partial settlement stays pending. Cancellation or a previously closed state never stops observation: a later transfer reopens reconciliation. A correction or cancellation that occurs after Finance has accepted or dispatched the affected reimbursement request requires explicit Finance resolution before closure. A post-payment adjustment also requires that resolution, even if net paid happens to match. Close reimbursed only when current approvals, obligation, net paid and all required resolutions agree and no issue remains. Zero entitlement, rejection and clean withdrawal close with an explicit non-payment reason and no unresolved financial effect.\n\"\"\"Source-traceable Finance reconciliation primitives.\n\nOnly explicit, source-classified settled and refund events affect confirmed\ncash. Finance obligations remain separate from caller-supplied authorized\nobligations. No policy entitlement or approval decision is made here.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom .event_validation import finance_errors, utc_time\nfrom typing import Any\n\n\n_NATIVE_EVENT_CLASSES = {\n    \"accepted\": \"obligation_accepted\",\n    \"settled\": \"confirmed_payment\",\n    \"refund\": \"confirmed_refund\",\n    \"failed\": \"failed_transfer\",\n    \"retry_authorized\": \"retry_authorization\",\n    \"cancellation_requested\": \"finance_cancellation_requested\",\n    \"cancelled\": \"finance_cancelled\",\n    # These are retained as non-cash Finance records; their amount describes\n    # an obligation, not a payment.\n    \"adjustment\": \"finance_adjustment\",\n    \"resolution\": \"finance_resolution\",\n}\n\n\ndef _values(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: cell.get(\"value\") for key, cell in record.get(\"values\", {}).items()}\n\n\ndef _source_ref(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: record.get(key) for key in (\"source_id\", \"source_sha256\", \"locator\")}\n\n\ndef _cents(value: Any) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"Convert exact EUR decimal input to integer cents; reject rounding.\"\"\"\n    if value is None or isinstance(value, bool):\n        return None\n    try:\n        amount = Decimal(str(value))\n    except (InvalidOperation, ValueError):\n        return None\n    if not amount.is_finite():\n        return None\n    scaled = amount * 100\n    if scaled != scaled.to_integral_value() or scaled < 0:\n        return None\n    return int(scaled)\n\n\ndef _payload(values: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    return {key: values[key] for key in sorted(values) if key != \"Arrival batch\"}\n\n\ndef _reference_text(ref: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    return f\"{ref.get('source_id')}@{ref.get('source_sha256')}#{ref.get('locator')}\"\n\n\ndef _positive_integer(value: Any) -> int | None:\n    try:\n        return int(value) if not isinstance(value, bool) and int(value) > 0 and float(value) == int(value) else None\n    except (ValueError, TypeError, OverflowError):\n        return None\n\n\ndef _recorded_obligations(history: list[dict], *, claim_id: str, current_revision: int,\n                          revisions: list[dict]) -> tuple[list[dict], dict | None, str | None]:\n    \"\"\"Read ledger observations, without deriving reimbursement authorization.\n\n    Obligation (EUR) is a recorded amount, not a cash delta. Native rows omit\n    claim revision; arrival context is retained separately from explicit links.\n    Only the first delivery establishes context; redelivery cannot rebind it.\n    \"\"\"\n    groups: dict[str, list[dict]] = defaultdict(list)\n    for event in history:\n        if event['classification'] in {'obligation_accepted', 'finance_adjustment', 'finance_resolution'}:\n            groups[event['event_id']].append(event)\n    records = []\n    problem = None\n    for event_id, occurrences in groups.items():\n        event = occurrences[0]\n        values = event['source_record']\n        batches = [e['source_record'].get('Arrival batch') for e in occurrences]\n        first_batch = min((_positive_integer(b) for b in batches if _positive_integer(b)), default=None)\n        context_rows = [r for r in revisions if first_batch is not None\n                        and _positive_integer(r.get('arrival_batch')) is not None\n                        and _positive_integer(r['arrival_batch']) <= first_batch]\n        context = max((r['revision'] for r in context_rows), default=None)\n        explicit = _positive_integer(values.get('Claim revision'))\n        matches = [r for r in revisions if r['revision'] == explicit] if explicit else []\n        link = ('explicit_current' if explicit == current_revision else 'explicit_historical') if matches else 'arrival_context_only' if context else 'unmatched'\n        refs = [_reference_text(e['source_ref']) for e in occurrences]\n        record = {\n            'event_id': event_id, 'event_type': event['event_type'], 'claim_id': claim_id,\n            'request_id': values.get('Request reference'), 'finance_officer': values.get('Finance officer'),\n            'payee_id': values.get('Payee ID'), 'currency': event['currency'],\n            'amount_cents': event['obligation_cents'], 'activity_time_utc': values.get('Activity time (UTC)'),\n            'claim_revision': explicit if matches else None, 'arrival_revision_context': context,\n            'revision_link_status': link, 'first_arrival_batch': first_batch,\n            'delivery_batches': batches, 'source_refs': list(dict.fromkeys(refs)),\n            'claim_source_refs': [deepcopy(r['source_ref']) for r in (matches or context_rows)\n                                  if r['revision'] == (explicit if matches else context)],\n        }\n        records.append(record)\n        if (event['currency'] != 'EUR' or event['obligation_cents'] is None or not first_batch\n                or not all(isinstance(values.get(key), str) and values[key].strip()\n                           for key in ('Request reference', 'Finance officer', 'Payee ID'))\n                or not all(all(e['source_ref'].get(key) for key in ('source_id', 'source_sha256', 'locator')) for e in occurrences)\n                or (values.get('Claim revision') is not None and not matches)):\n            problem = 'Obligation record lacks supported amount, request/payee/officer, source identity, arrival, or explicit revision match'\n    if not records:\n        return [], None, None\n    if len({(r['request_id'], r['payee_id'], r['currency']) for r in records}) != 1:\n        problem = 'Multiple request/payee/currency ledgers cannot be combined as one obligation'\n    # A single observation needs no ordering assumption. Multiple observations\n    # require explicit UTC event times; arrival numbers do not define business time.\n    if len(records) > 1:\n        try:\n            def stamp(record):\n                dt = datetime.fromisoformat(record['activity_time_utc'].replace('Z', '+00:00'))\n                # The retained header explicitly names UTC even when the cell\n                # serialization omits an offset.\n                if dt.utcoffset() is not None and dt.utcoffset().total_seconds() != 0:\n                    raise ValueError('not UTC')\n                return dt.replace(tzinfo=None)\n            records.sort(key=lambda r: (stamp(r), r['event_id']))\n            for left, right in zip(records, records[1:]):\n                if stamp(left) == stamp(right) and left['amount_cents'] != right['amount_cents']:\n                    problem = 'Conflicting obligation amounts have the same event time'\n        except (ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):\n            problem = 'Multiple obligation observations lack unambiguous UTC ordering'\n    return records, deepcopy(records[-1]) if not problem else None, problem\n\n\ndef reconcile_finance_events(\n    events: list[dict[str, Any]],\n    *,\n    claim_id: str,\n    current_revision: int,\n    authorized_obligation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n    revision_history: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None,\n    previous_reconciliation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n    owner: str = \"Finance\",\n    source_classifications: dict[str, str] | None = None,\n    event_context: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Reconcile source events for a claim without making policy decisions.\n\n    `authorized_obligation` is an independent, already-authorized input of\n    `{amount_cents, claim_revision, source_refs}`. This function neither\n    derives nor authorizes it. `source_classifications` may extend the native\n    workbook vocabulary when a retained source defines another event type;\n    unrecognized types otherwise remain unresolved.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not claim_id or isinstance(current_revision, bool) or not isinstance(current_revision, int) or current_revision < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"claim_id and a positive current_revision are required\")\n    if not owner:\n        raise ValueError(\"owner is required for reconciliation issues\")\n    if (previous_reconciliation and 'admitted_events' not in previous_reconciliation\n            and any(previous_reconciliation.get(k) for k in ('confirmed_payment_event_ids', 'confirmed_refund_event_ids',\n                'confirmed_payment_cents', 'confirmed_refund_cents', 'net_confirmed_cents'))):\n        raise ValueError('Legacy admission state requires explicit verified migration; refusing to erase or invent admitted money')\n\n    classes = dict(_NATIVE_EVENT_CLASSES)\n    if source_classifications:\n        allowed_classes = {\n            \"confirmed_payment\", \"confirmed_refund\", \"pending_transfer\",\n            \"obligation_accepted\", \"failed_transfer\", \"retry_authorization\",\n            \"finance_cancellation_requested\", \"finance_cancelled\",\n            \"finance_adjustment\", \"finance_resolution\",\n        }\n        for event_type, classification in source_classifications.items():\n            if not isinstance(event_type, str) or classification not in allowed_classes:\n                raise ValueError(f\"unsupported source event classification: {event_type!r} -> {classification!r}\")\n            classes[event_type] = classification\n\n    # Accept full-history or delta calls without dropping earlier raw deliveries.\n    retained = [{**deepcopy(h['source_ref']), 'values': {k: {'value': v} for k, v in h['source_record'].items()}}\n                for h in (previous_reconciliation or {}).get('event_history', []) if isinstance(h.get('source_ref'), dict) and 'source_record' in h]\n    deliveries = []\n    for record in retained + events:\n        if not any(_source_ref(r) == _source_ref(record) and _values(r) == _values(record) for r in deliveries):\n            deliveries.append(record)\n    events = deliveries\n    by_id: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\n    missing_id_records: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    for record in events:\n        event_id = _values(record).get(\"Activity reference\")\n        if not isinstance(event_id, str) or not event_id:\n            if _values(record).get(\"Claim reference\") == claim_id:\n                missing_id_records.append(record)\n        else:\n            by_id[event_id].append(record)\n\n    prior = deepcopy((previous_reconciliation or {}).get('admitted_events', {}))\n    admitted = deepcopy(prior)\n    history, duplicate_events, conflicting_events, unresolved = [], [], [], []\n    event_issue_by_id = {}\n\n    def item_for(record):\n        values = _values(record)\n        return {\"event_id\": values.get(\"Activity reference\"), \"source_ref\": _source_ref(record),\n                \"source_record\": deepcopy(values), \"event_type\": values.get(\"Activity type\"),\n                \"classification\": classes.get(values.get(\"Activity type\"), \"unresolved\"),\n                \"amount_cents\": _cents(values.get(\"Amount (EUR)\")),\n                \"obligation_cents\": _cents(values.get(\"Obligation (EUR)\")),\n                \"currency\": values.get(\"Currency\"), \"original_activity_id\": values.get(\"Original activity reference\")}\n\n    for event_id, occurrences in by_id.items():\n        relevant = [r for r in occurrences if _values(r).get('Claim reference') == claim_id]\n        if not relevant and event_id not in prior:\n            continue\n        payloads = [_payload(_values(r)) for r in occurrences]\n        if event_id in prior:\n            payloads.append(_payload(prior[event_id]['source_record']))\n        conflict = any(v != payloads[0] for v in payloads[1:])\n        if conflict:\n            conflicting_events.append({'event_id': event_id, 'source_refs': [_source_ref(r) for r in occurrences], 'payloads': payloads})\n            event_issue_by_id[event_id] = {\n                'record_id': f'finance-event-conflict:{event_id}', 'event_id': event_id,\n                'subject_type': 'claim', 'subject_id': claim_id, 'revision': current_revision,\n                'missing_or_return_reason': 'Conflicting immutable event replay; admitted history retained, new payload held',\n                'source_refs': [_source_ref(r) for r in occurrences], 'owner': owner,\n                'next_action': 'Finance to resolve the conflicting delivery without erasing admitted money'}\n        elif len(occurrences) > 1:\n            duplicate_events.append({'event_id': event_id, 'source_refs': [_source_ref(r) for r in occurrences],\n                                     'delivery_batches': [_values(r).get('Arrival batch') for r in occurrences]})\n        if event_id not in admitted:\n            batches = [_positive_integer(_values(r).get('Arrival batch')) for r in occurrences]\n            first_batch = min((v for v in batches if v is not None), default=None)\n            first = [r for r in occurrences if first_batch is not None and _positive_integer(_values(r).get('Arrival batch')) == first_batch]\n            if not first:\n                candidate = item_for(relevant[0])\n                candidate['validation_errors'] = ['missing or invalid positive integer arrival batch']\n                unresolved.append(candidate)\n            # Same-batch conflicting payloads have no supplied authority order.\n            if first and all(_payload(_values(r)) == _payload(_values(first[0])) for r in first):\n                candidate = item_for(first[0])\n                values = candidate['source_record']\n                reasons = finance_errors(values, candidate['classification'], event_context, _cents)\n                if candidate['classification'] == 'unresolved':\n                    reasons.append('unknown Finance event vocabulary')\n                if values.get('Claim reference') == claim_id and not reasons:\n                    candidate['validation_context'] = deepcopy(event_context)\n                    admitted[event_id] = candidate\n                elif values.get('Claim reference') == claim_id:\n                    candidate['validation_errors'] = reasons\n                    unresolved.append(candidate)\n        for record in relevant:\n            item = item_for(record)\n            canonical = admitted.get(event_id)\n            same = canonical is not None and _payload(item['source_record']) == _payload(canonical['source_record'])\n            item['admission_status'] = 'admitted-or-exact-replay' if same else 'held'\n            if not same:\n                item['classification'] = 'conflicting_event_id' if conflict else 'unresolved'\n            history.append(item)\n    for record in missing_id_records:\n        item = item_for(record); item['classification'] = 'missing_event_id'\n        item['validation_errors'] = ['immutable event identity missing']; history.append(item); unresolved.append(item)\n    # Previously admitted facts remain observable even on a delta-only invocation.\n    for event_id, item in prior.items():\n        if not any(h['event_id'] == event_id and _payload(h['source_record']) == _payload(item['source_record']) for h in history):\n            history.append(deepcopy(item))\n    typed = list(admitted.values())\n    payments = {item['event_id']: item for item in typed if item['classification'] == 'confirmed_payment'}\n    confirmed_refunds = [deepcopy(item) for item in prior.values() if item['classification'] == 'confirmed_refund']\n    recovered = defaultdict(int)\n    for item in confirmed_refunds:\n        recovered[item['original_activity_id']] += item['amount_cents']\n    refund_candidates = [item for item in typed if item['classification'] == 'confirmed_refund' and item['event_id'] not in prior]\n    refund_candidates.sort(key=lambda h: (_positive_integer(h['source_record'].get('Arrival batch')) or 0,\n                                         utc_time(h['source_record']['Activity time (UTC)']), h['event_id']))\n    for item in refund_candidates:\n        original = payments.get(item['original_activity_id'])\n        valid = original is not None and all(item['source_record'].get(k) == original['source_record'].get(k)\n                                             for k in ('Request reference', 'Payee ID', 'Currency', 'Claim reference'))\n        if valid:\n            valid = (utc_time(item['source_record']['Activity time (UTC)']) >= utc_time(original['source_record']['Activity time (UTC)'])\n                     and recovered[item['original_activity_id']] + item['amount_cents'] <= original['amount_cents'])\n        if not valid:\n            item['validation_errors'] = ['refund lacks matching settled request/payee/time or exceeds unrecovered transfer']\n            unresolved.append(item); admitted.pop(item['event_id'], None)\n        else:\n            confirmed_refunds.append(item); recovered[item['original_activity_id']] += item['amount_cents']\n    typed = list(admitted.values())\n    invalid_ids = {item['event_id'] for item in unresolved}\n    for item in history:\n        if item['event_id'] in invalid_ids and item['event_id'] not in admitted:\n            item['classification'] = 'unresolved'; item['admission_status'] = 'held'\n    invalid_payments = [item for item in payments.values() if item[\"amount_cents\"] is None]\n    unresolved.extend(invalid_payments)\n    confirmed_payment_cents = sum(item[\"amount_cents\"] for item in payments.values() if item[\"amount_cents\"] is not None)\n    confirmed_refund_cents = sum(item[\"amount_cents\"] for item in confirmed_refunds)\n    net_confirmed_cents = confirmed_payment_cents - confirmed_refund_cents\n\n    issues = list(event_issue_by_id.values())\n    for number, item in enumerate(unresolved, 1):\n        issue_id = f\"finance-unresolved:{item['event_id'] or number}\"\n        issue = {\n            \"record_id\": issue_id,\n            \"event_id\": item[\"event_id\"],\n            \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n            \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n            \"revision\": current_revision,\n            \"source_refs\": [item[\"source_ref\"]],\n            \"missing_or_return_reason\": (\n                f\"Finance event {item['event_id']!r} held: {', '.join(item.get('validation_errors', ['unmatched event']))}\"\n            ),\n            \"owner\": owner,\n            \"next_action\": \"Finance to confirm event meaning, amount, currency, or refund link from the native ledger\",\n        }\n        issues.append(issue)\n    obligation_history, recorded_obligation, recorded_problem = _recorded_obligations(\n        history, claim_id=claim_id, current_revision=current_revision, revisions=revision_history or [],\n    )\n    if recorded_problem:\n        issues.append({\n            \"record_id\": f\"finance-recorded-obligation:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n            \"subject_type\": \"claim\", \"subject_id\": claim_id, \"revision\": current_revision,\n            \"source_refs\": [e[\"source_ref\"] for e in history if e[\"event_id\"] in {r[\"event_id\"] for r in obligation_history}],\n            \"owner\": owner, \"missing_or_return_reason\": recorded_problem,\n            \"next_action\": \"Finance to confirm the obligation's request, amount, chronology and exact claim revision from retained source evidence\",\n        })\n    obligation = None\n    obligation_issue = None\n    if authorized_obligation is not None:\n        amount = authorized_obligation.get(\"amount_cents\")\n        obligation_revision = authorized_obligation.get(\"claim_revision\")\n        refs = authorized_obligation.get(\"source_refs\")\n        if (isinstance(amount, int) and not isinstance(amount, bool) and amount >= 0\n                and obligation_revision == current_revision and isinstance(refs, list)\n                and refs and all(isinstance(ref, str) and ref for ref in refs)):\n            obligation = {\"amount_cents\": amount, \"claim_revision\": obligation_revision, \"source_refs\": list(dict.fromkeys(refs))}\n        else:\n            obligation_issue = {\n                \"record_id\": f\"finance-obligation-invalid:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n                \"event_id\": None,\n                \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n                \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n                \"revision\": current_revision,\n                \"source_refs\": list(refs) if isinstance(refs, list) else [],\n                \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"authorized obligation is missing exact cents, current-revision match, or supporting source reference\",\n                \"owner\": owner,\n                \"next_action\": \"Finance to provide or confirm the authorized obligation for this claim revision\",\n            }\n    else:\n        obligation_issue = {\n            \"record_id\": f\"finance-obligation-missing:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n            \"event_id\": None,\n            \"subject_type\": \"claim\",\n            \"subject_id\": claim_id,\n            \"revision\": current_revision,\n            \"source_refs\": [e[\"source_ref\"] for e in history if e[\"event_id\"] in {r[\"event_id\"] for r in obligation_history}],\n            \"missing_or_return_reason\": (\"recorded Finance obligation exists, but current-revision reimbursement authorization and entitlement remain unconfirmed\"\n                                         if recorded_obligation else \"no supported authorized obligation was supplied for this claim revision\"),\n            \"owner\": owner,\n            \"next_action\": \"Finance to provide or confirm the authorized obligation for this claim revision\",\n        }\n    if obligation_issue is not None:\n        issues.append(obligation_issue)\n\n    has_unclassified_cash_event = any(item[\"classification\"] == \"unresolved\" for item in history)\n    event_set_complete = not unresolved and not conflicting_events and not missing_id_records and not has_unclassified_cash_event\n    balance = None\n    if obligation is not None and event_set_complete:\n        balance = obligation[\"amount_cents\"] - net_confirmed_cents\n\n    ledger_balance = None\n    if recorded_obligation is not None and event_set_complete and not recorded_problem:\n        # Cash for a different/missing request cannot be silently applied to this ledger.\n        cash_rows = [e for e in history if e['classification'] in {'confirmed_payment', 'confirmed_refund'}]\n        if all(e['source_record'].get('Request reference') == recorded_obligation['request_id']\n               and e['source_record'].get('Payee ID') == recorded_obligation['payee_id'] for e in cash_rows):\n            ledger_balance = recorded_obligation['amount_cents'] - net_confirmed_cents\n    if recorded_obligation is not None and event_set_complete and ledger_balance is None:\n        issues.append({\n            \"record_id\": f\"finance-recorded-cash-link:{claim_id}:{current_revision}\",\n            \"subject_type\": \"claim\", \"subject_id\": claim_id, \"revision\": current_revision,\n            \"source_refs\": [e[\"source_ref\"] for e in history if e['classification'] in {'confirmed_payment', 'confirmed_refund', 'obligation_accepted'}],\n            \"owner\": owner,\n            \"missing_or_return_reason\": \"Confirmed claim cash cannot be matched to the recorded obligation's request and payee\",\n            \"next_action\": \"Finance to verify each cash event's request and payee link before calculating a ledger difference\",\n        })\n    issues_by_owner = {}\n    for issue in issues:\n        issues_by_owner.setdefault(issue['owner'], []).append(issue)\n    issues_by_owner = {key: sorted(value, key=lambda row: row['record_id']) for key, value in sorted(issues_by_owner.items())}\n    invalidated = None\n    if previous_reconciliation is not None:\n        previous_revision = previous_reconciliation.get(\"claim_revision\")\n        if previous_revision != current_revision:\n            invalidated = {\n                \"claim_revision\": previous_revision,\n                \"reason\": \"material revision change invalidates the prior reconciliation basis\",\n                \"prior_net_confirmed_cents\": previous_reconciliation.get(\"net_confirmed_cents\"),\n                \"prior_balance_cents\": previous_reconciliation.get(\"balance_cents\"),\n                \"prior_recorded_obligation\": deepcopy(previous_reconciliation.get(\"recorded_obligation\")),\n                \"next_action\": \"Revalidate exact revision authorization; historical ledger and cash remain retained\",\n            }\n    revalidation_history = deepcopy((previous_reconciliation or {}).get(\"financial_revalidation_history\", []))\n    if invalidated is not None:\n        revalidation_history.append(deepcopy(invalidated))\n    return {\n        \"admitted_events\": deepcopy(admitted),\n        \"event_context\": deepcopy(event_context),\n        \"admitted_event_ids\": list(admitted),\n        \"claim_id\": claim_id,\n        \"claim_revision\": current_revision,\n        \"revision_history\": deepcopy(revision_history or []),\n        \"event_history\": history,\n        \"event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in history if item[\"event_id\"] is not None],\n        \"duplicate_events\": duplicate_events,\n        \"conflicting_events\": conflicting_events,\n        \"confirmed_payment_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in payments.values() if item[\"amount_cents\"] is not None],\n        \"confirmed_refund_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in confirmed_refunds],\n        \"pending_transfer_event_ids\": [item[\"event_id\"] for item in typed if item[\"classification\"] == \"pending_transfer\"],\n        \"unresolved_event_ids\": list(dict.fromkeys(item[\"event_id\"] for item in unresolved if item[\"event_id\"] is not None)),\n        \"finance_obligation_events\": [item for item in history if item[\"classification\"] == \"obligation_accepted\"],\n        \"recorded_obligation_history\": obligation_history,\n        \"recorded_obligation\": recorded_obligation,\n        \"recorded_ledger_balance_cents\": ledger_balance,\n        \"reimbursement_entitlement_confirmed\": False,\n        \"closure_authority_confirmed\": False,\n        \"authorized_obligation\": obligation,\n        \"confirmed_payment_cents\": confirmed_payment_cents,\n        \"confirmed_refund_cents\": confirmed_refund_cents,\n        \"net_confirmed_cents\": net_confirmed_cents,\n        \"balance_cents\": balance,\n        \"inputs_complete\": balance is not None,\n        \"repair_issues\": issues,\n        \"repair_issues_by_owner\": issues_by_owner,\n        \"invalidated_previous_reconciliation\": invalidated,\n        \"financial_revalidation_history\": revalidation_history,\n    }\n    if source_classifications:\n        domain[\"source_classifications\"].update(deepcopy(source_classifications))\n    previous_claim_revisions = {\n        subject_id: value[\"current_revision\"]\n        for subject_id, value in (domain.get(\"revision_history\") or {}).get(\"claim\", {}).items()\n    }\n    for name in (\"claim_revisions\", \"decisions\", \"finance_events\", \"cancellation_activities\"):\n        target_name = {\n            \"claim_revisions\": \"claim_records\", \"decisions\": \"decision_records\",\n            \"finance_events\": \"finance_records\", \"cancellation_activities\": \"cancellation_records\",\n        }[name]\n        domain[target_name].extend(deepcopy(delta[name]))\n    domain[\"processed_batches\"].append(arrival_batch)\n    domain[\"batch_input_hashes\"][str(arrival_batch)] = digest\n\n    history = build_revision_history({\n        \"records\": {\"claim_revisions\": domain[\"claim_records\"], \"trips\": parsed.get(\"records\", {}).get(\"trips\", [])}\n    })\n    domain[\"revision_history\"] = history\n    domain[\"decision_history\"] = match_decisions_to_subjects(domain[\"decision_records\"], history)\n    for decision, raw in zip(domain[\"decision_history\"], domain[\"decision_records\"]):\n        decision[\"arrival_batch\"] = row_values(raw).get(\"Arrival batch\")\n        decision[\"applied\"] = False\n    _sync_decision_and_revision_issues(domain, history=history, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id)\n    _material_correction_tasks(\n        domain, history=history, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id,\n        previous_revisions=previous_claim_revisions,\n    )\n\n    current_claims = {}\n    for claim_id, record_set in history.get(\"claim\", {}).items():\n        current_revision = record_set[\"current_revision\"]\n        claim_revision = next(row for row in reversed(record_set[\"revisions\"]) if row[\"revision\"] == current_revision)\n        current_claims[claim_id] = claim_revision\n    cancellation_rows = _cancellation_rows(domain, history=history, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id, parsed=parsed)\n    from .approvals import evaluate_permit\n    domain['permit_approvals']={}\n    for permit_id,subject in history.get('permit',{}).items():\n        current=next(r for r in reversed(subject['revisions']) if r['revision']==subject['current_revision'])\n        key=f\"{permit_id}:r{current['revision']}\"\n        review=evaluate_permit(parsed=parsed,trip_record=current['record'],decisions=domain['decision_records'],\n            arrival_batch=arrival_batch,observations=source_observations or [],\n            prior=before_batch.get('permit_approvals',{}).get(key),cancellations=cancellation_rows)\n        domain['permit_approvals'][key]=review\n        if not review['approved'] or not review['arrangement_authorized']:\n            item_id=f\"permit-approval:{key}\"\n            _open_issue_for_subject(domain['repair_queue'],item_id=item_id,subject_type='permit',subject_id=permit_id,\n                revision=current['revision'],refs=review['source_refs'],reason=f\"Permit review state: {review['state']}; arrangement authority/timing requires current evidence\",\n                owner='Travel Administration Lead',next_action='Obtain current permit-role decisions and resolve timing or cancellation holds',run_id=run_id,batch_id=batch_id)\n        if f\"permit-approval:{key}\" in domain['repair_queue']['items']:\n            record_evidence_validation(domain['repair_queue'],item_id=f\"permit-approval:{key}\",\n                supported=review['approved'] and review['arrangement_authorized'],source_refs=review['source_refs'],run_id=run_id,batch_id=batch_id)\n    domain.setdefault('permit_approval_history',[]).append({'batch_id':batch_id,'permits':deepcopy(domain['permit_approvals'])})\n    finance_results = {}\n    for claim_id, claim_revision in current_claims.items():\n        record_set = history[\"claim\"][claim_id]\n        prior_finance = domain[\"finance_reconciliations\"].get(claim_id)\n        finance_results[claim_id] = reconcile_finance_events(\n            domain[\"finance_records\"], claim_id=claim_id,\n            current_revision=claim_revision[\"revision\"],\n            authorized_obligation=domain[\"authorized_obligations\"].get(claim_id),\n            revision_history=record_set[\"revisions\"],\n            previous_reconciliation=prior_finance,\n            source_classifications=domain[\"source_classifications\"],\n            event_context=finance_context(parsed, record_set[\"revisions\"], domain[\"finance_records\"], claim_id, arrival_batch),\n        )\n        workflow = connect_claim(parsed=parsed, claim=claim_revision, decisions=domain[\"decision_records\"],\n            finance_events=domain[\"finance_records\"], finance=finance_results[claim_id],\n            cancellations=cancellation_rows, arrival_batch=arrival_batch,\n            source_observations=source_observations or [], prior_finance=prior_finance,\n            source_classifications=domain[\"source_classifications\"],\n            prior_workflow=before_batch.get(\"ordinary_workflows\", {}).get(claim_id))\n        finance_results[claim_id] = workflow.pop(\"finance\")\n        domain[\"ordinary_workflows\"][claim_id] = workflow\n        domain[\"ordinary_workflow_history\"].append({\"batch_id\": batch_id, \"workflow\": deepcopy(workflow)})\n    domain[\"finance_reconciliations\"] = finance_results\n    record_executed_rechecks(domain, before_batch, batch_id=batch_id)\n    _sync_finance_repairs(domain, finance_results, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id)\n\n    # Policy and case-clock blockers are copied from parser/source evidence and\n    # deliberately remain outside any fabricated claim/decision outcome.\n    blockers = []\n    for row in parsed.get(\"unresolved_issues\", []):\n        blocker = {\n            \"record_id\": row[\"record_id\"],\n            \"reason\": row.get(\"reason\", \"Unresolved source issue\"),\n            \"owner\": row.get(\"owner\", \"Exercise facilitator\"),\n            \"resolution_needed\": row.get(\"next_action\", \"Obtain the missing authoritative evidence\"),\n            \"subject_type\": row.get(\"subject_type\"),\n            \"subject_id\": row.get(\"subject_id\"),\n            \"affected_scope\": row.get(\"affected_scope\"),\n            \"evidence_needed\": row.get(\"evidence_needed\"),\n        }\n        blockers.append(blocker)\n    domain[\"policy_clock_blockers\"] = blockers\n\n\"\"\"POL-2026.2 review authority and business transitions, without financial closure.\"\"\"\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport re\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo\n\nfrom .exceptions import source_bound\nfrom .expenses import policy_valid, local_date\nfrom .workflow import _revision, row_values\n\nROLES = {'administration': 'Administration reviewer', 'budget_owner': 'Budget owner',\n         'supervisor': 'Supervisor', 'director': 'Director'}\n\n\ndef fields(row):\n    return {f['label'].strip(): f['value'] for f in row.get('fields', [])} if 'fields' in row else row_values(row)\n\n\ndef ref(row):\n    return f\"{row.get('source_id')}@{row.get('source_sha256')}#{row.get('locator')}\"\n\n\ndef table(parsed, key, name):\n    return parsed.get('records', {}).get(key, next((s['records'] for s in parsed.get('workbook_sheets', []) if s['name'] == name), []))\n\n\ndef utc_time(value):\n    if not isinstance(value, str) or 'T' not in value:\n        raise ValueError('Missing decision UTC time')\n    stamp = datetime.fromisoformat(value.replace('Z', '+00:00'))\n    # Native workbook column explicitly specifies UTC.\n    return stamp.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc) if stamp.tzinfo is None else stamp.astimezone(timezone.utc)\n\n\ndef versions(row):\n    return set(re.findall(r'\\b(?:SRC-D-\\d+|POL-\\d{4}\\.\\d+)\\b', row.get('text', '')))\n\n\ndef evidence_digest(rows, amount):\n    \"\"\"Compare material facts, retaining source versions but ignoring arrival metadata.\"\"\"\n    content=[]\n    for row in rows:\n        value=fields(row)\n        content.append(dict(source_id=row.get('source_id'), sha256=row.get('source_sha256'),\n                            values={k:v for k,v in value.items() if k not in {'Arrival batch', 'Status', 'Claim reason'}}))\n    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(dict(rows=content, amount=amount), sort_keys=True, default=str).encode()).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef evaluate_reviews(*, parsed, kind, subject_id, revision, trip_record, employee,\n                     subject_record, amount_cents, decisions, arrival_batch, observations,\n                     cost_ids=(), prior=None, dependency_rows=(), withdrawn=False, cancellation_ids=()):\n    \"\"\"Evaluate supplied replies only. Invalid/stale imports stay in deliveries.\"\"\"\n    trip=fields(trip_record); policy=policy_valid(parsed.get('expense_policy'))\n    people=[r for r in table(parsed,'people','People') if fields(r).get('Employee ID')==employee]\n    person=fields(people[0]) if len(people)==1 else {}\n    packets=table(parsed,'review_packets','Review packets')\n    required=['administration','budget_owner','supervisor']\n    amount_known=isinstance(amount_cents,int) and not isinstance(amount_cents,bool) and amount_cents>=0\n    if amount_known and amount_cents>100000: required.append('director')\n    basis_rows=[subject_record,trip_record]+people+list(dependency_rows)\n    digest=evidence_digest(basis_rows,dict(amount_cents=amount_cents,cost_ids=sorted(cost_ids) if kind=='claim' else [],cancellation_ids=sorted(cancellation_ids)))\n    material_same_revision=bool(prior and prior.get('revision')==revision and\n        (prior.get('evidence_digest')!=digest or prior.get('material_same_revision')))\n    invalidated_batch=(prior.get('invalidated_batch') if prior and prior.get('material_same_revision') and prior.get('revision')==revision else arrival_batch) if material_same_revision else None\n    deliveries=[]; identities={}; conflicts=set()\n    budget_ids={fields(r).get('Ledger reference') for r in table(parsed,'budget','Budget')}\n    for decision in decisions:\n        dv=fields(decision); identity=dv.get('Decision reference')\n        ps=[p for p in packets if fields(p).get('Decision reference')==identity]\n        relevant=(dv.get('Subject reference')==subject_id or any(fields(p).get('Trip reference')==trip.get('Trip reference')\n                  and fields(p).get('Employee ID')==employee for p in ps))\n        if not relevant: continue\n        item=dict(decision_id=identity, outcome=dv.get('Outcome'), roles=str(dv.get('Review roles') or '').splitlines(),\n                  reason=dv.get('Reason'), repair_requested=dv.get('Repair requested'), evidence_valid=False,\n                  active=False, import_status='rejected-import', source_refs=[ref(decision)]+[ref(p) for p in ps],\n                  raw_record=deepcopy(decision), rejection_reasons=[])\n        deliveries.append(item)\n        try:\n            batch=_revision(dv.get('Arrival batch'))\n            if batch is None or batch>arrival_batch: raise ValueError('Reply outside consumed arrival batches')\n            if not subject_id or _revision(revision) is None or not source_bound(subject_record,observations) or not source_bound(trip_record,observations):\n                raise ValueError('Missing verified subject/trip identity or revision')\n            if dv.get('Subject type')!=kind or dv.get('Subject reference')!=subject_id or _revision(dv.get('Revision'))!=revision:\n                raise ValueError('Wrong or stale subject type/ID/revision')\n            if not identity or not source_bound(decision,observations): raise ValueError('Missing decision identity/source binding')\n            if len(people)!=1 or not source_bound(people[0],observations): raise ValueError('Missing verified directory authority')\n            roles=item['roles']\n            if not roles or len(set(roles))!=len(roles) or not set(roles)<=set(ROLES): raise ValueError('Unknown or repeated role')\n            if len(roles)>1 and not (set(roles)=={'budget_owner','supervisor'} and person.get('Budget owner')==person.get('Supervisor')):\n                raise ValueError('Only directory-identical budget owner/supervisor may combine explicit roles')\n            if any(not person.get(ROLES[r]) or dv.get('Reviewer')!=person[ROLES[r]] or dv.get('Reviewer')==employee for r in roles):\n                raise ValueError('Wrong-role, self-review or unauthorized stable actor')\n            if not isinstance(dv.get('Reason'),str) or not dv['Reason'].strip(): raise ValueError('Missing review reason')\n            if item['outcome'] not in {'approve','return','reject'}: raise ValueError('Unknown decision outcome')\n            if item['outcome']=='return' and (not isinstance(dv.get('Repair requested'),str) or not dv['Repair requested'].strip()):\n                raise ValueError('Return requires a concrete repair request')\n            if len(ps)!=1 or not source_bound(ps[0],observations): raise ValueError('Missing, conflicting or unbound review packet')\n            pv=fields(ps[0]); supplied=str(dv.get('Source revisions') or '').splitlines()\n            policy_versions={v for v in supplied if v.startswith('POL-')}\n            if not supplied or pv.get('Policy revision')!='POL-2026.2' or policy_versions!={'POL-2026.2'}:\n                raise ValueError('Missing/stale policy source version')\n            exact=ref(subject_record) in supplied or subject_record.get('source_sha256') in supplied\n            printed=versions(subject_record)\n            declared={v for v in supplied if v.startswith('SRC-D-')}\n            if printed and declared-printed:\n                raise ValueError('Reply contains a stale printed source version')\n            if material_same_revision and batch<invalidated_batch:\n                raise ValueError('Reply predates material evidence revalidation')\n            if not exact and (material_same_revision or not printed.intersection(supplied)):\n                raise ValueError('Reply does not bind current subject source version')\n            if (pv.get('Employee ID')!=employee or pv.get('Trip reference')!=trip.get('Trip reference')\n                    or _revision(pv.get('Trip revision'))!=_revision(trip.get('Trip revision'))\n                    or any(pv.get(k)!=trip.get(k) for k in ('Business purpose','Client','Schedule coverage','Alternatives considered','Permit reference','Permit revision'))):\n                raise ValueError('Packet does not match current trip/permit evidence')\n            if kind=='claim' and set(str(pv.get('Expense references') or '').splitlines())!=set(cost_ids):\n                raise ValueError('Packet expense list does not match review subject')\n            if kind=='permit':\n                from .finance import _cents\n                if not amount_known or _cents(pv.get('Reviewed estimate (EUR)'))!=amount_cents:\n                    raise ValueError('Missing/mismatched reviewed permit estimate')\n            if not set(cancellation_ids)<=set(str(pv.get('Travel cancellation references') or '').splitlines()):\n                raise ValueError('Packet lacks current cancellation context')\n            budget_refs=set(str(pv.get('Budget record references') or '').splitlines())\n            if not budget_refs or not budget_refs<=budget_ids: raise ValueError('Missing referenced budget records; no budget decision inferred')\n            stamp=utc_time(dv.get('Decision time (UTC)'))\n            payload={k:v for k,v in dv.items() if k!='Arrival batch'}\n            if identity in identities and identities[identity][0]!=payload:\n                conflicts.add(identity)\n            elif identity not in identities: identities[identity]=(payload,item)\n            else:\n                item.update(import_status='exact-replay',replayed_decision_id=identity)\n                continue\n            item.update(evidence_valid=True,import_status='valid',order=stamp.isoformat(),decision_time=stamp.isoformat())\n        except (ValueError,TypeError,InvalidOperation) as exc:\n            item['rejection_reasons'].append(str(exc))\n    # Conflicting redelivery must hold an identity even when its later payload fails validation.\n    all_payloads={}\n    for item in deliveries:\n        dv=fields(item['raw_record']); identity=item['decision_id']\n        if (identity and dv.get('Subject reference')==subject_id and _revision(dv.get('Revision'))==revision\n                and _revision(dv.get('Arrival batch')) is not None and _revision(dv.get('Arrival batch'))<=arrival_batch):\n            payload={k:v for k,v in dv.items() if k!='Arrival batch'}\n            if identity in all_payloads and all_payloads[identity]!=payload: conflicts.add(identity)\n            all_payloads[identity]=payload\n    for item in deliveries:\n        if item['decision_id'] in conflicts:\n            item.update(evidence_valid=False,import_status='conflicting-replay')\n            item['rejection_reasons'].append('Immutable decision identity has conflicting deliveries')\n    role_states={}; selected=[]\n    for role in required:\n        candidates=[d for d in deliveries if d['evidence_valid'] and role in d['roles']]\n        if not candidates: role_states[role]='missing'; continue\n        latest=max(d['order'] for d in candidates)\n        matches=[d for d in candidates if d['order']==latest]\n        if len(matches)!=1:\n            role_states[role]='conflicting';continue\n        chosen=matches[0];chosen['active']=True;role_states[role]=chosen['outcome']\n        if chosen not in selected: selected.append(chosen)\n    withdrawal_valid=bool(withdrawn and source_bound(subject_record,observations) and source_bound(trip_record,observations)\n        and trip.get('Employee ID')==employee and len(people)==1 and source_bound(people[0],observations)\n        and isinstance(fields(subject_record).get('Claim reason'),str) and fields(subject_record)['Claim reason'].strip())\n    states=set(role_states.values())\n    state=('withdrawn' if withdrawal_valid else 'rejected' if 'reject' in states else 'returned' if 'return' in states\n           else 'approved' if states=={'approve'} and policy and amount_known else 'pending')\n    if not policy or conflicts and not withdrawal_valid: state='pending'\n    policy_binding=parsed.get('expense_policy') or {}\n    policy_refs=[f\"{policy_binding.get('path')}@{policy_binding.get('sha256')}#line {n}\" for n in (9,13,15,17)] if policy else []\n    return dict(policy_source_refs=policy_refs,subject_type=kind,subject_id=subject_id,revision=revision,state=state,required_roles=required,\n                amount_cents=amount_cents,amount_known=amount_known,evidence_digest=digest,withdrawal_requested=withdrawn,withdrawal_valid=withdrawal_valid,\n                material_same_revision=material_same_revision,invalidated_batch=invalidated_batch,policy_verified=policy,role_states=role_states,\n                deliveries=deliveries,active_decision_ids=[d['decision_id'] for d in selected],\n                source_refs=list(dict.fromkeys([ref(r) for r in basis_rows]+[r for d in deliveries for r in d['source_refs']])),\n                approved=state=='approved',repair_requests=[d['repair_requested'] for d in selected if d['outcome']=='return'])\n\n\ndef evaluate_permit(*, parsed, trip_record, decisions, arrival_batch, observations, prior=None, cost_ids=(), cancellations=()):\n    trip=fields(trip_record)\n    if trip.get('International') is False:\n        affected=[c for c in cancellations if c.get('trip_id')==trip.get('Trip reference')\n            and _revision(c.get('trip_revision'))==_revision(trip.get('Trip revision'))]\n        return dict(subject_type='permit',subject_id=None,revision=None,state='not-required',approved=True,\n                    arrangement_authorized=policy_valid(parsed.get('expense_policy')) and not affected,\n                    arrangements_at_commitment_supported=policy_valid(parsed.get('expense_policy')),\n                    cancellation_ids=[c['cancellation_id'] for c in affected], source_refs=[ref(trip_record)],deliveries=[])\n    from .finance import _cents\n    subject=deepcopy(trip_record)\n    # Newly parsed workbooks retain the printed source version in their preamble.\n    subject['text']='\\n'.join(str(c.get('value','')) for s in parsed.get('workbook_sheets',[])\n        if s.get('source_id')==trip_record.get('source_id') for c in s.get('preamble',[]))\n    result=evaluate_reviews(parsed=parsed,kind='permit',subject_id=trip.get('Permit reference'),revision=_revision(trip.get('Permit revision')),\n        trip_record=trip_record,employee=trip.get('Employee ID'),subject_record=subject,amount_cents=_cents(trip.get('Estimate (EUR)')),\n        decisions=decisions,arrival_batch=arrival_batch,observations=observations,cost_ids=cost_ids,prior=prior)\n    result['arrangement_authorized']=False\n    if result['approved'] and trip.get('International') is True:\n        commitment=trip.get('First commitment date')\n        if commitment in (None,''):\n            result['arrangement_authorized']=True\n        else:\n            try:\n                day=local_date(commitment)\n                active=[d for d in result['deliveries'] if d['active']]\n                latest=max(utc_time(d['decision_time']) for d in active).astimezone(ZoneInfo('Europe/Amsterdam')).date()\n                result['arrangement_authorized']=latest<day\n                result['timing_finding']=None if latest<day else 'late_permit' if latest>day else 'same-day-order-unconfirmed'\n            except (ValueError,TypeError): result['timing_finding']='missing-commitment-evidence'\n    result['arrangements_at_commitment_supported']=result['arrangement_authorized']\n    affected=[c for c in cancellations if c.get('trip_id')==trip.get('Trip reference')\n        and _revision(c.get('trip_revision'))==_revision(trip.get('Trip revision'))\n        and (c.get('target_type')=='trip' or (c.get('permit_id')==trip.get('Permit reference')\n             and _revision(c.get('permit_revision'))==_revision(trip.get('Permit revision'))))]\n    result['cancellation_ids']=[c['cancellation_id'] for c in affected]\n    if affected: result['arrangement_authorized']=False\n    return result\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":32924320},"formatted_output":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 13666)\nTotal output lines: 769\n\nTransport and conference have no category cap. Lodging uses the supplied cap per night; meals use the supplied cap per day. For each line, allowed original amount = min(supported gross amount, applicable cap × documented units); transport/conference use supported gross amount. Caps are in the expense currency for the destination and employee-payment date. Units are positive integers. No per diem or automatic allowance is payable. Apply Finance's exact payment-date EUR-per-currency-unit rate; EUR uses 1. Round each converted line to