{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T00:54:36.030Z","ordinal":3202,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a13d0d-c8fd-7102-9756-6220429f32e8","call_id":"call_e32d77093913460ebc8296b916f7183d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 15021)\nTotal output lines: 2\n\n{\"chunk_id\":\"23ae20\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.03387945,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":13666,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 13666)\\nTotal output lines: 769\\n\\nTransport and conference have no category cap. Lodging uses the supplied cap per night; meals use the supplied cap per day. For each line, allowed original amount = min(supported gross amount, applicable cap × documented units); transport/conference use supported gross amount. Caps are in the expense currency for the destination and employee-payment date. Units are positive integers. No per diem or automatic allowance is payable. Apply Finance's exact payment-date EUR-per-currency-unit rate; EUR uses 1. Round each converted line to EUR cents using decimal half-up; sum rounded line amounts. Finance can issue an explicit, version-bound exception with a replacement allowed amount and reason; neither the employee nor automation invents one. Each supplied exception states actor, claim/revision, cost, replacement allowed original amount, reason and `covered_issues`. That list may explicitly resolve `late_filing`, `late_permit`, `permit_unapproved` or `travel_cancellation` for reimbursement eligibility only; an amount-only exception uses an empty list. Retain the original finding and exception reference. No exception makes an unpaid cost paid or retroactively approves arrangements.\\n\\nDomestic trips do not need a permit. An international trip needs its own approved permit before the first arrangement/payment commitment. Permit administration, budget owner and supervisor review the trip estimate. Claim administration, budget owner and supervisor separately review actual reimbursement. A director additionally reviews amounts strictly above EUR 1,000.00 (reviewed estimate for permit, reviewed entitlement for claim). Exactly EUR 1,000.00 does not require a director. When budget owner and supervisor are the same stable person, one response with both roles satisfies those two positions for that subject/version. Administration and director never collapse into another role. A permit response never approves a claim. A late permit does not retroactively authorize travel arrangements; Finance may explicitly resolve reimbursement eligibility while the permit exception remains recorded.\\n\\nCosts may be claimed as soon as the employee has paid, including before travel. The latest ordinary filing date is two calendar months after trip end, inclusive, with a nonexistent day clamped to month end. For a trip ending 31 August, the deadline is 31 October. Earlier filing is allowed after payment. A later filing requires a Finance exception or remains held. The claim's submission date, not import time, is used. Corrections retain the initial submission date for unchanged costs; newly added costs use their own first submission date.\\n\\nAdministration checks identity, receipt/paid proof, trip/permit, category, deadline, rates/caps, prior cost obligations and calculated amount. Budget review receives the whole department/project/period ledger: allocation less net settled expenditure less remaining commitments. A commitment includes its settled portion; do not subtract the full commitment and its settled portion again. Include prior obligations outside the current batch and all accepted new requests. Adequate funds alone are not a budget approval. Supervisor considers business purpose, client commitment, schedule coverage and permit consistency. Director considers high spend, the documented exception, alternatives and budget-owner position. Reviewers may approve, return with a concrete repair request, or reject with a reason; their discretionary judgment is supplied by the scenario, not performed by the learner.\\n\\nRequests and replies identify subject type, subject ID/revision, role(s), stable actor, relevant source versions and reason. Consume only the trainer-supplied decision batches and the directory's applicable actor/roles. Missing responses for otherwise complete requests wait; missing policy/input definitions are package defects. Reject wrong-role, stale-version or wrong-subject replies for current authorization. Keep rejected imports visible. A return reopens the appropriate review; explicit rejection or clean withdrawal can close with a non-payment reason.\\n\\nA material change to employee, trip, dates, money, policy/evidence or authority invalidates dependent review, approvals and payment readiness even if the total is unchanged. Full recheck and justified dependency recheck are both valid. Preserve old versions and decisions as history. Before dispatch, rebuild readiness from current facts. After dispatch, hold replacement requests until Finance confirms cancellation/status. Pending cancellation is not confirmed cancellation. Withdrawal never erases an actual payment.\\n\\nA payment request is a proposal to Finance, not a transfer. Use a stable request ID for the same obligation; replay cannot create another request or reimbursement of a previously committed/settled cost. A later final claim may contain a previously prepaid cost; link and exclude that settled obligation, showing the remaining entitlement rather than paying it twice. Legitimate adjustments link the original claim/cost/request and preserve its transfers.\\n\\nOnly supplied Finance outcomes establish pending, failed, settled, cancellation, refund and resolution facts. Failed attempts do not change paid amount; a new attempt requires Finance authorization. An immutable event ID identifies one payload across all batches/versions: exact replay has no extra effect, conflicting replay holds the case without erasing admitted money. Validate request, payee, currency, positive integer cents, time and actor before admission. Unmatched/invalid events remain visible for Finance resolution. A confirmed refund must name a prior settled transfer and cannot exceed its unrecovered amount. Refund promises/requests do not change paid amount.\\n\\nNet paid = admitted confirmed transfers minus linked confirmed refunds. Current balance = current authorized obligation minus net paid; a negative balance is an overpayment requiring Finance resolution. Partial settlement stays pending. Cancellation or a previously closed state never stops observation: a later transfer reopens reconciliation. A correction or cancellation that occurs after Finance has accepted or dispatched the affected reimbursement request requires explicit Finance resolution before closure. A post-payment adjustment also requires that resolution, even if net paid happens to match. Close reimbursed only when current approvals, obligation, net paid and all required resolutions agree and no issue remains. Zero entitlement, rejection and clean withdrawal close with an explicit non-payment reason and no unresolved financial effect.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Source-traceable Finance reconciliation primitives.\\n\\nOnly explicit, source-classified settled and refund events affect confirmed\\ncash. Finance obligations remain separate from caller-supplied authorized\\nobligations. No policy entitlement or approval decision is made here.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom collections import defaultdict\\nfrom copy import deepcopy\\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\\nfrom datetime import datetime\\nfrom .event_validation import finance_errors, utc_time\\nfrom typing import Any\\n\\n\\n_NATIVE_EVENT_CLASSES = {\\n    \\\"accepted\\\": \\\"obligation_accepted\\\",\\n    \\\"settled\\\": \\\"confirmed_payment\\\",\\n    \\\"refund\\\": \\\"confirmed_refund\\\",\\n    \\\"failed\\\": \\\"failed_transfer\\\",\\n    \\\"retry_authorized\\\": \\\"retry_authorization\\\",\\n    \\\"cancellation_requested\\\": \\\"finance_cancellation_requested\\\",\\n    \\\"cancelled\\\": \\\"finance_cancelled\\\",\\n    # These are retained as non-cash Finance records; their amount describes\\n    # an obligation, not a payment.\\n    \\\"adjustment\\\": \\\"finance_adjustment\\\",\\n    \\\"resolution\\\": \\\"finance_resolution\\\",\\n}\\n\\n\\ndef _values(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    return {key: cell.get(\\\"value\\\") for key, cell in record.get(\\\"values\\\", {}).items()}\\n\\n\\ndef _source_ref(record: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    return {key: record.get(key) for key in (\\\"source_id\\\", \\\"source_sha256\\\", \\\"locator\\\")}\\n\\n\\ndef _cents(value: Any) -> int | None:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Convert exact EUR decimal input to integer cents; reject rounding.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if value is None or isinstance(value, bool):\\n        return None\\n    try:\\n        amount = Decimal(str(value))\\n    except (InvalidOperation, ValueError):\\n        return None\\n    if not amount.is_finite():\\n        return None\\n    scaled = amount * 100\\n    if scaled != scaled.to_integral_value() or scaled < 0:\\n        return None\\n    return int(scaled)\\n\\n\\ndef _payload(values: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    return {key: values[key] for key in sorted(values) if key != \\\"Arrival batch\\\"}\\n\\n\\ndef _reference_text(ref: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\\n    return f\\\"{ref.get('source_id')}@{ref.get('source_sha256')}#{ref.get('locator')}\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef _positive_integer(value: Any) -> int | None:\\n    try:\\n        return int(value) if not isinstance(value, bool) and int(value) > 0 and float(value) == int(value) else None\\n    except (ValueError, TypeError, OverflowError):\\n        return None\\n\\n\\ndef _recorded_obligations(history: list[dict], *, claim_id: str, current_revision: int,\\n                          revisions: list[dict]) -> tuple[list[dict], dict | None, str | None]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Read ledger observations, without deriving reimbursement authorization.\\n\\n    Obligation (EUR) is a recorded amount, not a cash delta. Native rows omit\\n    claim revision; arrival context is retained separately from explicit links.\\n    Only the first delivery establishes context; redelivery cannot rebind it.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    groups: dict[str, list[dict]] = defaultdict(list)\\n    for event in history:\\n        if event['classification'] in {'obligation_accepted', 'finance_adjustment', 'finance_resolution'}:\\n            groups[event['event_id']].append(event)\\n    records = []\\n    problem = None\\n    for event_id, occurrences in groups.items():\\n        event = occurrences[0]\\n        values = event['source_record']\\n        batches = [e['source_record'].get('Arrival batch') for e in occurrences]\\n        first_batch = min((_positive_integer(b) for b in batches if _positive_integer(b)), default=None)\\n        context_rows = [r for r in revisions if first_batch is not None\\n                        and _positive_integer(r.get('arrival_batch')) is not None\\n                        and _positive_integer(r['arrival_batch']) <= first_batch]\\n        context = max((r['revision'] for r in context_rows), default=None)\\n        explicit = _positive_integer(values.get('Claim revision'))\\n        matches = [r for r in revisions if r['revision'] == explicit] if explicit else []\\n        link = ('explicit_current' if explicit == current_revision else 'explicit_historical') if matches else 'arrival_context_only' if context else 'unmatched'\\n        refs = [_reference_text(e['source_ref']) for e in occurrences]\\n        record = {\\n            'event_id': event_id, 'event_type': event['event_type'], 'claim_id': claim_id,\\n            'request_id': values.get('Request reference'), 'finance_officer': values.get('Finance officer'),\\n            'payee_id': values.get('Payee ID'), 'currency': event['currency'],\\n            'amount_cents': event['obligation_cents'], 'activity_time_utc': values.get('Activity time (UTC)'),\\n            'claim_revision': explicit if matches else None, 'arrival_revision_context': context,\\n            'revision_link_status': link, 'first_arrival_batch': first_batch,\\n            'delivery_batches': batches, 'source_refs': list(dict.fromkeys(refs)),\\n            'claim_source_refs': [deepcopy(r['source_ref']) for r in (matches or context_rows)\\n                                  if r['revision'] == (explicit if matches else context)],\\n        }\\n        records.append(record)\\n        if (event['currency'] != 'EUR' or event['obligation_cents'] is None or not first_batch\\n                or not all(isinstance(values.get(key), str) and values[key].strip()\\n                           for key in ('Request reference', 'Finance officer', 'Payee ID'))\\n                or not all(all(e['source_ref'].get(key) for key in ('source_id', 'source_sha256', 'locator')) for e in occurrences)\\n                or (values.get('Claim revision') is not None and not matches)):\\n            problem = 'Obligation record lacks supported amount, request/payee/officer, source identity, arrival, or explicit revision match'\\n    if not records:\\n        return [], None, None\\n    if len({(r['request_id'], r['payee_id'], r['currency']) for r in records}) != 1:\\n        problem = 'Multiple request/payee/currency ledgers cannot be combined as one obligation'\\n    # A single observation needs no ordering assumption. Multiple observations\\n    # require explicit UTC event times; arrival numbers do not define business time.\\n    if len(records) > 1:\\n        try:\\n            def stamp(record):\\n                dt = datetime.fromisoformat(record['activity_time_utc'].replace('Z', '+00:00'))\\n                # The retained header explicitly names UTC even when the cell\\n                # serialization omits an offset.\\n                if dt.utcoffset() is not None and dt.utcoffset().total_seconds() != 0:\\n                    raise ValueError('not UTC')\\n                return dt.replace(tzinfo=None)\\n            records.sort(key=lambda r: (stamp(r), r['event_id']))\\n            for left, right in zip(records, records[1:]):\\n                if stamp(left) == stamp(right) and left['amount_cents'] != right['amount_cents']:\\n                    problem = 'Conflicting obligation amounts have the same event time'\\n        except (ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):\\n            problem = 'Multiple obligation observations lack unambiguous UTC ordering'\\n    return records, deepcopy(records[-1]) if not problem else None, problem\\n\\n\\ndef reconcile_finance_events(\\n    events: list[dict[str, Any]],\\n    *,\\n    claim_id: str,\\n    current_revision: int,\\n    authorized_obligation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\\n    revision_history: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None,\\n    previous_reconciliation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\\n    owner: str = \\\"Finance\\\",\\n    source_classifications: dict[str, str] | None = None,\\n    event_context: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\\n) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Reconcile source events for a claim without making policy decisions.\\n\\n    `authorized_obligation` is an independent, already-authorized input of\\n    `{amount_cents, claim_revision, source_refs}`. This function neither\\n    derives nor authorizes it. `source_classifications` may extend the native\\n    workbook vocabulary when a retained source defines another event type;\\n    unrecognized types otherwise remain unresolved.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if not claim_id or isinstance(current_revision, bool) or not isinstance(current_revision, int) or current_revision < 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"claim_id and a positive current_revision are required\\\")\\n    if not owner:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"owner is required for reconciliation issues\\\")\\n    if (previous_reconciliation and 'admitted_events' not in previous_reconciliation\\n            and any(previous_reconciliation.get(k) for k in ('confirmed_payment_event_ids', 'confirmed_refund_event_ids',\\n                'confirmed_payment_cents', 'confirmed_refund_cents', 'net_confirmed_cents'))):\\n        raise ValueError('Legacy admission state requires explicit verified migration; refusing to erase or invent admitted money')\\n\\n    classes = dict(_NATIVE_EVENT_CLASSES)\\n    if source_classifications:\\n        allowed_classes = {\\n            \\\"confirmed_payment\\\", \\\"confirmed_refund\\\", \\\"pending_transfer\\\",\\n            \\\"obligation_accepted\\\", \\\"failed_transfer\\\", \\\"retry_authorization\\\",\\n            \\\"finance_cancellation_requested\\\", \\\"finance_cancelled\\\",\\n            \\\"finance_adjustment\\\", \\\"finance_resolution\\\",\\n        }\\n        for event_type, classification in source_classifications.items():\\n            if not isinstance(event_type, str) or classification not in allowed_classes:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"unsupported source event classification: {event_type!r} -> {classification!r}\\\")\\n            classes[event_type] = classification\\n\\n    # Accept full-history or delta calls without dropping earlier raw deliveries.\\n    retained = [{**deepcopy(h['source_ref']), 'values': {k: {'value': v} for k, v in h['source_record'].items()}}\\n                for h in (previous_reconciliation or {}).get('event_history', []) if isinstance(h.get('source_ref'), dict) and 'source_record' in h]\\n    deliveries = []\\n    for record in retained + events:\\n        if not any(_source_ref(r) == _source_ref(record) and _values(r) == _values(record) for r in deliveries):\\n            deliveries.append(record)\\n    events = deliveries\\n    by_id: dict[str, list[dict[str, Any]]] = defaultdict(list)\\n    missing_id_records: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\\n    for record in events:\\n        event_id = _values(record).get(\\\"Activity reference\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(event_id, str) or not event_id:\\n            if _values(record).get(\\\"Claim reference\\\") == claim_id:\\n                missing_id_records.append(record)\\n        else:\\n            by_id[event_id].append(record)\\n\\n    prior = deepcopy((previous_reconciliation or {}).get('admitted_events', {}))\\n    admitted = deepcopy(prior)\\n    history, duplicate_events, conflicting_events, unresolved = [], [], [], []\\n    event_issue_by_id = {}\\n\\n    def item_for(record):\\n        values = _values(record)\\n        return {\\\"event_id\\\": values.get(\\\"Activity reference\\\"), \\\"source_ref\\\": _source_ref(record),\\n                \\\"source_record\\\": deepcopy(values), \\\"event_type\\\": values.get(\\\"Activity type\\\"),\\n                \\\"classification\\\": classes.get(values.get(\\\"Activity type\\\"), \\\"unresolved\\\"),\\n                \\\"amount_cents\\\": _cents(values.get(\\\"Amount (EUR)\\\")),\\n                \\\"obligation_cents\\\": _cents(values.get(\\\"Obligation (EUR)\\\")),\\n                \\\"currency\\\": values.get(\\\"Currency\\\"), \\\"original_activity_id\\\": values.get(\\\"Original activity reference\\\")}\\n\\n    for event_id, occurrences in by_id.items():\\n        relevant = [r for r in occurrences if _values(r).get('Claim reference') == claim_id]\\n        if not relevant and event_id not in prior:\\n            continue\\n        payloads = [_payload(_values(r)) for r in occurrences]\\n        if event_id in prior:\\n            payloads.append(_payload(prior[event_id]['source_record']))\\n        conflict = any(v != payloads[0] for v in payloads[1:])\\n        if conflict:\\n            conflicting_events.append({'event_id': event_id, 'source_refs': [_source_ref(r) for r in occurrences], 'payloads': payloads})\\n            event_issue_by_id[event_id] = {\\n                'record_id': f'finance-event-conflict:{event_id}', 'event_id': event_id,\\n                'subject_type': 'claim', 'subject_id': claim_id, 'revision': current_revision,\\n                'missing_or_return_reason': 'Conflicting immutable event replay; admitted history retained, new payload held',\\n                'source_refs': [_source_ref(r) for r in occurrences], 'owner': owner,\\n                'next_action': 'Finance to resolve the conflicting delivery without erasing admitted money'}\\n        elif len(occurrences) > 1:\\n            duplicate_events.append({'event_id': event_id, 'source_refs': [_source_ref(r) for r in occurrences],\\n                                     'delivery_batches': [_values(r).get('Arrival batch') for r in occurrences]})\\n        if event_id not in admitted:\\n            batches = [_positive_integer(_values(r).get('Arrival batch')) for r in occurrences]\\n            first_batch = min((v for v in batc…5021 tokens truncated…es']]\\n        if not candidates: role_states[role]='missing'; continue\\n        latest=max(d['order'] for d in candidates)\\n        matches=[d for d in candidates if d['order']==latest]\\n        if len(matches)!=1:\\n            role_states[role]='conflicting';continue\\n        chosen=matches[0];chosen['active']=True;role_states[role]=chosen['outcome']\\n        if chosen not in selected: selected.append(chosen)\\n    withdrawal_valid=bool(withdrawn and source_bound(subject_record,observations) and source_bound(trip_record,observations)\\n        and trip.get('Employee ID')==employee and len(people)==1 and source_bound(people[0],observations)\\n        and isinstance(fields(subject_record).get('Claim reason'),str) and fields(subject_record)['Claim reason'].strip())\\n    states=set(role_states.values())\\n    state=('withdrawn' if withdrawal_valid else 'rejected' if 'reject' in states else 'returned' if 'return' in states\\n           else 'approved' if states=={'approve'} and policy and amount_known else 'pending')\\n    if not policy or conflicts and not withdrawal_valid: state='pending'\\n    policy_binding=parsed.get('expense_policy') or {}\\n    policy_refs=[f\\\"{policy_binding.get('path')}@{policy_binding.get('sha256')}#line {n}\\\" for n in (9,13,15,17)] if policy else []\\n    return dict(policy_source_refs=policy_refs,subject_type=kind,subject_id=subject_id,revision=revision,state=state,required_roles=required,\\n                amount_cents=amount_cents,amount_known=amount_known,evidence_digest=digest,withdrawal_requested=withdrawn,withdrawal_valid=withdrawal_valid,\\n                material_same_revision=material_same_revision,invalidated_batch=invalidated_batch,policy_verified=policy,role_states=role_states,\\n                deliveries=deliveries,active_decision_ids=[d['decision_id'] for d in selected],\\n                source_refs=list(dict.fromkeys([ref(r) for r in basis_rows]+[r for d in deliveries for r in d['source_refs']])),\\n                approved=state=='approved',repair_requests=[d['repair_requested'] for d in selected if d['outcome']=='return'])\\n\\n\\ndef evaluate_permit(*, parsed, trip_record, decisions, arrival_batch, observations, prior=None, cost_ids=(), cancellations=()):\\n    trip=fields(trip_record)\\n    if trip.get('International') is False:\\n        affected=[c for c in cancellations if c.get('trip_id')==trip.get('Trip reference')\\n            and _revision(c.get('trip_revision'))==_revision(trip.get('Trip revision'))]\\n        return dict(subject_type='permit',subject_id=None,revision=None,state='not-required',approved=True,\\n                    arrangement_authorized=policy_valid(parsed.get('expense_policy')) and not affected,\\n                    arrangements_at_commitment_supported=policy_valid(parsed.get('expense_policy')),\\n                    cancellation_ids=[c['cancellation_id'] for c in affected], source_refs=[ref(trip_record)],deliveries=[])\\n    from .finance import _cents\\n    subject=deepcopy(trip_record)\\n    # Newly parsed workbooks retain the printed source version in their preamble.\\n    subject['text']='\\\\n'.join(str(c.get('value','')) for s in parsed.get('workbook_sheets',[])\\n        if s.get('source_id')==trip_record.get('source_id') for c in s.get('preamble',[]))\\n    result=evaluate_reviews(parsed=parsed,kind='permit',subject_id=trip.get('Permit reference'),revision=_revision(trip.get('Permit revision')),\\n        trip_record=trip_record,employee=trip.get('Employee ID'),subject_record=subject,amount_cents=_cents(trip.get('Estimate (EUR)')),\\n        decisions=decisions,arrival_batch=arrival_batch,observations=observations,cost_ids=cost_ids,prior=prior)\\n    result['arrangement_authorized']=False\\n    if result['approved'] and trip.get('International') is True:\\n        commitment=trip.get('First commitment date')\\n        if commitment in (None,''):\\n            result['arrangement_authorized']=True\\n        else:\\n            try:\\n                day=local_date(commitment)\\n                active=[d for d in result['deliveries'] if d['active']]\\n                latest=max(utc_time(d['decision_time']) for d in active).astimezone(ZoneInfo('Europe/Amsterdam')).date()\\n                result['arrangement_authorized']=latest<day\\n                result['timing_finding']=None if latest<day else 'late_permit' if latest>day else 'same-day-order-unconfirmed'\\n            except (ValueError,TypeError): result['timing_finding']='missing-commitment-evidence'\\n    result['arrangements_at_commitment_supported']=result['arrangement_authorized']\\n    affected=[c for c in cancellations if c.get('trip_id')==trip.get('Trip reference')\\n        and _revision(c.get('trip_revision'))==_revision(trip.get('Trip revision'))\\n        and (c.get('target_type')=='trip' or (c.get('permit_id')==trip.get('Permit reference')\\n             and _revision(c.get('permit_revision'))==_revision(trip.get('Permit revision'))))]\\n    result['canc