{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T01:19:38.425Z","ordinal":3498,"type":"compacted","payload":{"compaction_response_id":"resp_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad029e9494881909e451ae40e0ff057","first_window_id":"01a13bd1-7429-7262-9112-3a84f736e66f","guardian_history":[{"content":[{"text":"Continue implementing Project D in the existing ~/travel-expense-claim repository.\n\nThe previous milestone is committed and pushed as 65ee4f0. The offline replay already generates four linked batch snapshots, claims.csv, report.md, repair-queue.json, and offline-replay-state.json.\n\nImplement the next milestone now, not just a plan:\n\nInspect the current offline replay report generation, repair queue, and related tests.\n\nImprove report.md to clearly separate:\n\nClaim-specific actionable repair items, grouped by responsible owner, with traceable claim/subject/revision/source references and next actions.\n\nRun-level external blockers, including the inaccessible native Notion reimbursement policy and the unconfirmed authoritative case clock.\n\nClearly label this output as an offline replay of retained evidence, not a fresh live-source run.\n\nPreserve partial progress: unresolved claims must not prevent independent valid records from being processed.\n\nDo not invent policy rules, eligibility amounts, approvals, payment confirmations, or case-clock  dates.\n\nAdd or update automated tests for the report sections, grouping, traceability, and unresolved blockers.\n\nRun the complete test suite and git diff --check.\n\nRegenerate the offline replay outputs and summarize the actual results.\n\nDo not commit or push yet. Show me the files changed, tests passed, and any remaining blockers. Preserve all existing Git and Entire.io history.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a13bd3-423a-7082-8f73-b169f3b37bba","role":"user","turn_id":"01a13bd3-3cec-7081-b847-b31e41528363"},"revision":"retained_01a13bd3-423a-7082-8f73-b18698ae74cc"},"user_input_order":0},"id":"msg_01a13bd3-423a-7082-8f73-b169f3b37bba","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792005063.2267163,"turn_id":"01a13bd3-3cec-7081-b847-b31e41528363"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Preserve the completed Project D report-separation milestone in Git and Entire.io.\n\n1. Inspect `git status` and the exact diff.\n2. Stage ONLY these three source files:\n   - `README.md`\n   - `src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py`\n   - `tests/test_offline_replay.py`\n3. Do NOT stage `artifacts/runs/` or unrelated files.\n4. Run `git diff --cached --check` and the complete pytest suite.\n5. If validation passes, commit with the message:\n   `feat: separate Project D repairs and run blockers`\n6. Push the commit to `origin main`, allowing the existing Entire.io hooks to run.\n7. Verify the remote main commit and report whether the Entire.io checkpoint references were pushed.\n\nDo not rewrite history, force-push, or modify retained source artifacts.\n\nReport the commit hash, test results, push status, and any warnings.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a13bd7-4146-7772-a00f-d514bd3f3bd7","role":"user","turn_id":"01a13bd7-3aa0-7972-adeb-ce27fff74914"},"revision":"retained_01a13bd7-4146-7772-a00f-d5382053c075"},"user_input_order":5},"id":"msg_01a13bd7-4146-7772-a00f-d514bd3f3bd7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792005325.126499,"turn_id":"01a13bd7-3aa0-7972-adeb-ce27fff74914"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Continue implementing Project D in ~/travel-expense-claim.\n\nThe latest verified GitHub commit is 0f0acf3. Implement the next coding milestone: owner-specific follow-up drafts based on the existing repair queue.\n\nInspect the current repair-queue schema, report generation, and tests.\n\nGenerate a new artifact, follow-up-drafts.md, from unresolved repair items only.\n\nGroup draft messages by responsible owner, preserving claim IDs, revisions, evidence references, unresolved questions, and specific requested next actions.\n\nClearly distinguish claim-specific repairs, trip/permit repairs, and external run-level blockers.\n\nDo not generate messages for resolved items.\n\nTreat all messages as drafts requiring human review. Do not send emails or contact anyone.\n\nDo not invent email addresses, deadlines, reimbursement rules, approval decisions, payment events, or missing evidence.\n\nPreserve independent claim processing and existing immutable snapshot history.\n\nAdd automated tests for grouping, traceability, resolved-item exclusion, and human-review labeling.\n\nRun the complete test suite and git diff --check.\n\nRegenerate the offline replay outputs in a new retained-input run without overwriting prior artifacts.\n\nImplement the code now, not just a plan.\n\nDo not commit or push yet. Report the files changed, test results, generated draft count, and remaining blockers.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"retained_source":{"complete":true,"id":{"message_id":"msg_01a13bdd-4cde-7952-b26f-5b8f1fb8fc4b","role":"user","turn_id":"01a13bdd-4a66-7290-846d-c41f22484a9c"},"revision":"retained_01a13bdd-4cde-7952-b26f-5bae832ed06f"},"user_input_order":13},"id":"msg_01a13bdd-4cde-7952-b26f-5b8f1fb8fc4b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792005721.3107705,"turn_id":"01a13bdd-4a66-7290-846d-c41f22484a9c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Preserve the completed Project D owner-specific follow-up draft milestone in Git and Entire.io.\n\n    Inspect git status and the exact source diff.\n\n    Stage ONLY:\n\n        README.md\n\n        src