esenting the policy-to-implementation gap report.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":118},"id":"msg_01a13c40-42a7-7720-bad1-016e57645ad1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792012206.7595844,"turn_id":"01a13c40-3bbc-7d50-8ce8-5e7628d5b3da"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Project D — Step 171: Fix high-risk policy compliance defects.\n\nUse the verified POL-2026.2 browser copy and the completed Step 167 audit as authoritative references.\n\nFocus ONLY on these two areas:\n\nFinance event integrity:\n\nAn admitted confirmed transfer must never disappear because of a later conflicting event redelivery.\n\nExact immutable-event replay must have no additional effect.\n\nConflicting replay must retain the admitted event and hold the affected case for Finance resolution.\n\nValidate Finance event identity, request, payee, currency, positive integer cents, time and actor.\n\nPreserve unmatched and invalid events for review.\n\nIndependent cancellation validation:\n\nOnly the authorized directory supervisor can confirm a cancellation.\n\nConfirmation must reference the matching initiation and target.\n\nConfirmation must occur strictly after initiation.\n\nReject scheduled, backdated, stale-target, wrong-actor and future-observation confirmations as authority.\n\nPreserve invalid deliveries as visible evidence without changing admitted cancellation history.\n\nKeep business cancellation separate from Finance cancellation.\n\nRequirements:\n\nAdd focused regression tests reproducing the defects identified in the Step 167 synthetic probes.\n\nPreserve all earlier snapshots, financial outputs, original interview and policy copy.\n\nDo not silently alter unrelated eligibility, approval or closure rules.\n\nRun the complete test suite and report the results.\n\nReport any remaining ambiguity rather than inventing facts.\n\nDo not commit or push yet.\n\nStop after implementation, tests and a concise change summary.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":124},"id":"msg_01a13c45-9e2e-7f42-8320-94e33cef53b3","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792012557.8708947,"turn_id":"01a13c45-9846-7111-9cb7-eca8b1cc3957"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Project D — Step 172: Commit and push the verified event-integrity fixes.\n\nBefore committing:\n\n    Verify the current branch, Git status and diff.\n\n    Confirm the changes are limited to Step 171 Finance event integrity, cancellation validation, supporting fixtures and regression tests.\n\n    Run the complete test suite again and git diff --check.\n\n    Verify the original policy, interview, prior snapshots and retained outputs remain unchanged.\n\n    Stage only the reviewed Step 171 implementation and test files. Do not stage unrelated untracked artifacts or audit reports.\n\n    Commit with message: fix: preserve admitted finance and cancellation event integrity\n\nPush normally to the existing GitHub main branch. Do not force-push.\n\nVerify the remote commit matches the local commit and confirm the Entire.io checkpoint references were pushed.\n\nReport the full commit SHA, number of passing tests, changed files, remote verification and Entire.io checkpoint status.\n\nIf any verification fails, stop without pushing and explain the issue.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":130},"id":"msg_01a13c51-eb95-7671-8964-a9f57fb3039f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792013364.1171467,"turn_id":"01a13c51-e5b0-75a2-acee-0c608041a033"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Project D — Step 173: Implement policy-compliant expense calculations and filing deadlines.\n\nUse the exact recovered POL-2026.2 browser copy and the Step 167 policy gap audit.\n\nImplement only:\n\n    Expense calculation rules:\n\n    Require actual employee-paid expenses supported by matching receipt and settled merchant transaction.\n\n    Validate employee, trip, cost ID, currency and gross amount.\n\n    Treat personal purchases as zero entitlement.\n\n    Transport and conference costs have no category cap.\n\n    Lodging uses the applicable nightly cap; meals use the applicable daily cap.\n\n    Require positive integer documented units for capped expenses.\n\n    Resolve caps using destination, expense currency and employee-payment date.\n\n    Unknown categories, missing evidence, rates or caps must remain unresolved rather than becoming zero.\n\nApply Finance's exact payment-date EUR exchange rate; EUR rate is 1.\n\nRound each converted line to EUR cents using decimal ROUND_HALF_UP, then sum rounded lines.\n\nPreserve original expense and conversion evidence.\n\nFiling deadlines:\n\nCalculate the deadline as two calendar months after the trip end, inclusive, clamping nonexistent days to month end.\n\nAllow filing before travel when employee payment is established.\n\nUse submission dates rather than arrival/import dates.\n\nPreserve the original submission date for unchanged costs after correction.\n\nNewly added costs use their own first submission date.\n\nLate filing remains held pending an explicit Finance exception; do not invent one.\n\nRequirements:\n\nUse real retained source schemas and source-bound references.\n\nAdd tests for normal, missing-data and boundary cases, including August 31 to October 31, leap years, exactly-on-deadline filing, fractional units and half-cent FX rounding.\n\nDo not change Finance event admission, cancellation validation, approvals, closure gates or prior retained outputs.\n\nPreserve the original policy and interview.\n\nRun the complete test suite and report the results.\n\nDo not commit or push yet.\n\nStop after implementation and verification, reporting any policy ambiguity or missing source data.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":139},"id":"msg_01a13c57-7704-7291-ab72-dd6efbc80ce2","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792013727.4922955,"turn_id":"01a13c57-6fc6-7d93-a6e4-729352fb610c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Project D — Step 174: Verify, commit, and push the Step 173 expense-calculation and filing-deadline milestone.\n\nReview the seven changed files and confirm the changes are limited to Step 173.\n\nVerify tests/fixtures/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt is an exact-byte copy of the user-provided policy. Label it clearly as a browser-obtained fixture, not an independently fetched native Notion source.\n\nRerun the full test suite and Git diff checks.\n\nVerify the original interview, policy, prior snapshots, retained financial outputs, and Step 171 event-integrity code remain unchanged.\n\nStage only these seven reviewed files:\n\nREADME.md\n\nsrc/travel_claim/expenses.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/ordinary.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/integration.py\n\ntests/test_expenses.py\n\ntests/test_ordinary.py\n\ntests/fixtures/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt\n\nCommit with message: feat: validate policy expense calculations and filing deadlines\n\nPush normally to origin main without force-pushing.\n\nVerify remote main matches the local commit and all Entire.io checkpoint references are present.\n\nDo not stage unrelated untracked policy provenance or audit artifacts.\n\nReport the full commit SHA, test count, remote verification, and Entire.io checkpoint status. Stop if any check fails.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":145},"id":"msg_01a13c64-d9cc-7921-ab05-f8f112c93634","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792014604.7483475,"turn_id":"01a13c64-d22a-70e3-a215-409d6c4c2d93"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Project D — Step 175: Implement policy-compliant Finance exceptions.\n\nUse the verified POL-2026.2 browser-copy fixture and Step 167 audit.\n\nImplement and test Finance exception handling for:\n\nExplicit Finance actor and source-bound claim/revision/cost authority.\n\nReplacement allowed amount in the original expense currency, with a documented reason.\n\nExact covered_issues matching; an amount-only exception covers no eligibility issues.\n\nlate_filing, late_permit, permit_unapproved and travel_cancellation as independently tracked findings.\n\nTravel cancellation exceptions must reference the exact travel_cancellation_id and affected expense.\n\nExceptions never establish employee payment, retroactively approve arrangements, or erase original findings.\n\nMaterial replacement-amount changes invalidate dependent claim reviews and payment readiness until current authorization is supplied.\n\nPreserve previously admitted Finance events, cancellation history and immutable snapshots.\n\nUse actual retained source schemas. If a required exception field is absent, retain an unresolved finding instead of inventing authority.\n\nAdd focused positive, negative, stale-version and replay tests. Preserve earlier outputs and all protected source files. Do not modify unrelated budget, approval or closure logic.\n\nRun the complete test suite and Git diff checks. Report findings and any remaining blockers.\n\nDo not stage, commit or push yet. Stop after implementation and verification.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":155},"id":"msg_01a13c69-4208-7fc1-82da-8e2f72e81d24","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792014893.576473,"turn_id":"01a13c69-3978-7453-b087-16348d8b1d40"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Resume Project D Step 175 from the existing uncommitted working tree.\n\nCodex previously reached its usage limit during Finance exception implementation.\n\nDo not restart or overwrite the work.\n\nInspect all existing Step 175 changes, including exceptions.py, test_exceptions.py, retained exception fixtures, ordinary.py and integration.py.\n\nVerify the implementation against POL-2026.2 and the Step 167 audit.\n\nRun the complete test suite after all newly added tests.\n\nRun git diff --check and review the full diff.\n\nVerify the original interview, policy, earlier snapshots, admitted Finance events, cancellation history and previous commits remain unchanged.\n\nIdentify and fix any remaining Step 175 defects without expanding into unrelated budget or closure work.\n\nReport the final test count, changed files and unresolved issues.\n\nDo not stage, commit or push yet.\n\nStop after completing Step 175 implementation verification.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":159},"id":"msg_01a13cf2-e30b-71b1-b18d-e233f5194348","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792023913.2274709,"turn_id":"01a13cf2-cebe-70e1-8dae-3f683e534b00"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Project D — Step 176: Commit and push the verified Step 175 Finance exception milestone.\n\nVerify the current Git branch, status, and complete Step 175 diff.\n\nConfirm the eight changed files are limited to Finance exception handling, supporting integration, documentation, fixtures, and tests.\n\nRerun the complete test suite and Git diff checks.\n\nVerify the 128 preserved files remain unchanged, including the policy, interview, prior outputs, and event-integrity implementation.\n\nStage only these eight reviewed files:\n\nREADME.md\n\nsrc/travel_claim/exceptions.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/expenses.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/ordinary.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/integration.py\n\ntests/test_exceptions.py\n\ntests/test_ordinary.py\n\ntests/fixtures/retained_exception_records.json\n\nCommit with message: feat: validate source-bound finance exceptions\n\nPush normally to origin main without force-pushing.\n\nVerify remote main matches the local commit and all Entire.io checkpoint references match remotely.\n\nDo not stage unrelated audit reports or untracked provenance files.\n\nReport the full commit SHA, passing test count, changed files, and Entire.io verification.\n\nIf any verification fails, stop and report the issue.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":164},"id":"msg_01a13cf6-cbd2-7650-97de-2c660e3ab5a2","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792024169.4267108,"turn_id":"01a13cf6-c440-7750-8e5d-543e9f9b5950"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Project D — Step 177: Implement policy-compliant permit and reimbursement approval workflows.\n\nUse the verified POL-2026.2 policy fixture and the Step 167 gap audit.\n\nImplement and test:\n\n    Separate approval subjects for international travel permits and reimbursement claims. Domestic trips require no permit.\n\n    Permit reviews require administration, budget owner, and supervisor, with director review strictly above EUR 1,000 in reviewed estimate.\n\n    Claim reviews require administration, budget owner, and supervisor, with director review strictly above EUR 1,000 in reviewed entitlement.\n\n    Exactly EUR 1,000 does not require director approval.\n\nBudget owner and supervisor may share one response only when the directory identifies the same stable person and the response explicitly covers both roles.\n\nValidate subject type, ID, revision, role, stable actor, source versions, and reason.\n\nReject wrong-role, stale-version, wrong-subject, and unauthorized replies as current authority, while retaining their history.\n\nSupport approve, return-with-repair, reject-with-reason, and clean withdrawal transitions.\n\nMaterial changes invalidate dependent reviews and payment readiness; rebuild readiness from current evidence.\n\nNever treat permit approval as claim approval, or Finance exceptions as retroactive travel authorization.\n\nRequirements:\n\nUse actual retained review packets, decision batches, directory roles, and source references.\n\nPreserve historical decisions and rejected imports.\n\nAdd positive, negative, threshold, correction, and replay tests.\n\nPreserve prior snapshots, admitted financial events, cancellation history, policy, and interview.\n\nDo not modify unrelated budget reconciliation or financial closure logic.\n\nRun the complete test suite and diff checks.\n\nReport unresolved evidence or discretionary human decisions instead of inventing approvals.\n\nDo not stage, commit, or push yet. Stop after implementation and verification.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":174},"id":"msg_01a13cfb-3d1c-7b53-ae27-da9bcea1007a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792024460.572223,"turn_id":"01a13cfb-36ce-7122-9610-f91773084724"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Project D — Step 178: Commit and push the verified Step 177 approval workflow milestone.\n\nVerify the current branch, Git status, and complete diff.\n\nConfirm changes are limited to the 11 reviewed Step 177 implementation, documentation, fixture, and test files.\n\nRerun the full test suite and Git diff checks.\n\nVerify all 128 protected files remain unchanged, including the policy, interview, prior snapshots, financial outputs, and event-integrity code.\n\nStage only:\n\nREADME.md\n\nsrc/travel_claim/approvals.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/integration.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/ordinary.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/parsing.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/snapshots.py\n\ntests/test_approvals.py\n\ntests/test_exceptions.py\n\ntests/test_ordinary.py\n\ntests/fixtures/retained_approval_records.json\n\nCommit with message: feat: validate permit and claim approval workflows\n\nPush normally to origin main without force-pushing.\n\nVerify remote main matches the local commit and all Entire.io checkpoint references match remotely.\n\nDo not stage unrelated audit reports or user-provided policy provenance files.\n\nReport the full commit SHA, passing test count, committed files, and Entire.io checkpoint verification.\n\nIf any verification fails, stop and explain the issue.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":182},"id":"msg_01a13d08-9636-7042-bba6-b25f8a2c000a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792025335.350472,"turn_id":"01a13d08-8eb1-7b30-9180-e04d7a7ded55"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Project D — Step 179: Implement policy-compliant budget reconciliation.\n\nUse POL-2026.2, the Step 167 gap audit, and the actual retained workbook, claims, reviews, and Finance records.\n\nFirst inspect the exact policy sections governing budgets, prepaid costs, reimbursement obligations, and budget-owner authorization.\n\nImplement and test:\n\nBudget availability and commitments using the policy's actual accounting rules.\n\nCross-claim prepaid-cost attribution without double counting.\n\nCorrections and cancellations that change commitments while preserving financial history.\n\nSource-bound budget identities, amounts, currencies, revisions, and arrival batches.\n\nRevalidation of affected budget-owner approvals after material budget changes.\n\nConflict detection, exact replay deduplication, and unresolved-evidence holds.\n\nSeparate authorized obligations, confirmed payments, refunds, and outstanding balances.\n\nOwner-grouped repair findings with exact source references.\n\nNever invent missing allocations, rates, budgets, approvals, or financial events. Preserve unaffected valid claims and admitted Finance history.\n\nAdd focused synthetic and retained-data tests, including budget exhaustion, cross-claim prepaid costs, corrections, cancellations, and replay.\n\nPreserve the policy, interview, previous snapshots and outputs, and all protected event-integrity modules.\n\nDo not modify unrelated approval, Finance-exception, or closure rules.\n\nRun the complete test suite and diff checks. Report changed files, test results, and unresolved blockers.\n\nDo not stage, commit, or push yet. Stop after implementation and verification.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":193},"id":"msg_01a13d0d-a660-7553-99ec-3d0158a905df","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792025667.1689932,"turn_id":"01a13d0d-9f67-7c00-8955-722676671362"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_f5f77a7522d343d3a42328f562b88bfe","id":"ctc_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad026b3a0448190a1b3606d980c1117","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 - \u003c\u003c'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\np=Path('src/travel_claim/budget.py');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"        result['existing_recorded_commitment_cents']=sum(r['commitment_cents'] or 0 for r in own)\\\", \\\"        matching_own={x['request_id'] for line in lines for x in attribution['costs'].get(line['cost_id'],[])\\\\n            if x['claim_id']==claim['subject_id'] and x['signature']==list(cost_signature(record,line))}\\\\n        result['existing_recorded_commitment_cents']=sum(r['commitment_cents'] or 0 for r in own if r['request_id'] in matching_own)\\\")\\np.write_text(s)\\np=Path('tests/test_budget.py');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"replay=run_one(p,1,first) if False else integrate_arrival_batch\\\", \\\"replay=integrate_arrival_batch\\\");p.write_text(s)\\nPY\\ncat \u003e\u003e tests/test_budget.py \u003c\u003c'PY'\\n\\n\\ndef test_refund_alone_does_not_release_an_unchanged_commitment():\\n    p=synthetic();refund=deepcopy(p['records']['finance_events'][1])\\n    setfield(refund,'Activity reference','SYN-REFUND');setfield(refund,'Activity type','refund')\\n    setfield(refund,'Arrival batch',3);setfield(refund,'Amount (EUR)',20)\\n    setfield(refund,'Original activity reference',fields(p['records']['finance_events'][1])['Activity reference'])\\n    setfield(refund,'Activity time (UTC)','2026-09-13T12:00:00');p['records']['finance_events'].append(refund)\\n    results=batches(p);before=scope(results[1]);after=scope(results[-1])\\n    assert after['confirmed_refund_cents']==2000\\n    assert after['requests']['REQ-SYN-C01']['remaining_commitment_cents']==2000\\n    assert before['available_cents']==after['available_cents']\\n\\n\\ndef test_ambiguous_shared_cost_allocation_is_held_not_prorated():\\n    p=synthetic();result=run_one(p);record=p['records']['claim_revisions'][0]\\n    from travel_claim.ordinary import expense_lines\\n    attribution={'costs':{},'unallocated_costs':{'COST-01':[dict(claim_id='EARLIER',request_id='REQ-EARLIER',source_refs=[ref(record)])]}}\\n    view=claim_budget_view(parsed=p,claim=result['domain']['revision_history']['claim']['SYN-C01']['revisions'][0],\\n        lines=[dict(expense_lines(record)[0],calculated_cents=10000)],budgets=result['domain']['budget'],attribution=attribution,arrival_batch=1)\\n    assert view['remaining_request_cents'] is None and view['status']=='BLOCKED'\\n    assert any('allocation' in i['reason'] for i in view['issues'])\\n\\n\\ndef test_budget_owner_packet_must_include_the_whole_scope_ledger():\\n    p=synthetic();packet=table(p,'review_packets','Review packets')[1]\\n    setfield(packet,'Budget record references','B-AL