les.","turn_id":"01a13d0d-9f67-7c00-8955-722676671362"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad024ca91b4819083389761dc3f7020","order":195,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a13d0f-bea5-7fd1-b81f-b97c540f05b8","text":"The policy requires allocation minus net settled expenditure minus remaining commitments. The retained opening ledger therefore leaves €15,000 before new accepted requests: €20,000 less €2,000 settled and €3,000 still committed. I’ll reconcile accepted requests once by stable request ID, keep payments and refunds separate, and use the explicit C03/C24 cost linkage to prevent a second reimbursement. Ambiguous cost allocations will remain held.","turn_id":"01a13d0d-9f67-7c00-8955-722676671362"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad025f465a08190aa58978362347206","order":196,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a13d14-4c2c-7a70-a6a4-17d3f4b8eb29","text":"Budget reconciliation is now wired to the protected Finance admission ledger. Settlements, refunds, and request commitments remain separate, and a business cancellation alone releases no commitment. I’m adding focused tests for budget exhaustion, C03/C24 prepaid attribution, correction and cancellation effects, and budget-owner revalidation; ambiguous aggregate cost allocations remain explicit Finance repair items.","turn_id":"01a13d0d-9f67-7c00-8955-722676671362"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad02724d164819084c1bafbb1d94821","order":197,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a13d18-f036-77c0-8129-514f061673ac","text":"The retained-data tests confirm the key distinctions: C24’s linked €200 cost leaves a €50 remaining request; C19’s adjustment and refund preserve the original transfer; and C18’s late €100 payment still consumes budget after Finance cancellation. I also fixed a correction edge case so an old commitment for one cost cannot offset a corrected claim’s different cost. I’m now checking report/readiness consistency and the full regression suite.","turn_id":"01a13d0d-9f67-7c00-8955-722676671362"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad027b46ebc8190ac9bbf091f3d1e0a","order":198,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a13d1b-1d87-7592-abc5-8fbcdc5e7052","text":"The full suite passed with 370 tests. A final review identified one more distinction worth testing: cancelling a transfer attempt must not release the accepted request commitment or create a refund. That guard is now added. I’m running the final suite and preservation checks; no prior run artifacts have been regenerated.","turn_id":"01a13d0d-9f67-7c00-8955-722676671362"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad02879a8d081908d34d38f80ce4fcd","order":199,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a13d1e-44be-70f0-89dc-83e989147363","text":"The read-only calculation against all retained Finance records reports €20,000 allocated, €14,034.15 in net settled expenditure, €3,000 in remaining commitments, and €2,965.85 available across 104 request ledgers. These are accounting facts—not new approvals or closure decisions. The final checks distinguish newly arrived Finance facts from changes to the opening source, so budget-owner revalidation can use evidenced source versions appropriately.","turn_id":"01a13d0d-9f67-7c00-8955-722676671362"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad028ec8ed88190b5ae45ad73374ca7","order":200,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a13d1f-edd5-7c42-adbc-2834b3675974","text":"Implemented Step 179: source-bound budget reconciliation, prepaid-cost attribution, conflict/replay handling, and affected budget-owner revalidation.\n\n**Verification:** 376 tests passed, including 37 budget regressions. Diff checks passed. All 129 preservation hashes match; event-integrity, Finance-exception, and financial closure code remain unchanged.\n\nThe read-only full retained-ledger calculation reports:\n\n- Allocation: **€20,000**\n- Net settled expenditure: **€14,034.15**\n- Remaining commitments: **€3,000**\n- Available: **€2,965.85**\n\nRetained C03/C24 tests exclude the existing €200 obligation, leaving €50 for the additional request. Transfer cancellation, request cancellation, and refunds remain distinct.\n\nChanged files:\n\n- `README.md`\n- `src/travel_claim/budget.py`\n- `src/travel_claim/approvals.py`\n- `src/travel_claim/integration.py`\n- `src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py`\n- `src/travel_claim/ordinary.py`\n- `src/travel_claim/readiness.py`\n- `src/travel_claim/snapshots.py`\n- `tests/test_budget.py`\n- `tests/test_approvals.py`\n- `tests/test_exceptions.py`\n- `tests/fixtures/retained_budget_records.json`\n\nMissing current budget-owner authorization, insufficient source-version evidence, ambiguous cost allocations, and conflicting Finance facts remain held. Existing native request and closure gaps remain separate blockers; no real claim was newly authorized or closed.\n\nNothing staged, committed, or pushed.","turn_id":"01a13d0d-9f67-7c00-8955-722676671362"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad0296702588190a1292ed8eaf45e44","order":202,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a13d21-be24-7f50-b62c-a40a3cfc5273","text":"I’ll verify the 12-file diff against `7015dde`, rerun the tests and preservation checks, then commit and push through the existing Entire.io hooks if validation passes.","turn_id":"01a13d21-a9c0-7872-9e35-080056b8fba9"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":204,"user_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a13c64-d9cc-7921-ab05-f8f112c93634","order":145,"revision":"retained_01a13c64-d9cc-7921-ab05-f91bcd83b5c6","text":"Project D — Step 174: Verify, commit, and push the Step 173 expense-calculation and filing-deadline milestone.\n\nReview the seven changed files and confirm the changes are limited to Step 173.\n\nVerify tests/fixtures/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt is an exact-byte copy of the user-provided policy. Label it clearly as a browser-obtained fixture, not an independently fetched native Notion source.\n\nRerun the full test suite and Git diff checks.\n\nVerify the original interview, policy, prior snapshots, retained financial outputs, and Step 171 event-integrity code remain unchanged.\n\nStage only these seven reviewed files:\n\nREADME.md\n\nsrc/travel_claim/expenses.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/ordinary.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/integration.py\n\ntests/test_expenses.py\n\ntests/test_ordinary.py\n\ntests/fixtures/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt\n\nCommit with message: feat: validate policy expense calculations and filing deadlines\n\nPush normally to origin main without force-pushing.\n\nVerify remote main matches the local commit and all Entire.io checkpoint references are present.\n\nDo not stage unrelated untracked policy provenance or audit artifacts.\n\nReport the full commit SHA, test count, remote verification, and Entire.io checkpoint status. Stop if any check fails.","turn_id":"01a13c64-d22a-70e3-a215-409d6c4c2d93"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a13c69-4208-7fc1-82da-8e2f72e81d24","order":155,"revision":"retained_01a13c69-4208-7fc1-82da-8e47fd785dac","text":"Project D — Step 175: Implement policy-compliant Finance exceptions.\n\nUse the verified POL-2026.2 browser-copy fixture and Step 167 audit.\n\nImplement and test Finance exception handling for:\n\nExplicit Finance actor and source-bound claim/revision/cost authority.\n\nReplacement allowed amount in the original expense currency, with a documented reason.\n\nExact covered_issues matching; an amount-only exception covers no eligibility issues.\n\nlate_filing, late_permit, permit_unapproved and travel_cancellation as independently tracked findings.\n\nTravel cancellation exceptions must reference the exact travel_cancellation_id and affected expense.\n\nExceptions never establish employee payment, retroactively approve arrangements, or erase original findings.\n\nMaterial replacement-amount changes invalidate dependent claim reviews and payment readiness until current authorization is supplied.\n\nPreserve previously admitted Finance events, cancellation history and immutable snapshots.\n\nUse actual retained source schemas. If a required exception field is absent, retain an unresolved finding instead of inventing authority.\n\nAdd focused positive, negative, stale-version and replay tests. Preserve earlier outputs and all protected source files. Do not modify unrelated budget, approval or closure logic.\n\nRun the complete test suite and Git diff checks. Report findings and any remaining blockers.\n\nDo not stage, commit or push yet. Stop after implementation and verification.","turn_id":"01a13c69-3978-7453-b087-16348d8b1d40"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a13cf2-e30b-71b1-b18d-e233f5194348","order":159,"revision":"retained_01a13cf2-e30e-7490-bdfd-a01ded250e20","text":"Resume Project D Step 175 from the existing uncommitted working tree.\n\nCodex previously reached its usage limit during Finance exception implementation.\n\nDo not restart or overwrite the work.\n\nInspect all existing Step 175 changes, including exceptions.py, test_exceptions.py, retained exception fixtures, ordinary.py and integration.py.\n\nVerify the implementation against POL-2026.2 and the Step 167 audit.\n\nRun the complete test suite after all newly added tests.\n\nRun git diff --check and review the full diff.\n\nVerify the original interview, policy, earlier snapshots, admitted Finance events, cancellation history and previous commits remain unchanged.\n\nIdentify and fix any remaining Step 175 defects without expanding into unrelated budget or closure work.\n\nReport the final test count, changed files and unresolved issues.\n\nDo not stage, commit or push yet.\n\nStop after completing Step 175 implementation verification.","turn_id":"01a13cf2-cebe-70e1-8dae-3f683e534b00"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a13cf6-cbd2-7650-97de-2c660e3ab5a2","order":164,"revision":"retained_01a13cf6-cbd2-7650-97de-2c86ed66263c","text":"Project D — Step 176: Commit and push the verified Step 175 Finance exception milestone.\n\nVerify the current Git branch, status, and complete Step 175 diff.\n\nConfirm the eight changed files are limited to Finance exception handling, supporting integration, documentation, fixtures, and tests.\n\nRerun the complete test suite and Git diff checks.\n\nVerify the 128 preserved files remain unchanged, including the policy, interview, prior outputs, and event-integrity implementation.\n\nStage only these eight reviewed files:\n\nREADME.md\n\nsrc/travel_claim/exceptions.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/expenses.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/ordinary.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/integration.py\n\ntests/test_exceptions.py\n\ntests/test_ordinary.py\n\ntests/fixtures/retained_exception_records.json\n\nCommit with message: feat: validate source-bound finance exceptions\n\nPush normally to origin main without force-pushing.\n\nVerify remote main matches the local commit and all Entire.io checkpoint references match remotely.\n\nDo not stage unrelated audit reports or untracked provenance files.\n\nReport the full commit SHA, passing test count, changed files, and Entire.io verification.\n\nIf any verification fails, stop and report the issue.","turn_id":"01a13cf6-c440-7750-8e5d-543e9f9b5950"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a13cfb-3d1c-7b53-ae27-da9bcea1007a","order":174,"revision":"retained_01a13cfb-3d1c-7b53-ae27-dab4df7774d2","text":"Project D — Step 177: Implement policy-compliant permit and reimbursement approval workflows.\n\nUse the verified POL-2026.2 policy fixture and the Step 167 gap audit.\n\nImplement and test:\n\n    Separate approval subjects for international travel permits and reimbursement claims. Domestic trips require no permit.\n\n    Permit reviews require administration, budget owner, and supervisor, with director review strictly above EUR 1,000 in reviewed estimate.\n\n    Claim reviews require administration, budget owner, and supervisor, with director review strictly above EUR 1,000 in reviewed entitlement.\n\n    Exactly EUR 1,000 does not require director approval.\n\nBudget owner and supervisor may share one response only when the directory identifies the same stable person and the response explicitly covers both roles.\n\nValidate subject type, ID, revision, role, stable actor, source versions, and reason.\n\nReject wrong-role, stale-version, wrong-subject, and unauthorized replies as current authority, while retaining their history.\n\nSupport approve, return-with-repair, reject-with-reason, and clean withdrawal transitions.\n\nMaterial changes invalidate dependent reviews and payment readiness; rebuild readiness from current evidence.\n\nNever treat permit approval as claim approval, or Finance exceptions as retroactive travel authorization.\n\nRequirements:\n\nUse actual retained review packets, decision batches, directory roles, and source references.\n\nPreserve historical decisions and rejected imports.\n\nAdd positive, negative, threshold, correction, and replay tests.\n\nPreserve prior snapshots, admitted financial events, cancellation history, policy, and interview.\n\nDo not modify unrelated budget reconciliation or financial closure logic.\n\nRun the complete test suite and diff checks.\n\nReport unresolved evidence or discretionary human decisions instead of inventing approvals.\n\nDo not stage, commit, or push yet. Stop after implementation and verification.","turn_id":"01a13cfb-36ce-7122-9610-f91773084724"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a13d08-9636-7042-bba6-b25f8a2c000a","order":182,"revision":"retained_01a13d08-9636-7042-bba6-b27f21b73530","text":"Project D — Step 178: Commit and push the verified Step 177 approval workflow milestone.\n\nVerify the current branch, Git status, and complete diff.\n\nConfirm changes are limited to the 11 reviewed Step 177 implementation, documentation, fixture, and test files.\n\nRerun the full test suite and Git diff checks.\n\nVerify all 128 protected files remain unchanged, including the policy, interview, prior snapshots, financial outputs, and event-integrity code.\n\nStage only:\n\nREADME.md\n\nsrc/travel_claim/approvals.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/integration.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/ordinary.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/parsing.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/snapshots.py\n\ntests/test_approvals.py\n\ntests/test_exceptions.py\n\ntests/test_ordinary.py\n\ntests/fixtures/retained_approval_records.json\n\nCommit with message: feat: validate permit and claim approval workflows\n\nPush normally to origin main without force-pushing.\n\nVerify remote main matches the local commit and all Entire.io checkpoint references match remotely.\n\nDo not stage unrelated audit reports or user-provided policy provenance files.\n\nReport the full commit SHA, passing test count, committed files, and Entire.io checkpoint verification.\n\nIf any verification fails, stop and explain the issue.","turn_id":"01a13d08-8eb1-7b30-9180-e04d7a7ded55"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a13d0d-a660-7553-99ec-3d0158a905df","order":193,"revision":"retained_01a13d0d-a661-7250-a286-abec519b8c4f","text":"Project D — Step 179: Implement policy-compliant budget reconciliation.\n\nUse POL-2026.2, the Step 167 gap audit, and the actual retained workbook, claims, reviews, and Finance records.\n\nFirst inspect the exact policy sections governing budgets, prepaid costs, reimbursement obligations, and budget-owner authorization.\n\nImplement and test:\n\nBudget availability and commitments using the policy's actual accounting rules.\n\nCross-claim prepaid-cost attribution without double counting.\n\nCorrections and cancellations that change commitments while preserving financial history.\n\nSource-bound budget identities, amounts, currencies, revisions, and arrival batches.\n\nRevalidation of affected budget-owner approvals after material budget changes.\n\nConflict detection, exact replay deduplication, and unresolved-evidence holds.\n\nSeparate authorized obligations, confirmed payments, refunds, and outstanding balances.\n\nOwner-grouped repair findings with exact source references.\n\nNever invent missing allocations, rates, budgets, approvals, or financial events. Preserve unaffected valid claims and admitted Finance history.\n\nAdd focused synthetic and retained-data tests, including budget exhaustion, cross-claim prepaid costs, corrections, cancellations, and replay.\n\nPreserve the policy, interview, previous snapshots and outputs, and all protected event-integrity modules.\n\nDo not modify unrelated approval, Finance-exception, or closure rules.\n\nRun the complete test suite and diff checks. Report changed files, test results, and unresolved blockers.\n\nDo not stage, commit, or push yet. Stop after implementation and verification.","turn_id":"01a13d0d-9f67-7c00-8955-722676671362"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_01a13d21-b0c1-7f12-bd50-4aeeb77b1bdf","order":201,"revision":"retained_01a13d21-b0c1-7f12-bd50-4b07983b3121","text":"Project D — Step 180: Commit and push the verified Step 179 budget reconciliation milestone.\n\nVerify the current branch, Git status, and complete diff against HEAD 7015dde20ccd6a2327985c0eb26899ecf97c3974.\n\nConfirm the changes are limited to the 12 reviewed Step 179 files.\n\nRerun the full test suite and Git diff checks.\n\nVerify all 129 preserved-file hashes match, including the interview, policy, previous snapshots, outputs, and protected Finance and closure code.\n\nStage only these files:\n\nREADME.md\n\nsrc/travel_claim/budget.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/approvals.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/integration.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/offline_replay.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/ordinary.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/readiness.py\n\nsrc/travel_claim/snapshots.py\n\ntests/test_budget.py\n\ntests/test_approvals.py\n\ntests/test_exceptions.py\n\ntests/fixtures/retained_budget_records.json\n\nCommit with message: feat: reconcile budgets and prepaid cost commitments\n\nPush normally to origin main without force-pushing.\n\nVerify remote main matches the local commit and every Entire.io checkpoint reference matches remotely.","turn_id":"01a13d21-a9c0-7872-9e35-080056b8fba9"}],"user_messages_incomplete":true,"verified_answers":[]},"window_id":"01a13d24-b5ab-71b3-ac52-8b56db440db6","window_number":3}}
