istration/director non-collapse guard. [ordinary.py:100](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/ordinary.py:100); [ordinary.py:219](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/ordinary.py:219); [ordinary.py:236](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/ordinary.py:236). | [test_ordinary.py:241](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/tests/test_ordinary.py:241) tests a synthetic 5000-cent threshold, not permit/claim 100000 boundaries or allowed/forbidden role collapse. |\n| [POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:11](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:11) | Advance-paid filing; inclusive two calendar months; correction dates | **Missing** | Line first-submission dates are extracted, but no two-month/clamped inclusive deadline or submission-after-paid check is executed. Initial filing dates are not compared across revisions; new cost dates are not separately validated. Planned trip end must survive cancellation. [ordinary.py:32](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/ordinary.py:32); [ordinary.py:163](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/ordinary.py:163); [revalidation.py:7](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/revalidation.py:7). | Add 31-August to 31-October, month-end/leap-year, exact deadline/next day, paid-before-travel, late filing with/without exception, unchanged and added-cost dates. |\n| [POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:13](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:13) | Administration checks and full department/project/period budget | **Major missing calculation** | Packets only check that cited budget IDs exist; no allocation minus net settled expenditure minus remaining commitments calculation, ledger scope, pre-batch obligations or accepted-new-request accumulation is performed. Native Budget rows 6–8 contain allocation and prior obligation/settled data. Do not subtract both the full commitment and its settled component. [ordinary.py:213](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/ordinary.py:213). | No full-ledger/no-double-subtraction tests. Budget sufficiency must remain separate from human budget-owner approval. |\n| [POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:13](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:13) | Supervisor/director judgment and review context | **Partial; packet sufficiency gap** | Current packet matching compares trip business fields and expense IDs, but not calculated reviewed entitlement, complete estimate/director basis or full budget snapshot/position. Purpose/client/schedule/alternatives fields are retained. Automation correctly does not invent discretionary judgment. [ordinary.py:220](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/ordinary.py:220). | [test_ordinary.py:192](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/tests/test_ordinary.py:192) checks changed trip facts; add altered reviewed amount, estimate, budget-owner position and full packet source-version checks. |\n| [POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:15](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:15) | Decision subject/version/role/source validation; return/reject/withdrawal | **Partial; state transitions missing** | Claim current revision, roles and stable actor checks exist; rejected imports remain in history. Source revisions, affected fields and reason/repair requirements are not fully validated. Return/reject stop approvals but do not execute reviewer-specific reopening or legitimate rejected/withdrawn nonpayment terminal states. [workflow.py:115](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/workflow.py:115); [ordinary.py:202](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/ordinary.py:202); [ordinary.py:318](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/ordinary.py:318). | [test_ordinary.py:213](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/tests/test_ordinary.py:213) tests conflicting review IDs; add stale source versions,