alues, so a provenance-bound date+zone needs new coverage. Fresh five-location attempts remain a requirement; the copy does not repair earlier captures. |\n| [POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:5](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:5) | Actual paid costs, personal/unknown category, evidence and gross VAT | **Partial; missing personal-zero rule** | Current receipt/settled merchant matching checks employee, trip, cost, currency and gross amount. Gross rather than VAT recovery is used. Unknowns remain null. Personal purchases are treated as unsupported category rather than an explicit zero-entitlement finding; no native-policy eligibility mapping exists. [ordinary.py:125](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/ordinary.py:125); [ordinary.py:168](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/ordinary.py:168). | Identity/proof are covered by [test_ordinary.py:84](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/tests/test_ordinary.py:84) and missing-condition cases at line 135. Add explicit personal zero versus unknown unresolved, gross-tax and category cases. |\n| [POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:7](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:7) | Transport/conference uncapped; lodging/night and meal/day caps | **Partial; integer-unit defect** | Destination/category/currency/payment-date cap lookup and minimum arithmetic exist, but positive integral total_limit is checked instead of integral documented units. A synthetic lodging line with 1.5 units and a 40.00 cap produces 6000 allowed cents. Unknown/multiple rates/caps hold. [ordinary.py:171](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/ordinary.py:171). | [test_ordinary.py:221](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/tests/test_ordinary.py:221) tests a synthetic capped transport rule, not the native category/unit contract. Add lodging/meals, positive integers, missing caps and effective-date boundaries. |\n| [POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:7](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:7) | Payment-date FX, EUR=1, line half-up conversion and rounded-line sum | **Defect** | FX lookup is payment-date based, but EUR still requires an FX row. Conversion rejects fractional cents instead of decimal half-up rounding. Synthetic 100.00 USD at 1.23455 has matched evidence but no allowed amount; policy requires 12346 cents. Summation exists only after exact-integer conversions. [ordinary.py:184](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/ordinary.py:184); [finance.py:40](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_…11967 tokens truncated…y eligibility, approvals, financial closure, full native assignment compliance, or fresh execution from replay artifacts.\n   127\t\n   128\t## Current implementation boundary\n   129\t\n   130\tThe implementation supports fresh source capture, byte-bound manifests, loss-aware transcription, schema/hash-checked snapshots, policy-neutral arrival-ordered replay, source-classified Finance reconciliation, exact CSV output, and local owner-grouped repair tracking. `offline-replay` is a structural replay only: the inaccessible reimbursement policy and unconfirmed case clock keep policy conclusions, approval readiness, entitlement, and closure unresolved. Human replies are not imported automatically, and the command never sends repair drafts or moves money. Do not treat an offline replay as a fresh source read or completed claim processing.\n   131\t\n   132\tIf native evidence is unavailable or a business definition conflicts, record the affected scope and escalate to the exercise operator. People retain approval, exception, and payment authority. This tooling never sends requests, books travel, or moves money.\n   133\t\n   134\t## Step 157: correction and independent cancellation rechecks\n   135\t\n   136\tEvery corrected revision executes the connected evidence, calculation, trip/permit, human-review, request and Finance checks again. `material_corrections` retains changed field and expense-line facts, unchanged cost identities, excluded historical decisions, before-state evidence, and each executed batch result. A changed receipt invalidates readiness even when the amount is unchanged. Cash events and prior revision history remain intact; a passed receipt recheck cannot manufacture new approvals or current request authority.\n   137\t\n   138\t`correction-cancellation-verification.json` and `.md` demonstrate all retained corrections and independent trip/permit processes with source references, before/after cash facts, executed check results and next actions. They are explicitly retained-input offline outputs. The readiness command compares these artifacts with a deterministic replay and checks the sealed snapshot chain.\n   139\t\n   140\tCancellation processing preserves the first event delivery, duplicate deliveries, employee/supervisor evidence, initiation/confirmation chronology, historical versus current claim links, and observed Finance request IDs. Orphan or partial confirmations remain unresolved with owned repair actions. Linked requests are held; unrelated claims continue. Explicit cancellation-bound Finance exceptions are recorded separately from policy eligibility and financial completion. A transfer cancellation never counts as a cash refund. Unknown disposition, approval, policy, case clock or closure authority remains blocked; absence of a claim does not imply absence of financial effects.\n   141\t\n   142\t## Fresh native-source acquisition and transcription\n   143\t\n   144\t```bash\n   145\ttravel-claim live-run <new-run-id> artifacts/runs/<new-run-id> [--case-clock '<authoritative scenario timestamp>']\n   146\t```\n   147\t\n   148\t`live-run` attempts all five original locations using direct HTTP and native Google PDF/XLSX export routes, then verifies the manifest and transcribes accessible content from **this invocation**. It accepts no prior-run or cache input. Every run requires a new empty directory; existing manifests, parsed inputs, response files and snapshots cannot be reused. The optional clock is caller-supplied scenario evidence; retrieval timestamps never become a case clock.\n   149\t\n   150\tNew captures use `native-source-manifest/2`. Each entry records the original source identity/URL, attempted export URL, redirect destination, HTTP status, start/end UTC observations, ETag or Last-Modified when supplied, content hash/version, accessible scope, error and missing scope. Complete response bodies are retained verbatim under `responses/`, including error pages and unusable shells; usable complete or partial documents are also bound under `sources/`. The verifier checks hashes, scope/status consistency and fresh response bindings. Legacy `/1` manifests remain readable for historical replay; they do not gain fresh-access evidence.\n   151\t\n   152\tA `read` PDF must be structurally readable with extractable text on every page. Scanned or partially readable documents require further verification. XLSX exports must contain all ten known workbook tabs; all returned bytes, tab content, cell values and numeric source evidence remain retained. Partial HTTP responses, mismatched byte counts, corrupt documents and incomplete workbook exports cannot pass complete acquisition. Usable partial sources are transcribed independently, with missing scope retained. Malformed arrival membership is reported without rounding or supplying a default.\n   153\t\n   154\tPlain HTTP access to a Notion shell does not establish policy access. Even policy-related HTML is marked **partial** because this reader cannot establish the complete authoritative block tree. The current reader has no authenticated Notion API/browser/export adapter. Complete policy access and policy rule interpretation remain required before policy-dependent execution; source bytes are never replaced by interview-derived rules or earlier downloads.\n   155\t\n   156\t`live-run.json` and `live-run.md` distinguish acquisition status from final business compliance. Exit `2` means **BLOCKED** (source access, transcription, clock or policy processing remains incomplete); exit `1` means **FAIL** for integrity/execution errors. The command performs fresh acquisition and loss-aware transcription, but does not consume arrival batches or certify final live-source claim compliance. The separate `offline-replay` command remains explicitly labeled retained-input evaluation. A successful `verify-sources` establishes integrity of recorded evidence, including failure observations, rather than completeness of all five sources.\n   157\t\n   158\t## Step 171: event integrity admission\n   159\t\n   160\tFinance reconciliation now retains an immutable `admitted_events` ledger separately from raw deliveries. Exact replay has no cash effect; later conflicting payloads retain admitted money and event references while opening a Finance hold. New admissions require source-bound request/payee/currency and directory Finance authority, exact positive cash cents, and a valid observed UTC time. Invalid and unmatched deliveries remain visible. Legacy reconciliation state containing counted cash but no admission ledger requires explicit verified migration; it cannot silently become zero.\n   161\t\n   162\tIndependent cancellation admission checks the trip employee and directory supervisor, exact initiation/process/trip/permit binding, current target revision, strictly increasing UTC occurrence and effective time equal to confirmation occurrence. Invalid or conflicting deliveries do not overwrite admitted history, and deferred references are rechecked when initiation arrives. Business cancellation produces no Finance event or cash effect.\n   163\t\n   164\tCallers supply the admission cutoff explicitly via `event_clock` (an offset-bearing timestamp, or `{\"date\": \"2026-11-15\", \"timezone\": \"Europe/Amsterdam\"}` from verified POL-2026.2 line 3). A date-only clock permits unambiguously earlier local dates; observations on the case date remain held without a supplied cutoff instant. No current-system-time, midnight or end-of-day default is used. This admission context does not change the separate eligibility, approval or closure rule implementation, and earlier outputs are never rewritten.\n   165\t\n   166\t## Step 173: paid-expense calculations and filing dates\n   167\t\n   168\t`travel_claim.expenses.load_expense_policy(path)` verifies the complete, exact\n   169\tPOL-2026.2 browser copy against the user-supplied SHA-256. Explicitly attach its\n   170\treturned binding as `parsed['expense_policy']` before calling the arrival-batch\n   171\tintegrator. The binding (including original text, hash, path and browser-copy\n   172\tprovenance) participates in replay identity. No policy is silently loaded from\n   173\tan old run, and failed native Notion observations remain unchanged. The exact\n   174\tbrowser copy is also retained byte-for-byte as a regression-test fixture.\n   175\t\n   176\tEach ordinary workflow now retains `expense_calculation`, line-level conversion\n   177\tevidence and an owned `filing_deadline` check. Matching receipt and deduplicated,\n   178\tsettled employee merchant payments establish cost; destination/currency/payment-date\n   179\tcaps apply only to lodging and meals with positive integer units. Transport and\n   180\tconference are uncapped; supported personal purchases yield zero. EUR uses 1;\n   181\tother currencies require the exact payment-date Finance rate. Decimal half-up\n   182\trounding occurs per line before summation. Missing or conflicting evidence,\n   183\tunknown categories, caps and rates remain unresolved; independent valid line\n   184\tcalculations survive a blocked claim total. Calculated amounts do not establish\n   185\tapproval, entitlement authorization, a payment event or closure.\n   186\t\n   187\tDeadlines add two calendar months to the trip end, clamp nonexistent days, and\n   188\tinclude the final day. Filing must follow established employee payment, but may\n   189\tprecede travel. Unchanged cost history retains its initial source submission;\n   190\tnew costs use their own first-submission evidence, never import time. Late filing\n   191\tretains its original finding and requires an explicit directory-Finance,\n   192\tclaim/revision/cost-bound exception covering late filing. Amount-only exceptions\n   193\tcannot waive lateness. An exception changing the calculated amount remains held\n   194\tfor separate replacement-amount review; this milestone does not implement general\n   195\texception eligibility. Multiple payment dates for one expense likewise remain\n   196\theld pending source-supported allocation, rather than choosing an FX date or cap.\n   197\tExisting permission, human approval and financial closure authority requirements\n   198\tremain in force. No earlier run is regenerated by loading this module.\n   199\t\n   200\t## Step 175: Finance exception evidence and revalidation\n   201\t\n   202\tThe verified browser policy binding now supports the native claim-page exception\n   203\tfields: `Authorizing Finance officer`, `Applies to claim`, `Applies to revision`,\n   204\t`Expense reference`, `Allowed original amount`, `Exception reason`, and\n   205\t`Covered issues`. The exception and employee directory must have retained source\n   206\thash/locator bindings; the actor must match the directory Finance officer. The\n   207\treplacement amount is in the exact bound expense's original currency and uses\n   208\tits established payment-date FX conversion. Original gross, ordinary calculated\n   209\tamount, exception wording/references and conversion evidence remain available.\n   210\tMissing, invalid, ambiguous or stale exception authority holds the affected claim.\n   211\t\n   212\tOnly exact policy issue codes or their explicit native PDF display labels are\n   213\trecognized. Native `None` and an explicit empty list mean amount-only coverage;\n   214\ta missing field, unknown label or substring match never waives eligibility.\n   215\tEach cost retains separate original findings for `late_filing`, `late_permit`,\n   216\t`permit_unapproved`, and each `travel_cancellation_id`. Cancellation coverage\n   217\trequires `Travel cancellation reference` to identify the exact current process\n   218\tand affected expense. Independent findings become separate owned repair items.\n   219\tA covered finding remains recorded as `covered_for_reimbursement`; it does not\n   220\tbecome a business approval, a confirmed cancellation, employee payment, or cash.\n   221\t\n   222\tReplacement amount changes require current revision/source-bound claim reviews\n   223\tand matching request/Finance authorization. Earlier reviews remain historical.\n   224\tSame-revision material source changes retain a hold across later batches until\n   225\treview evidence identifies the changed retained source, rather than its unchanged\n   226\tprinted binder version alone. Admitted Finance events and cancellation history\n   227\tare preserved. The earlier Step 173 replacement-amount hold is superseded by\n   228\tthese checks; unrelated budget, role and financial closure gates remain in force.\n   229\tIn particular this milestone does not remove the existing blanket closure hold\n   230\tfor linked cancellations or repair the separate native permission/closure paths.\n   231\tSame-day permit approvals versus date-only commitments retain an unresolved\n   232\tordering finding; no time of day is invented.\n   233\t\n   234\t`tests/fixtures/retained_exception_records.json` contains verbatim selected C12,\n   235\tC19 and C121 claim/receipt/workbook records from the retained live attempt, with\n   236\toriginal hashes and page/row locators. These tests validate exception application,\n   237\tnot new approvals, fresh source retrieval or real claim closure. Synthetic tests\n   238\texercise authorization recovery, stale versions, conflicts and exact replay.\n   239\t\n   240\t## Step 177: separate permit and reimbursement approvals\n   241\t\n   242\t`travel_claim.approvals` evaluates supplied review ledger replies, packets and\n   243\tdirectory actors against the verified POL-2026.2 browser binding. International\n   244\tpermits review the trip estimate; claims independently review calculated\n   245\treimbursement entitlement. Administration, budget owner and supervisor are\n   246\trequired; director is additional strictly above EUR 1,000.00. Exactly EUR\n   247\t1,000.00 does not require a director. Only the directory's same budget owner and\n   248\tsupervisor may combine one reply explicitly naming both roles. Domestic travel\n   249\trequires no permit. No discretionary decision is generated.\n   250\t\n   251\tEvery considered delivery retains its raw row, source/page/row references and\n   252\tvalidation result, including wrong actors, wrong subjects, stale revisions,\n   253\tmissing reasons, conflicting IDs and duplicate deliveries. Current authority\n   254\trequires matching source versions and review packet facts. Exact replay adds\n   255\tno authority. Returns retain a concrete employee repair action; later supplied\n   256\tcurrent approval can supersede a return by decision time, rather than import\n   257\torder. Rejection reasons and employee withdrawals are business outcomes, not\n   258\tconfirmation of financial closure. Only source-supported clean cases without\n   259\trequests, obligations or cash history receive `rejected`/`withdrawn`; existing\n   260\tfinancial effects stay held for Finance disposition.\n   261\t\n   262\tCurrent claim workflows retain `claim_approval` and `permit_approval`. Independent\n   263\tpermit evaluations also appear in `permit_approvals` in new snapshots and replay\n   264\tstate, including permits without claims. Newly parsed workbooks retain exact\n   265\tpreamble cells so printed source versions are evidenced rather than inferred.\n   266\tHistorical parsed inputs without sufficient source-version evidence remain\n   267\tblocked; earlier captures are not silently enriched or rewritten. The snapshot\n   268\twriter accepts this optional evidence while preserving legacy snapshots.\n   269\t\n   270\tMaterial trip, expense/evidence, amount, policy-source or directory changes\n   271\tinvalidate affected readiness. Same-revision changes require fresh, explicitly\n   272\tsource-bound replies from the changed evidence batch onward; new revisions cannot\n   273\treuse historical replies. Source-bound Finance exceptions only resolve their\n   274\tspecified reimbursement findings; they never approve travel arrangements.\n   275\tCurrent-basis cancellation holds arrangement authority without deleting timely\n   276\thistorical permit decisions. Same-day approval/commitment ordering remains\n   277\tunconfirmed when only a commitment date is supplied.\n   278\t\n   279\tThe retained approval fixture includes actual C01/C02/C09/C13/C14/C21/C46\n   280\tclaim, permit, directory and packet records with original references. C02's\n   281\tEUR 1,100 permit estimate and USD 600 claim illustrate the independent thresholds.\n   282\tFull budget reconciliation, broader native entitlement/request adaptation and\n   283\tfinancial closure remain separate implementation boundaries. No earlier output\n   284\tis regenerated by these changes.\n   285\t\n   286\t## Step 179: budget reconciliation and prior-cost obligations\n   287\t\n   288\tNew snapshots and replay state retain `budget_reconciliation` and a budget\n   289\thistory. The native Budget headers explicitly specify EUR. Scope is the exact\n   290\tPeople/Budget department, project and budget period. Opening ledger identities\n   291\tremain source-version bound; missing native row revision or arrival fields stay\n   292\tnull. Exact replay is inert, conflicting identities hold the affected scope and\n   293\tretain admitted opening facts, and a verified replacement source version retains\n   294\tprior history. Raw budget deliveries, including invalid entries, remain visible.\n   295\t\n   296\tAvailability is allocation minus net settled expenditure minus remaining\n   297\tcommitments. Remaining commitment is `max(commitment - net paid, 0)`; a commitment\n   298\talready includes its settled portion. The supplied opening EUR 20,000 allocation,\n   299\tEUR 3,000 obligation with EUR 2,000 settled, and EUR 2,000 unsettled obligation\n   300\ttherefore leave EUR 15,000 before new requests. Stable accepted request IDs are\n   301\tcounted once, including requests outside the current batch. Overlapping opening\n   302\tsummaries and event histories must agree or remain held. Budget calculations read\n   303\tonly the protected Finance admission ledger: accepted/adjusted request amounts,\n   304\tconfirmed payments and linked refunds stay distinct from current authorized\n   305\treimbursement obligations and outstanding balances. Refunds do not silently\n   306\tcancel an outstanding commitment. Business cancellations release no Finance\n   307\tcommitment; only admitted request-bound Finance controls change it, and late\n   308\tpayments remain expenditure after cancellation.\n   309\t\n   310\tCross-claim cost attribution requires matching employee, trip, cost, receipt,\n   311\tcurrency and gross evidence, explicit earlier-claim linkage, and an exactly\n   312\tsupported request allocation. No proportional allocation is invented for an\n   313\tambiguous aggregate or partial per-cost settlement. Previously committed/paid\n   314\tcosts are excluded from the new request while original gross and conversion\n   315\tfacts remain intact. Retained C24 explicitly links C03: its EUR 200 COST-03 is\n   316\talready attributed to REQ-C03, leaving EUR 50 for COST-24. An old commitment for\n   317\ta different cost cannot offset a corrected claim's new cost. These are ledger\n   318\tand calculation facts, not newly supplied approvals or real claim closure.\n   319\t\n   320\tFunds alone never constitute budget-owner approval. Budget-role packets must\n   321\treference the whole opening scope ledger; later accepted requests, Finance\n   322\tadjustments and material budget-source changes require a current source-bound\n   323\tbudget-owner response. Other review roles retain their existing validation.\n   324\tPermit estimates remain forecasts, not invented accepted obligations. Missing\n   325\tallocations, scope mappings, evidence or cost attribution remain unresolved, and\n   326\towner-grouped repair findings retain exact claim/version and source references.\n   327\tUnrelated scopes continue independently. The report displays scope balances and\n   328\tprepaid links; readiness compares budget state/history with deterministic replay.\n   329\tNative request authorization, Finance exceptions and financial closure rules\n   330\tremain separate gates. Earlier policy/interview files and run artifacts are not\n   331\trewritten.\n"},"started_at_ms":1792027639166,"completed_at_ms":1792027639222}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-15T01:27:20.180Z","ordinal":3613,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a13bd1-7420-72c0-963e-58742d1be7bf","turn_id":"01a13d2b-8824-73d0-88b5-8e9d7fe27356","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4884cbda-a3d1-463d-ae45-c2f28d15a232","process_id":"51716","command":["/bin/bash","-lc","rg -n 'assignment|Project D|claims.csv|report.md|complete|four|batch|closure|final|Finance' interviews/project-d-travel-expense-claim-20261013-2210.md | tail -75; nl -ba src/travel_claim/ordinary.py | sed -n '165,345p'; nl -ba src/travel_claim/cli.py"],"cwd":"file:///home/maxg/travel-expense-claim","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'assignment|Project D|claims.csv|report.md|complete|four|batch|closure|final|Finance' interviews/project-d-travel-expense-claim-20261013-2210.md","query":"assignment|Project D|claims.csv|report.md|complete|four|batch|closure|final|Finance","path":"project-d-travel-expense-claim-20261013-2210.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba src/travel_claim/ordinary.py","name":"ordinary.py","path":"src/travel_claim/ordinary.py"},{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba src/travel_claim/cli.py","name":"cli.py","path":"src/travel_claim/cli.py"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"1:# Project D — Travel Expense Claim Interview\n13:I coordinate travel reimbursements at Alderbridge. Much of my time goes into checking evidence, chasing reviews, and finding out what Finance actually paid, especially when a claim changes. I would like help making the whole process repeatable. You can ask me about how we work, policy, the records we use, or the problems that keep coming back.\n43:When there are exceptions, like for late filings or specific amount limits, we need a Finance exception. This official exception is issued by Finance for a specific claim version to resolve a set issue, like late filing or an unapproved permit. However, it doesn't waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\n47:When you say Finance, is that a department?\n51:Yes, Finance refers to our financial department. They are responsible for issuing monetary tables like currency rates and spending caps, providing official exceptions for policy issues, and handling actual payment execution and reconciliation for claims.\n87:If a receipt is lost, the employee must provide alternative evidence or an explanation, but since Finance cannot waive missing receipts, the claim will remain unresolved until the evidence is provided.\n109:Financial activities include the pending, failed, or settled outcomes of payment requests, as well as accepted commitments, adjustments, refunds, and cancellations. These are all tracked and owned by the Finance department.\n117:Cancellations can target an entire trip or just a permit version independently of a claim. They must be initiated by the employee and confirmed by the supervisor, and these actions are tracked in the Travel cancellations workbook. If there were paid costs or Finance commitments, Finance will need to issue a specific disposition and resolve the money separately.\n125:Finance will issue a specific disposition bound to the cancellation ID, which confirms the reimbursement eligibility and provides a new allowed amount and reason for the affected costs.\n135:Yes, limits apply to specific categories. Lodging and meals are limited by daily or nightly caps set by Finance, based on the destination and date, which are then multiplied by the documented duration. Transport and conference expenses are not subject to these caps.\n143:The limits for lodging and meals are determined by daily or nightly caps set by Finance, based on your destination, expense currency, and the payment date. You can see these metrics in the Caps tab of the Travel registers workbook.\n153:How do incomplete claims affect independent work?\n157:Incomplete claims are held while the missing facts are addressed. You can continue processing independent claims separately while others are held, as long as the business impact is made clear.\n173:The available actions include requesting missing evidence from the employee, seeking an official exception from Finance for specific issues, or holding the claim until Finance confirms the resolution or provides the missing definitions.\n177:On average, how long does it take Finance to confirm resolution or provide the missing definitions?\n181:I don't have a set average for Finance response times. Their replies come in batches, and the time it takes depends on the volume and complexity of the request.\n185:When was the most recent time a Finance needed to confirm resolution that you can remember?\n189:I don't track specific dates for those resolutions in my head. Our Finance replies are delivered in versioned batches, and we process the needed resolutions as they arrive based on the specific claims and costs.\n193:How many people are in a batch?\n197:The batch size isn't fixed; it depends on the number of claims, requests, or reviewer replies being processed by Finance or the relevant budget owner at that time.\n201:How are batches organized? For example, could they be organized by a time slot or with a certain amount of people inside?\n213:I don't assign claims to a trainer. The replies you see come from versioned batches provided by Finance or other appropriate reviewers based on the business workflow.\n221:I don't have information about trainers. My work focuses on coordinating with the Finance department, budget owners, supervisors, and employees to process travel claims.\n229:I don't have information about trainers. My role is Travel Administration Lead, and the replies I receive come from Finance, budget owners, supervisors, and directors within the established business workflow.\n233:Tell me about the boundaries of Finance.\n237:Finance owns setting currency rates, managing spending caps, and issuing official policy exceptions. They also execute payments and resolve any monetary issues or cancellations, but they cannot waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\n245:Budget owners have the authority to approve, return, or reject a claim based on the complete department ledger. They assess funding availability and make discretionary decisions, which I receive in supplied reviewer replies.\n269:Directors provide an additional layer of authorization for high-spend situations, typically when the reviewed claim entitlement or permit estimate exceeds EUR 1,000.00. They evaluate the business necessity, exceptions, and alternatives, and their decisions arrive in supplied reply batches.\n285:Financial completion requires that current approvals match the reviewed entitlement, net confirmed payments equal the authorized amount, no issues remain, and all required Finance resolutions have been received.\n301:The accepted delivery scope is confirmed when the current approvals and reviewed entitlement agree with the net confirmed payment, and all required Finance resolutions have been received with no remaining issues.\n309:Issues refer to unresolved problems like missing receipts, incomplete payment proof, late filings, or mismatched data. For repair work, constraints involve organizing the missing evidence into usable local tasks, retaining the subject and revision, identifying the responsible owner, and ensuring corrections go through required reviews.\n341:Yes, cases can be placed on hold for missing facts or Finance resolutions, but they cannot be closed or considered complete until all required evidence and decisions are obtained.\n373:I communicate through formal requests and notifications. These include the subject type, IDs, stable role requesters, and relevant source versions, and I wait for replies from the authorized reviewers and Finance.\n377:Let me summarize to make sure I understand: the system route work based on four distinct human authority profiles: supervisors, budget owners, directors, and Finance.\n389:Hello! I coordinate travel reimbursements at Alderbridge. Much of my time goes into checking evidence, chasing reviews, and finding out what Finance actually paid, especially when a claim changes. You can ask me about how we work, our policy, the records we use, or the problems that keep coming back.\n397:The ordinary cycle begins when an employee pays for a travel cost and submits a claim. I review the claim against the trip permits, receipts, and merchant payments to calculate the reviewed entitlement. Then, I coordinate the necessary approvals based on the amount and policy, submit the request to Finance for transfer, and reconcile the payments until the case is closed.\n413:When you submit the request to Finance for transfer. what type of files or formats do you submit?\n425:Funding commitments are established when Finance accepts the reimbursement request, confirming the obligation and reserving the funds for budget tracking.\n433:When a cancellation occurs, the valid confirmation pauses payment readiness but does not erase the Finance commitment. If the original permit was lawful before arrangements, it remains lawful, and we record a specific cancellation issue rather than invalidating the permit.\n473:For international permits, I verify administrative completeness, then obtain reviews from the budget owner and supervisor. If the estimated cost is over one thousand euros, a director must also approve the permit before any travel arrangements are made.\n481:I match Finance outcomes against the authorized obligation for each claim. I calculate net paid by taking confirmed transfers minus any refunds, and compare that to the authorized amount to find the remaining balance or identify any overpayments requiring resolution.\n489:Common errors include missing receipts or payment proof, conflicting data like mismatched amounts or currencies, late filings, and unrecognized transactions that require Finance to resolve.\n493:When Finance resolves it, do they give you a piece of data so you can keep filling out your report?\n497:Yes, Finance provides formal records like eligibility exceptions or resolution events that include the covered issues, authorized amounts, and specific reason codes for the claim version.\n501:Is there ever a case where Finance can't resolve it and it becomes unresolved?\n505:Yes, if a required piece of evidence, such as a receipt or proof of payment, is persistently missing or a policy definition is unavailable, Finance cannot issue a resolution, and the item remains unresolved until the correct data is provided.\n529:Our business sources include the travel reimbursement policy, trip and permit records, expense claim forms paired with their receipts, and Finance activity logs for transfers and obligations.\n537:I coordinate with the exercise operator for policy definition gaps and with Finance for monetary exceptions, ensuring all data is resolved before any claims can move forward.\n571:Yes, exactly. Items like specific receipts, detailed expense claims, and Finance transaction logs are accessed directly from the official external registries during your case review.\n587:That is precisely correct. Every claim involves receiving the submission, validating all evidence and calculations, applying the policy rules, awaiting the necessary human approvals, and finally reconciling the payments for closure.\n599:What part of the workflow becomes the most complicated among batches rather than working with just individual case by case?\n603:Reconciling multiple batches becomes complicated when tracking Finance outcomes, such as partial payments or late transfers, across various batches and different versions of a claim.\n607:Is there a limit to how many batches you can handle at one time?\n611:There is no fixed limit on the number of batches I can process at once. The main challenge is carefully matching transaction IDs and amounts across all historical records and versions.\n619:Yes, we access several types of historical records, including previous claim versions, original receipt cards, past approval decisions, and historical Finance events like prior payments or adjustments.\n627:Authority for financial payments, settlements, and eligibility exceptions always rests with Finance, as they are the sole authority for monetary transfers and resolutions.\n631:What happens when Finance has their own expense travel claims?\n635:All employees, including those in Finance, follow the exact same reimbursement policy and workflow. Finance personnel still need reviews from budget owners, supervisors, and directors for their claims, depending on the amount and travel type.\n639:Is Finance allowed to handle their own files and cases?\n643:To maintain impartiality, Finance personnel cannot approve their own claims; they must still go through the required budget owner, supervisor, and director reviews based on the amount.\n667:Reimbursement caps for categories like lodging and meals are defined periodically by Finance, taking specific costs into account as set in the annual policy.\n720:Exactly. A budget rejection is a funding decision regarding entitlement, not a payment execution failure. It is documented as a rejection with its specific reason, separate from any Finance transfer issues.\n724:So, in the case of a payment execution failure, what types of codes or labels does Finance use?\n728:Finance provides specific outcome labels such as \"failed,\" \"pending,\" or \"cancelled\" in the Finance activity log. These indicate the status of the monetary transfer rather than a decision on the claim's entitlement.\n752:The operational sources are designed to be complementary and consistent. Each serves a different purpose in the workflow, such as policy definitions or payment records, and together they provide a complete case record.\n756:Does that ever lead to partial reviewer or Finance with replies with outdated revisions?\n768:It varies depending on when the reviewer or Finance processes the request, but I do not track the specific frequency, as my focus is on verifying each individual case.\n772:Tell me about a situation on how an agent should handle when Finance replies from an old claim version after an employee already submitted a correct version.\n776:When Finance replies for an outdated version, we reject that response since it isn't current authorization. We retain that record in the history but do not apply it to the new claim, simply waiting for the reply that matches the correct claim revision.\n792:No, core evidence such as a receipt or settled merchant payment cannot be marked as resolved if it is missing. Those are structural requirements under the policy, and the claim must be held until the required evidence or an explicit Finance exception is provided.\n796:To make sure I understand this, I want to summarize: an incoming batch component either there's a decision/reply input or a new claim correction, and if it's a decision/reply input, it's checking the version is current, whereas a new claim correction increments revisions and wipes downstream approvals.\n800:That is correct. Incoming batches contain either reviewer decisions or claim corrections; decisions must match the current revision, while corrections increment revisions and necessitate re-evaluation of subsequent approvals.\n   165\t    stage('policy_eligibility', policy_ok, policy_refs + evidence_refs,\n   166\t          'Expense calculation and filing are separate from travel permission, reviewed policy definitions and approvals',\n   167\t          lead, 'Resolve line findings and remaining policy/permission evidence before treating calculated amounts as entitlement')\n   168\t\n   169\t    for line in lines:\n   170\t        exception = line['exception']\n   171\t        if exception['status'] != 'absent':\n   172\t            stage(f\"finance_exception:{line['cost_id']}\", exception['status'] == 'valid', line['source_refs'],\n   173\t                  exception.get('reason', 'Source-bound Finance exception'), finance_owner,\n   174\t                  'Supply exact Finance actor, current claim/revision/cost, replacement amount, reason and covered issues')\n   175\t        for item in line['eligibility_findings']:\n   176\t            name = f\"eligibility:{line['cost_id']}:{item['issue']}\" + (f\":{item['travel_cancellation_id']}\" if item.get('travel_cancellation_id') else '')\n   177\t            stage(name, item['status'] == 'covered_for_reimbursement', item['source_refs'] + item['exception_source_refs'],\n   178\t                  item['original_finding'] + '; ' + item['status'], finance_owner,\n   179\t                  'Obtain explicit Finance coverage for this exact eligibility finding and affected expense; retain original arrangement history')\n   180\t\n   181\t    prior_lines = {l['cost_id']: l for l in (prior_workflow or {}).get('lines', [])}\n   182\t    def changed_exception_amount(line):\n   183\t        old = prior_lines.get(line['cost_id'], {})\n   184\t        before = old.get('conversion', {}).get('allowed_original_amount')\n   185\t        after = line.get('conversion', {}).get('allowed_original_amount')\n   186\t        # Unknown-to-known evidence and decimal display precision are not proof\n   187\t        # of a material replacement-amount change.\n   188\t        return bool(before is not None and after is not None\n   189\t            and (line.get('exception', {}).get('status') == 'valid' or old.get('exception', {}).get('status') == 'valid')\n   190\t            and Decimal(before) != Decimal(after))\n   191\t    same_revision_change = bool(prior_workflow and prior_workflow.get('revision') == revision and (\n   192\t        any(changed_exception_amount(line) for line in lines)\n   193\t        or prior_workflow.get('exception_revalidation', {}).get('same_revision_change')))\n   194\t    replacement_review = same_revision_change or any(\n   195\t        line.get('replacement_amount_changed') or changed_exception_amount(line) for line in lines)\n   196\t    line_refs={r for line in lines for r in line['source_refs']}\n   197\t    dependencies=[r for key,tab in [('receipts','Receipts'),('merchant_payments','Merchant payments'),('caps','Caps'),('fx_rates','FX')]\n   198\t                  for r in table(parsed,key,tab) if ref(r) in line_refs]\n   199\t    claim_review=evaluate_reviews(parsed=parsed,kind='claim',subject_id=claim_id,revision=revision,\n   200\t        trip_record=trips[0] if len(trips)==1 else {},employee=employee,subject_record=record,\n   201\t        amount_cents=budget_view['remaining_request_cents'] if calculation['status']=='PASS' else None,decisions=decisions,arrival_batch=arrival_batch,\n   202\t        observations=source_observations,cost_ids=[line['cost_id'] for line in lines],\n   203\t        dependency_rows=dependencies,prior=(prior_workflow or {}).get('claim_approval'),\n   204\t        withdrawn=linked and values.get('Status')=='withdrawn' and trusted(record),\n   205\t        cancellation_ids=[f['travel_cancellation_id'] for f in eligibility if f['issue']=='travel_cancellation'],budget_context=budget_view)\n   206\t    observed=claim_review['deliveries']\n   207\t    # Preserve Step 175's extra binding requirement on material Finance replacements.\n   208\t    for decision in observed:\n   209\t        decision['exception_binding_valid']=(not replacement_review or review_binds_exception(\n   210\t            decision['raw_record'],record,same_revision_change=same_revision_change,fields=fields,ref=ref))\n   211\t        if not decision['exception_binding_valid']:\n   212\t            decision['evidence_valid']=False\n   213\t    approvals=claim_review['approved'] and all(d['evidence_valid'] for d in observed if d['active'])\n   214\t    budget_replies=[d for d in observed if 'budget_owner' in d['roles']]\n   215\t    budget_authorized=any(d['active'] and d['evidence_valid'] and d.get('budget_evidence_valid',True) and d['outcome']=='approve' for d in budget_replies)\n   216\t    stage('budget_owner_authorization',budget_authorized,budget_view['source_refs']+[r for d in budget_replies for r in d['source_refs']],\n   217\t        '; '.join(dict.fromkeys(d['budget_revalidation_reason'] for d in budget_replies if d.get('budget_revalidation_reason'))) or 'Current discretionary budget-owner authorization required; funds alone are insufficient',\n   218\t        budget_view['owner'],'Supply a current budget-owner response bound to the complete scope ledger and this claim/version')\n   219\t    review_refs=claim_review['source_refs']\n   220\t    reviews_ok=all(claim_review['role_states'].get(role) not in {'missing','conflicting'} for role in claim_review['required_roles']) and all(d['evidence_valid'] for d in observed if d['active'])\n   221\t    stage('review_evidence',reviews_ok,review_refs,\n   222\t          'Current subject/version/role/actor/source/reason and complete review packets; rejected imports remain in history',\n   223\t          lead,'Supply current source-bound replies and complete packets; answer the concrete return repair requests')\n   224\t    stage('required_approvals',approvals,review_refs + policy_refs,\n   225\t          f\"Claim approval state: {claim_review['state']}; required roles: {', '.join(claim_review['required_roles'])}\",\n   226\t          lead,'Obtain the outstanding current-version human decisions; permit replies never approve a claim')\n   227\t\n   228\t    for reply in observed:\n   229\t        if reply['outcome']=='return' and reply['evidence_valid']:\n   230\t            stage(f\"review_return:{reply['decision_id']}\",not reply['active'],reply['source_refs'],\n   231\t                  f\"{reply['reason']}; repair requested: {reply['repair_requested']}\",employee or 'Employee',reply['repair_requested'])\n   232\t\n   233\t    exception_revalidated = not replacement_review or approvals\n   234\t    stage('exception_revalidation', exception_revalidated, evidence_refs + review_refs,\n   235\t          'Replacement amounts require current claim reviews bound to the replacement source version; earlier reviews remain historical',\n   236\t          lead, 'Obtain current revision/source-bound reviews of the Finance replacement amount and a matching reimbursement authorization')\n   237\t\n   238\t    requests = [r for r in table(parsed, 'reimbursement_requests', 'Reimbursement requests')\n   239\t                if trusted(r) and visible(r) and fields(r).get('Claim reference') == claim_id and fields(r).get('Revision') == revision]\n   240\t    request = fields(requests[0]) if len(requests) == 1 else {}\n   241\t    obligation = finance.get('recorded_obligation')\n   242\t    approved_ids = {d['decision_id'] for d in observed if d['outcome'] == 'approve' and d['evidence_valid'] and d['active']}\n   243\t    request_ok = bool(linked and reimbursement_permission and policy_ok and approvals and obligation and len(requests) == 1\n   244\t                      and request.get('Request reference') == obligation['request_id']\n   245\t                      and request.get('Payee ID') == person.get('Payee ID') == obligation['payee_id']\n   246\t                      and request.get('Currency') == 'EUR' and _cents(request.get('Amount (EUR)')) == allowed == obligation['amount_cents']\n   247\t                      and obligation['claim_revision'] == revision and obligation['finance_officer'] == finance_owner\n   248\t                      and set(str(request.get('Decision references') or '').splitlines()) == approved_ids\n   249\t                      and bool(approved_ids))\n   250\t    request_refs = [ref(r) for r in requests] + (obligation['source_refs'] if obligation else [])\n   251\t    stage('request_obligation', request_ok, request_refs,\n   252\t          'Recorded request/obligation linkage requires explicit claim revision, payee, amount and approval references; ledger arrival context is not authorization',\n   253\t          finance_owner, 'Provide the exact-revision reimbursement request and Finance acceptance linked to its approvals and authorized amount')\n   254\t    if request_ok:\n   255\t        authorization = dict(amount_cents=allowed, claim_revision=revision, source_refs=request_refs + review_refs + policy_refs)\n   256\t        finance = reconcile_finance_events(finance_events, claim_id=claim_id, current_revision=revision,\n   257\t            revision_history=finance['revision_history'], previous_reconciliation=prior_finance,\n   258\t            authorized_obligation=authorization, source_classifications=source_classifications, event_context=finance.get(\"event_context\"))\n   259\t    reconciled = finance.get('recorded_ledger_balance_cents') is not None and not finance['unresolved_event_ids'] and not finance['conflicting_events']\n   260\t    stage('financial_reconciliation', reconciled,\n   261\t          [ref(e) for e in finance_events if fields(e).get('Claim reference') == claim_id],\n   262\t          f\"Confirmed net cash {finance['net_confirmed_cents']} cents; recorded ledger difference {finance.get('recorded_ledger_balance_cents')}; authorized balance {finance['balance_cents']}\",\n   263\t          finance_owner, 'Resolve missing obligations, conflicting or unclassified events, request/payee links and outstanding balances')\n   264\t\n   265\t    authorities = [r for r in table(parsed, 'closure_authorities', 'Closure authorities') if trusted(r) and visible(r)\n   266\t                   and fields(r).get('Claim reference') == claim_id and fields(r).get('Revision') == revision]\n   267\t    clock_ok = False\n   268\t    try:\n   269\t        clock_ok = datetime.fromisoformat(parsed['case_clock'].replace('Z', '+00:00')).utcoffset() is not None\n   270\t    except (KeyError, ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):\n   271\t        pass\n   272\t    closure_authority = (len(authorities) == 1 and fields(authorities[0]).get('Confirmation') == 'financial-completion-conditions'\n   273\t                         and bool(fields(authorities[0]).get('Authority')) and fields(authorities[0]).get('Case clock') == parsed.get('case_clock'))\n   274\t    external = [i for i in parsed.get('unresolved_issues', []) if i.get('status', 'open') == 'open'\n   275\t                and (i.get('subject_type') in {'policy', 'scenario'} or i.get('subject_id') in {claim_id, trip_id, trip.get('Permit reference')})]\n   276\t    control_events = [e for e in finance['event_history'] if e['classification'] in {\n   277\t        'failed_transfer', 'retry_authorization', 'finance_cancellation_requested', 'finance_cancelled'}]\n   278\t    resolved_controls = set()\n   279\t    def event_stamp(event):\n   280\t        stamp = datetime.fromisoformat(event['source_record']['Activity time (UTC)'].replace('Z', '+00:00'))\n   281\t        return stamp.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc) if stamp.utcoffset() is None else stamp\n   282\t    for event in finance['event_history']:\n   283\t        value = event['source_record']\n   284\t        if (event['classification'] == 'finance_resolution' and value.get('Claim revision') == revision\n   285\t                and obligation and value.get('Request reference') == obligation['request_id']\n   286\t                and value.get('Finance officer') == finance_owner):\n   287\t            named = set(str(value.get('Resolved activity references') or '').splitlines())\n   288\t            for control in control_events:\n   289\t                try:\n   290\t                    if (control['event_id'] in named\n   291\t                            and control['source_record'].get('Request reference') == value['Request reference']\n   292\t                            and event_stamp(event) >= event_stamp(control)):\n   293\t                        resolved_controls.add(control['event_id'])\n   294\t                except (KeyError, ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):\n   295\t                    pass\n   296\t    controls_clear = not finance['pending_transfer_event_ids'] and all(e['event_id'] in resolved_controls for e in control_events)\n   297\t    cancellation_refs = [source for c in affected for source in c.get(\"source_refs\", [])]\n   298\t    stage('cancellation_readiness', not affected, cancellation_refs,\n   299\t          'Linked current or historical trip/permit cancellation requires specific Finance disposition and resolution; prior permission and money history are preserved' if affected else 'No linked cancellation dependency',\n   300\t          finance_owner, 'Verify cancellation-bound disposition, current request authority and monetary resolution before releasing payment readiness')\n   301\t    closed = (all(s['status'] == 'PASS' for s in stages) and controls_clear and request_ok and finance['balance_cents'] == 0\n   302\t              and not finance['repair_issues'] and not affected and clock_ok and closure_authority and not external)\n   303\t    stage('financial_closure', closed, [ref(r) for r in authorities] + request_refs + policy_refs,\n   304\t          'Closure requires supported completion conditions, authoritative clock, current evidence/approvals, entitlement/obligation/net cash agreement and no affected unresolved issue',\n   305\t          finance_owner, 'Confirm completion conditions and the authoritative clock; resolve every affected approval, Finance or cancellation dependency')\n   306\t    business_state=claim_review['state']\n   307\t    financial_clean=(len(trips)==1 and trusted(trips[0]) and not finance.get('recorded_obligation') and not finance['net_confirmed_cents']\n   308\t        and not finance['event_history'] and not requests and not affected)\n   309\t    disposition=business_state if business_state in {'rejected','withdrawn'} and financial_clean else None\n   310\t    if business_state in {'rejected','withdrawn'} and not financial_clean:\n   311\t        stage('nonpayment_disposition',False,review_refs + request_refs,\n   312\t              'Rejection/withdrawal recorded; existing Finance effects require disposition and are not erased',\n   313\t              finance_owner,'Confirm cancellation/status of dispatched obligations and resolve existing cash before financial completion')\n   314\t    pending = next((s for s in stages if s['status'] != 'PASS'), None)\n   315\t    return dict(claim_id=claim_id, revision=revision, trip_id=trip_id, trip_revision=claim.get('trip_revision'),\n   316\t                mode=parsed.get('evidence_mode', 'offline-replay'), status=disposition or ('held' if business_state in {'rejected','withdrawn'} else ('closed-reimbursed' if allowed else 'closed-no-payment') if closed else 'pending'),\n   317\t                claim_approval=claim_review,permit_approval=permit_review,\n   318\t                budget_view=budget_view, expense_calculation=calculation, exception_revalidation=dict(required=replacement_review, same_revision_change=same_revision_change, status='PASS' if exception_revalidated else 'BLOCKED'), allowed_cents=allowed, balance_cents=finance['balance_cents'], lines=lines, stages=stages,\n   319\t                observed_reviews=observed, request=deepcopy(requests[0]) if request_ok else None,\n   320\t                source_refs=list(dict.fromkeys([ref(record)] + [r for s in stages for r in s['source_refs']])),\n   321\t                next_owner=None if closed or disposition else (finance_owner if business_state in {'rejected','withdrawn'} else pending['owner']),\n   322\t                reason=f\"Clean business {disposition}: \" + (values.get('Claim reason','') if disposition=='withdrawn' else '; '.join(d['reason'] for d in observed if d['active'] and d['outcome']=='reject')) if disposition else 'Supported financial closure' if closed else pending['detail'],\n   323\t                finance=finance)\n   324\t\n   325\t\n   326\tdef ordinary_demo(workflows):\n   327\t    \"\"\"Render one observed claim with every stage, owner and retained reference.\"\"\"\n   328\t    claim_id = \"C01\" if \"C01\" in workflows else next(iter(sorted(workflows)), None)\n   329\t    lines = [\"# Connected ordinary claim workflow — OFFLINE REPLAY\", \"\",\n   330\t             \"Retained-input evaluation; no fresh reads, requests, approvals or payments were generated.\", \"\"]\n   331\t    if not claim_id:\n   332\t        return \"\\n\".join(lines + [\"No retained claim available for demonstration.\", \"\"])\n   333\t    workflow = workflows[claim_id]\n   334\t    lines += [f\"Claim `{claim_id}` revision {workflow['revision']}; trip `{workflow['trip_id']}` revision {workflow['trip_revision']}; status **{workflow['status']}**.\", \"\"]\n   335\t    for stage in workflow['stages']:\n   336\t        lines += [f\"## {stage['stage']} — {stage['status']}\", \"\", stage['detail'], \"\",\n   337\t                  f\"Owner: {stage['owner']}. Next action: {stage['next_action']}\", \"\"]\n   338\t        lines.extend(f\"- `{reference}`\" for reference in stage['source_refs'])\n   339\t        lines.append(\"\")\n   340\t    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n     1\t\"\"\"Command-line interface for travel claim tooling.\"\"\"\n     2\t\n     3\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     4\t\n     5\timport argparse\n     6\timport json\n     7\timport sys\n     8\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     9\t\n    10\tfrom jsonschema import Draft202012Validator, FormatChecker\n    11\t\n    12\tfrom .outputs import write_claims_csv\n    13\tfrom .live_run import run_live_sources\n    14\tfrom .offline_replay import run_offline_replay\n    15\tfrom .readiness import readiness_summary, validate_readiness, write_readiness_reports\n    16\tfrom .parsing import parse_retained_run\n    17\tfrom .snapshots import seal_batch_snapshot, verify_snapshot\n    18\tfrom .sources import capture_sources, verify_source_manifest\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\tdef _default_schema_path() -> Path:\n    22\t    \"\"\"Return the repository's authoritative snapshot schema path.\"\"\"\n    23\t    return Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2] / \"snapshot.schema.json\"\n    24\t\n    25\t\n    26\tdef validate_snapshot(snapshot_path: Path, schema_path: Path) -> list[str]:\n    27\t    \"\"\"Return validation errors for a snapshot and schema, or an empty list.\"\"\"\n    28\t    try:\n    29\t        with snapshot_path.open(encoding=\"utf-8\") as snapshot_file:\n    30\t            snapshot = json.load(snapshot_file)\n    31\t    except FileNotFoundError:\n    32\t        return [f\"Snapshot file not found: {snapshot_path}\"]\n    33\t    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n    34\t        return [f\"Could not read snapshot {snapshot_path}: {exc}\"]\n    35\t\n    36\t    try:\n    37\t        with schema_path.open(encoding=\"utf-8\") as schema_file:\n    38\t            schema = json.load(schema_file)\n    39\t    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n    40\t        return [f\"Could not read schema {schema_path}: {exc}\"]\n    41\t\n    42\t    validator = Draft202012Validator(schema, format_checker=FormatChecker())\n    43\t    errors = sorted(validator.iter_errors(snapshot), key=lambda error: list(map(str, error.absolute_path)))\n    44\t    return [\n    45\t        f\"{'.'.join(map(str, error.absolute_path)) or '<root>'}: {error.message}\"\n    46\t        for error in errors\n    47\t    ]\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\tdef build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n    51\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog=\"travel-claim\")\n    52\t    commands = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", required=True)\n    53\t\n    54\t    validate = commands.add_parser(\n    55\t        \"validate-snapshot\", help=\"validate a JSON snapshot against snapshot.schema.json\"\n    56\t    )\n    57\t    validate.add_argument(\"snapshot\", type=Path, help=\"path to the snapshot JSON file\")\n    58\t    validate.add_argument(\n    59\t        \"--schema\", type=Path, default=_default_schema_path(), help=\"schema JSON path\"\n    60\t    )\n    61\t\n    62\t    capture = commands.add_parser(\"capture-sources\", help=\"freshly retrieve and retain all five native sources\")\n    63\t    capture.add_argument(\"run_id\", help=\"new, stable run identifier\")\n    64\t    capture.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path, help=\"new artifacts/runs/<run-id> directory\")\n    65\t    capture.add_argument(\"--case-clock\", help=\"supplied scenario clock; omit only for source-only capture\")\n    66\t\n    67\t    live = commands.add_parser(\"live-run\", help=\"freshly attempt all five sources, retain and transcribe; report blockers without offline fallback\")\n    68\t    live.add_argument(\"run_id\")\n    69\t    live.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path)\n    70\t    live.add_argument(\"--case-clock\", help=\"explicit authoritative scenario clock; never inferred from retrieval time\")\n    71\t    live.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=float, default=30.0, help=\"per-request timeout seconds\")\n    72\t\n    73\t    verify_sources = commands.add_parser(\"verify-sources\", help=\"verify source manifest and retained-byte hashes\")\n    74\t    verify_sources.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path)\n    75\t\n    76\t    parse_sources = commands.add_parser(\"parse-retained\", help=\"transcribe hash-verified PDFs and workbook into traceable records\")\n    77\t    parse_sources.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path)\n    78\t    parse_sources.add_argument(\"--output\", type=Path, help=\"optional new output path; defaults to parsed-records.json in the run\")\n    79\t\n    80\t    seal = commands.add_parser(\"seal-batch\", help=\"schema-check and immutably seal one batch state JSON\")\n    81\t    seal.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path)\n    82\t    seal.add_argument(\"batch_id\")\n    83\t    seal.add_argument(\"state\", type=Path, help=\"JSON object containing claims, requests, cancellations, events, issues\")\n    84\t    seal.add_argument(\"--run-id\", required=True)\n    85\t    seal.add_argument(\"--predecessor\", type=Path)\n    86\t    seal.add_argument(\"--schema\", type=Path, default=_default_schema_path())\n    87\t\n    88\t    verify_batch = commands.add_parser(\"verify-batch\", help=\"verify schema and source/predecessor bindings\")\n    89\t    verify_batch.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path)\n    90\t    verify_batch.add_argument(\"snapshot\", type=Path)\n    91\t    verify_batch.add_argument(\"--schema\", type=Path, default=_default_schema_path())\n    92\t\n    93\t    csv_cmd = commands.add_parser(\"write-claims-csv\", help=\"write the exact current-claim CSV contract\")\n    94\t    csv_cmd.add_argument(\"claims_json\", type=Path, help=\"JSON array of current claim summary objects\")\n    95\t    csv_cmd.add_argument(\"output\", type=Path)\n    96\t\n    97\t    replay = commands.add_parser(\n    98\t        \"offline-replay\",\n    99\t        help=\"replay verified retained records in arrival order without fresh native-source reads\",\n   100\t    )\n   101\t    replay.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path, help=\"existing retained-source run directory\")\n   102\t    replay.add_argument(\"--schema\", type=Path, default=_default_schema_path(), help=\"snapshot schema path\")\n   103\t    readiness = commands.add_parser(\"validate-readiness\", help=\"check local submission evidence; PASS/BLOCKED/FAIL, never live compliance\")\n   104\t    readiness.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path)\n   105\t    readiness.add_argument(\"--schema\", type=Path, default=_default_schema_path())\n   106\t    readiness.add_argument(\"--repo\", type=Path, default=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2])\n   107\t    readiness.add_argument(\"--output-dir\", type=Path, required=True, help=\"new directory for readiness.json and readiness.md\")\n   108\t    return parser\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\tdef main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\n   112\t    args = build_parser().parse_args(argv)\n   113\t    if args.command == \"validate-readiness\":\n   114\t        try:\n   115\t            run_root = args.run_dir.resolve()\n   116\t            output_root = args.output_dir.resolve()\n   117\t            if output_root == run_root or output_root.is_relative_to(run_root):\n   118\t                raise ValueError(\"Readiness outputs must be outside the retained run directory\")\n   119\t            report = validate_readiness(args.run_dir, schema_path=args.schema, repo_dir=args.repo)\n   120\t            write_readiness_reports(report, args.output_dir)\n   121\t        except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:\n   122\t            print(f\"Could not validate readiness: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   123\t            return 1\n   124\t        print(readiness_summary(report))\n   125\t        print(f\"Readiness reports: {args.output_dir}\")\n   126\t        return {\"PASS\": 0, \"BLOCKED\": 2, \"FAIL\": 1}[report[\"status\"]]\n   127\t    if args.command == \"validate-snapshot\":\n   128\t        errors = validate_snapshot(args.snapshot, args.schema)\n   129\t        if errors:\n   130\t            print(\"Snapshot validation failed:\", file=sys.stderr)\n   131\t            for error in errors:\n   132\t                print(f\"- {error}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   133\t            return 1\n   134\t        print(f\"Snapshot is valid: {args.snapshot}\")\n   135\t        return 0\n   136\t    if args.command == \"live-run\":\n   137\t        try:\n   138\t            report = run_live_sources(args.run_dir, run_id=args.run_id, case_clock=args.case_clock, timeout=args.timeout)\n   139\t        except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:\n   140\t            print(f\"Live-source attempt failed: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   141\t            return 1\n   142\t        print(f\"LIVE SOURCE ATTEMPT {report['status']}: {args.run_id}; acquisition {report['acquisition_status']}; no cached fallback; final compliance not established\")\n   143\t        print(f\"Report: {args.run_dir / 'live-run.md'}\")\n   144\t        return {\"PASS\": 0, \"BLOCKED\": 2, \"FAIL\": 1}[report['status']]\n   145\t    if args.command == \"capture-sources\":\n   146\t        try:\n   147\t            manifest = capture_sources(args.run_dir, run_id=args.run_id, case_clock=args.case_clock)\n   148\t        except Exception as exc:\n   149\t            print(f\"Source capture failed: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   150\t            return 1\n   151\t        counts = {state: sum(row[\"status\"] == state for row in manifest[\"files\"]) for state in (\"read\", \"partial\", \"unavailable\")}\n   152\t        print(f\"Source capture {'PASS' if counts['read'] == 5 else 'BLOCKED'}: {args.run_id} ({counts['read']} read, {counts['partial']} partial, {counts['unavailable']} unavailable)\")\n   153\t        return 0 if counts[\"read\"] == 5 else 2\n   154\t    if args.command == \"verify-sources\":\n   155\t        errors = verify_source_manifest(args.run_dir)\n   156\t        if errors:\n   157\t            print(\"Source verification failed:\", file=sys.stderr)\n   158\t            for error in errors:\n   159\t                print(f\"- {error}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   160\t            return 1\n   161\t        print(f\"Source manifest and retained bytes are valid: {args.run_dir}\")\n   162\t        return 0\n   163\t    if args.command == \"parse-retained\":\n   164\t        try:\n   165\t            parsed = parse_retained_run(args.run_dir, output_path=args.output)\n   166\t        except (OSError, ValueError, FileExistsError) as exc:\n   167\t            print(f\"Could not parse retained sources: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   168\t            return 1\n   169\t        print(\n   170\t            f\"Parsed {len(parsed['records']['claim_revisions'])} claim revisions, \"\n   171\t            f\"{len(parsed['records']['trips'])} trips, {len(parsed['records']['permits'])} permits, \"\n   172\t            f\"{len(parsed['records']['receipts'])} receipt records, \"\n   173\t            f\"{len(parsed['records']['decisions'])} decisions, \"\n   174\t            f\"{len(parsed['records']['finance_events'])} Finance events, and \"\n   175\t            f\"{len(parsed['records']['cancellation_activities'])} cancellation activities; \"\n   176\t            f\"arrival batches {parsed['arrival_batches']}; case clock {parsed['case_clock_state']}\"\n   177\t        )\n   178\t        return 0 if not parsed[\"missing_sources\"] and not parsed.get(\"transcription_issues\") and parsed[\"case_clock\"] else 2\n   179\t    if args.command == \"seal-batch\":\n   180\t        try:\n   181\t            state = json.loads(args.state.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n   182\t            snapshot_path = seal_batch_snapshot(\n   183\t                args.run_dir,\n   184\t                run_id=args.run_id,\n   185\t                batch_id=args.batch_id,\n   186\t                claims=state[\"claims\"],\n   187\t                requests=state[\"requests\"],\n   188\t                travel_cancellations=state[\"travel_cancellations\"],\n   189\t                admitted_event_ids=state[\"admitted_event_ids\"],\n   190\t                issues=state[\"issues\"],\n   191\t                schema_path=args.schema,\n   192\t                predecessor_path=args.predecessor,\n   193\t            )\n   194\t        except (OSError, KeyError, json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError) as exc:\n   195\t            print(f\"Could not seal batch: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   196\t            return 1\n   197\t        print(f\"Sealed batch snapshot: {snapshot_path}\")\n   198\t        return 0\n   199\t    if args.command == \"verify-batch\":\n   200\t        errors = verify_snapshot(args.snapshot, args.run_dir, args.schema)\n   201\t        if errors:\n   202\t            print(\"Batch verification failed:\", file=sys.stderr)\n   203\t            for error in errors:\n   204\t                print(f\"- {error}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   205\t            return 1\n   206\t        print(f\"Batch snapshot and bindings are valid: {args.snapshot}\")\n   207\t        return 0\n   208\t    if args.command == \"write-claims-csv\":\n   209\t        try:\n   210\t            claims = json.loads(args.claims_json.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n   211\t            if not isinstance(claims, list):\n   212\t                raise ValueError(\"claims JSON must be an array\")\n   213\t            write_claims_csv(claims, args.output)\n   214\t        except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError) as exc:\n   215\t            print(f\"Could not write claims CSV: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   216\t            return 1\n   217\t        print(f\"Wrote claims CSV: {args.output}\")\n   218\t        return 0\n   219\t    if args.command == \"offline-replay\":\n   220\t        try:\n   221\t            result = run_offline_replay(args.run_dir, schema_path=args.schema)\n   222\t        except (OSError, KeyError, json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError, FileExistsError) as exc:\n   223\t            print(f\"Offline replay failed: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   224\t            return 1\n   225\t        print(f\"OFFLINE REPLAY complete: {result['run_id']} (no fresh native-source reads)\")\n   226\t        for snapshot in result[\"snapshots\"]:\n   227\t            print(f\"Snapshot: {snapshot}\")\n   228\t        for label, output in result[\"outputs\"].items():\n   229\t            print(f\"{label}: {output}\")\n   230\t        return 0\n   231\t    return 2\n   232\t\n   233\t\n   234\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n   235\t    raise SystemExit(main())\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"1:# Project D — Travel Expense Claim Interview\n13:I coordinate travel reimbursements at Alderbridge. Much of my time goes into checking evidence, chasing reviews, and finding out what Finance actually paid, especially when a claim changes. I would like help making the whole process repeatable. You can ask me about how we work, policy, the records we use, or the problems that keep coming back.\n43:When there are exceptions, like for late filings or specific amount limits, we need a Finance exception. This official exception is issued by Finance for a specific claim version to resolve a set issue, like late filing or an unapproved permit. However, it doesn't waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\n47:When you say Finance, is that a department?\n51:Yes, Finance refers to our financial department. They are responsible for issuing monetary tables like currency rates and spending caps, providing official exceptions for policy issues, and handling actual payment execution and reconciliation for claims.\n87:If a receipt is lost, the employee must provide alternative evidence or an explanation, but since Finance cannot waive missing receipts, the claim will remain unresolved until the evidence is provided.\n109:Financial activities include the pending, failed, or settled outcomes of payment requests, as well as accepted commitments, adjustments, refunds, and cancellations. These are all tracked and owned by the Finance department.\n117:Cancellations can target an entire trip or just a permit version independently of a claim. They must be initiated by the employee and confirmed by the supervisor, and these actions are tracked in the Travel cancellations workbook. If there were paid costs or Finance commitments, Finance will need to issue a specific disposition and resolve the money separately.\n125:Finance will issue a specific disposition bound to the cancellation ID, which confirms the reimbursement eligibility and provides a new allowed amount and reason for the affected costs.\n135:Yes, limits apply to specific categories. Lodging and meals are limited by daily or nightly caps set by Finance, based on the destination and date, which are then multiplied by the documented duration. Transport and conference expenses are not subject to these caps.\n143:The limits for lodging and meals are determined by daily or nightly caps set by Finance, based on your destination, expense currency, and the payment date. You can see these metrics in the Caps tab of the Travel registers workbook.\n153:How do incomplete claims affect independent work?\n157:Incomplete claims are held while the missing facts are addressed. You can continue processing independent claims separately while others are held, as long as the business impact is made clear.\n173:The available actions include requesting missing evidence from the employee, seeking an official exception from Finance for specific issues, or holding the claim until Finance confirms the resolution or provides the missing definitions.\n177:On average, how long does it take Finance to confirm resolution or provide the missing definitions?\n181:I don't have a set average for Finance response times. Their replies come in batches, and the time it takes depends on the volume and complexity of the request.\n185:When was the most recent time a Finance needed to confirm resolution that you can remember?\n189:I don't track specific dates for those resolutions in my head. Our Finance replies are delivered in versioned batches, and we process the needed resolutions as they arrive based on the specific claims and costs.\n193:How many people are in a batch?\n197:The batch size isn't fixed; it depends on the number of claims, requests, or reviewer replies being processed by Finance or the relevant budget owner at that time.\n201:How are batches organized? For example, could they be organized by a time slot or with a certain amount of people inside?\n213:I don't assign claims to a trainer. The replies you see come from versioned batches provided by Finance or other appropriate reviewers based on the business workflow.\n221:I don't have information about trainers. My work focuses on coordinating with the Finance department, budget owners, supervisors, and employees to process travel claims.\n229:I don't have information about trainers. My role is Travel Administration Lead, and the replies I receive come from Finance, budget owners, supervisors, and directors within the established business workflow.\n233:Tell me about the boundaries of Finance.\n237:Finance owns setting currency rates, managing spending caps, and issuing official policy exceptions. They also execute payments and resolve any monetary issues or cancellations, but they cannot waive missing evidence like receipts or proof of payment.\n245:Budget owners have the authority to approve, return, or reject a claim based on the complete department ledger. They assess funding availability and make discretionary decisions, which I receive in supplied reviewer replies.\n269:Directors provide an additional layer of authorization for high-spend situations, typically when the reviewed claim entitlement or permit estimate exceeds EUR 1,000.00. They evaluate the business necessity, exceptions, and alternatives, and their decisions arrive in supplied reply batches.\n285:Financial completion requires that current approvals match the reviewed entitlement, net confirmed payments equal the authorized amount, no issues remain, and all required Finance resolutions have been received.\n301:The accepted delivery scope is confirmed when the current approvals and reviewed entitlement agree with the net confirmed payment, and all required Finance resolutions have been received with no remaining issues.\n309:Issues refer to unresolved problems like missing receipts, incomplete payment proof, late filings, or mismatched data. For repair work, constraints involve organizing the missing evidence into usable local tasks, retaining the subject and revision, identifying the responsible owner, and ensuring corrections go through required reviews.\n341:Yes, cases can be placed on hold for missing facts or Finance resolutions, but they cannot be closed or considered complete until all required evidence and decisions are obtained.\n373:I communicate through formal requests and notifications. These include the subject type, IDs, stable role requesters, and relevant source versions, and I wait for replies from the authorized reviewers and Finance.\n377:Let me summarize to make sure I understand: the system route work based on four distinct human authority profiles: supervisors, budget owners, directors, and Finance.\n389:Hello! I coordinate travel reimbursements at Alderbridge. Much of my time goes into checking evidence, chasing reviews, and finding out what Finance actually paid, especially when a claim changes. You can ask me about how we work, our policy, the records we use, or the problems that keep coming back.\n397:The ordinary cycle begins when an employee pays for a travel cost and submits a claim. I review the claim against the trip permits, receipts, and merchant payments to calculate the reviewed entitlement. Then, I coordinate the necessary approvals based on the amount and policy, submit the request to Finance for transfer, and reconcile the payments until the case is closed.\n413:When you submit the request to Finance for transfer. what type of files or formats do you submit?\n425:Funding commitments are established when Finance accepts the reimbursement request, confirming the obligation and reserving the funds for budget tracking.\n433:When a cancellation occurs, the valid confirmation pauses payment readiness but does not erase the Finance commitment. If the original permit was lawful before arrangements, it remains lawful, and we record a specific cancellation issue rather than invalidating the permit.\n473:For international permits, I verify administrative completeness, then obtain reviews from the budget owner and supervisor. If the estimated cost is over one thousand euros, a director must also approve the permit before any travel arrangements are made.\n481:I match Finance outcomes against the authorized obligation for each claim. I calculate net paid by taking confirmed transfers minus any refunds, and compare that to the authorized amount to find the remaining balance or identify any overpayments requiring resolution.\n489:Common errors include missing receipts or payment proof, conflicting data like mismatched amounts or currencies, late filings, and unrecognized transactions that require Finance to resolve.\n493:When Finance resolves it, do they give you a piece of data so you can keep filling out your report?\n497:Yes, Finance provides formal records like eligibility exceptions or resolution events that include the covered issues, authorized amounts, and specific reason codes for the claim version.\n501:Is there ever a case where Finance can't resolve it and it becomes unresolved?\n505:Yes, if a required piece of evidence, such as a receipt or proof of payment, is persistently missing or a policy definition is unavailable, Finance cannot issue a resolution, and the item remains unresolved until the correct data is provided.\n529:Our business sources include the travel reimbursement policy, trip and permit records, expense claim forms paired with their receipts, and Finance activity logs for transfers and obligations.\n537:I coordinate with the exercise operator for policy definition gaps and with Finance for monetary exceptions, ensuring all data is resolved before any claims can move forward.\n571:Yes, exactly. Items like specific receipts, detailed expense claims, and Finance transaction logs are accessed directly from the official external registries during your case review.\n587:That is precisely correct. Every claim involves receiving the submission, validating all evidence and calculations, applying the policy rules, awaiting the necessary human approvals, and finally reconciling the payments for closure.\n599:What part of the workflow becomes the most complicated among batches rather than working with just individual case by case?\n603:Reconciling multiple batches becomes complicated when tracking Finance outcomes, such as partial payments or late transfers, across various batches and different versions of a claim.\n607:Is there a limit to how many batches you can handle at one time?\n611:There is no fixed limit on the number of batches I can process at once. The main challenge is carefully matching transaction IDs and amounts across all historical records and versions.\n619:Yes, we access several types of historical records, including previous claim versions, original receipt cards, past approval decisions, and historical Finance events like prior payments or adjustments.\n627:Authority for financial payments, settlements, and eligibility exceptions always rests with Finance, as they are the sole authority for monetary transfers and resolutions.\n631:What happens when Finance has their own expense travel claims?\n635:All employees, including those in Finance, follow the exact same reimbursement policy and workflow. Finance personnel still need reviews from budget owners, supervisors, and directors for their claims, depending on the amount and travel type.\n639:Is Finance allowed to handle their own files and cases?\n643:To maintain impartiality, Finance personnel cannot approve their own claims; they must still go through the required budget owner, supervisor, and director reviews based on the amount.\n667:Reimbursement caps for categories like lodging and meals are defined periodically by Finance, taking specific costs into account as set in the annual policy.\n720:Exactly. A budget rejection is a funding decision regarding entitlement, not a payment execution failure. It is documented as a rejection with its specific reason, separate from any Finance transfer issues.\n724:So, in the case of a payment execution failure, what types of codes or labels does Finance use?\n728:Finance provides specific outcome labels such as \"failed,\" \"pending,\" or \"cancelled\" in the Finance activity log. These indicate the status of the monetary transfer rather than a decision on the claim's entitlement.\n752:The operational sources are designed to be complementary and consistent. Each serves a different purpose in the workflow, such as policy definitions or payment records, and together they provide a complete case record.\n756:Does that ever lead to partial reviewer or Finance with replies with outdated revisions?\n768:It varies depending on when the reviewer or Finance processes the request, but I do not track the specific frequency, as my focus is on verifying each individual case.\n772:Tell me about a situation on how an agent should handle when Finance replies from an old claim version after an employee already submitted a correct version.\n776:When Finance replies for an outdated version, we reject that response since it isn't current authorization. We retain that record in the history but do not apply it to the new claim, simply waiting for the reply that matches the correct claim revision.\n792:No, core evidence such as a receipt or settled merchant payment cannot be marked as resolved if it is missing. Those are structural requirements under the policy, and the claim must be held until the required evidence or an explicit Finance exception is provided.\n796:To make sure I understand this, I want to summarize: an incoming batch component either there's a decision/reply input or a new claim correction, and if it's a decision/reply input, it's checking the version is current, whereas a new claim correction increments revisions and wipes downstream approvals.\n800:That is correct. Incoming batches contain either reviewer decisions or claim corrections; decisions must match the current revision, while corrections increment revisions and necessitate re-evaluation of subsequent approvals.\n   165\t    stage('policy_eligibility', policy_ok, policy_refs + evidence_refs,\n   166\t          'Expense calculation and filing are separate from travel permission, reviewed policy definitions and approvals',\n   167\t          lead, 'Resolve line findings and remaining policy/permission evidence before treating calculated amounts as entitlement')\n   168\t\n   169\t    for line in lines:\n   170\t        exception = line['exception']\n   171\t        if exception['status'] != 'absent':\n   172\t            stage(f\"finance_exception:{line['cost_id']}\", exception['status'] == 'valid', line['source_refs'],\n   173\t                  exception.get('reason', 'Source-bound Finance exception'), finance_owner,\n   174\t                  'Supply exact Finance actor, current claim/revision/cost, replacement amount, reason and covered issues')\n   175\t        for item in line['eligibility_findings']:\n   176\t            name = f\"eligibility:{line['cost_id']}:{item['issue']}\" + (f\":{item['travel_cancellation_id']}\" if item.get('travel_cancellation_id') else '')\n   177\t            stage(name, item['status'] == 'covered_for_reimbursement', item['source_refs'] + item['exception_source_refs'],\n   178\t                  item['original_finding'] + '; ' + item['status'], finance_owner,\n   179\t                  'Obtain explicit Finance coverage for this exact eligibility finding and affected expense; retain original arrangement history')\n   180\t\n   181\t    prior_lines = {l['cost_id']: l for l in (prior_workflow or {}).get('lines', [])}\n   182\t    def changed_exception_amount(line):\n   183\t        old = prior_lines.get(line['cost_id'], {})\n   184\t        before = old.get('conversion', {}).get('allowed_original_amount')\n   185\t        after = line.get('conversion', {}).get('allowed_original_amount')\n   186\t        # Unknown-to-known evidence and decimal display precision are not proof\n   187\t        # of a material replacement-amount change.\n   188\t        return bool(before is not None and after is not None\n   189\t            and (line.get('exception', {}).get('status') == 'valid' or old.get('exception', {}).get('status') == 'valid')\n   190\t            and Decimal(before) != Decimal(after))\n   191\t    same_revision_change = bool(prior_workflow and prior_workflow.get('revision') == revision and (\n   192\t        any(changed_exception_amount(line) for line in lines)\n   193\t        or prior_workflow.get('exception_revalidation', {}).get('same_revision_change')))\n   194\t    replacement_review = same_revision_change or any(\n   195\t        line.get('replacement_amount_changed') or changed_exception_amount(line) for line in lines)\n   196\t    line_refs={r for line in lines for r in line['source_refs']}\n   197\t    dependencies=[r for key,tab in [('receipts','Receipts'),('merchant_payments','Merchant payments'),('caps','Caps'),('fx_rates','FX')]\n   198\t                  for r in table(parsed,key,tab) if ref(r) in line_refs]\n   199\t    claim_review=evaluate_reviews(parsed=parsed,kind='claim',subject_id=claim_id,revision=revision,\n   200\t        trip_record=trips[0] if len(trips)==1 else {},employee=employee,subject_record=record,\n   201\t        amount_cents=budget_view['remaining_request_cents'] if calculation['status']=='PASS' else None,decisions=decisions,arrival_batch=arrival_batch,\n   202\t        observations=source_observations,cost_ids=[line['cost_id'] for line in lines],\n   203\t        dependency_rows=dependencies,prior=(prior_workflow or {}).get('claim_approval'),\n   204\t        withdrawn=linked and values.get('Status')=='withdrawn' and trusted(record),\n   205\t        cancellation_ids=[f['travel_cancellation_id'] for f in eligibility if f['issue']=='travel_cancellation'],budget_context=budget_view)\n   206\t    observed=claim_review['deliveries']\n   207\t    # Preserve Step 175's extra binding requirement on material Finance replacements.\n   208\t    for decision in observed:\n   209\t        decision['exception_binding_valid']=(not replacement_review or review_binds_exception(\n   210\t            decision['raw_record'],record,same_revision_change=same_revision_change,fields=fields,ref=ref))\n   211\t        if not decision['exception_binding_valid']:\n   212\t            decision['evidence_valid']=False\n   213\t    approvals=claim_review['approved'] and all(d['evidence_valid'] for d in observed if d['active'])\n   214\t    budget_replies=[d for d in observed if 'budget_owner' in d['roles']]\n   215\t    budget_authorized=any(d['active'] and d['evidence_valid'] and d.get('budget_evidence_valid',True) and d['outcome']=='approve' for d in budget_replies)\n   216\t    stage('budget_owner_authorization',budget_authorized,budget_view['source_refs']+[r for d in budget_replies for r in d['source_refs']],\n   217\t        '; '.join(dict.fromkeys(d['budget_revalidation_reason'] for d in budget_replies if d.get('budget_revalidation_reason'))) or 'Current discretionary budget-owner authorization required; funds alone are insufficient',\n   218\t        budget_view['owner'],'Supply a current budget-owner response bound to the complete scope ledger and this claim/version')\n   219\t    review_refs=claim_review['source_refs']\n   220\t    reviews_ok=all(claim_review['role_states'].get(role) not in {'missing','conflicting'} for role in claim_review['required_roles']) and all(d['evidence_valid'] for d in observed if d['active'])\n   221\t    stage('review_evidence',reviews_ok,review_refs,\n   222\t          'Current subject/version/role/actor/source/reason and complete review packets; rejected imports remain in history',\n   223\t          lead,'Supply current source-bound replies and complete packets; answer the concrete return repair requests')\n   224\t    stage('required_approvals',approvals,review_refs + policy_refs,\n   225\t          f\"Claim approval state: {claim_review['state']}; required roles: {', '.join(claim_review['required_roles'])}\",\n   226\t          lead,'Obtain the outstanding current-version human decisions; permit replies never approve a claim')\n   227\t\n   228\t    for reply in observed:\n   229\t        if reply['outcome']=='return' and reply['evidence_valid']:\n   230\t            stage(f\"review_return:{reply['decision_id']}\",not reply['active'],reply['source_refs'],\n   231\t                  f\"{reply['reason']}; repair requested: {reply['repair_requested']}\",employee or 'Employee',reply['repair_requested'])\n   232\t\n   233\t    exception_revalidated = not replacement_review or approvals\n   234\t    stage('exception_revalidation', exception_revalidated, evidence_refs + review_refs,\n   235\t          'Replacement amounts require current claim reviews bound to the replacement source version; earlier reviews remain historical',\n   236\t          lead, 'Obtain current revision/source-bound reviews of the Finance replacement amount and a matching reimbursement authorization')\n   237\t\n   238\t    requests = [r for r in table(parsed, 'reimbursement_requests', 'Reimbursement requests')\n   239\t                if trusted(r) and visible(r) and fields(r).get('Claim reference') == claim_id and fields(r).get('Revision') == revision]\n   240\t    request = fields(requests[0]) if len(requests) == 1 else {}\n   241\t    obligation = finance.get('recorded_obligation')\n   242\t    approved_ids = {d['decision_id'] for d in observed if d['outcome'] == 'approve' and d['evidence_valid'] and d['active']}\n   243\t    request_ok = bool(linked and reimbursement_permission and policy_ok and approvals and obligation and len(requests) == 1\n   244\t                      and request.get('Request reference') == obligation['request_id']\n   245\t                      and request.get('Payee ID') == person.get('Payee ID') == obligation['payee_id']\n   246\t                      and request.get('Currency') == 'EUR' and _cents(request.get('Amount (EUR)')) == allowed == obligation['amount_cents']\n   247\t                      and obligation['claim_revision'] == revision and obligation['finance_officer'] == finance_owner\n   248\t                      and set(str(request.get('Decision references') or '').splitlines()) == approved_ids\n   249\t                      and bool(approved_ids))\n   250\t    request_refs = [ref(r) for r in requests] + (obligation['source_refs'] if obligation else [])\n   251\t    stage('request_obligation', request_ok, request_refs,\n   252\t          'Recorded request/obligation linkage requires explicit claim revision, payee, amount and approval references; ledger arrival context is not authorization',\n   253\t          finance_owner, 'Provide the exact-revision reimbursement request and Finance acceptance linked to its approvals and authorized amount')\n   254\t    if request_ok:\n   255\t        authorization = dict(amount_cents=allowed, claim_revision=revision, source_refs=request_refs + review_refs + policy_refs)\n   256\t        finance = reconcile_finance_events(finance_events, claim_id=claim_id, current_revision=revision,\n   257\t            revision_history=finance['revision_history'], previous_reconciliation=prior_finance,\n   258\t            authorized_obligation=authorization, source_classifications=source_classifications, event_context=finance.get(\"event_context\"))\n   259\t    reconciled = finance.get('recorded_ledger_balance_cents') is not None and not finance['unresolved_event_ids'] and not finance['conflicting_events']\n   260\t    stage('financial_reconciliation', reconciled,\n   261\t          [ref(e) for e in finance_events if fields(e).get('Claim reference') == claim_id],\n   262\t          f\"Confirmed net cash {finance['net_confirmed_cents']} cents; recorded ledger difference {finance.get('recorded_ledger_balance_cents')}; authorized balance {finance['balance_cents']}\",\n   263\t          finance_owner, 'Resolve missing obligations, conflicting or unclassified events, request/payee links and outstanding balances')\n   264\t\n   265\t    authorities = [r for r in table(parsed, 'closure_authorities', 'Closure authorities') if trusted(r) and visible(r)\n   266\t                   and fields(r).get('Claim reference') == claim_id and fields(r).get('Revision') == revision]\n   267\t    clock_ok = False\n   268\t    try:\n   269\t        clock_ok = datetime.fromisoformat(parsed['case_clock'].replace('Z', '+00:00')).utcoffset() is not None\n   270\t    except (KeyError, ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):\n   271\t        pass\n   272\t    closure_authority = (len(authorities) == 1 and fields(authorities[0]).get('Confirmation') == 'financial-completion-conditions'\n   273\t                         and bool(fields(authorities[0]).get('Authority')) and fields(authorities[0]).get('Case clock') == parsed.get('case_clock'))\n   274\t    external = [i for i in parsed.get('unresolved_issues', []) if i.get('status', 'open') == 'open'\n   275\t                and (i.get('subject_type') in {'policy', 'scenario'} or i.get('subject_id') in {claim_id, trip_id, trip.get('Permit reference')})]\n   276\t    control_events = [e for e in finance['event_history'] if e['classification'] in {\n   277\t        'failed_transfer', 'retry_authorization', 'finance_cancellation_requested', 'finance_cancelled'}]\n   278\t    resolved_controls = set()\n   279\t    def event_stamp(event):\n   280\t        stamp = datetime.fromisoformat(event['source_record']['Activity time (UTC)'].replace('Z', '+00:00'))\n   281\t        return stamp.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc) if stamp.utcoffset() is None else stamp\n   282\t    for event in finance['event_history']:\n   283\t        value = event['source_record']\n   284\t        if (event['classification'] == 'finance_resolution' and value.get('Claim revision') == revision\n   285\t                and obligation and value.get('Request reference') == obligation['request_id']\n   286\t                and value.get('Finance officer') == finance_owner):\n   287\t            named = set(str(value.get('Resolved activity references') or '').splitlines())\n   288\t            for control in control_events:\n   289\t                try:\n   290\t                    if (control['event_id'] in named\n   291\t                            and control['source_record'].get('Request reference') == value['Request reference']\n   292\t                            and event_stamp(event) >= event_stamp(control)):\n   293\t                        resolved_controls.add(control['event_id'])\n   294\t                except (KeyError, ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):\n   295\t                    pass\n   296\t    controls_clear = not finance['pending_transfer_event_ids'] and all(e['event_id'] in resolved_controls for e in control_events)\n   297\t    cancellation_refs = [source for c in affected for source in c.get(\"source_refs\", [])]\n   298\t    stage('cancellation_readiness', not affected, cancellation_refs,\n   299\t          'Linked current or historical trip/permit cancellation requires specific Finance disposition and resolution; prior permission and money history are preserved' if affected else 'No linked cancellation dependency',\n   300\t          finance_owner, 'Verify cancellation-bound disposition, current request authority and monetary resolution before releasing payment readiness')\n   301\t    closed = (all(s['status'] == 'PASS' for s in stages) and controls_clear and request_ok and finance['balance_cents'] == 0\n   302\t              and not finance['repair_issues'] and not affected and clock_ok and closure_authority and not external)\n   303\t    stage('financial_closure', closed, [ref(r) for r in authorities] + request_refs + policy_refs,\n   304\t          'Closure requires supported completion conditions, authoritative clock, current evidence/approvals, entitlement/obligation/net cash agreement and no affected unresolved issue',\n   305\t          finance_owner, 'Confirm completion conditions and the authoritative clock; resolve every affected approval, Finance or cancellation dependency')\n   306\t    business_state=claim_review['state']\n   307\t    financial_clean=(len(trips)==1 and trusted(trips[0]) and not finance.get('recorded_obligation') and not finance['net_confirmed_cents']\n   308\t        and not finance['event_history'] and not requests and not affected)\n   309\t    disposition=business_state if business_state in {'rejected','withdrawn'} and financial_clean else None\n   310\t    if business_state in {'rejected','withdrawn'} and not financial_clean:\n   311\t        stage('nonpayment_disposition',False,review_refs + request_refs,\n   312\t              'Rejection/withdrawal recorded; existing Finance effects require disposition and are not erased',\n   313\t              finance_owner,'Confirm cancellation/status of dispatched obligations and resolve existing cash before financial completion')\n   314\t    pending = next((s for s in stages if s['status'] != 'PASS'), None)\n   315\t    return dict(claim_id=claim_id, revision=revision, trip_id=trip_id, trip_revision=claim.get('trip_revision'),\n   316\t                mode=parsed.get('evidence_mode', 'offline-replay'), status=disposition or ('held' if business_state in {'rejected','withdrawn'} else ('closed-reimbursed' if allowed else 'closed-no-payment') if closed else 'pending'),\n   317\t                claim_approval=claim_review,permit_approval=permit_review,\n   318\t                budget_view=budget_view, expense_calculation=calculation, exception_revalidation=dict(required=replacement_review, same_revision_change=same_revision_change, status='PASS' if exception_revalidated else 'BLOCKED'), allowed_cents=allowed, balance_cents=finance['balance_cents'], lines=lines, stages=stages,\n   319\t                observed_reviews=observed, request=deepcopy(requests[0]) if request_ok else None,\n   320\t                source_refs=list(dict.fromkeys([ref(record)] + [r for s in stages for r in s['source_refs']])),\n   321\t                next_owner=None if closed or disposition else (finance_owner if business_state in {'rejected','withdrawn'} else pending['owner']),\n   322\t                reason=f\"Clean business {disposition}: \" + (values.get('Claim reason','') if disposition=='withdrawn' else '; '.join(d['reason'] for d in observed if d['active'] and d['outcome']=='reject')) if disposition else 'Supported financial closure' if closed else pending['detail'],\n   323\t                finance=finance)\n   324\t\n   325\t\n   326\tdef ordinary_demo(workflows):\n   327\t    \"\"\"Render one observed claim with every stage, owner and retained reference.\"\"\"\n   328\t    claim_id = \"C01\" if \"C01\" in workflows else next(iter(sorted(workflows)), None)\n   329\t    lines = [\"# Connected ordinary claim workflow — OFFLINE REPLAY\", \"\",\n   330\t             \"Retained-input evaluation; no fresh reads, requests, approvals or payments were generated.\", \"\"]\n   331\t    if not claim_id:\n   332\t        return \"\\n\".join(lines + [\"No retained claim available for demonstration.\", \"\"])\n   333\t    workflow = workflows[claim_id]\n   334\t    lines += [f\"Claim `{claim_id}` revision {workflow['revision']}; trip `{workflow['trip_id']}` revision {workflow['trip_revision']}; status **{workflow['status']}**.\", \"\"]\n   335\t    for stage in workflow['stages']:\n   336\t        lines += [f\"## {stage['stage']} — {stage['status']}\", \"\", stage['detail'], \"\",\n   337\t                  f\"Owner: {stage['owner']}. Next action: {stage['next_action']}\", \"\"]\n   338\t        lines.extend(f\"- `{reference}`\" for reference in stage['source_refs'])\n   339\t        lines.append(\"\")\n   340\t    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n     1\t\"\"\"Command-line interface for travel claim tooling.\"\"\"\n     2\t\n     3\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     4\t\n     5\timport argparse\n     6\timport json\n     7\timport sys\n     8\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     9\t\n    10\tfrom jsonschema import Draft202012Validator, FormatChecker\n    11\t\n    12\tfrom .outputs import write_claims_csv\n    13\tfrom .live_run import run_live_sources\n    14\tfrom .offline_replay import run_offline_replay\n    15\tfrom .readiness import readiness_summary, validate_readiness, write_readiness_reports\n    16\tfrom .parsing import parse_retained_run\n    17\tfrom .snapshots import seal_batch_snapshot, verify_snapshot\n    18\tfrom .sources import capture_sources, verify_source_manifest\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\tdef _default_schema_path() -> Path:\n    22\t    \"\"\"Return the repository's authoritative snapshot schema path.\"\"\"\n    23\t    return Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2] / \"snapshot.schema.json\"\n    24\t\n    25\t\n    26\tdef validate_snapshot(snapshot_path: Path, schema_path: Path) -> list[str]:\n    27\t    \"\"\"Return validation errors for a snapshot and schema, or an empty list.\"\"\"\n    28\t    try:\n    29\t        with snapshot_path.open(encoding=\"utf-8\") as snapshot_file:\n    30\t            snapshot = json.load(snapshot_file)\n    31\t    except FileNotFoundError:\n    32\t        return [f\"Snapshot file not found: {snapshot_path}\"]\n    33\t    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n    34\t        return [f\"Could not read snapshot {snapshot_path}: {exc}\"]\n    35\t\n    36\t    try:\n    37\t        with schema_path.open(encoding=\"utf-8\") as schema_file:\n    38\t            schema = json.load(schema_file)\n    39\t    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n    40\t        return [f\"Could not read schema {schema_path}: {exc}\"]\n    41\t\n    42\t    validator = Draft202012Validator(schema, format_checker=FormatChecker())\n    43\t    errors = sorted(validator.iter_errors(snapshot), key=lambda error: list(map(str, error.absolute_path)))\n    44\t    return [\n    45\t        f\"{'.'.join(map(str, error.absolute_path)) or '<root>'}: {error.message}\"\n    46\t        for error in errors\n    47\t    ]\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\tdef build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n    51\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog=\"travel-claim\")\n    52\t    commands = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", required=True)\n    53\t\n    54\t    validate = commands.add_parser(\n    55\t        \"validate-snapshot\", help=\"validate a JSON snapshot against snapshot.schema.json\"\n    56\t    )\n    57\t    validate.add_argument(\"snapshot\", type=Path, help=\"path to the snapshot JSON file\")\n    58\t    validate.add_argument(\n    59\t        \"--schema\", type=Path, default=_default_schema_path(), help=\"schema JSON path\"\n    60\t    )\n    61\t\n    62\t    capture = commands.add_parser(\"capture-sources\", help=\"freshly retrieve and retain all five native sources\")\n    63\t    capture.add_argument(\"run_id\", help=\"new, stable run identifier\")\n    64\t    capture.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path, help=\"new artifacts/runs/<run-id> directory\")\n    65\t    capture.add_argument(\"--case-clock\", help=\"supplied scenario clock; omit only for source-only capture\")\n    66\t\n    67\t    live = commands.add_parser(\"live-run\", help=\"freshly attempt all five sources, retain and transcribe; report blockers without offline fallback\")\n    68\t    live.add_argument(\"run_id\")\n    69\t    live.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path)\n    70\t    live.add_argument(\"--case-clock\", help=\"explicit authoritative scenario clock; never inferred from retrieval time\")\n    71\t    live.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=float, default=30.0, help=\"per-request timeout seconds\")\n    72\t\n    73\t    verify_sources = commands.add_parser(\"verify-sources\", help=\"verify source manifest and retained-byte hashes\")\n    74\t    verify_sources.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path)\n    75\t\n    76\t    parse_sources = commands.add_parser(\"parse-retained\", help=\"transcribe hash-verified PDFs and workbook into traceable records\")\n    77\t    parse_sources.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path)\n    78\t    parse_sources.add_argument(\"--output\", type=Path, help=\"optional new output path; defaults to parsed-records.json in the run\")\n    79\t\n    80\t    seal = commands.add_parser(\"seal-batch\", help=\"schema-check and immutably seal one batch state JSON\")\n    81\t    seal.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path)\n    82\t    seal.add_argument(\"batch_id\")\n    83\t    seal.add_argument(\"state\", type=Path, help=\"JSON object containing claims, requests, cancellations, events, issues\")\n    84\t    seal.add_argument(\"--run-id\", required=True)\n    85\t    seal.add_argument(\"--predecessor\", type=Path)\n    86\t    seal.add_argument(\"--schema\", type=Path, default=_default_schema_path())\n    87\t\n    88\t    verify_batch = commands.add_parser(\"verify-batch\", help=\"verify schema and source/predecessor bindings\")\n    89\t    verify_batch.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path)\n    90\t    verify_batch.add_argument(\"snapshot\", type=Path)\n    91\t    verify_batch.add_argument(\"--schema\", type=Path, default=_default_schema_path())\n    92\t\n    93\t    csv_cmd = commands.add_parser(\"write-claims-csv\", help=\"write the exact current-claim CSV contract\")\n    94\t    csv_cmd.add_argument(\"claims_json\", type=Path, help=\"JSON array of current claim summary objects\")\n    95\t    csv_cmd.add_argument(\"output\", type=Path)\n    96\t\n    97\t    replay = commands.add_parser(\n    98\t        \"offline-replay\",\n    99\t        help=\"replay verified retained records in arrival order without fresh native-source reads\",\n   100\t    )\n   101\t    replay.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path, help=\"existing retained-source run directory\")\n   102\t    replay.add_argument(\"--schema\", type=Path, default=_default_schema_path(), help=\"snapshot schema path\")\n   103\t    readiness = commands.add_parser(\"validate-readiness\", help=\"check local submission evidence; PASS/BLOCKED/FAIL, never live compliance\")\n   104\t    readiness.add_argument(\"run_dir\", type=Path)\n   105\t    readiness.add_argument(\"--schema\", type=Path, default=_default_schema_path())\n   106\t    readiness.add_argument(\"--repo\", type=Path, default=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2])\n   107\t    readiness.add_argument(\"--output-dir\", type=Path, required=True, help=\"new directory for readiness.json and readiness.md\")\n   108\t    return parser\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\tdef main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\n   112\t    args = build_parser().parse_args(argv)\n   113\t    if args.command == \"validate-readiness\":\n   114\t        try:\n   115\t            run_root = args.run_dir.resolve()\n   116\t            output_root = args.output_dir.resolve()\n   117\t            if output_root == run_root or output_root.is_relative_to(run_root):\n   118\t                raise ValueError(\"Readiness outputs must be outside the retained run directory\")\n   119\t            report = validate_readiness(args.run_dir, schema_path=args.schema, repo_dir=args.repo)\n   120\t            write_readiness_reports(report, args.output_dir)\n   121\t        except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:\n   122\t            print(f\"Could not validate readiness: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   123\t            return 1\n   124\t        print(readiness_summary(report))\n   125\t        print(f\"Readiness reports: {args.output_dir}\")\n   126\t        return {\"PASS\": 0, \"BLOCKED\": 2, \"FAIL\": 1}[report[\"status\"]]\n   127\t    if args.command == \"validate-snapshot\":\n   128\t        errors = validate_snapshot(args.snapshot, args.schema)\n   129\t        if errors:\n   130\t            print(\"Snapshot validation failed:\", file=sys.stderr)\n   131\t            for error in errors:\n   132\t                print(f\"- {error}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   133\t            return 1\n   134\t        print(f\"Snapshot is valid: {args.snapshot}\")\n   135\t        return 0\n   136\t    if args.command == \"live-run\":\n   137\t        try:\n   138\t            report = run_live_sources(args.run_dir, run_id=args.run_id, case_clock=args.case_clock, timeout=args.timeout)\n   139\t        except (OSError, ValueError) as exc:\n   140\t            print(f\"Live-source attempt failed: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n   141\t            return 1\n   142\t        print(f\"LIVE SOURCE ATTEMPT {report['status']}: {args.run_id}; acquisition {report['acquisition_status']}; no cached fallback; final compliance not established\")\n   143\t      