88\t            for control in control_events:\n   289\t                try:\n   290\t                    if (control['event_id'] in named\n   291\t                            and control['source_record'].get('Request reference') == value['Request reference']\n   292\t                            and event_stamp(event) >= event_stamp(control)):\n   293\t                        resolved_controls.add(control['event_id'])\n   294\t                except (KeyError, ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):\n   295\t                    pass\n   296\t    controls_clear = not finance['pending_transfer_event_ids'] and all(e['event_id'] in resolved_controls for e in control_events)\n   297\t    cancellation_refs = [source for c in affected for source in c.get(\"source_refs\", [])]\n   298\t    stage('cancellation_readiness', not affected, cancellation_refs,\n   299\t          'Linked current or historical trip/permit cancellation requires specific Finance disposition and resolution; prior permission and money history are preserved' if affected else 'No linked cancellation dependency',\n   300\t          finance_owner, 'Verify cancellation-bound disposition, current request authority and monetary resolution before releasing payment readiness')\n   301\t    closed = (all(s['status'] == 'PASS' for s in stages) and controls_clear and request_ok and finance['balance_cents'] == 0\n   302\t              and not finance['repair_issues'] and not affected and clock_ok and closure_authority and not external)\n   303\t    stage('financial_closure', closed, [ref(r) for r in authorities] + request_refs + policy_refs,\n   304\t          'Closure requires supported completion conditions, authoritative clock, current evidence/approvals, entitlement/obligation/net cash agreement and no affected unresolved issue',\n   305\t          finance_owner, 'Confirm completion conditions and the authoritative clock; resolve every affected approval, Finance or cancellation dependency')\n   306\t    business_state=claim_review['state']\n   307\t    financial_clean=(len(trips)==1 and trusted(trips[0]) and not finance.get('recorded_obligation') and not finance['net_confirmed_cents']\n   308\t        and not finance['event_history'] and not requests and not affected)\n   309\t    disposition=business_state if business_state in {'rejected','withdrawn'} and financial_clean else None\n   310\t    if business_state in {'rejected','withdrawn'} and not financial_clean:\n1:# Project D — Travel Expense Claim Interview\n5:## Travel Administration Lead · Travel Administration Lead\n21:We follow policy POL-2026.2, which governs how expenses are reviewed and reimbursed. It outlines separate requirements for international permits and claims, specifies approval roles like the budget owner and supervisor, and sets limits on categories like lodging and meals. You can find all the details in the Travel reimbursement policy.\n465:The main difference is the permit stage. For international trips, you must obtain all necessary approvals before any travel arrangements are made. For domestic travel, that entire permit process is skipped, and you proceed directly to reviewing paid costs and receipts. Did you want to explore the specific approval requirements for international permits?\n792:No, core evidence such as a receipt or settled merchant payment cannot be marked as resolved if it is missing. Those are structural requirements under the policy, and the claim must be held until the required evidence or an explicit Finance exception is provided.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":100357788},"formatted_output":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 11066)\nTotal output lines: 634\n\n     1\t---\n     2\tname: travel-expense-claim\n     3\tdescription: Prepare traceable Alderbridge travel claim reviews, independent trip and permit work, repair drafts, and financial reconciliation from freshly retrieved native sources and authorized batch decisions. Never approve, invent evidence, send requests, book travel, or move money.\n     4\t---\n     5\t\n     6\t# Alderbridge Travel Expense Claim Skill\n     7\t\n     8\t## Inputs\n     9\t\n    10\t- A new run ID and the scenario's supplied case clock.\n    11\t- The five native source locations listed below, retrieved afresh on every new run.\n    12\t- The authorized arrival batch and its boundary/version, supplied by the exercise operator.\n    13\t- Any prior retained snapshot only when performing an explicitly labeled offline replay; this never substitutes for fresh reads on a new run.\n    14\t- Human reviewer, employee, and Finance responses only when present in supplied records.\n    15\t\n    16\tNever infer an approval, exception, source value, reply, or payment from a missing record.\n    17\t\n    18\t## Invocation\n    19\t\n    20\tInstall as described in the repository [README](../../README.md). Perform fresh acquisition and transcription for a new run with:\n    21\t\n    22\t```bash\n    23\ttravel-claim live-run <new-run-id> artifacts/runs/<new-run-id> [--case-clock '<authoritative scenario timestamp>']\n    24\t```\n    25\t\n    26\tThis attempts all five original sources, retains response evidence and emits `live-run.json`/`.md`. It never accepts prior inputs or consumes batches when clock/policy authority is missing. Direct Notion HTML cannot establish a complete policy block-tree read; authenticated native access remains required. Retrieval timestamps are observations, never an invented case clock. Source-only capture is also available:\n    27\t\n    28\t```bash\n    29\ttravel-claim capture-sources <run-id> artifacts/runs/<run-id> --case-clock '<scenario ISO timestamp>'\n    30\t```\n    31\t\n    32\tInspect the manifest status and verify retained bytes before processing a batch:\n    33\t\n    34\t```bash\n    35\ttravel-claim verify-sources artifacts/runs/<run-id>\n    36\ttravel-claim parse-retained artifacts/runs/<run-id>\n    37\t```\n    38\t\n    39\tSource-only acquisition does not consume a batch. Batch processing must preserve supplied arrival boundaries and use the public [`snapshot.schema.json`](../../snapshot.schema.json). Current foundation helpers are documented in [`travel_claim.sources`](../../src/travel_claim/sources.py), [`travel_claim.parsing`](../../src/travel_claim/parsing.py), [`travel_claim.workflow`](../../src/travel_claim/workflow.py), [`travel_claim.snapshots`](../../src/travel_claim/snapshots.py), and [`travel_claim.outputs`](../../src/travel_claim/outputs.py).\n    40\t\n    41\t`parse-retained` hash-verifies the run before transcribing the PDFs and workbook into page- and row-referenced records. The extracted source text and workbook values are evidence only. If the case clock or policy source is unavailable, leave it unresolved and do not consume policy-dependent decisions.\n    42\t\n    43\tStructural workflow helpers preserve every claim, trip and permit revision; identify whether a supplied decision references a found historical or latest source revision without applying its outcome; deduplicate repeated event IDs and report payload conflicts; and track independent trip/permit cancellation states. They do not calculate policy results. Repair items can be updated with new owner, evidence, reason, action, and subject revision while preserving prior updates. Revision advances reopen the item.\n    44\t\n    45\t## Native sources\n    46\t\n    47\t1. [Travel reimbursement policy — POL-2026.2](https://private-pecorino-70e.notion.site/REDACTED)\n    48\t2. [Initial claim binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/13sRj6s_kMeP1hsYGstWWmfkb6SCN1YOS/view)\n    49\t3. [Claim updates binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/REDACTED/view)\n    50\t4. [Receipt binder](https://drive.google.com/file/d/REDACTED/view)\n    51\t5. [Travel registers workbook](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/REDACTED/edit)\n    52\t\n    53\tRetain complete relevant bytes actually accessed. A response code or URL alone does not establish content access. Record partial and unavailable scopes separately. Never silently reuse a previous run's bytes in a new run.\n    54\t\n    55\t## Processing and authority boundaries\n    56\t\n    57\t1. Bind every fact and decision to its source, subject, and revision.\n    58\t2. Hold only claims or dependent work affected by missing/conflicting facts. Continue independent valid work. Each unresolved item retains subject type and exact ID, revision, missing/conflicting fact, responsible owner, source reference, and next action.\n    59\t3. Preserve every claim revision. After a material correction, use the corrected revision and revalidate affected evidence, calculations, trip/permit consistency, approvals, and Finance authorization. Preserve unrelated evidence only where it remains valid. Retain historical commitments, transfers, and refunds; do not use stale approvals as current.\n    60\t4. Keep trip cancellation and permit cancellation as independent processes, including processes without claims. Cancellation does not itself erase entitlement or Finance obligations. Record Finance disposition and monetary resolution separately when required.\n    61\t5. Use the owner-grouped local repair queue. Keep each item individually traceable. A partial response may resolve only the item(s) explicitly matched and supported by retained source evidence; unanswered, insufficient, or conflicting items stay open. Draft locally; never send requests.\n    62\t6. Preserve immutable Finance event identifiers. Reconcile only confirmed transfers and refunds. Do not duplicate events or obligations on replay.\n    63\t7. The provisional financial closure choice is to require current evidence and approvals, agreement between reviewed entitlement and authorized obligation, net confirmed payment equal to the authorized amount, required Finance resolutions, and no blocking issue. After the first actual processing result, pause for the operator to inspect reconciliation and unresolved cases and confirm final completion conditions and delivery scope.\n    64\t\n    65\tPeople retain business approval, exception, and payment authority. This Skill prepares work, validates supplied decisions, and records effects; it does not make discretionary approval recommendations, create replies, issue Finance exceptions, book travel, or move funds.\n    66\t\n    67\t## Outputs\n    68\t\n    69\t- `artifacts/runs/<run-id>/sources.json` and retained source bytes.\n    70\t- One immutable schema-valid `batches/<batch-id>.json` per consumed batch, with relative source and predecessor paths plus SHA-256 hashes.\n    71\t- `claims.csv` with exactly `claim_id,revision,trip_id,status,allowed_cents,paid_cents,balance_cents,next_owner,reason`.\n    72\t- Owner-grouped local repair queue with individual items and run/batch update history.\n    73\t- `report.md` describing completed work, obligations, unresolved items, owners, next actions, cancellations without claims, and source/run references.\n    74\t\n    75\tUnknown money is null in JSON and blank in CSV. Zero is a known amount. Never label incomplete work complete.\n    76\t\n    77\t## Errors, retries, and limitations\n    78\t\n    79\t- On source failure, retain the attempt URL, locator, UTC observation time, error, and missing scope. Hold only affected work and report its owner and resumption evidence.\n    80\t- On partial source access, retain usable pieces and explicitly list missing scope. Do not claim the source was fully read.\n    81\t- On invalid or conflicting batch data, preserve the input evidence, reject admission of unsupported effects, and create an owned issue; do not silently discard it.\n    82\t- Retry a failed fresh retrieval only by making another live request and recording the new observation. Do not overwrite a prior run's manifest, retained bytes, or sealed snapshot.\n    83\t- On replay, preserve obligation/event identity and money; detect conflicting content under an existing event ID.\n    84\t- Implemented paths include fresh HTTP/export acquisition and source-bound transcription, plus explicitly offline connected claim, correction, independent cancellation and Finance replay. New source manifests retain response observations and partial/error bodies. Complete native policy access, rule interpretation, authoritative case clock and supported completion authority remain required for final live business compliance; acquisition or offline integrity alone does not establish it.\n     1\t\"\"\"Fresh native acquisition and transcription, separate from retained replay.\n     2\t\n     3\tThis command never consumes an old manifest or seals business decisions with\n     4\tmissing clock/policy authority. Acquisition and business readiness are separate.\n     5\t\"\"\"\n     6\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     7\t\n     8\timport json\n     9\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    10\t\n    11\tfrom .parsing import parse_retained_run\n    12\tfrom .sources import capture_sources, sha256_bytes, verify_source_manifest\n    13\t\n    14\t\n    15\tdef run_live_sources(run_dir: Path, *, run_id: str, case_clock: str | None, **capture_options) -> dict:\n    16\t    \"\"\"Always capture all five URLs into a new directory before reading inputs.\"\"\"\n    17\t    manifest = capture_sources(run_dir, run_id=run_id, case_clock=case_clock, **capture_options)\n    18\t    errors = verify_source_manifest(run_dir)\n    19\t    parsed = None\n    20\t    if not errors:\n    21\t        try:\n    22\t            parsed = parse_retained_run(run_dir)\n    23\t        except Exception as exc:\n    24\t            errors.append(f\"Native transcription failed: {type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\")\n    25\t    checks = [{'check': 'manifest-integrity', 'status': 'FAIL' if errors else 'PASS',\n    26\t               'evidence': 'sources.json', 'detail': '; '.join(errors) or 'Fresh observations and retained bytes verified',\n    27\t               'next_action': 'Repair retrieval/transcription integrity in a new run' if errors else 'No integrity repair needed'}]\n    28\t    for row in manifest['files']:\n    29\t        checks.append({'check': f\"source:{row['source_id']}\", 'status': 'PASS' if row['status'] == 'read' else 'BLOCKED',\n    30\t                       'evidence': row['path'] or row['observation']['response_path'] or 'sources.json',\n    31\t                       'detail': row['error'] or 'Complete supported export read; retained bytes bound by SHA-256',\n    32\t                       'next_action': 'Obtain authorized native content and retry in a new run' if row['status'] != 'read' else 'Retain observed source version and wording'})\n    33\t    for issue in (parsed or {}).get('transcription_issues', []):\n    34\t        checks.append({'check': f\"transcription:{issue['source_id']}\", 'status': 'BLOCKED',\n    35\t                       'evidence': issue['path'], 'detail': issue['error'], 'next_action': issue['next_action']})\n    36\t    checks.append({'check': 'authoritative-case-clock', 'status': 'PASS' if case_clock else 'BLOCKED',\n    37\t                   'evidence': 'sources.json', 'detail': 'Caller-supplied scenario clock' if case_clock else 'No authoritative case clock supplied; retrieval timestamps are not scenario time',\n    38\t                   'next_action': 'Verify supplied authority before batch consumption' if case_clock else 'Obtain explicit date, time and timezone from the exercise facilitator'})\n    39\t    checks.append({'check': 'native-policy-processing', 'status': 'BLOCKED', 'evidence': 'sources.json',\n    40\t                   'detail': 'Complete native policy rule interpretation and final business compliance are not established by acquisition',\n    41\t                   'next_action': 'Obtain the full authoritative policy and validate rule coverage before policy-dependent processing'})\n    42\t    capture_complete = all(row['status'] == 'read' for row in manifest['files'])\n    43\t    status = 'FAIL' if errors else 'BLOCKED' if any(c['status'] == 'BLOCKED' for c in checks) else 'PASS'\n    44\t    report = {'schema_version': 'travel-claim-live-run/1', 'run_id': run_id, 'mode': 'live-source-attempt',\n    45\t              'status': status, 'fresh_reads_attempted': len(manifest['files']), 'cache_fallback_used': False,\n    46\t              'acquisition_status': 'PASS' if capture_complete and not errors else 'FAIL' if errors else 'BLOCKED',\n    47\t              'final_live_source_compliance': False, 'batches_consumed': [],\n    48\t              'source_manifest': {'path': 'sources.json', 'sha256': sha256_bytes((run_dir / 'sources.json').read_bytes())},\n    49\t              'parsed_records': {'path': 'parsed-records.json', 'sha256': sha256_bytes((run_dir / 'parsed-records.json').read_bytes())} if parsed else None,\n    50\t              'arrival_batches_observed': (parsed or {}).get('arrival_batches', []), 'checks': checks}\n    51\t    with (run_dir / 'live-run.json').open('x', encoding='utf-8') as stream:\n    52\t        stream.write(json.dumps(report, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + '\\n')\n    53\t    lines = ['# Project D fresh native-source attempt', '', f\"**{status}** — `{run_id}`; mode: `live-source-attempt`.\", '',\n    54\t             'All five original source locations were attempted in this invocation using native HTTP/export routes. '\n    55\t             'No previous retained input was substituted. Retrieval observations are not a case clock.', '',\n    56\t             f\"Acquisition: **{report['acquisition_status']}**. Final live-source compliance: **not established**. No arrival batches consumed.\", '',\n    57\t             'Complete relevant returned bytes, usable partial content and diagnostic responses are retained in this run and bound in `sources.json`.', '']\n    58\t    for check in checks:\n    59\t        lines += [f\"- **{check['status']}** `{check['check']}`: {check['detail']}\",\n    60\t                  f\"  - Evidence: `{check['evidence']}`; next action: {check['next_action']}\"]\n    61\t    with (run_dir / 'live-run.md').open('x', encoding='utf-8') as stream:\n    62\t        stream.write('\\n'.join(lines) + '\\n')\n    63\t    return report\n     1\t\"\"\"Deterministic claim summary CSV and owner-grouped local repair queue.\"\"\"\n     2\t\n     3\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     4\t\n     5\timport csv\n     6\timport json\n     7\timport os\n     8\timport tempfile\n     9\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    10\tfrom typing import Any\n    11\t\n    12\t\n    13\tCLAIMS_COLUMNS = (\n    14\t    \"claim_id\",\n    15\t    \"revision\",\n    16\t    \"trip_id\",\n    17\t    \"status\",\n    18\t    \"allowed_cents\",\n    19\t    \"paid_cents\",\n    20\t    \"balance_cents\",\n    21\t    \"next_owner\",\n    22\t    \"reason\",\n    23\t)\n    24\t\n    25\tCLAIM_STATUSES = {\n    26\t    \"pending\", \"held\", \"ready\", \"closed-reimbursed\", \"closed-no-payment\", \"rejected\", \"withdrawn\"\n    27\t}\n    28\t\n    29\tREPAIR_ITEM_FIELDS = (\n    30\t    \"item_id\",\n    31\t    \"subject_type\",\n    32\t    \"subject_id\",\n    33\t    \"revision\",\n    34\t    \"source_refs\",\n    35\t    \"missing_or_return_reason\",\n    36\t    \"owner\",\n    37\t    \"next_action\",\n    38\t)\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\tdef _money(value: Any, field: str, allow_negative: bool = False) -> int | None:\n    42\t    if value is None:\n    43\t        return None\n    44\t    if isinstance(value, bool) or not isinstance(value, int):\n    45\t        raise ValueError(f\"{field} must be integer cents or null\")\n    46\t    if not allow_negative and value < 0:\n    47\t        raise ValueError(f\"{field} cannot be negative\")\n    48\t    return value\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef write_claims_csv(claims: list[dict], path: Path) -> None:\n    52\t    \"\"\"Write one row per supplied current claim with the required exact header.\"\"\"\n    53\t    ids = [claim.get(\"claim_id\") for claim in claims]\n    54\t    if any(not value for value in ids) or len(ids) != len(set(ids)):\n    55\t        raise ValueError(\"claims must contain one nonempty, unique current row per claim_id\")\n    56\t    prepared = []\n    57\t    for claim in sorted(claims, key=lambda row: row[\"claim_id\"]):\n    58\t        missing = set(CLAIMS_COLUMNS) - set(claim)\n    59\t        if missing:\n    60\t            raise ValueError(f\"claim {claim.get('claim_id')} is missing CSV fields: {sorted(missing)}\")\n    61\t        row = {key: claim[key] for key in CLAIMS_COLUMNS}\n    62\t        if isinstance(row[\"revision\"], bool) or not isinstance(row[\"revision\"], int) or row[\"revision\"] < 1:\n    63\t            raise ValueError(f\"claim {claim['claim_id']} revision must be a positive integer\")\n    64\t        for key in (\"claim_id\", \"trip_id\", \"status\", \"reason\"):\n    65\t            if not isinstance(row[key], str) or not row[key]:\n    66\t                raise ValueError(f\"{key} must be a nonempty string\")\n    67\t        if row[\"status\"] not in CLAIM_STATUSES:\n    68\t            raise ValueError(f\"unsupported claim status {row['status']!r}\")\n    69\t        row[\"allowed_cents\"] = _money(row[\"allowed_cents\"], \"allowed_cents\")\n    70\t        row[\"paid_cents\"] = _money(row[\"paid_cents\"], \"paid_cents\")\n    71\t        row[\"balance_cents\"] = _money(row[\"balance_cents\"], \"balance_cents\", allow_negative=True)\n    72\t        for key in (\"next_owner\", \"reason\"):\n    73\t            if row[key] is not None and not isinstance(row[key], str):\n    74\t                raise ValueError(f\"{key} must be a string or null\")\n    75\t            row[key] = \"\" if row[key] is None else row[key]\n    76\t        prepared.append(row)\n    77\t    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    78\t    with path.open(\"x\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as stream:\n    79\t        writer = csv.DictWriter(stream, fieldnames=CLAIMS_COLUMNS, extrasaction=\"raise\")\n    80\t        writer.writeheader()\n    81\t        writer.writerows(prepared)\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\tdef new_repair_queue() -> dict:\n    85\t    return {\"queue_version\": \"owner-queue/1\", \"items\": {}, \"events\": []}\n    86\t\n    87\t\n    88\tdef add_repair_item(\n    89\t    queue: dict,\n    90\t    *,\n    91\t    item_id: str,\n    92\t    subject_type: str,\n    93\t    subject_id: str,\n    94\t    revision: int,\n    95\t    source_refs: list[str],\n    96\t    missing_or_return_reason: str,\n    97\t    owner: str,\n    98\t    next_action: str,\n    99\t    run_id: str,\n   100\t    batch_id: str,\n   101\t) -> None:\n   102\t    \"\"\"Add a distinct open item. Request content is a local draft only.\"\"\"\n   103\t    if not item_id or item_id in queue[\"items\"]:\n   104\t        raise ValueError(f\"repair item ID is empty or already exists: {item_id!r}\")\n   105\t    if subject_type not in {\"claim\", \"trip\", \"permit\"}:\n   106\t        raise ValueError(\"subject_type must be claim, trip, or permit\")\n   107\t    if not subject_id or not owner or not missing_or_return_reason or not next_action:\n   108\t        raise ValueError(\"subject, owner, reason, and next action are required\")\n   109\t    if isinstance(revision, bool) or not isinstance(revision, int) or revision < 1:\n   110\t        raise ValueError(\"revision must be a positive integer\")\n   111\t    if not isinstance(source_refs, list) or not all(isinstance(ref, str) and ref for ref in source_refs):\n   112\t        raise ValueError(\"source_refs must be a list of nonempty references\")\n   113\t    item = {\n   114\t        \"item_id\": item_id,\n   115\t        \"subject_type\": subject_type,\n   116\t        \"subject_id\": subject_id,\n   117\t        \"revision\": revision,\n   118\t        \"source_refs\": list(dict.fromkeys(source_refs)),\n   119\t        \"missing_or_return_reason\": missing_or_return_reason,\n   120\t        \"owner\": owner,\n   121\t        \"next_action\": next_action,\n   122\t        \"status\": \"open\",\n   123\t        \"run_id\": run_id,\n   124\t        \"batch_id\": batch_id,\n   125\t        \"response_id\": None,\n   126\t        \"resolution_source_refs…1066 tokens truncated…esolution_source_refs\"] = normalized_refs\n   213\t        else:\n   214\t            item[\"status\"] = \"open\"\n   215\t        queue[\"events\"].append({\n   216\t            \"event\": \"response-recorded\",\n   217\t            \"item_id\": item_id,\n   218\t            \"response_id\": response_id,\n   219\t            \"outcome\": kind,\n   220\t            \"note\": outcome.get(\"note\"),\n   221\t            \"source_refs\": normalized_refs,\n   222\t            \"run_id\": run_id,\n   223\t            \"batch_id\": batch_id,\n   224\t            \"status\": item[\"status\"],\n   225\t        })\n   226\t\n   227\t\n   228\tdef update_repair_item(\n   229\t    queue: dict,\n   230\t    *,\n   231\t    item_id: str,\n   232\t    update_id: str,\n   233\t    run_id: str,\n   234\t    batch_id: str,\n   235\t    revision: int | None = None,\n   236\t    source_refs: list[str] | None = None,\n   237\t    missing_or_return_reason: str | None = None,\n   238\t    owner: str | None = None,\n   239\t    next_action: str | None = None,\n   240\t) -> None:\n   241\t    \"\"\"Update a repair item's mutable trace fields without losing its history.\n   242\t\n   243\t    Item and subject identity never change. Advancing its subject revision\n   244\t    reopens the item and clears the prior resolution pointer while preserving\n   245\t    the prior response and fields in the append-only history.\n   246\t    \"\"\"\n   247\t    if not update_id:\n   248\t        raise ValueError(\"update_id is required\")\n   249\t    if item_id not in queue.get(\"items\", {}):\n   250\t        raise KeyError(f\"unknown repair item {item_id}\")\n   251\t    item = queue[\"items\"][item_id]\n   252\t    changes = {}\n   253\t    if revision is not None:\n   254\t        if isinstance(revision, bool) or not isinstance(revision, int) or revision < 1:\n   255\t            raise ValueError(\"revision must be a positive integer\")\n   256\t        if revision < item[\"revision\"]:\n   257\t            raise ValueError(\"repair item revision cannot move backwards\")\n   258\t        changes[\"revision\"] = revision\n   259\t    if source_refs is not None:\n   260\t        if not isinstance(source_refs, list) or not all(isinstance(ref, str) and ref for ref in source_refs):\n   261\t            raise ValueError(\"source_refs must be a list of nonempty references\")\n   262\t        changes[\"source_refs\"] = list(dict.fromkeys(source_refs))\n   263\t    for field, value in ((\"missing_or_return_reason\", missing_or_return_reason),\n   264\t                         (\"owner\", owner), (\"next_action\", next_action)):\n   265\t        if value is not None:\n   266\t            if not isinstance(value, str) or not value.strip():\n   267\t                raise ValueError(f\"{field} must be a nonempty string\")\n   268\t            changes[field] = value\n   269\t    replay = next((event for event in queue[\"events\"] if event.get(\"event\") == \"item-updated\"\n   270\t                   and event.get(\"update_id\") == update_id), None)\n   271\t    normalized = {key: changes[key] for key in sorted(changes)}\n   272\t    if replay is not None:\n   273\t        if replay.get(\"item_id\") == item_id and replay.get(\"changes\") == normalized:\n   274\t            return\n   275\t        raise ValueError(f\"conflicting replay for repair update {update_id}\")\n   276\t    if not changes:\n   277\t        raise ValueError(\"repair item update contains no field changes\")\n   278\t    before = {key: item[key] for key in changes}\n   279\t    if all(before[key] == changes[key] for key in changes):\n   280\t        raise ValueError(\"repair item update does not change any field\")\n   281\t    history = {\n   282\t        \"event\": \"item-updated\", \"update_id\": update_id,\n   283\t        \"previous\": before, \"changes\": normalized,\n   284\t        \"previous_status\": item[\"status\"], \"previous_response_id\": item[\"response_id\"],\n   285\t        \"previous_resolution_source_refs\": list(item[\"resolution_source_refs\"]),\n   286\t        \"run_id\": run_id, \"batch_id\": batch_id,\n   287\t    }\n   288\t    item[\"history\"].append(history)\n   289\t    item.update(changes)\n   290\t    if \"revision\" in changes and changes[\"revision\"] != before[\"revision\"]:\n   291\t        item[\"status\"] = \"open\"\n   292\t        item[\"response_id\"] = None\n   293\t        item[\"resolution_source_refs\"] = []\n   294\t    queue[\"events\"].append({\n   295\t        \"event\": \"item-updated\", \"item_id\": item_id, \"update_id\": update_id,\n   296\t        \"changes\": normalized, \"run_id\": run_id, \"batch_id\": batch_id,\n   297\t        \"status\": item[\"status\"],\n   298\t    })\n   299\t\n   300\t\n   301\tdef owner_grouped_view(queue: dict) -> dict[str, list[dict]]:\n   302\t    grouped: dict[str, list[dict]] = {}\n   303\t    for item in queue[\"items\"].values():\n   304\t        grouped.setdefault(item[\"owner\"], []).append(item)\n   305\t    return {owner: sorted(items, key=lambda row: row[\"item_id\"]) for owner, items in sorted(grouped.items())}\n   306\t\n   307\t\n   308\tdef load_repair_queue(path: Path) -> dict:\n   309\t    \"\"\"Load the persisted queue, validating individual item and audit structure.\"\"\"\n   310\t    try:\n   311\t        persisted = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n   312\t    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:\n   313\t        raise ValueError(f\"cannot read repair queue: {exc}\") from exc\n   314\t    if not isinstance(persisted, dict):\n   315\t        raise ValueError(\"repair queue must contain an object\")\n   316\t    if persisted.