ative reads in this run: **no**\",\n    53\t        f\"- Retained `sources.json` SHA-256: `{manifest_hash}`\",\n    54\t        (f\"- Case clock: **supplied** (`{parsed['case_clock']}`; supplied authority remains subject to human review).\"\n    55\t         if parsed.get(\"case_clock\") else\n    56\t         f\"- Case clock: **unresolved** ({clock_issue.get('owner', 'Exercise facilitator')}; {clock_issue.get('next_action', 'obtain authoritative case clock')})\"),\n    57\t        (\"- Reimbursement policy POL-2026.2: **retained**; eligibility, entitlement, caps, readiness, and final closure remain unresolved.\"\n    58\t         if policy_retained else\n    59\t         \"- Reimbursement policy POL-2026.2: **unavailable**; eligibility, entitlement, caps, readiness, and final closure remain unresolved.\"),\n    60\t        f\"- Parsed input: `{OUTPUT_NAME}` SHA-256 `{hashlib.sha256((snapshots[0].parents[1] / OUTPUT_NAME).read_bytes()).hexdigest()}`; parsed source content remains in that file.\",\n    61\t        \"- Retained source observations: \" + \"; \".join(\n    62\t            f\"`{row['source_id']}`={row['status']}\" for row in json.loads(\n    63\t                (snapshots[0].parents[1] / \"sources.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    64\t            )[\"files\"]\n    65\t        ) + \".\",\n    66\t        \"\",\n    67\t        \"## Batch projections\",\n    68\t        \"\",\n    69\t    ]\n    70\t    for path in snapshots:\n    71\t        snapshot = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    72\t        lines.append(\n    73\t            f\"- `{path.relative_to(path.parents[1])}` — {len(snapshot['claims'])} current claim rows, \"\n    74\t            f\"{len(snapshot['travel_cancellations'])} independent cancellation processes, \"\n    75\t            f\"{len(snapshot['issues'])} issues; schema and source/predecessor hashes verified.\"\n    76\t        )\n    77\t    lines.extend([\n    78\t        \"\",\n    79\t        \"Each snapshot retains the observed claim revision and matching decision IDs. Decisions are not treated as proof of policy compliance. Finance event identities and supported confirmed cash are retained. Recorded ledger obligations are separate from entitlement and current-revision authorization. Claim monetary entitlement and balance remain null when unsupported.\",\n    80\t        \"\",\n    81\t        \"Independent valid records continue through the replay while unresolved claims remain pending. External blockers prevent authoritative live-run conclusions, not retention of independent evidence or partial progress.\",\n    82\t        \"\",\n    83\t    ])\n    84\t    lines.extend([\n    85\t        \"## Recorded Finance obligations and cash\", \"\",\n    86\t        \"Obligation (EUR) is the ledger's recorded commitment amount, not a payment or approved reimbursement entitlement. \"\n    87\t        \"Ledger differences below compare that recorded amount with confirmed transfers minus linked refunds. \"\n    88\t        \"They do not establish claim eligibility, payment readiness or closure. Claim balance_cents remains null without a separately supported current-revision authorization.\", \"\",\n    89\t        \"Native Finance rows have no claim-revision column. Arrival revision context identifies the source-observed revision at first delivery; \"\n    90\t        \"it is not an explicit authorization binding, and redelivery never changes it. Adjustments/resolutions record obligation amounts rather than cash. \"\n    91\t        \"Cancellation/retry events are not refunds or proof that an obligation is zero.\", \"\",\n    92\t    ])\n    93\t    latest_snapshot = json.loads(snapshots[-1].read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    94\t    for claim in latest_snapshot[\"claims\"]:\n    95\t        evidence = claim.get(\"finance_evidence\", {})\n    96\t        obligation = evidence.get(\"recorded_obligation\")\n    97\t        if obligation is None:\n    98\t            continue\n