.py:265), compared with policy completion and cancellation rules at [policy line 23](tests/fixtures/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:23) and [line 33](tests/fixtures/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:33). |\n| 4 | **FAIL** | **Cancellation consequences cannot reach resolved/no-financial-effect states.** Projections always emit `financial_status=\"unresolved\"` at [integration.py:392](src/travel_claim/integration.py:392). All four retained processes, including no-claim TC122, consequently remain unresolved. |\n| 5 | **FAIL** | **Blank commitment evidence produces contradictory permit findings.** A synthetic approved permit with no first commitment was authorized by the permit evaluator, but eligibility generated `late_permit` by parsing `None` as a date: [exceptions.py:153](src/travel_claim/exceptions.py:153). [Policy line 27](tests/fixtures/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:27) explicitly defines blank as no commitment yet. |\n| 6 | **FAIL** | **Terminal claims receive misleading follow-ups and CSV reasons.** C13 is withdrawn and C14 rejected, yet each has eight open repairs requesting further authorization. Their CSV reason is “no supported authorized obligation,” replacing the supplied withdrawal/rejection reason. Sources: initial binder pages 13–14 and Review ledger row 40. See [integration.py:171](src/travel_claim/integration.py:171) and [offline_replay.py:268](src/travel_claim/offline_replay.py:268). |\n| 7 | **FAIL** | **The correction report contradicts the verified clock.** It still states that the authoritative case clock is unconfirmed, despite readiness passing the supplemental date binding. The wording is hardcoded at [revalidation.py:91](src/travel_claim/revalidation.py:91). |\n\nReadiness currently reproduces these outputs faithfully; therefore its structural checks can pass while these semantic defects remain.\n\n**External blockers and verification limits**\n\n- **BLOCKED:** Complete native Notion acquisition has not been established. The browser copy must remain distinctly labeled.\n- **BLOCKED:** Current claim-specific reviews, exceptions, request/version authority, and required Finance resolutions remain unresolved where unsupported. They must not be generated automatically.\n- **NOT VERIFIED:** Complete original assignment compliance—the repository links the assignment but lacks retained assignment text.\n- **Preservation:** All 129 hashes matched before interruption. The original preservation manifest is unavailable after resumption, so a fresh complete 129-file comparison is **NOT VERIFIED**. Policy and interview hashes match their known values; native retained-byte verification passes; tracked files remain unchanged.\n\n**Recommended Step 184**\n\nImplement **expense-source and reviewer-clock admission hardening** before broader closure work.\n\nScope: `expenses.py`, `approvals.py`, supporting integration/readiness checks where necessary, and focused regression tests.\n\nRequire verified bindings for calculation evidence and enforce the existing clock semantics before reviewer replies become current authority. Preserve rejected evidence and historical decisions. Tests should reproduce both confirmed defects, including future and same-day reviews, missing/mismatched hashes, unaffected valid claims, and prevention of closure from unbound evidence.\n\nAfterward: correct policy-grounded closure/cancellation transitions, unify permit findings, repair terminal-claim handoffs, rerun end-to-end validation, recover the original preservation manifest, and complete authoritative assignment/source-access verification.","started_at":1792061048,"completed_at":1792061472,"duration_ms":460022,"time_to_first_token_ms":6095}}
