out costs or financial obligations is recorded as a no-financial-effect trip/permit process, without inventing a claim. For already-spent costs, retain purchase and employee-payment evidence, initial filing dates and reviewed arithmetic; cancellation is not zero entitlement or a promised refund. The original planned trip end still sets the filing deadline. Add a travel_cancellation eligibility finding and require explicit Finance cost disposition plus fresh current claim review containing the cancellation context. A Finance exception covering travel_cancellation must also supply the exact travel_cancellation_id, bound actor, claim/revision, expense, replacement allowed original amount and reason. An amount-only or unrelated exception does not resolve it. Review packets expose trip/permit revisions and relevant travel_cancellation_ids; a pre-confirmation packet is not post-cancellation authorization. A later cancellation never by itself creates permit_unapproved for an arrangement/payment made with timely valid permission. Pre-existing late_permit or permit_unapproved findings remain independent and need their own explicit coverage. A cancellation waiver never retroactively approves arrangements. Do not guess ordering between a date-only payment and a same-day cancellation when the timing matters; retain the uncertainty for supervisor/Finance resolution.\n\nBusiness cancellation and Finance cancellation are distinct. When business cancellation is confirmed before any reimbursement request for the affected obligation has been accepted or dispatched, the bound Finance cost disposition and fresh cancellation-aware claim reviews establish the new reimbursement basis. Its first accepted request may close after confirmed settlement matches that basis and no other issue remains; the earlier business cancellation alone does not require a separate Finance resolution event. This does not waive the resolution requirement for a cancellation after acceptance/dispatch or reimbursement. After acceptance/dispatch retain the original request basis and hold competing replacements until supplied Finance status/cancellation/adjustment resolves the obligation. Only Finance accepted/adjustment/cancelled facts change accepted commitments; business confirmation cannot release them. After reimbursement reopen reconciliation; explicit current cost disposition and reviews, any needed linked confirmed refund and Finance resolution must agree before closure. Only the confirmed refund reduces net paid. Continue observing original requests after cancellation or claim reassignment, including late transfers. Maintain separate cancellation state and event references for every observed valid process, including trips with no claim; retain affected claim and original request links, unresolved/no-financial-effect/resolved consequence and next owner. Finance admitted event references remain separate from cancellation event references.","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":29738584},"formatted_output":"            issue(record, 'different repeated action for an admitted process; history retained'); continue\n        trip_id, trip_rev = value.get('Trip reference'), revision(value.get('Trip revision'))\n        known_trips = [r for r in trips if source_values(r).get('Trip reference') == trip_id\n                       and (source_values(r).get('Arrival batch') is None or revision(source_values(r)['Arrival batch']) is not None\n                            and (arrival_batch is None or revision(source_values(r)['Arrival batch']) <= arrival_batch))]\n        matching = [r for r in known_trips if revision(source_values(r).get('Trip revision')) == trip_rev]\n        latest = max((revision(source_values(r).get('Trip revision')) or 0 for r in known_trips), default=0)\n        if not text_id(trip_id) or trip_rev is None or len(matching) != 1 or trip_rev != latest:\n            issue(record, 'unmatched, conflicting or stale trip target revision'); continue\n        trip = source_values(matching[0])\n        def permit_tuple(v):\n            return v.get('Permit reference') or None, revision(v.get('Permit revision'))\n        if permit_tuple(value) != permit_tuple(trip) or (kind == 'permit' and not all(permit_tuple(value))):\n            issue(record, 'associated permit target does not match exact trip/permit revisions'); continue\n        if (bool(value.get('Permit reference')) != bool(revision(value.get('Permit revision')))\n                or value.get('Permit revision') not in (None, '') and revision(value.get('Permit revision')) is None):\n            issue(record, 'incomplete permit identity/revision'); continue\n        employee = trip.get('Employee ID')\n        directory = [r for r in people if source_values(r).get('Employee ID') == employee]\n        expected_actor = employee if action == 'requested' else source_values(directory[0]).get('Supervisor') if len(directory) == 1 else None\n        if len(directory) != 1 or not text_id(expected_actor) or value.get('Acting employee or supervisor') != expected_actor:\n            issue(record, 'cancellation actor is not the trip employee or authorized directory supervisor'); continue\n        try:\n            stamp = utc_time(value.get('Activity time (UTC)'))\n            error = observation_error(stamp, clock)\n            if error: raise ValueError(error)\n            if action == 'requested':\n                if value.get('Initiation activity reference') or value.get('Effective time (UTC)'):\n                    raise ValueError('initiation cannot name an initiation or effective time')\n            else:\n                initiation = admitted.get(value.get('Initiation activity reference'))\n                if not initiation:\n                    raise ValueError('confirmation has an unresolved initiation reference; recheck on arrival')\n                start = source_values(initiation)\n                if start.get('Action') != 'requested' or start.get('Cancellation reference') != process_id or target(start) != target(value):\n                    raise ValueError('confirmation does not match the exact initiation/process/target')\n                if stamp <= utc_time(start.get('Activity time (UTC)')):\n                    raise ValueError('confirmation must occur strictly after initiation')\n                if utc_time(value.get('Effective time (UTC)')) != stamp:\n                    raise ValueError('scheduled or backdated effective time is not cancellation authority')\n        except (ValueError, TypeError) as exc:\n            issue(record, str(exc)); continue\n        admitted[identity] = deepcopy(record); apply(record)\n    for record in records:\n        value = source_values(record); process_id = value.get('Cancellation reference'); kind = value.get('Cancelled subject')\n        if text_id(process_id) and kind in {'trip', 'permit'} and process_id not in processes:\n            processes[process_id] = {'cancellation_id': process_id,\n                'target': {'subject_type': kind, 'subject_id': value.get('Trip reference') if kind == 'trip' else value.get('Permit reference'),\n                           'revision': revision(value.get('Trip revision') if kind == 'trip' else value.get('Permit revision'))},\n                'state': 'unseen', 'activity_ids': [], 'history': [], 'next_action': 'resolve invalid or incomplete initiation evidence'}\n    return {'processes': processes, 'issues': issues, 'duplicate_events': duplicates, 'conflicting_events': conflicts,\n            'admitted_records': admitted, 'delivery_history': deepcopy(records), 'finance_effects': [], 'claim_effects': []}\n    for claim_id, record_set in history.get(\"claim\", {}).items():\n        current_revision = record_set[\"current_revision\"]\n        claim_revision = next(row for row in reversed(record_set[\"revisions\"]) if row[\"revision\"] == current_revision)\n        current_claims[claim_id] = claim_revision\n    cancellation_rows = _cancellation_rows(domain, history=history, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id, parsed=parsed)\n    finance_results = {}\n    for claim_id, claim_revision in current_claims.items():\n        record_set = history[\"claim\"][claim_id]\n        prior_finance = domain[\"finance_reconciliations\"].get(claim_id)\n        finance_results[claim_id] = reconcile_finance_events(\n            domain[\"finance_records\"], claim_id=claim_id,\n            current_revision=claim_revision[\"revision\"],\n            authorized_obligation=domain[\"authorized_obligations\"].get(claim_id),\n            revision_history=record_set[\"revisions\"],\n            previous_reconciliation=prior_finance,\n            source_classifications=domain[\"source_classifications\"],\n            event_context=finance_context(parsed, record_set[\"revisions\"], domain[\"finance_records\"], claim_id, arrival_batch),\n        )\n    from .budget import reconcile_budgets, attribute_costs\n    budgets=reconcile_budgets(parsed=parsed,history=history,finances=finance_results,arrival_batch=arrival_batch,\n        observations=source_observations or [],cancellations=cancellation_rows,prior=before_batch.get('budget'),raw_finance=domain['finance_records'])\n    attribution=attribute_costs(parsed=parsed,history=history,budgets=budgets,arrival_batch=arrival_batch,\n        observations=source_observations or [],cancellations=cancellation_rows)\n    budgets['cost_attribution']=attribution;budgets['claim_views']={}\n    domain['budget']=budgets\n    from .approvals import evaluate_permit\n    from .budget import permit_budget_context\n    domain['permit_approvals']={}\n    for permit_id,subject in history.get('permit',{}).items():\n        current=next(r for r in reversed(subject['revisions']) if r['revision']==subject['current_revision'])\n        key=f\"{permit_id}:r{current['revision']}\"\n        budget_context=permit_budget_context(parsed=parsed,trip_record=current['record'],budgets=budgets,\n            prior=(before_batch.get('permit_approvals',{}).get(key) or {}).get('budget_context'),arrival_batch=arrival_batch)\n        review=evaluate_permit(parsed=parsed,trip_record=current['record'],decisions=domain['decision_records'],\n            arrival_batch=arrival_batch,observations=source_observations or [],\n            prior=before_batch.get('permit_approvals',{}).get(key),cancellations=cancellation_rows,budget_context=budget_context)\n        domain['permit_approvals'][key]=review\n        if not review['approved'] or not review['arrangement_authorized']:\n            item_id=f\"permit-approval:{key}\"\n            _open_issue_for_subject(domain['repair_queue'],item_id=item_id,subject_type='permit',subject_id=permit_id,\n                revision=current['revision'],refs=review['source_refs'],reason=f\"Permit review state: {review['state']}; arrangement authority/timing requires current evidence\",\n                owner='Travel Administration Lead',next_action='Obtain current permit-role decisions and resolve timing or cancellation holds',run_id=run_id,batch_id=batch_id)\n        if f\"permit-approval:{key}\" in domain['repair_queue']['items']:\n            record_evidence_validation(domain['repair_queue'],item_id=f\"permit-approval:{key}\",\n                supported=review['approved'] and review['arrangement_authorized'],source_refs=review['source_refs'],run_id=run_id,batch_id=batch_id)\n    domain.setdefault('permit_approval_history',[]).append({'batch_id':batch_id,'permits':deepcopy(domain['permit_approvals'])})\n    for claim_id,claim_revision in current_claims.items():\n        prior_finance=before_batch.get('finance_reconciliations',{}).get(claim_id)\n        workflow = connect_claim(parsed=parsed, claim=claim_revision, decisions=domain[\"decision_records\"],\n            finance_events=domain[\"finance_records\"], finance=finance_results[claim_id],\n            cancellations=cancellation_rows, arrival_batch=arrival_batch,\n            source_observations=source_observations or [], prior_finance=prior_finance,\n            source_classifications=domain[\"source_classifications\"],\n            prior_workflow=before_batch.get(\"ordinary_workflows\", {}).get(claim_id),\n            budget_data=budgets,prepaid_data=attribution,prior_budget_view=before_batch.get(\"budget\",{}).get(\"claim_views\",{}).get(claim_id))\n        finance_results[claim_id] = workflow.pop(\"finance\")\n        budgets[\"claim_views\"][claim_id]=deepcopy(workflow[\"budget_view\"])\n        domain[\"ordinary_workflows\"][claim_id] = workflow\n        domain[\"ordinary_workflow_history\"].append({\"batch_id\": batch_id, \"workflow\": deepcopy(workflow)})\n    domain[\"finance_reconciliations\"] = finance_results\n    for scope in budgets['scopes'].values():\n        for request in scope['requests'].values():\n            result=finance_results.get(request['claim_id'],{})\n            matching=(result.get('recorded_obligation') or {}).get('request_id')==request['request_id']\n            authorization=result.get('authorized_obligation') if matching else None\n            request['authorized_obligation_cents']=authorization['amount_cents'] if authorization else None\n            request['authorized_balance_cents']=result.get('balance_cents') if authorization else None\n    domain.setdefault('budget_history',[]).append({'batch_id':batch_id,'budget':deepcopy(budgets)})\n    for claim_id,workflow in domain['ordinary_workflows'].items():\n        for n,issue in enumerate(workflow['budget_view']['issues']):\n            item_id=f\"budget-detail:{claim_id}:r{workflow['revision']}:{_digest(issue['reason'])[:12]}\"\n            _open_issue_for_subject(domain['repair_queue'],item_id=item_id,subject_type='claim',subject_id=claim_id,\n                revision=workflow['revision'],refs=issue['source_refs'],reason=issue['reason'],owner=issue['owner'],\n                next_action=issue['next_action'],run_id=run_id,batch_id=batch_id)\n        current={_digest(i['reason'])[:12] for i in workflow['budget_view']['issues']}\n        for item_id,item in domain['repair_queue']['items'].items():\n            if item_id.startswith(f\"budget-detail:{claim_id}:r{workflow['revision']}:\") and item_id.rsplit(':',1)[-1] not in current:\n                record_evidence_validation(domain['repair_queue'],item_id=item_id,supported=True,\n                    source_refs=workflow['budget_view']['source_refs'],run_id=run_id,batch_id=batch_id)\n    record_executed_rechecks(domain, before_batch, batch_id=batch_id)\n    _sync_finance_repairs(domain, finance_results, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id)\n\n    # Policy and case-clock blockers are copied from parser/source evidence and\n    # deliberately remain outside any fabricated claim/decision outcome.\n    blockers = []\n    for row in parsed.get(\"unresolved_issues\", []):\n        blocker = {\n            \"record_id\": row[\"record_id\"],\n            \"reason\": row.get(\"reason\", \"Unresolved source issue\"),\n            \"owner\": row.get(\"owner\", \"Exercise facilitator\"),\n            \"resolution_needed\": row.get(\"next_action\", \"Obtain the missing authoritative evidence\"),\n            \"subject_type\": row.get(\"subject_type\"),\n            \"subject_id\": row.get(\"subject_id\"),\n            \"affected_scope\": row.get(\"affected_scope\"),\n        ],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"cancellation_id\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          },\n          \"target_type\": {\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"trip\",\n              \"permit\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"trip_id\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          },\n          \"trip_revision\": {\n            \"type\": \"integer\",\n            \"minimum\": 1\n          },\n          \"permit_id\": {\n            \"type\": [\n              \"string\",\n              \"null\"\n            ],\n            \"minLength\": 1\n          },\n          \"permit_revision\": {\n            \"type\": [\n              \"integer\",\n              \"null\"\n            ],\n            \"minimum\": 1\n          },\n          \"status\": {\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"requested\",\n              \"confirmed\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"admitted_cancellation_event_ids\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"minLength\": 1\n            },\n            \"uniqueItems\": true,\n            \"minItems\": 1,\n            \"description\": \"Only lawfully admitted Travel cancellations activity IDs, retaining initiation/confirmation identity and authority through the bound source records.\"\n          },\n          \"requested_at\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"format\": \"date-time\"\n    item = final['domain']['repair_queue']['items']['ordinary:SYN-C01:r1:financial_closure']\n    assert item['status'] == 'resolved' and item['response_id'] is None\n    assert item['request_draft']['sent'] is False\n    assert item['history'][-1]['event'] == 'evidence-revalidated'\n    path = tmp_path / 'queue.json'\n    write_repair_queue(first['domain']['repair_queue'], path)\n    write_repair_queue(final['domain']['repair_queue'], path)\n    assert load_repair_queue(path)['items'][item['item_id']]['status'] == 'resolved'\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize('missing', ['receipt', 'settled-proof', 'policy', 'policy-source', 'review',\n                                  'request', 'request-amount', 'revision', 'closure-authority', 'clock'])\ndef test_synthetic_path_cannot_close_when_a_required_condition_is_missing(missing):\n    parsed = synthetic(); records = parsed['records']\n    if missing == 'receipt': records['receipts'] = []\n    elif missing == 'settled-proof':\n        next(s for s in parsed['workbook_sheets'] if s['name'] == 'Merchant payments')['records'][0]['values']['Payment status']['value'] = 'pending'\n    elif missing == 'policy': records['workflow_policy_rules'] = []\n    elif missing == 'policy-source': records['workflow_policy_rules'][0]['source_sha256'] = '0' * 64\n    elif missing == 'review': records['decisions'][0]['values']['Outcome']['value'] = 'return'\n    elif missing == 'request': records['reimbursement_requests'] = []\n    elif missing == 'request-amount': records['reimbursement_requests'][0]['values']['Amount (EUR)']['value'] = 80\n    elif missing == 'revision': records['finance_events'][0]['values']['Claim revision']['value'] = 2\n    elif missing == 'closure-authority': records['closure_authorities'] = []\n    else: parsed['case_clock'] = None\n    result = batches(parsed)[-1]\n    assert workflow(result)['status'] == 'pending'\n    assert any(stage['status'] != 'PASS' for stage in workflow(result)['stages'])\n    assert any(item['status'] == 'open' for item in result['domain']['repair_queue']['items'].values())\n\"\"\"POL-2026.2 exception authority; mutations are explicitly synthetic probes.\"\"\"\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom test_expenses import setup, setfield, evaluate, merchant\nfrom test_ordinary import synthetic, batches, workflow, stages\nfrom test_revalidation import corrected\nfrom travel_claim.exceptions import (apply_coverage, covered_issues, finding, travel_findings, validate_exception)\nfrom travel_claim.expenses import evaluate_expenses, load_expense_policy\nfrom travel_claim.ordinary import expense_lines, fields, ref, table\n\nFIXTURES=Path(__file__).parent/'fixtures'\n\n\ndef exception(record, *, amount='80.00', covered='None', **overrides):\n    values={'Authorizing Finance officer':'FIN-01','Applies to claim':fields(record)['Claim reference'],\n        'Applies to revision':fields(record)['Revision'],'Expense reference':expense_lines(record)[0]['cost_id'],\n        'Allowed original amount':amount,'Covered issues':covered,'Exception reason':'SYNTHETIC explicit Finance disposition'}\