istant","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Project D — Step 186: Investigate and correct financial closure and cancellation defects.\n\nStart from verified commit faf1f780728c17440f133d8c334222fe6a6cb0cb.\n\nReview the Step 183 audit findings and current implementation, including finance.py, ordinary.py, integration.py, revalidation.py, approvals.py, and related tests.\n\n    Identify the exact remaining financial closure and cancellation defects. Do not assume that a previously reported issue still exists; verify it against current code and retained source evidence.\n\n    Create focused regression tests that reproduce each confirmed defect before implementing a fix.\n\n    Correct demonstrated defects involving financial closure, reimbursement eligibility, cancellation timing, supported obligations, payment/refund reconciliation, and dependencies between these stages.\n\nPreserve all admitted Finance events, original revisions, cancellation history, and source references. Never erase legitimate payments or refunds to make a claim appear closed.\n\nRequire source-supported current approvals, authorized obligations, reconciled net payments, Finance resolution, and no unresolved dependent issues before final financial closure.\n\nKeep independent valid claims progressing while holding only affected claims and dependent stages.\n\nPreserve the distinction between a business cancellation and a Finance cancellation. Do not invent cancellation approval or reimbursement authority.\n\nAdd synthetic and retained-evidence tests for corrections, cancellation sequences, partial payments, refunds, zero obligations, duplicate events, and closure attempts with unresolved dependencies.\n\nRun the full automated test suite and Git diff checks.\n\nVerify protected-file preservation using the available baseline manifest. If unavailable, report the limitation explicitly.\n\nDo not overwrite prior run artifacts or change original source evidence.\n\nDo not stage, commit, or push anything during Step 186.\n\nReport confirmed defects, fixes, exact passing test count, changed files, preservation results, and remaining blockers. Stop for review.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":264},"id":"msg_01a13f48-7df7-77b0-9734-40d6149f3b60","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792063076.8796887,"turn_id":"01a13f48-7c83-7c72-a773-e78f5db417e4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"I’ll recheck the closure and cancellation findings against the current code and policy, add failing regressions for confirmed defects, and then fix them. I’ll keep admitted money, revisions, and cancellation history intact, and leave claims pending where the evidence does not support closure.","type":"output_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":265},"id":"msg_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad0b66a8134819099feb60e78a6e09a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1792063082.5107837,"turn_id":"01a13f48-7c83-7c72-a773-e78f5db417e4"},"phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_4cbfdc0ca01049d0821ffdef5e29c52f","id":"ctc_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad0b66bce548190b9243cfb0121a56c","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git rev-parse HEAD; git status --short; cat src/travel_claim/ordinary.py\",\"max_output_tokens\":11500}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat src/travel_claim/finance.py; sed -n '235,455p' src/travel_claim/integration.py\",\"max_output_tokens\":12500}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat tests/test_ordinary.py; cat tests/test_revalidation.py; cat tests/test_retained_finance.py | head -115; ls /tmp/*hash* 2\u003e/dev/null\",\"max_output_tokens\":10000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1792063083.811485,"turn_id":"01a13f48-7c83-7c72-a773-e78f5db417e4"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_4cbfdc0ca01049d0821ffdef5e29c52f","guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000},"id":"ctco_01a13f48-ac30-7472-a747-9f049577d715","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1792063089.7127616,"turn_id":"01a13f48-7c83-7c72-a773-e78f5db417e4"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.1 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 25930)\nTotal output lines: 3\n\n{\"chunk_id\":\"9dcba1\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.027053,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":7084,\"output\":\"faf1f780728c17440f133d8c334222fe6a6cb0cb\\n?? artifacts/runs/\\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-evidence-audit-f98e044.md\\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-live-source-audit-87dbd1c.json\\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-live-source-audit-87dbd1c.md\\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91-validated/\\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-readiness-efc7e91/\\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-step157-revalidation/\\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-step167-audit-probes.json\\n?? artifacts/verification/project-d-step167-policy-gap-audit.md\\n?? user-provided-sources/\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Connected claim evaluation from retained facts and explicitly sourced rules.\\n\\nNo native policy definitions are inferred from interview descriptions, caps,\\nreview outcomes, or Finance acceptance. Missing authority remains blocked.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom copy import deepcopy\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\nfrom decimal import Decimal\\nimport re\\n\\nfrom .finance import _cents, reconcile_finance_events\\nfrom .workflow import row_values\\nfrom .expenses import evaluate_expenses, policy_valid\\nfrom .exceptions import travel_findings, review_binds_exception, source_bound\\nfrom .approvals import evaluate_reviews, evaluate_permit\\n\\nROLE_FIELDS = {\\\"administration\\\": \\\"Administration reviewer\\\", \\\"budget_owner\\\": \\\"Budget owner\\\",\\n               \\\"supervisor\\\": \\\"Supervisor\\\", \\\"director\\\": \\\"Director\\\"}\\n\\n\\ndef ref(row):\\n    return f\\\"{row.get('source_id')}@{row.get('source_sha256')}#{row.get('locator')}\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef fields(row):\\n    return {f['label'].strip(): f['value'] for f in row.get('fields', [])} if 'fields' in row else row_values(row)\\n\\n\\ndef table(parsed, key, tab):\\n    return parsed.get('records', {}).get(key, next((s['records'] for s in parsed.get('workbook_sheets', []) if s['name'] == tab), []))\\n\\n\\ndef expense_lines(record):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Read complete rows from the retained PDF layout; never guess a row.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    lines = []\\n    for raw in record.get('text', '').splitlines():\\n        if not re.match(r'^\\\\s*\\\\d+\\\\s+', raw):\\n            continue\\n        tokens = raw.split()\\n        if len(tokens) == 6:\\n            number, cost, receipt, submitted, amount, currency = tokens\\n        else:\\n            number = tokens[0]; cost = tokens[1] if len(tokens) \u003e 1 else 'unknown'\\n            receipt = submitted = amount = currency = None\\n        lines.append(dict(line=int(number), cost_id=cost, receipt_id=receipt,\\n            first_submitted_date=submitted, original_amount=amount.replace(',', '') if amount else None,\\n            original_cents=_cents(amount.replace(',', '')) if amount else None,\\n            currency=currency, source_refs=[ref(record)]))\\n    return lines\\n\\n\\ndef connect_claim(*, parsed, claim, decisions, finance_events, finance, cancellations,\\n                  arrival_batch, source_observations, prior_finance=None, source_classifications=None, prior_workflow=None, budget_data=None, prepaid_data=None, prior_budget_view=None):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Evaluate an ordinary path; each result keeps its evidence and owner.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    record = claim['record']; values = fields(record)\\n    claim_id, revision = claim['subject_id'], claim['revision']\\n    employee, trip_id = values.get('Employee'), claim.get('trip_id')\\n    stages = []\\n    def stage(name, condition, refs, detail, owner, action, fail=False):\\n        row = dict(stage=name, status='PASS' if condition else 'FAIL' if fail else 'BLOCKED',\\n                   source_refs=list(dict.fromkeys([ref(record)] + refs)), detail=detail, owner=owner, next_action=action)\\n        stages.append(row)\\n        return bool(condition)\\n    def trusted(row):\\n        return bool(row.get('locator')) and any(o.get('source_id') == row.get('source_id') and\\n            o.get('sha256') == row.get('source_sha256') and o.get('status') == 'read' and not o.get('missing_scope')\\n            for o in source_observations)\\n    def visible(row):\\n        try:\\n            batch = fields(row).get('Arrival batch')\\n            return not isinstance(batch, bool) and int(batch) == float(batch) and 0 \u003c int(batch) \u003c= arrival_batch\\n        except (ValueError, TypeError, OverflowError):\\n            return False\\n\\n    trips = [r for r in table(parsed, 'trips', 'Trips') if fields(r).get('Trip reference') == trip_id\\n             and str(fields(r).get('Trip revision')) in {str(claim.get('trip_revision')), f\\\"{claim.get('trip_revision')}.0\\\"}]\\n    trip = fields(trips[0]) if len(trips) == 1 else {}\\n    linked = stage('claim_trip_link', len(trips) == 1 and trip.get('Employee ID') == employee\\n                   and len([r for r in finance['revision_history'] if r['revision'] == revision]) == 1,\\n                   [ref(record)] + [ref(r) for r in trips], 'Exact claim, trip revision and employee linkage',\\n                   'Travel Administration Lead', 'Verify the exact employee, trip ID and trip revision binding')\\n    people = [r for r in table(parsed, 'people', 'People') if fields(r).get('Employee ID') == employee]\\n    person = fields(people[0]) if len(people) == 1 else {}\\n    lead = person.get('Administration reviewer') or 'Travel Administration Lead'\\n    finance_owner = person.get('Finance officer') or 'Finance'\\n\\n    policy_source_ids = {'synthetic-policy'} if parsed.get('evidence_mode') == 'synthetic-test' else {'policy-pol-2026-2'}\\n    rules = [r for r in table(parsed, 'workflow_policy_rules', 'Workflow policy rules')\\n             if r.get('source_id') in policy_source_ids and trusted(r) and visible(r)]\\n    policy_record = rules[0] if len(rules) == 1 else None\\n    policy = fields(policy_record) if policy_record else {}\\n    policy_supported = (policy.get('Rule set') == 'exact-paid-costs-v1'\\n                        and isinstance(policy.get('Policy revision'), str) and bool(policy.get('Policy revision'))\\n                        and isinstance(policy.get('Eligible categories'), list)\\n                        and isinstance(policy.get('Uncapped categories'), list)\\n                        and isinstance(policy.get('Required claim roles'), list) and bool(policy.get('Required claim roles'))\\n                        and set(policy.get('Required claim roles')) \u003c= set(ROLE_FIELDS)\\n                        and policy.get('Receipt required') is True and policy.get('Settled merchant proof required') is True\\n                        and policy.get('No self review') is True and policy.get('FX date basis') == 'paid-date'\\n                        and policy.get('Closure rule') == 'entitlement-authorization-net-cash-no-blockers'\\n                        and isinstance(policy.get('Domestic permit required'), bool))\\n    policy_refs = [ref(policy_record)] if policy_record else []\\n    affected = [c for c in cancellations if claim_id in c['affected_claim_ids']]\\n    from .budget import permit_budget_context\\n    permit_budget=permit_budget_context(parsed=parsed,trip_record=trips[0] if len(trips)==1 else {},\\n        budgets=budget_data or {'scopes':{}},prior=((prior_workflow or {}).get('permit_approval') or {}).get('budget_context'),arrival_batch=arrival_batch)\\n    permit_review = evaluate_permit(parsed=parsed, trip_record=trips[0] if len(trips)==1 else {},\\n        decisions=decisions, arrival_batch=arrival_batch, observations=source_observations,\\n        prior=(prior_workflow or {}).get('permit_approval'),\\n        cost_ids=[line['cost_id'] for line in expense_lines(record)],cancellations=cancellations,budget_context=permit_budget)\\n    permission = linked and permit_review['arrangement_authorized']\\n    permission_refs = [ref(r) for r in trips] + policy_refs + permit_review['source_refs']\\n    stage('travel_permission', permission, permission_refs,\\n          'Travel permission requires sourced policy and exact permit authority/timing where required; affected cancellations block the ordinary path',\\n          lead, 'Obtain the policy-defined permission requirement and matching permit approvals/timing; resolve affected cancellations')\\n\\n    lines = expense_lines(record)\\n    eligibility = travel_findings(trip=trip, employee=employee, decisions=decisions, people=table(parsed, 'people', 'People'),\\n        cancellations=cancellations, fields=fields, ref=ref, observations=source_observations,\\n        trip_source_refs=[ref(r) for r in trips]) if policy_valid(parsed.get('expense_policy')) else []\\n    if trip.get('International') is True and not permit_review['approved'] and not any(f['issue']=='permit_unapproved' for f in eligibility):\\n        from .exceptions import finding\\n        eligibility.append(finding('permit_unapproved', 'Current permit replies/packets do not establish required approval authority', permit_review['source_refs']))\\n    calculation = evaluate_expenses(lines=lines, parsed=parsed, employee=employee, trip_id=trip_id,\\n        trip=trip, record=record, history=finance['revision_history'], fields=fields, ref=ref, table=table,\\n        eligibility_findings=eligibility, observations=source_observations)\\n    from .budget import claim_budget_view\\n    budget_view=claim_budget_view(parsed=parsed,claim=claim,lines=lines,budgets=budget_data or {'scopes':{}},\\n        attribution=prepaid_data or {'costs':{},'unallocated_costs':{}},prior=prior_budget_view,arrival_batch=arrival_batch)\\n    stage('budget_availability',budget_view['status']=='PASS',budget_view['source_refs'],\\n        '; '.join(i['reason'] for i in budget_view['issues']) or 'Complete scope ledger supports the incremental request; funds do not constitute approval',\\n        budget_view['owner'],'Review the complete department/project/period ledger and obtain current budget-owner authorization')\\n    stage('prior_cost_attribution',budget_view['remaining_request_cents'] is not None,budget_view['source_refs'],\\n        'Each cost is linked to supported earlier obligations or remains unresolved; no aggregate prorating',finance_owner,\\n        'Resolve exact original claim/cost/request links before any replacement or additional reimbursement')\\n    evidence_ok = bool(lines) and len({line['cost_id'] for line in lines}) == len(lines) and all(\\n        line['evidence_status'] == 'PASS' for line in lines)\\n    evidence_refs = [ref(record)] + [r for line in lines for r in line['source_refs']]\\n    stage('supporting_evidence', evidence_ok, evidence_refs,\\n          'Current revision receipts and settled merchant proof must match employee, trip, cost, currency and gross',\\n          employee or 'Employee', 'Supply matching receipts and settled merchant proof for every expense')\\n    filing_ok = bool(lines) and all(line['filing_status'] == 'PASS' for line in lines)\\n    stage('filing_deadline', filing_ok, evidence_refs,\\n          '; '.join(f\\\"{line['cost_id']}: {line['reason']}\\\" for line in lines) or 'Missing expense submissions',\\n          finance_owner, 'Verify cost-specific original submission dates, trip end and employee payment; obtain explicit Finance exception for late filing')\\n    waived_permission = bool(eligibility and any(f['issue'] in {'late_permit', 'permit_unapproved'} for f in eligibility)\\n        and lines and all(l['eligibility_status'] == 'PASS' for l in lines))\\n    reimbursement_permission = permission or (linked and permit_review.get('arrangements_at_commitment_supported',False)) or (linked and policy_supported and waived_permission)\\n    policy_ok = policy_supported and evidence_ok and linked and reimbursement_permission and calculation['status'] == 'PASS' and budget_view['remaining_request_cents'] is not None\\n    for line in lines:\\n        line['allowed_cents'] = line['calculated_cents'] if policy_ok else None\\n        if not policy_ok:\\n            line['status'] = 'unresolved'\\n    attributed={l['cost_id']:l for l in budget_view['lines']}\\n    for line in lines:\\n        if policy_ok:\\n            line['allowed_cents']=attributed[line['cost_id']]['remaining_request_cents']\\n            if line['allowed_cents'] is None:\\n                line['status']='unresolved';line['reason']='Prior cost attribution is unresolved; original calculation retained'\\n            if line['allowed_cents']==0 and attributed[line['cost_id']]['prior_reservations']:\\n                line['status']='excluded';line['reason']='Prior cost obligation linked and excluded from this request; gross/conversion evidence retained'\\n    allowed = budget_view['remaining_request_cents'] if policy_ok else None\\n    stage('policy_eligibility', policy_ok, policy_refs + evidence_refs,\\n          'Expense calculation and filing are separate from travel permission, reviewed policy definitions and approvals',\\n          lead, 'Resolve line findings and remaining policy/permission evidence before treating calculated amounts as entitlement')\\n\\n    for line in lines:\\n        exception = line['exception']\\n        if exception['status'] != 'absent':\\n            stage(f\\\"finance_exception:{line['cost_id']}\\\", exception['status'] == 'valid', line['source_refs'],\\n                  exception.get('reason', 'Source-bound Finance exception'), finance_owner,\\n                  'Supply exact Finance actor, current claim/revision/cost, replacement amount, reason and covered issues')\\n        for item in line['eligibility_findings']:\\n            name = f\\\"eligibility:{line['cost_id']}:{item['issue']}\\\" + (f\\\":{item['travel_cancellation_id']}\\\" if item.get('travel_cancellation_id') else '')\\n            stage(name, item['status'] == 'covered_for_reimbursement', item['source_refs'] + item['exception_source_refs'],\\n                  item['original_finding'] + '; ' + item['status'], finance_owner,\\n                  'Obtain explicit Finance coverage for this exact eligibility finding and affected expense; retain original arrangement history')\\n\\n    prior_lines = {l['cost_id']: l for l in (prior_workflow or {}).get('lines', [])}\\n    def changed_exception_amount(line):\\n        old = prior_lines.get(line['cost_id'], {})\\n        before = old.get('conversion', {}).get('allowed_original_amount')\\n        after = line.get('conversion', {}).get('allowed_original_amount')\\n        # Unknown-to-known evidence and decimal display precision are not proof\\n        # of a material replacement-amount change.\\n        return bool(before is not None and after is not None\\n            and (line.get('exception', {}).get('status') == 'valid' or old.get('exception', {}).get('status') == 'valid')\\n            and Decimal(before) != Decimal(after))\\n    same_revision_change = bool(prior_workflow and prior_workflow.get('revision') == revision and (\\n        any(changed_exception_amount(line) for line in lines)\\n        or prior_workflow.get('exception_revalidation', {}).get('same_revision_change')))\\n    replacement_review = same_revision_change or any(\\n        line.get('replacement_amount_changed') or changed_exception_amount(line) for line in lines)\\n    line_refs={r for line in lines for r in line['source_refs']}\\n    dependencies=[r for key,tab in [('receipts','Receipts'),('merchant_payments','Merchant payments'),('caps','Caps'),('fx_rates','FX')]\\n                  for r in table(parsed,key,tab) if ref(r) in line_refs]\\n    claim_review=evaluate_reviews(parsed=parsed,kind='claim',subject_id=claim_id,revision=revision,\\n        trip_record=trips[0] if len(trips)==1 else {},employee=employee,subject_record=record,\\n        amount_cents=budget_view['remaining_request_cents'] if calculation['status']=='PASS' else None,decisions=decisions,arrival_batch=arrival_batch,\\n        observations=source_observations,cost_ids=[line['cost_id'] for line in lines],\\n        dependency_rows=dependencies,prior=(prior_workflow or {}).get('claim_approval'),\\n        withdrawn=linked and values.get('Status')=='withdrawn' and trusted(record),\\n        cancellation_ids=[f['travel_cancellation_id'] for f in eligibility if f['issue']=='travel_cancellation'],budget_context=budget_view)\\n    observed=claim_review['deliveries']\\n    # Preserve Step 175's extra binding requirement on material Finance replacements.\\n    for decision in observed:\\n        decision['exception_binding_valid']=(not replacement_review or review_binds_exception(\\n            decision['raw_record'],record,same_revision_change=same_revision_change,fields=fields,ref=ref))\\n        if not decision['exception_binding_valid']:\\n            decision['evidence_valid']=False\\n    approvals=claim_review['approved'] and all(d['evidence_valid'] for d in observed if d['active'])\\n    budget_replies=[d for d in observed if 'budget_owner' in d['roles']]\\n    budget_authorized=any(d['active'] and d['evidence_valid'] and d.get('budget_evidence_valid',True) and d['outcome']=='approve' for d in budget_replies)\\n    stage('budget_owner_authorization',budget_authorized,budget_view['source_refs']+[r for d in budget_replies for r in d['source_refs']],\\n        '; '.join(dict.fromkeys(d['budget_revalidation_reason'] for d in budget_replies if d.get('budget_revalidation_reason'))) or 'Current discretionary budget-owner authorization required; funds alone are insufficient',\\n        budget_view['owner'],'Supply a current budget-owner response bound to the complete scope ledger and this claim/version')\\n    review_refs=claim_review['source_refs']\\n    reviews_ok=all(claim_review['role_states'].get(role) not in {'missing','conflicting'} for role in claim_review['required_roles']) and all(d['evidence_valid'] for d in observed if d['active'])\\n    stage('review_evidence',reviews_ok,review_refs,\\n          'Current subject/version/role/actor/source/reason and complete review packets; rejected imports remain in history',\\n          lead,'Supply current source-bound replies and complete packets; answer the concrete return repair requests')\\n    stage('required_approvals',approvals,review_refs + policy_refs,\\n          f\\\"Claim approval state: {claim_review['state']}; required roles: {', '.join(claim_review['required_roles'])}\\\",\\n          lead,'Obtain the outstanding current-version human decisions; permit replies never approve a claim')\\n\\n    for reply in observed:\\n        if reply['outcome']=='return' and reply['evidence_valid']:\\n            stage(f\\\"review_return:{reply['decision_id']}\\\",not reply['active'],reply['source_refs'],\\n                  f\\\"{reply['reason']}; repair requested: {reply['repair_requested']}\\\",employee or 'Employee',reply['repair_requested'])\\n\\n    exception_revalidated = not replacement_review or approvals\\n    stage('exception_revalidation', exception_revalidated, evidence_refs + review_refs,\\n          'Replacement amounts require current claim reviews bound to the replacement source version; earlier reviews remain historical',\\n          lead, 'Obtain current revision/source-bound reviews of the Finance replacement amount and a matching reimbursement authorization')\\n\\n    requests = [r for r in table(parsed, 'reimbursement_requests', 'Reimbursement requests')\\n                if trusted(r) and visible(r) and fields(r).get('Claim reference') == claim_id and fields(r).get('Revision') == revision]\\n    request = fields(requests[0]) if len(requests) == 1 else {}\\n    obligation = finance.get('recorded_obligation')\\n    approved_ids = {d['decision_id'] for d in observed if d['outcome'] == 'approve' and d['evidence_valid'] and d['active']}\\n    request_ok = bool(linked and reimbursement_permission and policy_ok and approvals and obligation and len(requests) == 1\\n                      and request.get('Request reference') == obligation['request_id']\\n                      and request.get('Payee ID') == person.get('Payee ID') == obligation['payee_id']\\n                      and request.get('Currency') == 'EUR' and _cents(request.get('Amount (EUR)')) == allowed == obligation['amount_cents']\\n                      and obligation['claim_revision'] == revision and obligation['finance_officer'] ==…15930 tokens truncated…'][0]\\n    assert cancellation['cancellation_id'] == 'TC122' and cancellation['affected_claim_ids'] == []\\n    assert cancellation['financial_status'] == 'unresolved'\\n\\n\\ndef test_current_review_packet_must_match_current_trip_facts():\\n    parsed = synthetic()\\n    packet = next(s for s in parsed['workbook_sheets'] if s['name'] == 'Review packets')['records'][0]\\n    packet['values']['Business purpose']['value'] = 'SYNTHETIC stale business purpose'\\n    value = workflow(batches(parsed)[-1])\\n    assert stages(value)['review_evidence']['status'] == 'BLOCKED'\\n    assert value['status'] == 'pending'\\n\\n\\ndef test_pending_transfer_is_not_ignored_just_because_net_cash_already_balances():\\n    parsed = synthetic()\\n    pending = deepcopy(parsed['records']['finance_events'][1])\\n    pending['values']['Activity reference']['value'] = 'SYNTHETIC-PENDING-TRANSFER'\\n    pending['values']['Activity type']['value'] = 'mystery-pending'\\n    pending['values']['Arrival batch']['value'] = 3\\n    parsed['records']['finance_events'].append(pending)\\n    result = batches(parsed)[-1]\\n    assert workflow(result)['status'] == 'pending'\\n    assert 'SYNTHETIC-PENDING-TRANSFER' in result['finance_reconciliations']['SYN-C01']['unresolved_event_ids']\\n\\n\\ndef test_conflicting_duplicate_review_id_cannot_supply_an_approval():\\n    parsed = synthetic()\\n    conflict = deepcopy(parsed['records']['decisions'][0])\\n    conflict['values']['Outcome']['value'] = 'return'\\n    parsed['records']['decisions'].append(conflict)\\n    assert stages(workflow(batches(parsed)[-1]))['required_approvals']['status'] == 'BLOCKED'\\n\\n\\ndef test_synthetic_source_defined_cap_changes_entitlement_without_changing_merchant_cost():\\n    parsed = synthetic()\\n    policy = parsed['records']['workflow_policy_rules'][0]['values']\\n    policy['Eligible categories']['value'] = ['lodging']\\n    policy['Uncapped categories']['value'] = []\\n    parsed['records']['receipts'][0]['fields'] = [dict(f, value='lodging') if f['label'] == 'Category' else f for f in parsed['records']['receipts'][0]['fields']]\\n    cap = row('synthetic-travel-registers-workbook', 'SYNTHETIC cap row', **{\\n        'Cap reference': 'SYN-CAP', 'Destination': 'NL', 'Category': 'lodging', 'Currency': 'EUR',\\n        'Effective from': '2026-01-01', 'Effective to': '2026-12-31', 'Amount per unit': 40,\\n    })\\n    parsed['workbook_sheets'].append({'name': 'Caps', 'records': [cap]})\\n    parsed['records']['reimbursement_requests'][0]['values']['Amount (EUR)']['value'] = 40\\n    for event in parsed['records']['finance_events']:\\n        for field in ('Amount (EUR)', 'Obligation (EUR)'):\\n            if field in event['values']: event['values'][field]['value'] = 40\\n    value = workflow(batches(parsed)[-1])\\n    assert value['lines'][0]['original_cents'] == 10000\\n    assert value['allowed_cents'] == 4000 and value['balance_cents'] == 0\\n    assert value['status'] == 'closed-reimbursed'\\n    assert any('SYNTHETIC cap row' in ref for ref in value['lines'][0]['source_refs'])\\n\\n\\ndef test_untrusted_synthetic_threshold_cannot_override_policy_director_threshold():\\n    parsed = synthetic()\\n    parsed['records']['workflow_policy_rules'][0]['values']['Director threshold cents'] = {'value': 5000}\\n    value = workflow(batches(parsed)[-1])\\n    assert stages(value)['required_approvals']['status'] == 'PASS'\\n    assert value['status'] == 'closed-reimbursed'\\n    assert all('director' not in d['roles'] for d in value['observed_reviews'])\\n\\n\\ndef test_failed_transfer_requires_a_supported_resolution_even_when_other_cash_balances():\\n    parsed = synthetic()\\n    failed = deepcopy(parsed['records']['finance_events'][1])\\n    failed['values']['Activity reference']['value'] = 'SYNTHETIC-FAILED'\\n    failed['values']['Activity type']['value'] = 'failed'\\n    failed['values']['Arrival batch']['value'] = 3\\n    failed['values'].pop('Amount (EUR)', None)\\n    parsed['records']['finance_events'].append(failed)\\n    result = batches(parsed)[-1]\\n    assert result['finance_reconciliations']['SYN-C01']['balance_cents'] == 0\\n    assert workflow(result)['status'] == 'pending'\\n    assert stages(workflow(result))['financial_closure']['status'] == 'BLOCKED'\\n\\n\\ndef test_conflicting_current_claim_revision_blocks_even_if_last_record_looks_complete():\\n    parsed = synthetic()\\n    duplicate = deepcopy(parsed['records']['claim_revisions'][0])\\n    duplicate['locator'] = 'SYNTHETIC conflicting duplicate revision'\\n    duplicate['text'] += '\\\\nSYNTHETIC conflicting evidence'\\n    parsed['records']['claim_revisions'].append(duplicate)\\n    value = workflow(batches(parsed)[-1])\\n    assert stages(value)['claim_trip_link']['status'] == 'BLOCKED'\\n    assert value['status'] == 'pending'\\n\\n\\ndef test_finance_or_workbook_source_cannot_be_misrepresented_as_a_policy_definition():\\n    parsed = synthetic()\\n    policy = parsed['records']['workflow_policy_rules'][0]\\n    policy['source_id'] = 'synthetic-travel-registers-workbook'\\n    policy['source_sha256'] = hashlib.sha256(policy['source_id'].encode()).hexdigest()\\n    assert stages(workflow(batches(parsed)[-1]))['policy_eligibility']['status'] == 'BLOCKED'\\n\\n\\ndef test_affected_cancellation_holds_eligibility_without_erasing_calculation_or_cash():\\n    parsed = synthetic()\\n    native_rows = json.loads((Path(__file__).parent / 'fixtures/retained_finance_records.json').read_text())['records']['cancellation_activities']\\n    for source in native_rows:\\n        if source['values']['Cancellation reference']['value'] != 'TC018': continue\\n        record = deepcopy(source)\\n        record['source_id'] = 'synthetic-travel-registers-workbook'\\n        record['source_sha256'] = hashlib.sha256(record['source_id'].encode()).hexdigest()\\n        record['locator'] = 'SYNTHETIC affected cancellation ' + record['locator']\\n        record['values']['Trip reference']['value'] = 'T01'\\n        parsed['records']['cancellation_activities'].append(record)\\n    final = batches(parsed)[-1]\\n    value = workflow(final)\\n    assert stages(value)['travel_permission']['status'] == 'BLOCKED'\\n    assert value['permit_approval']['arrangements_at_commitment_supported']\\n    assert value['allowed_cents'] is None\\n    assert value['lines'][0]['calculated_cents'] == 10000\\n    assert any(f['issue'] == 'travel_cancellation' and f['status'] == 'unresolved' for f in value['lines'][0]['eligibility_findings'])\\n    assert final['snapshot']['claims'][0]['paid_cents'] == 10000\\n    assert value['status'] == 'pending'\\n    assert stages(value)['financial_closure']['status'] == 'BLOCKED'\\n    assert final['snapshot']['travel_cancellations'][0]['financial_status'] == 'unresolved'\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Correction execution and independent cancellation regression evidence.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom copy import deepcopy\\nimport json\\n\\nimport pytest\\n\\nfrom test_ordinary import synthetic, batches, workflow, stages\\nfrom test_retained_finance import _fixture, _batches\\nfrom travel_claim.revalidation import correction_changes, verification_document\\nfrom travel_claim.workflow import reduce_cancellation_activities\\n\\n\\ndef corrected(parsed, *, receipt=None, amount=None):\\n    record = deepcopy(parsed['records']['claim_revisions'][0])\\n    for field in record['fields']:\\n        if field['label'] == 'Revision': field['value'] = '2'\\n        if field['label'] == 'Arrival batch': field['value'] = '3'\\n    record['locator'] = 'SYNTHETIC Step157 correction'\\n    if receipt: record['text'] = record['text'].replace('R-COST-01', receipt)\\n    if amount: record['text'] = record['text'].replace('100.00', amount)\\n    parsed['records']['claim_revisions'].append(record)\\n    return record\\n\\n\\n@pytest.mark.parametrize('change', ['unchanged', 'receipt', 'amount'])\\ndef test_executed_rechecks_reject_stale_approvals_and_requests_and_preserve_cash(change):\\n    parsed = synthetic()\\n    record = corrected(parsed, receipt='SYN-MISSING-RECEIPT' if change == 'receipt' else None,\\n                       amount='120.00' if change == 'amount' else None)\\n    before, paid, revised, final = batches(parsed)\\n    correction = final['domain']['material_corrections'][0]\\n    assert correction['before_workflow']['status'] == 'closed-reimbursed'\\n    assert correction['before_finance']['net_confirmed_cents'] == 10000\\n    assert len(correction['executed_rechecks']) == 2\\n    checks = {s['stage']: s for s in correction['executed_rechecks'][0]['checks']}\\n    assert checks['required_approvals']['status'] == 'BLOCKED'\\n    assert checks['request_obligation']['status'] == 'BLOCKED'\\n    assert checks['supporting_evidence']['status'] == ('PASS' if change == 'unchanged' else 'BLOCKED')\\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['SYN-C01']['net_confirmed_cents'] == 10000\\n    assert final['snapshot']['claims'][0]['balance_cents'] is None\\n    assert workflow(paid)['status'] == 'closed-reimbursed'\\n    changes = correction_changes(parsed['records']['claim_revisions'][0], record)\\n    assert changes['expense_lines'][0]['changed'] == (change != 'unchanged')\\n    assert all(c['source_refs'] for c in checks.values())\\n\\n\\ndef test_retained_correction_moves_trip_but_keeps_historical_cancellation_and_non_cash_event():\\n    results = _batches(_fixture()); final = results[-1]\\n    c18 = next(c for c in final['domain']['material_corrections'] if c['claim_id'] == 'C18')\\n    assert c18['changed_dependencies']['fields']['Trip reference'] == {'before': 'T18', 'after': 'T18B'}\\n    detail = final['domain']['cancellation_evidence']['TC018']\\n    assert detail['current_claim_ids'] == []\\n    cancellation = next(c for c in final['snapshot']['travel_cancellations'] if c['cancellation_id'] == 'TC018')\\n    assert cancellation['affected_claim_ids'] == ['C18']\\n    assert cancellation['original_request_ids'] == ['REQ-C18']\\n    finance = final['finance_reconciliations']['C18']\\n    assert finance['net_confirmed_cents'] == 10000\\n    assert any(e['event_id'] == 'F-C18-2' and e['classification'] == 'finance_cancelled' for e in finance['event_history'])\\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C01']['net_confirmed_cents'] == 10000\\n    assert not any(c['claim_id'] == 'C01' for c in final['domain']['material_corrections'])\\n\\n\\ndef test_no_claim_cancellation_and_duplicate_confirmation_keep_independent_history():\\n    final = _batches(_fixture())[-1]\\n    cancel = next(c for c in final['snapshot']['travel_cancellations'] if c['cancellation_id'] == 'TC122')\\n    assert cancel['status'] == 'confirmed' and cancel['affected_claim_ids'] == []\\n    assert cancel['original_request_ids'] == [] and cancel['financial_status'] == 'unresolved'\\n    assert cancel['admitted_cancellation_event_ids'] == ['TC122-requested', 'TC122-confirmed']\\n    history = final['domain']['cancellation_evidence']['TC122']['history']\\n    assert [h['arrival_batch'] for h in history] == [1, 2]\\n    assert history[0]['actor'] == 'EMP-01'\\n    assert \\\"row 7\\\" in cancel['source_refs'][1]  # first delivery, not batch-4 redelivery\\n\\n\\n@pytest.mark.parametrize('fault', ['orphan', 'missing-effective', 'bad-time', 'no-claim-permit'])\\ndef test_partial_and_independent_permit_cancellation(fault):\\n    parsed = _fixture()\\n    rows = [r for r in parsed['records']['cancellation_activities']\\n            if r['values']['Cancellation reference']['value'] == 'TC121']\\n    parsed['records']['cancellation_activities'] = rows\\n    if fault == 'orphan': parsed['records']['cancellation_activities'] = rows[1:]\\n    elif fault == 'missing-effective': rows[1]['values'].pop('Effective time (UTC)', None)\\n    elif fault == 'bad-time': rows[1]['values']['Activity time (UTC)']['value'] = '2026-09-01T00:00:00'\\n    else:\\n        parsed['records']['claim_revisions'] = []\\n        parsed['records']['finance_events'] = []\\n    final = _batches(parsed)[-1]\\n    process = final['domain']['cancellation_state']['processes']['TC121']\\n    if fault == 'no-claim-permit':\\n        assert process['state'] == 'confirmed'\\n        cancel = final['snapshot']['travel_cancellations'][0]\\n        assert cancel['target_type'] == 'permit' and cancel['affected_claim_ids'] == []\\n    else:\\n        assert process['state'] != 'confirmed'\\n        assert any(k.startswith('cancellation-evidence:') for k in final['domain']['repair_queue']['items'])\\n\\n\\ndef test_verification_is_derived_from_executed_checks_and_labeled_offline():\\n    parsed = synthetic(); corrected(parsed)\\n    final = batches(parsed)[-1]\\n    data, summary = verification_document(final['domain'], final['snapshot']['travel_cancellations'], run_id='test')\\n    assert data['fresh_native_reads_performed'] is False\\n    assert 'OFFLINE REPLAY' in summary and 'required_approvals | BLOCKED' in summary\\n    assert 'SYNTHETIC Step157 correction' in summary\\n    assert data['corrections'][0]['executed_rechecks']\\n\\n\\ndef test_retained_dispositions_are_exact_revision_bound_observations_not_closure():\\n    final = _batches(_fixture())[-1]\\n    for cancellation_id, claim, revision, amount, page in (\\n            ('TC121', 'C121', 2, '20.00', 'PDF page 6'),\\n            ('TC019', 'C19', 3, '80.00', 'PDF page 7')):\\n        detail = final['domain']['cancellation_evidence'][cancellation_id]\\n        disposition, = detail['dispositions']\\n        assert (disposition['claim_id'], disposition['revision'], disposition['allowed_original_amount']) == (claim, revision, amount)\\n        assert disposition['source_ref'].endswith(page)\\n        assert final['domain']['ordinary_workflows'][claim]['status'] == 'pending'\\n        item = final['domain']['repair_queue']['items'][f'cancellation-financial:{cancellation_id}']\\n        assert item['status'] == 'open'\\n        assert 'disposition recorded' in item['missing_or_return_reason']\\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C19']['net_confirmed_cents'] == 8000\\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C121']['net_confirmed_cents'] == 2000\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Regression examples transcribed verbatim from the retained native workbook.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom copy import deepcopy\\nimport json\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nfrom travel_claim.finance import reconcile_finance_events as _reconcile\\n\\n\\ndef reconcile_finance_events(*args, **kwargs):\\n    kwargs.setdefault('event_context', {'requests': {'REQ-C01': {'claim_id': 'C01',\\n        'payee_id': 'EMP-01', 'actor': 'FIN-01', 'currency': 'EUR'}},\\n        'clock': {'date': '2026-11-15', 'timezone': 'Europe/Amsterdam'}})\\n    return _reconcile(*args, **kwargs)\\nfrom travel_claim.integration import integrate_arrival_batch\\n\\nFIXTURE = Path(__file__).parent / \\\"fixtures/retained_finance_records.json\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef _fixture():\\n    parsed = json.loads(FIXTURE.read_text())\\n    # Exact retained directory records extend the selected-record test fixture.\\n    ordinary = json.loads((FIXTURE.parent / 'ordinary_claim_c01.json').read_text())\\n    parsed['records']['people'] = next(s['records'] for s in ordinary['workbook_sheets'] if s['name'] == 'People')\\n    parsed['event_clock'] = {'date': '2026-11-15', 'timezone': 'Europe/Amsterdam'}  # verified POL-2026.2 line 3\\n    return parsed\\n\\n\\ndef _batches(parsed):\\n    prior = None\\n    results = []\\n    for batch in parsed['arrival_batches']:\\n        prior = integrate_arrival_batch(\\n            parsed, arrival_batch=batch, run_id='retained-regression', batch_id=f'arrival-{batch:03d}',\\n            source_binding={'path': 'sources.json', 'sha256': 'a' * 64},\\n            predecessor={'path': f'batches/arrival-{batch-1:03d}.json', 'sha256': 'b' * 64} if prior else None,\\n            prior_result=prior,\\n        )\\n        results.append(prior)\\n    return results\\n\\n\\ndef test_native_obligation_fields_and_ledger_balances_do_not_become_entitlement():\\n    parsed = _fixture()\\n    assert 'Claim revision' not in parsed['provenance']['finance_headers']\\n    results = _batches(parsed)\\n    final = results[-1]\\n    c1 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C01']\\n    obligation = c1['recorded_obligation']\\n    assert obligation['event_id'] == 'F-C01-accepted'\\n    assert obligation['request_id'] == 'REQ-C01'\\n    assert obligation['finance_officer'] == 'FIN-01'\\n    assert obligation['payee_id'] == 'EMP-01'\\n    assert obligation['amount_cents'] == 10000\\n    assert obligation['claim_revision'] is None\\n    assert obligation['arrival_revision_context'] == 1\\n    assert obligation['revision_link_status'] == 'arrival_context_only'\\n    assert obligation['first_arrival_batch'] == 1\\n    assert obligation['source_refs'] == [\\n        'travel-registers-workbook@' + parsed['provenance']['workbook_sha256'] + \\\"#tab 'Finance activity', row 33\\\"\\n    ]\\n    assert obligation['claim_source_refs'][0]['locator'] == 'PDF page 1'\\n    assert c1['net_confirmed_cents'] == 10000  # delivered twice, counted once\\n    assert c1['duplicate_events'][0]['delivery_batches'] == [2, 4]\\n    assert c1['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\\n    assert c1['authorized_obligation'] is None\\n    assert c1['balance_cents'] is None\\n    assert c1['closure_authority_confirmed'] is False\\n    projected = next(c for c in final['snapshot']['claims'] if c['claim_id'] == 'C01')\\n    assert projected['finance_evidence']['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\\n    assert projected['allowed_cents'] is None and projected['status'] == 'pending'\\n\\n\\ndef test_native_corrections_keep_ledger_history_and_revalidate_authority_only_where_affected():\\n    results = _batches(_fixture())\\n    first, _, third, final = results\\n    initial = deepcopy(first)\\n    c19 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C19']\\n    assert [(r['event_id'], r['amount_cents'], r['arrival_revision_context']) for r in c19['recorded_obligation_history']] == [\\n        ('F-C19-accepted', 10000, 1), ('F-C19-2', 8000, 2), ('F-C19-4', 8000, 3),\\n    ]\\n    assert c19['confirmed_payment_cents'] == 10000\\n    assert c19['confirmed_refund_cents'] == 2000\\n    assert c19['recorded_ledger_balance_cents'] == 0\\n    assert c19['recorded_obligation']['claim_revision'] is None\\n    assert c19['invalidated_previous_reconciliation']['claim_revision'] == 2\\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C09']['recorded_obligation']['arrival_revision_context'] == 2\\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C12']['recorded_obligation']['amount_cents'] == 7000\\n    assert final['finance_reconciliations']['C01']['recorded_obligation'] == first['finance_reconciliations']['C01']['recorded_obligation']\\n    # C18 correction has no newly bound accepted amount. Retain r1 context;\\n    # neither cancellation nor a fresh payment silently reauthorizes revision 2.\\n    c18 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C18']\\n    assert c18['claim_revision'] == 2\\n    assert c18['recorded_obligation']['arrival_revision_context'] == 1\\n    assert c18['authorized_obligation'] is None\\n    assert c18['confirmed_payment_cents'] == 10000\\n    item = final['domain']['repair_queue']['items']['finance:finance-obligation-missing:C09:1']\\n    # Historic question remains historic; r2 has its own current authorization question.\\n    assert item['revision'] == 1\\n    current = final['domain']['repair_queue']['items']['finance:finance-obligation-missing:C09:2']\\n    assert current['source_refs']\\n    assert 'recorded Finance obligation exists' in current['missing_or_return_reason']\\n    assert current['status'] == 'open'\\n    assert first == initial\\n\\n\\ndef test_native_refund_and_finance_cancellation_are_independent_of_business_cancellations():\\n    final = _batches(_fixture())[-1]\\n    cancellations = {c['cancellation_id']: c for c in final['snapshot']['travel_cancellations']}\\n    assert cancellations['TC122']['affected_claim_ids'] == []\\n    assert cancellations['TC122']['target_type'] == 'trip'\\n    assert cancellations['TC121']['target_type'] == 'permit'\\n    assert all(c['financial_status'] == 'unresolved' for c in cancellations.values())\\n    c18 = final['finance_reconciliations']['C18']\\n    assert c18['recorded_obligation']['amount_cents'] == 10000\\n/tmp/step184-start-hashes.json\\n\"}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad0b682329c819090dcf9a78c1abe91","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a13f48-7c83-7c72-a773-e78f5db417e4"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_a9eb9aa93bbe4deb93fcaff61a9bb95d","id":"ctc_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad0b6826eac819099892dff97fdb84f","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '72,141p' src/travel_claim/finance.py; sed -n '142,190p' src/travel_claim/finance.py; cat src/travel_claim/event_validation.py; sed -n '286,351p' src/travel_claim/integration.py; sed -n '440,460p' src/travel_claim/integration.py; cat snapshot.schema.json | sed -n '285,385p'\",\"max_output_tokens\":6500}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1792063106.4350557,"turn_id":"01a13f48-7c83-7c72-a773-e78f5db417e4"},"name":"exec","status":"completed","type":"custom_tool_call"},{"call_id":"call_a9eb9aa93bbe4deb93fcaff61a9bb95d","guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000},"id":"ctco_01a13f48-f9a2-7910-be56-a4fd08422e49","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1792063109.538299,"turn_id":"01a13f48-7c83-7c72-a773-e78f5db417e4"},"output":[{"text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.8 seconds\nOutput:\n","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"934bf6\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.179313875,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":5980,\"output\":\"def _recorded_obligations(history: list[dict], *, claim_id: str, current_revision: int,\\n                          revisions: list[dict]) -\u003e tuple[list[dict], dict | None, str | None]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Read ledger observations, without deriving reimbursement authorization.\\n\\n    Obligation (EUR) is a recorded amount, not a cash delta. Native rows omit\\n    claim revision; arrival context is retained separately from explicit links.\\n    Only the first delivery establishes context; redelivery cannot rebind it.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    groups: dict[str, list[dict]] = defaultdict(list)\\n    for event in history:\\n        if event['classification'] in {'obligation_accepted', 'finance_adjustment', 'finance_resolution'}:\\n            groups[event['event_id']].append(event)\\n    records = []\\n    problem = None\\n    for event_id, occurrences in groups.items():\\n        event = occurrences[0]\\n        values = event['source_record']\\n        batches = [e['source_record'].get('Arrival batch') for e in occurrences]\\n        first_batch = min((_positive_integer(b) for b in batches if _positive_integer(b)), default=None)\\n        context_rows = [r for r in revisions if first_batch is not None\\n                        and _positive_integer(r.get('arrival_batch')) is not None\\n                        and _positive_integer(r['arrival_batch']) \u003c= first_batch]\\n        context = max((r['revision'] for r in context_rows), default=None)\\n        explicit = _positive_integer(values.get('Claim revision'))\\n        matches = [r for r in revisions if r['revision'] == explicit] if explicit else []\\n        link = ('explicit_current' if explicit == current_revision else 'explicit_historical') if matches else 'arrival_context_only' if context else 'unmatched'\\n        refs = [_reference_text(e['source_ref']) for e in occurrences]\\n        record = {\\n            'event_id': event_id, 'event_type': event['event_type'], 'claim_id': claim_id,\\n            'request_id': values.get('Request reference'), 'finance_officer': values.get('Finance officer'),\\n            'payee_id': values.get('Payee ID'), 'currency': event['currency'],\\n            'amount_cents': event['obligation_cents'], 'activity_time_utc': values.get('Activity time (UTC)'),\\n            'claim_revision': explicit if matches else None, 'arrival_revision_context': context,\\n            'revision_link_status': link, 'first_arrival_batch': first_batch,\\n            'delivery_batches': batches, 'source_refs': list(dict.fromkeys(refs)),\\n            'claim_source_refs': [deepcopy(r['source_ref']) for r in (matches or context_rows)\\n                                  if r['revision'] == (explicit if matches else context)],\\n        }\\n        records.append(record)\\n        if (event['currency'] != 'EUR' or event['obligation_cents'] is None or not first_batch\\n                or not all(isinstance(values.get(key), str) and values[key].strip()\\n                           for key in ('Request reference', 'Finance officer', 'Payee ID'))\\n                or not all(all(e['source_ref'].get(key) for key in ('source_id', 'source_sha256', 'locator')) for e in occurrences)\\n                or (values.get('Claim revision') is not None and not matches)):\\n            problem = 'Obligation record lacks supported amount, request/payee/officer, source identity, arrival, or explicit revision match'\\n    if not records:\\n        return [], None, None\\n    if len({(r['request_id'], r['payee_id'], r['currency']) for r in records}) != 1:\\n        problem = 'Multiple request/payee/currency ledgers cannot be combined as one obligation'\\n    # A single observation needs no ordering assumption. Multiple observations\\n    # require explicit UTC event times; arrival numbers do not define business time.\\n    if len(records) \u003e 1:\\n        try:\\n            def stamp(record):\\n                dt = datetime.fromisoformat(record['activity_time_utc'].replace('Z', '+00:00'))\\n                # The retained header explicitly names UTC even when the cell\\n                # serialization omits an offset.\\n                if dt.utcoffset() is not None and dt.utcoffset().total_seconds() != 0:\\n                    raise ValueError('not UTC')\\n                return dt.replace(tzinfo=None)\\n            records.sort(key=lambda r: (stamp(r), r['event_id']))\\n            for left, right in zip(records, records[1:]):\\n                if stamp(left) == stamp(right) and left['amount_cents'] != right['amount_cents']:\\n                    problem = 'Conflicting obligation amounts have the same event time'\\n        except (ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):\\n            problem = 'Multiple obligation observations lack unambiguous UTC ordering'\\n    return records, deepcopy(records[-1]) if not problem else None, problem\\n\\n\\ndef reconcile_finance_events(\\n    events: list[dict[str, Any]],\\n    *,\\n    claim_id: str,\\n    current_revision: int,\\n    authorized_obligation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\\n    revision_history: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None,\\n    previous_reconciliation: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\\n    owner: str = \\\"Finance\\\",\\n    source_classifications: dict[str, str] | None = None,\\n    event_context: dict[str, Any] | None = None,\\n) -\u003e dict[str, Any]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Reconcile source events for a claim without making policy decisions.\\n\\n    `authorized_obligation` is an independent, already-authorized input of\\n    `{amount_cents, claim_revision, source_refs}`. This function neither\\n    derives nor authorizes it. `source_classifications` may extend the native\\n    workbook vocabulary when a retained source defines another event type;\\n    unrecognized types otherwise remain unresolved.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if not claim_id or isinstance(current_revision, bool) or not isinstance(current_revision, int) or current_revision \u003c 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"claim_id and a positive current_revision are required\\\")\\n    if not owner:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"owner is required for reconciliation issues\\\")\\n    if (previous_reconciliation and 'admitted_events' not in previous_reconciliation\\n            and any(previous_reconciliation.get(k) for k in ('confirmed_payment_event_ids', 'confirmed_refund_event_ids',\\n                'confirmed_payment_cents', 'confirmed_refund_cents', 'net_confirmed_cents'))):\\n        raise ValueError('Legacy admission state requires explicit verified migration; refusing to erase or invent admitted money')\\n\\n    classes = dict(_NATIVE_EVENT_CLASSES)\\n    if source_classifications:\\n        allowed_classes = {\\n            \\\"confirmed_payment\\\", \\\"confirmed_refund\\\", \\\"pending_transfer\\\",\\n            \\\"obligation_accepted\\\", \\\"failed_transfer\\\", \\\"retry_authorization\\\",\\n            \\\"finance_cancellation_requested\\\", \\\"finance_cancelled\\\",\\n            \\\"finance_adjustment\\\", \\\"finance_resolution\\\",\\n        }\\n        for event_type, classification in source_classifications.items():\\n            if not isinstance(event_type, str) or classification not in allowed_classes:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"unsupported source event classification: {event_type!r} -\u003e {classification!r}\\\")\\n            classes[event_type] = classification\\n\\n    # Accept full-history or delta calls without dropping earlier raw deliveries.\\n    retained = [{**deepcopy(h['source_ref']), 'values': {k: {'value': v} for k, v in h['source_record'].items()}}\\n                for h in (previous_reconciliation or {}).get('event_history', []) if isinstance(h.get('source_ref'), dict) and 'source_record' in h]\\n    deliveries = []\\n    for record in retained + events:\\n        if not any(_source_ref(r) == _source_ref(record) and _values(r) == _values(record) for r in deliveries):\\n            deliveries.append(record)\\n    events = deliveries\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Shared evidence checks for Finance and business-cancellation admissions.\\n\\nA calendar-date clock never implies midnight or an end-of-day instant. Events\\non that same local date need an explicit cutoff before admission.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone, date\\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo\\n\\n\\ndef utc_time(value):\\n    if not isinstance(value, str) or 'T' not in value:\\n        raise ValueError('missing explicit UTC event date/time')\\n    stamp = datetime.fromisoformat(value.replace('Z', '+00:00'))\\n    # Native columns explicitly name UTC; offsetless serialization is UTC.\\n    if stamp.utcoffset() is not None and stamp.utcoffset().total_seconds() != 0:\\n        raise ValueError('event timestamp is not UTC')\\n    return stamp.replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\\n\\n\\ndef observation_error(stamp, clock):\\n    try:\\n        if isinstance(clock, str):\\n            cutoff = datetime.fromisoformat(clock.replace('Z', '+00:00'))\\n            if cutoff.utcoffset() is None:\\n                return 'case cutoff lacks timezone'\\n            return 'future observation' if stamp \u003e cutoff else None\\n        if isinstance(clock, dict):\\n            local = stamp.astimezone(ZoneInfo(clock['timezone'])).date()\\n            case_date = date.fromisoformat(clock['date'])\\n            if local \u003e case_date:\\n                return 'future observation'\\n            if local == case_date:\\n                return 'same-day cutoff is unknown; no time of day inferred'\\n            return None\\n    except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError):\\n        return 'invalid authoritative event cutoff'\\n    return 'authoritative event cutoff is unavailable'\\n\\n\\ndef text_id(value):\\n    return isinstance(value, str) and bool(value.strip()) and value == value.strip()\\n\\n\\ndef source_values(row):\\n    return {k: v.get('value') for k, v in row.get('values', {}).items()}\\n\\n\\ndef finance_context(parsed, revisions, events, claim_id, arrival_batch=None):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Bind source-observed request IDs to historical claim employees/directory.\\n\\n    Acceptance is request identity evidence, never reimbursement entitlement.\\n    A cash row cannot manufacture its own request binding.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    records = parsed.get('records', {})\\n    people = records.get('people', next((s['records'] for s in parsed.get('workbook_sheets', []) if s['name'] == 'People'), []))\\n    bindings = {}\\n    seen = set()\\n    for event in events:\\n        value = source_values(event)\\n        if value.get('Activity reference') in seen:\\n            continue\\n        seen.add(value.get('Activity reference'))\\n        if value.get('Claim reference') != claim_id or value.get('Activity type') != 'accepted':\\n            continue\\n        occurrences = [source_values(r) for r in events if source_values(r).get('Activity reference') == value.get('Activity reference')]\\n        try:\\n            first_batch = min(int(v['Arrival batch']) for v in occurrences)\\n            first = [v for v in occurrences if int(v['Arrival batch']) == first_batch]\\n            immutable = lambda v: {k: x for k, x in v.items() if k != 'Arrival batch'}\\n            if any(immutable(v) != immutable(first[0]) for v in first):\\n                continue  # A conflicted first delivery cannot establish a request.\\n            value = first[0]\\n            if observation_error(utc_time(value.get('Activity time (UTC)')), parsed.get('event_clock') or parsed.get('case_clock')):\\n                continue\\n            batch = int(value['Arrival batch'])\\n            available = [r for r in revisions if r.get('arrival_batch') is not None and int(r['arrival_batch']) \u003c= batch]\\n            revision = max(available, key=lambda r: r['revision'])\\n        except (TypeError, ValueError, KeyError):\\n            continue\\n        employee = next((f['value'] for f in revision['record'].get('fields', []) if f['label'] == 'Employee'), None)\\n        directory = [r for r in people if source_values(r).get('Employee ID') == employee]\\n        if len(directory) != 1:\\n            continue\\n        person = source_values(directory[0])\\n        if value.get('Finance officer') != person.get('Finance officer') or value.get('Payee ID') != person.get('Payee ID'):\\n            continue\\n        if value.get('Currency') != 'EUR':\\n            continue\\n        request = value.get('Request reference')\\n        if not all(text_id(x) for x in (request, person.get('Payee ID'), person.get('Finance officer'))):\\n            continue\\n        binding = dict(claim_id=claim_id, payee_id=person['Payee ID'], actor=person['Finance officer'], currency='EUR')\\n        # Conflicting request ownership is unresolved rather than last-wins.\\n        if request in bindings and bindings[request] != binding:\\n            bindings[request] = None\\n        else:\\n            bindings.setdefault(request, binding)\\n    for request_row in records.get('reimbursement_requests', []):\\n        value = source_values(request_row)\\n        batch = value.get('Arrival batch')\\n        try:\\n            if isinstance(batch, bool) or int(batch) != float(batch) or int(batch) \u003c 1 or arrival_batch is not None and int(batch) \u003e arrival_batch:\\n                continue\\n        except (TypeError, ValueError, OverflowError):\\n            continue\\n        matches = [r for r in revisions if r['revision'] == value.get('Revision')]\\n        if value.get('Claim reference') != claim_id or len(matches) != 1 or value.get('Currency') != 'EUR':\\n            continue\\n        employee = next((f['value'] for f in matches[0]['record'].get('fields', []) if f['label'] == 'Employee'), None)\\n        directory = [r for r in people if source_values(r).get('Employee ID') == employee]\\n        if len(directory) != 1:\\n            continue\\n        person = source_values(directory[0]); request = value.get('Request reference')\\n        if not text_id(request) or value.get('Payee ID') != person.get('Payee ID'):\\n            continue\\n        binding = dict(claim_id=claim_id, payee_id=person.get('Payee ID'), actor=person.get('Finance officer'), currency='EUR')\\n        if request in bindings and bindings[request] != binding:\\n            bindings[request] = None\\n        else:\\n            bindings.setdefault(request, binding)\\n    return {'requests': bindings, 'clock': parsed.get('event_clock') or parsed.get('case_clock')}\\n\\n\\ndef finance_errors(value, classification, context, cents):\\n    errors = []\\n    if not all(text_id(value.get(k)) for k in ('Activity reference', 'Claim reference', 'Request reference', 'Payee ID', 'Finance officer')):\\n        errors.append('missing or malformed event/request/claim/payee/actor identity')\\n    binding = (context or {}).get('requests', {}).get(value.get('Request reference'))\\n    if not binding:\\n        errors.append('request has no unambiguous source-bound directory authority')\\n    elif any(value.get(field) != binding.get(key) for field, key in (\\n            ('Claim reference', 'claim_id'), ('Payee ID', 'payee_id'), ('Finance officer', 'actor'), ('Currency', 'currency'))):\\n        errors.append('request/claim/payee/currency/Finance actor does not match authority')\\n    if value.get('Currency') != 'EUR':\\n        errors.append('unsupported Finance currency')\\n    if classification in {'confirmed_payment', 'confirmed_refund', 'pending_transfer'} or value.get('Amount (EUR)') is not None:\\n        amount = cents(value.get('Amount (EUR)'))\\n        if amount is None or amount \u003c= 0:\\n            errors.append('cash amount must be positive integer cents')\\n    if classification in {'obligation_accepted', 'finance_adjustment', 'finance_resolution'} and cents(value.get('Obligation (EUR)')) is None:\\n        errors.append('obligation amount lacks exact nonnegative cents')\\n    try:\\n        error = observation_error(utc_time(value.get('Activity time (UTC)')), (context or {}).get('clock'))\\n        if error:\\n            errors.append(error)\\n    except (ValueError, TypeError):\\n        errors.append('invalid UTC event time')\\n    return errors\\n                next_action=\\\"Obtain a consistent employee initiation and linked supervisor confirmation with explicit UTC times\\\",\\n                run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id)\\n    current_invalid = {i.get('event_id') for i in reduced['issues']}\\n    for item_id, item in domain['repair_queue']['items'].items():\\n        if item_id.startswith('cancellation-evidence:'):\\n            for event_id, record in reduced['admitted_records'].items():\\n                if item_id.startswith(f'cancellation-evidence:{event_id}:') and event_id not in current_invalid:\\n                    record_evidence_validation(domain['repair_queue'], item_id=item_id, supported=True,\\n                        source_refs=[_ref_text(_ref(record))], run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id)\\n    claim_revisions = _subject_claim_revisions(history)\\n    snapshot_rows = []\\n    for cancellation_id, process in sorted(reduced[\\\"processes\\\"].items()):\\n        target = process[\\\"target\\\"]\\n        target_revision = target.get(\\\"revision\\\")\\n        if (target.get(\\\"subject_type\\\") not in {\\\"trip\\\", \\\"permit\\\"} or not target.get(\\\"subject_id\\\")\\n                or isinstance(target_revision, bool) or not isinstance(target_revision, int) or target_revision \u003c 1):\\n            domain[\\\"projection_issues\\\"].append({\\n                \\\"record_id\\\": f\\\"cancellation-projection:{cancellation_id}\\\",\\n                \\\"reason\\\": \\\"cancellation process lacks a supported target identity and revision; process remains in the integration sidecar\\\",\\n                \\\"owner\\\": \\\"Travel Administration Lead\\\",\\n                \\\"resolution_needed\\\": \\\"verify the cancellation target and revision in the native workbook\\\",\\n            })\\n            continue\\n        record_order = process[\\\"activity_ids\\\"]\\n        if not record_order:\\n            continue  # Orphan evidence remains in cancellation_state and owned issues.\\n        request_id = record_order[0]\\n        request = raw_by_id[request_id]\\n        request_values = row_values(request)\\n        confirmation = next((raw_by_id[event_id] for event_id in record_order\\n                             if row_values(raw_by_id[event_id]).get(\\\"Action\\\") == \\\"confirmed\\\"), None)\\n        confirmation_values = row_values(confirmation) if confirmation else {}\\n        trip_id = request_values.get(\\\"Trip reference\\\")\\n        trip_revision = _as_batch(request_values.get(\\\"Trip revision\\\"))\\n        permit_id = request_values.get(\\\"Permit reference\\\") if target[\\\"subject_type\\\"] == \\\"permit\\\" else None\\n        permit_revision = request_values.get(\\\"Permit revision\\\") if target[\\\"subject_type\\\"] == \\\"permit\\\" else None\\n        permit_revision = _as_batch(permit_revision) if permit_revision is not None else None\\n        affected = []\\n        current_affected = []\\n        for claim_id, claim in claim_revisions.items():\\n            for claim_rev in claim[\\\"revisions\\\"]:\\n                if target[\\\"subject_type\\\"] == \\\"trip\\\":\\n                    matches = claim_rev.get(\\\"trip_id\\\") == target[\\\"subject_id\\\"] and claim_rev.get(\\\"trip_revision\\\") == target[\\\"revision\\\"]\\n                else:\\n                    trip_index = history.get(\\\"trip\\\", {}).get(str(claim_rev.get(\\\"trip_id\\\")), {})\\n                    matches = any(\\n                        trip_rev.get(\\\"revision\\\") == claim_rev.get(\\\"trip_revision\\\")\\n                        and trip_rev.get(\\\"permit_id\\\") == target[\\\"subject_id\\\"]\\n                        and trip_rev.get(\\\"permit_revision\\\") == target[\\\"revision\\\"]\\n                        for trip_rev in trip_index.get(\\\"revisions\\\", [])\\n                    )\\n                if matches:\\n                    affected.append(claim_id)\\n                    if claim_rev[\\\"revision\\\"] == claim[\\\"current_revision\\\"]:\\n                        current_affected.append(claim_id)\\n        affected = sorted(set(affected))\\n        task_id = f\\\"cancellation-financial:{cancellation_id}\\\"\\n        refs = [_ref_text(_ref(raw_by_id[event_id])) for event_id in record_order]\\n        reason = \\\"Finance effect of the independent travel cancellation has not been resolved from an authorized Finance record\\\"\\n        next_action = \\\"Finance to record whether this cancellation affects an accepted obligation, transfer, payment, or refund\\\"\\n        queue = domain[\\\"repair_queue\\\"]\\n        if task_id not in queue[\\\"items\\\"]:\\n            _open_issue_for_subject(\\n                queue, item_id=task_id,\\n                subject_type=target[\\\"subject_type\\\"], subject_id=str(target[\\\"subject_id\\\"]),\\n                revision=target_revision, refs=refs, reason=reason,\\n        if actor_item in queue[\\\"items\\\"]:\\n            record_evidence_validation(queue, item_id=actor_item, supported=actors_ok,\\n                source_refs=refs + actor_refs, run_id=run_id, batch_id=batch_id)\\n        domain[\\\"cancellation_evidence\\\"][cancellation_id] = {\\n            \\\"current_claim_ids\\\": sorted(set(current_affected)),\\n            \\\"source_refs\\\": refs + actor_refs + [d[\\\"source_ref\\\"] for d in dispositions],\\n            \\\"history\\\": deepcopy(process[\\\"history\\\"]),\\n            \\\"actor_status\\\": \\\"PASS\\\" if actors_ok else \\\"BLOCKED: verify employee and supervisor against the trip register\\\",\\n            \\\"dispositions\\\": dispositions,\\n            \\\"disposition_status\\\": \\\"recorded; eligibility and financial completion require recheck\\\" if dispositions else \\\"BLOCKED: no cancellation-bound Finance disposition\\\",\\n            \\\"request_effect\\\": \\\"hold payment readiness; retain obligation and cash history\\\",\\n        }\\n    return snapshot_rows\\n\\n\\ndef _sync_decision_and_revision_issues(\\n    domain: dict[str, Any], *, history: dict[str, Any], run_id: str, batch_id: str,\\n) -\u003e None:\\n    queue = domain[\\\"repair_queue\\\"]\\n    blockers = []\\n    for conflict in history.get(\\\"issues\\\", {}).get(\\\"repeated_subject_revisions\\\", []):\\n            \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n          },\\n          \\\"claim_id\\\": {\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n            \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n          },\\n          \\\"revision\\\": {\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\",\\n            \\\"minimum\\\": 1\\n          },\\n          \\\"amount_cents\\\": {\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"integer\\\",\\n            \\\"minimum\\\": 0\\n          },\\n          \\\"payee\\\": {\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n            \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n          },\\n          \\\"currency\\\": {\\n            \\\"const\\\": \\\"EUR\\\"\\n          },\\n          \\\"status\\\": {\\n            \\\"enum\\\": [\\n              \\\"proposed\\\",\\n              \\\"accepted\\\",\\n              \\\"dispatched\\\",\\n              \\\"cancel-pending\\\",\\n              \\\"cancelled\\\",\\n              \\\"settled\\\",\\n              \\\"held\\\"\\n            ]\\n          },\\n          \\\"decision_ids\\\": {\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n            \\\"items\\\": {\\n              \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n              \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n            },\\n            \\\"uniqueItems\\\": true\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"admitted_event_ids\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n      \\\"items\\\": {\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n        \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n      },\\n      \\\"uniqueItems\\\": true,\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Admitted Finance activity IDs only. Travel cancellation activity IDs belong exclusively in travel_cancellations[].admitted_cancellation_event_ids; neither kind may invent the other kind of effect.\\\"\\n    },\\n    \\\"issues\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n      \\\"items\\\": {\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n        \\\"required\\\": [\\n          \\\"record_id\\\",\\n          \\\"reason\\\",\\n          \\\"owner\\\",\\n          \\\"resolution_needed\\\"\\n        ],\\n        \\\"properties\\\": {\\n          \\\"record_id\\\": {\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n            \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n          },\\n          \\\"reason\\\": {\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n            \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n          },\\n          \\\"owner\\\": {\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n            \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n          },\\n          \\\"resolution_needed\\\": {\\n            \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n            \\\"minLength\\\": 1\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \\\"travel_cancellations\\\": {\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"One current row per valid observed cancellation_id, including processes without any claim. Confirmation and financial resolution are separate facts. Invalid orphan deliveries remain in issues and retained sources until a valid initiation establishes a process.\\\",\\n      \\\"items\\\": {\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n        \\\"required\\\": [\\n          \\\"cancellation_id\\\",\\n          \\\"target_type\\\",\\n          \\\"trip_id\\\",\\n          \\\"trip_revision\\\",\\n          \\\"permit_id\\\",\\n          \\\"permit_revision\\\",\\n          \\\"status\\\",\\n          \\\"admitted_cancellation_event_ids\\\",\\n          \\\"requested_at\\\",\\n          \\\"confirmed_at\\\",\\n          \\\"effective_at\\\",\\n          \\\"affected_claim_ids\\\",\\n          \\\"original_request_ids\\\",\\n\"}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad0b697a84c819086c047e25ac604dd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a13f48-7c83-7c72-a773-e78f5db417e4"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad0b6a724888190aa0b8afa3aa7873f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a13f48-7c83-7c72-a773-e78f5db417e4"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad0b6b443008190a95ae48408a8fe63","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a13f48-7c83-7c72-a773-e78f5db417e4"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"call_id":"call_609ce37320c947f2968f2068ca807ebb","id":"ctc_02f4b2bd528e1b90016ad0b6b45fd88190bb519c391aa19ad5","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '100,200p' src/travel_claim/cancellation.py; sed -n '595,688p' src/travel_claim/integration.py; sed -n '390,442p' snapshot.schema.json; sed -n '130,158p' tests/test_ordinary.py; sed -n '1,80p'