n, stale targets, future observations, process action conflicts and trip-versus-permit retirement/renewal. |\n| [POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:31](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:31) | Requested holds, no-financial-effect and cancellation-aware eligibility/reviews | **Major missing semantics** | Linked payment readiness holds, but new-arrangement pause is not modeled. Every process is projected financial_status=unresolved; supported no-cost/no-obligation processes cannot resolve to no-financial-effect. Cancellation exceptions are observed without covered-issue validation/application. Packet Travel cancellation references is present in retained evidence but ignored by current review checks. Existing lawful arrangements must not gain permit_unapproved solely from later cancellation. [integration.py:330](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/integration.py:330); [integration.py:380](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/integration.py:380); [integration.py:391](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/integration.py:391); [ordinary.py:220](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/src/travel_claim/ordinary.py:220). | [test_revalidation.py:63](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/tests/test_revalidation.py:63) currently expects an unresolved no-claim process; absence of a claim alone is not proof of no financial effect. Add scoped disposition coverage, post-confirmation packets, preserved planned end/initial filings and same-day ambiguity. |\n| [POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:33](/home/maxg/travel-expense-claim/user-provided-sources/step-167/POL-2026.2-browser-copy.txt:33) | Pre-acceptance versus post-acceptance/payment cancellation | **Major lifecycle over-hold and missing resolution linkage** | Ordinary closure rejects any affected cancellation, regardless of timing/disposition. Policy permits pre-acceptance cancellation with bound disposition and fresh cancellation-aware reviews without a separate F