nterview. Do not invent policy content or a case clock.\n\nDo not commit or push yet.\n\nReport changed files, native source access results, test count, and remaining blockers.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":95},"id":"msg_01a13c28-ce86-7022-8198-88f4bc47f48c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792010669.7020998,"turn_id":"01a13c28-c6bd-7171-9c10-8efd3c67b498"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Preserve the completed Project D Step 162 fresh native-source execution milestone.\n\n    Inspect git status, all source diffs, and the staging area.\n\n    Stage ONLY these implementation files, if present and changed:\n\n        README.md\n\n        skills/travel-expense-claim/SKILL.md\n\n        src/travel_claim/cli.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/sources.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/parsing.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/readiness.py\n\n        src/travel_claim/live_run.py\n\n        The changed or newly created test/helper files for this milestone, after listing their exact paths and verifying their contents.\n\n    Do not stage artifacts/runs/, artifacts/verification/, the original interview, or unrelated files.\n\n    Run git diff --cached --check and the complete pytest suite.\n\nVerify the new live-source manifest and retained response evidence.\n\nIf validation passes, commit with:\nfeat: capture and validate fresh native source runs\n\nPush to origin main, allowing the existing Entire.io hooks to run.\n\nVerify the exact remote main commit and Entire.io checkpoint references.\n\nConfirm the original interview and all 104 previously retained files remain unchanged.\n\nDo not force-push, rewrite history, or modify retained artifacts.\n\nReport the exact committed files, commit hash, test count, source-verification results, push verification, and warnings.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":104},"id":"msg_01a13c32-aa2f-73f1-901a-e19eda017436","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1792011315.7594304,"turn_id":"01a13c32-a4fc-7732-902b-be443b2f0740"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Project D — Step 167: Incorporate the newly recovered authoritative policy.\n\nI personally opened the original Alderbridge Consulting Notion policy URL in my browser and copied its complete visible text. It identifies itself as POL-2026.2 and explicitly states the case clock is 2026-11-15, Europe/Amsterdam.\n\nThe policy text is available from me, the user. Do not invent, paraphrase, or reconstruct any missing wording.\n\nFirst, help me save the exact policy text as a UTF-8 file under a clearly labeled user-provided-source directory. Ask me for the file or exact text if it is not accessible in your environment.\n\nPreserve its original wording and distinguish my authenticated/browser-visible copy from a fresh native Notion API or HTTP read. Do not retroactively mark earlier failed Notion captures successful.\n\nThen:\n\nVerify the policy identifier, case clock, and complete retained text.\n\nInspect the current implementation against every policy section, including eligibility, approvals, filing deadlines, caps, FX, Finance reconciliation, corrections, and independent cancellations.\n\nProduce a source-grounded implementation gap report with exact code and policy references.\n\nIdentify which blockers are resolved by the recovered policy and which still require independent evidence or human decisions.\n\nDo not alter earlier runs, snapshots, or financial conclusions.\n\nDo not commit or push yet.\n\nStop after the evidence audit and report the findings before making implementation changes.","type":"input_text"}],"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"mcp_attribution":{"status":"none"},"user_input_order":112},"id":"